b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to use Temporal Sympathy with Shifting Sands to target the moments you want to rewrite without using multiple rewind Reaches ? I always thought it was curious to use Reaches instead, since being limited to [Potency] turns means you have very little ways to deal with the ensuing butterfly effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Temporal Sympathy can only be used with spells that calls for it. Shifting Sands rewrites the most recent history of the subject, with Potency or Reaches determining how much. What you're describing is Corridors of Time, the Unmaking spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-06T10:17:02-08:00","id":1434694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1434688#post1434688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to use Temporal Sympathy with Shifting Sands to target the moments you want to rewrite without using multiple rewind Reaches ? I always thought it was curious to use Reaches instead, since being limited to [Potency] turns means you have very little ways to deal with the ensuing butterfly effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, per the description of Temporal Sympathy and the existence of Corridors of Time. If you want to troubleshoot your short-term time travel, you extend the Duration to keep the spell going until you reach the present again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T11:05:56-08:00","id":1434859,"title":"","content":"In 2ed, do archmasters expend mana or pneuma? Or are they capable of using both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T11:37:49-08:00","id":1434864,"title":"","content":"Possibly. Their mechanics are not scheduled for anything in process, and if someone were commissioned to write them it depends how much wordcount they get - ironically, the *fewer* words available, the more likely it will be &quot;they just always have Pneuma&quot; as that's shorter and less complicated than the alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T05:56:51-08:00","id":1434926,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply! I guess that I would head-canon believe that imperial spells could be made to cost Pneuma (which could be one more reason why normal Mages can't comprehend their operation) and then say that Archmages can still use mana for its utility in activating attainments, artifacts, etc.). They would perhaps have to have a level 6 universal attainment that allows them to convert the Pneuma that filters down their Golden Road via their Cintamani into Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T19:59:50-08:00","id":1435268,"title":"","content":"When a spell is withstood by Stamina, Composure, or Resolve, do ephemeral and Supernal beings withstand it with Resistance or Rank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T23:52:01-08:00","id":1435275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1435268#post1435268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a spell is withstood by Stamina, Composure, or Resolve, do ephemeral and Supernal beings withstand it with Resistance or Rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank, confirmed in page 127 of the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T18:52:16-08:00","id":1436482,"title":"","content":"Hello all, new questions:<br /> 1) Is it possible to create an astral sanctum? Especially one with as many trappings (eg safe place, ritual casting space, etc.) as possible for a real sanctum such that a cabal could be spread out around the world, but meet up in the astral. <br /> <br /> 2) Would it have to be in the Temenos, or could it be in the Oneiros of a particular member? Or even more exotically in the Anima Mundi?<br /> <br /> 3) I've read here why a hallow is a bad idea in a person's Oneiros, but could they exist in the Temenos or Anima Mundi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12468-letalis","name":"Letalis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T19:38:52-08:00","id":1436497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1436482#post1436482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, new questions:<br /> 1) Is it possible to create an astral sanctum? Especially one with as many trappings (eg safe place, ritual casting space, etc.) as possible for a real sanctum such that a cabal could be spread out around the world, but meet up in the astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not really much point to making a <i>Sanctum</i> that does that, given most potential threats are not going to be able to reach it, and you won't be going there bodily, and the Astral is rather thin on sources of Paradox that aren't nigh-omnipresent anyway. The Begotten have their Lairs, but there's no Wending-equivalent state for the soul-world of a dead Beast to get around the problem of tenancy and/or host management.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Would it have to be in the Temenos, or could it be in the Oneiros of a particular member? Or even more exotically in the Anima Mundi? </div> </div> </div>Putting it in the Anima Mundi is a bad idea for many reasons, most prominently the Ecstatic Wind, and putting it in someone's Oneiros is a recipe for mental problems that requires a pretty major extension of trust. Paths and Legacies have realms in the Temenos, so building the cachet necessary to generate a shared space in the dreams of humanity is about as much of a prerequisite as needed to put it in the Temenos, which is the best-fit least-objectionable layer of the Astral to keep a collective meeting place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) I've read here why a hallow is a bad idea in a person's Oneiros, but could they exist in the Temenos or Anima Mundi? </div> </div> </div>Similar problems: Temenos Realms that are host to a Hallow start to disconnect from their surrounding bits of the human unconscious, while Dreamtime locals don't take kindly to the feature and take steps to erase it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T00:00:05-08:00","id":1436516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1436482#post1436482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, new questions:<br /> 1) Is it possible to create an astral sanctum? Especially one with as many trappings (eg safe place, ritual casting space, etc.) as possible for a real sanctum such that a cabal could be spread out around the world, but meet up in the astral. <br /> <br /> 2) Would it have to be in the Temenos, or could it be in the Oneiros of a particular member? Or even more exotically in the Anima Mundi?<br /> <br /> 3) I've read here why a hallow is a bad idea in a person's Oneiros, but could they exist in the Temenos or Anima Mundi?</div> </div> </div> </div>In order for a Mastigos to accomplish what what you want, I reccomend a 3 layered solution:<br /> <br /> 1- Increase the storage space of a portable item to be able to hold a person (coat pocket, wallet, tie pocket, etc)<br /> <br /> 2- Create a Sanctum, ward it heavily, store in a Pocket Dimension, Reach for an Iris and make it lead to an entrance inside an item made in the previous step. Add a Key to make it only accessible to those that were told it was there and do not wish to steal or damage its contents.<br /> <br /> 3- Co-locate the interior of the other items to lead to the entrance made in step 2.<br /> <br /> With that you have a portable Sanctum, free of Paradox, easily accessible for hiding, coordinating logistics and moving the cabal across the globe. It will take a lot of time and Willpower to make it happen, but its an incredibly powerful resource to be able to access on the fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T08:15:57-08:00","id":1436547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Letalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1436482#post1436482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, new questions:<br /> 1) Is it possible to create an astral sanctum? Especially one with as many trappings (eg safe place, ritual casting space, etc.) as possible for a real sanctum such that a cabal could be spread out around the world, but meet up in the astral. <br /> <br /> 2) Would it have to be in the Temenos, or could it be in the Oneiros of a particular member? Or even more exotically in the Anima Mundi?<br /> <br /> 3) I've read here why a hallow is a bad idea in a person's Oneiros, but could they exist in the Temenos or Anima Mundi?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely possible. Results may vary. <br /> <br /> Soul Cage (an actual play run by Dave Brookshaw, <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/mage-the-awakening-the-soul-cage.375715/\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...l-cage.375715/</a>. Warning, if you start reading this thread it will suck you in and not let go) features a custom legacy whose main shtick is a shared Tenemos realm. It\u2019s noted that setting up and maintaining the realm required a fair bit of effort. The legacy\u2019s main attainment is being able to act in the Astral and Physical simultaneously, as well as having a portal directly from their Oneiroi to the shared Realm. <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I have an NPC in my current game who uses his Oneiros as a private sanctum. But he\u2019s a fourth-degree Master of Forces, Mind, Prime, and Space, so he can get away with a lot. And he throws amazing parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T11:04:36-08:00","id":1436561,"title":"","content":"Building on that, the Legacy (called the Parliament of the Needle) and its Attainments can be found here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/mage-the-awakening-the-soul-cage.375715/page-77\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?thre...375715/page-77</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T16:14:10-08:00","id":1436591,"title":"","content":"Is there an established method of making the visions granted by Postcognition visible to more than just the caster? Say, for example, other cabal members want to be able to cast their own Unveiling spells on a past scene? I know this effect should be possible, I\u2019m just not sure what the minimum requirements should be. An extra Reach when casting Postcognition? A Ruling of Time effect (akin to Scrying)?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 02-22-2021, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-22T17:18:01-08:00","id":1436598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1436591#post1436591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an established method of making the visions granted by Postcognition visible to more than just the caster? Say, for example, other cabal members want to be able to cast their own Unveiling spells on a past scene? I know this effect should be possible, I\u2019m just not sure what the minimum requirements should be. An extra Reach when casting Postcognition? A Ruling of Time effect (akin to Scrying)?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should just be additional targets. By default it allows the Mage to view the target's past, but you should be able to up the targets to two to give another subject the ability to view the past, and continue upping it to give more people the ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 02-22-2021, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T03:21:30-08:00","id":1436773,"title":"","content":"So...silly question here. Does anyone know what the line next to each Arcanum is for in the character sheet? What are we supposed to write there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T04:49:48-08:00","id":1436781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1436773#post1436773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...silly question here. Does anyone know what the line next to each Arcanum is for in the character sheet? What are we supposed to write there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what the official use is, but I write &quot;Ruling&quot; or &quot;Inferior&quot; there as a reminder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","name":"Enmai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T04:52:25-08:00","id":1436783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1436773#post1436773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...silly question here. Does anyone know what the line next to each Arcanum is for in the character sheet? What are we supposed to write there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they're for anything specifically; possibly just to make the page look neater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T05:16:22-08:00","id":1436788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1436773#post1436773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...silly question here. Does anyone know what the line next to each Arcanum is for in the character sheet? What are we supposed to write there?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just a leader connecting the names of the Arcana with the fillable dots. It makes the document more readable. You're not intended to write anything there. The fact that you can is just a bonus, so you could fill in stuff like Ruling/Inferior/Path if you'd like. Same thing for Skills; the leaders are primarily there for readability since many Skills don't leave enough space for proper notes, but you could use those lines to note Specialties if you'd like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T10:02:27-08:00","id":1436828,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks, everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T10:45:08-08:00","id":1437651,"title":"","content":"A couple less common use-scenarios for Goetic Summons:<br /> <br /> 1) The Reach options allow summoning of Goetia from the Astral if the Mage is \u201cin a place from which she could meditate into the Astral\u201d. Should the Astral Adept Merit then basically allow a Mage to summon Goetia from anywhere?<br /> <br /> 2) Being already present in the Astral should abrogate the need to be able to mediate in, yes? So if already in an Astral layer, do the Reach costs of summoning Goetia adjust proportionally? E.g. if in the Tenemos, summoning something from your Oneiros still costs 1 Reach, the Tenemos wouldn\u2019t cost Reach, and the Animus Mundi also costs 1?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 03-02-2021, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T10:59:41-08:00","id":1437655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1437651#post1437651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple less common use-scenarios for Goetic Summons:<br /> <br /> 1) The Reach options allow summoning of Goetia from the Astral if the Mage is \u201cin a place from which she could meditate into the Astral\u201d. Should the Astral Adept Merit then basically allow a Mage to summon Goetia from anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be the interaction, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Being already present in the Astral should abrogate the need to be able to mediate in, yes? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if already in an Astral layer, do the Reach costs of summoning Goetia adjust proportionally? E.g. if in the Tenemos, summoning something from your Oneiros still costs 1 Reach, the Tenemos wouldn\u2019t cost Reach, and the Animus Mundi also costs 1? </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's any rules for this in the book, but it would make sense to adjust the Reach requirements based on your &quot;location&quot; within the Astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T11:07:25-08:00","id":1437657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1437651#post1437651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple less common use-scenarios for Goetic Summons:<br /> <br /> 1) The Reach options allow summoning of Goetia from the Astral if the Mage is \u201cin a place from which she could meditate into the Astral\u201d. Should the Astral Adept Merit then basically allow a Mage to summon Goetia from anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mage is their own portal to the Astral. A Demesne or Hallow just makes opening that portal possible. If the mage has other means of opening that portal, then those should absolutely count for this spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1437651#post1437651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Being already present in the Astral should abrogate the need to be able to mediate in, yes? So if already in an Astral layer, do the Reach costs of summoning Goetia adjust proportionally? E.g. if in the Tenemos, summoning something from your Oneiros still costs 1 Reach, the Tenemos wouldn\u2019t cost Reach, and the Animus Mundi also costs 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'd still need a +1 Reach to summon Goetia outside your sensory range. So in the Temenos, it should still be a +1 Reach to summon a Goetic entity that is far away or not even in that particular sub-realm. But note that summoning Goetia from someone's Oneiros means you're casting the spell on them (unless it's your own Oneiros) and summon them that way. If you happen to be in the Anima Mundi you'd still only need one Reach to summon from an Oneiros because it's still only one step from the Oneiros to where you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T11:22:38-08:00","id":1437662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1437657#post1437657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you'd still need a +1 Reach to summon Goetia outside your sensory range. So in the Temenos, it should still be a +1 Reach to summon a Goetic entity that is far away or not even in that particular sub-realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the responses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T18:53:47-08:00","id":1437898,"title":"","content":"I've finally gone and bought the Mage Second Edition books, and am just working my way through the core. One thing I'm trying to get my head around is how sympathetic casting works.<br /> <br /> Is it that, no matter the nature of the yantra employed, the mage is casting through their own connection to the subject? Like, you could be using a lock of a person's hair, but if they're barely known to you the connection is only Weak (for the sake of simplicity, let's just assume the sympathetic name is known)? And you can't cast through the connection that another person you have direct access to has to your target (barring a spell to reconnect it, presumably)?<br /> <br /> Does the nature of the sympathetic yantra make any difference to the casting, or is a lock of hair as good as a crude drawing?<br /> <br /> It seems to me that Temporal Sympathy is more straightforward in that you're casting based on the subject's connection to its own past, i.e. having a more difficult time the more it has changed from your target time period, with the casting mage's personal connection being irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T19:05:37-08:00","id":1437900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1437898#post1437898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've finally gone and bought the Mage Second Edition books, and am just working my way through the core. One thing I'm trying to get my head around is how sympathetic casting works.<br /> <br /> Is it that, no matter the nature of the yantra employed, the mage is casting through their own connection to the subject? Like, you could be using a lock of a person's hair, but if they're barely known to you the connection is only Weak (for the sake of simplicity, let's just assume the sympathetic name is known)? And you can't cast through the connection that another person you have direct access to has to your target (barring a spell to reconnect it, presumably)?<br /> <br /> Does the nature of the sympathetic yantra make any difference to the casting, or is a lock of hair as good as a crude drawing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, the object used as a Yantra doesn't matter, the Mage's connection to the subject does.<br /> <br /> However, look at the spell <i>Borrow Threads</i>, this lets the Mage take the connection of a lock of hair or favorite doll or whatever.<br /> <br /> Personally, I shortcut this and use the yantra's connection to the subject, but that's not how the rules work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems to me that Temporal Sympathy is more straightforward in that you're casting based on the subject's connection to its own past, i.e. having a more difficult time the more it has changed from your target time period, with the casting mage's personal connection being irrelevant. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T19:07:27-08:00","id":1437901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1437898#post1437898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it that, no matter the nature of the yantra employed, the mage is casting through their own connection to the subject? Like, you could be using a lock of a person's hair, but if they're barely known to you the connection is only Weak (for the sake of simplicity, let's just assume the sympathetic name is known)? And you can't cast through the connection that another person you have direct access to has to your target (barring a spell to reconnect it, presumably)?<br /> <br /> Does the nature of the sympathetic yantra make any difference to the casting, or is a lock of hair as good as a crude drawing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without the use of Borrow Threads, sympathetic casting uses your own sympathetic connection to the target.<br /> <br /> Material sympathetic Yantras often have an existing sympathetic connection to the target that you can borrow, and while using the Yantra for the Attainment doesn't provide its bonus as a Sympathy Yantra, you can always just use it twice like you'd do for using any other Yantra for multiple categories of bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T19:43:12-08:00","id":1437906,"title":"","content":"Rriight, the convenience of having something to hand to adopt connections from makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1437900#post1437900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I shortcut this and use the yantra's connection to the subject, but that's not how the rules work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of a sensibility to like the idea of a preliminary spell for the process, for the idea that such advantageous casting requires additional prep work and resource allocation.<br /> <br /> That and I recall finding the system where it was up in the air where any given figure's sympathetic connections actually came from was kind of a nightmare. I already prefer the idea that each connection comes from a discrete subject in a unified fashion, and it's on mages to manipulate them. That and folding the link object into the wider concept of yantras.<br /> <br /> It's... cleaner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T23:51:00-08:00","id":1437923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1437898#post1437898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the nature of the sympathetic yantra make any difference to the casting, or is a lock of hair as good as a crude drawing?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not matter. For Sympathetic Range all Sympathetic Yantras are equal since you don't get the bonus. But if you cast using more than one Sympathetic Yantra, you gain the bonus for each additional Yantra.<br /> <br /> One small trick for Sympathetic Range is that you gain a connection to anyone or anything which is a subject to your spells. With planning that can be used quite effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T10:11:06-08:00","id":1437971,"title":"","content":"I presume that the Unmaking spell that sends things back through time refers to people mostly because they're capable of acting within the past. But could you cast a spell on an object before sending it back to change its performance in some key way?<br /> <br /> Although I suppose that Unmaking something's history after the point you send them back to might mean they don't get to take spells or anything else with them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T15:19:26-08:00","id":1438032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1437971#post1437971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume that the Unmaking spell that sends things back through time refers to people mostly because they're capable of acting within the past. But could you cast a spell on an object before sending it back to change its performance in some key way?<br /> <br /> Although I suppose that Unmaking something's history after the point you send them back to might mean they don't get to take spells or anything else with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading is that the rules for time travel are not meant to be completely ignored by sending things that it does no good to keep the camera on back in time instead of participating actors in the historical record, particularly given that Shifting Sands cancels most spells from the intervening period and Corridors of Time specifically has the subject inhabit their past self.<br /> <br /> It helps to remember that spells are discrete objects and Time magic interacts with the past in very particular ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T06:15:56-08:00","id":1438113,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that limitation is due to what Time can do alone, generally adding more Arcana can make up for a limitation. In this case, perhaps a conjunctional Weaving (to make sure the target's properties get sent back) or Patterning (so the object interacts in unusual ways with time) related to the target might address that. One example is that Space 4 could arguably let you move your past self to wherever you cast the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T08:50:07-08:00","id":1438129,"title":"","content":"The question is driven by the idea of sending things with longer histories than human lives back to historically significant times carrying spells that will change the course of history.<br /> <br /> Hard to find an actor old enough to be able to act in the 1910s, but could you send the Resolute Desk back to a moment when Woodrow Wilson was setting at it enchanted to explode, and so cause a major divergence in the 20th Century? Send Abe Lincoln's hat back to influence his mind? Cause the bullet that would kill JFK to melt before it hit him? Sabotage the Wright Brothers plane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T10:31:06-08:00","id":1438137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438129#post1438129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is driven by the idea of sending things with longer histories than human lives back to historically significant times carrying spells that will change the course of history.<br /> <br /> Hard to find an actor old enough to be able to act in the 1910s, but could you send the Resolute Desk back to a moment when Woodrow Wilson was setting at it enchanted to explode, and so cause a major divergence in the 20th Century? Send Abe Lincoln's hat back to influence his mind? Cause the bullet that would kill JFK to melt before it hit him? Sabotage the Wright Brothers plane?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because again, the time travel mechanics are there to be used, not ignored for the sake of black-boxing the entire process of casting spells in the past.<br /> <br /> You can theoretically borrow temporal sympathy from something, given the specific insulation against preventing your own birth and chapter fiction character who had just that occur, but if you want a spell that isn't time travel to happen in the past you go to the past and cast the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T11:18:31-08:00","id":1438146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438137#post1438137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because again, the time travel mechanics are there to be used, not ignored for the sake of black-boxing the entire process of casting spells in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you mean by this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can theoretically borrow temporal sympathy from something, given the specific insulation against preventing your own birth and chapter fiction character who had just that occur</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, what does temporal sympathy have to do with grandfather paradoxes not occurring one way or another?<br /> <br /> Mind, it's funny that they illustrate the principle with the idea of preventing one's own birth when Corridors of Time is pretty explicit that it can't send somebody to earlier than their own lifespan. I guess it matters for storylines that might involve stumbling upon an Iris that leads into a point in the past that would otherwise be inaccessible to a given individual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you want a spell that isn't time travel to happen in the past you go to the past and cast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would seem to be the simple answer to the question of sending very old things back through time as a way of altering events that no living person was around for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T14:43:14-08:00","id":1438174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438146#post1438146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand what you mean by this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The systems for time-travel includes a marker that disappears as soon as the view of events returns to the present, which any spell sending a non-character back in time definitionally does unless your ST follows the subject of any and every instance of time travel that affects the PCs' history in any way.<br /> <br /> Since the book does not propose doing that and the existing means of time travel are limited in the ways that they are, it is reasonable to conclude most applications of time travel with actual consequences are the ones that send an individual the game can follow back in time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, what does temporal sympathy have to do with grandfather paradoxes not occurring one way or another? </div> </div> </div>Borrow your grandfather's connection to the year he met your grandmother and you can prevent your father from being born even though that means you never come to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T16:17:30-08:00","id":1438194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438174#post1438174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The systems for time-travel includes a marker that disappears as soon as the view of events returns to the present, which any spell sending a non-character back in time definitionally does unless your ST follows the subject of any and every instance of time travel that affects the PCs' history in any way.<br /> <br /> Since the book does not propose doing that and the existing means of time travel are limited in the ways that they are, it is reasonable to conclude most applications of time travel with actual consequences are the ones that send an individual the game can follow back in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's going to really depend on your St rather then the book and how much he can deal with the fact that you've made the game an extended one player show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T16:41:26-08:00","id":1438200,"title":"","content":"It depends, if you are willing to take the time to invest in a higher scale factor, you can send the entire cabal on a time heist, which can be pretty awesome. What makes it all the better is that masters of this Arcanum can literally make time for anything.<br /> <br /> If they know Space, this is made easier by utilizing the Everywhere Attainment. If they know Prime, they can make Time travel imbued items. If they are particularly well connected, they can occasionally requisition them or trade one for a boon a crafter owes them.<br /> <br /> Then there are the complications of time travel, such as leaving your signature everywhere, having others believe you, being one dispellation away from undoing your hard work and being wary of other time travelers. It opens up a layer of strategy and hubris that can lead to some amusing tales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:05:19-08:00","id":1438226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438174#post1438174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Borrow your grandfather's connection to the year he met your grandmother and you can prevent your father from being born even though that means you never come to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does not seem to be how Corridors of Time works. That it is not targeting a time period as a destination, you're Unmaking the subject's history following the desired period. Temporal sympathy is needed to go back further than Unchanged time, but it's still modification of their personal timeline.<br /> <br /> The spell specifically lays out that it cannot send a person back to a point in time prior to their own life, that only Imperial magic can do that.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's plausible for there to be magic that kind of merges an older person's lifespan with your own such that you can place yourself back in their life as though it was your own, but... that also sounds beyond Making or Unmaking. Maybe summon a powerful fae to stitch your timelines together, sounds like the kind of thing they'd be into.<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking about casting spells back through time using temporal sympathy, but it seems to me that the only spells that can use that one are those which call it out. Otherwise it's like you see, actual retroactive alterations of the timeline require somebody to go back and do them, not casting spells or sending rigged objects and waiting around for the timeline to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T20:39:00-08:00","id":1438232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438226#post1438226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does not seem to be how Corridors of Time works. That it is not targeting a time period as a destination, you're Unmaking the subject's history following the desired period. Temporal sympathy is needed to go back further than Unchanged time, but it's still modification of their personal timeline.<br /> <br /> The spell specifically lays out that it cannot send a person back to a point in time prior to their own life, that only Imperial magic can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're going to have to wait until Fallen Worlds and/or Tome of the Pentacle come out to get a better answer, because I have little else to offer you on the topic of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970181#post970181\">&quot;there is a published character who specifically prevented their own birth by mistake&quot;</a> that is not simply retreading available forum conversations on Time magic from the last five years that the corebook has been out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose it's plausible for there to be magic that kind of merges an older person's lifespan with your own such that you can place yourself back in their life as though it was your own, but... that also sounds beyond Making or Unmaking. </div> </div> </div>Magic that messes with temporal sympathy has specific considerations equivalent to those for spatial sympathy, spatial sympathy requires you to Borrow a connection to a subject if you don't have one yourself, and temporal sympathy is used when the target of a spell is a past version of something you have access to in the present. Most of the described effects of temporal sympathy are memory-related and the main consequence of returning to a time where you no longer exist is that nobody remembers you.<br /> <br /> It's not beyond Mastery, it's just wildly irresponsible for a spell normally available to mages whose Path impresses upon them the weight of choice and consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T02:54:09-08:00","id":1438283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438232#post1438232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=970181#post970181&amp;quot;]&amp;quot;there</a> is a published character who specifically prevented their own birth by mistake&amp;quot;[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>If he did it when he was an Apprentice, he definitely wasn't doing it under his own power. Given that the description of New York includes both references to weird ley lines that shift things around (apparently most explicitly through space, but maybe not exclusively) and what may be a reference to an archmaster (unless arch-hierarch just refers to somebody presiding over their multiple Consilia), there seem to be several possible explanations for the guy doing that other than the spell that specifically says that it cannot do that.<br /> <br /> And when I made that earlier comment, I did acknowledge that it could be covering the circumstances where a person travels via an inexplicable Iris or the power of a Seeker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not beyond Mastery</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why does Corridors of Time say that it is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T04:39:35-08:00","id":1438290,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's possible to use Temporal Sympathy that way. It's a connection between a subject and its own past that measures how much the two has changed. Borrowing it doesn't make sense because either you borrow both ends, you'll just end up with a connection to your past self. If that past self doesn't exist (because you didn't exist yet) you suddenly have a connection to nothing and that doesn't seem usable. Or you're borrowing only one end, in which case you have a connection to someone else's past and I don't see how you can resolve that in a satisfactory way. Could you use that to affect someone else's past to cast spells on yourself? If you cast Corridors of Time on yourself, would you end up in the body of someone else? Not only does that seem like something you shouldn't be able to do with just Time, it also breaks the explicit limitation of not being able to be sent back in time before your own lifetime.<br /> <br /> A much simpler way to create a grandfather paradox that follows the rules is to just send your grandfather back in time using Corridors of Time to mess up that initial meeting with your grandmother. If he's not prepared to be flung many decades into the past, he's bound to have a major freak out and do something very different than he did in the original timeline. (Just make sure to cast Constant Presence on yourself before you do it unless you want an unnecessarily convoluted and retroactive suicide.)<br /> <br /> The way to prevent the ST from being swamped down with rewriting the timeline of the entire campaign is the simple social contract of don't do unnecessary stuff to create a shit ton of work for your co-players. That and a ton of mages (and higher beings) having a vested interest in not allowing that sort of behaviour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T05:19:38-08:00","id":1438294,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna assume that Dissonance doing the spell in prevents changes from being Lasting in the same way that dispelling it does.<br /> <br /> Also that the present is a bit sturdy against something like a butterfly effect, so there's no sending a person back for three turns and letting a slight deviation have far reaching effects (barring very specific and meaningful instances, like a gunman hesitating long enough to be prevented from shooting somebody).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T10:34:18-08:00","id":1438590,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s your dice pool when Scrutinizing using multiple Arcana? It sure reads a lot like you add the Arcanum ratings together but that would be too easy. Do all the Arcana used have to be relevant to the Mystery (i.e.- capable of revealing information about it other than \u201cSorry, try this Arcanum instead\u201d)?<br /> <br /> Do you spend Mana for extra Scrutiny successes before or after rolling? Two places on the same page contradict each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T16:05:33-08:00","id":1438648,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit unclear on how the Duel Arcane works, could somebody explain it to me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T16:47:50-08:00","id":1438656,"title":"","content":"Looks like you just take turns rolling (Attribute + Arcanum) at each other to open Doors social-maneuver-style until one of you is all the way open and loses, with the wrinkles that if you fail a roll you can\u2019t try that Arcanum on that Door again and you can give up your attack to contest your opponent\u2019s next attack (the point of that presumably being the aforementioned Arcanum lockout).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T17:00:09-08:00","id":1438657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438656#post1438656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like you just take turns rolling (Attribute + Arcanum) at each other to open Doors social-maneuver-style until one of you is all the way open and loses, with the wrinkles that if you fail a roll you can\u2019t try that Arcanum on that Door again and you can give up your attack to contest your opponent\u2019s next attack (the point of that presumably being the aforementioned Arcanum lockout).</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the simple Attack/Defend part system is an easily solved game (i.e. both characters can figure out the optimal strategy and then just hope the dice favours them) it's only the Negotiate move that's actually interesting. Basically, rather than play the game as a straight (and honestly quite boring) duel, you can try to use that move to buy your way to victory by offering favours that the opponent may value more than winning the duel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T01:32:31-08:00","id":1438699,"title":"","content":"It talks about the attacks spending Reach and needing to account for spell factors, what's that about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T03:21:57-08:00","id":1438706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438699#post1438699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It talks about the attacks spending Reach and needing to account for spell factors, what's that about?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird. There is absolutely no need to bother with spell factors unless the &quot;duel&quot; isn't actually a duel. One Reach needs to be spent on instant casting, and if you have more than one dot in your Arcanum I'd recommend spending one Reach on sensory range to avoid having to aim the spell. All other Reach options are completely irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T04:56:34-08:00","id":1438721,"title":"","content":"It seems to me as though Duel Arcane massively favours either the person with more Doors or, if they're both equal, the one who goes first. Being on the defensive about it feels like it can only ever drag the process out; you're forgoing the opportunity to progress towards victory in exchange for the opponent wasting your action with an Arcanum unlikely to work anyway or losing their best and possibly being stuck on one Door for a while. How many steps does it take to get an insurmountable lead? Or I guess in a case such as that you can try defending to stall them down to their worst Arcanum and then batter them to catch up. But that also is just dragging things out.<br /> <br /> It kind of makes me wonder if the optimal strategy is to not just defend with your best dice pool until the opponent has used up all of their Arcana and then just spend the next seven or so rounds breaking them down while refusing their offers and leaving them impotent. I guess that would be a reason for Apprentices to not challenge Masters.<br /> <br /> Although I guess that's a strategy that only needs to slip once, bad luck on your part or good on your opponent's, and you've ceded them the advantage of being one step ahead that they can ride to the end unless you try again to make a Door impregnable. But what if that slips up again and you're two Doors behind? Although, how else can you win if they can afford to lose Doors because a back and forth will get them to the end first?<br /> <br /> I suppose it can help to see it as practically more of an &quot;I know you know I know&quot; kind of battle of wits, although I find myself wondering if this is less character decisions and more gaming the system, and even then the aforementioned options don't quite seem sophisticated.<br /> <br /> I suppose the rewards for victory are valuable enough to encourage wading in occasionally, but I still wish it would have been a bit more elaborate and interesting if it was going to still be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T05:14:05-08:00","id":1438724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438721#post1438721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[..] but I still wish it would have been a bit more elaborate and interesting if it was going to still be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say it's the consensus, but it's definitely a common opinion. I would personally never bother with the Duel Arcane except as a plot point. I.e. two NPCs or a PC in their backstory went into a Duel Arcane and now owes/is owed a favour from the Negotiate move. But it's wholly uninteresting to actually play through, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T05:51:53-08:00","id":1438726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438724#post1438724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't say it's the consensus, but it's definitely a common opinion. I would personally never bother with the Duel Arcane except as a plot point. I.e. two NPCs or a PC in their backstory went into a Duel Arcane and now owes/is owed a favour from the Negotiate move. But it's wholly uninteresting to actually play through, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, personally i houseruled the Duel Arcane as a battle in Mage sight between &quot;platonic forms&quot; unlocked by the Prime spell (a normal battle, but with dream form stats and health level treated as doors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T06:55:10-08:00","id":1438739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438706#post1438706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's weird. There is absolutely no need to bother with spell factors unless the &amp;quot;duel&amp;quot; isn't actually a duel. One Reach needs to be spent on instant casting, and if you have more than one dot in your Arcanum I'd recommend spending one Reach on sensory range to avoid having to aim the spell. All other Reach options are completely irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Range shouldn\u2019t matter either, though scale arguably does if your opponent is Giant, because you\u2019re not actually casting the spells to know if the standard range ones would hit. The Duel Arcane is literally just trash-talking with special effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T14:45:18-08:00","id":1438810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438721#post1438721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me as though Duel Arcane massively favours either the person with more Doors or, if they're both equal, the one who goes first. Being on the defensive about it feels like it can only ever drag the process out; you're forgoing the opportunity to progress towards victory in exchange for the opponent wasting your action with an Arcanum unlikely to work anyway or losing their best and possibly being stuck on one Door for a while. How many steps does it take to get an insurmountable lead? Or I guess in a case such as that you can try defending to stall them down to their worst Arcanum and then batter them to catch up. But that also is just dragging things out.<br /> <br /> It kind of makes me wonder if the optimal strategy is to not just defend with your best dice pool until the opponent has used up all of their Arcana and then just spend the next seven or so rounds breaking them down while refusing their offers and leaving them impotent. I guess that would be a reason for Apprentices to not challenge Masters.<br /> <br /> Although I guess that's a strategy that only needs to slip once, bad luck on your part or good on your opponent's, and you've ceded them the advantage of being one step ahead that they can ride to the end unless you try again to make a Door impregnable. But what if that slips up again and you're two Doors behind? Although, how else can you win if they can afford to lose Doors because a back and forth will get them to the end first?<br /> <br /> I suppose it can help to see it as practically more of an &quot;I know you know I know&quot; kind of battle of wits, although I find myself wondering if this is less character decisions and more gaming the system, and even then the aforementioned options don't quite seem sophisticated.<br /> <br /> I suppose the rewards for victory are valuable enough to encourage wading in occasionally, but I still wish it would have been a bit more elaborate and interesting if it was going to still be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duel Arcane never really made sense to me in 2e simply because in actual play an apprentice with dominate mind can completely annihilate any master who doesn't have an absurd withstand or mind/prime protection. Personally, I prefer the alternate dual arcane that was proposed in one first edition book whether the contestants had to do a series of challenges rather than straight up fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T16:40:12-08:00","id":1438839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438810#post1438810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duel Arcane never really made sense to me in 2e simply because in actual play an apprentice with dominate mind can completely annihilate any master who doesn't have an absurd withstand or mind/prime protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does annihilate mean in this context, murder? Or put the master through some indignity before they're free to wield their practices in the world around you to make having assaulted and humiliated them in such a manner seem like a really bad idea? Or heck, not even use their own magic, just use their standing in mage society to censure you. Hopefully what you made that master do was worth what a number of Seers of the Throne who do have protections against mind control will do to a Pentacle mage that has been left out in the cold.<br /> <br /> Is this an actual play in which people are playing characters who have completely missed every indication that Pentacle society does not run solely on coercion and power play, that casting unsolicited spells on another mage is a severe violation, and that there are maybe several practical reasons to not eliminate or make enemies of the most powerful mages in your Consilium and Caucus?<br /> <br /> After all, the Duel Arcane is specifically laid out as a social convention that allows for conflict resolution without needing to let things go through tit for tat violence and violations that, nevermind what a distraction they would be from personal investigations of Mysteries and the pursuit of Order agendas, nevermind even the vulnerability that would leave against Seers and other opposition, is just... not how functional human societies work. Not even how they try to work. Normal people are wired to treat one another with some degree of respect, at least enough for basic cooperation.<br /> <br /> I would think that in a game about power and hubris it's apparent that many things a character can do are things that they shouldn't do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T16:48:09-08:00","id":1438840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438810#post1438810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duel Arcane never really made sense to me in 2e simply because in actual play an apprentice with dominate mind can completely annihilate any master who doesn't have an absurd withstand or mind/prime protection. Personally, I prefer the alternate dual arcane that was proposed in one first edition book whether the contestants had to do a series of challenges rather than straight up fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>1.) You don't actually apply any spell effects in the Duel Arcane. Which Arcana you have doesn't matter beyond ratings.<br /> <br /> 2.) The Duel Arcane is a comparatively civil conflict resolution decided upon by both parties. Debuffing the opponent before the Duel begins is a surefire way to make sure there's no Duel Arcane for you to attend.<br /> Basically, if your preparations for a duel consists of breaking your opponent's weapon arm, there's no chance in hell the duel will actually commence.<br /> <br /> 3.) You need to be at least a Disciple of Mind in order to affect any stats relevant to the Duel Arcane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T16:49:48-08:00","id":1438842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438839#post1438839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does annihilate mean in this context, murder? Or put the master through some indignity before they're free to wield their practices in the world around you to make having assaulted and humiliated them in such a manner seem like a really bad idea? Or heck, not even use their own magic, just use their standing in mage society to censure you. Hopefully what you made that master do was worth what a number of Seers of the Throne who do have protections against mind control will do to a Pentacle mage that has been left out in the cold.<br /> <br /> Is this an actual play in which people are playing characters who have completely missed every indication that Pentacle society does not run solely on coercion and power play, that casting unsolicited spells on another mage is a severe violation, and that there are maybe several practical reasons to not eliminate or make enemies of the most powerful mages in your Consilium and Caucus?<br /> <br /> After all, the Duel Arcane is specifically laid out as a social convention that allows for conflict resolution without needing to let things go through tit for tat violence and violations that, nevermind what a distraction they would be from personal investigations of Mysteries and the pursuit of Order agendas, nevermind even the vulnerability that would leave against Seers and other opposition, is just... not how functional human societies work. Not even how they try to work. Normal people are wired to treat one another with some degree of respect, at least enough for basic cooperation.<br /> <br /> I would think that in a game about power and hubris it's apparent that many things a character can do are things that they shouldn't do.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that the dual arcane as is, is very silly in this edition. Mages can easily win with a single roll provided they go first and interactions between arcana are limited. The Dual arcana as a way to show off how much more skilled you are then the other person seems very foolish when it's trying show essentially what would theoretically happen to the mages if they fought. My point about an apprentice of mind easily overpowering a master at almost anything but mind or prime is just a symptom of the issue I have with mage though I suppose. As a result, I think the dual arcane as represented in I think the Adamant Arrow book are much more interesting as it provides a challenge rather than what's considered a dual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-09-2021, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T17:27:31-08:00","id":1438850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438842#post1438842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When mages can easily win with a single roll</div> </div> </div> </div>What does win specifically mean here?<br /> <br /> Also, it might be a pretty severe gamble to take that the master doesn't have so much as the one dot of Mind necessary to throw at least six dice at the thing as a counterspell. That's assuming that the Apprentice can even get an audience with the higher ranked mage in the first place.<br /> <br /> By the way, you forgot to add Fate as an Arcanum that provides defences against mind control through spells and Attainment. Three out of five Paths are naturally inclined to resist that kind of magic. Thyrsus might also be able to invoke the help of appropriate spirits.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know, masters still have cabals. They might have members who can recognise and deal with mind controlling magic if they find one of their most prestigious mates subjected to it. They'll definitely have intimate people who will look into and respond to somebody like that dying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dual arcana as a way to show off how much more skilled you are then the other person seems very foolish when it's trying show essentially what would theoretically happen to the mages if they fought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though that should be taken in more strategic terms than strictly one on one tactical. That a Master of Time might employ phantasms to convey the capacity to go back and prevent your parents from ever being born. Your Apprentice sword of &quot;if I push myself to my absolute limit, I could control you for a scene&quot; might look a bit flaccid in comparison.<br /> <br /> Plus, I think this is a case where the strategy of defending for a while would work very well. A relatively new and weak mage probably has few Arcana that roll very small dice pools, which I think can be expected to have a hard time overcoming the 10+ dice of the Master's defence. They render all your attacks non-viable against their first Door, and then leisurely take you apart with representations of all the horrible things they could do to your personal history were it not for polite society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point about an apprentice easily overpowering a master at almost anything but mind or prime is just a symptom of the issue I have with mage though I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>What issue is that, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T17:39:07-08:00","id":1438851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438850#post1438850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does win specifically mean here?<br /> <br /> Also, it might be a pretty severe gamble to take that the master doesn't have so much as the one dot of Mind necessary to throw at least six dice at the thing as a counterspell. That's assuming that the Apprentice can even get an audience with the higher ranked mage in the first place.<br /> <br /> By the way, you forgot to add Fate as an Arcanum that provides defences against mind control through spells and Attainment. Three out of five Paths are naturally inclined to resist that kind of magic. Thyrsus might also be able to invoke the help of appropriate spirits.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know, masters still have cabals. They might have members who can recognise and deal with mind controlling magic if they find one of their most prestigious mates subjected to it. They'll definitely have intimate people who will look into and respond to somebody like that dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember there being a defense other than them casting a curse on the opposing mage. I'm not saying that there wouldn't be consequences just that it's not hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel as though that should be taken in more strategic terms than strictly one on one tactical. That a Master of Time might employ phantasms to convey the capacity to go back and prevent your parents from ever being born. Your Apprentice sword of &quot;if I push myself to my absolute limit, I could control you for a scene&quot; might look a bit flaccid in comparison.<br /> <br /> Plus, I think this is a case where the strategy of defending for a while would work very well. A relatively new and weak mage probably has few Arcana that roll very small dice pools, which I think can be expected to have a hard time overcoming the 10+ dice of the Master's defence. They render all your attacks non-viable against their first Door, and then leisurely take you apart with representations of all the horrible things they could do to your personal history were it not for polite society. </div> </div> </div>They don't really have to with a rote of their own and they also have their own defenses. I just think it's poor representation of what's happening because like I said magic has a hard time dealing with other types of magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> What issue is that, exactly? </div> </div> </div>Well it's just that mages can't really defend against other magic then their own and that most magic is set up in way where the only response is to not get hit with it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-09-2021, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T20:00:24-08:00","id":1438874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438851#post1438851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember there being a defense other than them casting a curse on the opposing mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate Shielding can protect a subject from attempts to command their destiny which includes mind control, and Adepts of Fate are innately resistant to such powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that there wouldn't be consequences just that it's not hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I regard this as a false dichotomy; a thing is hard if there are significant incentives not to do it.<br /> <br /> Mind, ease is irrelevant if most people can be expected to not do a thing. Breaking into a house is not hard, but it is uncommon because most are not motivated to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't really have to with a rote of their own and they also have their own defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really ought to quote more precisely, because I can't tell what this is addressing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think it's poor representation of what's happening because like I said magic has a hard time dealing with other types of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this not just incorrect but to be detaching the Duel Arcane from its stated social function. If the important thing is conflict resolution without needing to tear the Consilium apart, then it doesn't really matter if one could composes an elaborate thesis on how they could totally take you, actually. They make a flex empowered by a Weaving of Prime (an Arcanum concerned with representations of raw truth) under a social contract that the issue is closed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it's just that mages can't really defend against other magic then their own and that most magic is set up in way where the only response is to not get hit with it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that not fitting to a game where the primary function of magic is in the acquisition of information? They're mostly here to uncover Mysteries, not suborn the world to their will, let alone frequently get into death matches with other mages (and where mages do conduct war, the necessities of their low population density alone would incline towards one based on traps and ambushes and killing quick and clean). It's a game of sorcery hiding in the modern world, after all.<br /> <br /> Besides, I don't think it's a bad thing for the Arcana, and by extension mages, to be interdependent on one another. If you cannot Shield yourself, have a cabal mate do it. Or go to a neighbour who owes you a boon. Acquire a magical item. Heck, summon something from the Supernal that might provide a useful power.<br /> <br /> Mages aren't individuals, they're part of a larger world that is worth investing in to expand the breadth of their already considerable options.<br /> <br /> When that's fulfilled coherently, I don't see any reasonable basis for being critical of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T20:16:41-08:00","id":1438877,"title":"","content":"How are people inclined to handle improvised casting of spells that might be regarded as more esoteric or non-intuitive?<br /> <br /> For example, let's say the Stone Scribe spells for Final Names are still a thing, under either Fate or Death. They're a bit unusual as either Arcanum goes. Would people portray that as the sort of thing where any mage with the right Practices would repeat them with a snap, or the sort of thing where a bit of explanation is needed in character to help wrap one's head around the casting (not taking a form of spending experience or anything)? Perhaps even scrutinising the spell with Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Or how about total improvised casting? Would you go along with a character being all &quot;yeah, I can totally make a record of a person's final Pattern and sympathetic connections inscribed in written form&quot; independently, or want them to at least encounter a Mystery that introduces the concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T20:36:06-08:00","id":1438881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438877#post1438877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are people inclined to handle improvised casting of spells that might be regarded as more esoteric or non-intuitive?</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote myself from a Discord discussion two years back, it's probably prudent to operate under the assumption that supernatural power development needs some kernel of experiential focus rather than simple imagination and smushing concepts together.<br /> <br /> Mage is a game where gnostic insight and initiation into the Mysteries is the basis for your magic working and the vast majority of experienced mages can be expected to have permanently altered the shape of their soul-vessels to better harmonize with one specialized view of magic or another \u2014 research and/or comprehensive Scrutiny would be the bare minimum I'd expect for a mage to reasonably start considering throwing together a spell to handle a weird phenomenon they had no exposure to a week ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T21:03:45-08:00","id":1438883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438874#post1438874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find this not just incorrect but to be detaching the Duel Arcane from its stated social function. If the important thing is conflict resolution without needing to tear the Consilium apart, then it doesn't really matter if one could composes an elaborate thesis on how they could totally take you, actually. They make a flex empowered by a Weaving of Prime (an Arcanum concerned with representations of raw truth) under a social contract that the issue is closed.</div> </div> </div> </div> A lot of spells early on can just cleanly end a confrontation when there's no opposing defense against it. It's more about smart planning and casting that can end a fight. Yes, someone with fate 4 has a chance of prevent psychic domination but even a master with multiple arcana and experience doesn't mean they'll have it or even a majority of arcana. I guess I just find it silly because it's not remotely how an actual fight would go or even matter. It just favors the person who has more dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is that not fitting to a game where the primary function of magic is in the acquisition of information? They're mostly here to uncover Mysteries, not suborn the world to their will, let alone frequently get into death matches with other mages (and where mages do conduct war, the necessities of their low population density alone would incline towards one based on traps and ambushes and killing quick and clean). It's a game of sorcery hiding in the modern world, after all.<br /> <br /> Besides, I don't think it's a bad thing for the Arcana, and by extension mages, to be interdependent on one another. If you cannot Shield yourself, have a cabal mate do it. Or go to a neighbour who owes you a boon. Acquire a magical item. Heck, summon something from the Supernal that might provide a useful power.<br /> <br /> Mages aren't individuals, they're part of a larger world that is worth investing in to expand the breadth of their already considerable options.<br /> <br /> When that's fulfilled coherently, I don't see any reasonable basis for being critical of it. </div> </div> </div>Since we're devolving from your point, I think I'll not respond to this. I understand your point but I do disagree I just don't want to get into this right before I'm going to bed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-10-2021, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T21:07:58-08:00","id":1438884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438874#post1438874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then it doesn't really matter if one could composes an elaborate thesis on how they could totally take you, actually</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that\u2019s exactly what you\u2019re doing in a Duel Arcane. That you have to do it half a dozen times before your opponent admits defeat is, if anything, precisely because the rational response to a generic verbal statement of \u201cIf I wanted it you\u2019d be dead\u201d is \u201cYeah, so? Anyone in the consilium could say that about anyone else, you\u2019re not special.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T21:08:29-08:00","id":1438885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438877#post1438877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are people inclined to handle improvised casting of spells that might be regarded as more esoteric or non-intuitive?<br /> <br /> For example, let's say the Stone Scribe spells for Final Names are still a thing, under either Fate or Death. They're a bit unusual as either Arcanum goes. Would people portray that as the sort of thing where any mage with the right Practices would repeat them with a snap, or the sort of thing where a bit of explanation is needed in character to help wrap one's head around the casting (not taking a form of spending experience or anything)? Perhaps even scrutinising the spell with Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Or how about total improvised casting? Would you go along with a character being all &quot;yeah, I can totally make a record of a person's final Pattern and sympathetic connections inscribed in written form&quot; independently, or want them to at least encounter a Mystery that introduces the concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would depend on the person an how they view magic. No two people are the same after all. Personally, I do like the idea of someone organically learning how their magic works rather than looking at all the example spells and just picking the best one. Though, I personally prefer introspection to figure out rather than a concrete Mystery. Analyzing their own pattern analyzing other's patterns and their sympathetic connections. Then analyzing corpses to put 2+2 together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T21:17:49-08:00","id":1438886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438877#post1438877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are people inclined to handle improvised casting of spells that might be regarded as more esoteric or non-intuitive?</div> </div> </div> </div>The corebook and Signs both repeatedly describe how devising new spells is often a nontrivial process, but not once even mention the idea of enforcing that in play, much less discuss how to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T21:32:34-08:00","id":1438888,"title":"","content":"What do people think of the idea that some creative thaumaturgy, particularly for a more unusual or esoteric effect, innately Reaches heavily until the mage works out some of the bugs? Like, the base effect costs Reach the way that additional or deeper ones would in a more conventional or established one. And it takes a bit of experiment and adjustment to figure out a version that emerges most smoothly from the Practice.<br /> <br /> Given the description of Paradox, I'd find that a natural way to represent an imago that doesn't quite know how to fit all the symbols together.<br /> <br /> Although that raises the question of what it would mean to cast such a spell in a demesne or Supernal verge.<br /> <br /> Perhaps such a thing would also restrict yantras. You don't yet know what represents the component symbols of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T15:44:41-08:00","id":1439047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438888#post1438888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do people think of the idea that some creative thaumaturgy, particularly for a more unusual or esoteric effect, innately Reaches heavily until the mage works out some of the bugs? Like, the base effect costs Reach the way that additional or deeper ones would in a more conventional or established one. And it takes a bit of experiment and adjustment to figure out a version that emerges most smoothly from the Practice.<br /> <br /> Given the description of Paradox, I'd find that a natural way to represent an imago that doesn't quite know how to fit all the symbols together.<br /> <br /> Although that raises the question of what it would mean to cast such a spell in a demesne or Supernal verge.<br /> <br /> Perhaps such a thing would also restrict yantras. You don't yet know what represents the component symbols of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that can work but another option would just be to make the spell very basic and crude. A spell that only works against one thing until the mage develops it and refines it. Maybe he can only use the spell on water until he recognizes more properties and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:01:19-08:00","id":1439050,"title":"","content":"Bumping unanswered questions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438590#post1438590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s your dice pool when Scrutinizing using multiple Arcana? It sure reads a lot like you add the Arcanum ratings together but that would be too easy. Do all the Arcana used have to be relevant to the Mystery (i.e.- capable of revealing information about it other than \u201cSorry, try this Arcanum instead\u201d)?<br /> <br /> Do you spend Mana for extra Scrutiny successes before or after rolling? Two places on the same page contradict each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T18:02:37-08:00","id":1439078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439050#post1439050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bumping unanswered questions:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably only use the one that applies then if multiple apply add +1 or 2 dice per applicable arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T22:36:12-08:00","id":1439097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1438590#post1438590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s your dice pool when Scrutinizing using multiple Arcana? It sure reads a lot like you add the Arcanum ratings together but that would be too easy. Do all the Arcana used have to be relevant to the Mystery (i.e.- capable of revealing information about it other than \u201cSorry, try this Arcanum instead\u201d)?<br /> <br /> Do you spend Mana for extra Scrutiny successes before or after rolling? Two places on the same page contradict each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I interpret that line as &quot;Pick the best Arcanum rating&quot;, which is the same as what is used in the duration mentioned in the section covering multiple arcana ratings. I've not noticed any verbiage describing arcana affecting the results at all. It really <i>would</i> make sense to have penalties or bonuses like that, so if they are in there and I keep missing it I'd appreciate a reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T23:10:47-08:00","id":1439098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439050#post1439050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bumping unanswered questions:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that you are paying one Mana for each non ruling arcana added in the Scrutiny, it seems fair to me to use gnosis+best arcana rating<br /> <br /> For the extra successes, i would use it as a &quot;weapon modifier&quot;, so you must declare that you are using &quot;the weapon&quot; before rolling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T04:19:01-08:00","id":1439423,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit unclear on the boundaries of demesnes. Can you cast a spell on a discrete subject within its confines and then carry that thing out? Or is it that you're literally only safe from Paradox within the demesne, and... you can't retroactively apply it, so would you still roll for it on something you could or would take out? Or is it that it would be rolled as appropriate on something the moment it is taken out of the demesne?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T04:42:08-08:00","id":1439424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439423#post1439423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit unclear on the boundaries of demesnes. Can you cast a spell on a discrete subject within its confines and then carry that thing out? Or is it that you're literally only safe from Paradox within the demesne, and... you can't retroactively apply it, so would you still roll for it on something you could or would take out? Or is it that it would be rolled as appropriate on something the moment it is taken out of the demesne?</div> </div> </div> </div>A paradox roll is only done once the spell is finalized. It doesn't apply retroactively. Dissonance could provoke a paradox roll but that's seperate same for ubsafe reliquishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T04:50:04-08:00","id":1439425,"title":"","content":"Just for check: a mage in a legacy, can have only ONE Attainment Legacy for Level, it is? You cannot have 2 &quot;First Level Attainment&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T05:15:06-08:00","id":1439427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439425#post1439425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for check: a mage in a legacy, can have only ONE Attainment Legacy for Level, it is? You cannot have 2 &amp;quot;First Level Attainment&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically you have one main Attainment that is progress mandatory and one that is optional, which is normally based on an Arcana of the parent Path (sometimes combined with the Legacy's Ruling Arcanum).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T07:01:59-08:00","id":1439435,"title":"","content":"Lets say a mage creates a room sized anti-magic bubble centered around a character, probably using an Unmaking of Prime or Making of Death. If they enter a house sized AoE spell, would it affect the entire spell, only the surrounding area or nothing at all due to an insufficient Scale factor ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T07:42:57-08:00","id":1439439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439435#post1439435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say a mage creates a room sized anti-magic bubble centered around a character, probably using an Unmaking of Prime or Making of Death. If they enter a house sized AoE spell, would it affect the entire spell, only the surrounding area or nothing at all due to an insufficient Scale factor ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would only affect the overlap.<br /> AoE spells cover an area, but they don't have Size so Scale doesn't matter. The effect of an AoE spell only works within the AoE, so the first spell can't affect the entirety of the second spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T10:59:09-08:00","id":1439481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439424#post1439424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A paradox roll is only done once the spell is finalized. It doesn't apply retroactively.</div> </div> </div> </div>So then yes, you can cast a spell with as much Reach as you wish without rolling Paradox and then there is no further problem if its subject walks out of the demesne/verge?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dissonance could provoke a paradox roll</div> </div> </div> </div>It can? I can't find a reference to that. Unless you're referring to the triggered Paradox roll from a Sleeper witness.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T15:01:49-08:00","id":1439521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439481#post1439481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So then yes, you can cast a spell with as much Reach as you wish without rolling Paradox and then there is no further problem if its subject walks out of the demesne/verge?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It can? I can't find a reference to that. Unless you're referring to the triggered Paradox roll from a Sleeper witness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically. Yes. Otherise a demsene wouldn't be so appealling. <br /> <br /> Last time I checked an exceptional success on a dissonance roll could cause paradox roll but I might be blurring it with sleeper witnesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T16:22:45-08:00","id":1439532,"title":"","content":"So... Paradox is rolled before casting but sleepers haven\u2019t witnessed obvious magic until the spell is successfully cast. Is that retrocausality I smell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T16:45:55-08:00","id":1439541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439532#post1439532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Paradox is rolled before casting but sleepers haven\u2019t witnessed obvious magic until the spell is successfully cast. Is that retrocausality I smell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox is rolled before casting but factors in sleeper witnesses. It's just because there's no point to rolling a spell if you fail the paradox roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T17:19:08-08:00","id":1439548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439521#post1439521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Basically. Yes. Otherise a demsene wouldn't be so appealling.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, <i>less</i> appealing sure, but when risk of Paradox is tied directly to things that influence spell strength I could honestly still see the value of a spell that was so confined, compared to last Edition. Having it be that you can up factors and increase effect on some kind of bolstering without concern and then walk out into the world with it is just gangbusters.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also really helps that you don't need a damn Master to make the thing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439532#post1439532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Paradox is rolled before casting but sleepers haven\u2019t witnessed obvious magic until the spell is successfully cast. Is that retrocausality I smell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the effect is in the Imago, and I think whether or not it will be obvious is easy enough to suss out before it actually takes place.<br /> <br /> If Paradox is a result of spells warped by Imagos that Reached too far until they become weird and contradictory, I would think of the observation of Sleepers as something that exerts a kind of constant pressure on those Imagos. If the effect described is not one the Sleeper could discern, then its place in the Imago is less delicate and rigid, so it's only the rest of it that might bring the Abyss in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439541#post1439541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just because there's no point to rolling a spell if you fail the paradox roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... there's the chance of getting exceptional successes (greater if a Praxis is used), the possibility of the spell failing and the player being given the option to make it dramatic in exchange for Beats, and really, not bothering to roll a spell that failed to trigger Paradox (which means, what, never rolling a spell that was within Reach?) would seem to bely the value of taking dice penalties to improve the spell's factors. I'd think there would be a natural trade off there, in which one gives careful consideration to whether the Potency, Duration or targeting range of the spell is worth the increased risk of it failing.<br /> <br /> Just, if there's no point in rolling the spell when the Paradox roll fails (or never took place), what's the point of the Yantras?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T17:27:46-08:00","id":1439550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439548#post1439548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, <i>less</i> appealing sure, but when risk of Paradox is tied directly to things that influence spell strength I could honestly still see the value of a spell that was so confined, compared to last Edition. Having it be that you can up factors and increase effect on some kind of bolstering without concern and then walk out into the world with it is just gangbusters.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also really helps that you don't need a damn Master to make the thing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It also means you have something that can if stolen screw you over massively. Soul Stones are really strong. If they're stolen they're an incredible vulnerability. It's also a willpower dot and a wisdom roll to make. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I mean... there's the chance of getting exceptional successes (greater if a Praxis is used), the possibility of the spell failing and the player being given the option to make it dramatic in exchange for Beats, and really, not bothering to roll a spell that failed to trigger Paradox (which means, what, never rolling a spell that was within Reach?) would seem to bely the value of taking dice penalties to improve the spell's factors. I'd think there would be a natural trade off there, in which one gives careful consideration to whether the Potency, Duration or targeting range of the spell is worth the increased risk of it failing.<br /> <br /> I mean, if there's no point in rolling the spell when the Paradox roll fails (or never took place), what's the point of the Yantras? </div> </div> </div>Only path tools reduce paradox the rest increase bonus dice. Also, paradox can undo reach you added to the spell and add their number of successes into a penalty to the spell casting roll so it's not like you can just roll and then apply paradox unless you can to change paradox to reduce <b>successes</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-12-2021, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T18:09:20-08:00","id":1439570,"title":"","content":"Even if you have to roll Paradox when you leave the demesne that\u2019s still only one Paradox no matter how many tries it took to cast the spell instead of a Paradox per attempt with the cumulative bonus for that.<br /> <br /> Question that Epimetheus just made me think of: Who decides what your three favors are, you or the person who wants their soul stone back from you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T18:28:23-08:00","id":1439572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439570#post1439570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you have to roll Paradox when you leave the demesne that\u2019s still only one Paradox no matter how many tries it took to cast the spell instead of a Paradox per attempt with the cumulative bonus for that.<br /> <br /> Question that Epimetheus just made me think of: Who decides what your three favors are, you or the person who wants their soul stone back from you?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was the case you'd suffer every paradox the moment you left the demesne not just one under that situation. Which is why I can't imagine the point of a demesne is just to prolong a paradox roll. it just doesn't make sense with the current rolling rules. <br /> <br /> I believe the the person who has the soul stone gets to dictate the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T19:16:00-08:00","id":1439580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439550#post1439550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also means you have something that can if stolen screw you over massively. Soul Stones are really strong. If they're stolen they're an incredible vulnerability. It's also a willpower dot and a wisdom roll to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but at least these risks are being measured against something more useful and accessible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only path tools reduce paradox the rest increase bonus dice. Also, paradox can undo reach you added to the spell and add their number of successes into a penalty to the spell casting roll so it's not like you can just roll and then apply paradox unless you can to change paradox to reduce <b>successes</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, what did you mean by &quot;there's no point rolling the spell if you fail the Paradox roll&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T21:12:52-08:00","id":1439590,"title":"","content":"Small reminders:<br /> <br /> Demesnes, like Verges, apply their Paradox negation to spells that qualify for their Yantra bonus, which are limited by their semiotics. The artificial nature of a demesne is such that, as with less invested Sancta, its owner is likely to customize their ritual space to be appropriate to the types of magic they use it for, which opportunity cost means cannot be all possible types even before filtering down to the relevant Arcana.<br /> <br /> It is explicitly noted, for good reason, that most spells a demesne benefits are ritually-cast; it is implicit in the ways demesnes' boundaries and applications are described that they are established in Safe Places of sufficient privacy to practice magic without uninvited witnesses. A mage's Sanctum is a place in which one should endeavor not to fight them, because they can more easily marshall their Gnosis to maintain control of multiple spells at once in that space without risking Paradox (demesne or no demesne), but this also means an unexpected confrontation with Sleepers in your Sanctum is more likely to explode or go sideways.<br /> <br /> Demesnes can be subject to Dissonance (and have the hardest Withstand to scale against it) despite having no overt supernatural qualities of their own, and their Paradox negation only does not stop Sleeper witnesses from triggering and worsening the phenomenon \u2014 so it's probably safe to assume being seen casting in a demesne by a Sleeper is what risks Dissonance for a demesne.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1260824-mechanics-of-delayed-paradox?p=1261554#post1261554\">There are no mechanics for retroactively applying Paradox rolls</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T21:47:41-08:00","id":1439592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439580#post1439580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, what did you mean by &quot;there's no point rolling the spell if you fail the Paradox roll&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant that the spell gets affected by paradox. You can't have paradox apply after you roll because of the way the paradox mechanics work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T08:13:37-08:00","id":1439662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439439#post1439439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would only affect the overlap.<br /> AoE spells cover an area, but they don't have Size so Scale doesn't matter. The effect of an AoE spell only works within the AoE, so the first spell can't affect the entirety of the second spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent, then a mage creating a localized Ansho with Death and Prime is doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T19:07:32-07:00","id":1439958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439590#post1439590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is explicitly noted, for good reason, that most spells a demesne benefits are ritually-cast</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes. I'm still at that point where it can take me a few looks at a piece of information for some details to sink in.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm on board with this. I can see several reasons to establish the idea that, in most cases, the features of a demesne that can be harnessed as a Yantra to make a spell Paradox-proof would only align with something cast ritually. I could get ahead of myself with the image of freely casting a bunch of instant spells, but if I reflect on it that would feel like it cheapens the significance of the demesne in character to just a convenient and functional tool rather than a space aligned with the Supernal for the sake of enhancing particular spells. Like, reinforce the idea of needing to immerse oneself in its nature, rather than popping by, casting a few spells, and then leaving.<br /> <br /> Plus the balance concerns, so any attempt to load up on spells can be offset by the potential for their duration to be eaten away by each further spell cast.<br /> <br /> Even with all of those considerations, I would still like these demenses more than the old ones. It's all about the fact that Paradox arises from how much power you wanted out of the spell. Even with all of those other caveats, it just <i>feels</i> more significant to have this space where a spell can have more depth while being safeguarded from the usual risks of that.<br /> <br /> Aaand... the notion that somebody could bring a spell of the demesne's Ruling Arcana in that <i>does</i> cause Paradox feels like it has its own significance. I think there can be a lot of fun to mine from how a demense's owner reacts to a walker of the same Path bringing an Abyssal Environment into their space. The profound outrage to it. And causing a Manifestation is just... I imagine blood feuds have been conducted for less.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T22:04:10-07:00","id":1439975,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been looking around for a thread on this but haven\u2019t found something that\u2019s really what I\u2019m asking.<br /> <br /> What exactly can I do with ectoplasm? Death spells let me produce and shape it at fairly low levels but what is the point of doing that? I suppose I can make some simple tools, but outside of that I\u2019m not really sure of what one could do.<br /> <br /> What are the properties of ectoplasm? Magical or otherwise. Is there any specific reason I would want to build something out of ectoplasm outside of just being caught without other material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T22:10:38-07:00","id":1439976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439975#post1439975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve been looking around for a thread on this but haven\u2019t found something that\u2019s really what I\u2019m asking.<br /> <br /> What exactly can I do with ectoplasm? Death spells let me produce and shape it at fairly low levels but what is the point of doing that? I suppose I can make some simple tools, but outside of that I\u2019m not really sure of what one could do.<br /> <br /> What are the properties of ectoplasm? Magical or otherwise. Is there any specific reason I would want to build something out of ectoplasm outside of just being caught without other material?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ectoplasm and anything it's coating are Open to all ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T15:42:50-07:00","id":1440121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1439976#post1439976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ectoplasm and anything it's coating are Open to all ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also able of being used as a weapon in twilight right? If you shape it into one at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T12:30:20-07:00","id":1440959,"title":"","content":"Should a ring carrying a few contingency stored spells be invisible, it will not trigger the Peripheral Sight at all, correct ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T14:51:05-07:00","id":1440976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1440959#post1440959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a ring carrying a few contingency stored spells be invisible, it will not trigger the Peripheral Sight at all, correct ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. \u201cPeripheral Mage Sight notices only active supernatural effects. Any supernatural attempt at concealment hides the effect from the mage, without a Clash of Wills or any other mechanical effect.\u201c pg. 90.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T10:43:47-07:00","id":1441526,"title":"","content":"Excellent, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T23:58:44-07:00","id":1442147,"title":"","content":"Hi, I have some questions regarding Supernal entities after reading Mage Core Rulebook and Sign of Sorcery. I would like to know if any of following questions has already been answered, thank you for your kind assistance.<br /> <br /> 1.Are Supernal beings able to use Attainments (except for those related to Supernal Summoning and Rotes)? For example, can they utilize Arcana to protect themselves(a.k.a. Mage Armors)? Maybe they can\u2019t use Yantras in spells, but can they cast spells through sympathetic or temporal sympathetic links?<br /> <br /> 2.Do the Bounds (exiled Supernal entities) lose Corpus over time? If they discorporate, will they be taken away by Abyss or reform in their prisons?<br /> <br /> 3.If an Ochemata is no longer governed by Sub-Soul trait and becomes a free-willed individual (as described in &quot;Vital Autonomy&quot;), will it still return to its creator after it discorporate?<br /> <br /> 4.Since Supernal entities might lose Attributes every time they suffer damage, are the points lost permanently or temporarily? Like, after it returns to Supernal Realm, are those trait points still lost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23765-agrelletto","user":"agrelletto","date":".  Correct typo and make questions more clear. 03-31-2021, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23765-agrelletto","name":"agrelletto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T00:09:43-07:00","id":1442149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>agrelletto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442147#post1442147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I have some questions regarding Supernal entities after reading Mage Core Rulebook and Sign of Sorcery. I would like to know if any of following questions has already been answered, thank you for your kind assistance.<br /> <br /> 1.Are Supernal beings able to use Attainments (except for those related to Supernal Summoning and Rotes)? For example, can they utilize Arcana to protect themselves(a.k.a. Mage Armors)? Maybe they can\u2019t use Yantras in spells, but can they cast spells through sympathetic or temporal sympathetic links?<br /> <br /> 2.Do the Bounds (exiled Supernal entities) lose Corpus over time? If they discorporate, will they be taken away by Abyss or reform in their prisons?<br /> <br /> 3.If an Ochemata is no longer governed by Sub-Soul trait, will it still return to its creator after it discorporate?<br /> <br /> 4.Since Supernal entities might lose Attributes every time they suffers damage, are the points lost permanently or temporarily? Like, when it is summoned again, are those trait points still lost?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the 1)<br /> It s not stated anywhere, but it would be silly to me if creatures with such mastery over arcana could not use arcana attainments.<br /> For the symp yantras, they probably use the rules for magic items (no bonus, but usable for the symp casting if i remember it rightly)<br /> <br /> 2)from the core, it seems that they lose only mana and returns in their prisons wnen they drop to 0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 03-31-2021, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T00:38:45-07:00","id":1442232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442149#post1442149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the 1)<br /> It s not stated anywhere, but it would be silly to me if creatures with such mastery over arcana could not use arcana attainments.<br /> For the symp yantras, they probably use the rules for magic items (no bonus, but usable for the symp casting if i remember it rightly)<br /> <br /> 2)from the core, it seems that they lose only mana and returns in their prisons wnen they drop to 0</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for your reply! About the first and second questions<br /> <br /> 1) Does it mean that Supernal entities just use sympathetic links in spells without the requirement of mediums (and thus no bonus from the Sympathy Yantras)?<br /> <br /> 2) So it seems that the magic of prisons not only bind the Bounds to Atlantean temples but also protect them from the constant erosion of Fallen World or Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23765-agrelletto","name":"agrelletto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T02:02:33-07:00","id":1442234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>agrelletto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442232#post1442232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you very much for your reply! About the first and second questions<br /> <br /> 1) Does it mean that Supernal entities just use sympathetic links in spells without the requirement of mediums (and thus no bonus from the Sympathy Yantras)?<br /> <br /> 2) So it seems that the magic of prisons not only bind the Bounds to Atlantean temples but also protect them from the constant erosion of Fallen World or Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that they require a link and a yantra, but the yantra gives no bonuses and only allows the spell to be cast sympathetically","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T06:18:14-07:00","id":1442246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442234#post1442234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that they require a link and a yantra, but the yantra gives no bonuses and only allows the spell to be cast sympathetically</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see.<br /> <br /> Sympathy Yantras are necessary to utilize sympathetic links, while the bonus die of them represents the benefit to the mind work of mages, which is not applicable to Supernal beings as they cast spells in more instinctual way.<br /> <br /> Thanks for answering my questions! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23765-agrelletto","name":"agrelletto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T08:48:35-07:00","id":1442261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>agrelletto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442246#post1442246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I see.<br /> <br /> Sympathy Yantras are necessary to utilize sympathetic links, while the bonus die of them represents the benefit to the mind work of mages, which is not applicable to Supernal beings as they cast spells in more instinctual way.<br /> <br /> Thanks for answering my questions! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Sympathy Yantras only provide bonus dice if used at Sensory or touch range.<br /> <br /> If used at Sympathetic range they provide no die bonus at all, but are necessary for casting the spell.<br /> <br /> The benefit to a good (high Connection) sympathy yantra for Sympathetic Casting is that you can use <i>Borrow Threads</i> to gain the sympathy to the target of the item.<br /> <br /> [edit]See Satchel's clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 04-01-2021, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T09:09:11-07:00","id":1442269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442261#post1442261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> Sympathy Yantras only provide bonus dice if used at Sensory or touch range.<br /> <br /> If used at Sympathetic range they provide no die bonus at all, but are necessary for casting the spell.<br /> <br /> The benefit to a good (high Connection) sympathy yantra for Sympathetic Casting is that you can use <i>Borrow Threads</i> to gain the sympathy to the target of the item.</div> </div> </div> </div>I misread the symapthy yantra part in the rulebook, thank you for pointing out this.<br /> <br /> The benefit of sympathetic links derived from yantras is really useful if the caster doesn't have the link to the target or the link is too weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23765-agrelletto","name":"agrelletto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T09:20:17-07:00","id":1442270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442261#post1442261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathy Yantras only provide bonus dice if used at Sensory or touch range.<br /> <br /> If used at Sympathetic range they provide no die bonus at all, but are necessary for casting the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or rather, you have to use them for both the Attainment and the bonus to apply the bonus to a sympathetic casting, as you would for any other case where you used a Yantra that qualified for multiple bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T09:27:56-07:00","id":1442271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442270#post1442270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or rather, you have to use them for both the Attainment and the bonus to apply the bonus to a sympathetic casting, as you would for any other case where you used a Yantra that qualified for multiple bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, what i meant is that i think that supernal beings can only use those yantras in the first way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T10:59:57-07:00","id":1442285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442270#post1442270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or rather, you have to use them for both the Attainment and the bonus to apply the bonus to a sympathetic casting, as you would for any other case where you used a Yantra that qualified for multiple bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're correct, I remembered the wording incorrectly, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T17:31:01-07:00","id":1442564,"title":"","content":"Two questions: <br /> <br /> 1- Is there a limit to how much Reach a Mage can try, even with paradoxes? <br /> <br /> 2- Is a Demesne still Paradox-free? If so, how does reach work (if without a limit)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T18:11:13-07:00","id":1442565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442564#post1442564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions:<br /> <br /> 1- Is there a limit to how much Reach a Mage can try, even with paradoxes?<br /> <br /> 2- Is a Demesne still Paradox-free? If so, how does reach work (if without a limit)?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No<br /> 2) Demesne's are only paradox free inside themselves. If you target an area larger then it or outside of it, it's still subject to paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T18:26:09-07:00","id":1442566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442564#post1442564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- Is a Demesne still Paradox-free? If so, how does reach work (if without a limit)?</div> </div> </div> </div>One can apply as many Reach effects as desired and that the spell can accommodate, and no Paradox is rolled for it (within the spatial limits of the demesne).<br /> <br /> As I was reminded of with my own questions earlier, the design of a given demesne does not necessarily render it a valid Yantra for every kind of spell within the appropriate Arcana, and it needs to be a Yantra to insulate from Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T20:48:07-07:00","id":1442577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442565#post1442565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) No<br /> 2) Demesne's are only paradox free inside themselves. If you target an area larger then it or outside of it, it's still subject to paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442566#post1442566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One can apply as many Reach effects as desired and that the spell can accommodate, and no Paradox is rolled for it (within the spatial limits of the demesne).<br /> <br /> As I was reminded of with my own questions earlier, the design of a given demesne does not necessarily render it a valid Yantra for every kind of spell within the appropriate Arcana, and it needs to be a Yantra to insulate from Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, guys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T23:59:29-07:00","id":1442589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442566#post1442566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One can apply as many Reach effects as desired and that the spell can accommodate, and no Paradox is rolled for it (within the spatial limits of the demesne).<br /> <br /> As I was reminded of with my own questions earlier, the design of a given demesne does not necessarily render it a valid Yantra for every kind of spell within the appropriate Arcana, and it needs to be a Yantra to insulate from Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, things like a sleeper witness can still cause paradoxes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T08:56:53-07:00","id":1442613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442589#post1442589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But, things like a sleeper witness can still cause paradoxes</div> </div> </div> </div>Can they? I haven't read it in a while but I thought the rules said that they only cause disbelief on the demesne which can shut it off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T09:05:12-07:00","id":1442614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442613#post1442613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can they? I haven't read it in a while but I thought the rules said that they only cause disbelief on the demesne which can shut it off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sleepers are specifically described as causing Paradox in Verges and Demesnes. Sleepers also causing Dissonance against Demesnes (as long as they see obvious magic within it) is a separate rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442566#post1442566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One can apply as many Reach effects as desired and that the spell can accommodate, and no Paradox is rolled for it (within the spatial limits of the demesne).<br /> <br /> As I was reminded of with my own questions earlier, the design of a given demesne does not necessarily render it a valid Yantra for every kind of spell within the appropriate Arcana, and it needs to be a Yantra to insulate from Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that a spell only needs to <i>qualify</i> for the Yantra bonus to gain the Paradox free advantage. You don't actually need to use the Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T14:05:18-07:00","id":1442637,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Paradox, mages can extend the casting time of an Instant spell to allow them to progressively spend their per turn limit in Mana as necessary for the spell's costs. Does this also work for applying Mana to reduce the Paradox dice pool; can you add a few extra turns to spend the Mana that will whittle it down? Or does your last turn spent casting the spell only afford whatever Mana is left over in you limit and then the dice need to be rolled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T14:08:52-07:00","id":1442638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442637#post1442637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Paradox, mages can extend the casting time of an Instant spell to allow them to progressively spend their per turn limit in Mana as necessary for the spell's costs. Does this also work for applying Mana to reduce the Paradox dice pool; can you add a few extra turns to spend the Mana that will whittle it down? Or does your last turn spent casting the spell only afford whatever Mana is left over in you limit and then the dice need to be rolled?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't spend (or haven't spent) enough Mana during the turns you've used for applying Yantras, you can extend the casting time. No reason for Mana spent towards mitigating Paradox to be an exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T14:09:27-07:00","id":1442639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442637#post1442637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Paradox, mages can extend the casting time of an Instant spell to allow them to progressively spend their per turn limit in Mana as necessary for the spell's costs. Does this also work for applying Mana to reduce the Paradox dice pool; can you add a few extra turns to spend the Mana that will whittle it down? Or does your last turn spent casting the spell only afford whatever Mana is left over in you limit and then the dice need to be rolled?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mages attempting a feat that requires Mana above their Gnosis-derived spending limits may take as many Turns as needed before the action to spend the required Mana. If they are interrupted or change their minds part-way through, Mana spent is still lost.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T17:55:00-07:00","id":1442659,"title":"","content":"I find the wording of &quot;attempting a feat&quot; to be a tad ambiguous, is all. The more restrained part of me leans towards reading it as referring to the deliberate undertaking of the mage, which Paradox is not. The more forgiving side would conceive of the feat in question as being the deliberate act of mitigating the Paradox.<br /> <br /> I'd be satisfied to go along with the apparent consensus. Or at least the first few people who said so.<br /> <br /> Besides, I'm kind of inclined towards anything that makes instant casting need to take longer. The mage is readying this Life-Force Assault that will definitely kill the werewolf in one go without even the benefit of Defence, but it's going to take a few seconds more to line up all the Yantras and smooth out the Reaching imago. Gives time for complications to intrude.<br /> <br /> I want to say that a spell being cast at sensory range is disrupted if the mage loses track of the target; you've spent four turns prepping this thing, only for the werewolf to duck behind a wall and quiet down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-04T18:07:59-07:00","id":1442663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442659#post1442659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the wording of &amp;quot;attempting a feat&amp;quot; to be a tad ambiguous, is all. The more restrained part of me leans towards reading it as referring to the deliberate undertaking of the mage, which Paradox is not. The more forgiving side would conceive of the feat in question as being the deliberate act of mitigating the Paradox.<br /> <br /> I'd be satisfied to go along with the apparent consensus. Or at least the first few people who said so.<br /> <br /> Besides, I'm kind of inclined towards anything that makes instant casting need to take longer. The mage is readying this Life-Force Assault that will definitely kill the werewolf in one go without even the benefit of Defence, but it's going to take a few seconds more to line up all the Yantras and smooth out the Reaching imago. Gives time for complications to intrude.<br /> <br /> I want to say that a spell being cast at sensory range is disrupted if the mage loses track of the target; you've spent four turns prepping this thing, only for the werewolf to duck behind a wall and quiet down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would allow to spend extra turns for reducing paradox with mana.<br /> I think that if you can spend extra turns to incorporate a yantra dice bonus, there is no reason to ban extra turns removing a malus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T01:52:11-07:00","id":1442694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442663#post1442663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if you can spend extra turns to incorporate a yantra dice bonus, there is no reason to ban extra turns removing a malus</div> </div> </div> </div>Removing a what now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T03:06:46-07:00","id":1442698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1442694#post1442694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Removing a what now?</div> </div> </div> </div>A penalty i mean","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T09:12:19-07:00","id":1443266,"title":"","content":"1) Could a general intelligence ai be made from forces only? <br /> 1.5) could it be made from a forces version of shaping and craftsman\u2019s eye?<br /> 2) Would a spell that weaved the property \u201ccan spawn spirits\u201d of resonance into a nimbus be entirely prime, or would it need some spirit?<br /> 2.5) How horrifically bad of an idea is it to do to yourself?<br /> 3) what minimum practice would needed to make a nimbus knot?<br /> 4) can a prime spell lower the amount of mana needed for pattern restoration? Or increase the amount you get from pattern scouring?<br /> 5) can a prime spell allow you to pattern restore someone else?<br /> 6) can platonic form make a space suit?<br /> 7) could death shielding protect you from hard vacuum?<br /> 8) can death stop you from the need to breathe?<br /> 9) does the void of space register to death mage sight?<br /> 10) could a prime perfecting give you the rote quality on rolls using the nimbus tilt?<br /> 11) could prime weaving make a node with the properties of the nimbus?<br /> 12) can the effects of being aligned with a node be bestowed on a nimbus using just prime, or would it be their respective arcanum?<br /> 13) can a life/ mind spell physically transport you to your oneiros?<br /> 13.5) can you use a life/mind spell to make your astral projection physical and project to the fallen world?<br /> 14) how bad of an idea is it to reverse gravity on myself with the right timing so I can fall to the moon.<br /> 14.5) if I never enter the shadow, how likely is it that I get attacked by void spirits while on the moon?<br /> 15) what practices would I need to include physical stats into the calculation of my dream form stats?<br /> 16) is there a spirit of the galaxy?<br /> 16.5) how could a mage communicate with it?<br /> 17) can a weaving of life and forces make somebody travel at light speed? <br /> 18) can a prime patterning turn a node into a hallow?<br /> 19) can a nimbus be turned into mana?<br /> 20) is a eidolon with true mind, not a goetia possible?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T10:03:09-07:00","id":1443271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443266#post1443266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Could a general intelligence ai be made from forces only?<br /> 1.5) could it be made from a forces version of shaping and craftsman\u2019s eye?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean by &quot;Artificial Intelligence&quot;. Forces could be used to create a complex computer program that was at the bleeding edge of sophistication and then enhance the capabilities of the hardware to support the processing required, but it wouldn't be a &quot;true&quot; intelligence like what could be created with Mind, it would still be a computer program.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Would a spell that weaved the property \u201ccan spawn spirits\u201d of resonance into a nimbus be entirely prime, or would it need some spirit?<br /> 2.5) How horrifically bad of an idea is it to do to yourself? </div> </div> </div>All sources of Essence eventually spawn spirits (or, rather, the Essence coalesces into a Spirit if it's not consumed by another Spirit, Essence is basically Rank NULL Spirits).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) what minimum practice would needed to make a nimbus knot? </div> </div> </div>I don't know what this means, but minor alterations to the Nimbus are generally going to be Prime Weaving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) can a prime spell lower the amount of mana needed for pattern restoration? Or increase the amount you get from pattern scouring? </div> </div> </div>Probably Prime Perfecting. Something like: &quot;Duration Primary, Cost: 1 Mana, for the Duration Pattern Restoration costs 1 Mana less and Scouring grants 1 additional Mana. +1 Reach: the reduction/increase is 2 Mana.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the Life 2 Attainment &quot;Improved Pattern Restoration&quot; accomplishes the former.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) can a prime spell allow you to pattern restore someone else? </div> </div> </div>Prime 3 Weaving if they're a Mage or Prime 4 Patterning if they're not, would be my guess for the Practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) can platonic form make a space suit? </div> </div> </div>Yes, with the +2 Reach option to allow for a complex device.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7) could death shielding protect you from hard vacuum? </div> </div> </div>No, Death shielding cannot shield you from the abstract concept of death.<br /> <br /> Forces shielding can, and Time Shielding can prevent you from asphyxiating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8) can death stop you from the need to breathe? </div> </div> </div>Yes, via <i>Shadow Flesh</i> or moving into Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9) does the void of space register to death mage sight? </div> </div> </div>How do you mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10) could a prime perfecting give you the rote quality on rolls using the nimbus tilt? </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it would cost a Mana for the spell and would have Potency &quot;charges.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 11) could prime weaving make a node with the properties of the nimbus? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 12) can the effects of being aligned with a node be bestowed on a nimbus using just prime, or would it be their respective arcanum? </div> </div> </div>Would <i>not</i> require the respective Arcanum, but it wouldn't be useful to grant a Nimbus Node properties, since the Nimbus would have to be stationary to glean any benefit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 13) can a life/ mind spell physically transport you to your oneiros? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure, but probably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 13.5) can you use a life/mind spell to make your astral projection physical and project to the fallen world? </div> </div> </div>Yes, you can create a new body and control it remotely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 14) how bad of an idea is it to reverse gravity on myself with the right timing so I can fall to the moon. </div> </div> </div>Make sure you're prepared to survive the trip and the destination!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 14.5) if I never enter the shadow, how likely is it that I get attacked by void spirits while on the moon? </div> </div> </div>They're more likely to hitch a ride than attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 15) what practices would I need to include physical stats into the calculation of my dream form stats? </div> </div> </div>You could use Mind/Life Weaving to let you choose between the highest of Mental, Social, <i>or</i> Physical Attributes for Power/Finesse/Resistance, but you couldn't just add you Physical Attributes to your Dream Form (I guess you <i>could</i> but it'd be easier to just boost your Dream Form Attributes directly).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 16) is there a spirit of the galaxy? </div> </div> </div>Probably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 16.5) how could a mage communicate with it? </div> </div> </div>By traversing the Sidereal Wastes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 17) can a weaving of life and forces make somebody travel at light speed? </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I'd recommend adding a Conditional Duration of &quot;when I would be absorbed&quot; so that you don't end up dead.<br /> <br /> Also, don't miss your target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 18) can a prime patterning turn a node into a hallow? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 19) can a nimbus be turned into mana? </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the Mana would &quot;go away&quot; after the Duration of the spell ended, so use it first!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 20) is a eidolon with true mind, not a goetia possible? </div> </div> </div>That's what the Mind 5 conjunctional for the spell does, it doesn't create a Goetia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 04-09-2021, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T10:30:31-07:00","id":1443276,"title":"","content":"If an entire galaxy has a spirit in the Shadow, then it's probably Rank 10, which by all description places it in a category of almost impossible to verify even for an archmaster and so distantly removed from our frame of reference that mutual communication is basically impossible.<br /> <br /> Like, a spirit of the planet Earth is in the area of &quot;largely theoretical and probably incomprehensible and uncomprehending&quot;, something notably bigger than that is likely way out of the realms of practically all beings of lesser power.<br /> <br /> Besides, Luna does not really like the idea of things coming down from the spirit world beyond the boundaries of the Earth, and Helios doesn't like them rising away from it.<br /> <br /> As for the Astral, travel into the psychic reflections of the universe beyond the Solar System is technically possible, but severely impractical owing to the thousands of years of subjective time it is likely to take and the constant bombardment with the Ecstatic Wind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T11:23:27-07:00","id":1443281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443266#post1443266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">13) can a life/ mind spell physically transport you to your oneiros?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically, you\u2019d use Space 4 + Mind 2 to physically transport yourself into the Astral. But, after giving it some thought, I think you can pull this off with Life 4 and Mind 4: <br /> Step 1: Convert your body to astral-ephemera with a Life/Mind Patterning effect. <br /> Step 2: Use Mind Perfecting to reverse-summon your newly ephemeral body into your Oneiros. <br /> Step 3: End the spell from step 1, and ta-dah you are now physically inside your Oneiros.<br /> Step 4: When you are ready to leave, end the spell from step 2. <br /> <br /> The limitation of this approach (aside from needing Mind 4) is that the reverse-summoning spell would be duration limited. You could theoretically use Mind Patterning as a sort of teleportation that wouldn\u2019t run out of duration, but then you\u2019d be stuck in your oneiros. You couldn\u2019t reverse-summon yourself out, because you\u2019d no longer have any kind of anchor to summon yourself from. However, adding Space 2 would fix this, since you could cast the reverse-summoning spell with Sympathy. (You wouldn\u2019t need Sympathy to pull yourself into your Oneiros, just like you don\u2019t need it to summon things out of it, because you carry your oneiros within yourself. But once inside the astral, you\u2019d have no way of targeting anywhere in the physical world without Sympathy). <br /> <br /> Short version: yes, an sufficiently clever Life 4/Mind 4 spell (probably costing a reach above normal to get you into your oneiros) will let you bodily enter the astral, but when the spell\u2019s duration runs out, you\u2019ll be kicked back to where you entered. (A persistent version of this spell could exist, but would be inadvisable unless you have the necessary Space to get back out.)<br /> <br /> Edit: oh, also this spell would only bring your body, no clothing or equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 04-09-2021, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T11:59:30-07:00","id":1443288,"title":"","content":"Unrelated question: the core book states &quot;Supernal beings follow the same rules as the Awakened for using their Arcana, paying Mana as appropriate&quot;. So obviously supernal entities pay Mana for spells that explicitly require it, but what about spells that don't? Supernals don't use Rotes or Praxis, so theoretically any spell they cast is &quot;Improvised&quot;. However, they also don't have a distinction between Primary, Common, and Inferior Arcana, so do said Improvised spells cost Mana, or not?<br /> <br /> I lean towards &quot;not&quot;: since they're Made of Magic, it seems safe to assume that any Arcana they possess could be considered effectively &quot;Ruling&quot;. But what say ye?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T12:32:01-07:00","id":1443291,"title":"","content":"thank you both for responding!<br /> I had typed a exhaustive and quoted response to the answers, but I think I might have accidently deleted it when I tried to quote Isator Levi. Is there any way to avoid that in the future?<br /> <br /> proindrakenzol<br /> 1) I meant a ai that would register to mind sight, like a animal created by life making. That would seem to be a thing, as otherwise you would have to puppeteer the creature.<br /> <br /> 2) I am trying to create spirits of a mage's nimbus from a resonance of that mages nimbus. 10, 11,and 12, were to make a place of power that said nimbus spirits can feed from. If I understand right, the nimbus weaved node should spread the nimbus resonance to other node via lay lines.<br /> <br /> 3) nimbus knots are described on pages 92-93 of signs of sorcery. They are formed when a mage dies while casting a spell. They contain memories, but seem to be a prime only effect.<br /> 7,8,9) this was practice of my knowledge of the arcanum. Void seems to be under the purview of Death. Death is absence, and vacuum is the absence of matter. Corpses don't need to breathe, so I wondered if Death could shield your from breathing.<br /> <br /> 13, 15) Now I can make a Bloodborne inspired legacy!<br /> <br /> 14.5) Would they just follow me in twilight or would they use manifestations?<br /> <br /> 20) I reread the spell Psychic Genesis as it is the one referenced by golem and other spells. When it says &quot;gains traits as a rank 1 Goetia&quot; that dosn't mean it makes a Goetia?<br /> <br /> Isator Levi<br /> So theoretically it's possible, but damaging to mind and soul to try, especially if you use knowing spells or mage sight to just download the information into yourself. Sounds like a fun rapt motivation to me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T12:40:11-07:00","id":1443292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443281#post1443281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Typically, you\u2019d use Space 4 + Mind 2 to physically transport yourself into the Astral. But, after giving it some thought, I think you can pull this off with Life 4 and Mind 4:<br /> Step 1: Convert your body to astral-ephemera with a Life/Mind Patterning effect.<br /> Step 2: Use Mind Perfecting to reverse-summon your newly ephemeral body into your Oneiros.<br /> Step 3: End the spell from step 1, and ta-dah you are now physically inside your Oneiros.<br /> Step 4: When you are ready to leave, end the spell from step 2.<br /> <br /> The limitation of this approach (aside from needing Mind 4) is that the reverse-summoning spell would be duration limited. You could theoretically use Mind Patterning as a sort of teleportation that wouldn\u2019t run out of duration, but then you\u2019d be stuck in your oneiros. You couldn\u2019t reverse-summon yourself out, because you\u2019d no longer have any kind of anchor to summon yourself from. However, adding Space 2 would fix this, since you could cast the reverse-summoning spell with Sympathy. (You wouldn\u2019t need Sympathy to pull yourself into your Oneiros, just like you don\u2019t need it to summon things out of it, because you carry your oneiros within yourself. But once inside the astral, you\u2019d have no way of targeting anywhere in the physical world without Sympathy).<br /> <br /> Short version: yes, an sufficiently clever Life 4/Mind 4 spell (probably costing a reach above normal to get you into your oneiros) will let you bodily enter the astral, but when the spell\u2019s duration runs out, you\u2019ll be kicked back to where you entered. (A persistent version of this spell could exist, but would be inadvisable unless you have the necessary Space to get back out.)<br /> <br /> Edit: oh, also this spell would only bring your body, no clothing or equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for answering! This would probably put a hamper on a legacies devoted to the idea of merging your astral and physical form. I will work on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T12:44:18-07:00","id":1443293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443288#post1443288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated question: the core book states &quot;Supernal beings follow the same rules as the Awakened for using their Arcana, paying Mana as appropriate&quot;. So obviously supernal entities pay Mana for spells that explicitly require it, but what about spells that don't? Supernals don't use Rotes or Praxis, so theoretically any spell they cast is &quot;Improvised&quot;. However, they also don't have a distinction between Primary, Common, and Inferior Arcana, so do said Improvised spells cost Mana, or not?<br /> <br /> I lean towards &quot;not&quot;: since they're Made of Magic, it seems safe to assume that any Arcana they possess could be considered effectively &quot;Ruling&quot;. But what say ye?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine you are correct, as archmasters, partially made of magic, consider all arcana to be ruling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T13:22:11-07:00","id":1443294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443292#post1443292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for answering! This would probably put a hamper on a legacies devoted to the idea of merging your astral and physical form. I will work on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Legacies can stretch the rules of what the Practices can do a little bit. So, for a legacy like you describe, I\u2019d actually allow an Attainment that lets you meditate bodily into the astral using just Life and Mind. (Spitballing: if it requires a scene of meditation, make it the fourth attainment, or the fifth if it can be done as Instant action.) That\u2019s a cool legacy idea too.<br /> <br /> Edit: as for the problem of equipment: your astral body reflects your self image, which for most people probably includes clothes, and you can will path tools into existence. If the justification for the legacy is that their astral form is merged with their body, then you could hand-waved these features as applying to their combo-form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 04-09-2021, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T14:05:47-07:00","id":1443298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443294#post1443294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Legacies can stretch the rules of what the Practices can do a little bit. So, for a legacy like you describe, I\u2019d actually allow an Attainment that lets you meditate bodily into the astral using just Life and Mind. (Spitballing: if it requires a scene of meditation, make it the fourth attainment, or the fifth if it can be done as Instant action.) That\u2019s a cool legacy idea too.<br /> <br /> Edit: as for the problem of equipment: your astral body reflects your self image, which for most people probably includes clothes, and you can will path tools into existence. If the justification for the legacy is that their astral form is merged with their body, then you could hand-waved these features as applying to their combo-form.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is that the \u201creal\u201d body stays permanently in the oneiros, the projection can only escape by falling asleep in the oneiros, so the meditation option is perfect. I\u2019m fine with no clothes or clothes being your skin or something weird. I don\u2019t think equipment fits the spell. The idea is the project spawns in places where one would sleep, like on your bed, or in a tent. The idea is that it is somewhere where you have truly slept, and that is at least conceptually safe and restful.<br /> <br /> This is kinda based off a interpretation of bloodborne, where the beasts were forced to have a physical form that is the same as their mental form. I don\u2019t know if you played the game, but a significant part of the game takes place in the hunter\u2019s dream. It\u2019s literally the first hunter\u2019s dream of a peaceful world. The entire game you astrally project out of it, into another astral realm. That other realm is the games \u201creal\u201d world. The entire game takes place in various dreams or nightmares that are just as real as the real world. The games plot revolves around a plague that alters the mind and body to make them monsters. Both are effected at the same time, because it\u2019s a dream world. Meditation and calm slows or prevents the decent into as evidenced by one of the bosses being a priestess who\u2019s concentration was broken by the player immensely transformation into one of the most horrific monsters.<br /> <br /> Anyways the mind body merging, and being permanently stuck in a dream both were interesting as a legacy. If there is great interest, I will make a separate post, as I have never made a legacy before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T16:06:40-07:00","id":1443302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443291#post1443291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thank you both for responding!<br /> I had typed a exhaustive and quoted response to the answers, but I think I might have accidently deleted it when I tried to quote Isator Levi. Is there any way to avoid that in the future?<br /> <br /> proindrakenzol<br /> 1) I meant a ai that would register to mind sight, like a animal created by life making. That would seem to be a thing, as otherwise you would have to puppeteer the creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>A program based AI (as opposed to an intelligence created with Mind) would not have a Mind to Mind sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) I am trying to create spirits of a mage's nimbus from a resonance of that mages nimbus. 10, 11,and 12, were to make a place of power that said nimbus spirits can feed from. If I understand right, the nimbus weaved node should spread the nimbus resonance to other node via lay lines. </div> </div> </div>Resonance generally is described by a single word, but, yeah, that should work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) nimbus knots are described on pages 92-93 of signs of sorcery. They are formed when a mage dies while casting a spell. They contain memories, but seem to be a prime only effect. </div> </div> </div>Considering that they don't even always form when a Mage dies in the middle of casting, I'd say the best you could do is cast a spell that ensures that if the &quot;dying while casting a spell&quot; condition is met then a nimbus knot is guaranteed, but they probably can't be artificially created.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7,8,9) this was practice of my knowledge of the arcanum. Void seems to be under the purview of Death. Death is absence, and vacuum is the absence of matter. Corpses don't need to breathe, so I wondered if Death could shield your from breathing. </div> </div> </div>Death Mage Sight &quot;allows a mage to detect the presence of the Anchor Condition (p. 258) or manifested ghosts and related phenomena. With a glance, a mage using Mage Sight can tell if someone has a soul, or if a body is, in fact, dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's it, that's what it does.<br /> <br /> Death cannot shield you from having to breathe because breathing is not under the purview of Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 13, 15) Now I can make a Bloodborne inspired legacy! </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 14.5) Would they just follow me in twilight or would they use manifestations? </div> </div> </div>Depends on the spirit; the spirits on the Moon that are imprisoned there are the idigam, they're the ones that would hitch a ride. Spirits of &quot;void&quot; wouldn't be on the Moon due to the Moon not being a void.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 20) I reread the spell Psychic Genesis as it is the one referenced by golem and other spells. When it says &quot;gains traits as a rank 1 Goetia&quot; that dosn't mean it makes a Goetia? </div> </div> </div>Sort of, they're not technically Goetia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T17:03:34-07:00","id":1443308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443281#post1443281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Step 1: Convert your body to astral-ephemera with a Life/Mind Patterning effect.<br /> Step 2: Use Mind Perfecting to reverse-summon your newly ephemeral body into your Oneiros.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with this, because it seems pretty consistent that the Astral Realms do not consist of some kind of differently attuned substance, they are literally purely conceptual*. In the Astral Realms book, even the Flying Saucer Artifact, which in its own substance is capable of crossing between Astral and waking world, does not take bodies with it; if it appears before a person and they walk onto it before it transitions back to the Astral, their physical body immediately teleports asleep to their bed. <br /> <br /> I say that if a mage converts themselves into a form of ephemera on the same wavelength as a summoned Goetia and then enters the Astral through meditation or spells, they still leave the ephemeral body behind.<br /> <br /> The prospect of a mage fully subsuming bodily into the Astral sounds like it's only really viable as a form of lichdom. Really, I find a question of what the advantage of being physically within the Astral is; I would expect it puts one's life at greater risk.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a>, I think your desire to transcribe elements of Bloodborne is best suited with a combination of archmaster related stuff (Wendings and orphaned Chantries), Emanations and a locally placed Mystery. Perhaps something like a more intense but less frequent version of the Astral Intrusions of Los Angeles. In a particular city on particular nights, the boundaries between waking and certain Realms seems to become blurred in a manner that mages can't readily categorise. Figuring out exactly where their bodies and minds are and how they cross from one experience to another becomes very murky. <br /> <br /> Although it depends precisely on what is wanted out of the endeavour.<br /> <br /> * I admit that I don't know enough about Beasts to be sure if they can physically enter their Lairs, but in a case such as that I'd regard it as them operating on principles that mages less than archmasters simply cannot grasp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T18:06:41-07:00","id":1443313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443308#post1443308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I admit that I don't know enough about Beasts to be sure if they can physically enter their Lairs, but in a case such as that I'd regard it as them operating on principles that mages less than archmasters simply cannot grasp.</div> </div> </div> </div>The short version: Beasts can physically enter their Lairs, but without opening a Primordial Pathway to another part of the Astral they can <i>only</i> physically enter their Lairs; if you bring someone into your Lair and they try to just walk out, they'll either transition into a Burrow leading to another Chamber or exit into the Primordial Dream as a Dream Form whose wake-up point is the Lair that they left. Otherwise, doing so is the equivalent of Demon's general-purpose &quot;open a gate to another dimension&quot; Exploit in terms of is-this-supposed-to-happen.<br /> <br /> The Begotten are also operating on a power setup whose core supernatural facets are the meeting place between &quot;incredibly resonant personal nightmare locale&quot; and &quot;goetia of Fear Subtype drawn out of the Dreamtime and given form by the Temenos&quot;; their approach to the Astral is physical because they're dealing with the &quot;realest&quot; parts of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T19:07:56-07:00","id":1443324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443308#post1443308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't agree with this, because it seems pretty consistent that the Astral Realms do not consist of some kind of differently attuned substance, they are literally purely conceptual*. In the Astral Realms book, even the Flying Saucer Artifact, which in its own substance is capable of crossing between Astral and waking world, does not take bodies with it; if it appears before a person and they walk onto it before it transitions back to the Astral, their physical body immediately teleports asleep to their bed.<br /> <br /> I say that if a mage converts themselves into a form of ephemera on the same wavelength as a summoned Goetia and then enters the Astral through meditation or spells, they still leave the ephemeral body behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I see what you're getting at. I personally have been sticking with the model that the Astral is basically like the Shadow or the Underworld, where everything native to it is composed of ephemera. I'd be fine with the idea that everything in the astral is purely conceptual, but I don't think the books are explicit/consistent about it. 1e definitely leaned in that direction, but then again, the rules for ephemeral entities, the different phases of twilight, etc. weren't fully fleshed out. As I recall, the 1e goetic summons spell required Spirit on top of Mind, wheres the 2e version only requires it if you want to Materialize the summoned entity. Basically, I don't think 1e had a real conception of mind-ephemera as a thing, where 2e definitely does. If 2e astral space were not intended to be composed of the same mind-ephemera that astral entities exist as in the physical world, then I would hope that the 2e descriptions would make mention. As it stands, 2e seems to imply that the Astral/Shadow/Underworld operate on the same basic rules, except where otherwise spelled out. So, from a purely 2e standpoint, I don't see any reason to think that mind-ephemera isn't the basic substance of the astral. Otherwise, things like Goetic Summons and the Los Angeles verges would have to also create/slap together an ephemeral body for the entity crossing over.<br /> <br /> There's enough room that I'd understand if someone wanted to rule the other way for their game. But I don't think it's the intended reading for 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * I admit that I don't know enough about Beasts to be sure if they can physically enter their Lairs, but in a case such as that I'd regard it as them operating on principles that mages less than archmasters simply cannot grasp. </div> </div> </div>So Beasts are specifically weird in this regard, so they don't clarify the situation much. Anything entering their Lair from the physical world does so fully physically and interacts with everything thing from the astral on equal footing (there's no astral-Twilight in a Lair). <i>But</i>, anyone exiting the Lair into the astral drops their body and continues as a Dream Form. So really Lairs are more like weird astral verges where the physical and astral overlap, rather then normal astral sub-realms.<br /> <br /> If anyone has good counter arguments or explicit explanations I've missed, feel free to hit me with them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I've been running an astral-heavy campaign for a while now, and trying to keep the metaphysics straight has been a lots of &quot;fun&quot;. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T23:03:58-07:00","id":1443335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443308#post1443308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The prospect of a mage fully subsuming bodily into the Astral sounds like it's only really viable as a form of lichdom. Really, I find a question of what the advantage of being physically within the Astral is; I would expect it puts one's life at greater risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as one stays in the oneiros, and in safe conceptual areas, I would think it would be far safer than the real world. The unlimited reach on every spell in the oneiros is a nice bonus. Honestly it\u2019s probably one of the worst paths to lichdom. Astral time flows differently, and there is no telling how much you body ages while you project outward. It is nice if you need to die, or are expecting to be killed, and still want to live though. I doubt I will use it in the legacy I\u2019m building as it is rather impractical.<br /> The clear best use of it though, is to project physically out of the oneiros, use words of truth on somebody, and say \u201c I put my soul into a recursive loop, what have you done today\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443308#post1443308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a>, I think your desire to transcribe elements of Bloodborne is best suited with a combination of archmaster related stuff (Wendings and orphaned Chantries), Emanations and a locally placed Mystery. Perhaps something like a more intense but less frequent version of the Astral Intrusions of Los Angeles. In a particular city on particular nights, the boundaries between waking and certain Realms seems to become blurred in a manner that mages can't readily categorise. Figuring out exactly where their bodies and minds are and how they cross from one experience to another becomes very murky.<br /> <br /> Although it depends precisely on what is wanted out of the endeavour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I only wanted a spell that referenced Bloodborne. Actually getting to play or dm mage is a bit of pipe dream right now, as all the people I would do that with only want to do 5e d&amp;d. I think Bloodborne is better suited to deviant or hunter than mage, but your ideas on how to do it for mage are awesome, and will be included if I ever can run a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443308#post1443308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I admit that I don't know enough about Beasts to be sure if they can physically enter their Lairs, but in a case such as that I'd regard it as them operating on principles that mages less than archmasters simply cannot grasp.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this has already been answered, I find it relevant that changelings can physically enter the astral through the gate of horn, and then through the dreaming roads. At least, they are implied to. I\u2019m mostly referring to the stranger paths side bar, and it makes no mention of having to be in dream form to leave the dreaming roads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T23:48:35-07:00","id":1443339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443298#post1443298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea is that the \u201creal\u201d body stays permanently in the oneiros, the projection can only escape by falling asleep in the oneiros, so the meditation option is perfect. I\u2019m fine with no clothes or clothes being your skin or something weird. I don\u2019t think equipment fits the spell. The idea is the project spawns in places where one would sleep, like on your bed, or in a tent. The idea is that it is somewhere where you have truly slept, and that is at least conceptually safe and restful.<br /> <br /> This is kinda based off a interpretation of bloodborne, where the beasts were forced to have a physical form that is the same as their mental form. I don\u2019t know if you played the game, but a significant part of the game takes place in the hunter\u2019s dream. It\u2019s literally the first hunter\u2019s dream of a peaceful world. The entire game you astrally project out of it, into another astral realm. That other realm is the games \u201creal\u201d world. The entire game takes place in various dreams or nightmares that are just as real as the real world. The games plot revolves around a plague that alters the mind and body to make them monsters. Both are effected at the same time, because it\u2019s a dream world. Meditation and calm slows or prevents the decent into as evidenced by one of the bosses being a priestess who\u2019s concentration was broken by the player immensely transformation into one of the most horrific monsters.<br /> <br /> Anyways the mind body merging, and being permanently stuck in a dream both were interesting as a legacy. If there is great interest, I will make a separate post, as I have never made a legacy before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that sounds more like a Walker, a type of Rapt (0 Wisdom mages) found in Nameless &amp; Accursed. You could make it so a powerful being from the Sideral Wastes caused their soul to shatter in a peculiar way, granting them a task to hunt certain targets in exchange for their freedom.<br /> <br /> First they work on mental manipulations (dreams, Oneiros hunts, etc). Then they move on to possessing their hunting vessels. <br /> <br /> When they realize this might take a while and the logical problems pile up, they start learning Spirit so they can Manifest more easily, have some control of the physical again and recruit &quot;hunting hounds&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Legacy (Spirit and Mind) would come in as part of the prize or solution that allows them to regaining normal Wisdom. The real challenge starts after, for they have proven themselves by being initiated into the Hunter's Workshop and a hunter must hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T03:23:56-07:00","id":1443351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443335#post1443335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The unlimited reach on every spell in the oneiros is a nice bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it only works within the Oneiros, how much can be accomplished with it?<br /> <br /> And you can still do that stuff while your body is sleeping in the waking world, it doesn't strictly enhance your capabilities. Maybe it makes you less vulnerable, but it's an extreme proposition relative to the vulnerability of being asleep.<br /> <br /> As for staying to the safe parts, as a realm of experience and associations, moving around the Oneiros might not necessarily be conscious; one could encounter an image or memory that connects to something more threatening even if the mage did not mean it to. And the daimon has a lot of latitude, and probably some opinions about retreating too much from the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly it\u2019s probably one of the worst paths to lichdom. Astral time flows differently, and there is no telling how much you body ages while you project outward. It is nice if you need to die, or are expecting to be killed, and still want to live though. </div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that becoming a Morphean generally entails total separation from the body in the first place. Not ideal (although some may find roaming the Temenos for eternity appealing), but might be considered preferable to death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The clear best use of it though, is to project physically out of the oneiros, use words of truth on somebody, and say \u201c I put my soul into a recursive loop, what have you done today\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really follow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this has already been answered, I find it relevant that changelings can physically enter the astral through the gate of horn, and then through the dreaming roads. At least, they are implied to. I\u2019m mostly referring to the stranger paths side bar, and it makes no mention of having to be in dream form to leave the dreaming roads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the Hedge being the Astral Threshold suggests some strange things about what the Wyrd can do to the relationship between physical and conceptual, but I'm still thinking that's a frame of reference mages don't really capture within conventional Practices.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose something close is that a mage going around in conceptual worlds might cast an Unmaking of Life on their own body to temporarily remove their physical presence from the world, although such a thing might be risky. Like, be sure you don't allow a Paradox to give the thing the Reach to be Lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T09:14:07-07:00","id":1443371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443351#post1443351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it only works within the Oneiros, how much can be accomplished with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you get infinite reach on spells that works on something brought in that doesn\u2019t need to be long lasting. If you can bring it out, and the spell has done it\u2019s work, then effectively you have usable infinite reach. Say like using mend with all the reach options, usually requires 6 reach to make instant. Demesne aren\u2019t hard to acquire in point of the game, but this a demesne of every path, that nobody can steal. The oneiros has some restrictions on how the spells can be used, but surely that sounds useful at some point? If you are looking for a more practical answer than that, I at least cannot provide one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443351#post1443351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you can still do that stuff while your body is sleeping in the waking world, it doesn't strictly enhance your capabilities. Maybe it makes you less vulnerable, but it's an extreme proposition relative to the vulnerability of being asleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends entirely on how much danger you believe yourself to be. If you anger everybody in the seers and pentacle, or the god machine, your own soul isn\u2019t a bad hiding place. Mages can also get REALLY paranoid, and some rather scared people might think that it\u2019s a good option. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443351#post1443351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for staying to the safe parts, as a realm of experience and associations, moving around the Oneiros might not necessarily be conscious; one could encounter an image or memory that connects to something more threatening even if the mage did not mean it to. And the daimon has a lot of latitude, and probably some opinions about retreating too much from the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admittedly don\u2019t understand how traveling in the oneiros works then. I get it\u2019s conceptual travel, but while in the oneiros don\u2019t you still have to physically move? The daimon is admittedly not something I had considered. I don\u2019t think using the oneiros would anger the daimon, but you never know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443351#post1443351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that becoming a Morphean generally entails total separation from the body in the first place. Not ideal (although some may find roaming the Temenos for eternity appealing), but might be considered preferable to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really haven\u2019t read about them, but I imagine many mages who regularly do this would not find becoming a goetica to be a abhorrent idea.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443351#post1443351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a joke, apparently one only funny to me. It was really late for me when I got home from work last night, and I thought it was a good idea to attempt humor. I was clearly wrong. The idea was that if you meditate into the astral while in the astral, you wind up... in the astral. It\u2019s like walking into a room with a door on the other side, that opens into the same room with the same door. Astral space is often poetically called the soul, despite being different from the thing inside humans which is also called the soul. The joke is revealing the mind bending weirdness of the actions to someone, and watching their confusion. Since words of truth crosses all boundaries in communication, they will know exactly what you did, phrased in a way that\u2019s technically true, while being way more confusing then a more detailed explanation. ... I thought it was funny at the time.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443351#post1443351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, the Hedge being the Astral Threshold suggests some strange things about what the Wyrd can do to the relationship between physical and conceptual, but I'm still thinking that's a frame of reference mages don't really capture within conventional Practices.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose something close is that a mage going around in conceptual worlds might cast an Unmaking of Life on their own body to temporarily remove their physical presence from the world, although such a thing might be risky. Like, be sure you don't allow a Paradox to give the thing the Reach to be Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the route changelings use is completely accessible to everyone else in the setting, as long as they can enter the hedge. Granted, that\u2019s a almost impossible journey for anyone without a wyrd score. Practically nobody will even know it\u2019s even possible. It is still something the setting allows. I don\u2019t know if that means mages can\u2019t enter the astral physically though below archmastery practices, but it\u2019s possible without the use of any spells, by just walking to the right place on the right path. Through one of the most hazardous environments in the setting for a mage that doesn\u2019t flat out just kill them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T10:03:37-07:00","id":1443373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443371#post1443371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the route changelings use is completely accessible to everyone else in the setting, as long as they can enter the hedge. Granted, that\u2019s a almost impossible journey for anyone without a wyrd score. Practically nobody will even know it\u2019s even possible. It is still something the setting allows. I don\u2019t know if that means mages can\u2019t enter the astral physically though below archmastery practices, but it\u2019s possible without the use of any spells, by just walking to the right place on the right path. Through one of the most hazardous environments in the setting for a mage that doesn\u2019t flat out just kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gate of Horn is a Hedgeway. Finding it requires a chase that the Hedge wins more easily the more Obsessions you have. If you don't have Glamour, using it requires a Key, the bypassing of which requires Fate 3 and Mind 1 for the Awakened. Even once you're into the Dreaming Roads, you still need to navigate to find the Bastion you're looking for, which is subject to the same wrinkles of navigation as the regular Hedge.<br /> <br /> And once you get there you're not even actually getting into the Astral \u2014 a Bastion contains dreams, not the deeper realms of the soul, as evidenced by the fact that the spell you use to breach them without going through the physical process of breaking in is just Dream Reaching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T10:18:58-07:00","id":1443376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443373#post1443373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gate of Horn is a Hedgeway. Finding it requires a chase that the Hedge wins more easily the more Obsessions you have. If you don't have Glamour, using it requires a Key, the bypassing of which requires Fate 3 and Mind 1 for the Awakened. Even once you're into the Dreaming Roads, you still need to navigate to find the Bastion you're looking for, which is subject to the same wrinkles of navigation as the regular Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>This should probably be asked in the changeling version of this thread, but does sacrificing a goblin fruit work? I\u2019m going to guess it doesn\u2019t, but I still want to know. Also where is the rules for mortals and hedgeways? I can\u2019t seem to find it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443373#post1443373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And once you get there you're not even actually getting into the Astral \u2014 a Bastion contains dreams, not the deeper realms of the soul, as evidenced by the fact that the spell you use to breach them without going through the physical process of breaking in is just Dream Reaching.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m using the stranger paths side bar on page 221 for my evidence, which does say you can make it into the astral. Admittedly that side bar is really vague, and I can see somebody having a different interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T10:26:18-07:00","id":1443377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443376#post1443376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This should probably be asked in the changeling version of this thread, but does sacrificing a goblin fruit work? I\u2019m going to guess it doesn\u2019t, but I still want to know. Also where is the rules for mortals and hedgeways? I can\u2019t seem to find it.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Never mind I found it. Page 198-199. I\u2019m still not seeing anything about a glamor cost, just a resolve+composure roll or a key.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T11:09:45-07:00","id":1443380,"title":"","content":"1) Can remote control allow someone to use a prosthetic hand to a similar degree as a normal hand.<br /> 2) What practice would speed up a chemical reaction, just using matter. <br /> 3) Does the spell lodestone create energy?<br /> 4) Can a mage use lodestone to collect air pollution and concentrate it for easy collection?<br /> 4.5) The only way to do the above efficiently is by using advanced scale to collect a large area, would pms trigger in every mage inside, and as long a they could see it, outside the area?<br /> 4.75) what would be the average response of mages who didn\u2019t know what was happening?<br /> 5) what would be the practice used to spilt material into their elemental form, in the scientific sense?<br /> 6) Do animals and spirits register to mind mage sight?<br /> 7) is it possible to only perfect part of a object, like perfecting half a bar of silver?<br /> 8) is there anyway to have a ai familiar? <br /> 9) Can Ochemata fall or otherwise be striped of it\u2019s powers?<br /> 9.5) Can said said hypothetical fallen Ochemata undergo divergence? Or start a pilgrimage?<br /> 9.75) What happens if it returns to the being that spawned it?<br /> 10) What does perfected light do?<br /> 11) Is it possible there are other emanation realms of other planets besides Mars?<br /> 11.5) How would one go about searching for one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T11:28:45-07:00","id":1443385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443377#post1443377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 198-199. I\u2019m still not seeing anything about a glamor cost, just a resolve+composure roll or a key.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am referring to the fact that if you're not a changeling you're not getting through without the Key, Vice indulgence (for which the Wits + Composure roll suffers a penalty equal to half your Gnosis as a mage), or following one of the Lost.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Lost can enter the Hedge through any portal, (p109, &quot;To open a door to the Hedge, the changeling must have access to a closeable portal that she could fit through, such as a door, window, or manhole. The changeling spends a point of Glamour, and must make a request for the portal to open into the Hedge.&quot;) replacing the mundane world beyond with a darkly verdant elsewhere and turning that door into a dormant Hedgeway, or gate into the Hedge.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;After a gateway has been used, it remains a dormant Hedgeway until the seasons change. During that time, other Lost do not need to spend Glamour to open the passageway, but once the season is up, they must establish the gateway again.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Humans cannot open a Hedgeway by touch \u2014 the world they see is solid and the Mask is reality. To enter the Hedge, they need to find another way in, and a few exist[\u2026]&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hedgeways exist wholly inside the Hedge, too, cordoning off some areas from the rest. The Gate of Horn that separates the Dreaming Roads from the Hedge proper is one example; the myriad hidden entrances to mirror space are another. Finding and stepping through these gates works just the same way as [for normal Hedgeways].&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443376#post1443376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m using the stranger paths side bar on page 221 for my evidence, which does say you can make it into the astral. Admittedly that side bar is really vague, and I can see somebody having a different interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using the &quot;Mages in the Hedge&quot; mechanics provided in Dark Eras 2 (page 376-7), which specify what mages can do to enter a Bastion and specifically contrast the Hedge and the Astral.<br /> <br /> Stranger Paths is talking about venturing off the path in a place where everywhere that's not one of the Roads or the surroundings of a Bastion is reality-is-out-to-lunch territory that's treated mechanically the same as the Thorns. &quot;Desperate changelings may flee into the surrounding chaos, but a traveler who strays off the beaten path risks wandering into an inhuman dreamscape or an alien realm of existence&quot; \u2014 functionally the outcome is interchangeable with the didn't-get-out-in-time results described in A Bastion's End on the next page.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you go into one of the deepest parts of a rabbit hole practically built to fuck with mages and then jump into the wildest parts of it, you <i>might</i> be able to physically enter the Astral if you don't wind up in some fresher hell instead&quot; is nowhere near consistent enough to be talking about definitions of possible that are consistently reproducible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T12:16:05-07:00","id":1443386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443385#post1443385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If you go into one of the deepest parts of a rabbit hole practically built to fuck with mages and then jump into the wildest parts of it, you <i>might</i> be able to physically enter the Astral if you don't wind up in some fresher hell instead&quot; is nowhere near consistent enough to be talking about definitions of possible that are consistently reproducible.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for the purposes of this conversation, it is possible to be physically in the astral. Just insanely difficult to try, assuming a spell can\u2019t do that for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T12:26:27-07:00","id":1443387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443380#post1443380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Can remote control allow someone to use a prosthetic hand to a similar degree as a normal hand.<br /> 2) What practice would speed up a chemical reaction, just using matter. <br /> 3) Does the spell lodestone create energy?<br /> 4) Can a mage use lodestone to collect air pollution and concentrate it for easy collection?<br /> 4.5) The only way to do the above efficiently is by using advanced scale to collect a large area, would pms trigger in every mage inside, and as long a they could see it, outside the area?<br /> 4.75) what would be the average response of mages who didn\u2019t know what was happening?<br /> 5) what would be the practice used to spilt material into their elemental form, in the scientific sense?<br /> 6) Do animals and spirits register to mind mage sight?<br /> 7) is it possible to only perfect part of a object, like perfecting half a bar of silver?<br /> 8) is there anyway to have a ai familiar? <br /> 9) Can Ochemata fall or otherwise be striped of it\u2019s powers?<br /> 9.5) Can said said hypothetical fallen Ochemata undergo divergence? Or start a pilgrimage?<br /> 9.75) What happens if it returns to the being that spawned it?<br /> 10) What does perfected light do?<br /> 11) Is it possible there are other emanation realms of other planets besides Mars?<br /> 11.5) How would one go about searching for one?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yes, provided there was an adequate power source<br /> 2) Perfecting to act as a catalyst <br /> 3) Not at all: &quot;Unless the object can move under its own power, this spell can only nudge the object when an external force is applied to it&quot;<br /> 4) You would require Shaping, for the reason stated above<br /> 4.5) Yes, it triggers when any supernatural effect happens<br /> 4.75) Use active sight. Inexperienced ones would use Shielding spells. Veterans would know this could be bait tossed out by a Banisher (or worse) and would use a Veiling alongside the active sight, before even considering Shielding.<br /> 5) Weaving to separate alloys (specially Shaping), Unraveling to break them into composing elements <br /> 6) Yes, it detects all sentient beings. However, if you are unable to perceive beings in that specific frequency of Twilight, they will not appear. If you are in their native Realms, they are always visible, whoch solves that<br /> 7) Probably simply fine tuning the Imago, but you would still need to have enough Scale to encompass the full subject <br /> 8) Probably with a Making of Forces (electric AI matrix), having an ephemeral entity Posses an item or using the Golem spell on the target tool<br /> 9) Not without Imperial spells. Even then, its not worth the hassle, the archmage can just dismiss them and make more<br /> 9.5) The Divine Fire doesn't play nice with Supernal magic. While technically anything is possible with archmages, its a very weird edge case that would be very unlikely to happen.<br /> 9.75) Depends, what was their Pilgrimage like ? Knowing archmages and assuming this was all planned, the most likely answer is &quot;become the Quintessence to a terrifying Act of Imperium of unprecedented power&quot;<br /> 10) Undocumented, probably illumites all frequencies of Twilight, acts as sunlight to vampies and works on any supernatural darkness <br /> 11) There definitely are<br /> 12) Stumble upon them, find research about them, ask your Orders for data (especially the Mystagogue in the cabal) or, in this specific case, barter with a Thrice Great lodge. If all else fails, cast Serendipity or Strings of Fate.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-10-2021, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T12:34:36-07:00","id":1443390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443380#post1443380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Can remote control allow someone to use a prosthetic hand to a similar degree as a normal hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably better, since it would always succeed without a roll, only downside is no Exceptional (unless your ST considers potency 5 to grant an automatic exceptional).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) What practice would speed up a chemical reaction, just using matter. </div> </div> </div>Probably Perfecting, but you might be able to achieve the same effect with clever application of Ruling or even Compelling.<br /> <br /> My ruling would be that Compelling would cause all the materials to react (usually efficiency is sub-100%), Ruling could halve the reaction time, and Perfecting could have the time per potency. This is based on eyeballing conceptually similar spells in other Arcana (especially Forces).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Does the spell lodestone create energy? </div> </div> </div>A teeny-tiny amount, but nothing exploitable, really it's just saying that if something would move anyway, it moves in a particular direction if possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Can a mage use lodestone to collect air pollution and concentrate it for easy collection? </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, if the pollution would be able to naturally move/be moved towards the thing it would, but if a force pushed it elsewhere it would still be pushed away from the collection point. <i>Shaping</i> is really the spell you're looking for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4.5) The only way to do the above efficiently is by using advanced scale to collect a large area, would pms trigger in every mage inside, and as long a they could see it, outside the area? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4.75) what would be the average response of mages who didn\u2019t know what was happening? </div> </div> </div>Activate Active Mage Sight and investigate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) what would be the practice used to spilt material into their elemental form, in the scientific sense? </div> </div> </div>Depends; if it's a composite material then <i>Shaping</i> would let you separate them, if it's a chemical compound you'd need Patterning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) Do animals and spirits register to mind mage sight? </div> </div> </div>The former yes, the latter only if they're manifested or the Mage can otherwise sense them (e.g. Spirit 2 Attainment or the <i>Exorcist's Eye</i> spell).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7) is it possible to only perfect part of a object, like perfecting half a bar of silver? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8) is there anyway to have a ai familiar? </div> </div> </div>Assuming you mean a computer-program AI and not a Goetia created via Mind 5: no, &quot;Familiar&quot; is a manifestation granted to ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9) Can Ochemata fall or otherwise be striped of it\u2019s powers?<br /> 9.5) Can said said hypothetical fallen Ochemata undergo divergence? Or start a pilgrimage?<br /> 9.75) What happens if it returns to the being that spawned it? </div> </div> </div>Messing with someone else's Ochemata would require very specific Acts of Imperium, if possible at all, and definitely be a violation of the Pax Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10) What does perfected light do? </div> </div> </div>Good question! There's no official rules, but it would probably do something weird like treat every substance as having a refractive index of 1.000 for all wavelengths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 11) Is it possible there are other emanation realms of other planets besides Mars? </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 11.5) How would one go about searching for one? </div> </div> </div>Investigate Mysteries and places aligned to those planets.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 04-10-2021, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T16:56:39-07:00","id":1443424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443324#post1443324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be fine with the idea that everything in the astral is purely conceptual, but I don't think the books are explicit/consistent about it. 1e definitely leaned in that direction, but then again, the rules for ephemeral entities, the different phases of twilight, etc. weren't fully fleshed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the implication in the statement of &quot;The Astral Realms proper are made of thoughts, emotions, and other ephemeral creations of the soul, but the Arcana affect their creations using the same rules as they do on the material realm. In a place of symbols, each Arcanum\u2019s dominion has equally symbolic importance. Matter affects visions of stone, for instance. That said, a place of thoughts and emotions made manifest eases the use of the Mind Arcanum.&quot; But some of it is from the sense that for the time being, the First Edition Astral Realms book is still a very strong guideline for what to do with the subject, and I find significance in descriptions of how most places in the Astral don't naturally have their own ephemera.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I just think it's neat to regard the Astral as distinguished by basically amounting to sensory stimulus devoid of physical inputs and being deeply immersed in mental visualisation, rather than something with a total physical reality.<br /> <br /> Although that being said, I actually do find myself thinking that it's not necessarily invalid for a mage to use both Life and Mind for a Patterning to convert flesh into that kind of sensory experience entirely, without even needing to be embodied as ephemera, but I still wonder at its viability for entering the Astral. I guess if it ever came up in a context for application, then in the interests of compromise I would go with such a state of existence being able to meditate its way into the Astral and having some particular advantages there, but also being extremely vulnerable. That without a body to anchor you back to material reality, you can be damaged or imprisoned on a very severe level, and the spell's Duration ending while still in the Astral can severely mess you up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, the 1e goetic summons spell required Spirit on top of Mind, wheres the 2e version only requires it if you want to Materialize the summoned entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Goetic spells in the First Edition core seem a bit awkward in several respects, such as how they're cordoned off from the spell lists. I kind of get an impression of them as being interested in depicting a particular kind of magic in a privileged position, but without a full sense of how they interact with the Oneiros. Certainly by the time that Summoners introduced spells to draw forth entities from the Astral, it made them pure Mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, things like Goetic Summons and the Los Angeles verges would have to also create/slap together an ephemeral body for the entity crossing over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I expect that they actually do. Or at least they facilitate the process of Goetia existing in the Twilight of the material world where natural laws cause ephemeral substance to form for them.<br /> <br /> Bringing up the spell and the Mystery reminds me of the fact that barring such interventions, it's supposed to be basically impossible for Goetia to exist outside of the Astral in the first place. Astral Irises aren't even crossing over points for them. The Shadow and Underworld come across as more physically adjacent places when all the inhabitants need to do to enter the world is locate the proper passageways. Those beings are constructed of substance that can walk into and out of the material realm as they please, but the Goetia stay put barring magic.<br /> <br /> Magic that doesn't even work if you're not somewhere that you could meditate to the Astral. You can cast Spirit Summons from anywhere and even if the target can't cross the Gauntlet it will still feel the pull and travel to your vicinity, but an Astral summoning needs something to create the proper mental channel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T17:03:48-07:00","id":1443425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443424#post1443424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find the implication in the statement of &quot;The Astral Realms proper are made of thoughts, emotions, and other ephemeral creations of the soul, but the Arcana affect their creations using the same rules as they do on the material realm. In a place of symbols, each Arcanum\u2019s dominion has equally symbolic importance. Matter affects visions of stone, for instance. That said, a place of thoughts and emotions made manifest eases the use of the Mind Arcanum.&quot; But some of it is from the sense that for the time being, the First Edition Astral Realms book is still a very strong guideline for what to do with the subject, and I find significance in descriptions of how most places in the Astral don't naturally have their own ephemera.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I just think it's neat to regard the Astral as distinguished by basically amounting to sensory stimulus devoid of physical inputs and being deeply immersed in mental visualisation, rather than something with a total physical reality.<br /> <br /> Although that being said, I actually do find myself thinking that it's not necessarily invalid for a mage to use both Life and Mind for a Patterning to convert flesh into that kind of sensory experience entirely, without even needing to be embodied as ephemera, but I still wonder at its viability for entering the Astral. I guess if it ever came up in a context for application, then in the interests of compromise I would go with such a state of existence being able to meditate its way into the Astral and having some particular advantages there, but also being extremely vulnerable. That without a body to anchor you back to material reality, you can be damaged or imprisoned on a very severe level, and the spell's Duration ending while still in the Astral can severely mess you up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked it wasn't possible to affect your body while you were in the astral. Spells couldn't cross the astral barrier which is why you'd have to use life spells before you got into the astral to stop yourself from starving to death while you were exploring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T14:49:00-07:00","id":1443512,"title":"","content":"Which book is the Liberatore Legacy in? It's in the wiki, but I can't see any citation for source there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T15:53:02-07:00","id":1443526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443512#post1443512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which book is the Liberatore Legacy in? It's in the wiki, but I can't see any citation for source there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tome of the Watchtowers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T15:59:58-07:00","id":1443529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443526#post1443526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tome of the Watchtowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks! I've dug through all the Order books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T11:02:22-07:00","id":1443617,"title":"","content":"1) Can a matter unveiling allow one to receive tactile information from a object, ie can a amputee regain their sense of touch with a prosthetic?<br /> 2) Can time weaving weave the properties of all the seasons together?<br /> 2.5) If cast on a tree, what would happen?<br /> 2.75) How would that interact with changeling seasonal court bargains, oaths, and hedgeways?<br /> 3) What is the difference between the nimbus, resonance, and essence?<br /> 4) Does hone the perfected form REALLY need matter for it's forces option? This seems like a basic function of the perfecting practice.<br /> 5) Can you use hone the perfected form on things other than matter and forces? Like a perfected sympathetic connection, or a perfected season, or time of day, or a perfected nimbus, or perfected mana.<br /> 5.5) Has this ever come up in a game?<br /> 6) Is it possible to make a mana spirit?<br /> 7) is there a good resource for understanding spirits, spirit ecologies, and the shadow that's still relevant for 2e mage?<br /> 8) What would the the practices and Arcanum for a spell that increases the potency of the Amnion?<br /> 9) What is the point of spell potions?<br /> 10) Can a plutonic form provide nutritional value?<br /> 10.5) Can can pattern restoration remove hunger?<br /> 11) Which order do you think has the highest wisdom on average?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-12-2021, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T11:43:53-07:00","id":1443624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443617#post1443617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Can a matter unveiling allow one to receive tactile information from a object, ie can a amputee regain their sense of touch with a prosthetic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems reasonable enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Can time weaving weave the properties of all the seasons together?<br /> 2.5) If cast on a tree, what would happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what do you mean by properties of the seasons? Weaving is able to add in elements of different parts of a timeline, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.75) How would that interact with changeling seasonal court bargains, oaths, and hedgeways?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you be more specific about what parts of those things you think might have an interaction?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) What is the difference between the nimbus, resonance, and essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nimbus is the mystical aura of a mage symbolizing their qualities as a willworker. It comes in the Immediate Nimbus which is visible to Mage Sight when they cast spells and inflicts a Tilt based on its qualities, the Signature which is their characteristic feel on subjects spells were cast on, and the Long-Term which causes uncanny occurrences to accumulate around the subjects of a mage's sympathetic connections (although adhering to a Shadow Name limits that to only things connected to the mage identity).<br /> <br /> Essence is the mystical energy that powers spirits and werewolves. It is acquired from loci (kind of an equivalent to Hallows) and appropriate kinds of feeding.<br /> <br /> Resonance is a kind of mystical conceptual quality attached to a person, place or thing that most determines which kinds of spirits can feed around it (as well as having some implications for fettering and possession). It can be channelled in the ley lines that Prime can manipulate, and when it colours the tone of Hallows results in mana that can act as a Yantra for appropriate spells. Murder resonance lets a murder spirit draw Essence, and if it's in mana can add a dice bonus for casting killing spells. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Does hone the perfected form REALLY need matter for it's forces option? This seems like a basic function of the perfecting practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think of it in terms of a particular alchemical kind of perfecting that is more native to the Matter Arcanum than it is to Forces, but I doubt anything breaks if you rule what makes more sense to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Can you use hone the perfected form on things other than matter and forces? Like a perfected sympathetic connection, or a perfected season, or time of day, or a perfected nimbus, or perfected mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't really be inclined to it, but if a player had a compelling idea that the Storyteller was on board with I'd say that's in the spirit of the game. For some of those, I think a Perfected time period is conceptual in a way that most magic doesn't really touch on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) Is it possible to make a mana spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess with Spirit 5 + Prime 4 you could produce such an entity, although there's going to be issues if it wants to feed off of mana, which is scarce enough for mages as it is. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">7) is there a good resource for understanding spirits, spirit ecologies, and the shadow that's still relevant for 2e mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the general concepts in Book of Spirits and Predators holds up, and Werewolf Second Edition has a suitably elaborate explanation of what's going on there with a few sample spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">8) What would the the practices and Arcanum for a spell that increases the potency of the Amnion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Perfecting would be the Practice, and I think any Subtle Arcanum can be suitable for it, although I'd say an improved Amnion should increase the impairment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">9) What is the point of spell potions?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage can prepare a good spell in safety and where they aren't under pressure or risk of interruption to be used later (and if they don't have the Time to Hang it), or else it's a way of lending mages the use of a spell they couldn't cast themselves which is a bit more accessible than Imbuing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">10) Can a plutonic form provide nutritional value?</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume you're referring to Eidoforms, in which case, sure, if one takes the form of food there's no obstacle to eating it. They're still actual examples of what they are. It's just a real waste for something so rare and valuable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">10.5) Can can pattern restoration remove hunger?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it should.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">11) Which order do you think has the highest wisdom on average?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a difficult question to answer when many different characters can have their own standards of Wisdom that are correct to them, as well as how a lot of the philosophies of the Orders are just as much impediments to Wisdom as facilitators of it.<br /> <br /> Like, the Guardians of the Veil are an Order with maybe the most direct provisions to encourage taking personal responsibility and casting with the utmost care, while also holding an ideal that if haste or morally dubious actions need to be undertaken, better the burden fall upon them than be on other mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T12:13:44-07:00","id":1443627,"title":"","content":"Thank you for answering!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443624#post1443624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, what do you mean by properties of the seasons? Weaving is able to add in elements of different parts of a timeline, at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can you be more specific about what parts of those things you think might have an interaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, seasons seem to be a property of time, at least I think so. I'm asking because I am stumped as to what happens when it is simultaneously multiple seasons at once. lets go with the bargains as a example, does a huntsman have to obey both spring and summers bargains at the same time with this spell? Hedgegates close after a season, does this spell effect them? does the year and a day type stuff get muddled or otherwise disturbed?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443624#post1443624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nimbus is the mystical aura of a mage symbolizing their qualities as a willworker. It comes in the Immediate Nimbus which is visible to Mage Sight when they cast spells and inflicts a Tilt based on its qualities, the Signature which is their characteristic feel on subjects spells were cast on, and the Long-Term which causes uncanny occurrences to accumulate around the subjects of a mage's sympathetic connections (although adhering to a Shadow Name limits that to only things connected to the mage identity).<br /> <br /> Essence is the mystical energy that powers spirits and werewolves. It is acquired from loci (kind of an equivalent to Hallows) and appropriate kinds of feeding.<br /> <br /> Resonance is a kind of mystical conceptual quality attached to a person, place or thing that most determines which kinds of spirits can feed around it (as well as having some implications for fettering and possession). It can be channelled in the ley lines that Prime can manipulate, and when it colours the tone of Hallows results in mana that can act as a Yantra for appropriate spells. Murder resonance lets a murder spirit draw Essence, and if it's in mana can add a dice bonus for casting killing spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be correct in saying then that essence is refined resonance? The nimbus always stuck me as similar to resonance, as both provide dice bonuses to things in their themes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443624#post1443624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't really be inclined to it, but if a player had a compelling idea that the Storyteller was on board with I'd say that's in the spirit of the game. For some of those, I think a Perfected time period is conceptual in a way that most magic doesn't really touch on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time is general throws me off, so it's interesting to see if anyone had some idea on what that might do<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443624#post1443624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess with Spirit 5 + Prime 4 you could produce such an entity, although there's going to be issues if it wants to feed off of mana, which is scarce enough for mages as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just wondering if it can use influence: mana to do odd things, might be a nice mystery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443624#post1443624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Perfecting would be the Practice, and I think any Subtle Arcanum can be suitable for it, although I'd say an improved Amnion should increase the impairment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might use that for my legacy then<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443624#post1443624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume you're referring to Eidoforms, in which case, sure, if one takes the form of food there's no obstacle to eating it. They're still actual examples of what they are. It's just a real waste for something so rare and valuable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the spell actually. Although if pattern restoration can't, I would be inclined to say no to the spell. Even I am not crazy enough to eat a Eidoform! Would that not be the same as killing a supernal entity levels of hubris?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443624#post1443624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a difficult question to answer when many different characters can have their own standards of Wisdom that are correct to them, as well as how a lot of the philosophies of the Orders are just as much impediments to Wisdom as facilitators of it.<br /> <br /> Like, the Guardians of the Veil are an Order with maybe the most direct provisions to encourage taking personal responsibility and casting with the utmost care, while also holding an ideal that if haste or morally dubious actions need to be undertaken, better the burden fall upon them than be on other mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! I'm just looking for opinions on this anyway, especially since wisdom does not equal goodness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-12-2021, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T13:58:43-07:00","id":1443646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443627#post1443627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for answering!<br /> lets go with the bargains as a example, does a huntsman have to obey both spring and summers bargains at the same time with this spell? Hedgegates close after a season, does this spell effect them? does the year and a day type stuff get muddled or otherwise disturbed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I've not yet read Changeling Second Edition, but on a preliminary basis I would think that if a being is targeted with effects that would blend periods in time such as that (either directly or coming into an area of effect), it's valid enough but might have to contend first with a potentially powerful Withstand rating and then with with any Clash of Wills when a supernatural power contrary to it comes up. I think that would be a particular case when it's a matter of being constrained by the season.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be correct in saying then that essence is refined resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that's one way to look at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nimbus always stuck me as similar to resonance, as both provide dice bonuses to things in their themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think when it comes to Resonance flavoured mana, functioning as a Yantra means that the bonus isn't quite inherent to the mana itself so much as semiotics of the sensations it conveys aiding in visualising the imago.<br /> <br /> And I think of Nimbus Tilt as simply systemizing how that aura has always been described as conveying certain sensations. Like, there have always been examples of things like &quot;people feel an improved sense of direction&quot;, it's just that it is now represented in an actual dice bonus to something like navigation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just wondering if it can use influence: mana to do odd things, might be a nice mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think as an Influence it still needs to target a Resonance, which requires it to be a more substantive thing than a supernatural energy trait. I could see being constructed of mana providing some unusual benefits besides, but the Influence still needs to be something like Wolves, Machines, Fire, Motivation, those sorts of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant the spell actually. Although if pattern restoration can't, I would be inclined to say no to the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, of course. With the description of how it is obviously magical by default, I envision Platonic Forms as looking kind of like Dr. Strange glowing wireframe things. I think they can perform physical functions, but lack something like chemical properties. It's mana given shape that can substitute for objects, but still composed of mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that not be the same as killing a supernal entity levels of hubris?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't think it's that severe. An Eidoform is not an actual thing of the Supernal, just about as close an approximation as can be. An entity actually came out of the Supernal, carries some of the substance of its function with it, and being consumed by the Abyss is a greater damage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat! I'm just looking for opinions on this anyway, especially since wisdom does not equal goodness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I at least think the voice of the Guardians in the Diamond is a big part of why Wisdom is held as something to aspire to, a counterweight to Silver Ladder ideals that might think of such a thing as only another constraint on the right of Imperium.<br /> <br /> But no, suggesting that any one is notably more Wise would ultimately only convey a personal bias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T19:20:37-07:00","id":1443684,"title":"","content":"Has anyone done a legacy based around the Aeons? Specifically Lilith?<br /> On the topic of legacies did anyone finish converting illuminated path to 2e? Would illuminated path be the same thing as tamers of light?<br /> edit: is there a place in the temenos representing the concept of self like the mainspring represents the concept of sentience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-12-2021, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T20:52:28-07:00","id":1443690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443684#post1443684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">edit: is there a place in the temenos representing the concept of self like the mainspring represents the concept of sentience?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wellspring is a weird recurring phenomenon in the Anima Mundi. You can find increasingly narrow subsets of the collective idea-space for just about any concept in the Temenos, but it's not necessarily going to bring weird earth-shattering concepts into play like the freaky shit that lives in the Dreamtime \u2014 Temenotic spaces and their resident goetia may be influential, but their influence is largely confined to the mental and social spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T18:47:57-07:00","id":1443966,"title":"","content":"Is there a legacy based around increasing your ability to pursue mysteries, at a major cost to your health, unless you actively pursue mysteries? I have a idea about a new legacy, but I want to see if it\u2019s treading new ground. Yes, I will be finishing my current one first before I begin a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T19:05:21-07:00","id":1443969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443966#post1443966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a legacy based around increasing your ability to pursue mysteries, at a major cost to your health, unless you actively pursue mysteries? I have a idea about a new legacy, but I want to see if it\u2019s treading new ground. Yes, I will be finishing my current one first before I begin a new one.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the Unforgotten Scions have a similar mindset, but not abilities like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T19:46:17-07:00","id":1444588,"title":"","content":"Mages always know when their spells are clashing; do you think a clash would awaken a sleeping mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26661-autumnking","name":"AutumnKing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T23:01:35-07:00","id":1444600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutumnKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1444588#post1444588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages always know when their spells are clashing; do you think a clash would awaken a sleeping mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, in the same way as other physical stimulus, but a clash has a short duration.<br /> Think of it as your cat that pokes your face to awaken you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T15:44:31-07:00","id":1444725,"title":"","content":"Does anybody else have a collection of Mage books that is only a few items shy of being complete?<br /> <br /> I just ask because after more than a decade of getting them, I finally got a copy of Guardians of the Veil (and The Free Council is on the way). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:04:32-07:00","id":1445087,"title":"","content":"Okay, actual question. The rules state that Supernal beings use their Arcana in the same manner as the Awakened, but do people think that should exclude the use of Yantras? Nothing specifically says that they can't as far as I know, but I feel with that restriction you get both character emphasis (that enabling the imago with semiotic shortcuts is both unnecessary when they intuit the Supernal and not possible from that mindset) and keeping some things within reason when their casting already rolls such high traits that can be boosted by spending Mana and gets unlimited Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T13:37:34-07:00","id":1445111,"title":"","content":"I agree that many yantras wouldn\u2019t make sense, especially from the semiotic shortcut point of view. But I\u2019d allow (or require) some other yantra that lend their power from some essential quality in the yantra itself - like using resonance from the environment. I\u2019d probably still require temporal and sympathetic yantras where applicable. Although it\u2019d be totally in theme to summon a Supernal for the boon of getting a sympathetic yantra that\u2019s otherwise inaccessible - but I\u2019d have that be it\u2019s own Trial, wholly separate from *using* it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T14:43:20-07:00","id":1445127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445087#post1445087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, actual question. The rules state that Supernal beings use their Arcana in the same manner as the Awakened, but do people think that should exclude the use of Yantras? Nothing specifically says that they can't as far as I know, but I feel with that restriction you get both character emphasis (that enabling the imago with semiotic shortcuts is both unnecessary when they intuit the Supernal and not possible from that mindset) and keeping some things within reason when their casting already rolls such high traits that can be boosted by spending Mana and gets unlimited Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feels like Concentration, Mantra (High Speech), and Persona could be used by Supernals. But for others, yeah, sounds reasonable to disallow them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T16:43:38-07:00","id":1445157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445111#post1445111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I\u2019d allow (or require) some other yantra that lend their power from some essential quality in the yantra itself - like using resonance from the environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the impression that's a thing, not when even Demesnes are described as functioning as Yantras based on their semiotics. I mean, the general description of Yantras says that they don't function based on any kind of inherent power, just aids in visualising the Imago.<br /> <br /> I think Concentration and Mantra make better cases, but I'd find them dependent on how one envisions the mind of a Supernal being working, particularly as it relates to casting magic. I'm not really sold on Persona. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:08:03-07:00","id":1445195,"title":"","content":"It may be relevant that Signs of Sorcery specifically describes Ochemata created by Archmasters as using &quot;Yantras, magical tools, Oblations, and Pattern scouring as mages do...&quot;, as opposed to &quot;Ochemata created by other beings possess Arcana and use them as Supernal entities.&quot; (pg. 115). The implication is that normal Supernals don't use Yantras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T23:26:46-07:00","id":1445226,"title":"","content":"Persona and a lot of other Yantras that are dependent on the caster are all represented through Merits in one way or another, which naturally disallows Supernal beings from using them because they don't have Merits. I also think Path Tools might not work because while all summoned Supernal beings align with a Path, they don't actually have Paths.<br /> Most other Yantras are mystically significant in their own regard rather than reliant on the caster. Concentration is the only one that sticks out to me as caster-centric despite not being flavoured by the caster.<br /> <br /> That said, there's something pure about the idea that they only use their natural dice pool and not any Yantras. It means instant casting truly is instant and their dice pools are naturally large. Additionally, by setting an upper bound on their dice pools, their spells generally comes across as more direct; more here and now. They have trouble pushing up spell factors to ridiculous levels and instead generally go to the lower ends of the Advanced factors if the Standard factors aren't enough. Even Potency can be increased with their infinite Reach by swapping primary factor, at the cost of having Duration be one turn or scene (before spending dice).<br /> <br /> I kinda like that. And if necessary, they generally have enough dice to spend on spell factors anyway so it's certainly not a hard limit. But on the other hand, it's always cool to have the Trial take the form of a material offering that the entity uses as a Sacrament to fulfil your request. I suppose that, if fitting or if required by Arcana Attainments, I'd allow for Yantras but generally avoid them as to not disturb the percieved purity of direct and unaided casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T01:38:02-07:00","id":1445242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445226#post1445226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have trouble pushing up spell factors to ridiculous levels and instead generally go to the lower ends of the Advanced factors if the Standard factors aren't enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the kinds of dice pools innate to an entity Rank 3 and up?<br /> <br /> If a Rank 5 Supernal ever comes upon an unprepared mage with violence then they're almost certainly fucked, because that Unmaking murder spell won't even need factors, at 25 to 30 dice you're pretty well guaranteed an exceptional success to make being Withstood meaningless (which means the mage's preparations need to take a form other than a very Potent Prime Shielding). They could take the penalty to increases Scale and still have enough to reliably roll five.<br /> <br /> This subject was prompted by my having considered how Seers of the Throne depicts the Shadow of the General as having a casting pool of 25 dice, which Second Edition would reduce to 20 just by virtue of removing the Arcanum from it (before it spent Mana to boost its Attributes by up to five each). The kind of dice pool that your basic Master would need a ritual pushed to the limit and all Yantras on deck to achieve.<br /> <br /> I'd say there's a reason that the books state or imply that most times a cabal is the target of an Exarch's Ochema, they die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T02:51:31-07:00","id":1445247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445242#post1445242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the kinds of dice pools innate to an entity Rank 3 and up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Compare to a mage of similar &quot;advancement&quot;:<br /> A Rank 3 entity has between 15-25 dots over all three Attributes, capped in 9 per Attribute. That leads to a minimum of 6 dice, maximum of 18 dice, and an average of 12 dice (if averaging min and max distributions) or ~13.33 dice (if averaging Attribute spreads from gained Attribute dots).<br /> A Gnosis 3 mage with 3 dots in an Arcanum has a base of 6 dice and the possibility of applying 3 Yantras. The absolutely best Yantras are +5 from Mudra, +4 from Persona and +3 from Sacraments, leading to a maximum dice pool of 18. Someone who hasn't minmaxed the right Merits (and found a hella good Sacrament) will likely get an average of +2 from each Yantra when they're trying, for a normal dice pool of 12.<br /> <br /> In this case I equated Rank and Gnosis which is in the Supernal entity's favour, but I do concede that they actually match up eerily good in dice pool potential before allowing Yantras for the entities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445242#post1445242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say there's a reason that the books state or imply that most times a cabal is the target of an Exarch's Ochema, they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>In second edition the Ochemata of the Exarchs and other Ascended beings start at Rank 5, with a dice pool of 21-30 (average Attribute yields 27) dice with Rote Action on their attacks (before Attribute boosting). <i>Start at.</i> Anything other than the lowliest Ochema is in the realm of plot device, and if the plot device's purpose is to kill someone, they die. Slapping Arcana (at least one of which being almost certainly on Archmaster tier) as well as additional unspecified special powers on top of that is one hell of a bonus but hardly necessary to maintain such rumours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T05:04:29-07:00","id":1445256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445247#post1445247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Gnosis 3 mage with 3 dots in an Arcanum has a base of 6 dice and the possibility of applying 3 Yantras. The absolutely best Yantras are +5 from Mudra, +4 from Persona and +3 from Sacraments, leading to a maximum dice pool of 18. Someone who hasn't minmaxed the right Merits (and found a hella good Sacrament) will likely get an average of +2 from each Yantra when they're trying, for a normal dice pool of 12.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's just a technicality or not so far as the final maths checks out, but I still think it's worth being clear and consistent on the fact that no combination of Yantras can raise the original dice pool over five, after offsetting penalties.<br /> <br /> Actually, maybe it does matter for the maths, let me think. Your Disciple wants to cast an Indefinite spell, so they've got to put themselves at -4 for that, Mudra puts them to 1 die, Persona puts them to 5, Sacrament to 8, then maybe take -4 if they want to bump the Potency up two levels and cast on four dice... Nnno, it's in the same place for the Supernal entity in those factor terms at least. The entity at least has an easier time taking penalties and then having a dice pool high enough to let exceptional success account for other factor boosts.<br /> <br /> Still, when you're talking about a mage pushing Yantras to the limit, and only for the spells learned as rotes, to get the kind of dice pool the entity has by default, I think that effectively disputes the idea that the entity has trouble pushing spell factors up.<br /> <br /> And again, before considering that mana can boost their dice pools by four for each Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:27:12-07:00","id":1445384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445242#post1445242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the kinds of dice pools innate to an entity Rank 3 and up?<br /> <br /> If a Rank 5 Supernal ever comes upon an unprepared mage with violence then they're almost certainly fucked, because that Unmaking murder spell won't even need factors, at 25 to 30 dice you're pretty well guaranteed an exceptional success to make being Withstood meaningless (which means the mage's preparations need to take a form other than a very Potent Prime Shielding). They could take the penalty to increases Scale and still have enough to reliably roll five.<br /> <br /> This subject was prompted by my having considered how Seers of the Throne depicts the Shadow of the General as having a casting pool of 25 dice, which Second Edition would reduce to 20 just by virtue of removing the Arcanum from it (before it spent Mana to boost its Attributes by up to five each). The kind of dice pool that your basic Master would need a ritual pushed to the limit and all Yantras on deck to achieve.<br /> <br /> I'd say there's a reason that the books state or imply that most times a cabal is the target of an Exarch's Ochema, they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>All you need is a simple shield with the current rules. Anything with a Rank is practically a joke to a mage baring the counter spell numina, which can negate all their attack spells. It doesn't matter how many dice they throw out when one shield forces clash of wits which on normal attacks is reduced to rank with influence it's increased to rank + influence. Granted supernal beings can also cast spells but without it, they'll be equal or losing against a mage. A mage with an advanced shielding that lasts one month can with 3 gnosis and 3 prime/spirit/mind whatever +4 flash dice. Have 10 dice for clashes with one reach and 1 mana to make it indefinite he can have 11 dice. So a starting base mage can equal a rank 5 beings powers and double their dice with their normal attacks and numina. Since all ephemeral spirits have a withstand of rank, it's also rather easy for a mage to use a spell to shut them down without much trouble. <br /> <br /> Ochema kill cabals though because they tend to be 6+ beings in the exarches case.<br /> <br /> Edit-I will say I'm REALLY not in favor of how this works but this is the rules as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-22-2021, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T23:43:53-07:00","id":1445440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445384#post1445384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All you need is a simple shield with the current rules. Anything with a Rank is practically a joke to a mage baring the counter spell numina, which can negate all their attack spells. It doesn't matter how many dice they throw out when one shield forces clash of wits which on normal attacks is reduced to rank with influence it's increased to rank + influence. Granted supernal beings can also cast spells but without it, they'll be equal or losing against a mage. A mage with an advanced shielding that lasts one month can with 3 gnosis and 3 prime/spirit/mind whatever +4 flash dice. Have 10 dice for clashes with one reach and 1 mana to make it indefinite he can have 11 dice. So a starting base mage can equal a rank 5 beings powers and double their dice with their normal attacks and numina. Since all ephemeral spirits have a withstand of rank, it's also rather easy for a mage to use a spell to shut them down without much trouble. <br /> <br /> Ochema kill cabals though because they tend to be 6+ beings in the exarches case.<br /> <br /> Edit-I will say I'm REALLY not in favor of how this works but this is the rules as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, that s the reason i prefer to use rank+power or resistance in clash of wills","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T00:41:49-07:00","id":1445444,"title":"","content":"Of course, that's assuming you can put up Shielding spells against the attacks of Supernal beings. Shielding spells are generally not supposed to work against attacks, and the few examples we've got are specifically against ephemeral entities. It's conceivable to have a similar reach option on Wards &amp; Signs to protect against Supernal entities, but not something I would count on since it could change from table to table. Additionally, Supernal beings only have Arcana and no other powers (barring things like Ascended Ochemata) so normally they'd always use Rank+Arcanum in their CoW dice pools and always be capable of using Advanced Potency for a +1 due to infinite Reach.<br /> <br /> Note that rolling Rank alone is only stated in Werewolf about spirits. I think that it makes sense in the context of that particular game that PCs would have an edge over spirits (especially considering they're the only ones who can get dice tricks on CoW rolls, hinting that werewolf powers definitely should take precedence in Werewolf games), but not necessarily in other games. If we instead look to Demon we get the splat-agnostic general rule that you roll Supernatural Tolerance + dot rating of power OR governing Attribute if the power isn't dot rated.<br /> Another way to handle it that I've seen is to take Rank + highest rated Influence (or Arcanum) for Numina and other powers that aren't dot rated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T01:39:53-07:00","id":1445448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445384#post1445384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All you need is a simple shield with the current rules. Anything with a Rank is practically a joke to a mage baring the counter spell numina, which can negate all their attack spells. It doesn't matter how many dice they throw out when one shield forces clash of wits which on normal attacks is reduced to rank with influence it's increased to rank + influence. Granted supernal beings can also cast spells but without it, they'll be equal or losing against a mage. A mage with an advanced shielding that lasts one month can with 3 gnosis and 3 prime/spirit/mind whatever +4 flash dice. Have 10 dice for clashes with one reach and 1 mana to make it indefinite he can have 11 dice. So a starting base mage can equal a rank 5 beings powers and double their dice with their normal attacks and numina. Since all ephemeral spirits have a withstand of rank, it's also rather easy for a mage to use a spell to shut them down without much trouble.<br /> <br /> Ochema kill cabals though because they tend to be 6+ beings in the exarches case.<br /> <br /> Edit-I will say I'm REALLY not in favor of how this works but this is the rules as written.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Err... what Shielding spell are you talking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T05:48:37-07:00","id":1445465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445440#post1445440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, that s the reason i prefer to use rank+power or resistance in clash of wills</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think that's a little too much. I do think it should be more of a 50:50 so i do like using rank x2 or rank +influence depending on the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T05:59:32-07:00","id":1445468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445444#post1445444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, that's assuming you can put up Shielding spells against the attacks of Supernal beings. Shielding spells are generally not supposed to work against attacks, and the few examples we've got are specifically against ephemeral entities. It's conceivable to have a similar reach option on Wards &amp; Signs to protect against Supernal entities, but not something I would count on since it could change from table to table. Additionally, Supernal beings only have Arcana and no other powers (barring things like Ascended Ochemata) so normally they'd always use Rank+Arcanum in their CoW dice pools and always be capable of using Advanced Potency for a +1 due to infinite Reach.<br /> <br /> Note that rolling Rank alone is only stated in Werewolf about spirits. I think that it makes sense in the context of that particular game that PCs would have an edge over spirits (especially considering they're the only ones who can get dice tricks on CoW rolls, hinting that werewolf powers definitely should take precedence in Werewolf games), but not necessarily in other games. If we instead look to Demon we get the splat-agnostic general rule that you roll Supernatural Tolerance + dot rating of power OR governing Attribute if the power isn't dot rated.<br /> Another way to handle it that I've seen is to take Rank + highest rated Influence (or Arcanum) for Numina and other powers that aren't dot rated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see why they wouldn't be subject to that rank ruling because spirits have a withstand of rank. It's extremely easy for spirit mages to dominate the higher rank spirits with much less effort then anyone else in the game. I'm not in favor of it as written but it is what it is. <br /> <br /> And it's hard to know what the intention with orchema are. They clearly use spirit rules but it doesn't quite say how they work. Also, death and mind shielding also protect from ephermal attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T06:32:06-07:00","id":1445475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445468#post1445468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see why they wouldn't be subject to that rank ruling because spirits have a withstand of rank. It's extremely easy for spirit mages to dominate the higher rank spirits with much less effort then anyone else in the game. I'm not in favor of it as written but it is what it is. <br /> <br /> And it's hard to know what the intention with orchema are. They clearly use spirit rules but it doesn't quite say how they work. Also, death and mind shielding also protect from ephermal attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh...<br /> <br /> Ephemerals and Supernals/Abyssals have different rules, don\u2019t they? I mean, they have the simplified Attributes, and are written on the same section, but they work differently. Why is everyone suddenly lumping them together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T06:45:44-07:00","id":1445476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445468#post1445468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see why they wouldn't be subject to that rank ruling because spirits have a withstand of rank. It's extremely easy for spirit mages to dominate the higher rank spirits with much less effort then anyone else in the game. I'm not in favor of it as written but it is what it is.<br /> <br /> And it's hard to know what the intention with orchema are. They clearly use spirit rules but it doesn't quite say how they work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The invisible entities rules are generic. That means that the rules can be used for several different types of beings that aren't the same and doesn't work the same in many other circumstances. Spirits are ephemeral entities who use the invisible entities rules, but they are two steps removed from Supernal beings (1. by being a subset of ephemeral entities, and 2. by Supernal beings not being a type of ephemeral entity) and are bad precedents without additional logic to back it up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, death and mind shielding also protect from ephermal attacks. </div> </div> </div><i>I know:</i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445444#post1445444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, that's assuming you can put up Shielding spells against the attacks of Supernal beings. Shielding spells are generally not supposed to work against attacks, <b>and the few examples we've got are specifically against ephemeral entities.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T07:14:57-07:00","id":1445479,"title":"","content":"Got interested in the topic and evasive about RL stuff I should be doing right now, so I'm skimming through the 2E core books and writing a long post.<br /> <br /> <br /> Demon says the dice is Supernatural Tolerance + the power's own rating <i>or</i> the power's governing Attribute's rating. This seems to be the general rule.<br /> <br /> Werewolf says spirits only roll Rank for Clashes, and only adds its Influence rating if it is actually using one. I'm inclined to interpret this as an exception to the general rule with the following logic; since Manifestations and Numina don't even have dot ratings, and some of them are not dice-rolled at all, that part of the equation just gets axed. It does fit the narrative of werewolves being natural born spirit-hunters. This same narrative could extend to mages, who are the masters of the invisible arts.<br /> <br /> So, yes, mages have an advantage over spirits.... sort of. The Counterspell Numen exists. But I forgot its mechanics at the moment, so I'll leave them be for now. And besides, there's always the question of why a spirit would drive itself into that much of a corner.<br /> <br /> But what about Supernals? Mages may be the masters of the invisible arts, but Supernal entities ARE the invisible arts. So there's no reason to cripple their Clash of Wills dice pool to using solely Rank, unless a rule specifically says so. The rule does not specifically says so, so let's probe further.<br /> <br /> In a 'normal' situation where there's no Clash of Wills involved, the entity rolls Power + Finesse to cast. That's a deceptively large dice pool, as others pointed out. An angry Supernal can toss around uppity mages without much problem.<br /> <br /> Buuuuut if a Clash of Wills would somehow occur, I think the entity would roll Rank + Arcanum, as the general rules. Same as the mage offending it. A considerably smaller dice pool for the Supernal. Now, because the Clash of Wills dice pool isn't actually a spellcasting roll, the mage should not be able to use Yantras to boost them, and neither can the Supernal benefit from boosting its Power or Finesse (they aren't even there!). Okay, so that sounds even.<br /> <br /> But wait, Advanced Potency adds a +1 to the Clash dice pool. The mage has to Reach, and so does the entity, but the latter gets infinite Reach. So the entity is advantageous here.<br /> <br /> Also, the spell's Duration gives bonuses to the Clash pool as well. The maximum is +4, from year-long or indefinite Duration. A year-long Duration requires Advanced Duration and a -8 penalty. Indefinite Duration requires Reaching twice, 1 Mana, and a -10 dice pool. Now, all this dice penalties are the cost of Spell Factors, and thus originally had to come from the <i>spellcasting dice pool</i>, NOT the Clash dice pool. Mages would have to work in lots of Yantras and/or be significantly powerful to get all that dice. Supernals are relatively less burdened, because <i>their </i>original spellcasting dice pool is Power + Finesse, which should be usually larger than what most mages work with. So Supernals have another advantage here.<br /> <br /> One last question, though. Can a mage even cast a Shielding spell that blocks Supernals in general? Since there's no RAW, let's see RAI. We have the Wards and Signs spell, which explicitly adds Withstand ratings against spells than enable a Clash of Wills, in contrast with the anti-ephemera Shielding spells from Spirit, Death, and Mind. The RAI seems to be that there's no such safety against spells and Supernals, or if there is, it shouldn't be easy.<br /> <br /> But wait, we already have ways of no-selling spells; the Counterspell Attainment. It uses the Clash of Wills system, so all the stuff I said above should hold here as well. This seems to be the intended &quot;general Shielding spell&quot; against Supernals. And the Supernals have an advantage, it seems.<br /> <br /> What if the Supernal flat-out decides to punch the mage? Well... why would it? A direct damage spell (the ones that have Potency=Damage) would be much better. And even without 3 dots in an Arcanum (where direct damage spells become accessible), the two-dot Ruling spells offer much creative ways to wound people. Only one dot? Well, the Supernal won't be picking a fight in the first place. A mage could, but good luck dodging the accusations of fellow mages who'd now suspect you're some Scelestus who likes to kill weak Supernals and condemn them to the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  clarity 04-23-2021, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T07:34:14-07:00","id":1445481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445479#post1445479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Supernal flat-out decides to punch the mage? Well... why would it? A direct damage spell (the ones that have Potency=Damage) would be much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would because attack dice pools are Power+Finesse instead of just one Attribute or one Attribute+Rank as for all other mundane actions, and Supernal beings gain Rote Action on all their mundane actions. Spells have the bonus of having bonus steps in the Primary Spell Factor and doesn't have to deal with Defense, but each extra Potency costs 2 dice which could instead roll an average of ~1.13 extra damage for an attack. If the entity happens to be armed (or otherwise is in a form that would deal lethal damage instead of bashing), then straight up attacking will often be much more effective than direct damage spells below Rank 4 (where they finally can deal lethal damage with spells).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T07:37:59-07:00","id":1445483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445481#post1445481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would because attack dice pools are Power+Finesse instead of just one Attribute or one Attribute+Rank as for all other mundane actions, and Supernal beings gain Rote Action on all their mundane actions. Spells have the bonus of having bonus steps in the Primary Spell Factor and doesn't have to deal with Defense, but each extra Potency costs 2 dice which would translate to an average of ~1.13 extra damage for an attack. If the entity happens to be armed (or otherwise is in a form that would deal lethal damage instead of bashing), then straight up attacking will often be much more effective than direct damage spells below Rank 4 (where they finally can deal lethal damage with spells).</div> </div> </div> </div>They got Rote quality on mundane rolls? I must\u2019ve missed that. <br /> <br /> And there was some context where I mentioned normal attacks that made more sense, but, uh, I forgot them. I guess my brain\u2019s trying to close the doors for today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T07:43:36-07:00","id":1445484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445483#post1445483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They got Rote quality on mundane rolls? I must\u2019ve missed that.<br /> <br /> And there was some context where I mentioned normal attacks that made more sense, but, uh, I forgot them. I guess my brain\u2019s trying to close the doors for today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, my bad. It's first at Rank 4 (where they get access to lethal/aggravated damage spells) they get Rote Action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T11:07:58-07:00","id":1445501,"title":"","content":"Hey, it's been a little bit. I'm afraid I am a little sick today, nothing too serious, just some lethargy in body and mind. If my questions are a bit hard to understand, that's probably why.<br /> <br /> 1. What are the limits of remote control? Can it make a non powered object move? Example: Can it make a non powered poseable m<span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">annequin grab someone? Does it have to be electrical power if not? Can a pully system under tension count towards helping it move? If cast with a scale factor, would a mage be able to give orders to objects all at the same time or only one by one?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2. Would it break anything if nodes could have a subtle Arcanum instead of gross? Could a mage in a normal game force a node to display these effects? What would a example subtle node even do?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3. Can a Mage use stored spell to get around the must know the spell? Example: a prime mage who doesn't know life tries to imbue a item with mend, because the have mend as a stored spell. Can a mage use a rote to get extra reach on a imbued item?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">4.Can a blind mage use prime or matter knowing to instantly read a book? Can a blind mage use prime unveiling to navigate around a city by unveiling symbolism?<br /> 5. Why is </span></span></span>Eidolon<span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> making? Should it not be patterning, as it is a more advanced platonic form? Golem, the nearest comparable spell, is patterning.<br /> 6. Lets say a mage gives his nimbus x rote charges, and flares the nimbus, and then the nimbus effects a few people. Would those x charges be spread among the people, or would everyone get x charges?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T11:30:01-07:00","id":1445502,"title":"","content":"Hmm... TempleBuilder, when I try to quote your post it is heavily filled with script instructions that make it hard to partition. Would you know anything that could prevent that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445501#post1445501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. What are the limits of remote control? Can it make a non powered object move? Example: Can it make a non powered poseable m<span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">annequin grab someone? Does it have to be electrical power if not? Can a pully system under tension count towards helping it move? If cast with a scale factor, would a mage be able to give orders to objects all at the same time or only one by one?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's limited mechanical actions of the function. Don't think it needs to be electrical, pneumatic machinery and the like seems like fair game. I think Scale would mean all the intended functions to activate are part of the Imago. Maybe there are occasions where a sequence of instant actions would need to play out, something like combat, but I'd want an example before trying to figure that out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2. Would it break anything if nodes could have a subtle Arcanum instead of gross? Could a mage in a normal game force a node to display these effects? What would a example subtle node even do?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything would break, but I do like the idea that the energy flowing through the node would most effectively contact something physical. I wouldn't know offhand what it might do to Fate or Mind and the like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3. Can a Mage use stored spell to get around the must know the spell? Example: a prime mage who doesn't know life tries to imbue a item with mend, because the have mend as a stored spell. Can a mage use a rote to get extra reach on a imbued item?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><br /> <br /> What do you mean by stored spell here?<br /> <br /> I emphatically think that rotes should not be Imbued.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4.Can a blind mage use prime or matter knowing to instantly read a book? Can a blind mage use prime unveiling to navigate around a city by unveiling symbolism?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <br /> I want to say that a Knowing spell cast on a book will provide a working summary of its contents, but not the total experience of reading it, while an Unveiling will bestow the capacity to perceive its features and information. I think an Unveiling of Prime would convey information about surrounding structures, but not in a manner that readily enables navigation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. Why is</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eidolon[FONT=Google Sans, arial, sans-serif][COLOR=#222222][SIZE=12px] making? Should it not be patterning, as it is a more advanced platonic form? Golem, the nearest comparable spell, is patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Golem is working on a pre-existing subject. I'm happy to go with the idea that a pattern that functions as a living thing with something as obscure as mana as its base requires Making to bring forth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T11:39:19-07:00","id":1445505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445501#post1445501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, it's been a little bit. I'm afraid I am a little sick today, nothing too serious, just some lethargy in body and mind. If my questions are a bit hard to understand, that's probably why.<br /> <br /> 1. What are the limits of remote control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything the device is capable of performing that falls within a single instant action (extended actions with the reach effect).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can it make a non powered object move? </div> </div> </div>It can control a lightswitch and cause a car to shift gears, neither of which are necessarily powered, so yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Example: Can it make a non powered poseable m<span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">annequin grab someone?</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it have to be electrical power if not? Can a pully system under tension count towards helping it move? </div> </div> </div>Anything the object could reasonably do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If cast with a scale factor, would a mage be able to give orders to objects all at the same time or only one by one? </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Everything in the area would receive the exact same command.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2. Would it break anything if nodes could have a subtle Arcanum instead of gross? Could a mage in a normal game force a node to display these effects? What would a example subtle node even do?</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Arguably a Locus is a Spirit Node, a Hallow is a Prime Node, &amp;c.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3. Can a Mage use stored spell to get around the must know the spell? Example: a prime mage who doesn't know life tries to imbue a item with mend, because the have mend as a stored spell.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">No, the Mage still doesn't know the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a mage use a rote to get extra reach on a imbued item? </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> No, Imbuing an item is not a spell and cannot benefit from a Rote. I did come up with the idea of &quot;Schematics&quot; that would have an effect similar to a grimoire but for making Imbued Items, but a regular rote wouldn't apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">4.Can a blind mage use prime or matter knowing to instantly read a book?</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Matter for a physical book, Forces for a digital one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a blind mage use prime unveiling to navigate around a city by unveiling symbolism? </div> </div> </div>No better than they could without Prime Unveiling. Forces and Life would have the easiest time bypassing blindness.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">5. Why is E</span></span></span>idolon<span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> making? Should it not be patterning, as it is a more advanced platonic form? Golem, the nearest comparable spell, is patterning.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Golem</i> animates an extant statue, <i>Eidolon</i> can create a wide range of things from nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. Lets say a mage gives his nimbus x rote charges, and flares the nimbus, and then the nimbus effects a few people. Would those x charges be spread among the people, or would everyone get x charges? </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> The rote quality would be applied to the roll, the number of people <i>a</i>ffected each time is irrelevant. Note: this spell would cost a Mana (as do all spells that grant the rote action quality).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:01:44-07:00","id":1445510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445384#post1445384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It doesn't matter how many dice they throw out when one shield forces clash of wits which on normal attacks is reduced to rank with influence it's increased to rank + influence.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Clash of Wills forced by Shielding spells only work a number of times equal to the spell's Potency, and then the spell ends prematurely. Unless the mage is very well prepared, it's probably a good idea to not get into a battle of attrition with something that has Corpus above 10 and dice pools between 15 and 30.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Granted supernal beings can also cast spells but without it, they'll be equal or losing against a mage.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They're not ephemeral.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A mage with an advanced shielding that lasts one month can with 3 gnosis and 3 prime/spirit/mind whatever +4 flash dice.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Prime Shielding does not force Clash of Wills, it provides added Withstand against Supernal magic. An opponent that rolls an exceptional success on spellcasting can ignore Withstand.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So a starting base mage can equal a rank 5 beings powers and double their dice with their normal attacks and numina.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think that doesn't consider some creative applications of the Mass Create Influence, things that might make the environment surrounding the mage more perilous. I should think that Clash of Wills based on Rank is not about making it trivial to overcome such beings, but to ensure that they cannot be easily obliterated by such hefty dice pools. Make it a slightly more even contest.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since all ephemeral spirits have a withstand of rank, it's also rather easy for a mage to use a spell to shut them down without much trouble.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Alternatively, it becomes necessary to spend a few turns making the spell with the necessary Potency have a dice pool that will reliably return a success, in which case the target can interrupt or get out of sensory range.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epiemetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ochema kill cabals though because they tend to be 6+ beings in the exarches case.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I should think that's a violation of the Pax Arcanum, and unnecessary for a being capable of casting Unmaking spells that can probably roll exceptional successes frequently enough to make defences worthless.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It has occurred to me that Ochemata likely have Bans and Banes, which may be integral in opposing them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's extremely easy for spirit mages to dominate the higher rank spirits with much less effort then anyone else in the game.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I think this perspective does not give full consideration to not only the strains of casting spells of high Potency and long duration (including Paradox and mana expenditure), but the matter of obstacles to even being in the presence of Rank 4 and 5 entities (and while in their presence, what they might do while the mage is in the process of casting the spell).<br /> <br /> Plus the greater implications. Messing around with a high Rank Goetia can have effects in the psychology of the world at large. High Rank spirits are part of an ecology and a political scene that will respond if mages disrupt it too much.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:33:50-07:00","id":1445515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445510#post1445510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Clash of Wills forced by Shielding spells only work a number of times equal to the spell's Potency, and then the spell ends prematurely. Unless the mage is very well prepared, it's probably a good idea to not get into a battle of attrition with something that has Corpus above 10 and dice pools between 15 and 30.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Quick note: The Potency condition was removed from all such spells during the process of the book. It's still present in the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines, but considering their removal from the very spells they'd specifically affect it's almost certainly intended for such spells not to fizzle out after Potency uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:42:12-07:00","id":1445518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445502#post1445502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... TempleBuilder, when I try to quote your post it is heavily filled with script instructions that make it hard to partition. Would you know anything that could prevent that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am afraid I know very little about computers in general and forums in particular. I think that I copied Eidolon then pasted it into a word document and then copied it from there and pasted into the post. I will refrain from doing that again. I apologize for the inconvenience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445502#post1445502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it's limited mechanical actions of the function. Don't think it needs to be electrical, pneumatic machinery and the like seems like fair game. I think Scale would mean all the intended functions to activate are part of the Imago. Maybe there are occasions where a sequence of instant actions would need to play out, something like combat, but I'd want an example before trying to figure that out.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you, that\u2019s pretty much what I wanted to know. I just wanted to see if I could make a horror movie moment when all the dolls start reaching for someone. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445502#post1445502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anything would break, but I do like the idea that the energy flowing through the node would most effectively contact something physical. I wouldn't know offhand what it might do to Fate or Mind and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was planning on them being rarer. The effects are so minor, I would say something like a 9-again on fated rolls, and maybe memories become easier to remember.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445502#post1445502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by stored spell here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the spell in signs of sorcery, where it keeps another spell inside of it, and a mage can then spend a mana to cast as though they cast it themselves. I thought it might be a loophole in the imbued items rules, that I would like to be able to argue against as I don\u2019t believe it to be intended.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445502#post1445502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I emphatically think that rotes should not be Imbued.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445502#post1445502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say that a Knowing spell cast on a book will provide a working summary of its contents, but not the total experience of reading it, while an Unveiling will bestow the capacity to perceive its features and information. I think an Unveiling of Prime would convey information about surrounding structures, but not in a manner that readily enables navigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just driving when I realized how much of a city we cover in painted symbolism, from language to road signs and markings. Shops usually have signs that symbolize their names. A blind mage could potentially make their way around to various locations using this method.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445502#post1445502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Golem is working on a pre-existing subject. I'm happy to go with the idea that a pattern that functions as a living thing with something as obscure as mana as its base requires Making to bring forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but how is that different from platonic form? The symbol of that form didn\u2019t exist a moment ago, or if it did, why is eidolon different? At least from my understanding, both should be making then. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything the device is capable of performing that falls within a single instant action (extended actions with the reach effect).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can control a lightswitch and cause a car to shift gears, neither of which are necessarily powered, so yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, alright. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything the object could reasonably do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it\u2019s that reasonable part that is tricky to me as magic already breaks the laws of physics.<br /> [/SIZE][/COLOR][/FONT]<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything in the area would receive the exact same command.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Not ideal but workable. Could extra reach allow different commands to different objects?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably a Locus is a Spirit Node, a Hallow is a Prime Node, &amp;c.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I\u2019m not sure that is the case, nodes are often aligned with Hallows and Locus, but they are different things. Maybe a spirit one would allow a mage to see spirit twilight when attuned. I think a prime one should be a yantra, maybe a plus 2? They seem rare enough to qualify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">[SIZE=12px]No, the Mage still doesn't know the spell.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Google Sans, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><br /> I will use this argument if this ever comes up.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Imbuing an item is not a spell and cannot benefit from a Rote. I did come up with the idea of &quot;Schematics&quot; that would have an effect similar to a grimoire but for making Imbued Items, but a regular rote wouldn't apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that in the creative thaumaturgy thread?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Matter for a physical book, Forces for a digital one.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> Words are symbols, right? Prime can\u2019t show symbols to a mage?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No better than they could without Prime Unveiling. Forces and Life would have the easiest time bypassing blindness.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span>Well, if prime can show symbols, and humanity continues to create symbols through words and symbolic objects. It might make navigation a little easier. If that\u2019s not the case, then my argument is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[FONT=Google Sans, arial, sans-serif][COLOR=#222222][SIZE=12px]<i>Golem</i> animates an extant statue, <i>Eidolon</i> can create a wide range of things from nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, fair. But then how does plutonic form work? You also create something out of \u201cnothing\u201d if Tass and Mana don\u2019t count. If both are different, then what stops a mage from animating a plutonic form statue?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445505#post1445505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rote quality would be applied to the roll, the number of people <i>a</i>ffected each time is irrelevant. Note: this spell would cost a Mana (as do all spells that grant the rote action quality).</div> </div> </div> </div>alright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:53:09-07:00","id":1445523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445518#post1445518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am afraid I know very little about computers in general and forums in particular. I think that I copied Eidolon then pasted it into a word document and then copied it from there and pasted into the post. I will refrain from doing that again. I apologize for the inconvenience.</div> </div> </div> </div>What happened was that you brought the formatting of the text from the other program into the forum which translates it to equivalent BBCode tags.<br /> <br /> To avoid it in the future, just use CTRL+SHIFT+V when pasting back into the forum. That pastes only the raw text without formatting. Can be quite useful in other circumstances as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T13:25:01-07:00","id":1445527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445518#post1445518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it\u2019s that reasonable part that is tricky to me as magic already breaks the laws of physics.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Remote Control</i> is a Compelling spell, which means it's limited to what's possible. If you could make the subject of the spell do what you want using a minimal amount of physical force and no tools then <i>Remote Control</i> should be able to do it.<br /> <br /> Making a mannequin with moveable joints grab someone is likely within the bounds of the spell, making that mannequin do acrobatics and start sword fighting is not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cool. Not ideal but workable. Could extra reach allow different commands to different objects? </div> </div> </div>Probably.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well I\u2019m not sure that is the case, nodes are often aligned with Hallows and Locus, but they are different things. Maybe a spirit one would allow a mage to see spirit twilight when attuned. I think a prime one should be a yantra, maybe a plus 2? They seem rare enough to qualify. </div> </div> </div>Obviously they're different things, but since Subtle Arcana Nodes aren't described, I'm saying that Hallows, Loci, &amp;c are the logical equivalent.<br /> <br /> You can do what you want in your game, but I wouldn't use what you're suggesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was that in the creative thaumaturgy thread? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Words are symbols, right? Prime can\u2019t show symbols to a mage? </div> </div> </div>Prime Knowing on a book would reveal the symbolic themes of the book. If it's a textbook you'd get the symbols relevant to the subject, if it was a work of fiction you'd get the symbols of what the book was trying to convey: lessons, morals, cultural references, what have you.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't let you just read the book.<br /> <br /> I would be funny, though, because you'd know <i>what</i> the author was trying to say, but not how they said it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, if prime can show symbols, and humanity continues to create symbols through words and symbolic objects. It might make navigation a little easier. If that\u2019s not the case, then my argument is irrelevant. </div> </div> </div>Prime would be able to tell you what any symbols you see <i>mean</i> (&quot;Food Here,&quot; &quot;Bathroom,&quot; &quot;Restricted Area&quot;), but wouldn't help you just walk around without bumping into people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, fair. But then how does plutonic form work? You also create something out of \u201cnothing\u201d if Tass and Mana don\u2019t count. If both are different, then what stops a mage from animating a plutonic form statue? </div> </div> </div>*Platonic. <i>Platonic Form</i> creates a simple object (or a complex one with a reach) that completely falls apart once it's out of Mana and burns through Mana with every use, <i>Eidolon </i>maintains its shape.<br /> <br /> Nothing stops a Mage from making a <i>Platonic Form</i> robot if they have Prime 3, but <i>Eidolon</i> is generally going to be better. Also, <i>Eidolon </i>has fewer limits than <i>Platonic Form</i>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:29:57-07:00","id":1445544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445527#post1445527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Remote Control</i> is a Compelling spell, which means it's limited to what's possible. If you could make the subject of the spell do what you want using a minimal amount of physical force and no tools then <i>Remote Control</i> should be able to do it.<br /> <br /> Making a mannequin with moveable joints grab someone is likely within the bounds of the spell, making that mannequin do acrobatics and start sword fighting is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that\u2019s a useful boundary, because it\u2019s not in the nature of mannequins to sword fight. I can work with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445527#post1445527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously they're different things, but since Subtle Arcana Nodes aren't described, I'm saying that Hallows, Loci, &amp;c are the logical equivalent.<br /> <br /> You can do what you want in your game, but I wouldn't use what you're suggesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, honestly the problem is that nodes have almost completely narrative effects, and are so situational that they can probably be safely forgotten about. My discontentment with Hallows and Locus is that they don\u2019t fit in with making plants grow faster, or plus two to initiative. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445527#post1445527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445527#post1445527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime Knowing on a book would reveal the symbolic themes of the book. If it's a textbook you'd get the symbols relevant to the subject, if it was a work of fiction you'd get the symbols of what the book was trying to convey: lessons, morals, cultural references, what have you.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't let you just read the book.<br /> <br /> I would be funny, though, because you'd know <i>what</i> the author was trying to say, but not how they said it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I can see a awakened art critic/snob that casually understands what a creator meant, and only judges a work based on that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445527#post1445527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime would be able to tell you what any symbols you see <i>mean</i> (&quot;Food Here,&quot; &quot;Bathroom,&quot; &quot;Restricted Area&quot;), but wouldn't help you just walk around without bumping into people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, other people. The bane of my existence. Had forgotten about them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445527#post1445527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Platonic. <i>Platonic Form</i> creates a simple object (or a complex one with a reach) that completely falls apart once it's out of Mana and burns through Mana with every use, <i>Eidolon </i>maintains its shape.<br /> <br /> Nothing stops a Mage from making a <i>Platonic Form</i> robot if they have Prime 3, but <i>Eidolon</i> is generally going to be better. Also, <i>Eidolon </i>has fewer limits than <i>Platonic Form</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops. I really should have consulted the book for the name.<br /> <br /> Nitpick: actually Platonic Form doesn\u2019t actually consume mana per use unless the mage spends potency to make it do so.<br /> <br /> I had forgotten about Platonic Form dissolving when out of mana, and that Eidolon doesn\u2019t. Now that I\u2019m reading the spells, it says that Platonic Form weaves Tass and Mana together to make a object. That forms a pattern of a object, but it is still Mana. Eidolon flat out makes the pattern, leaving it without Mana does nothing then as it\u2019s not made of Mana. I still say there is probably a patterning spell that acts like Golem for Platonic Form, but it\u2019s honestly probably not worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T15:22:22-07:00","id":1445552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445515#post1445515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quick note: The Potency condition was removed from all such spells during the process of the book. It's still present in the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines, but considering their removal from the very spells they'd specifically affect it's almost certainly intended for such spells not to fizzle out after Potency uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also removed the potency limit to a lot of spells that were limited to arcanum dots right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-23-2021, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T17:14:50-07:00","id":1445573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445515#post1445515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quick note: The Potency condition was removed from all such spells during the process of the book. It's still present in the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines, but considering their removal from the very spells they'd specifically affect it's almost certainly intended for such spells not to fizzle out after Potency uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is based only on an inference rather than something that a writer ever said, I'd be of a mind to discount it.<br /> <br /> After all, an alternative reason to not redundantly repeat a condition every time it comes up is that eats up a lot of word count in a book that, with a great many concepts to establish and detail compared to most other Chronicles of Darkness core books, needs all the words it can get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T01:56:34-07:00","id":1445630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445573#post1445573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is based only on an inference rather than something that a writer ever said, I'd be of a mind to discount it.<br /> <br /> After all, an alternative reason to not redundantly repeat a condition every time it comes up is that eats up a lot of word count in a book that, with a great many concepts to establish and detail compared to most other Chronicles of Darkness core books, needs all the words it can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>1.) I'm pretty sure word count was already accounted for when they first were included.<br /> <br /> 2.) It's really weird only that particular thing was removed from spells as opposed to basically every other repeated aspect of many spells.<br /> <br /> 3.) Removing that limitation from the texts of those spells means those spells simply doesn't have that limitation. It's not just an option that you could read somewhere else you could slap on to certain spells (like, say, the preserved Reach option for those very same spells to protect against mundane attacks made by ephemeral entities, or the constant &quot;Add Death/Mind/Spirit to also affect the other types of ephemeral entities with this Death/Mind/Spirit spell&quot; options); it's an integral part of how the spell works.<br /> <br /> 4.) The removal of the limitation from those spells was the absolutely latest edit relating to that topic. It's far more reasonable to assume that when the spells are reworked to function differently, that's how the spells are supposed to work and the text in the guidelines being outdated. After all, it's much more likely the writer forgot to change one instance of a rule that's written in four places rather than the writer changing the three places where that rule is applicable with the assumption that the player would know to apply the rule from the guideline to the spells that aren't written to work according to that rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T16:06:18-07:00","id":1445726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1445630#post1445630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1.) I'm pretty sure word count was already accounted for when they first were included.<br /> <br /> 2.) It's really weird only that particular thing was removed from spells as opposed to basically every other repeated aspect of many spells.<br /> <br /> 3.) Removing that limitation from the texts of those spells means those spells simply doesn't have that limitation. It's not just an option that you could read somewhere else you could slap on to certain spells (like, say, the preserved Reach option for those very same spells to protect against mundane attacks made by ephemeral entities, or the constant &quot;Add Death/Mind/Spirit to also affect the other types of ephemeral entities with this Death/Mind/Spirit spell&quot; options); it's an integral part of how the spell works.<br /> <br /> 4.) The removal of the limitation from those spells was the absolutely latest edit relating to that topic. It's far more reasonable to assume that when the spells are reworked to function differently, that's how the spells are supposed to work and the text in the guidelines being outdated. After all, it's much more likely the writer forgot to change one instance of a rule that's written in four places rather than the writer changing the three places where that rule is applicable with the assumption that the player would know to apply the rule from the guideline to the spells that aren't written to work according to that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a really convoluted and kind of obscure way of saying that a prior complete and published draft of the core had the Shielding spells state that they had a &quot;per Potency&quot; limit that id not present in the currently available version?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm going to leave this post as I initially wrote it as an expression of taking responsibility, but reading posts elsewhere on this forum has reminded me that speaking in such terse and irritable fashion does conversation no favours. For this, I apologise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-24-2021, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T09:12:58-07:00","id":1446106,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to transform other supernatural fuels into Mana?<br /> Like, Vitae, Glamour, Essence, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T09:21:06-07:00","id":1446108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446106#post1446106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to transform other supernatural fuels into Mana?<br /> Like, Vitae, Glamour, Essence, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Essence is Prime 4 + Spirit 4 for Spirit-flavored Essence, Prime 4 + Death 4 for Ghost flavored Essence, and Prime 4 + Mind 4 for Goetia-flavored Essence.<br /> <br /> Glamor would be Prime 4 + Fate 4 + Mind ?, probably Mind 2 or 3 based on the spells in <i>Dark Eras 2</i>.<br /> <br /> Vitae is more complicated; my gut instinct is Prime 4 + Life 4 + Space 2/3 (based on the Tamers of Blood Legacy and properties of Vitae), but you could probably argue Prime 4 + Death 4 or Prime 4 + Life 4.<br /> <br /> Plasm would be Prime 4 + Death 4, since it's just Ectoplasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T10:49:41-07:00","id":1446119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446108#post1446108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae is more complicated; my gut instinct is Prime 4 + Life 4 + Space 2/3 (based on the Tamers of Blood Legacy and properties of Vitae)</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitae has a capacity to change or create or transmit relationships sure, but I think even First Edition standards wouldn't have gotten that granular in terms of what properties a thing possesses before you can affect or transform it, and Second Edition certainly doesn't. If it did I think questions of Essence would get unnecessarily complicated by needing to account for Resonance and the like. If the Tamers of Blood has anything else to do with Space, I should think that's particular to their applications of sympathetic magic rather than something concerning the subject of blood.<br /> <br /> Besides, it should always be remembered that Vitae is not the blood itself, but an energy carried within the blood but native to the vampire. I think that's worth considering in comparison to mages who might deal more in actual blood.<br /> <br /> I find myself thinking that regular magic can convert Vitae into Mana, but the process in reverse (either for the sake of vampires or to satisfy a personal addiction to the stuff) eludes them. But that's based in my interpretation that the origin of Vitae is in a transmutation elicited by the vampiric template (compared to at least Essence, which is an extant part of the world). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T10:57:04-07:00","id":1446121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446119#post1446119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vitae has a capacity to change or create or transmit relationships sure, but I think even First Edition standards wouldn't have gotten that granular in terms of what properties a thing possesses before you can affect or transform it, and Second Edition certainly doesn't. If it did I think questions of Essence would get unnecessarily complicated by needing to account for Resonance and the like. If the Tamers of Blood has anything else to do with Space, I should think that's particular to their applications of sympathetic magic rather than something concerning the subject of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the argument, and I don't disagree with it; I'm just basing my ballpark on the Fate + Mind requirement for Changeling related stuff. Re: Resonance, that's already covered by Prime, so it's accounted for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, it should always be remembered that Vitae is not the blood itself, but an energy carried within the blood but native to the vampire. I think that's worth considering in comparison to mages who might deal more in actual blood.<br /> <br /> I find myself thinking that regular magic can convert Vitae into Mana, but the process in reverse (either for the sake of vampires or to satisfy a personal addiction to the stuff) eludes them. But that's based in my interpretation that the origin of Vitae is in a transmutation elicited by the vampiric template (compared to at least Essence, which is an extant part of the world). </div> </div> </div>I don't think there are any other examples of things being asymmetric in such a fashion with regards to Supernal Magic, if you can convert it one direction you can convert it the other direction.<br /> <br /> If you do run it that way, it'd be a huge Mystery.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T16:38:55-07:00","id":1446189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446121#post1446121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there are any other examples of things being asymmetric in such a fashion with regards to Supernal Magic, if you can convert it one direction you can convert it the other direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's kind of like... you can turn vampires into lawnchairs but you can't turn lawnchairs into vampires.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's an argument that you can only turn a vampire into a lawnchair that can still use its Disciplines and the like, but depending on exactly what powers it has I think there's an argument to be made that you can give it a form that wouldn't logically be able to apply them. You can multiple Speed with Celerity, but six times the zero that an inanimate object can move is still zero*.<br /> <br /> That's getting off track a bit, but I think it conveys the idea of being able to grasp certain qualities of the template and converting them into something widely applicable while things that entail creating the actual nature of the template are Imperial. Come to think of it, a better example might by how Patterning Time can be used to rewrite a vampire's history to ensure that they weren't Embraced but probably can't be used to write a human's history to one in which they were.<br /> <br /> And I'm thinking this qualifies for Vitae more than it does Essence or even Glamour just because that's a particular kind of energy that is never really external to a vampire and exactly where it comes from is kind of ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Mind, this is the kind of logic where I'd also think that letting the Vitae be something that can be targeted for draining and conversion is generous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do run it that way, it'd be a huge Mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a facet of the mystery that is vampires themselves.<br /> <br /> * Although, Clash of Wills might apply... I mean the vampire is already an animating force for something naturally immobile, it's not a huge stretch that it could compel an object to move at least a bit.. I think it still gets the idea across.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T17:38:40-07:00","id":1446199,"title":"","content":"If, on the other hand, vitae is a vital force contained within the living that vampires and strix are uniquely capable of extracting, it\u2019s either Life, Death, or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T08:58:21-07:00","id":1446611,"title":"","content":"Only a few questions today, mostly opinions.<br /> 1. Would creating merits that require a legacy to gain be a good idea for a setting that places more emphasis on legacies? <br /> 1.5. Would alternate or secondary attainments be a better idea?<br /> 2. Are there any ways to get into contact with the lower depths in 2e, or summon something from a specific lower depth?<br /> 3. Would anyone like to see the singers in silence redone for 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T09:33:03-07:00","id":1446617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446611#post1446611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only a few questions today, mostly opinions.<br /> 1. Would creating merits that require a legacy to gain be a good idea for a setting that places more emphasis on legacies? <br /> 1.5. Would alternate or secondary attainments be a better idea?<br /> 2. Are there any ways to get into contact with the lower depths in 2e, or summon something from a specific lower depth?<br /> 3. Would anyone like to see the singers in silence redone for 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>1: Merits can have such a wide range of effects that it\u2019s really hard to answer this question. Sure, if you added a merit - something like Mystery Cult maybe - it could emphasize the prominence of legacies. Having an extraordinarily enticing unique merit for each legacy might be a little ambitious, though.<br /> 1.5: that can also be a way of emphasizing that legacies give you unique, badass powers.<br /> 1: ....But legacies have a whole lot of useful stuff already. It\u2019s pretty well worth it for any character. In my experience, if a player doesn\u2019t go for a legacy, it\u2019s often because they\u2019re still trying to figure out the system\u2019s mechanic is general, and aren\u2019t ready for another layer of complexity. That, or, legacies can feel like a super special personalization, and they may not feel like they know their character or the direction of the game well enough to commit to that.<br /> Without knowing what your goals are for emphasizing legacies, I recommend focusing on the \u2018fluff side\u2019. Give every NPC a legacy, make them networks of mentors and allies, make each one a mystery. Have several legacies for each character that have a hook for their specialties. Emphasize that it\u2019s the true way mages discover the Supernal, and that it\u2019s their best way to push back against the Lie.<br /> <br /> 2: Most lower depths have *a* means of intrusion that can be used to summon or contact them, but these are entirely unique to each realm... because each realm is totally unique. There\u2019s no formal or shared process, like summoning Supernals. The realms are not actually related to each other in any way; \u201clower depth\u201d just means \u201cwe aren\u2019t really sure, but it seems hungry.\u201d Figuring out how to contact or summon from one is a Mystery - probably following up on an intrusion that already happened \u201cnaturally\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T11:37:04-07:00","id":1446637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446611#post1446611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1. Would creating merits that require a legacy to gain be a good idea for a setting that places more emphasis on legacies?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's reasonable for there to be some Merits that represent a bit of particular focus or insight provided by the Legacy that is in keeping with the structure of other Mage specific Merits. Not for every Legacy, but if it's fitting why not.<br /> <br /> As far as &quot;good idea&quot; goes, I think such things would work best as benefits that only members of the Legacy would really want or benefit from. Not broadly applicable things that a player interested in optimization would be weighing and measuring. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.5. Would alternate or secondary attainments be a better idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here do you mean the powers called Legacy Attainments, or the Attainments that come from having Arcana levels?<br /> <br /> I feel as though a magical thing a Legacy member would benefit from innately and permanently would be best modelled as one of their actual Attainment powers rather than anything else. It's perfectly fine for a character to develop the Legacy down an alternative path (although it still needs to be a variation on the core idea that they initiated into; an Eleventh Question mage might decide they want the Third Attainment to be something other than specialized Divination, but still focused on investigation to uncover mysteries).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Are there any ways to get into contact with the lower depths in 2e, or summon something from a specific lower depth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Contacting the Lower Depths is described as being possible with the Irises called Scars, but the general rule is that the nature of those deprived realities breaks down all non-native entities who go into them. Either that or a human would be in drastic danger from the absence of something they need to remain alive.<br /> <br /> Before anything else, I think that summoning things from a Lower Depth is going to encounter the limitation inherent to all such spells; if the targeted entity is not within sensory range, calling it must be cast sympathetically (and if not in the same realm of existence, might require additional Arcana to target that realm)*. How would you propose to form the level of association for even a weak sympathetic connection to a Lower Depths entity?<br /> <br /> Lower Depths can be very different from one another, so some might have a form of reality cohesive enough to be targeted with certain Arcana and some do not. The dangers inherent to Scars and limits of analysing them probably means that most of the time when a mage encounters an Iris they conclude leads to a Lower Depth, it's hard to even know what's on the other side let alone figure out what Arcana, if any, are good for trying to do anything with it. If they do know that, they might be capable of issuing a general summons to something on the immediate other side of a Scar. <br /> <br /> Even with a sympathetic connection and knowledge of compatible Arcana, I think it wouldn't be possible to summon a known entity that is currently residing in its home while you have no door to it. Summoning from the Shadow is different because it exists in a pervasive parallel to the material realm, separated &quot;only&quot; by the Gauntlet (of varying strength to Withstand the spell). A Lower Depth (and the Underworld, for that matter) might be seen as functionally having Gauntlets of infinite strength, impossible to cast spells through.<br /> <br /> It's a bit easier in the case of things from Lower Depths that are active in the world already. If one regards the Strix as originating from a Lower Depth, then summoning them can be a matter of having Death magic that targets shadows or shadow beings which are Potent enough to overcome their Resistance. But again, doing that on anything other than a Strix within sensory range requires sympathetic magic. Although I think in their case they'd experience it less as a compelling call to another presence and more like the entity being forcefully dragged. I think commanding a strix would require a separate spell, and be a perilous proposition in any event. And the Strix might be among the more comprehensible Lower Depths entities.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, there may be cases where a mage has learned of some Mystery, some procedure or ritual that keys into a quality of a Lower Depth or its inhabitants that would call upon them without use of the Arcana. If one learns of such methods, I'd say they are used at one's peril.<br /> <br /> I would think that the overall attitude towards Lower Depths in the dedicated summoning lore of the Awakened is &quot;it's a really bad idea to trying calling upon entities that you have a poor understanding of&quot;, and so generally discouraged.<br /> <br /> * Summoning from the Astral differs from this, but that's a matter of the relationship it has with the rest of the world. The Anima Mundi is always inside of you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Would anyone like to see the singers in silence redone for 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure I'd like to see all of the Legacies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T13:24:08-07:00","id":1446649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's reasonable for there to be some Merits that represent a bit of particular focus or insight provided by the Legacy that is in keeping with the structure of other Mage specific Merits. Not for every Legacy, but if it's fitting why not.<br /> <br /> As far as &quot;good idea&quot; goes, I think such things would work best as benefits that only members of the Legacy would really want or benefit from. Not broadly applicable things that a player interested in optimization would be weighing and measuring.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, this is for a hypothetical setting where the orders never quite managed to organize themselves...and the silver ladder is outright missing thanks to some archmastery or exarch level reality warping. In the setting legacies fill the same role as orders for the most part. Since orders have merits due to their size, (and having people ascend with their symbolism), I figured legacies would have them too. The extremely narrow merits is great advice, it both makes sense and helps with creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here do you mean the powers called Legacy Attainments, or the Attainments that come from having Arcana levels?<br /> <br /> I feel as though a magical thing a Legacy member would benefit from innately and permanently would be best modelled as one of their actual Attainment powers rather than anything else. It's perfectly fine for a character to develop the Legacy down an alternative path (although it still needs to be a variation on the core idea that they initiated into; an Eleventh Question mage might decide they want the Third Attainment to be something other than specialized Divination, but still focused on investigation to uncover mysteries).</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess a mix of both. The idea is certain large legacies have broad themes, and rather specific attainments. Secondary attainments would be attainments one could only after earning the main path of attainments and would have smaller and narrower attainments. For example, a mage focused on bio tech and another on artificial intelligence would have different secondary attainments, but still be transhuman engineers and have main attainments as such.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contacting the Lower Depths is described as being possible with the Irises called Scars, but the general rule is that the nature of those deprived realities breaks down all non-native entities who go into them. Either that or a human would be in drastic danger from the absence of something they need to remain alive.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like a emanation realm.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before anything else, I think that summoning things from a Lower Depth is going to encounter the limitation inherent to all such spells; if the targeted entity is not within sensory range, calling it must be cast sympathetically (and if not in the same realm of existence, might require additional Arcana to target that realm)*. How would you propose to form the level of association for even a weak sympathetic connection to a Lower Depths entity?</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe use what it is missing as bait, with some mana to make it even more attractive by reinforcing the symbolism? When something notices, pull the line up. Maybe you might catch something that way.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lower Depths can be very different from one another, so some might have a form of reality cohesive enough to be targeted with certain Arcana and some do not. The dangers inherent to Scars and limits of analysing them probably means that most of the time when a mage encounters an Iris they conclude leads to a Lower Depth, it's hard to even know what's on the other side let alone figure out what Arcana, if any, are good for trying to do anything with it. If they do know that, they might be capable of issuing a general summons to something on the immediate other side of a Scar.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, actually getting into a lower depth is in my mind similarly to going into the Supernal, or the Abyss. It might be possible, but you will die or worse in process.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with a sympathetic connection and knowledge of compatible Arcana, I think it wouldn't be possible to summon a known entity that is currently residing in its home while you have no door to it. Summoning from the Shadow is different because it exists in a pervasive parallel to the material realm, separated &quot;only&quot; by the Gauntlet (of varying strength to Withstand the spell). A Lower Depth (and the Underworld, for that matter) might be seen as functionally having Gauntlets of infinite strength, impossible to cast spells through.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s good analysis. What about at a scar, equivalent to a locus? Would that have a Effective Gauntlets strength of zero?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bit easier in the case of things from Lower Depths that are active in the world already. If one regards the Strix as originating from a Lower Depth, then summoning them can be a matter of having Death magic that targets shadows or shadow beings which are Potent enough to overcome their Resistance. But again, doing that on anything other than a Strix within sensory range requires sympathetic magic. Although I think in their case they'd experience it less as a compelling call to another presence and more like the entity being forcefully dragged. I think commanding a strix would require a separate spell, and be a perilous proposition in any event. And the Strix might be among the more comprehensible Lower Depths entities.</div> </div> </div> </div> The bait idea seems like a even better idea for something like a positive relationship, but requires very specific knowledge that most mages wouldn\u2019t have. Could a mage directly effect a entity from the depths with the arcanum of the missing reality? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, there may be cases where a mage has learned of some Mystery, some procedure or ritual that keys into a quality of a Lower Depth or its inhabitants that would call upon them without use of the Arcana. If one learns of such methods, I'd say they are used at one's peril.</div> </div> </div> </div> It\u2019s interesting, because fallen magic seems better suited to dealing with the depths than supernal magic. That\u2019s probably intentional, as the lie supposedly separates the fallen world and the supernal.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that the overall attitude towards Lower Depths in the dedicated summoning lore of the Awakened is &quot;it's a really bad idea to trying calling upon entities that you have a poor understanding of&quot;, and so generally discouraged.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, yeah. The thing is people, and thereby mages are crazy. There is a legacy about sticking a abyssal parasite in your body, mages do foolish things with horrifying consequences all the time. Somebody will at some point think that summoning a thing hungry for a piece of reality is a good idea.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Summoning from the Astral differs from this, but that's a matter of the relationship it has with the rest of the world. The Anima Mundi is always inside of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the various realms invisible relationship to the fallen world is very interesting. The way it informs the rest of the game is interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446637#post1446637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure I'd like to see all of the Legacies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> ok, it\u2019s added to the queue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T16:54:23-07:00","id":1446685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446649#post1446649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a emanation realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the sense of limited access (although some Legacies have innate access, like the Walkers in Mists to... the Mists), but they're vastly more survivable. Like, some of them have native communities of humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe use what it is missing as bait, with some mana to make it even more attractive by reinforcing the symbolism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bait makes sense. An appropriate Prime spell might make it more enticing, depending on the nature of the place. I wouldn't think Lower Depths are necessarily working on the same symbolic logic as the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Still, even with that there could be cases where what the Depth wants is difficult for mages to present and the inhabitants might not be lured. Like, if you can find a passage to Duat, might be a bad idea to try actively messing about with Sekhem in front of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s good analysis. What about at a scar, equivalent to a locus? Would that have a Effective Gauntlets strength of zero?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I said there. It seems to be consistent that being in the presence of an Iris lets you cast spells unimpeded to the other side. Although I think Irises might need to be unlocked with their Keys before they can be cast through. Ways into the Shadow, Underworld and probably Emanations can be unlocked with spells, but I think most Scars would not afford such an option.<br /> <br /> Oh hey, it says that some of those portals let one hear entities on the other side begging to be raised. That might afford some insight into bringing them over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a mage directly effect a entity from the depths with the arcanum of the missing reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could vary. Sometimes the Arcanum might compel them with what they're missing, sometimes it might be that their Patterns lack anything for the Arcanum to interact with it, sometimes what the Depth lacks might be more complex or esoteric than Awakened spells typically interact with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s interesting, because fallen magic seems better suited to dealing with the depths than supernal magic. That\u2019s probably intentional, as the lie supposedly separates the fallen world and the supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe. The term &quot;Fallen magic&quot; can cover a lot of disparate elements. It's like the descriptions in the Fallen Worlds section of the core book; mages encounter loads of things that don't map directly to the Supernal, the Abyss or even other realms they have some conception of, and they debate the question of how all these things relate to one another. Some of it are the Lies contradictions or ways that it's flawed, some of it is qualities slipping in from unknown dimensions (not all of which qualify as Lower Depths to them), some of it seems to arise naturally from the Fallen World itself and have means of rising to greater power. It's all weird and messy.<br /> <br /> I would think that no mage who is dedicated to the study of Lower Depths would feel confident with a broad declaration about which form of magic better engages with them (or even necessarily whether a given Mystery that they might respond to qualifies as magic) because they ultimately recognise that the ones that are known of are too many and varied to make such a broad generalisation, and there are plenty that are unknown. And I expect there's a big argument about whether or not the Lower Depths precede the Lie/Abyss* and what such a thing might say about their nature (maybe they're far enough from Supernal purity that the Lie doesn't even actually reach them).<br /> <br /> * I think there's plenty of debate among mages about whether the Abyss actually predates becoming a barrier of separation from the Supernal. There are plenty of Scelesti who regard it as the original and most authentic expression of reality, even it was held back by the solid reality that blossomed in its heart before the Fall provided means of insinuation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah. The thing is people, and thereby mages are crazy. There is a legacy about sticking a abyssal parasite in your body, mages do foolish things with horrifying consequences all the time. Somebody will at some point think that summoning a thing hungry for a piece of reality is a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>People like that would be why the manuals need to include the warnings, sure. Still, I think the more dangerous mage is the one who has held back carefully and made an extensive study of a subject and feels confident that they know what they're doing; the texts didn't say &quot;don't mess around with this at all&quot;. Therefore hubris. The Mysterium has Censoriums for a reason; you never throw any discovery away no matter how deleterious, you keep it for the study of people who you're sure will handle it safely and not abuse it. Proper handling can be <i>a</i> way to describe what they do with it next.<br /> <br /> Mages can be scariest not when they act with ignorance but with a certainty that they're in the know which is not entirely displaced. This isn't Things Man Was Not Meant to Know, it's Things Man Knows and Therefore Has Licence to Use.<br /> <br /> Saying we should leave all of this stuff well alone... sounds like Banisher talk to me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the various realms invisible relationship to the fallen world is very interesting. The way it informs the rest of the game is interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Need to buy the rest of the Second Edition cores...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T04:04:15-07:00","id":1446772,"title":"","content":"I think it's also worth considering that the definition of a Lower Depth can be mages categorising something they encounter according to a frame of reference that is most intuitive to them, but might not exactly be an accurate description of that world's deal. They get impressions about Duat and how the Judges direct the Arisen to channel Sekhem into it and think &quot;ah, Sekhem is something fundamental that the realm lacks and hungers for&quot;, and that's a fairly understandable way for them to see it. The Judges might view the nature of themselves and their realm and how that drives their agendas differently. The mages aren't necessarily wrong, but it might be the map being different from the territory.<br /> <br /> A matter complicated when there are worlds that can be more confidently regarded as lacking fundamental qualities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T09:56:26-07:00","id":1446805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, in the sense of limited access (although some Legacies have innate access, like the Walkers in Mists to... the Mists), but they're vastly more survivable. Like, some of them have native communities of humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of the heart of a emanation realm, which dissolves none archmasters because it\u2019s a iris to the Supernal. The scar is similar to the outside emanation realm, the lower depths are comparable to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bait makes sense. An appropriate Prime spell might make it more enticing, depending on the nature of the place. I wouldn't think Lower Depths are necessarily working on the same symbolic logic as the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thinking about it, there is probably a lower depth that completely resembles our world, because it\u2019s missing the supernatural. Our obsession with fantasy could be taken as a hunger for it... maybe. Probably needs some work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, even with that there could be cases where what the Depth wants is difficult for mages to present and the inhabitants might not be lured. Like, if you can find a passage to Duat, might be a bad idea to try actively messing about with Sekhem in front of it.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, and the bait method is risky all on it\u2019s own, since it provides power to the creature, and very little control.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I said there. It seems to be consistent that being in the presence of an Iris lets you cast spells unimpeded to the other side. Although I think Irises might need to be unlocked with their Keys before they can be cast through. Ways into the Shadow, Underworld and probably Emanations can be unlocked with spells, but I think most Scars would not afford such an option.</div> </div> </div> </div> Can Space unlock most irises without a key? If a spell could open a scar, how long before the scar eats it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh hey, it says that some of those portals let one hear entities on the other side begging to be raised. That might afford some insight into bringing them over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? That probably is enough for space to form a weak sympathetic connection, unless I really misunderstood those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it could vary. Sometimes the Arcanum might compel them with what they're missing, sometimes it might be that their Patterns lack anything for the Arcanum to interact with it, sometimes what the Depth lacks might be more complex or esoteric than Awakened spells typically interact with.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems like one could find a lower depths entity that is missing enough arcanum to be a good shield against another mage. Might be a use for them outside of bargains.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, maybe. The term &quot;Fallen magic&quot; can cover a lot of disparate elements. It's like the descriptions in the Fallen Worlds section of the core book; mages encounter loads of things that don't map directly to the Supernal, the Abyss or even other realms they have some conception of, and they debate the question of how all these things relate to one another. Some of it are the Lies contradictions or ways that it's flawed, some of it is qualities slipping in from unknown dimensions (not all of which qualify as Lower Depths to them), some of it seems to arise naturally from the Fallen World itself and have means of rising to greater power. It's all weird and messy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Certainly, and it\u2019s not helped by not being able to explore and scrutinize these realms in a meaningful fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that no mage who is dedicated to the study of Lower Depths would feel confident with a broad declaration about which form of magic better engages with them (or even necessarily whether a given Mystery that they might respond to qualifies as magic) because they ultimately recognise that the ones that are known of are too many and varied to make such a broad generalisation, and there are plenty that are unknown. And I expect there's a big argument about whether or not the Lower Depths precede the Lie/Abyss* and what such a thing might say about their nature (maybe they're far enough from Supernal purity that the Lie doesn't even actually reach them).</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting. I thought that the Abyss/Lie acted as a filter for the Supernal, and the fallen world acted as a second filter to the lower depths. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I think there's plenty of debate among mages about whether the Abyss actually predates becoming a barrier of separation from the Supernal. There are plenty of Scelesti who regard it as the original and most authentic expression of reality, even it was held back by the solid reality that blossomed in its heart before the Fall provided means of insinuation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Given the Abyss is everything not True that still is, I imagine it would be both originating from the fall, and the Supernal originated from it, at the same time. It may even be neither at the same time as it is both.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People like that would be why the manuals need to include the warnings, sure. Still, I think the more dangerous mage is the one who has held back carefully and made an extensive study of a subject and feels confident that they know what they're doing; the texts didn't say &quot;don't mess around with this at all&quot;. Therefore hubris. The Mysterium has Censoriums for a reason; you never throw any discovery away no matter how deleterious, you keep it for the study of people who you're sure will handle it safely and not abuse it. Proper handling can be <i>a</i> way to describe what they do with it next.</div> </div> </div> </div> People like that are just as likely to awaken as anyone else. Somebody had to find out the soul sucking being from beyond our world can kill you horribly, how many had to find that out the hard way? (Side note: I am coming to the conclusion that I would be very dead quickly as a Mage. I have a very poor grasp on what exactly my limits are, bar a few, and I would so completely wrapped up in my obsessions I might forget the rest of the world exists.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can be scariest not when they act with ignorance but with a certainty that they're in the know which is not entirely displaced. This isn't Things Man Was Not Meant to Know, it's Things Man Knows and Therefore Has Licence to Use.</div> </div> </div> </div> In my humble opinion, that\u2019s more tragic than horrifying. Humans and Mages know a lot, but neither is omniscient. Maybe one day, after the gates of heaven are cast open, and the cruel tyrants that made us are replaced, we can become enlightened so. Until then, Humanity does not Know, but Uses Anyway. Mages attain Truth, and gain great knowledge, but even the best and brightest that don\u2019t ascend can\u2019t know everything. Eventually, someone will make a honest, well meaning mistake. They truly believe that they are doing good, or at least the best they can. We all suffer the Ruin\u2019s curse, and so the worst can and will happen from the best of intentions. <br /> <br /> The scariest mage to me is the one with a cause, one that they will snap reality in two for. For they will stop at no length so see their hopes and dreams fulfilled, and let nothing stand in there way. The scariest words are \u201cit will all be worth it in the end\u201d, not \u201c I definitely can do this\u201d. Admittedly combining both is actually probably for the best. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying we should leave all of this stuff well alone... sounds like Banisher talk to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think my cynicism on human nature is bleeding through somewhat. I never meant to imply that we shouldn\u2019t use it ever, just that most circumstances where this is a viable option, there are probably safer ways to achieve your goals. Hence my choice of the word foolishness. The only time where I can see a circumstance where summoning is a good idea, is one where there is knowledge to be found, and a mystery to seek.<br /> <br /> I would definitely be a terrible Banisher, I can\u2019t even think about possibly hurting someone without getting horribly depressed. I think I would be a better Seer honestly. At least then I could delude myself until it was too late and I have a miniature Exarch in my Oneiros.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446685#post1446685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Need to buy the rest of the Second Edition cores...</div> </div> </div> </div>One of these years... Werewolf or Giest is up next. I have Changeling, Beast, and I kickstarted Deviant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T11:45:09-07:00","id":1446816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446805#post1446805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it, there is probably a lower depth that completely resembles our world, because it\u2019s missing the supernatural. Our obsession with fantasy could be taken as a hunger for it... maybe. Probably needs some work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! My immediate thought - to tie in the themes of the lower depths being hungry and corrosive to the Fallen - was that if someone from a \u201cmundane\u201d realm breaks out into the CoD, they gain magic like human dark mages in Dragon Prince: sacrificing supernatural creatures briefly gives them access to related spells.<br /> <br /> Maybe they still suffer breaking points (but not lunacy/quiescence/etc) for witnessing magic - but gain the \u201cobsessed\u201d condition from it. <br /> They could be refined with a thaumavore merit that lets them dispel (consume) long-lasting spells for the same effect. And further refined with basically becoming a bane to supernaturals - so they don\u2019t have to defeat a vampire, just grab it.<br /> <br /> And you play off of Mage cosmology for even deeper levels of horror: all sleepers have a shard of the abyss in their soul to cause quiescences... That might be something the dark mages can learn to sacrifice as well - gaining selesti powers from the most common supernatural power in the setting.<br /> And worse still, if you want to attach any moral quandary to these antagonists, what if they didn\u2019t kill their \u2018sacrifices\u2019 (or could learn not to) - they just strip the magic from them. Potentially turning Sleepers into Sleepwalkers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:02:37-07:00","id":1446820,"title":"","content":"New questions for today:<br /> 1) The Ascending Ones have access to elixirs. Can a mage replicate or enhance the fallen magic with matter, or is life/ whatever arcanum the effect falls under necessary as well?<br /> 2) At what point do life patterns become matter patterns? Example: if a mage takes a branch from a tree, at what point will it respond to matter spells to shape it?<br /> 3) Can Matter perfecting enhance the effect of substances on Living creatures without Life? Examples: making something extremely addicting and making the withdrawal symptoms even worse. Or increase the effect of performance enhancing drugs.<br /> 4) If I made a legacy based around the idea of Enlightenment through Drugs or just Chemistry, based on the above, should the ruling arcanum be Life or Matter?<br /> <br /> Todays questions were inspired by the Blight from dead by daylight, and me asking myself how I would do a mammon seer. Yes, I am aware the Blight most closely resembles a Ascending One slasher or Broken, but I think a rapt based of it would be interesting.<br /> <br /> Bonus Question:<br /> 5) Are mortals with a supernatural merit more or less likely to awaken? Do endowments count as a supernatural merit?<br /> 5.5) I vaguely remember a elixir that increases the roll for morality degradation, making it more likely that they achieve the required exceptional success. Does that mean there is a large ( for a mage population) number of ex Ascending Ones? Can they still access their endowments?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:08:43-07:00","id":1446821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446816#post1446816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh! My immediate thought - to tie in the themes of the lower depths being hungry and corrosive to the Fallen - was that if someone from a \u201cmundane\u201d realm breaks out into the CoD, they gain magic like human dark mages in Dragon Prince: sacrificing supernatural creatures briefly gives them access to related spells.<br /> <br /> Maybe they still suffer breaking points (but not lunacy/quiescence/etc) for witnessing magic - but gain the \u201cobsessed\u201d condition from it.<br /> They could be refined with a thaumavore merit that lets them dispel (consume) long-lasting spells for the same effect. And further refined with basically becoming a bane to supernaturals - so they don\u2019t have to defeat a vampire, just grab it.<br /> <br /> And you play off of Mage cosmology for even deeper levels of horror: all sleepers have a shard of the abyss in their soul to cause quiescences... That might be something the dark mages can learn to sacrifice as well - gaining selesti powers from the most common supernatural power in the setting.<br /> And worse still, if you want to attach any moral quandary to these antagonists, what if they didn\u2019t kill their \u2018sacrifices\u2019 (or could learn not to) - they just strip the magic from them. Potentially turning Sleepers into Sleepwalkers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn\u2019t there a hunter compact or conspiracy that stole supernatural and Supernal and possibly Abyssal power from their victims? ( I don\u2019t own hunter yet, remembering from a trip through white Wolf wiki.) Maybe it could tie into the Mundane (my name for said depth) and the Logophages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:44:06-07:00","id":1446829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446816#post1446816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh! My immediate thought - to tie in the themes of the lower depths being hungry and corrosive to the Fallen - was that if someone from a \u201cmundane\u201d realm breaks out into the CoD, they gain magic like human dark mages in Dragon Prince: sacrificing supernatural creatures briefly gives them access to related spells.<br /> <br /> Maybe they still suffer breaking points (but not lunacy/quiescence/etc) for witnessing magic - but gain the \u201cobsessed\u201d condition from it.<br /> They could be refined with a thaumavore merit that lets them dispel (consume) long-lasting spells for the same effect. And further refined with basically becoming a bane to supernaturals - so they don\u2019t have to defeat a vampire, just grab it.<br /> <br /> And you play off of Mage cosmology for even deeper levels of horror: all sleepers have a shard of the abyss in their soul to cause quiescences... That might be something the dark mages can learn to sacrifice as well - gaining selesti powers from the most common supernatural power in the setting.<br /> And worse still, if you want to attach any moral quandary to these antagonists, what if they didn\u2019t kill their \u2018sacrifices\u2019 (or could learn not to) - they just strip the magic from them. Potentially turning Sleepers into Sleepwalkers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible tangent: The humans from the Mundane wouldn\u2019t have souls, right? Because souls are supernatural? Would they start to experience soul loss as they consume more magic, due to their pattern \u201cfixing\u201d itself? Maybe they could even eat souls like the Tremere, to stave soul loss off for a while. Throw in the actual Tremere, and you have a great plot!<br /> <br /> (This post was a edit, but I don\u2019t think it went through for some reason, if it did and I didn\u2019t see it for some reason, I am sorry for the double post.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T13:28:44-07:00","id":1446837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446820#post1446820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New questions for today:<br /> 1) The Ascending Ones have access to elixirs. Can a mage replicate or enhance the fallen magic with matter, or is life/ whatever arcanum the effect falls under necessary as well?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think Signs of Sorcery had rules for making potions - I\u2019d skim those to try replicating elixirs. Most likely, you need an arcanum for the spell effects and matter to make it a potion. I don\u2019t think enhancing is possible, since spells of the same effect don\u2019t stack, but prolonging it might be possible with Time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) At what point do life patterns become matter patterns? Example: if a mage takes a branch from a tree, at what point will it respond to matter spells to shape it? </div> </div> </div> After they\u2019re finished transforming through Death. I would say that If the tree branch can still be planted and grow a new plant, it\u2019s still alive. If there\u2019s some kind of preservation, or processing, or something to make it a workable material, it wouldn\u2019t be matter until after that occurs. Trees specifically are a little tough for me to grok, but like with animals, once decomposition has finished and you\u2019re left with bones, that would be the point Death finishes and leaves Matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bonus Question:<br /> 5) Are mortals with a supernatural merit more or less likely to awaken? Do endowments count as a supernatural merit?<br /> 5.5) I vaguely remember a elixir that increases the roll for morality degradation, making it more likely that they achieve the required exceptional success. Does that mean there is a large ( for a mage population) number of ex Ascending Ones? Can they still access their endowments? </div> </div> </div>From what I recall, having supernatural merits means that the character is much more likely to keep investing in those powers, rather than seek deeper levels of enlightenment. <br /> <br /> There was a great quote from Dave B (prior to SOS, so it may have changed), that Sleepers Awaken when they have enough Arcane EXP to buy a dot of gnosis. Having some powers can ensure that you have more novel experiences with the supernatural (the primary way mortals could earn Arcane beats) without dying or going insane. But the character is much more likely to spend that on the powers they have / know are available / help them with short term goals, rather than save up to Awaken - which they might not know exists, and which could still go horribly wrong.<br /> <br /> They lose other intrinsic supernatural powers when they awaken, but I believe they can keep purely external merits (like Relics). I don\u2019t know enough about the Ascending Ones to guess how much is lost for them specifically. If it took a merit to make elixirs for themself, I believe that would be lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T13:44:23-07:00","id":1446841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446821#post1446821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn\u2019t there a hunter compact or conspiracy that stole supernatural and Supernal and possibly Abyssal power from their victims? ( I don\u2019t own hunter yet, remembering from a trip through white Wolf wiki.) Maybe it could tie into the Mundane (my name for said depth) and the Logophages?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t really get into Hunter, so I\u2019m not sure. Cheiron Group did have an abyssal worm thaumatech, and I think a mana-eating one. There may have been other stuff in Witch Finders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possible tangent: The humans from the Mundane wouldn\u2019t have souls, right? Because souls are supernatural? Would they start to experience soul loss as they consume more magic, due to their pattern \u201cfixing\u201d itself? Maybe they could even eat souls like the Tremere, to stave soul loss off for a while. Throw in the actual Tremere, and you have a great plot! </div> </div> </div>Up to you! That can be a great way to make them more intrinsically antagonistic - and possibly more sympathetic, as Soul Loss is comparable to \u201cunder a curse that motivates their worse coping strategies and degrades their Will.\u201d If they do have souls, then it\u2019s more of a choice to murder and consume magic out of envy and hubris. And progressively acquiring Soul Loss as they use dark magic would reinforce the downward spiral of terrible decisions, as the consequences motivate even worse ones to cope. So it depends on what themes you\u2019d want to use, and what kinds of conflicts you want to introduce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T13:49:14-07:00","id":1446842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446820#post1446820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New questions for today:<br /> 1) The Ascending Ones have access to elixirs. Can a mage replicate or enhance the fallen magic with matter, or is life/ whatever arcanum the effect falls under necessary as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Enhancing the effects of an Ascending Ones' potion would probably be Matter 3 Perfecting, diminishing its effects would be Matter 3 Fraying.<br /> <br /> Replicating the effects would be the spell <i>Spell Potion</i> (Matter 3 + Prime 2, <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>) and then whatever other spell would replicate the effects of the specific potion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) At what point do life patterns become matter patterns? Example: if a mage takes a branch from a tree, at what point will it respond to matter spells to shape it? </div> </div> </div>Once it's no longer dying, it is a bit of a grey area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Can Matter perfecting enhance the effect of substances on Living creatures without Life? Examples: making something extremely addicting and making the withdrawal symptoms even worse. Or increase the effect of performance enhancing drugs. </div> </div> </div>Yes, Matter perfecting can enhance the effects of anything under its purview, even if that thing is then used on a living creature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) If I made a legacy based around the idea of Enlightenment through Drugs or just Chemistry, based on the above, should the ruling arcanum be Life or Matter? </div> </div> </div>Probably a Thyrsus Matter/Life Legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Todays questions were inspired by the Blight from dead by daylight, and me asking myself how I would do a mammon seer. Yes, I am aware the Blight most closely resembles a Ascending One slasher or Broken, but I think a rapt based of it would be interesting.<br /> <br /> Bonus Question:<br /> 5) Are mortals with a supernatural merit more or less likely to awaken? Do endowments count as a supernatural merit? </div> </div> </div>Mortals with Supernatural Merits are probably slightly more likely to Awaken, but being told about the Supernal makes you less likely to Awaken.<br /> <br /> Some Endowments count as Supernatural, others don't. Advanced Armory definitely doesn't, Benedictions and Castigations definitely do, and Thaumatech (the Cheiron kind) are borderline. Basically, if it's an inherent power, it makes you count as a Sleepwalker, if it's an external power it doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5.5) I vaguely remember a elixir that increases the roll for morality degradation, making it more likely that they achieve the required exceptional success. Does that mean there is a large ( for a mage population) number of ex Ascending Ones? Can they still access their endowments? </div> </div> </div>Probably not, and no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T16:45:07-07:00","id":1446864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446821#post1446821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn\u2019t there a hunter compact or conspiracy that stole supernatural and Supernal and possibly Abyssal power from their victims? ( I don\u2019t own hunter yet, remembering from a trip through white Wolf wiki.) Maybe it could tie into the Mundane (my name for said depth) and the Logophages?</div> </div> </div> </div>The compact you're thinking of is probably the Promethean Brotherhood from the Witch Finders supplement, who study a rite to ritually sacrifice witches to gain Gnosis on a temporary basis. Witch Finders uses the word &quot;witch&quot; to describe both supernal sorcerers and other kinds of will-workers and ritualists, mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T17:41:32-07:00","id":1446872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446805#post1446805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Space unlock most irises without a key?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think only if it traverses space within the same realm. I can't really buy Space opening an Avernian Gate or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? That probably is enough for space to form a weak sympathetic connection, unless I really misunderstood those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so. I mean, look at the description of a Weak connection. Casual acquaintances, co-workers... there's got to be <i>some</i> kind of consistent relationship there, even if it doesn't go very deep. Enough that the figure is recognisable and routine. As far as hearing whispers on the other side of a Scar goes, I think it would be necessary to distinguish one voice from another and visit it a fair number of times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like one could find a lower depths entity that is missing enough arcanum to be a good shield against another mage. Might be a use for them outside of bargains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd find that consistent with other portrayals, like the one Paternoster uses to make Hollow Ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">People like that are just as likely to awaken as anyone else. Somebody had to find out the soul sucking being from beyond our world can kill you horribly, how many had to find that out the hard way? (Side note: I am coming to the conclusion that I would be very dead quickly as a Mage. I have a very poor grasp on what exactly my limits are, bar a few, and I would so completely wrapped up in my obsessions I might forget the rest of the world exists.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that's why they spend a year or two fostering new mages; at least try to teach them some sensible practices for approaching Mysteries. And being able to document this stuff so future generations know what they're getting into before they approach it is another reason to have Orders.<br /> <br /> Heck, going to explore something that destroys you is also a reason to have cabals and Consilia, so there'll be people who notice you disappeared and try to figure out where you vanished so they can at least put hazard signs up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my cynicism on human nature is bleeding through somewhat. I never meant to imply that we shouldn\u2019t use it ever, just that most circumstances where this is a viable option, there are probably safer ways to achieve your goals. Hence my choice of the word foolishness. The only time where I can see a circumstance where summoning is a good idea, is one where there is knowledge to be found, and a mystery to seek.</div> </div> </div> </div>That comment was meant more as ironic in-character. I like to think that part of being Addicted to Mysteries is that there's a social pressure to not be too reserved about the use of or investigation into magic, and that &quot;Banisher&quot; is a slur or an accusation that might end up levelled at a mage who is too vocal about things related to magic or the Awakened being really messed up. A very cautiously applied one, as I think being frivolous with calling other members of the community Banishers, the kind of thing that is serious enough that it can greatly hurt your standing without something to back it up.<br /> <br /> Still, I think it would play into the whole element of Banishers as memetic virus more likely to convert other mages than be converted back. I think it's lower key than other deviancies, but there are always some mages who are on the lookout for other people developing tendencies or sympathies for that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T17:45:51-07:00","id":1446873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446820#post1446820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New questions for today:<br /> 1) The Ascending Ones have access to elixirs. Can a mage replicate or enhance the fallen magic with matter, or is life/ whatever arcanum the effect falls under necessary as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, let me check some First Edition examples to get a frame of reference... mostly a few kinds of bonuses or being able to make minor bodily modifications.<br /> <br /> Awakened magic is going to replicate effects according to its own frame of reference with the Practices and Arcana. They're gonna make a potion that they imprint with a Death Veiling to make somebody look like they're on the verge of dying, rather than improve some kind of lesser alchemical mixture. The Awakened, I think, can often understand things like mortal thaumaturgies or the basis of Endowments, but their Supernal power is generally superior to these things and might be said to crowd out attempts to internalise the methods for actually doing them.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd be inclined to give mages the flex of being able to use Perfecting to enhance the effects of an Elixir that a hunter had already concocted, if not by too much. Less so the powers of Malleus Maleficarum or the Lucifuge, that's getting into supernatural stuff the Arcana don't readily grasp directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) At what point do life patterns become matter patterns? Example: if a mage takes a branch from a tree, at what point will it respond to matter spells to shape it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's safe when there's no biological process going on anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Can Matter perfecting enhance the effect of substances on Living creatures without Life? Examples: making something extremely addicting and making the withdrawal symptoms even worse. Or increase the effect of performance enhancing drugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) If I made a legacy based around the idea of Enlightenment through Drugs or just Chemistry, based on the above, should the ruling arcanum be Life or Matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the thing about Legacies is that the Arcana involved are rooted in the result, not the method. You could have something like Ascension's Cult of Ecstasy, where drugs and sex are all part of the process of shaping one's Gnosis and the Oblations and Yantras, but the actual Attainments would use Time and Mind to represent altered states of awareness and controlling one's sense of the moment. To me, your proposition sounds like the drugs, or even the chemistry, constitute the Knowledge and Indoctrination components of the Legacy, but the Arcana are going to be in what the Legacy's conception of what enlightenment actually looks like on the other side.<br /> <br /> The alternative is the idea of a Legacy focused on enhancing the quality of the drugs, but honestly I think that's a bit... limited as far as Legacy ideas go. Plus, I think published and homebrew Legacies should have a focus on applicability in play. It's like, I presume your Uncrowned King is going on to <i>do</i> something in the storyline with the mental capabilities enhanced by introspection on their crafted works, rather than pure naval-gazing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Are mortals with a supernatural merit more or less likely to awaken? Do endowments count as a supernatural merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think people who have regular contact with the supernatural are being inured to it functioning as a Confrontation with the Lie necessary for Awakening. At least while they stay in their line; the possibility of encountering something new and as shocking as if they'd never acknowledge the supernatural is still there, but perhaps hardly more likely than if they were a typical Sleeper. Possibly even less, because it may be that even if it's something unlike what you ever encountered before it's still a <i>bit</i> more expected than the totally novel experience. You need it to be something that shakes up your conception of the world for when the Watchtower comes calling.<br /> <br /> The importance of that latter one needing to be emphasized; all Awakening requires the intercession of a Watchtower, in accordance with inscrutable criteria. The Watchtower probably doesn't intercede the first time you encounter the supernatural, and repeated exposure is kind of wasting opportunities for it.<br /> <br /> One thing I think matters for consideration is that the Chronicles of Darkness might be assumed to have a fair number of people who are engaged in underground occult activity, whether that be learning thaumaturgy or getting involved in freaky cults or hunting monsters, and that's not really where the majority of Awakened seem to come from. Probably not even close, that the vast majority were regular (if obsessed) people before they saw the Supernal. That could be observed as a simple numbers game (the pool of Awakening prospects among the uninitiated is just way bigger), but I'd say lots of mages are inclined to speculate that people with Supernatural Merits are either reducing their capacity to Confront the Lie or even disqualifying themselves in the eyes of the Watchtowers.<br /> <br /> I'd also think it could be neat to have mages who investigate these societies come to realise that a lot of them are people who <i>already</i> experienced the Awakening, and then failed their tests. That they got into this world trying to fill the hole left in their hearts from knowing their was a chance for true understanding that they blew. It would be ironic if they immerse themselves into things that make the chance for a do over dwindle away.<br /> <br /> I'd count any Endowments that aren't purely based in an external tool that doesn't require any esoteric insight to use. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5.5) I vaguely remember a elixir that increases the roll for morality degradation, making it more likely that they achieve the required exceptional success. Does that mean there is a large ( for a mage population) number of ex Ascending Ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... not sure what the connection is?<br /> <br /> (Mages get no Supernatural Merits belonging to anything that is not Awakened. The process of getting Gnosis and the Arcana burns that lesser knowledge and power out of them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T17:51:49-07:00","id":1446875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446837#post1446837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a great quote from Dave B (prior to SOS, so it may have changed), that Sleepers Awaken when they have enough Arcane EXP to buy a dot of gnosis. Having some powers can ensure that you have more novel experiences with the supernatural (the primary way mortals could earn Arcane beats) without dying or going insane. But the character is much more likely to spend that on the powers they have / know are available / help them with short term goals, rather than save up to Awaken - which they might not know exists, and which could still go horribly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>No that's just... how the process of Awakening is systematized. The <i>only</i> people who can earn Arcane Beats are Awakened mages and people undergoing an Awakening, the latter accruing them from passing the tests the Watchtower presents to them. When they've encountered enough during the Awakening to collect five Arcane Experience, they're presented with the opportunity to sign the Watchtower, which is the process of buying their first Gnosis dot. If they fail the Awakening at any time, Arcane Beats convert into their regular counterpart (so hey... might be able to at least transform the experience into some heightened professional experience).<br /> <br /> Arcane Experience can be spent on <b>nothing</b> besides Gnosis, Arcana up to the maximum of one's Path, Praxes, Legacy Attainments or Wisdom. They can't even use that stuff to buy their own Merits like Astral Adept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-01-2021, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T18:06:42-07:00","id":1446878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446875#post1446875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No that's just... how the process of Awakening is systematized. The <i>only</i> people who can earn Arcane Beats are Awakened mages and people undergoing an Awakening, the latter accruing them from passing the tests the Watchtower presents to them. When they've encountered enough during the Awakening to collect five Arcane Experience, they're presented with the opportunity to sign the Watchtower, which is the process of buying their first Gnosis dot. If they fail the Awakening at any time, Arcane Beats convert into their regular counterpart (so hey... might be able to at least transform the experience into some heightened professional experience).<br /> <br /> Arcane Experience can be spent on <b>nothing</b> besides Gnosis, Arcana up to the maximum of one's Path, Praxes, Legacy Attainments or Wisdom. They can't even use that stuff to buy their own Merits like Astral Adept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, i think it's to systemized with those rules but yeah arcane experience has limited applications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T18:58:55-07:00","id":1446888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446873#post1446873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm... not sure what the connection is?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cIn play, the confrontation with the Lie should be a breaking point against Integrity in which the player gains an exceptional success. If the event sparks an Awakening, do not grant a Condition for the exceptional success. See Mage: The Awakening Second Edition p. 299 for a condensed form of the Integrity rules, or the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook, pp. 73-75 for full systems. \u201c Pg 130 of signs of sorcery. I am at work so I can\u2019t answer in full now, I will later.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T20:26:56-07:00","id":1446896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446888#post1446888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cIn play, the confrontation with the Lie should be a breaking point against Integrity in which the player gains an exceptional success. If the event sparks an Awakening, do not grant a Condition for the exceptional success. See Mage: The Awakening Second Edition p. 299 for a condensed form of the Integrity rules, or the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook, pp. 73-75 for full systems. \u201c Pg 130 of signs of sorcery. I am at work so I can\u2019t answer in full now, I will later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right right.<br /> <br /> An Ascending One might have the benefit of an elixir to maintain their Integrity in the face of what would otherwise qualify as a confrontation with the Lie, but I think between the possibility of the encounter being more expected and deliberate and the process of such an elixir easing the experience of it, it lacks the necessary shock to the system.<br /> <br /> In any case, a greater frequency of exceptional successes on Integrity rolls still won't increase the rate of Watchtower intervention or necessarily mean they have what it takes to face the Adyton. Ascending Ones don't seem particularly more likely to become mages.<br /> <br /> Plus they're still hunters, they're using these drugs for the sake of keeping it together in opposition to the supernatural. Ascending Ones strike me as liable to see the beginning of Awakening as a dreadful trick and reject it in short order.<br /> <br /> Somebody with that background following it to the beginning of their Path would be a particular novelty (and maybe also subject to a bit of observation to not have Banisher inclinations).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446878#post1446878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, i think it's to systemized with those rules but yeah arcane experience has limited applications.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how it emphasizes that Awakening is not some divine endowment, that the Watchtower calls but the aspirant builds the Path out of intent and insight accrued from the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T22:59:21-07:00","id":1446916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446873#post1446873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, let me check some First Edition examples to get a frame of reference... mostly a few kinds of bonuses or being able to make minor bodily modifications.<br /> <br /> Awakened magic is going to replicate effects according to its own frame of reference with the Practices and Arcana. They're gonna make a potion that they imprint with a Death Veiling to make somebody look like they're on the verge of dying, rather than improve some kind of lesser alchemical mixture. The Awakened, I think, can often understand things like mortal thaumaturgies or the basis of Endowments, but their Supernal power is generally superior to these things and might be said to crowd out attempts to internalise the methods for actually doing them.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd be inclined to give mages the flex of being able to use Perfecting to enhance the effects of an Elixir that a hunter had already concocted, if not by too much. Less so the powers of Malleus Maleficarum or the Lucifuge, that's getting into supernatural stuff the Arcana don't readily grasp directly.</div> </div> </div> </div> With hunter powers origins being somewhat ambiguous, that\u2019s probably fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446873#post1446873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the thing about Legacies is that the Arcana involved are rooted in the result, not the method. You could have something like Ascension's Cult of Ecstasy, where drugs and sex are all part of the process of shaping one's Gnosis and the Oblations and Yantras, but the actual Attainments would use Time and Mind to represent altered states of awareness and controlling one's sense of the moment. To me, your proposition sounds like the drugs, or even the chemistry, constitute the Knowledge and Indoctrination components of the Legacy, but the Arcana are going to be in what the Legacy's conception of what enlightenment actually looks like on the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my biggest problem when coming up with legacies is that I come up with mechanical effects first, when the opposite path works better. Since I have no experience with any drugs other than Tylenol, or of any real life beliefs involving enlightenment and drugs, I\u2019m at something of a loss on enlightenment part. If I pull from the source inspiration... I get drugs as a means to push humanity past it\u2019s limits. I seem to have a hard time figuring out a matter dominated legacy\u2019s theory. Maybe because it\u2019s late and I just got off work.<br /> (Side note: why on earth is the Cult of Ecstasy\u2019s thing time? Altered states of awareness sounds way more like a Life or Mind or Spirit thing than time.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446873#post1446873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alternative is the idea of a Legacy focused on enhancing the quality of the drugs, but honestly I think that's a bit... limited as far as Legacy ideas go. Plus, I think published and homebrew Legacies should have a focus on applicability in play. It's like, I presume your Uncrowned King is going on to <i>do</i> something in the storyline with the mental capabilities enhanced by introspection on their crafted works, rather than pure naval-gazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my mental picture of the legacy involved them trying to find, harvest, and figure out the magical properties of supernatural flora and fauna. Like mandrake root, vampire ash/ blood, werewolf glands, and maybe even vitriol. Most of the time the legacy would act as potion makers as potions are just magic drugs anyways. Poisons would also be on brand for them. I guess I imagined them to chemists as the forge masters are to blacksmiths. I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s enough for a legacy though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446873#post1446873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I think people who have regular contact with the supernatural are being inured to it functioning as a Confrontation with the Lie necessary for Awakening. At least while they stay in their line; the possibility of encountering something new and as shocking as if they'd never acknowledge the supernatural is still there, but perhaps hardly more likely than if they were a typical Sleeper. Possibly even less, because it may be that even if it's something unlike what you ever encountered before it's still a <i>bit</i> more expected than the totally novel experience. You need it to be something that shakes up your conception of the world for when the Watchtower comes calling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, but there <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446873#post1446873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The importance of that latter one needing to be emphasized; all Awakening requires the intercession of a Watchtower, in accordance with inscrutable criteria. The Watchtower probably doesn't intercede the first time you encounter the supernatural, and repeated exposure is kind of wasting opportunities for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Watchtower is a bit of randomness that really can\u2019t be accounted for. I mostly ignored it, even as important as it is, because it\u2019s not useful when estimating mage population statistics.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446873#post1446873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I think matters for consideration is that the Chronicles of Darkness might be assumed to have a fair number of people who are engaged in underground occult activity, whether that be learning thaumaturgy or getting involved in freaky cults or hunting monsters, and that's not really where the majority of Awakened seem to come from. Probably not even close, that the vast majority were regular (if obsessed) people before they saw the Supernal. That could be observed as a simple numbers game (the pool of Awakening prospects among the uninitiated is just way bigger), but I'd say lots of mages are inclined to speculate that people with Supernatural Merits are either reducing their capacity to Confront the Lie or even disqualifying themselves in the eyes of the Watchtowers.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, that\u2019s disappointing, but not unexpected.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446873#post1446873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also think it could be neat to have mages who investigate these societies come to realise that a lot of them are people who <i>already</i> experienced the Awakening, and then failed their tests. That they got into this world trying to fill the hole left in their hearts from knowing their was a chance for true understanding that they blew. It would be ironic if they immerse themselves into things that make the chance for a do over dwindle away.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s just tragic. I am so using that if I ever get the chance.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446873#post1446873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd count any Endowments that aren't purely based in an external tool that doesn't require any esoteric insight to use.</div> </div> </div> </div> I forget, do the Ascending Ones need internal alchemy to do their thing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446896#post1446896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right right.<br /> <br /> An Ascending One might have the benefit of an elixir to maintain their Integrity in the face of what would otherwise qualify as a confrontation with the Lie, but I think between the possibility of the encounter being more expected and deliberate and the process of such an elixir easing the experience of it, it lacks the necessary shock to the system.</div> </div> </div> </div> Makes sense, how would that translate into the game? Having to pick one of the conditions for a exceptional success instead?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446896#post1446896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, a greater frequency of exceptional successes on Integrity rolls still won't increase the rate of Watchtower intervention or necessarily mean they have what it takes to face the Adyton. Ascending Ones don't seem particularly more likely to become mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they still need that first pillar fulfilled, but I still see more chances to get chosen than the average human. If the elixir truly works by dulling their perceptions though, it would seem to counteract the pillar though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446896#post1446896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus they're still hunters, they're using these drugs for the sake of keeping it together in opposition to the supernatural. Ascending Ones strike me as liable to see the beginning of Awakening as a dreadful trick and reject it in short order.</div> </div> </div> </div> Now this is something i hadn\u2019t considered. I always figured that it was somewhat common that hunters would awaken simply due relative commonplace breaking points, and needing to investigate in order to kill the monster. It never occurred to me that most hunters would probably reject the awakening. It makes a great deal of sense though. Hunters have to be extremely paranoid in order to survive, doesn\u2019t make the best start to a awakening.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446896#post1446896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somebody with that background following it to the beginning of their Path would be a particular novelty (and maybe also subject to a bit of observation to not have Banisher inclinations).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like fun times.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T23:34:37-07:00","id":1446918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446916#post1446916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, my mental picture of the legacy involved them trying to find, harvest, and figure out the magical properties of supernatural flora and fauna. Like mandrake root, vampire ash/ blood, werewolf glands, and maybe even vitriol. Most of the time the legacy would act as potion makers as potions are just magic drugs anyways. Poisons would also be on brand for them. I guess I imagined them to chemists as the forge masters are to blacksmiths. I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s enough for a legacy though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Thyrsus Legacy.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Mastigos Legacy, if the focus is less on &quot;brave the edges of what's safe and not to bring back enlightening knowledge,&quot; and more on &quot;spit in the face of what people say whether it's safe or not, because enlightenment was never safe in the first place.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T03:54:01-07:00","id":1446936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446805#post1446805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like one could find a lower depths entity that is missing enough arcanum to be a good shield against another mage. Might be a use for them outside of bargains.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446872#post1446872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd find that consistent with other portrayals, like the one Paternoster uses to make Hollow Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes and no. It really depends on what's missing, how it's missing, and how you manage to take advantage of that. Hollow Ones, for example, have their sense of self and personality completely wiped out by a Lower Depth entity. But the way it works is that their now completely blank minds becomes <i>extra susceptible</i> to Mind magic, allowing anyone with Mind to reprogram them indefinitely.<br /> Where the protection comes from is that without Mana for upkeep, their minds will be wiped again, taking any potential secrets with them and allowing them to be reused much more securely than a regular mind controlled Sleepwalker. The fact that they have to be reprogrammed also means anyone who tries to mess with their current programming will always face a Clash of Wills against the original programmers, who are naturally quite good at what they do or they wouldn't be chosen as programmers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T06:16:03-07:00","id":1446962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446916#post1446916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget, do the Ascending Ones need internal alchemy to do their thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an entire story about how the concoctions are mixed with deadly poisons to prevent undisciplined overuse, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T09:07:07-07:00","id":1446988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446916#post1446916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my mental picture of the legacy involved them trying to find, harvest, and figure out the magical properties of supernatural flora and fauna. Like mandrake root, vampire ash/ blood, werewolf glands, and maybe even vitriol. Most of the time the legacy would act as potion makers as potions are just magic drugs anyways. Poisons would also be on brand for them. I guess I imagined them to chemists as the forge masters are to blacksmiths. I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s enough for a legacy though.</div> </div> </div> </div> quoted for a minor fix, I wanted them to be herbalists too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446918#post1446918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like a Thyrsus Legacy.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Mastigos Legacy, if the focus is less on &quot;brave the edges of what's safe and not to bring back enlightening knowledge,&quot; and more on &quot;spit in the face of what people say whether it's safe or not, because enlightenment was never safe in the first place.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I love that second quote, it\u2019s just perfectly in line with my idea for the legacies founder. But I think that\u2019s just their personal perspective, not the legacies as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446962#post1446962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an entire story about how the concoctions are mixed with deadly poisons to prevent undisciplined overuse, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s a great idea, going to steal it.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I\u2019m going to be very busy the next week and a half, so no time to actually make my legacies, but I think I can do some prep work for them right now.<br /> <br /> I noticed there is a real lack of matter primary legacies besides transhuman engineers, and lords of the inanimate. Makes me want to make this a Matter primary legacy even more. Most Matter legacies seem to come from either engineering or other working of materials. I have not seen a Chemistry legacy yet, that I am aware of.<br /> <br /> Legacy themes: Strange Formulas, Toxic Elixirs, Self Experimentation, Studying the effects of Ingredients on Bodies and Minds. unethical procurement of ingredients, The legacy having been \u201cPurchased\u201d by a avatar or agent of the Chancellor, Heavy Involvement in the supernatural community, Keeping gardens of harvestable crypto flora.<br /> <br /> Legacy members should include Doctors, Explorers, and Drug Dealers. <br /> <br /> I imagine legacy members seek a perfect elixir that grants enlightenment and ascension to those that take it.<br /> <br /> The rest of it I\u2019m not too sure on. I feel like there should be a subtle Arcanum as a secondary Arcanum, but I\u2019m not sure which one would fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T22:26:31-07:00","id":1447113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446805#post1446805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it, there is probably a lower depth that completely resembles our world, because it\u2019s missing the supernatural. Our obsession with fantasy could be taken as a hunger for it... maybe. Probably needs some work.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRL is a Lower Depth confirmed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really? That probably is enough for space to form a weak sympathetic connection, unless I really misunderstood those. </div> </div> </div>No but it does establish sensory range. It\u2019s <i>sensory</i> range, not <i>vision</i> range; if you can hear the unspeakable horror\u2019s mad gibbering from beyond the veil you can cast spells on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T04:03:45-07:00","id":1447170,"title":"","content":"One thing that I think can be worthwhile for designing Legacies is to consider that not all of the burden of what the Legacy is about needs to rest on the Attainments.<br /> <br /> I think there are other examples, but a prominent one is the Echo Walkers. Their Attainments are about using Life and Prime to enhance themselves into an image of angelic proto-humans. But where they get that image from is using a Death + Prime spell that messes around with people's souls and provides a glimpse inside of them, which they regard as providing insight into a more primal soul.<br /> <br /> You could have other characters where they use spells to modify drugs to imbibe as a procedure for using Attainments that do other things.<br /> <br /> Although now, as far as powers go, I'm imagining a Legacy that imbibes substances for the purpose of forming a deeply intuitive sense of them and kind of sympathy, internal processing to facilitate external transformation.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Thyrsus who extend the Path's usual image of interconnected natural world to the substance things are composed of (in their own right rather than by way of Spirit), with shaping and transmutation through a lens of living properties in seemingly non-living things. It starts off with modification to substances that can interact in a biology (maybe not just drugs, also salt and soil) and builds up to the creation of objects that can grow and heal akin to living things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:45:37-07:00","id":1447232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447170#post1447170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I think can be worthwhile for designing Legacies is to consider that not all of the burden of what the Legacy is about needs to rest on the Attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, but attainments seem easiest to figure out for me. Actual narrative reasons for the legacy to exist <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447170#post1447170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there are other examples, but a prominent one is the Echo Walkers. Their Attainments are about using Life and Prime to enhance themselves into an image of angelic proto-humans. But where they get that image from is using a Death + Prime spell that messes around with people's souls and provides a glimpse inside of them, which they regard as providing insight into a more primal soul.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had forgotten about the echo walkers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447170#post1447170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have other characters where they use spells to modify drugs to imbibe as a procedure for using Attainments that do other things.</div> </div> </div> </div> It seems I have room for two legacies, a Cult of Ecstasy style one using the drug for the perception to use their attainments, and the legacy of chemists attempting to puzzle out the metaphysical effects of substances on the body, mind, and soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447170#post1447170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although now, as far as powers go, I'm imagining a Legacy that imbibes substances for the purpose of forming a deeply intuitive sense of them and kind of sympathy, internal processing to facilitate external transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is pretty much what I would like from the first legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447170#post1447170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking Thyrsus who extend the Path's usual image of interconnected natural world to the substance things are composed of (in their own right rather than by way of Spirit), with shaping and transmutation through a lens of living properties in seemingly non-living things. It starts off with modification to substances that can interact in a biology (maybe not just drugs, also salt and soil) and builds up to the creation of objects that can grow and heal akin to living things.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems good, the healing of objects like a living thing might be a way to harvest small amounts of a object indefinitely, as I\u2019m pretty a lost finger doesn\u2019t disappear if you regrow it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, I\u2019m going to make both legacies when I have time. For the second Cult of Ecstasy style legacy, is Time really the way to go for arcanum? I think maybe Mind or Spirit could be interesting? The closest thing i have found is the Whipping Boys, which has a Mind component...<br /> <br /> New question: Is there a official timeline of the Nameless War (I love that name), and the Great Refusal? If not, is there a good fan made one?<br /> <br /> I think I want the legacy to be Free Council/ Seer and that seems like a good time period to found it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:59:47-07:00","id":1447234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447232#post1447232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I\u2019m going to make both legacies when I have time. For the second Cult of Ecstasy style legacy, is Time really the way to go for arcanum? I think maybe Mind or Spirit could be interesting? The closest thing i have found is the Whipping Boys, which has a Mind component...</div> </div> </div> </div>Cult of Ecstasy in Ascension focuses on Time, so if that's what you're trying to replicate or invoke then Time makes the most sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T13:26:59-07:00","id":1447255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447234#post1447234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cult of Ecstasy in Ascension focuses on Time, so if that's what you're trying to replicate or invoke then Time makes the most sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I\u2019m trying to go for their practices anyway. From what I understand, they use extreme sensations to put their mind new states. A quote from the white Wolf wiki <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">To Ecstatics, they are not simple chemicals, they are tools to expand their minds and turn their perceptions inside-out.</span></span></span><br /> I just have trouble associating Time with altered perceptions. The only spells or attainments that would work would seem to be unveiling, and neither of times two example spells fit well. I have never played Mage: the ascension and thus have no sacred cows to hold.<br /> <br /> I just thought of this, but what if the legacy focuses on the unveiling practice for attainments, or expanding mage sight effects for the different arcanums?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T13:42:46-07:00","id":1447257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447255#post1447255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I\u2019m trying to go for their practices anyway. From what I understand, they use extreme sensations to put their mind new states. A quote from the white Wolf wiki<br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">To Ecstatics, they are not simple chemicals, they are tools to expand their minds and turn their perceptions inside-out.</span></span></span><br /> I just have trouble associating Time with altered perceptions. The only spells or attainments that would work would seem to be unveiling, and neither of times two example spells fit well. I have never played Mage: the ascension and thus have no sacred cows to hold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oracular visions through drug induced hallucinations is a pretty common trope.<br /> <br /> The question is: what do you want the Legacy to be able to accomplish? If you're not basing it off of Ascension's Cult of Ecstasy, what <i>are</i> you basing it on? Not the drug use, I get that, but do you have a framework for the sorts of powers you want them to have?<br /> <br /> Because a Time/X Legacy that has orgies that reveal the future and a Prime/X Legacy that drops acid to navigate the raw symbolism of the Universe are both valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T14:50:43-07:00","id":1447275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447257#post1447257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oracular visions through drug induced hallucinations is a pretty common trope.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will take your word for it, I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve heard of prophets that use drug induced hallucinations, I\u2019ve heard of entrails, and human sacrifices, the stars above, and tea leaves, playing cards, and the wrinkles of hands, but never drug use. None of those things besides the stars have anything to do with Time by themselves , so I\u2019m open to the idea at least.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447257#post1447257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is: what do you want the Legacy to be able to accomplish?</div> </div> </div> </div> Being a distinct Legacy from every other legacy, tapping into \u201cHigher understanding through Drugs\u201d tropes, and that\u2019s it. I\u2019m doing this because it seems like nobody has done it before in mage 2e, and because it seemed like a interesting direction to take a legacy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447257#post1447257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're not basing it off of Ascension's Cult of Ecstasy, what <i>are</i> you basing it on?</div> </div> </div> </div> Isator Levi\u2019s comments on my other legacy idea, my intuition, and any inspiration I can find. The Cult of Ecstasy\u2019s basic framework of how their magick works was useful to communicate the basic idea of the legacy, and may continue to inform certain aspects of it, but it\u2019s not strictly based off of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447257#post1447257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the drug use, I get that, but do you have a framework for the sorts of powers you want them to have?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think I want the Unveiling practice to be emphasized, but other than that, no. This is the earliest formations of the legacy, I probably won\u2019t have anything solid for a few days. And I will be in the middle of finals by then. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447257#post1447257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a Time/X Legacy that has orgies that reveal the future and a Prime/X Legacy that drops acid to navigate the raw symbolism of the Universe are both valid.</div> </div> </div> </div> yeah, and of the two I would lean toward the Prime option, but that\u2019s just because I don\u2019t get the connection between sex/drugs/any other ecstatic practice and Time. That\u2019s not to say there is not one, it\u2019s just a connection I personally can\u2019t see.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T17:02:30-07:00","id":1447301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447232#post1447232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">New question: Is there a official timeline of the Nameless War (I love that name), and the Great Refusal?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I expect that or something close to it would be in the history section of the Free Council book (at this time the last remaining absence from my collection).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mind, I would find it logical that the Nameless War didn't exactly lend itself to a straightforward timeline. Not when it was distributed across so many fronts of numerous columns who had common cause but loose organisation. I expect that when it comes to compiling information about the thing, many Awakened scholars would find it easier to make timelines in the history of particular Assemblies, or some of the most famous columns and Strategos, rather than a singular cohesive timeline covering the whole effort.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And even then I expect that there are a lot of secrets that were never jotted down and that the interests of cohesion in the Pentacle would prefer to let lie. Cruel actions taking place in the shadows that could still spark outrage if brought up.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Still, I'll be interested to see what the book makes of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(As far as I'm concerned, Kosciej the Deathless is close enough to canon as one of the Free Council's Founders, although not exactly in a position to create a new Celestial Ladder.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447255#post1447255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">To Ecstatics, they are not simple chemicals, they are tools to expand their minds and turn their perceptions inside-out.</span></span></span><br /> I just have trouble associating Time with altered perceptions. The only spells or attainments that would work would seem to be unveiling, and neither of times two example spells fit well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let me have a look...<br /> <br /> Time 1: Divination and Postcognition can qualify after a fashion, but Perfect Timing is probably the closest to a sense of altered perceptions focused in the here and now (which might be more of an Ecstatic thing).<br /> Time 2: Choose the Thread has that element of glimpsing to improve the efficiency of actions, and the experience of Tipping the Hourglass to speed up and slow down the experience of time has a perceptual element. One might opt to portray Constant Presence as a kind of firm awareness of self that can't be infringed upon.<br /> Time 3: Acceleration could be regarded as an extreme increase in perceptual speed. A thematically modified version of Temporal Summoning could make the reclaimed past self less of a physical thing and more evoking a prior state of mind for purposes of reclaiming lost perspectives or exploring alternative ways they might have developed. <br /> Time 4: Present as Past has a pretty direct perceptual element, I think, a heightened state of awareness for events that are about to happen, and an openly stated element for social interaction either in becoming harder to persuade from anticipating all approaches or seeing paths directly to another's heart. Prophecy might be closer to a perceptual thing than actual Divination is, since it's based not on analysing what will be but meditating on possible outcomes for hypothetical actions or methods that might be used to achieve a desired result. Rewrite History could build off of that prior rendition of Temporal Summoning, a mage being able to immerse themselves in the memory of learning skills and other experiences with such a heightened state of mind that they can effectively construct how those efforts might have gone into different paths in life.<br /> Time 5: Blink of an Eye or Temporal Pocket are basically Philip Fry on 100 cups of coffee, your mind racing to such a degree that everything else seems to be standing still in comparison.<br /> <br /> In addition, while there are no published spells to affect Temporal Sympathy, it is stated how the experience of that has a perceptual element; a stronger sympathy creates a sense of more &quot;closeness&quot; to the time in question, making the memory of it easier and more vivid and compelling, and a destroyed sympathy is said to cause memory of a history to fade away. One could include elements for a mage to manipulate their own sympathy along those lines, perhaps in a bit of reverse order whereby what they can recall or obscure being the part that alters the actual substance of the thread.<br /> <br /> At a moment like this, I think the descriptions of Mage Sight in Signs of Sorcery could be useful, the descriptions of what each Arcanum looks like to each Path. Time as a Cult of Ecstasy might regard it could be more fitting to Mastigos than Acanthus, and its internally focused purposes could be something that aligns with common Mastigos aspirations of self-awareness and mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T17:36:01-07:00","id":1447308,"title":"","content":"To expand a bit with new insight, one thing I'd imagine about the Nameless War in the current milieu is that different historiographers have different opinions about what even qualified as a starting point (assuming it could be given a direct one rather than being seen as a trickle of hostilities gathering momentum over time). A traditional narrative might hold it as a 19th century thing, but having just started reading Dark Eras 2 I could imagine some scholars holding that the Silver Ladder residents of the American colonies opening hostilities with the Nameless Order established in the Pirate Republic in the early 1700s constitutes the true start point of the War. That it was a major inciting incident of the Diamond conducting hostilities with mages firmly apart from their society, and with an ethos reminiscent of a prototype Free Assembly to boot. Plus the part where the Ladder could be seen as responding with undue violence to a Mystery implying that ethos (which the later Free Council might regard as demonstrating Humanity as Magical and/or refutation of hierarchy) could actually change the Supernal.<br /> <br /> Even if there was a gap between that war and the dedicated fighting of Nameless and Diamond, perhaps original agitators would point back to what happened both as a demonstration that the Atlantean mysticism was not as preeminent as the Orders held it to be but that their hostility to such a truth demonstrated that co-existence with them was impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T20:32:56-07:00","id":1447326,"title":"","content":"Well, I had a nice well written response, but I managed to accidentally delete it by accidentally refreshing the page. The idea was that I thought the spells relating to the present were the best choice with the order going: Perfect Timing, Chose the Thread, mental only Temporal Summoning, Present as Past, and the final attainment would be Rewrite History with a extra reach. The general reasoning was I wanted the legacy to be very internal, and the other options were too physical or situational.<br /> Even before I read the post, I was thinking Acanthus or Mastigos as the path. I\u2019m sorry this isn\u2019t in great detail but I\u2019m tired and I just deleted the work of a better part of a hour by accident. You haven\u2019t quite convinced me Time would be best Primary Arcanum, but this write up sold me on it being a good option. You have given me much to ponder... tomorrow if I have time because if I\u2019m tired enough to accidentally delete my post, I\u2019m not in a fit state of mind for history questions.<br /> <br /> Edit: I forgot to mention, my current idea was by drinking a solution of Lunargent, Hermium, and Alkahest as the first potion, one might be able to see spirits or something else in twilight for that seeing real things nobody else can effect. Yes, the potion is supposed to be extremely deadly, you need spells at first to survive it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-03-2021, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T01:25:40-07:00","id":1447370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447326#post1447326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I had a nice well written response, but I managed to accidentally delete it by accidentally refreshing the page.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that pain. You have my sympathies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T10:14:26-07:00","id":1447417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447232#post1447232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question: Is there a official timeline of the Nameless War (I love that name), and the Great Refusal?</div> </div> </div> </div>So it turns out that the original Free Council book opted to be pretty bare bones about the nature and history of the Nameless War. There's context for <i>why</i> there were lots of revolutionary Nameless opposed to the Diamond through the 19th century, and that they were intertwined with Sleeper revolutions, but not much about events.<br /> <br /> The Great Refusal does receive a bit of elaboration, though, in terms of more nuanced and messy history. Its stated that Seer emissaries made contact with Nameless groups as early as 1895, that there were ongoing rejections based in ideology that prompted violent reprisal from Seers, and then some prominent figures promoting and coordinating a plan to string Seers along until they were vulnerable, complicated by columns who actually wanted to join up, leading to the game being given away early and efforts divided between hitting Seers and purging those among their own who were looking to join.<br /> <br /> New Year's Eve 1899 is maintained as the official date of the Assembly that brought them together as a fully realised Order, while the Silver Ladder book briefly described the Great Convocation that resolved to invite them into an alliance.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'd maintain the idea that the Nameless War took a form that defies compiling a straightforward timeline as opposed to describing a century of continuous hostility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T06:24:45-07:00","id":1447805,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for mages to protect other supernatural beings against their bans and banes? For example, veiling a Vampire from the sun with Force or a Werewolf/Changeling from silver/iron with Matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T06:36:07-07:00","id":1447806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447805#post1447805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for mages to protect other supernatural beings against their bans and banes? For example, veiling a Vampire from the sun with Force or a Werewolf/Changeling from silver/iron with Matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, but it would require a Shielding, Veiling hides the phenomenon rather than defend against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T06:51:41-07:00","id":1447808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447805#post1447805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for mages to protect other supernatural beings against their bans and banes? For example, veiling a Vampire from the sun with Force or a Werewolf/Changeling from silver/iron with Matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the sense of removing a Bane or Ban from the supernatural being, but mages can definitely do a lot to prevent interactions. Forces Shielding can prevent sunlight and fire from hitting the vampire. Matter can make a werewolf physically repel silver, but should something be able to force silver through the spell's effect to make contact, the werewolf will react as usual. Same thing for changelings and iron, but even the presence of iron can do a lot to mess with changelings, and that's difficult to do anything about without straight up removing the iron completely from the location.<br /> Bans can be a lot more difficult to circumvent depending on their nature, but Fate can go a long way to avoid situations where a Ban would come into effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-07-2021, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T06:56:03-07:00","id":1447809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447805#post1447805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for mages to protect other supernatural beings against their bans and banes? For example, veiling a Vampire from the sun with Force or a Werewolf/Changeling from silver/iron with Matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>What others said; messing with 'templates' is generally archmage territory, at least for Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T11:27:00-07:00","id":1447833,"title":"","content":"A Patterning of Spirit can transform a spirit's Ban and Bane, can't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T11:33:14-07:00","id":1447834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1447833#post1447833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Patterning of Spirit can transform a spirit's Ban and Bane, can't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's an explicit effect of the spell <i>Shape Spirit</i> (MtAw 2e pg 184).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T12:59:01-07:00","id":1447836,"title":"","content":"It still needs to be fitting to Rank, and I would say you can't be totally arbitrary about it so it has to match the spirit's nature unless some of the Potency changed that as well, but I expect it would suffice to remove a spirit's vulnerability to a thing that is currently in their presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T08:26:01-07:00","id":1448046,"title":"","content":"If I use Forge Thaumium (SoS, 62) with high Duration or even make it Lasting, does its Clash of Wills dice pool gain bonuses from duration (Mage, 118)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T08:37:34-07:00","id":1448047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448046#post1448046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I use Forge Thaumium (SoS, 62) with high Duration or even make it Lasting, does its Clash of Wills dice pool gain bonuses from duration (Mage, 118)?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd get the Duration bonuses. In this particular case (but not with most other spells) you'd get the full +4 if it's lasting instead of whatever bonus you would've gotten from the spell's Duration. It's the longevity of the effect that matters, not the underlying spell. It's just that spells generally stop having an effect when they end, and any lasting effects tends to not be supernatural and thus won't Clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T18:53:09-07:00","id":1448374,"title":"","content":"What would be the effects (if any) of an Exarch adding a legacies symbolism to their symbolism? The idea is that a legacy founder made a legacy, then much later in life \u201csold\u201d the legacy to the Chancellor in exchange for exceptional knowledge and power. What would happen to anyone bearing the legacy afterward?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T20:41:38-07:00","id":1448384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448374#post1448374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the effects (if any) of an Exarch adding a legacies symbolism to their symbolism? The idea is that a legacy founder made a legacy, then much later in life \u201csold\u201d the legacy to the Chancellor in exchange for exceptional knowledge and power. What would happen to anyone bearing the legacy afterward?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would need more information, given that the Exarchs being tied to a thing tends to represent itself in the Exarchs' symbolism being added to the other thing rather than the other way around.<br /> <br /> And much as the Tremere can't make a House out of any old Legacy, I don't imagine you're likely to see an Exarch taking a personal interest in a Legacy that isn't already suited to being an instrument of Tyranny \u2014 at which point the effect is &quot;the Legacy sold out to the Architects of the Lie and its membership and particulars shifted accordingly.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T21:26:49-07:00","id":1448387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448384#post1448384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would need more information, given that the Exarchs being tied to a thing tends to represent itself in the Exarchs' symbolism being added to the other thing rather than the other way around.<br /> <br /> And much as the Tremere can't make a House out of any old Legacy, I don't imagine you're likely to see an Exarch taking a personal interest in a Legacy that isn't already suited to being an instrument of Tyranny \u2014 at which point the effect is &quot;the Legacy sold out to the Architects of the Lie and its membership and particulars shifted accordingly.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, so Bellow as Above? I guess if the fallen and Supernal both influence each other, the action in the fallen and the Supernal are the same thing. Assuming the legacy isn\u2019t a hive mind, and some peoples object it becomes a variant of the legacy? I guess a lot of legacies have left handed variations. I guess there\u2019s probably not Supernal copyright Lawyers coming to destroy anything that infringes the Exarch\u2019s claim on something, just the seers that try to kill or subvert the remaining legacy members.<br /> <br /> Interesting to note that the Exarchs get added to something, rather than the other way around. That\u2019s because otherwise it would violate the Pax, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T21:53:38-07:00","id":1448388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448387#post1448387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, so Bellow as Above? I guess if the fallen and Supernal both influence each other, the action in the fallen and the Supernal are the same thing. Assuming the legacy isn\u2019t a hive mind, and some peoples object it becomes a variant of the legacy? I guess a lot of legacies have left handed variations. I guess there\u2019s probably not Supernal copyright Lawyers coming to destroy anything that infringes the Exarch\u2019s claim on something, just the seers that try to kill or subvert the remaining legacy members.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically. That strengthened sympathy between Legacy members can make ideological disputes within the group rather tense, I'd imagine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interesting to note that the Exarchs get added to something, rather than the other way around. That\u2019s because otherwise it would violate the Pax, right? </div> </div> </div>More that the Exarchs' aggregate symbolism tends to be pretty\u2026 blatant. Iron Seals in Aedes being oppressively overt in their symbolic language, their Ochemata's true forms being wildly out of harmony with themselves, Mystery Commands locking out Prelates' other Obsessions until they're followed, etc.<br /> <br /> Plus, y'know, the Exarchs are the foremost advocates for the relationship between the Supernal and the Phenomenal being a one-way street, and that means the de facto rulers of the heavens don't need to lower themselves to bargaining with Fallen beings who aren't tractable to the carrot and stick for stuff they wouldn't be using anyway. It's not like with the Mysterium, where they're squirreling away a million diverse magical curiosities for a rainy day \u2014 there's a world of difference between putting a Legacy's secrets in cold storage and turning them into an extension of an established power.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at, I suppose, is that there's a very good case to be made for the Legacy founder having joined up with the Seers and taken what students would come along with them. It may be worth exploring the schism in progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T01:01:05-07:00","id":1448396,"title":"","content":"Magic is payment, but it's for service not products. I can only see a scenario where the Exarchs provide some great boon in exchange for a Legacy when the nature of the Legacy is offensive and something about the possessor means that it's preferable to Excise it rather than just Command a Seer to kill them.<br /> <br /> Perhaps occasionally a mage who joined up later in their career was required to have a Legacy ripped out as a show of good faith. True Power requires Sacrifice. Mind, I think that's a business where the person is directed to present themselves before a Tetrarch who will actually undertake the deed. It's a bit beneath the Exarchs to attend to that sort of thing personally.<br /> <br /> Invoking the symbolism of the Exarchs for power is a show of submission. On the occasions where it isn't, you're dancing to the edge of a line where they will drag you off and either make you submit or kill you. I expect those rare Pentacle mages who come back alive from their trip through the Iron Door have a lot of work to do to redress their deficit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T14:41:29-07:00","id":1448537,"title":"","content":"Player A\u2019s character casts a spell with exceptional success on Player B\u2019s character. Player B then resolves the condition in the scene. Who gets the arcane beat? Player A or Player B? <br /> <br /> For the life of me I can\u2019t find this answered in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11410-mclugh","name":"McLugh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T15:00:15-07:00","id":1448539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McLugh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448537#post1448537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player A\u2019s character casts a spell with exceptional success on Player B\u2019s character. Player B then resolves the condition in the scene. Who gets the arcane beat? Player A or Player B? <br /> <br /> For the life of me I can\u2019t find this answered in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who was the Condition attached to? That\u2019s the one who gets the Beat, I think; not the one who made the Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T15:11:32-07:00","id":1448541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McLugh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448537#post1448537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player A\u2019s character casts a spell with exceptional success on Player B\u2019s character. Player B then resolves the condition in the scene. Who gets the arcane beat? Player A or Player B?<br /> <br /> For the life of me I can\u2019t find this answered in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> <br /> The person with the condition gets the beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T15:34:57-07:00","id":1448542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448539#post1448539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who was the Condition attached to? That\u2019s the one who gets the Beat, I think; not the one who made the Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Player B is the subject of both the spell and the condition, apologies for being unclear there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11410-mclugh","name":"McLugh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T15:40:38-07:00","id":1448544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McLugh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448542#post1448542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Player B is the subject of both the spell and the condition, apologies for being unclear there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then B it is. This way we can have swim-or-sink mentors who deliberately afflict pupils with maladies to make them grow, which I think was once said by the writers to be a thing in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T16:46:38-07:00","id":1448549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448544#post1448544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then B it is. This way we can have swim-or-sink mentors who deliberately afflict pupils with maladies to make them grow, which I think was once said by the writers to be a thing in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the sidebar titled &quot;The Beat Goes On...&quot; on page 126 of the MtAw2e book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T17:04:02-07:00","id":1448551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448549#post1448549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the sidebar titled &amp;quot;The Beat Goes On...&amp;quot; on page 126 of the MtAw2e book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it really was one of the writers then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T13:47:53-07:00","id":1448617,"title":"","content":"If you have a broom under the Possessed Manifestation, does it allow it to fly and sweep on its own ? Because moving and sweeping are things that would be done to it under normal use, would that be considered a valid use ? If an ephemeral entity Possesses an entire house or complex, how fine tuned its control would be ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T13:59:24-07:00","id":1448620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448617#post1448617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a broom under the Possessed Manifestation, does it allow it to fly and sweep on its own ? Because moving and sweeping are things that would be done to it under normal use, would that be considered a valid use ? If an ephemeral entity Possesses an entire house or complex, how fine tuned its control would be ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's beyond the intention of the power. It specifically mentions corpses and articulated objects as being capable of movement, because given only manipulation of their own parts they could move by themselves. A broom is a mostly static object with no proper moving parts. A possessed broom could bend its bristles but not much else unless the entity spends Essence to go beyond the object's limits (and cause damage to it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T08:55:28-07:00","id":1448694,"title":"","content":"Quick Question: Is a spell to guarantee a ghost forms when a person dies Ruling or Patterning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T09:42:59-07:00","id":1448698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448694#post1448694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick Question: Is a spell to guarantee a ghost forms when a person dies Ruling or Patterning?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Haunting&quot; spell from 1e is Patterning; &quot;Ghostly Object,&quot; which turns a destroyed item into an object in Twilight, is Weaving in 1e.<br /> <br /> Given the changes to ghosts between editions and the fact that 2e's example spells were made specifically to match effects to their Practices instead of attaching a Practice to the Arcanum level the spell felt like it should be at, this may not be much precedent (Quicken Ghost dropped from Death 5 to Death 3, for instance), but considering that making a ghost from scratch based on an existing person is a Making effect and ghosts aren't the beings that produce them, it seems reasonable to put it at Patterning as a rewiring of someone's Death Pattern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T10:09:22-07:00","id":1448702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1448694#post1448694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick Question: Is a spell to guarantee a ghost forms when a person dies Ruling or Patterning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating water out of thin air is Making. Transforming a rock to water is Patterning. Getting water out of ice (which naturally transforms into liquid water at the right conditions) is Weaving.<br /> <br /> Creating a ghost wholesale is Making. Transforming someone into a ghost (if possible; templates and such) would be Patterning. Destroying an object and guaranteeing that it becomes a ghost (or Castoff, if we're to use the correct terms) is Weaving as per Ghost Gate. Removing the destructive/transformative aspect of it and simply guaranteeing that a subject who dies or is destroyed leaves a ghost, I would say Ruling because you're simply forcing one possible outcome of a natural process. Not everyone might agree with that, but it's certainly not more difficult than Weaving; we already have an official example that Weaving is enough for objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T10:53:41-07:00","id":1448706,"title":"","content":"Thank you Satchel and Tessie.<br /> I\u2019m going to go and say it\u2019s both, with slightly different effects. The Ruling makes a completely \u201cnormal\u201d ghost, and the Patterning one makes a ghost under the mages influence, whether it turns back into someone or their shadow depending on how a mage makes it when the spell expires. I will be using the ruling option for the Singer\u2019s in Silence, as that fits them better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T11:14:31-07:00","id":1449473,"title":"","content":"The Limited Use Item spells from SoS all have a stated cost of 1 mana. They also say that a mage must spend 1 mana to then store a spell in the item. At first I assumed that these were the same cost, but reading closer I think they are separate. Is this correct, that effectively a limited-use item will always cost at least two mana (one to cast, one per spell stored)? (Conversely, Hung Spell from the core has no upfront mana cost, only the cost for storing spells.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T11:26:34-07:00","id":1449475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1449473#post1449473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Limited Use Item spells from SoS all have a stated cost of 1 mana. They also say that a mage must spend 1 mana to then store a spell in the item. At first I assumed that these were the same cost, but reading closer I think they are separate. Is this correct, that effectively a limited-use item will always cost at least two mana (one to cast, one per spell stored)? (Conversely, Hung Spell from the core has no upfront mana cost, only the cost for storing spells.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the Mana is spent on storage, not just to create the item, though it is confusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T19:42:33-07:00","id":1449740,"title":"","content":"Has there been any discussion/sources on what the precise Arcana requirements for manipulating Glamour are? That section in Dark Eras 2 was tantalizing in it's brevity....<br /> <br /> In particular, I want to be able to transfer Glamour similar to the Channel Essence spell (Fate 1 + Mind 2 probably?), and to temporarily store it in something, like a cross between the Mana Battery spell and the Bottle Glamour dread power (Fate 2 + Mind 2, maybe? Glamour seems to take varied forms and/or infuse things easier than Mana).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T20:39:53-07:00","id":1449750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1449740#post1449740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any discussion/sources on what the precise Arcana requirements for manipulating Glamour are? That section in Dark Eras 2 was tantalizing in it's brevity....<br /> <br /> In particular, I want to be able to transfer Glamour similar to the Channel Essence spell (Fate 1 + Mind 2 probably?), and to temporarily store it in something, like a cross between the Mana Battery spell and the Bottle Glamour dread power (Fate 2 + Mind 2, maybe? Glamour seems to take varied forms and/or infuse things easier than Mana).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say Fate 2 + Mind 1 or 2. Both Fate and Mind are needed for fae-magic, but it seems Fate is given more weight in general.<br /> <br /> ...... But then again, Glamour is basically psychic energy, so it may be Mind 2 + Fate 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Scratch that, just read Dark Eras 2. Mind is more important for Glamour manipulation. So Mind 2 + Fate 1, or Fate 2. Malleable Thorns is Mind 2 + Fate 2, so we could say Glamour bottling is Mind 2 + Fate 1 for sake of avoiding too much overlapping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T21:08:41-07:00","id":1449753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1449750#post1449750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd say Fate 2 + Mind 1 or 2. Both Fate and Mind are needed for fae-magic, but it seems Fate is given more weight in general.<br /> <br /> ...... But then again, Glamour is basically psychic energy, so it may be Mind 2 + Fate 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Scratch that, just read Dark Eras 2. Mind is more important for Glamour manipulation. So Mind 2 + Fate 1, or Fate 2. Malleable Thorns is Mind 2 + Fate 2, so we could say Glamour bottling is Mind 2 + Fate 1 for sake of avoiding too much overlapping.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the exact sequence of conclusions my brain followed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T20:59:28-07:00","id":1449921,"title":"","content":"Wait, how did we calculate costs for Enhanced Items again? Was it the same as Imbued Items?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind - the obvious idea of just using the rule in the core never occurred to me for some reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T08:42:21-07:00","id":1450178,"title":"","content":"Quick question for my legacy: Is it Weaving to add the Mana generation properties of a Hallow to a Node? Or is it Making or Patterning?<br /> <br /> Edit: Does anyone know where the Ghost Mage rules are for 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T14:03:24-07:00","id":1450225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450178#post1450178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question for my legacy: Is it Weaving to add the Mana generation properties of a Hallow to a Node? Or is it Making or Patterning?<br /> <br /> Edit: Does anyone know where the Ghost Mage rules are for 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaving can transfer the properties from one to another, analogous to <i>Wonderful Machine</i> from Matter.<br /> <br /> Regarding ghost mages, a 2ed conversion can be found here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/05/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-ghost-mages_7.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/05/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-ghost-mages_7.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/05/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-ghost-mages_7.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/05/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-ghost-mages_7.html?m=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There are also some interesting Legacies in there, I recommend the Transhuman Engineers and Fortune Dealers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T14:23:48-07:00","id":1450228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450225#post1450225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weaving can transfer the properties from one to another, analogous to <i>Wonderful Machine</i> from Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div> So without a Hallow inside or beside the node, I can't give the Node Mana generating properties? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450225#post1450225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding ghost mages, a 2ed conversion can be found here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/05/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-ghost-mages_7.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/05/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-ghost-mages_7.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/05/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-ghost-mages_7.html?m=1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/05/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-ghost-mages_7.html?m=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There are also some interesting Legacies in there, I recommend the Transhuman Engineers and Fortune Dealers.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T03:45:17-07:00","id":1450300,"title":"","content":"I'll note that per old statements from Dave Brookshaw as developer, there are two kinds of ghost mages.<br /> <br /> In most cases, it's just the ghost of a mage; they might be unusually cogent and get Influences and Numina reminiscent of their rotes and praxes, but are otherwise nothing special and cannot use Supernal magic.<br /> <br /> In some cases, mages undergo processes to basically transform their living selves into ghosts; they become ephemeral beings and I think still get tied to anchors and the Underworld, but retain the entirety of their consciousness and full range of their powers. This constitutes a form of lich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T06:15:41-07:00","id":1450442,"title":"","content":"Since I\u2019m back at the drawing board, I have generated new ideas. Yeah, I know most of these don\u2019t have rules. Anyway:<br /> 1) What would the effect be of a Perfected Node?<br /> 2) What would Perfected Resonance do?<br /> 3) Pneuma is Perfected Mana, right?<br /> 4) Would a Aedes that shows up in every Supernal World be a appropriate Final Attainment?<br /> 4.5) Would it be better to have a separate Aedes for every World, changed by the World\u2019s symbolism?<br /> 5) What would a Perfected Nimbus be like?<br /> <br /> Edit: Is a Manteion better than a Aedes since it\u2019s tied to a physical place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-31-2021, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T07:04:29-07:00","id":1450445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450442#post1450442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I\u2019m back at the drawing board, I have generated new ideas. Yeah, I know most of these don\u2019t have rules. Anyway:<br /> 1) What would the effect be of a Perfected Node?<br /> 2) What would Perfected Resonance do?<br /> 3) Pneuma is Perfected Mana, right?<br /> 4) Would a Aedes that shows up in every Supernal World be a appropriate Final Attainment?<br /> 4.5) Would it be better to have a separate Aedes for every World, changed by the World\u2019s symbolism?<br /> 5) What would a Perfected Nimbus be like?<br /> <br /> Edit: Is a Manteion better than a Aedes since it\u2019s tied to a physical place?</div> </div> </div> </div>1, 2 &amp; 5- They have never been officially defined, so you would need to apply some creative thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> 3- Pneuma is the pure, undiluted energy of the Supernal, before being sublimated into the Fallen World. This is what archmages build their Golden Roads out of. Its not perfected mana, but rather the most purified and raw expression of Supernal energy that exists. Its also one of the rarest, most valuable, nearly legendarily rare magical materials a normal mage could ever get their hands on.<br /> <br /> 4- Since no mage normally has the perspective of all the Watchtowers, that would normally be impossible. Creating an Aedes, especially one that exists in all the known Supernal Realms, would require either one of the most powerful archmages in the modern day or a incredibly rare and dangerous Atlantean device, bleeding edge even by their standards. Its punching way above the weight class of what a final Attainment should be able to accomplish.<br /> <br /> 4.5- You would require very high mastery of both Arcana of that Realm. The spell would be of the Practice of Dominions, which means the caster would need at least 8 dots in both Arcana and the required Quintessence. All that is squarely in the domain of archmages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T07:31:10-07:00","id":1450450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450445#post1450445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1, 2 &amp; 5- They have never been officially defined, so you would need to apply some creative thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> 3- Pneuma is the pure, undiluted energy of the Supernal, before being sublimated into the Fallen World. This is what archmages build their Golden Roads out of. Its not perfected mana, but rather the most purified and raw expression of Supernal energy that exists. Its also one of the rarest, most valuable, nearly legendarily rare magical materials a normal mage could ever get their hands on.<br /> <br /> 4- Since no mage normally has the perspective of all the Watchtowers, that would normally be impossible. Creating an Aedes, especially one that exists in all the known Supernal Realms, would require either one of the most powerful archmages in the modern day or a incredibly rare and dangerous Atlantean device, bleeding edge even by their standards. Its punching way above the weight class of what a final Attainment should be able to accomplish.<br /> <br /> 4.5- You would require very high mastery of both Arcana of that Realm. The spell would be of the Practice of Dominions, which means the caster would need at least 8 dots in both Arcana and the required Quintessence. All that is squarely in the domain of archmages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for answering. I guess 3-4.5 were long shots anyways. 1,2,and 5 means I will have to make them myself. Probably not in cards for the legacy anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T09:07:02-07:00","id":1450457,"title":"","content":"Nodes are something like weak inverse Annullities, right? They strengthen Supernal symbolism instead of weakening it. If this is correct a Perfected Node should logically have the opposite effect of it's respective Annullity. A Perfected Life Node heals Damage very turn, a Perfected Space Node gives navigation rolls the rote quality and all Irises are automatically opened and sympathetic connections raise by 2 steps.. etc. All spells using that Arcanum gain 2 dice that isn't a Yantra...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T10:03:25-07:00","id":1450463,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit on how much Mana a mage can draw form a Manteion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T16:36:49-07:00","id":1450518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450442#post1450442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">4) Would a Aedes that shows up in every Supernal World be a appropriate Final Attainment?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What exactly do you mean by this? Like, creating an Aedes with the Fifth Attainment of a Legacy?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450445#post1450445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4- Since no mage normally has the perspective of all the Watchtowers, that would normally be impossible. Creating an Aedes, especially one that exists in all the known Supernal Realms, would require either one of the most powerful archmages in the modern day or a incredibly rare and dangerous Atlantean device, bleeding edge even by their standards. Its punching way above the weight class of what a final Attainment should be able to accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I feel as though Aedes might be a reasonable way to convey awareness of Imperium Rites and other actions in the Supernal that any archmaster is capable of taking.<br /> <br /> Considering that archmages have no Paths, the subject of how they interact with particular Supernal Realms is a bit up in the air, particularly considering that Iron Seals are also perceived by all Mage Sight. I'm thinking that an archmage equivalent of such would be way smaller by default and uncommon because action that would create such constitutes a significant affront against the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450457#post1450457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nodes are something like weak inverse Annullities, right? They strengthen Supernal symbolism instead of weakening it. If this is correct a Perfected Node should logically have the opposite effect of it's respective Annullity. A Perfected Life Node heals Damage very turn, a Perfected Space Node gives navigation rolls the rote quality and all Irises are automatically opened and sympathetic connections raise by 2 steps.. etc. All spells using that Arcanum gain 2 dice that isn't a Yantra...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Supernal Verges and demesnes are really the opposite of Annulities. Nodes are described in the Mage core, they're just spots where intersecting ley lines provide a mixture of Resonances (which can be useful for harvesting tass that can have varied Yantra applications, if they happen to coincide with a Hallow) and can provide extra energy via a Prime spell.<br /> <br /> I actually think that when the whole Perfected material concept works on the logic of giving something mundane a form more like it possesses in the Supernal, then things that already have Supernal qualities cannot be Perfected any further (at least alone those lines, you might still cast a Practice of Perfecting to enhance them). Mages debate exactly how Supernal Nodes are, but I'd say they are enough to not really be subject to that transformation.<br /> <br /> The relationship between mana and Pneuma is a bit interesting, because mana is described as the palpable form of the Supernal presence in the Fallen World, while Pneuma is the symbol of energy present in the Supernal itself. So I'd think you can't really Perfect mana because it's already in its best form for the frame of reference in which you can interact with it, while Pneuma is something that only makes sense in the presence of the true Supernal, barring the exceptional closeness to the Supernal experienced by one undergoing Awakening (and even then, once being in the Watchtower's Lustrum ends, it rapidly assumes the form of mana, going back to the idea of that being the state of Supernal substance in the Fallen World). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450463#post1450463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a limit on how much Mana a mage can draw form a Manteion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it says that you only get one point per qualifying action, but otherwise it would appear there is not, just so long as one can continuously cast spells appropriate to the Manteion's legend.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly stated in the rules, but I would interpret the concept in terms where you can't exactly keep repeating the same legendary gesture over and over until it becomes mundane. That you'd have to draw on different steps to adhere to the fact that the symbols correspond with an unfolding narrative, rather than being something singular.<br /> <br /> Either way, though, it would reflect the fact that they're a particularly rare mystical resource.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T17:59:49-07:00","id":1450523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450518#post1450518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What exactly do you mean by this? Like, creating an Aedes with the Fifth Attainment of a Legacy?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. For context, I\u2019m making a legacy and the 5th attainment is giving me a problem. So I\u2019m coming up with any possible effect that might fit, and will pick one from there. It started with the creation of a artificial Soul Stone, but the problem is Demesnes are too potent and too small. I would like some wide range effect that significantly changes landscape for mages, that doesn\u2019t hurt sleepers by its nature, and one that\u2019s potent enough to be comparable with a artificial Demesne. Everything is either not in theme or way too powerful a effect for the legacy. So I\u2019m coming up with every possible idea, so I can eliminate the ones that don\u2019t work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450518#post1450518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I feel as though Aedes might be a reasonable way to convey awareness of Imperium Rites and other actions in the Supernal that any archmaster is capable of taking.</div> </div> </div> </div> It\u2019s a Dominions effect though, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450518#post1450518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that archmages have no Paths, the subject of how they interact with particular Supernal Realms is a bit up in the air, particularly considering that Iron Seals are also perceived by all Mage Sight. I'm thinking that an archmage equivalent of such would be way smaller by default and uncommon because action that would create such constitutes a significant affront against the Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought Archmasters could experience and effect every Supernal Realm they wanted, included the ones not accessible to regular mages. If a non arch-master level Legacy could make one, they would probably play a big part in the ascension war. They probably would be great pawns, because they weren\u2019t arch master but messed with the field significantly anyways. Makes me think it\u2019s not possible because that seems like the thing that would change the setting a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450518#post1450518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Supernal Verges and demesnes are really the opposite of Annulities. Nodes are described in the Mage core, they're just spots where intersecting ley lines provide a mixture of Resonances (which can be useful for harvesting tass that can have varied Yantra applications, if they happen to coincide with a Hallow) and can provide extra energy via a Prime spell.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I would agree because that\u2019s literally the definition of a Annulity, but Annulities break down the Fallen laws of reality in a way Demesnes don\u2019t reinforce them. Demesnes boost the Connection to the Supernal, while Annulities push the Fallen towards something like the Lower Depths. Nodes do a much weaker form of the opposite, reinforcing the Fallen to the Attuned. Perfected substances seem to have two rules, new supernatural properties based on their symbolism or perfect properties of their physical properties. I figured a Perfected Node would have mechanics that mirrored Annulities in their mechanics if they were even possible. I still am unsure what properties a Node has to perfect (as in the Practice). Maybe the ones with a dice bonus can be increased, but how does provide all the energy need of devices hooked up to get better?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450518#post1450518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that when the whole Perfected material concept works on the logic of giving something mundane a form more like it possesses in the Supernal, then things that already have Supernal qualities cannot be Perfected any further (at least alone those lines, you might still cast a Practice of Perfecting to enhance them). Mages debate exactly how Supernal Nodes are, but I'd say they are enough to not really be subject to that transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div> So you don\u2019t think resonance has different properties in the Supernal that can be brought to it\u2019s Fallen form? You are probably correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450518#post1450518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The relationship between mana and Pneuma is a bit interesting, because mana is described as the palpable form of the Supernal presence in the Fallen World, while Pneuma is the symbol of energy present in the Supernal itself. So I'd think you can't really Perfect mana because it's already in its best form for the frame of reference in which you can interact with it, while Pneuma is something that only makes sense in the presence of the true Supernal, barring the exceptional closeness to the Supernal experienced by one undergoing Awakening (and even then, once being in the Watchtower's Lustrum ends, it rapidly assumes the form of mana, going back to the idea of that being the state of Supernal substance in the Fallen World).</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, if it could be generated, it probably wouldn\u2019t be so sought after by other mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450518#post1450518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it says that you only get one point per qualifying action, but otherwise it would appear there is not, just so long as one can continuously cast spells appropriate to the Manteion's legend.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly stated in the rules, but I would interpret the concept in terms where you can't exactly keep repeating the same legendary gesture over and over until it becomes mundane. That you'd have to draw on different steps to adhere to the fact that the symbols correspond with an unfolding narrative, rather than being something singular.<br /> <br /> Either way, though, it would reflect the fact that they're a particularly rare mystical resource.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s probably a good rule of thumb. I was thinking it was kinda like legacy oblations where you can only get a number of mana equal to the highest legacy arcanum, only without the restriction on which arcanum it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-31-2021, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T20:21:14-07:00","id":1450540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450523#post1450523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a Dominions effect though, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I don't believe Imperial Mysteries had much to say on the matter of casting spells within or upon things of the Supernal. It may be that Imperium Rites are necessary to accomplish anything of force there.<br /> <br /> That being said, I don't think creation of an Aedes as such would be Dominion, although bonding oneself to one may be. Keeping in mind that an Aedes is a prominent Supernal ecology and the Practice of Dominions is about incorporating a subject into one's soul (or evoking something, an Ochema, out of it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Archmasters could experience and effect every Supernal Realm they wanted, included the ones not accessible to regular mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that gets into questions regular mages can only speculate upon concerning whether or not Supernal Realms strictly exist outside of their Paths engaging with them, plus questions of how to reconcile Imperial Mysteries to the revised presentation of the Supernal. As it stands though, I don't recall the book presenting archmage sojourns to the Supernal in terms of the familiar Realms; rather, they move around one Lustrum at a time, even if that Lustrum incorporates multiple symbols. So when you're interacting with the Hunter in Green, a recognisable world doesn't exist beyond the boundaries of that interaction, because you haven't made it take such a form for the sake of not being obliterated yet.<br /> <br /> Of course Emanations add further complications to this.<br /> <br /> I suppose the simplest idea could be that the actions of Seekers in the Supernal at times create effects that Travellers perceive as an Aedes of the Realm most fitting to its particular theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a non arch-master level Legacy could make one, they would probably play a big part in the ascension war. They probably would be great pawns, because they weren\u2019t arch master but messed with the field significantly anyways. Makes me think it\u2019s not possible because that seems like the thing that would change the setting a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see the nature of certain Aedes being of significance to certain Supernal beings, although for the most part the Ascension War is fought in the Fallen World. Within the Supernal the Exarchs are supposed to be quite secure in their palaces. It is the Fallen World and Sleepers within it that could undermine their dominance by weakening the phenomenal expression of their symbolism. Aedes alone don't necessarily threaten them on that count, as their effects are felt only by mages.<br /> <br /> (Too tired right now for the rest)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T20:31:29-07:00","id":1450542,"title":"","content":"Thank you for what you have written. Please rest well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T04:02:07-07:00","id":1450564,"title":"","content":"Quick question to the Mage 2ed. Becuase in the book it was not cleared but one reddit thread lead me here. When you roll for Wisdom? I know why: the act of Hubris. But i wonder when is it?&quot;<br /> Ater each instance of the Act of Hubris or is it after the scene (like when you roll Integrity or other Morality Rolls)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12764-zwinniak","name":"Zwinniak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T11:21:15-07:00","id":1450614,"title":"","content":"Minor Disclaimer: I haven't played the game yet, so I don't know if this works yet.<br /> Wisdom is the measure of control a mage has over their magic. It is threatened by acts that show lack of control (duh). A mage actually loses Wisdom by justifying their actions, telling themselves that what they are doing is Necessary, or Right, or Just. &quot; I did _____ because it ________ and that makes it ok&quot; . You probably know this. The reason I bring it up is because I think the time to make the roll is variable. A saintly mage doing their chores by magic in order to save time for study probably makes the roll right away. They have already justified their action. A warrior that makes a few bad calls during a battle probably makes the roll at the end of the Scene. A mage so driven by Obsession that they are hanging by a thread that finally snaps should roll Immediately. The examples go on. You can pick on or the other, but I think a hard and fast rule here makes you lose something. It's when the mage has time and the opportunity to think about their actions that Wisdom falters. Premeditated actions should always roll Immediately in my opinion, they have had time to think about it before hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T13:23:03-07:00","id":1450632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zwinniak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450564#post1450564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question to the Mage 2ed. Becuase in the book it was not cleared but one reddit thread lead me here. When you roll for Wisdom? I know why: the act of Hubris. But i wonder when is it?&quot;<br /> Ater each instance of the Act of Hubris or is it after the scene (like when you roll Integrity or other Morality Rolls)?</div> </div> </div> </div>No Integrity analogue on the books delays its risk or loss to the end of the scene without specific conditions that make it do so. You test your Wisdom after each Act of Hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T09:23:54-07:00","id":1450966,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s say I wanted a left handed leaning legacy interested in dolls, golems, and maybe turning people into dolls. What arcanum should that be, Matter/Life or Matter/Mind?<br /> edit: Maybe I should use both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 06-04-2021, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T10:33:07-07:00","id":1450967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450966#post1450966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let\u2019s say I wanted a left handed leaning legacy interested in dolls, golems, and maybe turning people into dolls. What arcanum should that be, Matter/Life or Matter/Mind?<br /> edit: Maybe I should use both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean by dolls and what you want to do with them. The awesome thing about Mage is that there are always multiple Arcana combinations that can be used to approach a problem.<br /> <br /> Lets say you want to create an archive of magical souls and knowledge, an artificial afterlife in defiance of the Psychopomp, a lore repository and emergency source of troops akin to the Infinity Circuit of the Eldar. Prime and Death could accomplish such a thing.<br /> <br /> Should you prefer to make living beings into golems, you would need a Patterning of Life and the target Arcanum. For manipulating dolls and creating golems, Matter could be of aid.<br /> <br /> Another approach is that the mage wants everything to be in a perfect pattern, all integrating into gears as the mage makes optimal decisions with absolute certainty and builds mechanical enforcers of their perfect timeline, akin to the Vex from Destiny. Time and Matter could be used to such an end.<br /> <br /> In the end, it all depends on figuring out the mix that best aligns with the Mysteries they focus on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T11:07:07-07:00","id":1450970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450967#post1450967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on what you mean by dolls and what you want to do with them. The awesome thing about Mage is that there are always multiple Arcana combinations that can be used to approach a problem.<br /> <br /> Lets say you want to create an archive of magical souls and knowledge, an artificial afterlife in defiance of the Psychopomp, a lore repository and emergency source of troops akin to the Infinity Circuit of the Eldar. Prime and Death could accomplish such a thing.<br /> <br /> Should you prefer to make living beings into golems, you would need a Patterning of Life and the target Arcanum. For manipulating dolls and creating golems, Matter could be of aid.<br /> <br /> Another approach is that the mage wants everything to be in a perfect pattern, all integrating into gears as the mage makes optimal decisions with absolute certainty and builds mechanical enforcers of their perfect timeline, akin to the Vex from Destiny. Time and Matter could be used to such an end.<br /> <br /> In the end, it all depends on figuring out the mix that best aligns with the Mysteries they focus on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it was the second option, but now I want all three. I was wondering if I should go with body control, or mind control. I was thinking of the creepy doll aesthetic and something like those characters from blazblue, I never played, so I don\u2019t know their names. I was thinking of a forces matter spell that made \u201cdata\u201d physical like the Vex do, but that never really had a practical purpose.<br /> <br /> Edit: That last one could be really really good with demon or God Machine involvement","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 06-04-2021, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T15:32:50-07:00","id":1450991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450970#post1450970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it was the second option, but now I want all three. I was wondering if I should go with body control, or mind control. I was thinking of the creepy doll aesthetic and something like those characters from blazblue, I never played, so I don\u2019t know their names. I was thinking of a forces matter spell that made \u201cdata\u201d physical like the Vex do, but that never really had a practical purpose.<br /> <br /> Edit: That last one could be really really good with demon or God Machine involvement</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the Vex based idea as being linked to a Wending: the Vault of Glass. What the archmage originally made it for and what happened to them is a Mystery in itself, but power and clarity can still be drawn from it. Its a Legacy idea that has been in my head for a bit, but I haven't had the time to flesh it out yet.<br /> <br /> A Forces and Matter spell can be used to create something akin to the Necron from 40k. It can allow one to create schematics and create a magical 3D printer, regardless of the device's complexity. It also allows transporting them via emails, phone calls, flashlight beams, movies, etc. A Weaving can allow one to heal with electricity. A making of Forces can allow you to create an electric matrix to run devices (a Forces variation of Psychic Genesis that automatically instills the Possessed condition). There are a lot of interesting ways to create dolls, starting with manipulating gadgets, drones and clockwork devices at low levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-04-2021, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T21:24:28-07:00","id":1451013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1450991#post1450991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see the Vex based idea as being linked to a Wending: the Vault of Glass. What the archmage originally made it for and what happened to them is a Mystery in itself, but power and clarity can still be drawn from it. Its a Legacy idea that has been in my head for a bit, but I haven't had the time to flesh it out yet.<br /> <br /> A Forces and Matter spell can be used to create something akin to the Necron from 40k. It can allow one to create schematics and create a magical 3D printer, regardless of the device's complexity. It also allows transporting them via emails, phone calls, flashlight beams, movies, etc. A Weaving can allow one to heal with electricity. A making of Forces can allow you to create an electric matrix to run devices (a Forces variation of Psychic Genesis that automatically instills the Possessed condition). There are a lot of interesting ways to create dolls, starting with manipulating gadgets, drones and clockwork devices at low levels.</div> </div> </div> </div> I for one would be extremely happy to see this Legacy. It\u2019s very cool. You do you, of course, but if you do make it I will be excited about it.<br /> The Necron/Vex idea is so Free Council I\u2019m a bit surprised it\u2019s not already there. Who needs zombies or spirits when you can use Science! for minions. Now I want a Adeptus Mechanicus and Foundation style Tech Priests using Matter/Spirit. <br /> I believe I forgot to type on my last post, but a artificial afterlife actually makes a lot of sense for the Mysterium. You (hopefully) don\u2019t lose knowledge when someone passes away, and it makes security easier. Silver Ladder might like it because it would be a human made afterlife you could opt into. It is definitely a interesting and intriguing idea, with loads of story potential.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T21:46:54-07:00","id":1451017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1451013#post1451013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I for one would be extremely happy to see this Legacy. It\u2019s very cool. You do you, of course, but if you do make it I will be excited about it.<br /> The Necron/Vex idea is so Free Council I\u2019m a bit surprised it\u2019s not already there. Who needs zombies or spirits when you can use Science! for minions. Now I want a Adeptus Mechanicus and Foundation style Tech Priests using Matter/Spirit. <br /> I believe I forgot to type on my last post, but a artificial afterlife actually makes a lot of sense for the Mysterium. You (hopefully) don\u2019t lose knowledge when someone passes away, and it makes security easier. Silver Ladder might like it because it would be a human made afterlife you could opt into. It is definitely a interesting and intriguing idea, with loads of story potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your wish is granted, it also has influences from Bioshock and Prey, with a solarpunk theme:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402100-the-anima-meccanica-a-moros-legacy-of-entrepreneuring-inventors\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402100-the-anima-meccanica-a-moros-legacy-of-entrepreneuring-inventors\"> The Anima Meccanica, a Moros Legacy of Entrepreneuring Inventors - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402100-the-anima-meccanica-a-moros-legacy-of-entrepreneuring-inventors\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402100-the-anima-meccanica-a-moros-legacy-of-entrepreneuring-inventors </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In short: A solarpunk Legacy of inventors that focuses on merging technology with spirits and sponsoring new green innovations. The Attainments and yantras reward </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T19:15:45-07:00","id":1451094,"title":"","content":"Should a Sleeper have their dream form summoned, can they take a journey to the Underworld without causing a breaking point or triggering Quiescence ? By that I mean, should they see no clue in everyday life, can they dismiss it as really weird yet insightful dream ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T19:29:52-07:00","id":1451096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1451094#post1451094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a Sleeper have their dream form summoned, can they take a journey to the Underworld without causing a breaking point or triggering Quiescence ? By that I mean, should they see no clue in everyday life, can they dismiss it as really weird yet insightful dream ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for one thing, going to the Underworld doesn't cause Quiescence anyway, it isn't Supernal or Abyssal.<br /> <br /> I think a person would need more elaborate magic than that to make a person resist breaking points entailed by encountering the Underworld, because it's incredibly freaky in its own right. Assuming a person has a rational capacity to evaluate their dreams as they experience them (an unusual occurrence already), I should think the Underworld cuts through that to effect on an emotional level. It's getting the imaginary juices flowing.<br /> <br /> You'll wake up thinking it wasn't real, but it certainly felt real enough to leave you Shaken or Guilty.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think at times actual dreams in real life can do something like that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T04:28:16-07:00","id":1451125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1451094#post1451094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a Sleeper have their dream form summoned, can they take a journey to the Underworld without causing a breaking point or triggering Quiescence ? By that I mean, should they see no clue in everyday life, can they dismiss it as really weird yet insightful dream ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever you do to bring them out of a dream is sure to trigger Quiescence, and will most likely put them in a lucid state. Bringing them into the Underworld doesn't trigger Quiescence unless you're sloppy about it. Provided they are lucid due to being brought out of their dream, experiencing the Underworld is definitely a breaking point in its own right. However, experiencing it as if it was a dream should grant a nice bonus on the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-06-2021, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T04:51:45-07:00","id":1451126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1451125#post1451125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, experiencing it as if it was a dream should grant a nice bonus on the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an issue with this is that dreaming people typically engage with their dreams as though they're real anyway, no matter what they consist of. If the Underworld is existentially disturbing and aesthetically horrifying beyond what a person's dreams would conjure, then I don't think it appearing as a dream is blunting it all that much, and possibly makes it worse; a waking person might be better at denying what's happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T03:37:54-07:00","id":1451193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1451126#post1451126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an issue with this is that dreaming people typically engage with their dreams as though they're real anyway, no matter what they consist of. If the Underworld is existentially disturbing and aesthetically horrifying beyond what a person's dreams would conjure,</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that dreams still respond with dream logic, and that dreams, even nightmares, have a dampening effect on the dreamer to the point where mages can cast spells affecting the dream and its narrative without them being considered obvious magic to a dreaming Sleeper.<br /> I want to note that neither mages nor changelings (nor Sleepwalkers with the Astral Adept Merit) have any special rules for dealing with mental stress when they are lucid dreaming and travelling the Astral/Dreaming Roads/Hedge/etc. With these precedents coupled with the fact that a Sleeper in dream form outside their dream shouldn't enjoy its special protection, makes me assume that Sleepers in dream forms have no extra protection against breaking points. A horrible nightmare might technically be scarier than the Underworld, but the former comes with built-in protections that are definitely missing from the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> then I don't think it appearing as a dream is blunting it all that much, </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't appear as a dream when it actually happens (i.e. why I wouldn't grant bonus dice on breaking points for that alone), but the context matters a whole lot. Even though it's seemingly (and actually) as real as when entering the Underworld bodily, waking up after such an experience (rather than having recollection of the chain of events leading to descent and ascent, and quite possibly a noted absence in the material world during that time) makes it so much easier to rationalise it as a dream after the fact.<br /> <br /> Let's say that a character witnesses a horribly accident and calls 112/911. If the event is worthy of a breaking point for that character, it should always be rolled. However, if the responders have a professional (like a trained EMT or police officer) with them that helps ground the character and go through the shock, then that should make the event somewhat less traumatic compared to if the character was only approached to give a statement. In both cases the character experiences the same breaking point, but in the former case they should definitely have a better chance of succeeding on the breaking point roll. It's basically the same principle for experiencing the supernatural, except based in ease of denial instead of mental health support.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and possibly makes it worse; a waking person might be better at denying what's happening. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T13:54:29-07:00","id":1452052,"title":"","content":"Would anything significant about character balance change if I altered the Inferior Arcana? For some reason, them not being all Gross or all Subtle bothers me, on a purely aesthetic level. So I was thinking...<br /> <br /> For all Subtle, I'd change: <br /> <br /> Mastigos - Fate (instead of Matter). My reasoning is the theme of the Mastigos is all about Will, Identity, the Self, and so forth, rather than the role it is meant to play by impersonal cosmic forces.<br /> <br /> Acanthus - Prime (instead of Forces). My reasoning is that Arcadia is all about the role a thing plays in a story or chronology, rather than its &quot;inherent&quot; nature. <br /> <br /> Obrimos would stay at Death, Thyrus at Mind, and Moros at Spirit. <br /> <br /> For all Gross, I'd change...<br /> <br /> Moros would go to Life. Pretty obvious Death/Life contrast, there. <br /> <br /> Obrimos would go to Space. Universal godhead, omnipresence of the divinity, blah blah blah. <br /> <br /> Thyrsus would go to Time because animals and nature generally are about relative time (hungry or sated, dark or light outside, etc). At least my dog only knows breakfast time, dinner time, and bed time. <br /> <br /> I might even say PCs get a <i>choice </i>of inferior arcana, with the following spread:<br /> <br /> Mastigos= Fate/Matter<br /> Acanthus= Prime/Forces<br /> Obrimos= Death/Space<br /> Thyrsus= Mind/Time<br /> Moros= Life/Spirit.<br /> <br /> Would this break anything important? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T16:18:05-07:00","id":1452089,"title":"","content":"The main issue with letting Moros get higher in Spirit without a teacher is that it gives that Path a big leg up on all things ephemeral in a manner that does not fit with the intended distribution of Path competencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T16:23:27-07:00","id":1452090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1452089#post1452089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main issue with letting Moros get higher in Spirit without a teacher is that it gives that Path a big leg up on all things ephemeral in a manner that does not fit with the intended distribution of Path competencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems fair enough. Would just swapping the Acanthus to Prime and Magistos to Fate cause any issues, though? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T16:31:42-07:00","id":1452092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1452090#post1452090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems fair enough. Would just swapping the Acanthus to Prime and Magistos to Fate cause any issues, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>The most obvious thing that comes to mind is that making the Mastigos the only Path that needs a teacher to be able to render themselves resistant to having their destinies messed with by outside forces (through the Arcanum's Greater Utility Attainment) is directly opposed to your stated reasoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T16:38:22-07:00","id":1452094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1452092#post1452092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most obvious thing that comes to mind is that making the Mastigos the only Path that needs a teacher to be able to render themselves resistant to having their destinies messed with by outside forces (through the Arcanum's Greater Utility Attainment) is directly opposed to your stated reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that seems acceptable. I can appreciate the dramatic irony there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 06-13-2021, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T12:35:10-07:00","id":1452980,"title":"","content":"A question that came to me from someone else's recent post:<br /> <br /> How, by RAR, does the local Diamond tend to deal with Nameless orders and vice versa. Are any local Nameless mages with enough numbers just treated like a local diamond order, are nameless order mages allowed to hold concillium positions, sit on the council etc, or do they tend to be treated by the diamond mages as permanent outsiders? Or a third option? Just realized I am not clear on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T13:55:11-07:00","id":1452988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1452980#post1452980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How, by RAR, does the local Diamond tend to deal with Nameless orders and vice versa. Are any local Nameless mages with enough numbers just treated like a local diamond order, are nameless order mages allowed to hold concillium positions, sit on the council etc, or do they tend to be treated by the diamond mages as permanent outsiders? Or a third option? Just realized I am not clear on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the kind of thing that varies by location and exactly what the principles of the Nameless Order are, but I think a general rule of thumb is that a Consilium will see members of the Diamond make a point of shunning this other Order and denying them access to some of the more choice resources and Mysteries, unless they should have something particularly worthwhile to bargain with. It can be possible to agree to abide by the Consilium's laws and offices, in which case one at least gets the benefit of it not being total open season on them by Pentacle mages, but still often be treated with less regard and find it a bit difficult to get some of the choice positions (although I think a Herald could be a good offering to them), just from a case of lacking the usual advocates.<br /> <br /> Free Council Assemblies are way more accommodating (even if you still have to fulfil the usual requirements to become a voting member outside of the Order) and I'd think they'd try to advocate on behalf in a Consilium, but I'd present it that in many cases there's an underlying tension of lowkey pressure from some of the Libertines for these Nameless to join up with them altogether.<br /> <br /> The sample location of Tucson in the core constitutes an exceptional example where Nameless who periodically gather into an ad hoc Order are the majority and have good standing with their direct Pentacle neighbours, but that's an explicitly unusual relationship. <br /> <br /> I think in any case it can be easier to be a member of a Nameless Order part of a cabal that is otherwise Pentacle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T15:40:37-07:00","id":1452995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1452980#post1452980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question that came to me from someone else's recent post:<br /> <br /> How, by RAR, does the local Diamond tend to deal with Nameless orders and vice versa. Are any local Nameless mages with enough numbers just treated like a local diamond order, are nameless order mages allowed to hold concillium positions, sit on the council etc, or do they tend to be treated by the diamond mages as permanent outsiders? Or a third option? Just realized I am not clear on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the era. As long as the Nameless Order does not espouse ideals truly antithetical to the Pentacle, they're likely to be accepted into the Consilium as long as they follow Consilium rules. I imagine that most members of the Diamond would treat such a Nameless Order as basically being part of the Council of Free Assemblies (even if they aren't). It is to the Consilium's benefit to welcome all Mages into the Consilium, so long as they're willing to follow the rules.<br /> <br /> In areas where an Assembly dominates, the Nameless Order would have an even easier time integrating, should they choose to do so.<br /> <br /> That said, my reading of the information we have on the small Nameless Orders that did not integrate into the Free Council post-Great Refusal are that they're cults of personality or otherwise don't mesh with Consilium/Assembly structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T16:45:40-07:00","id":1452998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1452995#post1452995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is to the Consilium's benefit to welcome all Mages into the Consilium</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I think the Diamond Orders at the least have a tendency towards being a bit chauvinistic towards belief systems outside of their dogma and lineage. That's not to say it <i>isn't</i> beneficial, just that it's plausible for characters to prioritize something higher.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, my reading of the information we have on the small Nameless Orders that did not integrate into the Free Council post-Great Refusal are that they're cults of personality or otherwise don't mesh with Consilium/Assembly structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some of the big things for not wanting to join with the Free Council are not holding to their perspective on the connection between magic and humanity and not being enthused for war with the Seers.<br /> <br /> That's the payoff for becoming part of an Assembly; everybody gets a vote, but everybody needs to abide by the vote. The Free Council is welcoming, but if they outnumber you and all elect to do something like conduct operations against the Seer tetrarchy, you're expected to participate.<br /> <br /> The Consilium at least is a body that doesn't really impose upon its constituents. Being obligated to get into a fight with a Pylon is more likely there as some kind of punishment for a severe infraction. <br /> <br /> Consilium structure really only amounts to having cordial relations with neighbouring cabals and a body of elders to bring grievances to. Standing (and hence access to certain common resources) is improved by performing voluntary services of benefit to community or council.<br /> <br /> Convocation, on the other hand, is something that I think Nameless Orders are very definitively excluded from. At best I could see some representative being brought along as the guest of another mage when their Order has information significant to a major topic under discussion, but otherwise they have no place or voice there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T09:34:36-07:00","id":1453758,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to track reincarnations of souls throughout history? Assuming of course that is what happens with souls, and they aren\u2019t created and destroyed by birth and death. I know the pilgrimage can make souls, and vampires can run across people who are pretty much the same as people in their past who are dead, so it has some evidence towards reincarnation.<br /> Is it possible to try and remember past reincarnations past the part where the Psychopomp removes the Awakened structure of the soul, along with any residual memories? I was thinking of a Legacy that (eventually) combined all the past lives (and possibly future lives) into the present.<br /> I guess if temporal sympathy works on souls that would be one way to find out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T10:08:52-07:00","id":1453760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1453758#post1453758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to track reincarnations of souls throughout history? Assuming of course that is what happens with souls, and they aren\u2019t created and destroyed by birth and death. I know the pilgrimage can make souls, and vampires can run across people who are pretty much the same as people in their past who are dead, so it has some evidence towards reincarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because no one (even the Exarchs) knows whether reincarnation is real, if it were trackable it'd be verifiable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it possible to try and remember past reincarnations past the part where the Psychopomp removes the Awakened structure of the soul, along with any residual memories? I was thinking of a Legacy that (eventually) combined all the past lives (and possibly future lives) into the present.<br /> I guess if temporal sympathy works on souls that would be one way to find out. </div> </div> </div>Again, there is no evidence that souls reincarnate, it's purely a non-verifiable religious belief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T10:35:24-07:00","id":1453765,"title":"","content":"What about hypothetical reincarnations, like temporal sympathy to people you have never been?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T10:59:26-07:00","id":1453766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1453765#post1453765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about hypothetical reincarnations, like temporal sympathy to people you have never been?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Mystery!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T11:15:23-07:00","id":1453768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1453766#post1453766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like a Mystery!</div> </div> </div> </div>If only someone in my game was interested in Time.<br /> On that topic, while explaining how Shifting Sands works, one of my players asked me if he channeled mana from a Hallow, then went back in time before it was channeled, should he keep the Mana that he got from the now refilled hallow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T12:15:28-07:00","id":1453776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1453768#post1453768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that topic, while explaining how Shifting Sands works, one of my players asked me if he channeled mana from a Hallow, then went back in time before it was channeled, should he keep the Mana that he got from the now refilled hallow?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to make that call yourself, but the lack of mutual inclusivity of &quot;Spent Mana and Willpower do not return&quot; with &quot;Gained Mana and Willpower are not retained,&quot; combined with the fact that the more powerful time-travel spell just has you inhabit your past self and the line generally respects entropy suggests to me that no, he doesn't keep it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T15:19:20-07:00","id":1453794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1453765#post1453765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about hypothetical reincarnations, like temporal sympathy to people you have never been?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make that the tip of the iceberg, the sympathetic ties are to the previous loops of a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244944-homebrew-legacy-the-kalachakra-feedback-wanted\">Kalachakra</a><br /> <br /> Then I would make the archmage who created them be Saint Germain (a Time and Space specialist), from European folklore. Then you could borrow some elements from the character from the Castlevania animation, making him be unknowingly mentored by an ochemata of the Psychopomp, probably to become the Quintessence to something bone chilling. His Omens would be based on Saint Germain from Unknown Armies, embodying the archetype of The First and Last Human.<br /> <br /> Lastly, make his chantry be the Vault of Glass from Destiny and his Supernal Omen to connect it to the lost Wending known as the Infinite Corridor. Now he can be anywhere and anywhen history is being made. The Kalachakra are his cat's paws and the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1280217#post1280217\">Eternal Soul Sentinels</a> are the Psychopomp's. <br /> <br /> With that basis, you can build a web of intrigue that echoes throughout history. That should be a cool incentive for them to learn Time. There are enough plot hooks for them to examine things with other Arcana, but depending on the convenient ally or mentor that knows it will really make them miss it when they are unavailable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-29-2021, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T01:25:37-07:00","id":1453825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1453760#post1453760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, because no one (even the Exarchs) knows whether reincarnation is real</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing the idea that the Exarchs don't know on?<br /> <br /> I think both yourself and TempleBuilder are asking the question too much in terms of absolutes. Is there a way to track reincarnating souls? The Guardians of the Veil are certainly looking for one. Their information so far might be regarded as promising, but far from conclusive.<br /> <br /> That can be slotted in with things such as the belief of the House of Ariadne in city gods and the foundation of the existence of the Diamond itself. Verification is the Obsession of many mages, and one they don't quite get a satisfying conclusion on.<br /> <br /> I expect it's the kind of Obsession most likely to lead Guardians to archmastery (and the kind where not all become Exemplars), although while that perspective provides a lot more info to go on they often decide that only Ascension will bring the full answers they seek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T17:27:39-07:00","id":1454557,"title":"","content":"So with the nature of Reach for Artifacts, does that mean a lot of the time it's necessary to use them for ritual casting if you want to use something like Advanced Duration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T09:44:59-07:00","id":1454890,"title":"","content":"Do people think that the Ruling Practice of Matter would be sufficient to catalyse chemical reactions? Something like making coal dust ignite in the air without providing a spark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T05:35:50-07:00","id":1454956,"title":"","content":"What is happening to a mage &quot;under the hood&quot; when the Supernal Harrowing condition is replacing/replaces his Wisdom with Integrity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T08:58:39-07:00","id":1454973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1454956#post1454956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is happening to a mage &quot;under the hood&quot; when the Supernal Harrowing condition is replacing/replaces his Wisdom with Integrity?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abyss taints the Mage's soul in the same manner it taints the soul of a Sleeper.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T13:32:33-07:00","id":1454988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1454890#post1454890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people think that the Ruling Practice of Matter would be sufficient to catalyse chemical reactions? Something like making coal dust ignite in the air without providing a spark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagine its not enough by itself, since you are introducing more energy into the system. One possible solution is to Perfect its explosive properties (Forces could also be used for this), so room temperature heat would be enough. Alternatively, you could take a similar approach to Roy Mustang from FMA: tightly pack the element to be ignited into the target, creating a corridor from a possible ignition source to the target, such as a lighter. While you depend on having such a tool handy, it makes it viable with aonly Ruling. Mechanically speaking, I would model it after Lure &amp; Repel for drawing the substance in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T14:28:53-07:00","id":1454991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1454890#post1454890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people think that the Ruling Practice of Matter would be sufficient to catalyse chemical reactions? Something like making coal dust ignite in the air without providing a spark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say that (for the specific coal dust example) making the dust ignite immediately without sparks is Ruling, but making the dust ignitable without sparks is Weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T00:14:17-07:00","id":1455012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1454973#post1454973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Abyss taints the Mage's soul in the same manner it taints the soul of a Sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely it's got to be more than that though, because if it was just a taint on the soul you could swap souls with a sleepwalker to get a clean one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T10:59:40-07:00","id":1455032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1454973#post1454973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Abyss taints the Mage's soul in the same manner it taints the soul of a Sleeper.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> They retain Integrity but they don't experience Dissonance or cause additional Paradox, so I don't think the Abyss has anything to do with it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1454956#post1454956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is happening to a mage &quot;under the hood&quot; when the Supernal Harrowing condition is replacing/replaces his Wisdom with Integrity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in character, that's probably going to amount to one of the Mysteries innate to the soul; I don't think mages at large have the best idea of how Integrity becomes Wisdom in the first place.<br /> <br /> Out of character, I would propose that the transition from Integrity to Wisdom entails the Gnosis, the Supernal connection to the Watchtower that is one's Path, suffuses the soul in a manner that stabilises and reinforces self-identity; a mage may not always be satisfied or honest about who they are, but they recognise it on a deep level that is preserved against the usual destabilising experiences of shocks to one's intimately held truths or connection to others. In place of that are the Acts of Hubris; the need to transition away from Integrity in the first place leave the line between soul and Gnosis in a certain state of tension. Humanity and magic being intertwined means that each exerts an effect on the other, as irresponsible use of magic and imbalanced sense of one's place in the wider pattern of existence places stress on that tension in the manner that destabilises Imagos, bleeds the Nimbus, and ultimately causes the soul to fracture and become Enraptured.<br /> <br /> The Harrowing Awakening might be concluded to be a form where the interconnection of Gnosis and the soul goes wrong in some fashion. It might rest on the Lucid themselves, that some part of their tests were accomplished in a manner that furthered the journey to sign the Watchtower but did not entail the proper self-reflection or other personal insight for the Gnosis to stabilise. It might be that sometimes the Adyton the Watchtower creates happens to be a kind that is too abstracted away from humanity to allow the usual insights, so a person is left with their own magic as an alien presence in their soul. Maybe it's a result of some rare and unusual disruption of the usual process on either side of the Abyss. That's on top of the conventional explanations of a person who was not really personally seeking Mysteries being pushed far enough by outside influences to have the confrontation with the Lie and get caught up by the Watchtower.<br /> <br /> In any event, the soul is not properly stabilised against the usual shocks to its stability, and worse than that is placed in constant proximity to an awareness and experience that destabilises it.<br /> <br /> At least you're not so hooked into Gnosis that it can pull your soul apart in Rapture. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1455012#post1455012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Surely it's got to be more than that though, because if it was just a taint on the soul you could swap souls with a sleepwalker to get a clean one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Souls are interchangeable, but I don't think there's ever a sense that giving a person another's soul ever gives additional properties (possibly barring a few Reaping Legacies). Especially with the Awakened, with the Gnosis that holds the shape of their soul in that way meaning you retain Legacies even with soul-swapping. Perhaps it's a case where the aspects of oneself under the purview of subtle Arcana arise out of the soul, but feed back into it in turn; you can take the soul of a person with Integrity 1 and replace it with a donation from Integrity 10, but the qualities of their overall pattern formed from things like Mind, Fate, perhaps even Prime, they'll flow back in and shake the soul with the truth of the person's current state.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Awakened had better ideas about how to manage this kind of thing before the Tremere ran off with most of the soul lore.<br /> <br /> Mind, even if such soul replacement was going to work (a question to deal with the fact that Sleepwalkers also have Integrity), a Harrowed Banisher is still a mage and it takes a Master of Death to remove their soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T11:40:43-07:00","id":1455034,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay, I had forgotten some of the terminology so mistook the nature of the question.<br /> <br /> Without proposing idea about the underlying cause of it, I'd say that the process of a regular mage becoming Harrowed by the exposure to a Banisher is one where the tension between Gnosis and stability of their soul gets resolved in a manner different from the usual slide towards Rapture, namely that it kind of recedes a bit in a manner that undermines and ultimately withdraws the usual stabilising effect. Or perhaps, given that it occurs on a dramatic failure for rolling one's Wisdom in the midst of an Act of Hubris, it's more like the Gnosis dislodging a bit from the soul as it adjusts, akin to a physical shock causing one's retinas to detach a bit.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that the experience in-character is of a mage starting to feel as though their confidence about who they are is beginning to slip. You haven't experienced breaking points about your concerns about your sexuality ever since you Awakened, but since you got close to that Banisher some of those harmful intrusive thoughts and mental loops from back then start to have sharp relief in your mind whenever your own powers hurt you. With the right push, you can fall back into that state again, the vulnerability to what you're scared of or unwilling to confront about yourself.<br /> <br /> Oh, plus the stuff about being unable to reconcile oneself to the supernatural existing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T12:04:26-07:00","id":1455036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1455034#post1455034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without proposing idea about the underlying cause of it</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, that's the bit I'm specificly interested in. Things that might serve as a starting point for an IC investigation into the phenomina.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T12:20:50-07:00","id":1455037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1455036#post1455036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alas, that's the bit I'm specificly interested in. Things that might serve as a starting point for an IC investigation into the phenomina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those who Awaken Harrowed are in a way only partially Awakened. They're full mages with everything that comes to mages, but their fundamental human nature has not been properly prepared/transformed to be fully compatible with being mages. Basically, it's like getting new hardware for your computer without bothering to install any drivers for it; even though the hardware might be fully functional, there's a disconnect between it and the rest of the computer that hasn't &quot;learned&quot; how to use the new hardware.<br /> Where that simile breaks down is that being Harrowed is somehow <i>contagious</i> through long-term nimbi. But disregarding that, I'm pretty sure it's a deeply personal thing on the same metaphysical layer as other stuff you can't directly affect (more than temporary) like the Abyssal shard that turns people into Sleepers and the changes brought on by joining/advancing a Legacy or becoming a Tremere. Basically, irreversible template stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T16:51:31-07:00","id":1455055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1455036#post1455036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alas, that's the bit I'm specificly interested in. Things that might serve as a starting point for an IC investigation into the phenomina.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose something along the lines that the trauma of the Harrowed soul, and the close proximity of the source of that trauma, predisposes it to be hostile to magic and mages, and at the same time the not entirely integrated Gnosis creates a kind of low pressure state. The resulting Nimbus has an odd quality that kind of entangles with the Nimbus of another mage with sufficient metaphysical proximity (to examination it might resemble the effects of a cabal theme, but far more intense), and in that tug of war the Banisher soul has the advantage.<br /> <br /> Mind, I would think that's more of an allegorical explanation of what a mage might uncover with Scrutiny than a strictly accurate one. And it may speak to a certain bias in mages, a preference to interpret the evidence in terms of Harrowed Banishers being a kind of contaminant.<br /> <br /> Because the other possibility is that Awakening doesn't rest as easy on mages as they like to think, that the Harrowed state calls out to doubts and weaknesses within them and that with enough time it makes a call the soul heeds to reject the Awakening and retreat back into the normalcy of their original state, which can only ever stall halfway.<br /> <br /> I think the original Banishers book is worth reading or re-reading for the ideas and the general tone and mood it conveys around the point that Banishers present some really unsettling and compelling Mystery to mages who try too hard to figure them out. The details of the particular &quot;possible secret sixth Order&quot; stuff don't fit anymore, but I think the bones of the mage hunters being more than they appear at first glance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-18T11:38:30-07:00","id":1455120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1454890#post1454890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people think that the Ruling Practice of Matter would be sufficient to catalyse chemical reactions? Something like making coal dust ignite in the air without providing a spark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. If and only if you are talking about a system that could spontaneously combust, though, so not just fuel-air, but dry, as well, for example. <br /> <br /> (You can make things move with Ruling &amp; you can generate a static charge by making things move.)<br /> <br /> If nothing else, convert a small blob into something that will flare in its current environment, so Weaving would be the most you'd need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 07-18-2021, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T15:57:39-07:00","id":1456042,"title":"","content":"Sorry by advance if the question has aready been asked, google fails me.<br /> <br /> Strengthening or Weakening Temporal Sympathy should be Time 3 spells, respectively perfecting and fraying, just like Web-Weaver in Space? The section about temporal sympathy evokes changes to the connections but Time spells don't provide any exemples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T16:40:55-07:00","id":1456043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1456042#post1456042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry by advance if the question has aready been asked, google fails me.<br /> <br /> Strengthening or Weakening Temporal Sympathy should be Time 3 spells, respectively perfecting and fraying, just like Web-Weaver in Space? The section about temporal sympathy evokes changes to the connections but Time spells don't provide any exemples?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds legit, though I think not all Space sympathy spells can be translated directly to Time sympathy spells.<br /> <br /> Have you searched in the Creative Thaumaturgy thread in this forum? It probably has some examples. I can guarantee it has at least one example, since I wrote one a few days ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T03:57:41-07:00","id":1456065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1456042#post1456042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The section about temporal sympathy evokes changes to the connections but Time spells don't provide any exemples?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the examples are really more in the table of sympathy strengths. It's not a direct function of those spells so much as what it means to have a given connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T14:53:48-07:00","id":1457142,"title":"","content":"How easy/difficult do you make deciphering a normal (&quot;normal&quot;) Grimoire? Should any mage who reads it automatically be able to tell what Rotes it contains, do you require an Intelligence + Occult roll, make it a Mystery, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T16:38:43-07:00","id":1457155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1457142#post1457142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How easy/difficult do you make deciphering a normal (&amp;quot;normal&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Grimoire? Should any mage who reads it automatically be able to tell what Rotes it contains, do you require an Intelligence + Occult roll, make it a Mystery, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t have the books with me right now, but my knee-jerk response is Opacity equal to rating of highest Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T17:20:08-07:00","id":1457741,"title":"","content":"How difficult it is to destroy an Artifact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T18:45:29-07:00","id":1457749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1457741#post1457741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How difficult it is to destroy an Artifact?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I can tell in at least Second Edition descriptions, Artifacts are virtually indestructible to anything within reach of conventional mages; there's no mention of how to assign Durability to them, and the spell concerned directly with destroying magical items cannot work on them. I'd want to go back over my First Edition books to check for the extent they had to say on the topic, but I note that Imperial Mysteries describes the destruction of an Artifact as a possible effect for an archspell.<br /> <br /> There's always the option of tossing it into the Ocean Oroboros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T13:20:10-07:00","id":1458562,"title":"","content":"How hard should it be to find the Key to a spell such as Ward? Should I include it in it's Deep Information, or should I make it harder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T15:41:20-07:00","id":1458578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1458562#post1458562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How hard should it be to find the Key to a spell such as Ward? Should I include it in it's Deep Information, or should I make it harder?</div> </div> </div> </div>Deep Info sounds fitting. Surface Info is too easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T18:03:39-07:00","id":1458591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1458578#post1458578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deep Info sounds fitting. Surface Info is too easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was thinking Deep at the very least, my main concern is whether it's too easy, especially for low level spells like Ward, but I guess that's why people use those spells to increase Opacity or Supernal Veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T01:04:16-07:00","id":1458626,"title":"","content":"Maybe not so simple, but:<br /> I swear there was this post that contextualized and analyzed each of the Arcana with two concepts, and where each concept overlapped with other Arcana (like how in Classic philosophy, Fire is Warm + Dry, and Air is Warm + Wet, so both share Warm). Any body remember that? And where it was?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T09:16:41-07:00","id":1459019,"title":"","content":"All questions involving signs of Sorcery. <br /> <br /> Question: What is the easiest way for a Moros to make lasting perfected metals without an existing gate or spirit arcana?<br /> <br /> Question: explain to me how Primal transfer helps as it still requires you to hold a spell? <br /> Also how does time limit actually help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":811,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/811-santino","user":"Santino","date":". 09-06-2021, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/811-santino","name":"Santino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar811_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T10:41:38-07:00","id":1459025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Santino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459019#post1459019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All questions involving signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Question: What is the easiest way for a Moros to make lasting perfected metals without an existing gate or spirit arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Moros is more likely to have enough Death to bring the material into and out of Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Santino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459019#post1459019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: explain to me how Primal transfer helps as it still requires you to hold a spell?<br /> Also how does time limit actually help?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can transfer control of more than one spell. The other mage gets to control when to cancel any of these spells or if they wish to relinquish them, having them pay the cost instead of the caster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T11:58:03-07:00","id":1459040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459025#post1459025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Moros is more likely to have enough Death to bring the material into and out of Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question to this is how? What spells cause it seems like ghost gate just eats the items material existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/811-santino","name":"Santino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar811_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T13:20:41-07:00","id":1459053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Santino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459040#post1459040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seems like ghost gate just eats the items material existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by that?<br /> <br /> Ghost Gate says it creates a two-dimensional plane that converts anything that moves through it into Twilight, or transforms directly with Reach. The rules for Perfecting metals say that it can be done by passing something back and forth from Twilight. I don't see any contradiction between the two.<br /> <br /> Time Limit helps by letting a mage creating an Imbued Item relinquish the spell they put into it without heavier costs such as Willpower dots or things like murder or soul destruction. A limit to use the item of weeks or months is fairly reasonable, especially if a decent amount of the imago is given to the Potency. Keep in mind that as a three dot spell with Duration as the primary factor, if you Reach for Advanced then the spell lasts for a week without even needing to take penalties, to enchant an extended action that takes only an hour per roll. If you put most of the penalties into Potency, you end up with a spell that can readily let the item maker complete their work and end up with an object that will hold its power for a fairly long time.<br /> <br /> It's probably best employed if somebody has a specific use in mind for the spell that will be imbued. Really, in a lot of cases it's going to amount to the same thing as a person being given an imbued item on temporary loan, just with the altered case where it could be custom made for them and takes less energy out of the person who made it.<br /> <br /> Actually... I'd missed it before, but it seems as though the time limit only even applies per user; the item will still retain power that can be used by somebody else thereafter, for the same limited period. So yeah, even more like just getting an item on loan, in that once your time with it is up you give it to people who can still use it. Spend six months using your wand of fireball, and then when it no longer works anymore trade it away to somebody else in exchange for something nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T13:42:04-07:00","id":1459057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459053#post1459053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by that?<br /> <br /> Ghost Gate says it creates a two-dimensional plane that converts anything that moves through it into Twilight, or transforms directly with Reach. The rules for Perfecting metals say that it can be done by passing something back and forth from Twilight. I don't see any contradiction between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost Gate also says any item is destroyed once it passes through the gate. Passing the ephemeral object back into material form requires either temporarily making it physical (which doesn't actually convert it back from ephemera, just like how a Materialised ghost also still is made out of ephemera) or by straight up transforming it back with Death 4/Matter 4, which could potentially be ruled as not working since the when the object transforms back it should retain the properties it had before it was transformed.<br /> <br /> But it's kinda stupid and nothing prevents a different spell to function consistently that just doesn't destroy items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T14:46:49-07:00","id":1459066,"title":"","content":"Thanks a bunch both of you that's what I needed to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/811-santino","name":"Santino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar811_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T17:18:10-07:00","id":1459218,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26982-avenging-hathor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26982_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26982\" data-vbnamecard=\"26982\">Avenging Hathor</a>, if I can just continue addressing your spell question here:<br /> <br /> I made a slight mistake in calculating the yantra bonus, 5+4+3 would be 12 dice not 11, so applying that before additional modifiers would put the pool at -1. With the full length ritual that puts it at 4 dice, or 7 with Willpower. <br /> <br /> On top of that, Conditional Duration could be a consideration. If going with Duration as Primary Factor, the penalty for raising it to a month could be eliminated entirely just with an improbable condition (&quot;when a person says oranges are blue while doing a handstand&quot;), putting two dice back into the pool. Alternatively, Potency could be made Primary and the mage could be willing to go with a far more common condition (&quot;when I encounter an orange&quot;), and be left with the relatively more manageable -14 penalty. Either way, it might require less optimised yantras or give a few extra dice to the final pool to improve chances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T23:41:23-07:00","id":1459258,"title":"","content":"Higher Gnosis is likely if you're going to use ritual casting for extra dice (since low Gnosis ritual intervals takes ages), meaning you already get extra dice from that and more Yantra slots. Higher Arcanum rating would also grant extra dice as well as extra Primary Factor steps.<br /> You need a total of 12 factor steps (3 for Duration 1 month, and 9 for Potency 10), with up to 3 of those coming from a higher Arcanum rating. If stats are maxed, you end up at 15-(2*9)= -3 dice, and if you get the full +5 from extra ritual intervals you end up with a positive dice pool before you even start applying Willpower or Yantras. Yantras by themselves could also completely negate the penalties for such a character (5+4+3+2+2+2=18).<br /> It's rare for someone to have a character with maxed Gnosis, but this demonstrates how large the margin could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T00:38:30-07:00","id":1459262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459258#post1459258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Higher Gnosis is likely if you're going to use ritual casting for extra dice (since low Gnosis ritual intervals takes ages), meaning you already get extra dice from that and more Yantra slots. Higher Arcanum rating would also grant extra dice as well as extra Primary Factor steps.<br /> You need a total of 12 factor steps (3 for Duration 1 month, and 9 for Potency 10), with up to 3 of those coming from a higher Arcanum rating. If stats are maxed, you end up at 15-(2*9)= -3 dice, and if you get the full +5 from extra ritual intervals you end up with a positive dice pool before you even start applying Willpower or Yantras. Yantras by themselves could also completely negate the penalties for such a character (5+4+3+2+2+2=18).<br /> It's rare for someone to have a character with maxed Gnosis, but this demonstrates how large the margin could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it's easiest if maxed out, but I was trying to account for it being reported as something a player stated they were doing regularly, which presumably meant accessible early on.<br /> <br /> Six hours on a spell at Gnosis 3, it's a lot but it can be managed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T11:08:32-07:00","id":1459319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459218#post1459218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26982-avenging-hathor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26982_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26982\" data-vbnamecard=\"26982\">Avenging Hathor</a>, if I can just continue addressing your spell question here:<br /> <br /> I made a slight mistake in calculating the yantra bonus, 5+4+3 would be 12 dice not 11, so applying that before additional modifiers would put the pool at -1. With the full length ritual that puts it at 4 dice, or 7 with Willpower.<br /> <br /> On top of that, Conditional Duration could be a consideration. If going with Duration as Primary Factor, the penalty for raising it to a month could be eliminated entirely just with an improbable condition (&quot;when a person says oranges are blue while doing a handstand&quot;), putting two dice back into the pool. Alternatively, Potency could be made Primary and the mage could be willing to go with a far more common condition (&quot;when I encounter an orange&quot;), and be left with the relatively more manageable -14 penalty. Either way, it might require less optimised yantras or give a few extra dice to the final pool to improve chances.</div> </div> </div> </div>So to wrap it up:<br /> A disciple of Prime should first of all make the following preparations:<br /> - A very strong shadow name merit (to be roleplayed fully, shouldn't it need a bit of time, so that the &quot;mage's legend&quot; will strenghten and be known by the whole supernatural - magical world? The fluff seemed to imply that this is the case).<br /> - For the character to learn a good rote, and then raising that rote's skill up to 5. (some rp time should pass as well? I'm SURE I found a thread about &quot;rpg, learning skills, spending xps, and game time passing - how much game time should pass&quot; but I since lost it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> - For some kind of blessings from spirits (sacraments... are those in MtAw 2ed? In Signs of sorcery?)<br /> - Spending hours as a ritual spell. +5. I guess it would rise up to 6hrs for a 3 gnosis spell. Got it. Long, but doable.<br /> <br /> ...Possible conditional duration if the character has Fate 2 as well.<br /> If the character has Fate 2, couldn't he also preventively use Exceptional luck, spending reach to make it affect his spellcasting rolls, and even more reach to give the 8 again quality? Am I getting this right so far?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26982-avenging-hathor","name":"Avenging Hathor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T12:32:35-07:00","id":1459332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459319#post1459319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- A very strong shadow name merit (to be roleplayed fully, shouldn't it need a bit of time, so that the &quot;mage's legend&quot; will strenghten and be known by the whole supernatural - magical world? The fluff seemed to imply that this is the case).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a Shadow Name necessarily needs to be famous, just that high dots in the Merit means you go deep into it when you're doing mage stuff. You dress it up, you carry yourself differently and speak differently, you act like you're a separate person.<br /> <br /> Note that in this case, the Shadow identity needs to be based on symbolism fitting the spell.<br /> <br /> Getting the extra requires it to match with cabal symbolism as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- For the character to learn a good rote, and then raising that rote's skill up to 5. (some rp time should pass as well? I'm SURE I found a thread about &quot;rpg, learning skills, spending xps, and game time passing - how much game time should pass&quot; but I since lost it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>I think time developing Skills can often go during downtime. In any case, it <i>is</i> possible to start off with five dots in a Skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- For some kind of blessings from spirits (sacraments... are those in MtAw 2ed? In Signs of sorcery?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacraments are yantras that get destroyed in the course of casting, whether it's tearing a photo in half, stabbing a wax figure, burning a sample of hair or melting an ice sculpture. The +3 bonus is if it's something otherworldly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Possible conditional duration if the character has Fate 2 as well.<br /> If the character has Fate 2, couldn't he also preventively use Exceptional luck, spending reach to make it affect his spellcasting rolls, and even more reach to give the 8 again quality? Am I getting this right so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all correct.<br /> <br /> Oh! Other mages who know Prime can contribute to the ritual with teamwork. If they have Prime 2 or higher, they roll the full dice pool and give successes to the leader, if they only have one dot they'd do Gnosis-3. Mages with no Prime function as a yantra, they're not really worth it here.<br /> <br /> Signs of Sorcery added rules where mages who have practiced the ritual out in detail beforehand give a +2 bonus to the helpers, and +1 if they've done it before but not practiced this time. There's also a Mind 2 spell to link ritual participants together and give the secondary actors Potency as a dice bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 09-08-2021, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T12:44:11-07:00","id":1459333,"title":"","content":"Note that Exceptional Luck doesn't actually help. 8-Again increases the average amount of successes on a roll (as long as it's not a chance die) but it doesn't increase the chance of rolling at least one success which is the only thing that matters for getting this spell off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T16:52:46-07:00","id":1459370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459333#post1459333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that Exceptional Luck doesn't actually help. 8-Again increases the average amount of successes on a roll (as long as it's not a chance die) but it doesn't increase the chance of rolling at least one success which is the only thing that matters for getting this spell off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it a bit uncertain. In the list of general boon effects, the dice tricks are the only one listed with a Reach effect to let it affect spellcasting. But in Exceptional Luck, it lists a Reach price for just applying boon in general terms to spellcasting. Other spells that apply boons do not do that.<br /> <br /> So is it a case where Exceptional Luck allows dice bonuses to be applied to spellcasting while every other spell that applies boons is limited only to providing dice tricks, or is it a case where it's the one time that it lists the Reach cost for dice tricks and is meant to be read in combination with the prior passage? Can Monkey's Paw or Sworn Oath provide 9- and 8-again for spellcasting if extra Reach is put into them, even though their specific entries don't state as such?<br /> <br /> Can you use Exceptional Luck +2 Reach to apply the Inspired Condition to a spell?<br /> <br /> In any case, Fools Rush In can be used to apply dice bonuses to spells. That <i>might</i> mean Exceptional Luck is not intended to, but they wouldn't be redundant if they both could; the dice bonus boon can only be provided to a particular kind of action, whereas Fools Rush In can provide its bonus to whatever action the character wishes, but it needs to be instant and unplanned (this would be how the spells aren't redundant even in their mundane aspects).<br /> <br /> So one way or another, it's possible to use a Ruling of Fate to provide bonus dice to spellcasting, it just becomes a question of whether or not that would preclude ritual spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T17:22:59-07:00","id":1459372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459370#post1459370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it a bit uncertain. In the list of general boon effects, the dice tricks are the only one listed with a Reach effect to let it affect spellcasting. But in Exceptional Luck, it lists a Reach price for just applying boon in general terms to spellcasting. Other spells that apply boons do not do that.<br /> <br /> So is it a case where Exceptional Luck allows dice bonuses to be applied to spellcasting while every other spell that applies boons is limited only to providing dice tricks, or is it a case where it's the one time that it lists the Reach cost for dice tricks and is meant to be read in combination with the prior passage? Can Monkey's Paw or Sworn Oath provide 9- and 8-again for spellcasting if extra Reach is put into them, even though their specific entries don't state as such?<br /> <br /> Can you use Exceptional Luck +2 Reach to apply the Inspired Condition to a spell?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1260630-time-liches?p=1261556#post1261556\">This is an <i>old</i> </a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1260630-time-liches?p=1261556#post1261556\">conversation</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T17:29:27-07:00","id":1459373,"title":"","content":"I don't doubt it, but I <i>was</i> away from Mage for the best part of four years. I'll happily catch myself up when resources are pointed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T17:41:57-07:00","id":1459374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459373#post1459373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't doubt it, but I <i>was</i> away from Mage for the best part of four years. I'll happily catch myself up when resources are pointed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I linked a post that links four other posts, the earliest being from February of 2017. If you want other resources, they do not exist. A basic argument from the effects of allowing the spell to apply anything other than dice tricks to spellcasting is presented in the first of those linked posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T18:09:47-07:00","id":1459380,"title":"","content":"The &quot;when&quot; there was pointing towards the thing that had happened, not enquiring after something further. A &quot;this is my characteristic&quot; kind of statement rather than waiting on something.<br /> <br /> Look, from what I've seen there some interesting and worthwhile points are made even if I don't 100% agree with them, and... well you seem tired of that conversation anyway so I'll just have it in mind for the future if ever it comes up with another new person rather than speculate on future discussions that are fresh to me and exhausting for you.<br /> <br /> That's the best I can come up with. I just hope that any other conversations in future can be reasonable and cordial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T07:35:26-07:00","id":1459555,"title":"","content":"Oh, for the sake of those spell calculations, I'd also point out that somebody with the correct Order and rote encoded with the right Skill could also get an additional die to the pool. With the suggested Skills that would favour the Arrow or Mysterium, but I don't think Crafts, Persuasion or Subterfuge are out of bounds as additional Skills that a Wards and Signs rote could be built with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T02:52:25-07:00","id":1459637,"title":"","content":"Hey all! A few questions from a soon-to-be Awakening ST. If the questions below are too complex to be in this topic, please let me know! In your experience, does magic in MtAw 2e feel magical? What do you do to prevent it from becoming straight up miracle working?<br /> <br /> I have a more substantial background in Ascension, so I\u2019m used to the characters\u2019 capabilities being heavily limited by their beliefs and practices. In Awakening, however, it seems like mages possess a gnostic understanding of how to disrupt the Lie via their connection to the Supernal, their own beliefs becoming somewhat secondary. Am I correct in this reading or am I just overthinking? Yantras seem like a wonderful way to get my players more immersed in the mage fantasy, but are they enough? Maybe I should house rule a negative dice modifier for casting with no attached semiotics?<br /> <br /> Sorry if this is incoherent. I\u2019m glad there is a place to go to with this kind of questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26473,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26473-ewrygn","user":"ewrygn","date":".  Cleaned up my formatting 09-11-2021, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26473-ewrygn","name":"ewrygn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T06:42:27-07:00","id":1459649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ewrygn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459637#post1459637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a more substantial background in Ascension, so I\u2019m used to the characters\u2019 capabilities being heavily limited by their beliefs and practices. In Awakening, however, it seems like mages possess a gnostic understanding of how to disrupt the Lie via their connection to the Supernal, their own beliefs becoming somewhat secondary. Am I correct in this reading or am I just overthinking? Yantras seem like a wonderful way to get my players more immersed in the mage fantasy, but are they enough? Maybe I should house rule a negative dice modifier for casting with no attached semiotics?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main thing is that spell factors other than the primary one apply penalties to raise beyond the base level, which Yantras are mostly there to offset after you've gotten a base spellcasting pool above, say, five dice.<br /> <br /> There's a Hunter supplement that briefly mentions an in-universe term for mages that's especially relevant in 2e now that the way the Long-Term Nimbus works offers more of a run-up to how the Enraptured work: PHFNs, or Psychics and Human Fortean Nexi. Being theoretically able to cast any spell anywhere with no semiotic grounding means that a mage is <i>someone around whom weird things happen.</i> The mnemonic aids of Yantras make it easier to get it to happen on-purpose and to-plan, and that's especially important when attempting to push the limits of your abilities like your Obsessions will tend to want you to.<br /> <br /> (Remember also that Gnosis can't be raised without hitting some kind of milestone and that Arcana need enough Gnosis to support them and surpassing Path limitations requires instruction by an appropriately knowledgeable mentor.)<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't say there's any need to penalize raw spellcasting, just\u2026 start from the bottom and keep the advancement process in mind. Rotes and Shadow Names and sacraments and other powerful common Yantras are especially important at the base of the Gnosis ladder, and that's where a lot of personalization can shine through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-11-2021, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T08:58:42-07:00","id":1459662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459649#post1459649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Hunter supplement that briefly mentions an in-universe term for mages that's especially relevant in 2e now that the way the Long-Term Nimbus works offers more of a run-up to how the Enraptured work: PHFNs, or Psychics and Human Fortean Nexi. Being theoretically able to cast any spell anywhere with no semiotic grounding means that a mage is The mnemonic aids of Yantras make it easier to get it to happen on-purpose and to-plan, and that's especially important when attempting to push the limits of your abilities like your Obsessions will tend to want you to.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing Long-Term Nimbus/Entraptured Magi through the lens of HtV reframes these phenomena so nicely! I'm definitely getting around to reading more Hunter books, they seem like a good place to find inspirational material. Also, mage-as-<i>someone around whom weird things happen</i> is such a tasteful justification for non-semiotic spellcasting. Thank you so, so much. Your reply has resolved some of the few points of contention I've had with Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26473,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26473-ewrygn","user":"ewrygn","date":". 09-11-2021, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26473-ewrygn","name":"ewrygn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T12:59:18-07:00","id":1459682,"title":"","content":"Regarding spells that impose Environmental Tilts, such as <i>Swarm of Locusts</i> and <i>Control Weather</i>, how wide is the area affected by them ? Would it be determined by the Area of Effect scale factor or would it instead be anything that seems thematically appropriate ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T13:27:12-07:00","id":1459684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459682#post1459682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding spells that impose Environmental Tilts, such as <i>Swarm of Locusts</i> and <i>Control Weather</i>, how wide is the area affected by them ? Would it be determined by the Area of Effect scale factor or would it instead be anything that seems thematically appropriate ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T15:50:12-07:00","id":1459701,"title":"","content":"Cool, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T16:21:36-07:00","id":1459705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ewrygn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459637#post1459637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a more substantial background in Ascension, so I\u2019m used to the characters\u2019 capabilities being heavily limited by their beliefs and practices. In Awakening, however, it seems like mages possess a gnostic understanding of how to disrupt the Lie via their connection to the Supernal, their own beliefs becoming somewhat secondary.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what Satchel said, I would put forward that the depiction in various parts of First Edition often present matters including cultural imagery and occult ideas that might be picked up after Awakening can often form the manner in which mages form terminology and concepts for processing their encounters with and ideas about the Mysteries, as well as the symbols that they might form imagos out of. They're not empowered above and beyond those things specifically, and the culture of the Orders broadens horizons a bit, but it still often helps them to form ideas.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Free Council is liable to have mages who more deeply immerse themselves in specific cultural motifs out of a combined belief that those motifs will be the result of a common Supernal awareness of humanity and that those ideas can themselves influence the nature of the Truth that one Awakens to.<br /> <br /> And there's always Legacies, which often emerge very strongly from particular larger cultural practices that mages can be part of or inspired by. And because they represent something that a mage is more deeply dedicated to pursuing or developing, I'd say they often inform practices even apart from their specific powers and oblations. Like, if you're one of the Thrice-Great, it's not just that you've become empowered to do things that resemble the pursuits of Hermeticism, you're part of a tradition with deep roots in Hellenistic philosophies and mysticism that maintains that they've got a stronger insight into the Supernal than many others, even to the point of having a guidepost to Ascension. I think that's the kind of thing that creates an inclination towards related yantras, rituals and Obsessions even when they're not directly part of the Legacy practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T13:20:04-07:00","id":1459762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ewrygn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1459637#post1459637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey all! A few questions from a soon-to-be Awakening ST. If the questions below are too complex to be in this topic, please let me know! In your experience, does magic in MtAw 2e feel magical? What do you do to prevent it from becoming straight up miracle working?<br /> <br /> I have a more substantial background in Ascension, so I\u2019m used to the characters\u2019 capabilities being heavily limited by their beliefs and practices. In Awakening, however, it seems like mages possess a gnostic understanding of how to disrupt the Lie via their connection to the Supernal, their own beliefs becoming somewhat secondary. Am I correct in this reading or am I just overthinking? Yantras seem like a wonderful way to get my players more immersed in the mage fantasy, but are they enough? Maybe I should house rule a negative dice modifier for casting with no attached semiotics?<br /> <br /> Sorry if this is incoherent. I\u2019m glad there is a place to go to with this kind of questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to what others have said, I would also contend that miracle working is also quite magical, to me at least.<br /> <br /> If you want to foster certain aesthetic, in which magic is arcane words and gestures and long arduous rituals and onoreous preparations, then one suggestions is that you talk to your players about not using the Shadow Name merit, and encourage them to lean into their Orders Tools, like Techn\u00e9, Adamant Hand and Lex Magica. Especially Techn\u00e9, better if they all agree on the same focus on some real world occult practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T06:38:13-07:00","id":1460214,"title":"","content":"Can Mind spells detect beings in Twilight without other Arcana, such as locating a ghost or spirit by searching for minds nearby ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T07:13:02-07:00","id":1460218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1460214#post1460214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mind spells detect beings in Twilight without other Arcana, such as locating a ghost or spirit by searching for minds nearby ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only goetia i think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T16:19:09-07:00","id":1460265,"title":"","content":"Got it, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T16:23:22-07:00","id":1460266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1460214#post1460214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Mind spells detect beings in Twilight without other Arcana, such as locating a ghost or spirit by searching for minds nearby ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dave Brookshaw has verified that Mind magic can detect the minds of things in twilight (ghosts etc.) with no additional arcana needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T06:18:56-07:00","id":1460520,"title":"","content":"Do people suppose that firearms are sufficiently complex to be disabled by the blackout zones of Temples?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T08:35:36-07:00","id":1460534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1460520#post1460520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people suppose that firearms are sufficiently complex to be disabled by the blackout zones of Temples?</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks like it. Perhaps especially modern firearms using propellants discovered in the past century or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T05:29:28-07:00","id":1460636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1460520#post1460520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people suppose that firearms are sufficiently complex to be disabled by the blackout zones of Temples?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that anything more complex than a crossbow would probably be disabled. A flintlock pistols may get a pass, perhaps the number of moving parts could be the deciding factor. This could have all sorts of interesting ramifications on how archeomancers prepare for an expedition. It could also create a whole niche for items that have been made functional due to Supernal engineering and perfected materials being used to reduce the number of parts, but it might also make the life of a character that fights with firearms more difficult than it needs to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T06:34:58-07:00","id":1460648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1460636#post1460636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it might also make the life of a character that fights with firearms more difficult than it needs to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's one reason for the Adamantine Arrow to value adaptability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T06:50:11-07:00","id":1460655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1460636#post1460636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">perhaps the number of moving parts could be the deciding factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the main quote is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blackout usually affects all electronics and any technology that relies on complex chemical processes. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but it might also make the life of a character that fights with firearms more difficult than it needs to be. </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, it's an excuse to actually break out the cool melee weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T15:26:35-07:00","id":1461097,"title":"","content":"Do Mages get to know the withstand rating of a target while casting a spell? Or do they determine the Potency first and hope it works?<br /> <br /> Like, as a Storyteller do I tell a player that they'll have a -4 penalty or something or do they need to learn it's beyond the potency of the Spell when the Spell simply doesn't work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T15:30:31-07:00","id":1461098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris_John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1461097#post1461097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Mages get to know the withstand rating of a target while casting a spell? Or do they determine the Potency first and hope it works?<br /> <br /> Like, as a Storyteller do I tell a player that they'll have a -4 penalty or something or do they need to learn it's beyond the potency of the Spell when the Spell simply doesn't work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was the latter, and that a mage wouldn\u2019t <i>inherently</i> know whether her spell lacked enough Potency or the spell doesn\u2019t work for some other reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T15:52:23-07:00","id":1461103,"title":"","content":"That said, learning of a target's relevant stats is surely a Knowing spell, so it's not the most onerous thing to find out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T23:01:24-07:00","id":1461161,"title":"","content":"In many cases you can also figure it out by observing the effect. If your Potency 4 Know Spirit spell gets two questions, you don't have to waste a question to know it's Rank 2.<br /> <br /> Just to repeat: The player decides the Potency of the spell when casting it. If the spell doesn't have enough Potency, it simply doesn't have an effect. A reminder: The subject can also spend WP to momentarily increase their Withstand rating by 2.<br /> If their Withstand rating decreases after the fact, any non-instantaneous spells increases in effective Potency, potentially allowing spells that were reduced to zero Potency to suddenly take effect. Example: Mage casts a Life spell to transform two subjects into frogs with a Potency 4 spell. The first subject has Stamina 2 but spends WP to raise it temporarily to 4, staving off the transformation for one turn. The second subject has Stamina 4 and is unaffected. The mage casts Degrading the Form with Potency 5 to reduce the second subject's Stamina by [Potency 5 - Stamina 4 = effective Potency 1] and their Stamina is now below the Potency of the first spell and the subject turns into a frog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T06:53:21-07:00","id":1461204,"title":"","content":"Although I think it's interesting to look at a few examples of the kinds of spells where a mage might not be initially sure if the effect has taken hold or not. You throw Exceptional Luck to hex somebody whose Composure turns out to be higher than you expected, it would take further observation to be sure of whether or not they're actually being inhibited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T00:10:29-07:00","id":1462096,"title":"","content":"The entry for Brontium in Signs of Sorcery says that Brontium items give a &quot;+2 bonus to defend against debilitating effects&quot;. What does this bonus apply to?<br /> <br /> EG - if I have an active ghost shield spell on myself, and someone casts &quot;Enervation&quot; on me, which I think pretty clearly qualifies as debilitating - do I get +2 dice on my clash of wills from Ghost Shield, +2 on my Stamina Withstand, or both?<br /> <br /> Is this an equipment bonus, and so only applies if the equipment could be used to defend against the debilitating effect, or does it simply apply to any opposed roll/stat against any debilitating effect?<br /> <br /> As written, it reads like a benefit to defense against pretty much any possible negative condition or tilt, which seems .... strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T00:20:04-07:00","id":1462097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1462096#post1462096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entry for Brontium in Signs of Sorcery says that Brontium items give a &amp;quot;+2 bonus to defend against debilitating effects&amp;quot;. What does this bonus apply to?<br /> <br /> EG - if I have an active ghost shield spell on myself, and someone casts &amp;quot;Enervation&amp;quot; on me, which I think pretty clearly qualifies as debilitating - do I get +2 dice on my clash of wills from Ghost Shield, +2 on my Stamina Withstand, or both?<br /> <br /> Is this an equipment bonus, and so only applies if the equipment could be used to defend against the debilitating effect, or does it simply apply to any opposed roll/stat against any debilitating effect?<br /> <br /> As written, it reads like a benefit to defense against pretty much any possible negative condition or tilt, which seems .... strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like an equipment bonus. It should work for contested actions, but dunno about Clash of Wills. Most likely not intended to raise Withstand, though. Still, yeah it\u2019s handy to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T00:38:01-07:00","id":1462098,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. Maybe if you use the brontium as a tool Yantra for the defensive spell you could get the equipment bonus to the clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T13:25:46-07:00","id":1462149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1462098#post1462098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense. Maybe if you use the brontium as a tool Yantra for the defensive spell you could get the equipment bonus to the clash of wills.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My understanding is that, apart from the bonus it gives the +2 bonus to any protection or warding spells, the user gains 2 extra Withstand levels against any spells that apply negative Conditions, as well as those reduce Attributes or Skills. By that standard, and the fact it can be mass produced either by a Master of Matter or Time (using <i>Blink of an Eye</i> near an Avernian Gate. Loci or portal to Twilight) and the fact that it does not require any kind of resource recharge means its arguably a more valuable resource than Thaumium. Such a property makes it essential equipment for any combative mage (or experienced Banisher) Something as innocuous as a kassiterium coin in a subject's wallet can make a notable difference in their survivability without requiring any spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T16:59:46-07:00","id":1462177,"title":"","content":"What is the Master of Matter doing, and how does Blink of an Eye help?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T15:02:01-07:00","id":1462327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1462177#post1462177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Master of Matter doing, and how does Blink of an Eye help?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, my mistake, Disciple of Matter is all that is needed. In the case of a Master of Time, they can use Blink of an Eye near a portal to Twilight (or a similar gateway to the Underworld or Hisil) to shorten the time needed to naturally perfect metals. The passes take mere moments and the time needed for the base materials to rest can be shortened, allowing the entire process to be completed very quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-01-2021, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T10:19:27-07:00","id":1462440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1462327#post1462327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, my mistake, Disciple of Matter is all that is needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have issues with referring to the use of that spell (of any spell) as mass production. There is the matter of how it caps a bit at the ten that the most resolute and composed person in the world can manage before they can't relinquish it anymore and are going to be wracking up Reach for every additional spell they're casting and retaining.<br /> <br /> And presumably making Indefinite, so that's at least two Mana per casting. That's going to drain the pool fairly quickly, and the options for replenishing it are a bit sparse.<br /> <br /> I guess a character could relinquish their Perfecting spells (which still cost two Mana a pop) unsafely, but that might hurt their reputation if they're giving out material that is going to ultimately have the spell decay.<br /> <br /> I'm personally inclined to be a bit rigid with the application of Blink of an Eye, that its power largely affects things that take the form of extended actions in any case, and that particularly with regards to perfecting material an idea that the metaphysics of the process can't accelerate the convalescence period.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T11:44:38-07:00","id":1462572,"title":"","content":"Silly question, but does Speak with Beasts work on humans?<br /> I\u2019d assume so, but I don\u2019t have the book on me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T13:35:31-07:00","id":1462585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1462572#post1462572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silly question, but does Speak with Beasts work on humans?<br /> I\u2019d assume so, but I don\u2019t have the book on me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably so, since humans are technically highly intelligent animals. However, since this involves gesturing that sound approximately correct or the target speaking in their own language, which the other party somehow understands, the effect is probably very overt. That means it would probably be seen as obvious magic when used on any Sleepers, but should allow mages to speak with other supernaturals without having to learn a new language (or use Mind magic). Plus it can allow them to bribe animals to spy for them with zero traceable spells (or pings on the Peripheral Sight), which combined with Animal Handling makes for a very subtle spy network.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-03-2021, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T18:04:19-07:00","id":1462599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1462585#post1462585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, since this involves gesturing that sound approximately correct or the target speaking in their own language, which the other party somehow understands, the effect is probably very overt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although now I'm thinking that a subject of the spell could mumble towards somebody in what sounds like an approximation of their language, and the listener could assume that they're comprehending something inarticulate but recognisable. Or possibly that the subject keeps it simple and then lets a listener run on the idea that they're getting the gist of something reasonably understandable in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus it can allow them to bribe animals to spy for them with zero traceable spells (or pings on the Peripheral Sight), which combined with Animal Handling makes for a very subtle spy network.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although fairly limited in their capabilities, depending on the chosen animal. They won't necessarily have a good sense of information that would be useful to a mage or much retention, and their commitment might lag a bit; not necessarily loyal to any food provided now, or attached to promises of more food later if they have a need to eat and opportunity presents itself elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Plus how more than a few animals that might go unnoticed won't necessarily have senses useful for acquiring the kind of information a mage might require. You send insects to watch a person, but they don't perceive the same mental picture that we do; you'd need a Weaving to give them something like a human visual acuity first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T11:05:27-07:00","id":1463007,"title":"","content":"I have an absolutely crazy idea, and thought I\u2019d consult people here before doing any writing.<br /> <br /> Is it possible for a single location to be a Locus, a Hallow, a Verge, an Aedes and a Manteion <i>simultaneously</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T11:42:17-07:00","id":1463013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1463007#post1463007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an absolutely crazy idea, and thought I\u2019d consult people here before doing any writing.<br /> <br /> Is it possible for a single location to be a Locus, a Hallow, a Verge, an Aedes and a Manteion <i>simultaneously</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Signs of Sorcery outright describes stacking multiple types of those locations together. Doesn't use Locus in its specific wording, but also mentions ley line Nodes and passages to Emanations. The intention is very much that they can be customized by virtue of not being exclusive. Just suggests that there should be a common theme weaving them together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T13:25:47-07:00","id":1463028,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Time to start brewing up ideas....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T15:31:07-07:00","id":1463751,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone. Long time reader, first time caller. I have finally started playing in my first Mage game. While we have be taking it slow and most of our play sessions are explaining thing and seeing how things work in a &quot;classroom&quot; setting, I have a lot of questions on spells and what you can do with them. I am a Moros and I have Death 3. There is a spell that really speaks to me: Shadow Crafting. Can you make any object you want? Can you make objects appear at a distance? Can you make a spike and impale someone with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T17:00:00-07:00","id":1463763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1463751#post1463751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone. Long time reader, first time caller. I have finally started playing in my first Mage game. While we have be taking it slow and most of our play sessions are explaining thing and seeing how things work in a &amp;quot;classroom&amp;quot; setting, I have a lot of questions on spells and what you can do with them. I am a Moros and I have Death 3. There is a spell that really speaks to me: Shadow Crafting. Can you make any object you want? Can you make objects appear at a distance? Can you make a spike and impale someone with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gut instinct tells me that\u2026<br /> 1) Any object the caster knows how it works. Knives are easy. Pistols, probably not, though your ST may allow a follow-up Skill roll to craft something complex. Or just extra Reach.<br /> 2) You can only target shadows in your Range, so crafting shadows from a distance shouldn\u2019t be done without sensory range.<br /> 3) This looks like a separate attack roll, not a function of the spell itself. Or just extra Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T17:05:53-07:00","id":1463764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1463751#post1463751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a spell that really speaks to me: Shadow Crafting. Can you make any object you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, with the caveat that the damage modifier/equipment bonus/Armor rating means it's not going to be an extremely good specimen of whatever object it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you make objects appear at a distance? </div> </div> </div>With Advanced/Sensory Range or a successful Aimed Spell roll, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you make a spike and impale someone with it? </div> </div> </div>You can make a spike, which can be used as a weapon or, with Reach, a stage hazard (per the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines on making Environmental Tilts) on which someone could be impaled with enough damage done to impale them normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T11:18:59-07:00","id":1463861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1463763#post1463763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gut instinct tells me that\u2026<br /> 1) Any object the caster knows how it works. Knives are easy. Pistols, probably not, though your ST may allow a follow-up Skill roll to craft something complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the spell description itself doesn't present any such requirement. Nor do comparable spells such as Platonic Form and Ex Nihilo. Shaping does, but I'd find that to be a function of how the shape the matter assumes is a bit secondary to the effect of the spell being causing the matter to have a pliant form.<br /> <br /> That leaves it to the observer to rule on, and my observation would be inclined in a direction away from stating that people with greater education in technical subjects get a leg up on the use of magic. I would think that what you want to make is contingent on how you can incorporate the desired result into an imago, and while a given individual can probably use technical knowledge there, I think it can be sufficient to just have perceptual familiarity to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) You can only target shadows in your Range, so crafting shadows from a distance shouldn\u2019t be done without sensory range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, now I'm wondering about aligning yourself to ensure that the shadow you cast crosses over with another shadow. Does the combined one count as a single subject?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T14:31:44-07:00","id":1463885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1463861#post1463861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026... Shaping does, but I'd find that to be a function of how the shape the matter assumes is a bit secondary to the effect of the spell being causing the matter to have a pliant form.<br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mm, good call.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, now I'm wondering about aligning yourself to ensure that the shadow you cast crosses over with another shadow. Does the combined one count as a single subject? </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026 maybe Scale limits the size of the targetable shadow then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T17:41:00-07:00","id":1463918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1463885#post1463885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm\u2026 maybe Scale limits the size of the targetable shadow then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't think there's any maybe about it.<br /> <br /> The point of it would be being able to get access to a larger shadow without needing to Reach to cast the spell as sensory; you extend to it with one that is either already touching you (if connection to feet is considered valid) or that you can reach down to touch.<br /> <br /> I said aligning oneself before, but Shadow Sculpting would allow one to twist their own shadow into a form that can merge with other ones regardless of angle to light sources. Make it long and thin, maybe a bit mobile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T18:03:37-07:00","id":1465073,"title":"","content":"Maybe not so simple a question, but anyways:<br /> <br /> Has anybody who played with the Tremere came across the 'magical consequences' backing up the Sevenfold Oaths? I don't think the book (NH-NA) detailed what exactly happens if someone breaks them. See, I'm thinking of homebrewing a House that teeters on breaking the seventh one by pretending they're keeping the sixth one...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 10-23-2021, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T18:56:39-07:00","id":1465079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465073#post1465073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe not so simple a question, but anyways:<br /> <br /> Has anybody who played with the Tremere came across the 'magical consequences' backing up the Sevenfold Oaths? I don't think the book (NH-NA) detailed what exactly happens if someone breaks them. See, I'm thinking of homebrewing a House that teeters on breaking the seventh one by pretending they're keeping the sixth one...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reasonably certain that just means the Sevenfold Oath is taken under Sworn Oaths or a similar Fate spell, which likewise means the variable wording alluded to sees equally variable consequences in the form of the hex breaking the oath applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T03:10:32-07:00","id":1465114,"title":"","content":"Speaking of hexes, do people think it would be valid to combine other Arcana with Fate to extend some of the possibilities of hexes and boons? Still as things expressed as quirks of bad luck, but maybe with specified vectors or physical effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T03:22:05-07:00","id":1465115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465079#post1465079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reasonably certain that just means the Sevenfold Oath is taken under Sworn Oaths or a similar Fate spell, which likewise means the variable wording alluded to sees equally variable consequences in the form of the hex breaking the oath applies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465114#post1465114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of hexes, do people think it would be valid to combine other Arcana with Fate to extend some of the possibilities of hexes and boons? Still as things expressed as quirks of bad luck, but maybe with specified vectors or physical effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like adding Forces to hex someone into fritzing every electronic he comes across? Cool. Though without homebrew, I suppose we need something like Conditional Duration and Hung Spell to pull it off.<br /> <br /> Still in the realm of homebrew, but certain Fate-heavy Legacies ought to have workarounds, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T06:05:09-07:00","id":1465129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465115#post1465115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though without homebrew, I suppose we need something like Conditional Duration and Hung Spell to pull it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T06:39:15-07:00","id":1465130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465129#post1465129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was speaking from a strictest sense of RAW. Of course tables may vary; I\u2019d allow it for one, though maaaaybe with +1 Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T07:12:41-07:00","id":1465133,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, Sworn Oaths is a template that models the most basic capacity of oaths. The target willingly swears an oath, then they receive the benefit of a spell for adhering to it or a downside for violing it. The key detail is that the downside cannot be mitigated since it has no Withstand, but requires the willing participation of the target.<br /> <br /> With Fate 5, for example, they could swear to fight a Banisher that is an enemy of the caster and be Destined to be very efficient in opposing them. But should they cooperate with them, they will be hit by an Unmaking of Fate, ending their treachery.<br /> <br /> Another example is to use Life 2. Should the subject adhere to the oath, they continue to look like a different person. But should they start revealing the caster's involvement, they become subject to a Ruling effect that stops them from speaking.<br /> <br /> In summary, a hex and a boon are the most elementary things to add to an oath. But more variation is certainly possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-24-2021, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:14:39-07:00","id":1465203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465130#post1465130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was speaking from a strictest sense of RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was thrown a bit by your referring to it as homebrew. Admittedly, that's a bit of an ambiguous term when we have something like Creative Thaumaturgy and improvised magic.<br /> <br /> I mean, you say in the strictest sense of rules as written, but what about the idea would break rules?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a>, I feel changing appearance would put it a bit more dramatically beyond what I think would qualify as a boon, which admittedly makes me question the viability of the idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T18:13:30-07:00","id":1465226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465203#post1465203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you say in the strictest sense of rules as written, but what about the idea would break rules?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The \u2018strictest\u2019 was in the sense of \u201cWell, no one said we <i>can</i> do it\u2026\u201d, as opposed to \u201cHey, no one said we <i>can\u2019t</i> do it\u2026\u201d <br /> <br /> <br /> And now that you\u2019ve thrown this idea at us, now I\u2019m thinking of how the Carnival Melancholy\u2019s Attainments could work\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T19:46:52-07:00","id":1465234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465226#post1465226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The \u2018strictest\u2019 was in the sense of \u201cWell, no one said we <i>can</i> do it\u2026\u201d, as opposed to \u201cHey, no one said we <i>can\u2019t</i> do it\u2026\u201d <br /> <br /> <br /> And now that you\u2019ve thrown this idea at us, now I\u2019m thinking of how the Carnival Melancholy\u2019s Attainments could work\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Constaine show, he drunkenly enchants his friend with a warding spell. Whenever someone died, they would be unwillingly trapped by him, like a human soul jar. He would automatically use a soul to survive death once. Constantine's luck being what it is, everyone in the same pub as his friend died after he left the room, giving him a stock of 50 souls.<br /> <br /> I was thinking that could be a thing they could do, burn a soul reflexively to gain a powerful boon or hex. This means they could use Charmed to constantly survive deadly situations, or Steadfast and Inspired to succeed in key moments (that one appeal to the angry werewolf or blending in with the escaping crowd). A hex at sensory range can also work as a type of anti-casting, by breaking sensory range, decreasing the dice pool, etc. It could be very versatile, so long as their stock holds.<br /> <br /> Just an idea. I think the theme of the Legacy is cool, but they never got justifiable mechanical benefits that made it a tempting path to pursue. The revised Cloud Infinite, however, certainly did. Looking forward to how you update them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-24-2021, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T10:23:27-07:00","id":1465292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465234#post1465234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the theme of the Legacy is cool, but they never got justifiable mechanical benefits that made it a tempting path to pursue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd still maintain that in First Edition terms, the idea of Left-Handed and particularly Reaper Legacies as needing to constitute temptation was the wrong way to look at it, and that they were more an avenue for expressing a messed up perspective on the world. The Carnival Melancholy didn't need to be <i>right</i> about the idea that good fortune in the face of disaster was a zero sum game (arguably there are issues inherent to saying &quot;that's correct, actually&quot;), it just needed to be a thing they were really invested in validating for themselves.<br /> <br /> That being said, I would say that the more strictly codified and narrow scope of Second Edition Legacies provides a reasonable mechanical hook for Reaper characters being able to put a bit more out of them by way of fuelling them with souls (in the same way that the Hand of Destiny in Nameless and Accursed demonstrates that a Scelesti Legacy can use Befouled Attainments to improve factors beyond the usual parameters with Paradox), at the expense of being limited to only being functional with that fuel.<br /> <br /> But even then, I wouldn't portray it as the character having become a Reaper <i>because</i> they really wanted that Attainment to have a few extra steps of Potency then it would have had in a more benign Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T03:16:36-07:00","id":1465994,"title":"","content":"What do you suppose happens if you cast Rewrite History with indefinite duration to turn a vampire human, and they age to the point of death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T03:52:50-07:00","id":1465997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465994#post1465994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you suppose happens if you cast Rewrite History with indefinite duration to turn a vampire human, and they age to the point of death?</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* Maybe a Revenant (the Vampire kind)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T11:40:43-07:00","id":1466038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465994#post1465994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you suppose happens if you cast Rewrite History with indefinite duration to turn a vampire human, and they age to the point of death?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could read the spell as implying that the subject is still in the place that they are now:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...making her present self as though her life took a very different course. </div> </div> </div>That might imply that if they died, they just wouldn't be able to be in the same place; so the whole spell just wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> I admit that's a pretty tenuous reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T13:32:17-07:00","id":1466047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1465994#post1465994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you suppose happens if you cast Rewrite History with indefinite duration to turn a vampire human, and they age to the point of death?</div> </div> </div> </div>A random result between several options:<br /> <br /> 1- They become a slightly older-looking vampire of random clan/bloodline, as Fate has it that this person still became a Vampire;<br /> <br /> 2- They become a VtR Revenant, turning upon death;<br /> <br /> 3- They die of old age, but the ghost lingers. It may or may not be even more powerful than before, it may or may not know more about you than before. It would be interesting if the ghost considers the spell itself as the act that truly killed them;<br /> <br /> 4- They die of old age, but the sheer amount of time paradoxes created (with or without the added power of Paradox) cause the Supernal or/and the Abyss to manifest something to take their due;<br /> <br /> 5- They die and that's that. The universe says &quot;fuck you causality&quot; and that's that. Not game-breaking, just boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T14:34:20-07:00","id":1466052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1466038#post1466038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could read the spell as implying that the subject is still in the place that they are now:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That might imply that if they died, they just wouldn't be able to be in the same place; so the whole spell just wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> I admit that's a pretty tenuous reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand this, and think it may rise from a mistake about my meaning.<br /> <br /> Scenario: a vampire was Embraced six months ago at the age of 21. A mage casts a Patterning of Time to rewrite his history so he was never Embraced, turning him into a 22 year old. The spell is indefinite. Fifty years later, the guy passes away of natural causes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1466047#post1466047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5- They die and that's that. The universe says &amp;quot;fuck you causality&amp;quot; and that's that. Not game-breaking, just boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not <i>just</i> that. It's not a Lasting spell, there's always the possibility it could be dispelled. <br /> <br /> Rewrite History doesn't actually state a limitation of not working on the dead like Temporal Summoning does (although I still assume that writing premature death out of a person's past still doesn't recall their soul). A thing with a vampire could kind of be a reverse of that, although I'm not certain what would happen to their soul...<br /> <br /> Mind, it may be that the principle that magic less than seven dots cannot alter templates. You can transform a timeline to remove an Embrace, but you don't really change the essential modification within them, it just kind of becomes really inert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T15:21:39-07:00","id":1466056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1466052#post1466052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not <i>just</i> that. It's not a Lasting spell, there's always the possibility it could be dispelled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered that, although I'd say a vampire that young becoming a mortal again isn't that big of a problem. But let me explore it a bit more.<br /> <br /> Both a Revenant or a Ghost could still be viable targets for a dispel, turning the subject into a &quot;living&quot; vampire again.<br /> <br /> The better suggestions I can give to keep the &quot;Sanctity of Template&quot;, though, would be:<br /> <br /> 1- Fate lingers, as it have a stronger grasp on anything with a Template. Unless the Mage can unravel a very strong Fate-related effect, the target will become a Vampire again sooner or later, or the spell WILL be dispelled sooner or later;<br /> <br /> 2- The grasp of the Template on the target's soul can't be undone. As such the target becomes a vampire again despite it being now a Paradox. If the target dies first, they still rise again as what should be a Revenant, but is actually a full Kindred;<br /> <br /> 3- Abyss or/and Supernal shenanigans. You achieve it, yet reality is pissed off. The role of Vampires in the Supernal shouldn't be trifled with. Supernal entity comes, dispels the effect and proceeds to beat Mage.<br /> <br /> Even if nothing exceptional seems to happen, Vampire have the Revenant rule to deal with it. A person touched by vampirism may become quite literally fated to come back as a pseudo-vampire that can become a full vampire through diablerie. This is the most likely state of the subject upon death, and a potential target for dispel.<br /> <br /> One way or another there is the concept of damnation. It makes sense to think that the soul of a vampire doesn't leave the body under such circumstances as you imposed death upon it, but not Final Death. This corpse may have all kinds of weird properties because of the lingering cursed soul. Maybe the sun can cleanse it, and effectively kill the &quot;vampire within&quot;, maybe not.<br /> <br /> You can also apply all sorts of effects on the &quot;living&quot; subject during the spell effect, like Ghoul-like traits, weakness or allergy under the sun, and others. It may even be that the sun itself is able to &quot;harm the spell&quot; the same way it would harm a vampire. Disciplines trying to manifest could do the same. Many things that shouldn't unravel a common spell could start to unravel this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T07:46:38-08:00","id":1467162,"title":"","content":"Question: Could a mage end a werewolf's blood rage early? It's come up in my contagion game, and I'm thinking it'd be something with Mind or Time. Though this has more created a somewhat narrative issue- the whole &quot;I'm a danger to everyone around me&quot; aspect of being a werewolf versus &quot;I want my magic to actually be able to do things&quot; aspect of being a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27146-elifloof","name":"EliFloof","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T08:30:42-08:00","id":1467166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EliFloof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467162#post1467162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Could a mage end a werewolf's blood rage early? It's come up in my contagion game, and I'm thinking it'd be something with Mind or Time. Though this has more created a somewhat narrative issue- the whole &quot;I'm a danger to everyone around me&quot; aspect of being a werewolf versus &quot;I want my magic to actually be able to do things&quot; aspect of being a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it probably can.<br /> <br /> One key aspect of any crossover is that its themes don't simply overlap with the main themes of a splat. Instead, you must be willing to sacrifice standard themes for the ones of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> So the question should be what's more interesting for the game you're going to have. Mixing splats <b>will</b> deride their individual themes in favor of something new the chronicle creates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T08:37:33-08:00","id":1467167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EliFloof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467162#post1467162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Could a mage end a werewolf's blood rage early? It's come up in my contagion game, and I'm thinking it'd be something with Mind or Time. Though this has more created a somewhat narrative issue- the whole &quot;I'm a danger to everyone around me&quot; aspect of being a werewolf versus &quot;I want my magic to actually be able to do things&quot; aspect of being a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clear Thoughts (Mind 3) should be sufficient (even though Death Rage isn\u2019t technically a Condition or Tilt), with the caveat that, not only does it trigger a Clash of Wills for suppressing a supernatural effect, but the Mage would also suffer the 2x Primal Urge penalty for trying to deter someone in Death Rage. (Presumably you just subtract that from the casting pool, but it\u2019s a little weird since ordinarily the spell casting die pool isn\u2019t resisted.) Also, don\u2019t forget to account for the Garou\u2019s increased Size in the Scale factor.<br /> I think the difficulty in ending (or suppressing) Death Rage isn\u2019t one of complexity, but magnitude. Many Mages will struggle to come up with the die pool necessary to overcome all of the penalties, especially at a moment\u2019s notice.<br /> Also, keep in mind how Mages tend to find indirect solutions to such problems. If all you care about is keeping the werewolf from eating people, a Ban (Space 3) will be easier to cast. <br /> In any case, I think that difficulty and chance of failure inherent in the magic system should be sufficient to preserve the tension and danger of a werewolf\u2019s rage, while still allowing the Mage to approach the situation on their terms.<br /> Edit: it\u2019s also worth noting that werewolves already have a very reliable method of ending Death Rages with the Elodoth\u2019s auspice ability. So allowing a mage to attempt the same kind of thing shouldn\u2019t cause much of a thematic problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 11-08-2021, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T08:38:32-08:00","id":1467168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EliFloof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467162#post1467162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Could a mage end a werewolf's blood rage early? It's come up in my contagion game, and I'm thinking it'd be something with Mind or Time. Though this has more created a somewhat narrative issue- the whole &quot;I'm a danger to everyone around me&quot; aspect of being a werewolf versus &quot;I want my magic to actually be able to do things&quot; aspect of being a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's some excluded middle there. Magic can actually do <i>a lot</i>. It could do a lot of things using the specified Arcana to mitigate the danger of a werewolf in Kuruth even if it can't do the specific thing you're asking for. Like, you could give a werewolf hallucinations to attack instead of actual people or objects.<br /> <br /> I think it's reasonable for Death Rage to be one of those innate mystical qualities that the non-Imperial Practices can't directly touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T07:59:34-08:00","id":1467261,"title":"","content":"I think you should be able to do it with a Ruling practice, but it should require at least 2 extra reach and as mentioned above produce a clash of wills. I don't remember all the exact rules of Death Rage, but if they did include any kind of penalty to try to calm them down I would apply them to the CoW or somehow translate them to an increased Withstand rating instead of applying them directly to the spellcasting roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T16:46:52-08:00","id":1467302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467261#post1467261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember all the exact rules of Death Rage, but if they did include any kind of penalty to try to calm them down I would apply them to the CoW</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for Kuruth (specifically Basu-im) present the point that mundane or supernatural attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the werewolf's course of action suffer a penalty equal to twice the Primal Urge, over and above Supernatural Tolerence. This doesn't seem to be a case of calming the Raging werewolf down, just pointing them in another direction.<br /> <br /> However, it doesn't really work for dealing with spells. Supernatural Tolerance is mostly irrelevant to the question of whether Awakened magic works, and part of the point of Withstand is because external penalties really mess up the dynamic of mages taking intentional penalties to enhance spell factors.<br /> <br /> But even that isn't about calming them down. Within Forsaken, I think the only thing that can stop Death Rage is the once per chapter Auspice Benefit of the Elodeth.<br /> <br /> Well, whatever spell might be cast on them, it's at least going to need to take the penalty to cast on a subject of Size 7, for a start.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T07:45:14-08:00","id":1467444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467302#post1467302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it doesn't really work for dealing with spells. Supernatural Tolerance is mostly irrelevant to the question of whether Awakened magic works, and part of the point of Withstand is because external penalties really mess up the dynamic of mages taking intentional penalties to enhance spell factors.<br /> <br /> But even that isn't about calming them down. Within Forsaken, I think the only thing that can stop Death Rage is the once per chapter Auspice Benefit of the Elodeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I say you can't do crossover without being willing to break the native themes of the splats in some ways.<br /> <br /> If you do it by RAW, then Mage rules don't work well. If you don't, you don't, you're still making calls and choosing one theme or the other. When you decide who takes precedence, the other have a thematic change, even if not a drastic rules change. The Uratha defies Supernal influence or Mages can rid them of Kuruth's greater problems.<br /> <br /> Going by RAW, I'd say that magic that enhances your ability to talk to the Uratha would work the best to keep things simple, as you increase a dice pool that can handle better the external penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T11:00:24-08:00","id":1467457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467444#post1467444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Uratha defies Supernal influence</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it needs to be that far, just a matter of whether it's within available Practices.<br /> <br /> We can talk about themes, but I do not think the themes of Mage preclude there being things that are weird enough that it can be hard to figure out the applications of the Arcana to them or deep enough that some manipulations of them become the province of the archmasters. Hell, the history of the game is supposed to include the idea that the Awakened had greater understanding of ways to manipulate the soul before the Tremere absconded with most of that knowledge which has yet to be rediscovered, and the subject of creating them remains as yet unrealised to the very few Fifth Degree Masters that have made the attempt.<br /> <br /> Plus you get things like the description of Perfected Material as still fairly esoteric in Signs of Sorcery. Heck, coming at it from that angle, I could come around to the idea that some direct manipulations of Death Rage are within the powers of regular mages, but exactly how is not widely understood. A player could make some headway with it in a game, enough to accomplish <i>something</i>, but I think not quite comprehensively or reliably. Not the kind of thing to completely take the teeth out of a werewolf's potential to rampage.<br /> <br /> I do not think Mage: the Awakening has a theme of &quot;go where you please and do as you wish&quot; so much as &quot;go somewhere it's maybe inadvisable to be and try to keep one step ahead of it&quot;. It would fit for running with Uratha to remain somewhat perilous.<br /> <br /> Besides, the real way to deal with a rampaging werewolf is to put a Ban around them, so long as they don't have the Gift Facet to let them break out of confinement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T13:29:49-08:00","id":1467472,"title":"","content":"Mages being able to bring a halt to Kuruth doesn't seem that big a deal. Supernal magic might offer mitigation, but it's not a long-term solution unless you're going to go full archmastery and rewrite how werewolves work. It actually seems like a really good synergy of the two themes. The hubris of a mage thinking they can totally fix a werewolf, next to the werewolf who can trick themselves into thinking that the mages help means they have total control of their rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T17:09:19-08:00","id":1467499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467472#post1467472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages being able to bring a halt to Kuruth doesn't seem that big a deal. Supernal magic might offer mitigation, but it's not a long-term solution unless you're going to go full archmastery and rewrite how werewolves work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine in the abstract, but my issue would be with what it does to the presence of Death Rage in actual play.<br /> <br /> Considering the range of possible triggers for it and how deviating to either end of Harmony can open those up a lot, dancing around Kuruth looks like a thing that is supposed to be a major part of games involving the Uratha, and a ready option to just shut it down immediately seems like it would leave how they play a lot more uninhibited.<br /> <br /> On a mechanical side, it also seems to me like it would allow the Gauru form to become a lot more accessible than it's supposed to be. Stay shifted into it for longer than your allotted turns or shift again before the natural reset, make sure friends are further away than enemies, and have somebody on standby to bring it back under control when enemies are dealt with or any of them stray out of bounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T18:09:52-08:00","id":1467504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467499#post1467499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine in the abstract, but my issue would be with what it does to the presence of Death Rage in actual play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually my point. It seemed like you guys were getting caught up in abstractions rather than an actual game. Like...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering the range of possible triggers for it and how deviating to either end of Harmony can open those up a lot, dancing around Kuruth looks like a thing that is supposed to be a major part of games involving the Uratha, and a ready option to just shut it down immediately seems like it would leave how they play a lot more uninhibited. On a mechanical side, it also seems to me like it would allow the Gauru form to become a lot more accessible than it's supposed to be. Stay shifted into it for longer than your allotted turns or shift again before the natural reset, make sure friends are further away than enemies, and have somebody on standby to bring it back under control when enemies are dealt with or any of them stray out of bounds. </div> </div> </div>This is the kind of situation I'd want your troupe to be playing in. It feels awesome to coordinate properly together to overcome an inherent limitation; but it's a very brittle solution and easily made a problem. Like, if the Uratha and the mage aren't around each other for some reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T19:30:40-08:00","id":1467510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467499#post1467499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine in the abstract, but my issue would be with what it does to the presence of Death Rage in actual play.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage with two dots in Death and Mind can outright stop a vampire's frenzy with a Ruling effect. Frenzy is sufficiently central to Vampire's actual play that interacting with Touchstones is required to safely clear the two Conditions whose effects are different mechanical expressions of &quot;frenzy is harder to resist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Frenzy has an explicit &quot;trying to get the vampire to act counter to the Beast's desires fails&quot; rule statement. Death Rage does not have this restriction, when it ends you're not in the Killing Form anymore, and your personal trigger only applies to you once per night in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T21:38:02-08:00","id":1467523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467499#post1467499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine in the abstract, but my issue would be with what it does to the presence of Death Rage in actual play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my point. Any decision becomes a change of how the game develops in actual play. It may be minor or greater, but it is there.<br /> <br /> You don't have to throw old themes out of the window, but you must be prepared to accept their changes, expected and unexpected.<br /> <br /> And this particular interaction is just one of many that will happen in actual play that can affect their themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467504#post1467504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually my point. It seemed like you guys were getting caught up in abstractions rather than an actual game. Like...</div> </div> </div> </div>The theme of Forsaken on the matter is that Kuruth is a constant danger that can't ever be downplayed. You either avoid it, treat it as a calamitous scenario, or accept the dire consequences that come with it.<br /> <br /> Giving the Uratha a tool to risk it and still avoid the consequences with some regularity changes nothing on the rules, but affects how it plays out in actual game.<br /> <br /> How reliable is this tool changes the theme <i><u>of this tool</u></i> in the game, but it is still a change in theme. The theme of Forsaken isn't that you have to worry with Kuruth if you're alone. It isn't Kuruth as a tempting option that may go wrong. It is risking Kuruth as the nuclear option or a catastrophic accident.<br /> <br /> You're not understanding what theme means. And an important point is that changing themes doesn't mean eliminating themes in exchange for nothing or weakening the game.<br /> <br /> It just means changing themes. Accepting that the game will play out differently and create other stories, some similar, some vert different. Some that twist old themes or explore them in ways the solo splat isn't meant to. It isn't good or bad, it just is.<br /> <br /> But I like to emphasize this because a lot of people treat some themes as holy cows that can't be touched, without considering context. And crossover have a tendency to bring the kind of context that deserves reconsideration of normal themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T12:50:41-08:00","id":1467592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467523#post1467523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not understanding what theme means.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I understand it fine. I just don't agree with your version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T16:49:43-08:00","id":1467611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467510#post1467510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage with two dots in Death and Mind can outright stop a vampire's frenzy with a Ruling effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a Contagion Chronicle thing?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T19:44:40-08:00","id":1467628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467611#post1467611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that a Contagion Chronicle thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from the Player's Guide, yes. Inciting frenzy without a trigger is easier (Compelling) but uses the same Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T22:50:59-08:00","id":1467761,"title":"","content":"Do Mages have to be in an Order to use Mudra Yantras? The flavor text says that Mudras are taught by the orders but none of the mechanics text says that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T23:35:27-08:00","id":1467768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris_John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467761#post1467761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Mages have to be in an Order to use Mudra Yantras? The flavor text says that Mudras are taught by the orders but none of the mechanics text says that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if they weren\u2019t a Master who\u2019s using their own Rotes, they had to get the Rote from <i>somewhere</i>, and Order membership is the easiest way to solve that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T23:55:11-08:00","id":1467770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467768#post1467768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well if they weren\u2019t a Master who\u2019s using their own Rotes, they had to get the Rote from <i>somewhere</i>, and Order membership is the easiest way to solve that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But RAW you do not need to be in an Order to have the 3 starting rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T00:07:43-08:00","id":1467772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris_John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467770#post1467770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But RAW you do not need to be in an Order to have the 3 starting rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don\u2019t? Still, I\u2019m reasonably confident that the RAI is that most mage characters belong to an Order, even if Nameless. Or have a mentor (not necessarily a Mentor) who brought them in to the larger Awakened society, who could\u2019ve passed on known Rotes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, three starting Rotes? I though it was six dots worth of Rotes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 11-14-2021, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T02:10:20-08:00","id":1467779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris_John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467770#post1467770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But RAW you do not need to be in an Order to have the 3 starting rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark eras starting mages scheme says &quot;Starting Neolithic Awakened have no Rotes, although they earn Praxes as normal&quot;<br /> <br /> But i don t see any wrong with a character buying Mentor or Nameless order Status to justify starting with rotes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T09:06:03-08:00","id":1467797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467592#post1467592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I understand it fine. I just don't agree with your version.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a matter of fact, that sounded far less obtuse in my head before I posted. My bad anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T13:07:34-08:00","id":1467814,"title":"","content":"Since they are not using Supernal magic, ghosts and spirits do not cause Quiescence, correct ? Which means that a mortal that is able to see and remember them does not necessarily should not be assumed to be a Sleepwalker ? They have unusual talents, but are still at risk of breaking points from witnessing Awakened magic ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T13:22:46-08:00","id":1467815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467814#post1467814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since they are not using Supernal magic, ghosts and spirits do not cause Quiescence, correct ? Which means that a mortal that is able to see and remember them does not necessarily should not be assumed to be a Sleepwalker ? They have unusual talents, but are still at risk of breaking points from witnessing Awakened magic ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T13:30:21-08:00","id":1467817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris_John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467770#post1467770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But RAW you do not need to be in an Order to have the 3 starting rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you kinda do. The character creation chapter assumes the character is part of an Order and thus grants everything that membership in an Order normally entails: 3 Rotes, 1 dot of Occult, 1 dot of Order Status, the High Speech Merit, and 3 Rote Skills. The core book just doesn't directly spell out that a mage is assumed to get their first Rotes through their Order, but it's definitely implied and also confirmed in Signs of Sorcery (see below)<br /> Neither variant version of character creation (one in Dark Eras when Orders didn't exist yet, and one in Signs of Sorcery for the newly Awakened) assumes Order membership and thus doesn't grant any of those things.<br /> <br /> Character creation tends to assume that the character has some prior experience than someone who's just Awakened, and includes some additional stuff. That's why you start with 6 Arcana dots instead of just 3 that are limited to only the Ruling Arcana, as well as only 7 dots of Wisdom instead of the 8 dots you Awaken with (as described in Signs of Sorcery). That book also includes this passage for newly Awakened mages: <br /> &quot;<b>Orderless:</b> The character does not have a dot in Occult, a dot in Order Status, rotes, rote skills, or the High Speech Merit.&quot;<br /> <br /> But as already mentioned, there's nothing wrong with giving a nameless mage some Rotes. You'll just have to come up with some other explanation for it. As long as you learn the Rote (i.e. pay an XP for it and not just cast it from a Grimoire) you also gain access to its Mudra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467772#post1467772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Wait, three starting Rotes? I though it was six dots worth of Rotes?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the beta version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T13:40:22-08:00","id":1467819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467817#post1467817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the beta version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that explains it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T15:42:59-08:00","id":1467830,"title":"","content":"Are Command Ghost/Command Spirit type spells always an Act of Hubris? If so/not, why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T16:17:59-08:00","id":1467831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467830#post1467830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Command Ghost/Command Spirit type spells always an Act of Hubris? If so/not, why?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I normally rule it as being an Act of Hubris if its against the creature's own interests. So if you make them move left just before a stealth attacker, then no harm. If they make them stop moving, stop attacking or stay in an area to create an opportunity to flee or negotiate, then no problem. The Act of Hubris happens when there is a deliberate and malicious subversion of their free will, or when the mage is intentionally shaming or humiliating the target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T16:43:41-08:00","id":1467834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467831#post1467831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I normally rule it as being an Act of Hubris if its against the creature's own interests. So if you make them move left just before a stealth attacker, then no harm. If they make them stop moving, stop attacking or stay in an area to create an opportunity to flee or negotiate, then no problem. The Act of Hubris happens when there is a deliberate and malicious subversion of their free will, or when the mage is intentionally shaming or humiliating the target.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So would a Death mage commanding a ghost to keep a look out for him while he/she sneaks into a building, would an action in that vein be considered an Act of Hubris?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T16:56:26-08:00","id":1467837,"title":"","content":"I think it's reasonable to let a Nameless character have the character creation rotes on the assumption that <i>somebody</i> was able to teach them some custom mudras and mnemonic recall principles, but maybe make it a complication in learning further rotes.<br /> <br /> For Acts of Hubris, I'll point out that the list given for Understanding Wisdom includes binding a being to a task. I think it's reasonable to say that even for a spirit of fire, pinning it to work involving burning things can be an Act of Hubris, because the central thesis isn't being bad, it's acting without proper consideration for or comprehension of the consequences of your actions. The spirit might be perfectly fine with what it's been commanded to do, but the outcome of commanding it, both in what it does and in what it then becomes unable to do, may go off in directions that are not great. There are also elements of the ethics of taking choice away even if the subject might well choose to do that thing of their own accord, and how the mage is taking on responsibility for actions beyond themselves on a deep spiritual level.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that Command Spirit would be an Act of Hubris on every occasion under those conditions; you could command it to do something of smaller scope or shorter term, that aren't throwing things too much out of harmony.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the provided list of Acts of Hubris is not supposed to be exhaustive or proscriptive, and the first paragraph about losing Wisdom states that different mages doing the same thing might not have the same risk of degeneration. So I'd say it can also account for things like how one generally portrays the character (the degree to which they act cautiously and observe spells in action carefully), or else what they're doing around this spell in particular to manage its risks. Commanding an ephemeral entity can be Hubris if it's an ad hoc thing then left to its own devices, but if you've got a good handle on the situation and supervise it, then I think you wouldn't need to roll.<br /> <br /> In any event, I'd still say Wisdom is written to be something characters risk with decent frequency. It's just part of the general tone of the game, that mages really dance a lot with becoming unconcerned with what their actions cause.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I'm strongly of the mind that actions that aren't magic should still be capable of risking Wisdom, because I see the whole point of that stat as being that the mage's Awakening and Gnosis makes them sensitive to a general interconnectedness of things that makes the management of their place in the grand scheme relevant to the stability of their souls. It's like, connection to the Supernal hardens your soul against those things that once risked its Integrity, but the substance of what reinforces it also creates a certain rigidity and is formed from a deeper presence in the Tapestry.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T02:59:18-08:00","id":1467980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467628#post1467628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's from the Player's Guide, yes. Inciting frenzy without a trigger is easier (Compelling) but uses the same Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard that there's something in there about Mummies and Time magic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T07:36:34-08:00","id":1468002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467980#post1467980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard that there's something in there about Mummies and Time magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be in Mummy 2e Core, specifying that Time and Fate spells cast on the Arisen add the highest used rating from those two Arcana to Paradox pools (and successful Paradox rolls apply the Abyssal Backlash Condition representing the Judges' attention a la &quot;Paradox Conditions&quot; from the Ecstatic Wind), and any spell of those two Arcana other than Knowing and Unveiling spells automatically fails (though a mage has no intrinsic knowledge of this fact).<br /> <br /> Basically, the Judges have a tight grip on the Arisen's Names (i.e. their Fate Patterns, and by extension their Time Patterns) and don't take kindly to probing, much less attempting to alter them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T12:32:38-08:00","id":1468038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468002#post1468002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That'd be in Mummy 2e Core</div> </div> </div> </div>Their attitude about whether or not each game line is supposed to take the existence of the others as a given is so confusing to me.<br /> <br /> In any case, such a thing suggests to me that there's reasonably a spectrum concerning how much of another supernatural being's nature can be affected by non-Imperial Awakened magic. The Arisen are at an extreme far end, but I think it would be reasonable for somebody to interpret Kuruth as being sacrosanct in the middle, even if I'd agree that the example of Frenzy also makes it reasonable to see mages being able to subordinate it.<br /> <br /> To my mind, Frenzy doesn't quite have the oomph that Death Rage does, just enough to make me accepting of magic being able to mess with it in comparison to the weight of Kuruth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T15:00:52-08:00","id":1468052,"title":"","content":"Was it WoD, I'd put a vampire's Frenzy above a Garou's for that matter. Not the Rage itself, but while the Garou's frenzy is just loosing control of your rage, a vampire is being overtaken by an unholy alien force that's trying to eat their very soul.<br /> <br /> But in CoD, Kuruth isn't just a frenzy, it is the <u>spiritual manifestation of the pure concept of unstoppable fury</u>. This beats curse in intensity on my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T16:24:53-08:00","id":1468069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468052#post1468052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in CoD, Kuruth isn't just a frenzy, it is the <u>spiritual manifestation of the pure concept of unstoppable fury</u>. This beats curse in intensity on my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is\u2026 unsubstantiated, to say the least. It's a bigger deal to werewolves, culturally, because it's a blackout where your sole aim is murder, destruction, and cannibalism, but the problems it presents for a werewolf don't go away from being able to use Awakened magic to pull you out of it any more than they do for a pack full of Elodoth.<br /> <br /> Wasu-Im can be stopped by a Gift Facet that isn't even from the Rage set (and the Rage Facet to trigger Wasu-Im costs more to use and is more limited in its applicable frequency), and the rite to turn &quot;roll an exceptional success to keep Soft Rage from turning into Hard Rage&quot; into &quot;roll a total of five successes&quot; is rated at one dot, isn't tribally-locked, takes minutes to perform and lasts for a month.<br /> <br /> Vampires need to spend Willpower to hold off frenzy or act contrary to the goal of the frenzy, and sufficiently disastrous failure (including any failure to steer the frenzy, which also costs Willpower) makes it last specifically until you risk losing a stat that costs Experience to raise, unless you're lucky enough to have a Touchstone present to make a roll that's harder the more powerful you are; successfully holding off frenzy makes later frenzies harder to resist, there's no limit to how many times you can risk frenzy in a night, and the only workarounds in common circulation involve enhancing your ability to steer.<br /> <br /> Werewolves just need to roll Resolve + Composure to maintain lucidity, and the average PC Harmony range gives you several minutes to work with in addition to the above-mentioned rite and Facet and a Merit that lets you just shut it off with a single successful roll and a point of Willpower; again, most of the trigger conditions that don't involve being in the form built for murder can only affect you once per night. The main problem with Kuruth is that it's contagious at the moment of Hard Rage and a lot of really troublesome Gift Facets activate automatically and for free when you're Raging.<br /> <br /> It might take conjunctional Spirit and the spell factor for affecting a Size 7 target to pull it off, but the problems of berserk hunter demigods being prone to fits of murderous rage are not substantially enshrined in the metaphysics for them to be significantly harder to pull back to lucidity than it is to stop a vampire from giving into the worst of their atavistic urges under stress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T17:25:39-08:00","id":1468081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468052#post1468052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it WoD, I'd put a vampire's Frenzy above a Garou's for that matter. Not the Rage itself, but while the Garou's frenzy is just loosing control of your rage, a vampire is being overtaken by an unholy alien force that's trying to eat their very soul.<br /> <br /> But in CoD, Kuruth isn't just a frenzy, it is the <u>spiritual manifestation of the pure concept of unstoppable fury</u>. This beats curse in intensity on my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be nitpicking anything, but, uh, I thought it was the other way around\u2026?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T20:16:22-08:00","id":1468093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468069#post1468069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the problems it presents for a werewolf don't go away from being able to use Awakened magic to pull you out of it any more than they do for a pack full of Elodoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to make myself clear, I'm not defending that it should be harder to affect. I don't really care either way. I'm just commenting on thematic differences for what it represents to the splat, and in that I think it has a more fatalistic sense of a force of destruction within, while in Vampire it is more like the presence of the alien entity slowly stripping you of agency and identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468081#post1468081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be nitpicking anything, but, uh, I thought it was the other way around\u2026?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage in Apocalypse is a resource, and have heavy undertones of righteous fury. Pure in a moral sense, but not conceptually, as in &quot;unadulterated&quot;. While it may get out of hand and certainly isn't as unquestionably moral as Garou like to pretend, the themes and mechanics of the game are about embracing your Rage, using it regularly, directing it to good deeds (as you define them).<br /> <br /> It is also spiritual more in the religious sense, since while Garou are part-spirit, they're so in a sense of holiness instead of strangeness.<br /> <br /> Forsaken delves more into the notion of otherworldly, inhuman and derived from ideas. More importantly, Uratha are half-spirits in a more literal sense than Garou. They are not wolves, they're the essence of wolves, including the notions that only exist in culture and myth. And their frenzy comes from there, from the idea of the murderous beast, the cursed skin changer, the Beast of G\u00e9vaudan terrorizing people.<br /> <br /> Pure as in undiluted. The loss of higher thought to the beast within, beast in a sense that never existed outside human myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T21:31:47-08:00","id":1468096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468093#post1468093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage in Apocalypse is a resource, and have heavy undertones of righteous fury. Pure in a moral sense, but not conceptually, as in &amp;quot;unadulterated&amp;quot;. While it may get out of hand and certainly isn't as unquestionably moral as Garou like to pretend, the themes and mechanics of the game are about embracing your Rage, using it regularly, directing it to good deeds (as you define them).<br /> <br /> It is also spiritual more in the religious sense, since while Garou are part-spirit, they're so in a sense of holiness instead of strangeness.<br /> <br /> Forsaken delves more into the notion of otherworldly, inhuman and derived from ideas. More importantly, Uratha are half-spirits in a more literal sense than Garou. They are not wolves, they're the essence of wolves, including the notions that only exist in culture and myth. And their frenzy comes from there, from the idea of the murderous beast, the cursed skin changer, the Beast of G\u00e9vaudan terrorizing people.<br /> <br /> Pure as in undiluted. The loss of higher thought to the beast within, beast in a sense that never existed outside human myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh so that\u2019s what it was.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I still think Uratha Rage isn\u2019t too sacrosanct compared to vampiric Frenzy, precisely <i>because</i> it\u2019s not-exactly-holy-but-instead-otherworldly nature.<br /> <br /> I mean, they\u2019re called <i>ephemeral</i> beings around here.<br /> <br /> But yeah, we probably shouldn\u2019t get mired up on this. It\u2019s a relatively minor business compared to blasphemies I\u2019ve been pondering, like \u201cCan I homebrew up a Mage Legacy about stealing Gift-brands via Prime and Spirit magic?\u201d To which the response should be \u201cWait what?\u201d <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T09:05:00-08:00","id":1468139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468096#post1468096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh so that\u2019s what it was.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I still think Uratha Rage isn\u2019t too sacrosanct compared to vampiric Frenzy, precisely <i>because</i> it\u2019s not-exactly-holy-but-instead-otherworldly nature.<br /> <br /> I mean, they\u2019re called <i>ephemeral</i> beings around here.<br /> <br /> But yeah, we probably shouldn\u2019t get mired up on this. It\u2019s a relatively minor business compared to blasphemies I\u2019ve been pondering, like \u201cCan I homebrew up a Mage Legacy about stealing Gift-brands via Prime and Spirit magic?\u201d To which the response should be \u201cWait what?\u201d <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have seen <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2017/01/mage-awakening-2nd-ed-new-legacy.html\" target=\"_blank\">something similar</a> being homebrewed for Geists, but it inherently required them to destroy or eat a Geist in order to join, with the only other alternative being a deal with a Kerberoi. This would lead to tense situations when the truth would come to light. Perhaps that can serve as a starting point for your idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T10:25:09-08:00","id":1468151,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, it's funny to me that you can still cast Knowing Time spells on a mummy, as I would have assumed part of the point was to prevent using Postcognition to see things in their past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T11:06:47-08:00","id":1468155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468151#post1468151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, it's funny to me that you can still cast Knowing Time spells on a mummy, as I would have assumed part of the point was to prevent using Postcognition to see things in their past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I thought it was to prevent Shenanigans with either adding or subtracting a few decades to a Mummy\u2019s Descent. Also the Arisen are outside of Time, interacting with it, but not a part of it, so there is that to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T21:42:44-08:00","id":1468224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468151#post1468151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, it's funny to me that you can still cast Knowing Time spells on a mummy, as I would have assumed part of the point was to prevent using Postcognition to see things in their past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Postcognition's Unveiling, using it for that purpose requires temporal sympathy and half an idea what you're looking for, mummies sleeping through the ages means they aren't doing anything interesting in the vast majority of recorded history, and if this was the goal we'd have seen it pop up in other gamelines where the unreliability of memory is a thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;It risks Paradox and gives you a Paradox Condition that risks more Paradox as the demon-gods made of suffering have noticed you&quot; feels like a reasonable price to pay, given this doesn't give the Arisen reliable information about previous or future Descents and messing with their Memory is <i>also</i> hard-locked from outside tampering (albeit without its own extra consequences).<br /> <br /> They're the terrifying patrons of secretive cults who hide them away in tombs where they sleep for years, decades, or centuries, and when they wake up they might remember the last time you saw them, the time they first woke up thousands of years ago, the time they <i>will</i> wake up thousands of years <i>from now</i>, the time they awakened in a parallel timeline to tilt the currents from a tide of death, or nothing at all on account of this being the first time they've arisen ever from their perspective. Getting information about their history through magic is only going to make things <i>more</i> confusing, which is the entire point of the section where the sidebar detailing their interaction with Awakened magic appears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T22:14:23-08:00","id":1468230,"title":"","content":"On a semi-relevant side note, being shown your past is not the same thing as experiencing Memory, any more than watching a video of your childhood is an experience of Memory. It can trigger memories for you, sure, but even if one assumes you have the context for what is shown, it's not immediately the same thing as coming upon them yourself, particularly since any given Arisen's chain of memories is now part of the cloud of unintended effects of the Rite and therefore has metaphysical signficance when the collisions of magic and psychological sympathies line up.<br /> <br /> But a little more on point, the Judges stake is in making ensuring their second-hand agents of edification and judgment that they got from their ungrateful and faithless kids keep up what they're supposed to do in this game they've got going on with Sutek's impositions. Despite the flaws of the Rite, and with the whole damn world, the Judges aren't particularly worried about Apotheosis all that much, and know they couldn't actually do much about it even if they tried-Sutek's decrees pretty much guarentee they can't close that door. For the most part, their investment in the Arisen that manifests against outside tampering is to make sure that the second-hand game pieces play <i>mostly</i> like their supposed to, and not get thrown the fuck off course by some-any-petty ante sorcerer with delusions of godhood.<br /> <br /> Let the Arisen remember-what good will it do them as the tide pulls it away, when suffering is still the dominant law of reality? So long as the pieces are on the board, all but the most unfortunate will eventually end up playing the game. That settings include the far flung future where the rest of humanity has returned to the dust but the Arisen still act is a testament to how much the Judges really have to worry about this passing breeze called Memory.<br /> <br /> EDIT: On the off chance a certain element of this wasn't clear, though:<br /> <br /> In a world where people can produce all matter of physical &quot;evidence&quot; even without magic, implant fake memories, or change their appearance or any number of other things, the Judges are about as concerned about a mage using Postcognition as they are a changeling using Skinmask and a camcorder-not very much, since the near universal Chronicles maxim of &quot;Not everything is as it seems&quot; is as useful a blinder as it is a lens.<br /> <br /> If there's anything like a hole the Judges <i>should</i> be worried about, it's that, depending on how seriously you apply <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1353525#post1353525\">this post</a> to your games, there's a huge hole in the defense that demons, of all people, could exploit. If you apply Bunyip's take, you know someone amongst the 42 assholes is slapping their head(/approximate appendage/symbol/concept) over <i>that</i> oversight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-18-2021, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T17:45:44-08:00","id":1468314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468224#post1468224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Postcognition's Unveiling, using it for that purpose requires temporal sympathy and half an idea what you're looking for, mummies sleeping through the ages means they aren't doing anything interesting in the vast majority of recorded history, and if this was the goal we'd have seen it pop up in other gamelines where the unreliability of memory is a thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;It risks Paradox and gives you a Paradox Condition that risks more Paradox as the demon-gods made of suffering have noticed you&quot; feels like a reasonable price to pay, given this doesn't give the Arisen reliable information about previous or future Descents and messing with their Memory is <i>also</i> hard-locked from outside tampering (albeit without its own extra consequences).<br /> <br /> They're the terrifying patrons of secretive cults who hide them away in tombs where they sleep for years, decades, or centuries, and when they wake up they might remember the last time you saw them, the time they first woke up thousands of years ago, the time they <i>will</i> wake up thousands of years <i>from now</i>, the time they awakened in a parallel timeline to tilt the currents from a tide of death, or nothing at all on account of this being the first time they've arisen ever from their perspective. Getting information about their history through magic is only going to make things <i>more</i> confusing, which is the entire point of the section where the sidebar detailing their interaction with Awakened magic appears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sincerely good to know.<br /> <br /> Arc, I don't think I've seen a post of yours in writer mode thus far. It's nice to see, and compelling stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T16:20:14-08:00","id":1468536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1467837#post1467837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's reasonable to let a Nameless character have the character creation rotes on the assumption that <i>somebody</i> was able to teach them some custom mudras and mnemonic recall principles, but maybe make it a complication in learning further rotes.<br /> <br /> For Acts of Hubris, I'll point out that the list given for Understanding Wisdom includes binding a being to a task. I think it's reasonable to say that even for a spirit of fire, pinning it to work involving burning things can be an Act of Hubris, because the central thesis isn't being bad, it's acting without proper consideration for or comprehension of the consequences of your actions. The spirit might be perfectly fine with what it's been commanded to do, but the outcome of commanding it, both in what it does and in what it then becomes unable to do, may go off in directions that are not great. There are also elements of the ethics of taking choice away even if the subject might well choose to do that thing of their own accord, and how the mage is taking on responsibility for actions beyond themselves on a deep spiritual level.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that Command Spirit would be an Act of Hubris on every occasion under those conditions; you could command it to do something of smaller scope or shorter term, that aren't throwing things too much out of harmony.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the provided list of Acts of Hubris is not supposed to be exhaustive or proscriptive, and the first paragraph about losing Wisdom states that different mages doing the same thing might not have the same risk of degeneration. So I'd say it can also account for things like how one generally portrays the character (the degree to which they act cautiously and observe spells in action carefully), or else what they're doing around this spell in particular to manage its risks. Commanding an ephemeral entity can be Hubris if it's an ad hoc thing then left to its own devices, but if you've got a good handle on the situation and supervise it, then I think you wouldn't need to roll.<br /> <br /> In any event, I'd still say Wisdom is written to be something characters risk with decent frequency. It's just part of the general tone of the game, that mages really dance a lot with becoming unconcerned with what their actions cause.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I'm strongly of the mind that actions that aren't magic should still be capable of risking Wisdom, because I see the whole point of that stat as being that the mage's Awakening and Gnosis makes them sensitive to a general interconnectedness of things that makes the management of their place in the grand scheme relevant to the stability of their souls. It's like, connection to the Supernal hardens your soul against those things that once risked its Integrity, but the substance of what reinforces it also creates a certain rigidity and is formed from a deeper presence in the Tapestry.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It isn't so much that I am worried about dodging Wisdom degradation, it is more of the long the lines of a more meta understanding of what the limits and bounds of Acts of Hubris are. Our Storyteller doesn't want anything innured, so playing careful with what spells can or cannot do before starting to interact with Hubris seems to have much more weight in our game than it otherwise would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T17:06:37-08:00","id":1468538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468536#post1468536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It isn't so much that I am worried about dodging Wisdom degradation, it is more of the long the lines of a more meta understanding of what the limits and bounds of Acts of Hubris are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I didn't mean to insinuate anything; the line about risks coming up often was really intended to stake a position on what the meta function would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our Storyteller doesn't want anything innured, so playing careful with what spells can or cannot do before starting to interact with Hubris seems to have much more weight in our game than it otherwise would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well inuring can only be done for one spell per Gnosis dot, so I don't think it really works out as something that massively shifts how things would play out anyway. Maybe in the case of a particular spell that the player wishes to be a signature of the character without constantly rolling for degeneration.<br /> <br /> Although bringing it up does point me to the wording about how an inured spell doesn't risk loss of Wisdom &quot;no matter the action&quot;, which I think reinforces the idea that few spells are blanket Acts of Hubris. Spells to bind a spirit may or may not be hubris depending on the action, even if inuring makes it permanently not so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T01:49:11-08:00","id":1468576,"title":"","content":"I believe inuring any spells at all is quite rare. In order to inure a spell, you need to end up losing Wisdom from using it, and predict that you're using that particular spell often enough in ways that are Acts of Hubris. On top of that, you must also consider the added Paradox risk (or increase of existing Paradox risk) to be worth it despite it being a spell you plan on using multiple times in the future. On top of all that, I wouldn't be surprised if most players just straight up forget that inurement is a thing during the few times they end up losing Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T14:04:25-08:00","id":1468631,"title":"","content":"Inuring also means having to deal with Paradox every single time. Which means its a balancing act, since the mage uses the spell often enough and in a way that is damaging to Wisdom. Now every time they cast that specific spell there is a cost benefit analysis, because either they need to expend the resources to contain the Paradox, deal with the Paradox Condition or the consequences of unleashing it. Since Paradox accumulation is a cascading effect, it means they need to use it sparingly or they could end up summoning anomalies, make someone possessed by an Abyssal being, summon an Invader into reality or even corrupting a sacred site. Imagine if the mage needs to cast a spell to deal with an emergency during a summoning, when invading another's Sanctum (Seer, abandoned workshop, rival's, etc) or when investigating an Aedes. Now they could potentially corrupt the summon, taint the Hallow, twist the Aedes into an Aberrance or worse, which could create far worse Acts of Hubris. Inuring doesn't eliminate the risk to Wisdom entirely, it merely changes the risks associated with casting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-22-2021, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T13:53:22-08:00","id":1468701,"title":"","content":"Lets say a mage finds a dying Sleeper. This mage is a master of Time, so they figure that since change is in the Arcanum's purview, then they can use an Unmaking to undo all negative change, a Time Heal that is analogous to Deny The Reaper. Since the subject is a Sleeper, it means that they will suffer a breaking point from it, so would healing them be an Act of Hubris ? Its arguable that deciding their life is more important than their soul's stability could be seen as one. However, its could also be argued that just being there and having the power to do something means the choice will always be up to them, since apathy or, to give a Greek equivalent, Acedia, could be seen an inability to judge when to use magic. Would this be a case of the Act of Hubris being subjective depending on the individual's perspective ?<br /> <br /> On an unrelated question, when Interconnections detects sympathetic connections between subjects, does it allow them to understand the nature of them and track them ? Since this is an area where Space and Fate seem to overlap to a degree, it makes me wonder if similar Reach effects could be applied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T18:16:34-08:00","id":1468716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468701#post1468701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say a mage finds a dying Sleeper. This mage is a master of Time, so they figure that since change is in the Arcanum's purview, then they can use an Unmaking to undo all negative change, a Time Heal that is analogous to Deny The Reaper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for a start, it's not necessary to be a Master to do this. Temporal Summoning (Weaving Practice) explicitly says that it can be used to heal injuries, in the form without requiring the Sympathy Attainment even. You'd have the issue of them returning to the damaged state when the spell ends, but so does Deny the Reaper. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the subject is a Sleeper, it means that they will suffer a breaking point from it, so would healing them be an Act of Hubris ? Its arguable that deciding their life is more important than their soul's stability could be seen as one. However, its could also be argued that just being there and having the power to do something means the choice will always be up to them, since apathy or, to give a Greek equivalent, Acedia, could be seen an inability to judge when to use magic. Would this be a case of the Act of Hubris being subjective depending on the individual's perspective ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the last one, although I'd lean more often in favour of it risking degeneration (albeit with a bonus like what acting in accordance with Virtue gets). I'm personally inclined to rule towards Wisdom not generally being risked by a mage being most reserved and cautious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated question, when Interconnections detects sympathetic connections between subjects, does it allow them to understand the nature of them and track them ? Since this is an area where Space and Fate seem to overlap to a degree, it makes me wonder if similar Reach effects could be applied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'd start with noting the distinction where Interconnections is an Unveiling spell and Correspondence is a Knowing one; the former works through allowing the mage to perceive new things, the latter works by transmitting information to them directly. It also means that the Fate mage is only really seeing the links so far as is within their sensory range. Space is also a bit more comprehensive with it with sympathy being more firmly under its purview.<br /> <br /> That being said, I could see a separately cast Knowing of Fate being able to give some sense of the nature of a connection between two or more subjects on the basis of how they affect one another's journey towards respective Fates. Hmm, I'd be inclined to make that function a bit differently than just straight up telling you the form of their relationship, and communicate it more in terms of the impact they're having. A Fate spell won't straight up tell you that this person's connection is to a romantic partner, but it will tell you that it's a tie to somebody guiding them towards disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T20:17:54-08:00","id":1468723,"title":"","content":"I am a bit confused, I thought Temporal Summoning simply loaded your state at one point in history into your current one. <br /> <br /> But Deny The Reaper and Temporal Healing would be Unmaking, which means the entropy or negative change were deleted altogether. In other words, much like healing with Life, the effects are Lasting, which is why they are Potency primary. <br /> <br /> The revival effect in Deny The Reaper is the only one that seems to have a set duration and it requires enough entropy to be reversed such that the corpse was in a state where it was within the spell's target interval (such as using multiple casts reverting the 200 year old skeleton to how they looked 3 months after death before they could be revived).<br /> <br /> If that is not the case, wouldn't that mean the healing spells in Life should also only have temporary effects ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T23:39:43-08:00","id":1468734,"title":"","content":"Knit and Mend are lasting because they're based on direct damage spells which are lasting regardless of Practice.<br /> Temporal Summoning does indeed use Temporal Sympathy, but assumes most injuries are gained within the timespan the subject is considered &quot;unchanged&quot;.<br /> Deny the Reaper is not lasting because Making/Unmaking spells are generally not lasting. Most Unmaking spells are merely suppressing what they're supposed to remove, causing whatever's removed to reappear once the spell ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T10:30:38-08:00","id":1468766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468723#post1468723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But Deny The Reaper and Temporal Healing would be Unmaking, which means the entropy or negative change were deleted altogether. In other words, much like healing with Life, the effects are Lasting, which is why they are Potency primary.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I would find healing effects of Life to be Lasting because they're expediting a natural healing process. Deny the Reaper and theoretical deletion of events from a person's past are much more impositions in a manner that is consistently dependent on continuing Duration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The revival effect in Deny The Reaper is the only one that seems to have a set duration and it requires enough entropy to be reversed such that the corpse was in a state where it was within the spell's target interval (such as using multiple casts reverting the 200 year old skeleton to how they looked 3 months after death before they could be revived).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think that there is no way that such decay reversal would be Lasting, and if it is not then your proposition runs into the fact that spells do not stack. You can cast as many such spells as you want on a skeleton, and only the one with the highest Potency will work.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468734#post1468734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deny the Reaper is not lasting because Making/Unmaking spells are generally not lasting. Most Unmaking spells are merely suppressing what they're supposed to remove, causing whatever's removed to reappear once the spell ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although the instant death spells are going to have Lasting effects. Like, you Unmake all electrical activity in a person's pattern, maybe it returns when the spell ends, but that won't change the fact that your vital processes shut down completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T13:33:51-08:00","id":1468775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468766#post1468766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although the instant death spells are going to have Lasting effects. Like, you Unmake all electrical activity in a person's pattern, maybe it returns when the spell ends, but that won't change the fact that your vital processes shut down completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is generally* true. The reason why Lasting isn't listed along Practices and Primary Factors in spell descriptions is because the term is literally just referring to the consequences of the spell. All spells have consequences, but whether specific effects are Lasting or not depends on what's part of the spell's effect and what's a consequence of that effect.<br /> <br /> This is why Knit and Mend are lasting; they're making the body heal the damage, but when they stop making the body heal damage, the damage doesn't return. That's the same (but inverted) way direct damage spells work; the spell ending removes the source of the damage, but any damage already inflicted by that source of damage still remains.<br /> <br /> This is also why Regeneration isn't Lasting. The spell makes the subject have a restored limb (or whatever) and when the spell ends the restored limb disappears with it. The way to circumvent this is to make a spell that causes the body itself to regenerate the missing limb, which would funnily enough be Weaving (or possibly Perfecting) rather than Patterning, but it would also definitely take more time.<br /> <br /> <br /> *A theoretical spell that would Unmake your entire person would just restore you completely to your pre-Unmade state when it ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T16:31:43-08:00","id":1468792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468775#post1468775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is generally* true. The reason why Lasting isn't listed along Practices and Primary Factors in spell descriptions is because the term is literally just referring to the consequences of the spell. All spells have consequences, but whether specific effects are Lasting or not depends on what's part of the spell's effect and what's a consequence of that effect.<br /> <br /> This is why Knit and Mend are lasting; they're making the body heal the damage, but when they stop making the body heal damage, the damage doesn't return. That's the same (but inverted) way direct damage spells work; the spell ending removes the source of the damage, but any damage already inflicted by that source of damage still remains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we've got a sidebar along the general spell factors description giving the basic concept and usual terms in which it applies, and then a number of spells that give it as a Reach effect. In a lot of cases, I feel as though whether something comes with the option to make it Lasting comes down a lot to it being excessively inconvenient for it not to be (and other times when it's suitably dramatic).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way to circumvent this is to make a spell that causes the body itself to regenerate the missing limb, which would funnily enough be Weaving (or possibly Perfecting) rather than Patterning, but it would also definitely take more time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best one ought to be able to do with Weaving is bestow a regenerative capability that already comfortably exists in nature, which is often going to be inadequate for human needs. Back in the day, you got a lot of people asking why you couldn't make somebody regrow limbs like a starfish; I proposed that you could let people do that... like a starfish. It's not something that's going to be able to handle bones or some of the more complex human musculature, you're not getting a functional hand out of it.<br /> <br /> Plus stuff like the calories it's going to require<br /> <br /> Bestowing a regenerative healing factor that fully rebuilds everything functionally like what werewolves have is going to be the Imperial Practice of Entities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T23:25:03-08:00","id":1468817,"title":"","content":"Of course, the regenerative properties of an <b>axolotl</b> is fully capable of generating bones, cartilage, ligaments, muscles, and most other organs <i>from scratch</i>. A much better choice than a starfish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T05:06:23-08:00","id":1468829,"title":"","content":"Well my priority is to proceed from an assumption that you can't make better regeneration than what the Patterning spell provides, so it would still look at such an animal as insufficient to restore something like the highly dextrous human hand, the sharp human eye, or incomparably complex human brain.<br /> <br /> If I needed to reconcile that with other effects of Transform Life, it would be in an idea that those other traits are more direct in their capabilities, where the end results of an added animal regeneration end up being secondary to the addition of the regeneration itself. That is to say, it becoming part of your anatomy is magic, but it doesn't perform additional magical feats.<br /> <br /> Would probably be very useful for integrating organ transplants, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T05:42:04-08:00","id":1468837,"title":"","content":"The Patterning spell is still <b>instant</b>. That's pretty good.<br /> <br /> And yes, the kind of regeneration an axolotl has would indeed be sufficient to recreate the dextrous hand of a human, since it's not actually any more complicated than their own limbs. We've got more bones and everything is larger, but that's artificial complexity arising from the scale rather than any inherent difficulty in human anatomy. The fact that there's more to do only factors into the time it takes for the limb to regenerate. The same applies for eyes and other organs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T09:53:24-08:00","id":1468844,"title":"","content":"Axolotls are researched precisely because their regeneration triggers the wholesale formation of limbs and organs, so I have to agree that at this point it should be just complete regeneration.<br /> <br /> Of course, it isn't actually without drawbacks, they don't form scar tissue and the whole process is time, energy and protein consuming, and they can't get a thing back if they can't survive until then. But it <b>is</b> complete regeneration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T10:26:52-08:00","id":1468847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468837#post1468837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Patterning spell is still <b>instant</b>. That's pretty good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't enough to maintain validity for the spell in possibly anything other than emergencies when the time it takes to cast it is compared against the efforts of making it last and the prospect of it being dispelled.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's a four dot spell that can at best get two free Reach and might be the kind of thing where the risk of Paradox wants to be as minimal as possible. It seems that Reach is better spent on it being Advanced and Indefinite Duration than moving out of Ritual casting.<br /> <br /> These are not conditions sufficient to keep it (and the dramatic potential inherent to it) from being rendered redundant by a lower dot spell, and I take issue with such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T10:42:44-08:00","id":1468850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468847#post1468847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It isn't enough to maintain validity for the spell in possibly anything other than emergencies when the time it takes to cast it is compared against the efforts of making it last and the prospect of it being dispelled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eighteen hours of ritual casting is preferable to a time probably measured in days at minimum for borrowed animal regeneration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T11:20:00-08:00","id":1468857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468850#post1468850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eighteen hours of ritual casting is preferable to a time probably measured in days at minimum for borrowed animal regeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely and beyond that.<br /> <br /> The regeneration of an animal would intrinsically bring a lot of issues since, as stated, the magic makes it work but doesn't work in a &quot;magical&quot; way, it follows natural rules as in the animal.<br /> <br /> And even for the amazing regenerative abilities of an axolotl that would mean a very sensitive tissue (remember, no scarring), the natural-paced growth of a new organ or limb, fueled by time, energy and needed materials.<br /> <br /> You can do a quick search on the internet to run the correct numbers or make shit up for the game, but as a rule of thumb nothing should grow in such a pace as to be more noticeable than your hair and nails growing, by mass, not perceived volume, and the quicker it happens it should require more energy and raw materials above regular nutrition requirements.<br /> <br /> Since this is a complex internal process, you can apply on the fly tiredness and fever as symptoms along with the sensitive tissue, so keeping it at the fastest pace, while shortening the time with symptoms, would worsen them.<br /> <br /> Finally, just as with axolotls, it may have potential side effects as regeneration may incur in errors by itself. It shouldn't be common, but extra limbs do happen and aren't as useful as it seems when your body isn't actually meant to have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T13:18:13-08:00","id":1468930,"title":"","content":"In the case of Unmaking, isn't the principle behind <i>Blink of an Eye</i> to Unmake the time needed to execute actions ? The subject does not need to experience the steps of doing the actions later, so the destroyed time doesn't seem to come back once duration expires. Similarly, <i>Annihilate Matter</i> and <i>Annihilate Spirit</i> suggest that a subject is destroyed utterly and permanently. However, <i>Corridors of Time</i> seems to destroy the events entirely and allow the Fallen World to fill in the temporal vaccum based on the new actions. Due to these examples and the fact that page 125 of the core book does not expand upon this, I believe it can be inferred that the Practice allows for variation based on intent.<br /> <br /> Regarding regeneration via Weaving, I think a mix of it and Perfecting would get rid of any anomalies. The biggest issues would be disguising a regrowing limb, explaining such a miraculous heal without causing Disbelief and maintaining the spell for the full interval needed for the regrowth. However, a master of Time could basically make a bubble with Veil of Moments (avoids nutrient deficiency) and Temporal Pocket to allow a subject to &quot;instantly&quot; complete the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-27-2021, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T09:10:49-08:00","id":1468992,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to access a person\u2019s Oneiros after their death? Assuming there\u2019s no ghost left behind them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26473-ewrygn","name":"ewrygn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T09:41:21-08:00","id":1468995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ewrygn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468992#post1468992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to access a person\u2019s Oneiros after their death? Assuming there\u2019s no ghost left behind them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Oneiros is the inside of the individual soul and the soul moves on after death, so probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T09:48:48-08:00","id":1468996,"title":"","content":"Hmm, this brings up more questions, like are ghosts represented in the Astral? Presumably in the Anima Mundi? If they are, think it would be possible to find the shattered \u201cremains\u201d of someone\u2019s Oneiros? It probably wouldn\u2019t be their actual Oneiros, but like the impression of one, much like a ghost, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T09:57:25-08:00","id":1468998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468996#post1468996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, this brings up more questions, like are ghosts represented in the Astral? Presumably in the Anima Mundi? If they are, think it would be possible to find the shattered \u201cremains\u201d of someone\u2019s Oneiros? It probably wouldn\u2019t be their actual Oneiros, but like the impression of one, much like a ghost, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>There can be some Irises connecting the Underworld to places in the Temenos, especially the Realm of Death, so the odd ghost might drift in that way, but ghosts are neither native to the Astral nor naturally capable of travelling there via meditation as they do not have the souls that it exists within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T10:02:00-08:00","id":1468999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468998#post1468998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There can be some Irises connecting the Underworld to places in the Temenos, especially the Realm of Death, so the odd ghost might drift in that way, but ghosts are neither native to the Astral nor naturally capable of travelling there via meditation as they do not have the souls that it exists within.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, might have miscommunicated something there. I meant like a realm devoted towards representing a ghosts thoughts, not actually a ghost in the astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T10:28:04-08:00","id":1469002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468996#post1468996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, this brings up more questions, like are ghosts represented in the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e Astral Realms book discussed the unusual phenomenon of ghosts turning up in the Realm of Death or elsewhere in the Temenos, and there are a few animal ghosts that show up in the Dreaming Earth. They're slightly more common to come across than spirits, but unless you're looking for them you might confuse them with normal goetia \u2014 like Temenotic Residents, many ghosts in the Astral don't realize they're in a shared dream-space.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Presumably in the Anima Mundi? If they are, think it would be possible to find the shattered \u201cremains\u201d of someone\u2019s Oneiros? It probably wouldn\u2019t be their actual Oneiros, but like the impression of one, much like a ghost, right? </div> </div> </div>The Oneiros only debatably exists as an experienceable world when someone's not exploring it, and ghosts aren't souls. Depending on how you interpret the material in the Beast Player's Guide to interact with the Awakened approach to the Astral, you might be able to use Time spells to restore lost connections between the Temenos and a dead individual's Oneiros in the same way one visits an isolated Temenos realm, but the greater plasticity and instability of the individual soul is such that even that might be trickier than just time-traveling back to a point where the Oneiros was intact and making the journey there directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T13:51:39-08:00","id":1469015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1468999#post1468999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant like a realm devoted towards representing a ghosts thoughts, not actually a ghost in the astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have the presence to contribute to the Astral.<br /> <br /> I believe that humans and Beasts are the only thing that really do (although werewolves have a connection to the Anima Mundi, a Realm which is not shaped by cultural perspective).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T14:20:48-08:00","id":1469020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469015#post1469015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't have the presence to contribute to the Astral.<br /> <br /> I believe that humans and Beasts are the only thing that really do (although werewolves have a connection to the Anima Mundi, a Realm which is not shaped by cultural perspective).</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans and <i>mages</i> contribute to the Astral (in the form of personal Oneiroi and collectively to Temenotic realms). Beasts have a unique relationship to the Astral because one of the two entities that form a Beast is native.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T14:58:02-08:00","id":1469025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469015#post1469015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that humans and Beasts are the only thing that really do (although werewolves have a connection to the Anima Mundi, a Realm which is not shaped by cultural perspective).</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have souls, as twisted as they may be, why Vampires, Changelings and Sin Eaters don't have Oneiroi and weight in the Temenos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T15:15:34-08:00","id":1469026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469015#post1469015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't have the presence to contribute to the Astral.<br /> <br /> I believe that humans and Beasts are the only thing that really do (although werewolves have a connection to the Anima Mundi, a Realm which is not shaped by cultural perspective).</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe this is head-canon that I forgot wasn\u2019t canon, but I thought everything that thinks contributes to the Astral somewhere. Normally rocks can\u2019t think, (that I know of anyway,) but everything has a spirit. And spirit thoughts contribute to the Anima Mundi. That\u2019s why you can have a Werewolf connected to Anima Mundi, because they are literally half spirit. I\u2019d argue they should be connected to the Temenos too, because werewolf are half human too. But if Deviants aren\u2019t connected, werewolf definitely aren\u2019t. I guess the question on whether something can connect to the Temenos is the same as asking if it\u2019s human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T15:33:57-08:00","id":1469028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469025#post1469025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have souls, as twisted as they may be, why Vampires, Changelings and Sin Eaters don't have Oneiroi and weight in the Temenos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires and changelings don't have human or near-human souls, which is required for linking up to the Temenos and quite possibly also to having an Oneiros. They have equivalents that are too far removed to count as human for such purposes. Mages are the only supers that have souls that are human-like enough to still link up to the Temenos.<br /> <br /> Bound/Sin-Eaters straight up don't have souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T15:58:44-08:00","id":1469033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469026#post1469026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this is head-canon that I forgot wasn\u2019t canon, but I thought everything that thinks contributes to the Astral somewhere. Normally rocks can\u2019t think, (that I know of anyway,) but everything has a spirit. And spirit thoughts contribute to the Anima Mundi. That\u2019s why you can have a Werewolf connected to Anima Mundi, because they are literally half spirit. I\u2019d argue they should be connected to the Temenos too, because werewolf are half human too. But if Deviants aren\u2019t connected, werewolf definitely aren\u2019t. I guess the question on whether something can connect to the Temenos is the same as asking if it\u2019s human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves' souls aren't entirely human, changelings' souls were damaged by the Thorns and their durance, and vampires straight-up shouldn't have souls anymore by the common metaphysics. All three keep Touchstones to maintain their ability to relate to the world around them in a healthy fashion.<br /> <br /> Of the other three splats that have non-optional Touchstones, Sin-Eaters are the only ones who don't have a human soul and are instead a pair of ghosts managing unifying pursuits in a way not unlike those produced by a deviant's Conviction and Loyalty; hunters have tweaked their Integrity to work in tiers at the cost of alienating their fellow mortals, and when the Arisen have Touchstones, it's in service of developing their historical perspective by attending to the strengths and weaknesses of their companions.<br /> <br /> The Astral is made of <i>ideas</i>. It's the universal unconscious, which is part of why the pettier drives are so well-represented there. Whether because their experiences have changed their mindset too far to align with the common thoughts of humanity or because the forces that power their magic are jealous and alien gods, supernatural beings who've stopped being human and aren't part monster-born-of-human-culture don't contribute to the Temenos directly through their thoughts and dreams, and the Anima Mundi is\u2026 <i>bigger</i> than werewolves, vampires, et cetera \u2014 whatever they could contribute would be a drop in the bucket even before the Ecstatic Wind swept it across the world-soul in a thousand-thousand pieces.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't have free will, being the sum of their parts, and human ghosts are in many ways the photo negative of a soul in trauma, bound up in the circumstances of their creation and buried under so much Underworld poison; their influence on human culture is largely limited to the same indirect means that everyone else uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T17:21:12-08:00","id":1469048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469020#post1469020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humans and <i>mages</i> contribute to the Astral</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are entirely human, it was not an addition I thought worth making.<br /> <br /> In Chronicles of Darkness terms, I'd say something becomes inhuman when, like ephemeral entities and horrors, its bodily structure and capabilities undergoes some major alterations and it acquires weird compulsions and weaknesses (basically equivalent to a Ban and Bane).<br /> <br /> There's no substance mages will take aggravated damage from for magical reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-27-2021, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T18:11:10-08:00","id":1469052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469048#post1469048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are entirely human, it was not an addition I thought worth making.<br /> <br /> In Chronicles of Darkness terms, I'd say something becomes inhuman when, like ephemeral entities and horrors, its bodily structure and capabilities undergoes some major alterations and it acquires weird compulsions and weaknesses (basically equivalent to a Ban and Bane).<br /> <br /> There's no substance mages will take aggravated damage from for magical reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that this is wrong, I actually this this is a pretty interesting take, but aren\u2019t there sorcerers that gain bans and/or banes for power over stuff? (Not Mages, but that would be a pretty interesting legacy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T18:33:37-08:00","id":1469054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469052#post1469052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that this is wrong, I actually this this is a pretty interesting take, but aren\u2019t there sorcerers that gain bans and/or banes for power over stuff? (Not Mages, but that would be a pretty interesting legacy)</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Occultists from Werewolf (Shunned by the Moon)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T18:43:32-08:00","id":1469056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469054#post1469054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadow Occultists from Werewolf (Shunned by the Moon)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? Considering I don\u2019t own that book, I\u2019m not sure. But that sounds right, it was something shadow related. I was just pointing out that technically you can stitch bans and banes on a human without them becoming a monster. Can those Shadow Occultists lose their banes and/or banes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T19:03:05-08:00","id":1469058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469056#post1469056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe? Considering I don\u2019t own that book, I\u2019m not sure. But that sounds right, it was something shadow related. I was just pointing out that technically you can stitch bans and banes on a human without them becoming a monster. Can those Shadow Occultists lose their banes and/or banes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc, they first get their patron spirit\u2019s Bane, and a Taboo modeled from their patron spirit\u2019s Ban, and then can build up more Influence dots at the cost of picking up more Taboos. Though I\u2019m saying this purely from memory at the moment, so take it with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> Also, even without bringing in Werewolf, the 2E official (and partial) writeup for the Keepers of the Covenant mention the potential of mages getting Claimed, so there\u2019s that avenue too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T01:42:03-08:00","id":1469078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469056#post1469056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe? Considering I don\u2019t own that book, I\u2019m not sure. But that sounds right, it was something shadow related. I was just pointing out that technically you can stitch bans and banes on a human without them becoming a monster. Can those Shadow Occultists lose their banes and/or banes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have questions about how much such power is really integrated into the subject so that the compulsion and weakness could be considered an aspect of themselves rather than innate to a power they're touching off of.<br /> <br /> Still, there would also be the point about a change in their physical nature; something equivalent to how the vampires get the undead body, need Vitae to rise each night and can spend it to enhance Attributes, and can go into a torpid state.<br /> <br /> If it's a case that somebody has integrated a power that is also altering them at that level, then I would think they're drifting further from humanity in a metaphysical sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T03:23:39-08:00","id":1469081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469048#post1469048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are entirely human, it was not an addition I thought worth making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are not entirely humans. That's the whole point of having mages as a splat. Not to mention that souls are key to how something links up to the Astral, and mages specifically don't have human souls. Just souls that are close enough that one can be transformed into the other (and likely vice versa).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-28-2021, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T05:42:49-08:00","id":1469088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469081#post1469081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are not entirely humans. That's the whole point of having mages as a splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters are a splat, all the way down to unmodified cell level. The blue book primarily portrays the humans who fumble in ignorance and weakness, and all additional ones depict characters with more agency in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> mages specifically don't have human souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that specified?<br /> <br /> I'll point out that we've got at least one Order who is very much of the idea that mages are not distinguished from humanity, seeing the Imperium Mysteriorum as the sacred right of all of them.<br /> <br /> It's less direct in the Free Council creed, but still the implication of human work containing magical secrets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T06:11:17-08:00","id":1469091,"title":"","content":"One question I have in this regard:<br /> <br /> Given how little impact they would have anyway due to their low numbers, what would effectively change in the game if all splats had still Oneiroi and impact on the Temenos? And what would that imply?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T06:25:42-08:00","id":1469092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469081#post1469081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are not entirely humans. That's the whole point of having mages as a splat. Not to mention that souls are key to how something links up to the Astral, and mages specifically don't have human souls. Just souls that are close enough that one can be transformed into the other (and likely vice versa).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469088#post1469088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is that specified?<br /> <br /> I'll point out that we've got at least one Order who is very much of the idea that mages are not distinguished from humanity, seeing the Imperium Mysteriorum as the sacred right of all of them.<br /> <br /> It's less direct in the Free Council creed, but still the implication of human work containing magical secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div> Funny, you both are right. Technically, Mages have their souls reforged in the fires of Supernal truth. This makes them Human . As opposed to human. They are what Humanity should be, but aren\u2019t. Does this make them inhuman? A Mage\u2019s connection to the Temenos implies that it does not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469091#post1469091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question I have in this regard:<br /> <br /> Given how little impact they would have anyway due to their low numbers, what would effectively change in the game if all splats had still Oneiroi and impact on the Temenos? And what would that imply?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would imply that they all were still human, at least when considered from our current viewpoint. It technically goes against several game lines themes, like Promethean and Deviant. That being said I don\u2019t feel it would mess up the Temenos at all, there just might be a spot representing that creatures types creation. Enter Changeling\u2019s and Deviant\u2019s at your own risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T06:36:19-08:00","id":1469094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469091#post1469091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how little impact they would have anyway due to their low numbers, what would effectively change in the game if all splats had still Oneiroi and impact on the Temenos? And what would that imply?</div> </div> </div> </div>It creates a lopsided power dynamic where the splats with innate ability to access the Astral can poke around in the minds of monsters and steer their cultures through Temenotic meddling and the others can't; the headcount needed to add a shared idea to the Temenos is <i>two</i>, and smaller groups are easier to influence through actions in the Temenos.<br /> <br /> By the same token, the ability to create metaphorical solutions (however temporary) to mental and emotional issues in the Oneiros would either shortcut past many of the problems various splats deal with or necessitate hard-coding the ways mystically-backed traumas were resistant to such handling; if access to the Astral isn't limited to the splats that already have it, then the question also arises of whether non-mages use the same (mostly geographical) methods to meditate into their Oneiros or something more particular to their nature, either of which can tilt the focus of How Well-Adjusted/Influential Characters Are Placed re: local resource allocation.<br /> <br /> It'd be an interesting setting hack either way, to be sure, but Mage and Beast occupy the particular niche where self-reflection and mass social influence through metaphor-space are appropriate compared to the more personal and on-the-ground approaches everyone else is stuck with in the setting as-written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T08:27:14-08:00","id":1469098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469088#post1469088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is that specified?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not explicitly stated, but the differences between human and Awakened souls are numerous enough that I think it should be given:<br /> There's two different spells for removing human and Awakened souls. A soulless mage gaining a human soul as replacement recovers much slower than if it was an Awakened soul. The &quot;health&quot; of human souls are measured by Integrity, while mages have Wisdom instead.<br /> Tremere from Nameless &amp; Accursed gives additional examples: Only Awakened souls can be used as payment during the Hollowing. A second Awakened soul has to be consumed to finalise the Hollowing. Awakened souls grants vastly more sustenance than human souls for Tremere. And again, there's two different powers for removing human and Awakened souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T09:31:34-08:00","id":1469101,"title":"","content":"It's mostly a difference of ignorance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T09:48:44-08:00","id":1469105,"title":"","content":"What symbolism is associated with Azoth ? I imagine the divine fire has associations with Creation, Life, Change, Destruction and Transformation, but are there any others I have missed ? <br /> <br /> Its mentioned that everyone has Pyros and that its the fuel of Azoth, but does that mean only living beings or only beings with souls? If a Reaper were to feed souls to it, would the Promethean gain a temporary boost due to having a fuel it could burn through more slowly/efficiently?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T10:50:40-08:00","id":1469107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469105#post1469105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What symbolism is associated with Azoth ? I imagine the divine fire has associations with Creation, Life, Change, Destruction and Transformation, but are there any others I have missed ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle, Pyros can be used as a Yantra for spells symbolically resonant with change, transformation, alchemy, or causality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its mentioned that everyone has Pyros and that its the fuel of Azoth, </div> </div> </div>Where? Every <i>Promethean</i> has Pyros, generated <i>by</i> their Azoth, which is the palpable form of the Divine Fire condensed by Promethean creation rituals, but Pyros as an energy is spread thin just about everywhere \u2014 sleeping in proximity to their resonant element and existing when the sun rises generate Pyros just as readily as spending time around humans (or, for sublimati, eating human flesh in place of Promethean flesh).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Reaper were to feed souls to it, would the Promethean gain a temporary boost due to having a fuel it could burn through more slowly/efficiently? </div> </div> </div>Prometheans don't eat Pyros (they eat food, however broadened their palate may be for defining that term) and their Azoth is not powered by souls, so no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T22:06:20-08:00","id":1469146,"title":"","content":"I found a post from Dave B. that says that Acts of Hubris can be mundane action. Most of the list of Acts of Hubris can easily be considered mundane, the only of which would be soul stone creation (but self mutilation is mundane as well), using magic in front of sleepers, and using magic instead of mundane action. Wouldn't Legacy Attainments rules of &quot;using Legacy Attainments do not provoke Acts of Hubris&quot;, wouldn't this just mean that using magic in front of sleepers or if you were enlightened would be the only thing stopped by the Legacy Attainment?<br /> <br /> Is there a more in depth look at Act of Hubris, Wisdom, Inurement, and Legacy Attainments that isn't fragmented lines in different parts of different books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T09:33:53-08:00","id":1469178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469146#post1469146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Legacy Attainments rules of &amp;quot;using Legacy Attainments do not provoke Acts of Hubris&amp;quot;, wouldn't this just mean that using magic in front of sleepers or if you were enlightened would be the only thing stopped by the Legacy Attainment?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so by the explanation given in the Legacy section of how it works. Acts of Hubris are based on inadequacies in awareness and responsibility, Attainments are based in a deep integration of the power's meaning into oneself.<br /> <br /> You can be accused of using an Attainment to do something terrible, but not of being unaware of what you're doing, and that's the thing that matters for Wisdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>House</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a more in depth look at Act of Hubris, Wisdom, Inurement, and Legacy Attainments that isn't fragmented lines in different parts of different books?</div> </div> </div> </div>The most dedicated look at Wisdom would be in Tome of the Mysteries, although that would be a little out-of-date now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T17:26:00-08:00","id":1469282,"title":"","content":"Been a while since I asked a bunch of odd questions. Today is space themed.<br /> 1) Can a Weaving of Death and Matter make a vacuum breathable? Or edible?<br /> 2) If I\u2019m moving near the speed of light, and use Forces to move faster than the speed of light, do I start to go back in time?<br /> 3) What\u2019s the best way reduce the mental fatigue of the long journeys between the stars? (Opinion is fine)<br /> 4) If I wanted to make a starship out of imbued items, and maybe a building or three, what would the various Orders think about it?<br /> 5) How weird is \u201cExplore the Universe!\u201d as a obsession considered in game?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T19:37:42-08:00","id":1469283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469282#post1469282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Can a Weaving of Death and Matter make a vacuum breathable? Or edible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think even in terms of the Supernal, an absence of anything is not itself a thing, so in vaccum you have nothing to target.<br /> <br /> I think a Weaving of Death could make yourself sufficiently undead to not require breathing, and Matter might aid in retaining and recycling air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) If I\u2019m moving near the speed of light, and use Forces to move faster than the speed of light, do I start to go back in time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the principles of it as a spell would override direct physical implications. The symbols would be concerned only with going faster.<br /> <br /> It would be like how increasing regular speed with Forces is not concerned with exerting pressure on your own body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) What\u2019s the best way reduce the mental fatigue of the long journeys between the stars? (Opinion is fine)</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably Perfecting of Mind, although perhaps inadvisable to become dependent on it; that kind of thing can make you Rapt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) If I wanted to make a starship out of imbued items, and maybe a building or three, what would the various Orders think about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Pentacle, a strange eccentricity, and likely unacceptable to use community resources, but otherwise you do you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) How weird is \u201cExplore the Universe!\u201d as a obsession considered in game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say many would look a bit askance at something so directed away from bigger concerns of their culture, and a bit of a waste to pursue something without guaranteed returns, but the Awakened are free to follow such wishes.<br /> <br /> Might be encouraged to try the less extreme route of traveling the Sidereal Wastes in the Astral.<br /> <br /> (Mind, the easiest way to journey through space is to seperate yourself from the flow of time with conditional duration to return when you encounter something.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T20:48:21-08:00","id":1469285,"title":"","content":"Thank you for responding!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469283#post1469283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think even in terms of the Supernal, an absence of anything is not itself a thing, so in vaccum you have nothing to target.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm. Wasn\u2019t there a thought experiment on these forums where someone created a \u201cNull\u201d, or a thing that was no thing? Maybe similar principles apply? Possibly a bit of a stretch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469283#post1469283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Weaving of Death could make yourself sufficiently undead to not require breathing, and Matter might aid in retaining and recycling air.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think Death or Matter is essential for this project. Life might be able to suffice for food and water, but that\u2019s more long term spells that risk Rapture, and I\u2019m pretty sure Life can\u2019t make you immune to breathing. At least, I\u2019m unaware of any creature that doesn\u2019t require the intake of something as breathe like. (Not a Biologist, if there is one, my bad) With the risk of Rapture, I think Matter actually edges out the other options. I don\u2019t think bringing a refreshing air bubble with you will risk you going Rapt, and you can always make something food like from the air. With some Death you can make food from your own Shadow, which is nice. Or I guess food from Light with Forces.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469283#post1469283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the principles of it as a spell would override direct physical implications. The symbols would be concerned only with going faster.<br /> <br /> It would be like how increasing regular speed with Forces is not concerned with exerting pressure on your own body.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469283#post1469283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably Perfecting of Mind, although perhaps inadvisable to become dependent on it; that kind of thing can make you Rapt.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I\u2019m pretty sure any option for this is risking Rapture. Maybe some Time manipulation can help.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469283#post1469283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Pentacle, a strange eccentricity, and likely unacceptable to use community resources, but otherwise you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u201cBut think of the Mysteries we could find, think of the Yantras!\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469283#post1469283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say many would look a bit askance at something so directed away from bigger concerns of their culture, and a bit of a waste to pursue something without guaranteed returns, but the Awakened are free to follow such wishes.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can see the effective abandonment of society being a bit of a problem for most of the Orders. Hmm, maybe the Mysterium might appreciate what a Mage is trying to do by traveling and exploring space?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469283#post1469283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be encouraged to try the less extreme route of traveling the Sidereal Wastes in the Astral.<br /> <br /> (Mind, the easiest way to journey through space is to seperate yourself from the flow of time with conditional duration to return when you encounter something.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we just take a moment to appreciate these sentiments? It\u2019s just so Mage. Yeah, it\u2019s more socially acceptable and safer to go explore the collective soul of the universe than try and physically go through space. And the best way to travel is to remove yourself from Time. I love this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T03:53:19-08:00","id":1469302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469285#post1469285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm. Wasn\u2019t there a thought experiment on these forums where someone created a \u201cNull\u201d, or a thing that was no thing? Maybe similar principles apply? Possibly a bit of a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't know myself, I was out of the loop for the first few years of Second Edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Death or Matter is essential for this project. Life might be able to suffice for food and water, but that\u2019s more long term spells that risk Rapture, and I\u2019m pretty sure Life can\u2019t make you immune to breathing. At least, I\u2019m unaware of any creature that doesn\u2019t require the intake of something as breathe like. (Not a Biologist, if there is one, my bad)</div> </div> </div> </div>All organisms need respiration, but there are forms of it that don't require oxygen or carbon dioxide (mostly done by microorganisms). Still needs something like nitrates or sulfates, though.<br /> <br /> I think Life could dramatically lower one's requirements, but not totally eliminate them, yeah. At least not before archmastery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Matter actually edges out the other options. I don\u2019t think bringing a refreshing air bubble with you will risk you going Rapt, and you can always make something food like from the air. With some Death you can make food from your own Shadow, which is nice. Or I guess food from Light with Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well converting things that are not food into food is going to require Patterning, although that leads back to my thought that imbibing something that has been transformed can be a dubious proposition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u201cBut think of the Mysteries we could find, think of the Yantras!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say there's a question of the &quot;we&quot; there, if many expect the trip to be one-way (at least as far as those left behind are around for).<br /> <br /> It depends on how one wants to handle the subject of Space magic to instantly return from trips far beyond the Earth. I'm thinking about the Dark Eras Mysteries where it was hard enough to teleport away from Caribbean desert islands or across the continental US to think that being so far removed comes with its own obstacles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can see the effective abandonment of society being a bit of a problem for most of the Orders. Hmm, maybe the Mysterium might appreciate what a Mage is trying to do by traveling and exploring space?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Mysterium would be concerned but accepting if a Sophiad led beyond the Earth, Arrow would acknowledge somebody seeking the challenge, Ladder and Council could make a case for staking a claim for humanity and even Guardians could have an interest in what the Lie and Abyss are like far removed from humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we just take a moment to appreciate these sentiments? It\u2019s just so Mage. Yeah, it\u2019s more socially acceptable and safer to go explore the collective soul of the universe than try and physically go through space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quicker too. You can spend subjective centuries crossing the Astral reflection of deep space (generally agreed to mirror the real thing) while only days pass in the waking world.<br /> <br /> Although perhaps more accessible than safe; you're constantly bombarded with Ecstatic Winds like that, unless some greater power protects you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And the best way to travel is to remove yourself from Time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I often think about implications of that spell being made indefinite. I picture a scenario where mages exploring some Roman catacomb come across a temporal distortion and dispel it, and before them materialises a young woman speaking Latin whom an ancient mage maliciously sealed from time for rejecting his advances. The cabal who found her had to balance between the desire to get her first hand accounts of everything and gently help her adjust to the experience.<br /> <br /> Sleepwalker, to keep things a bit simpler. Probably already associated with and a bit knowing about mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T04:56:00-08:00","id":1469306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469282#post1469282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) If I\u2019m moving near the speed of light, and use Forces to move faster than the speed of light, do I start to go back in time?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell doesn't wave off physics, yes.<br /> <br /> But you also collapse into a black hole in the process. A fairly massive one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T08:12:50-08:00","id":1469316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469302#post1469302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't know myself, I was out of the loop for the first few years of Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you are interested, I found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1373121#post1373121\">what</a> I was talking about. It\u2019s a bit less than I thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469302#post1469302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All organisms need respiration, but there are forms of it that don't require oxygen or carbon dioxide (mostly done by microorganisms). Still needs something like nitrates or sulfates, though.<br /> <br /> I think Life could dramatically lower one's requirements, but not totally eliminate them, yeah. At least not before archmastery.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s disappointing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469302#post1469302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well converting things that are not food into food is going to require Patterning, although that leads back to my thought that imbibing something that has been transformed can be a dubious proposition.</div> </div> </div> </div> This probably going to restart this debate again, but I\u2019m not sure I see the problem? The effects of food seem Lasting. Maybe it does create some new material, but not much. Otherwise spells like Lodestone wouldn\u2019t work because they require the creation of Force. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469302#post1469302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say there's a question of the &quot;we&quot; there, if many expect the trip to be one-way (at least as far as those left behind are around for).</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s what Space is for!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469302#post1469302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on how one wants to handle the subject of Space magic to instantly return from trips far beyond the Earth. I'm thinking about the Dark Eras Mysteries where it was hard enough to teleport away from Caribbean desert islands or across the continental US to think that being so far removed comes with its own obstacles.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, right. If there every was going to be a problem with Space, the vast distance and difference in environment will make one. That\u2019s unfortunate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469302#post1469302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Mysterium would be concerned but accepting if a Sophiad led beyond the Earth, Arrow would acknowledge somebody seeking the challenge, Ladder and Council could make a case for staking a claim for humanity and even Guardians could have an interest in what the Lie and Abyss are like far removed from humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m sorry for the Guardians, but I don\u2019t think the experiment will ever have conditions without humans. Even without that shard of the abyss, Mages still churn the waters so to speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469302#post1469302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quicker too. You can spend subjective centuries crossing the Astral reflection of deep space (generally agreed to mirror the real thing) while only days pass in the waking world.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, that\u2019s the thing though. Does it mirror the Fallen World? How would you ever know, without going to see for yourself? Now the time saving aspect of the Astral is a major point in it\u2019s favor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469302#post1469302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although perhaps more accessible than safe; you're constantly bombarded with Ecstatic Winds like that, unless some greater power protects you.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019d say it\u2019s safer, even if you die, you come back to you body with some spiritual damage. Some major damage if killed by the winds, but still healable. The same is not true of the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469302#post1469302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often think about implications of that spell being made indefinite. I picture a scenario where mages exploring some Roman catacomb come across a temporal distortion and dispel it, and before them materialises a young woman speaking Latin whom an ancient mage maliciously sealed from time for rejecting his advances. The cabal who found her had to balance between the desire to get her first hand accounts of everything and gently help her adjust to the experience.<br /> <br /> Sleepwalker, to keep things a bit simpler. Probably already associated with and a bit knowing about mages.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wow. I severely dislike that ancient mage now, and I\u2019m not even playing. Good scenario!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469306#post1469306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the spell doesn't wave off physics, yes.<br /> <br /> But you also collapse into a black hole in the process. A fairly massive one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um do you mind explaining this a bit further? I think you are referring to the length part of Special Relativity, correct? Isn\u2019t that an only observable from another rest frame? And isn\u2019t actually something the moving object experiences on its frame of reference? And wouldn\u2019t any object moving that faster than the speed of light have a negative length, whatever that means for the Universe? And I\u2019m not sure how massive such a black hole would be since the spell isn\u2019t adding mass. It\u2019d be just me and my ship\u2019s mass with a impossible density.<br /> <br /> Though all of this is more of a argument towards physics not working with the spell, much like those Time spells avoid paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T14:11:56-08:00","id":1469356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469316#post1469316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um do you mind explaining this a bit further? I think you are referring to the length part of Special Relativity, correct? Isn\u2019t that an only observable from another rest frame? And isn\u2019t actually something the moving object experiences on its frame of reference? And wouldn\u2019t any object moving that faster than the speed of light have a negative length, whatever that means for the Universe? And I\u2019m not sure how massive such a black hole would be since the spell isn\u2019t adding mass. It\u2019d be just me and my ship\u2019s mass with a impossible density.<br /> <br /> Though all of this is more of a argument towards physics not working with the spell, much like those Time spells avoid paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> is handling the rest very well.<br /> <br /> Two main effects happen at such speed. First, the length part isn't just a 'frame of reference' thing in this sense. It's real. That's what so weird about it, given how space and time bend it is completely real despite not being seen by the object itself. That alone is enough to turn you into a Black Hole because the key <b>is</b> density, and you're into a process, before achieving faster-than-light speed you'll reach near-light and light speed. So you'll have an infinite density at some point, which is the definition of a singularity.<br /> <br /> In other words, if you don't turn into a Black Hole because of the increasing density (which should happen), you become a Black Hole by definition when reaching light speed. It wouldn't make you supermassive, though.<br /> <br /> But there's the equivalence between energy and mass. You <b>are </b>adding mass to yourself because <u>energy has mass</u>. In a demonstration in another thread I calculated some situations, the Krakatoa's eruption in the 19th century released so much energy that the <b>energy itself</b> of the eruption weighted about 5.5 Kg.<br /> <br /> Energy has mass and it behaves as normal. It has momentum, inertia and gravity. That's why you can't actually reach the speed of light: the faster you are, the more mass you have due to all that kinetic energy, and so the more energy must be added to accelerate you the same amount again, building up to infinity. Reaching the speed of light would require infinite energy, getting too close to it would require the entire energy output of the universe.<br /> <br /> And that weighs. <b>That's</b> what would make you supermassive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T14:32:14-08:00","id":1469360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469356#post1469356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> is handling the rest very well.<br /> <br /> Two main effects happen at such speed. First, the length part isn't just a 'frame of reference' thing in this sense. It's real. That's what so weird about it, given how space and time bend it is completely real despite not being seen by the object itself. That alone is enough to turn you into a Black Hole because the key <b>is</b> density, and you're into a process, before achieving faster-than-light speed you'll reach near-light and light speed. So you'll have an infinite density at some point, which is the definition of a singularity.<br /> <br /> In other words, if you don't turn into a Black Hole because of the increasing density (which should happen), you become a Black Hole by definition when reaching light speed. It wouldn't make you supermassive, though.<br /> <br /> But there's the equivalence between energy and mass. You <b>are </b>adding mass to yourself because <u>energy has mass</u>. In a demonstration in another thread I calculated some situations, the Krakatoa's eruption in the 19th century released so much energy that the <b>energy itself</b> of the eruption weighted about 5.5 Kg.<br /> <br /> Energy has mass and it behaves as normal. It has momentum, inertia and gravity. That's why you can't actually reach the speed of light: the faster you are, the more mass you have due to all that kinetic energy, and so the more energy must be added to accelerate you the same amount again, building up to infinity. Reaching the speed of light would require infinite energy, getting too close to it would require the entire energy output of the universe.<br /> <br /> And that weighs. <b>That's</b> what would make you supermassive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I had forgotten. Thank you. This was a very clear and detailed answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T06:01:26-08:00","id":1469393,"title":"","content":"With how SoS introduced the idea of applying an imbued item into a creature instead of an item and how that creature if it possesses essance it may sound that essance in place of mana to fuel the imbued effect, would it be too much of a stretch to allow that to apply to other &quot;fuel stats&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T06:20:27-08:00","id":1469395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469393#post1469393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With how SoS introduced the idea of applying an imbued item into a creature instead of an item and how that creature if it possesses essance it may sound that essance in place of mana to fuel the imbued effect, would it be too much of a stretch to allow that to apply to other &amp;quot;fuel stats&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna have to reread the relevant parts, but\u2026 Both Essence and Mana are shaped by Resonance and thus \u2018close enough\u2019 for niche uses, I suspect the internal logic goes. Not so sure if the other fuels can be explained away that way. Maybe with a Merit or two, or some weird irregular trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T06:24:00-08:00","id":1469396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469395#post1469395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gonna have to reread the relevant parts, but\u2026 Both Essence and Mana are shaped by Resonance and thus \u2018close enough\u2019 for niche uses, I suspect the internal logic goes. Not so sure if the other fuels can be explained away that way. Maybe with a Merit or two, or some weird irregular trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bet with relevant Arcanum, you can modify the process, so you don\u2019t need those things. Certain fuels are cheaper than others, so maybe a exchange rate might be warranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T07:36:34-08:00","id":1469398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469396#post1469396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet with relevant Arcanum, you can modify the process, so you don\u2019t need those things. Certain fuels are cheaper than others, so maybe a exchange rate might be warranted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely fair. In part I consider it because it isnt like they'll waste the word count on every possible fuel stat when in most common situations in a mage game essence will be the main non mana fuel, baring crossover ofc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T08:26:41-08:00","id":1469401,"title":"","content":"Looking over how things are actually written, I'd just straight up go &quot;if you manage to Imbue a spell into a vampire, they can spend Vitae to activate it&quot;. <br /> <br /> The &quot;if&quot; there is dependent on an appropriate Weaving spell the same way as imbuing into any other subject than an item is, but I'd keep it simple. I think that in most cases supernatural energies are not transferable, but if you've got something set in place like an empowered item then I'd go with a logic that there's a channel ready to accommodate things.<br /> <br /> I'm not just looking at the stuff in Signs of Sorcery there, I'm also considering how the Prime 1 spell to directly activate magical items lets you include one dot from any other suitable Arcanum to activate other items as well, and spend Mana in lieu of their usual costs. I'm not sure if there are ever items that would be fuelled by Vitae, but if there are any Initiate of Prime and Death could use them with substituted Mana, so I'd accept it going both ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T16:15:57-08:00","id":1469430,"title":"","content":"Umm. Random thought time but, but what does someone\u2019s astral form look like if they have Multiple Personality Disorder or Dissociative Identity Disorder? Is it based on the current personality or are they both (or more) represented at the same time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T17:30:37-08:00","id":1469443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469430#post1469430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm. Random thought time but, but what does someone\u2019s astral form look like if they have Multiple Personality Disorder or Dissociative Identity Disorder? Is it based on the current personality or are they both (or more) represented at the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably depends on the person's relationship with their own condition. I'd recommend looking for blogs and vlogs of people with the condition before asserting on an answer.<br /> <br /> On my own searches I heard and read good things about the self advocates <b>MultiplicityAndMe</b>, <b>Entropy System</b>, <b>DissociaDID</b> and <b>Team Pi\u00f1ata</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T17:41:17-08:00","id":1469446,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, all of that talk about Perfecting something moving at relativistic speeds made me consider that casting a Potency 3 spell (i.e. the default since that's the primary factor) can make a propeller aircraft about as fast as the X-15.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T19:46:07-08:00","id":1469461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469443#post1469443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On my own searches I heard and read good things about the self advocates <b>MultiplicityAndMe</b>, <b>Entropy System</b>, <b>DissociaDID</b> and <b>Team Pi\u00f1ata</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for sharing!<br /> *reads the <b>MultiplicityAndMe </b>blog, particularly the parts about getting fired and getting unpleasant messages from strangers and not-strangers* Well, now I am sad. I guess I forget how awful people can be sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T18:19:34-08:00","id":1469546,"title":"","content":"New questions: <br /> 1)Is damage done to a living creature under Deaths purview? <br /> 1.5)Can I move the damaged area, like changing Leg Wrack to Arm Wrack?<br /> 2)If I have damage to my pattern, would it be possible to transfer that damage to someone or something else, effectively healing the damage? Kinda like transferring charges between batteries, if damage was charge. <br /> 2.5)Can I do that with just Death?<br /> 3)Can I transfer momentum between two subjects?<br /> 4)Can I redirect my rotational velocity around the sun, or galaxy as a means to gain a rather high velocity quickly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T21:13:16-08:00","id":1469552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469546#post1469546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New questions: <br /> 1)Is damage done to a living creature under Deaths purview? <br /> 1.5)Can I move the damaged area, like changing Leg Wrack to Arm Wrack?<br /> 2)If I have damage to my pattern, would it be possible to transfer that damage to someone or something else, effectively healing the damage? Kinda like transferring charges between batteries, if damage was charge. <br /> 2.5)Can I do that with just Death?<br /> 3)Can I transfer momentum between two subjects?<br /> 4)Can I redirect my rotational velocity around the sun, or galaxy as a means to gain a rather high velocity quickly?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yep, entropy and endings are within its purview <br /> 1.5) It would probably require a Reach, but the Condition would end when with the duration does<br /> 2) You can with a Weaving of Death<br /> 2.5) Yes, by transfering Potency damage to the target, withstood by Stamina. You can arguably do it with Weaving of Life as well, or transfer the lastest Potency turns of damage via Time's purview of change (resisted by Composure)<br /> 3 &amp; 4) I feel like it would be a Weaving of Forces with Potency determing how much, but not sure how that translates mechanically. I also feel you are thinking of replicating some of the abilities of Accelerator from Index.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-04-2021, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T21:56:11-08:00","id":1469556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469546#post1469546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4)Can I redirect my rotational velocity around the sun, or galaxy as a means to gain a rather high velocity quickly?</div> </div> </div> </div>This would probably change your referential for movement, since you would be targeting your speed in relation to something else than the ground. That means you would have to also calculate the resulting movement in relation to the same reference.<br /> <br /> It would be pretty unpredictable, and would only work towards a distinct direction than the one you're already moving, but for space travel could give you a pretty decent starting point for a motion away from the sun/quasar. For moving around them, though, it would just keep you in stationary orbit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T22:11:25-08:00","id":1469557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469552#post1469552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Yep, entropy and endings are within its purview<br /> 1.5) It would probably require a Reach, but the Condition would end when with the duration does<br /> 2) You can with a Weaving of Death<br /> 2.5) Yes, by transfering Potency damage to the target, withstood by Stamina. You can arguably do it with Weaving of Life as well,</div> </div> </div> </div> Yay, I though it was fine, but sometimes I just feel like double checking. I don\u2019t know why but vampiric healing necromancy seemed like it should be a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469552#post1469552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or transfer the lastest Potency turns of damage via Time's purview of change (resisted by Composure)</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait\u2026What? Time can do that?\u2026Wow. I guess I never thought about transferring causality of events before with Time. Time is way broader than I thought. (Granted, Time is my second worst Arcanum in comprehension)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469552#post1469552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 &amp; 4) I feel like it would be a Weaving of Forces with Potency determing how much, but not sure how that translates mechanically. I also feel you are thinking of replicating some of the abilities of Accelerator from Index.</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably. I mean, that\u2019s pretty much how I think I would use Forces in game, Force, Light, and Gravity are my favorite Forces. I\u2019d also use Forces veiling to block light pollution whenever I wanted to see stars. I\u2019m trying to plan on how to in game make it to Alpha Centauri (and not take 400 years). <br /> (Side question: it has been forever since I watched \u201cA Certain Magical Index\u201d. I think I stopped fairly early on, I remember being annoyed by the amnesia drama and the fan service\u2026did it ever get any better after that?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T22:34:17-08:00","id":1469558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469556#post1469556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would probably change your referential for movement, since you would be targeting your speed in relation to something else than the ground. That means you would have to also calculate the resulting movement in relation to the same reference.<br /> <br /> It would be pretty unpredictable, and would only work towards a distinct direction than the one you're already moving, but for space travel could give you a pretty decent starting point for a motion away from the sun/quasar. For moving around them, though, it would just keep you in stationary orbit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I\u2019m *really* not thrilled to use these because they really complicates matters, but at the same time, they were the most effective of my apparent options for interplanetary and interstellar travel. Honestly seems especially easy to screw up, and that would be extremely bad with this amount power. That said, a perfectly stationary orbit could be useful somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T06:14:20-08:00","id":1469572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469558#post1469558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, I\u2019m *really* not thrilled to use these because they really complicates matters, but at the same time, they were the most effective of my apparent options for interplanetary and interstellar travel. Honestly seems especially easy to screw up, and that would be extremely bad with this amount power. That said, a perfectly stationary orbit could be useful somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your purpose <b>is</b> rocket science. Which actually gives you an advantage.<br /> <br /> Your character will probably screw up if they try it on intuition alone, but we do have the science and calculations for that kind of stuff. You can probably use mundane but specialized skills and computers to figure out moment and local of departure and a route to achieve your goal.<br /> <br /> From the two ideas you had, robbing momentum from another object will be the most efficient, since momentum is speed in relation to mass. So when you manage to rob momentum from a heavier object you'll accelerate more than that object, while redirecting your own vector won't give you that much astronomically speaking. Earth's orbit is still too slow for interstellar travel, slower actually than our current space crafts (otherwise they wouldn't manage to reach anywhere).<br /> <br /> Gravitational slings are a thing to consider, too, and you can manipulate them with Forces. Also, remember that once in space you won't have friction robbing you of speed, so any increase in speed during the trip is permanent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T07:12:58-08:00","id":1469576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469557#post1469557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yay, I though it was fine, but sometimes I just feel like double checking. I don\u2019t know why but vampiric healing necromancy seemed like it should be a thing.<br /> <br /> Wait\u2026What? Time can do that?\u2026Wow. I guess I never thought about transferring causality of events before with Time. Time is way broader than I thought. (Granted, Time is my second worst Arcanum in comprehension)<br /> <br /> Probably. I mean, that\u2019s pretty much how I think I would use Forces in game, Force, Light, and Gravity are my favorite Forces. I\u2019d also use Forces veiling to block light pollution whenever I wanted to see stars. I\u2019m trying to plan on how to in game make it to Alpha Centauri (and not take 400 years).<br /> (Side question: it has been forever since I watched \u201cA Certain Magical Index\u201d. I think I stopped fairly early on, I remember being annoyed by the amnesia drama and the fan service\u2026did it ever get any better after that?)</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ironically, Forces is the Arcanum I have the most trouble with by a wide margin, whereas Time and Fate are the most intuitive. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time is how we frame reality. So you could <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1430312#post1430312\">use a Weaving (same principle as Shifting Sands) to rewrite who received a change</a>. The chair across the room received the damage from the attack, not you. The Seer didn't persuade his werewolf ally out of a frenzy, but was talking to the the potted plant in the corner. Weave the conditions to interact with objects in the timeline and you get <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1441659#post1441659\">temporal phasing</a>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even Veiling can have multiple angles. Used broadly on your entire past can make you Anonymous or Untouchable by mundane investigations. Creating disposable and airtight Alternative Identities is also simple. Veil yourself entirely from being detected in the present and you make Temporal Invisibility. Alternatively, capture Potency turns of actions and falsify your present self with a realistic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1318502#post1318502\">looping temporal echo</a> to make an Acanthus Alibi. You can also make people think its a specific time of day in order to control guard shifts or use a Ruling so they loop their actions, making them think its the first time they did something and they see things as they were when they did it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Patterning, you can mix Temporal Stutter with Fate's ability to read intentions to create a container that sends things to the future and retrieves exactly what you want (provided it fit in there), a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1408432#post1408432\">temporal bag of holding</a>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even Shielding is great, invert Veil of Moments to make sure all natural healing stops, no food is processed, no rest is sufficient and negative condition timers do not advance. A Ruling can make bleedout from lethal and aggravated damage happen in much smaller intervals, half per Potency level or a quarter for a Reach. Use a Weaving to put that into a bullet and foes fall from blood loss immediately after the first hit. Place a powerful version into a lunargent bullet and even a veteran werewolf will go splat in moments.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time is pretty great, to me the least explored part of its purview is <i>change</i>. Whereas for Fate the same is true for <i>intentions</i>, like Knowing a person's long term intentions (Aspirations and Obsessions) or Unveiling their current intentions (what do they want from this scene ? Do they intend to lie to me ?), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1404124#post1404124\">distorting </a>or even <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1420598#post1420598\">altering the details of their intentions</a> can be surprisingly helpful. I think its one of the reasons why a dedicated Acanthus can be disturbingly precise and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1333907#post1333907\">terrifying </a>when pushed.<br /> <br /> Index has gotten a lot better and the animation is still solid, I think its worth a watch, Regarding Alpha Centauri, so long as you have visual via telescope, satellite or the like, they are all valid targets for Co-Location. Alternatively, if you can find a place, time or Mystrery related to it, maybe there is a Emanation realm for it, which could lead to a shortcut to the real one. Its still an unexplored infinite dimension, but if anything, that is just more incentive for mages to poke around the unknown</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-04-2021, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T10:07:19-08:00","id":1469582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469572#post1469572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, your purpose <b>is</b> rocket science. Which actually gives you an advantage.<br /> <br /> Your character will probably screw up if they try it on intuition alone, but we do have the science and calculations for that kind of stuff. You can probably use mundane but specialized skills and computers to figure out moment and local of departure and a route to achieve your goal.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, any character I do this with will be way better at this than me, that\u2019s for sure. I just have my basic physics understanding, but it\u2019s fun to try to do this. I\u2019m leaning towards wanting Time 2 so I can do precise motions, and I can set up the majority of spells in advance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469572#post1469572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the two ideas you had, robbing momentum from another object will be the most efficient, since momentum is speed in relation to mass. So when you manage to rob momentum from a heavier object you'll accelerate more than that object, while redirecting your own vector won't give you that much astronomically speaking. Earth's orbit is still too slow for interstellar travel, slower actually than our current space crafts (otherwise they wouldn't manage to reach anywhere).</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, nothing says I just have to use only one type. Hmm I\u2019m going to have to do so more math to figure out exactly how much momentum I need, and it\u2019s relative amount compared to the Earth. Also I feel inexplicably guilty about stealing momentum from the Earth. I know this is pretty much how Gravitational slings work and they barely affect anything, but it still feels wrong somehow.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469572#post1469572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gravitational slings are a thing to consider, too, and you can manipulate them with Forces. Also, remember that once in space you won't have friction robbing you of speed, so any increase in speed during the trip is permanent.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very true. For Interstellar travel, I\u2019m probably going to need them to reach anything like the speed I want. That said, I\u2019m going to need to reduce my velocity somehow if I don\u2019t want to just skip right past whatever I want to explore. Hmm, I wonder if I can get a teapot in a stable orbit between Mars and Jupiter. That would be amusing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469576#post1469576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ironically, Forces is the Arcanum I have the most trouble with by a wide margin, whereas Time and Fate are the most intuitive. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s pretty awesome though, you totally have a Acanthus (Acanthian?) mindset. I\u2019m pretty close to a Orbimos mindset, Forces and Truth are my best, but my worst is Spirit. I just don\u2019t get Spirit ecologies. I have all the puzzle pieces, I just can\u2019t put them together. I really feel like you need to know a entire area, to a crazy level of detail before you can make the local Shadow. And without getting the context of the Shadow, I can\u2019t do Spirit very well.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469576#post1469576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time is how we frame reality. So you could <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1430312#post1430312\">use a Weaving (same principle as Shifting Sands) to rewrite who received a change</a>. The chair across the room received the damage from the attack, not you. The Seer didn't persuade his werewolf ally out of a frenzy, but was talking to the the potted plant in the corner. Weave the conditions to interact with objects in the timeline and you get <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1441659#post1441659\">temporal phasing</a>.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m going be honest, this makes my brain hurt.I think I understand how this works, especially since you explained it, but the concept of this really doesn\u2019t do good things to my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469576#post1469576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even Veiling can have multiple angles. Used broadly on your entire past can make you Anonymous or Untouchable by mundane investigations. Creating disposable and airtight Alternative Identities is also simple. Veil yourself entirely from being detected in the present and you make Temporal Invisibility. Alternatively, capture Potency turns of actions and falsify your present self with a realistic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1318502#post1318502\">looping temporal echo</a> to make an Acanthus Alibi. You can also make people think its a specific time of day in order to control guard shifts or use a Ruling so they loop their actions, making them think its the first time they did something and they see things as they were when they did it.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> Veiling is probably the best practice after Weaving, I can think of tons of thing you can do with Veiling from all the Arcanum. You can veil your past, and present? What about further Veiling your future so people can\u2019t know what you are planning? The Alibi is actually pretty cool. The Veiling of daytime is actually the only one on the list I\u2019ve thought of before. Now I had (very wrongly) considered that the limit of usefulness of Veiling Time. The loop is cool if you need to waste someone\u2019s time, useful in a fight too. Why is Forces everyone\u2019s go to combat Arcanum, Time seems way more combat oriented? In a fight, sheer brute force is nice, but precise timing is much better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469576#post1469576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Patterning, you can mix Temporal Stutter with Fate's ability to read intentions to create a container that sends things to the future and retrieves exactly what you want (provided it fit in there), a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1408432#post1408432\">temporal bag of holding</a>.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> *sound of my brain breaking, again* what? I guess that makes sense if I think about it, but how in the world did you think this up? The Free Council in my games is so going to be selling these now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469576#post1469576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even Shielding is great, invert Veil of Moments to make sure all natural healing stops, no food is processed, no rest is sufficient and negative condition timers do not advance. A Ruling can make bleedout from lethal and aggravated damage happen in much smaller intervals, half per Potency level or a quarter for a Reach. Use a Weaving to put that into a bullet and foes fall from blood loss immediately after the first hit. Place a powerful version into a lunargent bullet and even a veteran werewolf will go splat in moments.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> See above about Time being more combat focused than Forces? This is why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469576#post1469576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time is pretty great, to me the least explored part of its purview is <i>change</i>. Whereas for Fate the same is true for <i>intentions</i>, like Knowing a person's long term intentions (Aspirations and Obsessions) or Unveiling their current intentions (what do they want from this scene ? Do they intend to lie to me ?), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1404124#post1404124\">distorting </a>or even <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1420598#post1420598\">altering the details of their intentions</a> can be surprisingly helpful. I think its one of the reasons why a dedicated Acanthus can be disturbingly precise and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1333907#post1333907\">terrifying </a>when pushed.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Acanthus are the most terrifying Mages, and always have been in my opinion. Sure, Orbimos can just flat out kill you, and Moros can just outright kill you (or leave you permanently on the verge of death) and rip out your soul, and Thyrsus can make every living moment agony, and Mastigos can do worse than all the others and get you from your friends, but only Acanthus can get you at any time in your life. Have a perfect hidden pocket dimension? You weren\u2019t always in it. Stupid heavy ward? Had to cast it at some point. Going to heal all damage? They are just going either just speed up how much damage you take, or remove you from the timeline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469576#post1469576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Index has gotten a lot better and the animation is still solid, I think its worth a watch, Regarding Alpha Centauri, so long as you have visual via telescope, satellite or the like, they are all valid targets for Co-Location. Alternatively, if you can find a place, time or Mystrery related to it, maybe there is a Emanation realm for it, which could lead to a shortcut to the real one. Its still an unexplored infinite dimension, but if anything, that is just more incentive for mages to poke around the unknown</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span> All of these are good answers, but I have always imagined having to set up way points so others can teleport to whatever location I\u2019m going to. Hmm, the Emanation realm isn\u2019t a angle I had considered. I will think more on that. I\u2019m probably still going to try it the Obrimos way just to see how bad it is. (I will give Index another try)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T10:56:33-08:00","id":1469583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469582#post1469582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *sound of my brain breaking, again* what? I guess that makes sense if I think about it, but how in the world did you think this up? The Free Council in my games is so going to be selling these now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would advise taking Afini's suggestions with a grain of salt; they tend to be a bit power-creep-y vis-a-vis their assumptions of how the metaphysics work compared to published example spells.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also like to point out that the way the setting is described, you're going to need a pretty strong <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AnthropicPrinciple\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Principle</a> justifying travel outside the solar system in material reality as a Storyteller, because to all available evidence it's mostly empty space and barren landscapes as in real life, and other dimensions usually provide the requisite novelty or alien-ness for greater returns without having to go nearly as far afield.<br /> <br /> That is to say, if you're going to spend a significant portion of your game trying to get light-years away in objective time and space, you'd better have something to do there that's worth dedicating camera time and gameplay to, especially if there are other players for whom extrasolar exploration is not a focal activity nor something they have the means or motive to help you with.<br /> <br /> Obsessions relate specifically to mages' drive to explore the supernatural, and other sources of Arcane Beats are similarly magically-oriented \u2014 figuring out how to use magic to facilitate superluminal travel, searching for ruins of the Time Before on other planets, researching the planetary angels that occasionally make their way to the terrestrial Shadow from across the void, investigating the relationship between space and the Abyss, and so on are all going to keep a mage's enlightened attention, as might more particular and esoteric things, but just Trying To Go To Space isn't going to advance your Gnosis or strengthen your grasp of the Arcana.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say &quot;don't try to go to Alpha Centauri&quot; so much as &quot;bring it back to magic in some way and make sure the story can have a worthwhile payoff if this is more than a distant dream you're planning to end the chronicle on.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T11:10:02-08:00","id":1469584,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thank you, glad you liked them. A part of them come from thinking in how to do cool things from other Arcana in an Acanthus way. It leads to some terrifying possibilities, like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1430053#post1430053\">forcibly creating or adapting Dedicated Tools on the fly</a>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another one is to use Patterning so you don't suffer negative changes, at all. So apart from making indestructible Grimmoires and unbreakable Sanctum walls, the most terrifying thing is applying it on living subjects. Walking barefooted in a volcano, swimming in the lava and breathing in the toxic fumes ? Sure, no problem. Taking a walk through no man's land while being hit by cross fire and stepping on land mines ? Meh, not even a real challenge. Stepping between two angry dueling spirits and shouting them down ? All part of the job, how else will they understand that <i>The Silver Ladder is the path to victory </i> ? Essentially this is a variation of the Eternal Object spell from 1ed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Inspiration wise, I am currently in a homebrew D&amp;D campaign where our DM is mixing elements of Destiny, Dark Souls, Re:Zero and Genshin Impact with a lot of lore from all editions. Chronomancers and dunamancers are on top of mind, since they had a big impact in the backstory (the previous master chronomancer / greater god of time was basically Destiny's Clovis Bray mixed with FMA's Father). There is a reason 2ed chronomancy was considered insanely powerful and even the 5ed chronurgy is very strong. The Awakened can do a lot of those spells without archmastery. He is doing an incredible job, so I have time magic on top of mind, which inspired me to see what kind of original spells I could come up with. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But yeah, my ideas do tend to be power creepy, partially because I keep wondering how mages would push the limits of the Arcana and how to come up with new and interesting veins of them to explore.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As for useful resources, I highly recommend the lore of Destiny, especially about the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hhiFQkychEs\" target=\"_blank\">Vex</a>, their take on sci-fi time magic is brilliant. Byf is a great lore channel for that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I would particularly love to make the Vault of Glass and the Vex into a Wending of Prime/Truth, Space and Time. After all, its not just about &quot;fixing&quot; the Abyss, but doing so in such a way that the Exarch can't have free reign to send down unlimited resources (ochemata, Artifacts, etc) to complete their conquest. What happened to the archmage who created that ? Don't know, probably locked away somewhere. Some kind of Time and Space Legacy and some Artifacts would probably be linked to it, just so I could throw in a few elements of the Infinite Corridor from the Castlevania animated series.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-04-2021, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T12:40:44-08:00","id":1469586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469583#post1469583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like to point out that the way the setting is described, you're going to need a pretty strong <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AnthropicPrinciple\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Principle</a> justifying travel outside the solar system in material reality as a Storyteller, because to all available evidence it's mostly empty space and barren landscapes as in real life, and other dimensions usually provide the requisite novelty or alien-ness for greater returns without having to go nearly as far afield.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m fine with there being void. Personally I\u2019d love to examine the symbols of the Heliopause, and I\u2019m still really curious if one can manipulate near total void with Death. Frankly, there are tons a magical experiments one can do with complete void. Heck, maybe there are Hallows in the void. Granted the Mana those generate probably would in no way be safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469583#post1469583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is to say, if you're going to spend a significant portion of your game trying to get light-years away in objective time and space, you'd better have something to do there that's worth dedicating camera time and gameplay to, especially if there are other players for whom extrasolar exploration is not a focal activity nor something they have the means or motive to help you with.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even with a very generous estimation for how fast I can get a ship to go, I\u2019m probably looking at at least 40 year journey to the closest star system. That is a rather long time. The best way to deal this with seems to be a Colocation that adjusts ones relative velocity to match that of the other side. Which means I definitely will need a ship with life support for other to visit in. At worst it will be like a pocket dimension my Mage hangs out in too much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469583#post1469583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obsessions relate specifically to mages' drive to explore the supernatural, and other sources of Arcane Beats are similarly magically-oriented \u2014 figuring out how to use magic to facilitate superluminal travel, searching for ruins of the Time Before on other planets, researching the planetary angels that occasionally make their way to the terrestrial Shadow from across the void, investigating the relationship between space and the Abyss, and so on are all going to keep a mage's enlightened attention, as might more particular and esoteric things, but just Trying To Go To Space isn't going to advance your Gnosis or strengthen your grasp of the Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean, all this is very true. I guess I need to define the Obsession better then. There unlimited things to try and figure out in Physical Outer Space. Physical Outer Space in general seems to not be much of a concern for most Mages. And that makes it worth exploring on it\u2019s own. Who really knows what we might find. I mean, the Exarchs made probably want us to stay put on Earth, why not see what they don\u2019t want us to see?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469583#post1469583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which isn't to say &quot;don't try to go to Alpha Centauri&quot; so much as &quot;bring it back to magic in some way and make sure the story can have a worthwhile payoff if this is more than a distant dream you're planning to end the chronicle on.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair. If I\u2019m going to really devote chronical time to this, it seems interplanetary travel is my best bet for something that is both interesting to everyone and takes relatively little time. I think I can reasonably get that time down to about a month and a week round trip for Saturn, two weeks with a colocation back. That\u2019s reasonable for down time in a chronicle, right? Or a story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-04-2021, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T12:53:28-08:00","id":1469587,"title":"","content":"New question:<br /> I remember the long term nimbus itself being untouchable, but is it possible to weave other effects in addition to it, or have an effect spread like a long term nimbus? Or is it completely outside of a Mage\u2019s reach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-04-2021, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T13:37:16-08:00","id":1469589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469587#post1469587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question:<br /> I remember the long term nimbus itself being untouchable, but is it possible to weave other effects in addition to it, or have an effect spread like a long term nimbus? Or is it completely outside of a Mage\u2019s reach?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Long-Term Nimbus is a narrative convention for &quot;Path-appropriate supernatural phenomenon tend to be attracted to a mage's sympathetic connections based on their Wisdom and the maintenance of their Shadow Name. You can certainly have an effect target things a mage has a sympathetic connection to, but making effects that &quot;spread&quot; in general is the domain of Dynamics spells and thus limited to archmagic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469586#post1469586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I\u2019m fine with there being void. Personally I\u2019d love to examine the symbols of the Heliopause, and I\u2019m still really curious if one can manipulate near total void with Death. Frankly, there are tons a magical experiments one can do with complete void. Heck, maybe there are Hallows in the void. Granted the Mana those generate probably would in no way be safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious about what those experiments might be, but as mentioned, you're going to have to get to that point first, whether by having seen something in your Periphery in a photo or through a telescope or by being given a revelation during your Awakening; there's a reason one of the most evident long-term project-oriented mages is a type of barrow-lich that wakes up every few decades to do astronomy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even with a very generous estimation for how fast I can get a ship to go, I\u2019m probably looking at at least 40 year journey to the closest star system. That is a rather long time. The best way to deal this with seems to be a Colocation that adjusts ones relative velocity to match that of the other side. Which means I definitely will need a ship with life support for other to visit in. At worst it will be like a pocket dimension my Mage hangs out in too much. </div> </div> </div>Symbolically speaking, a place is a place, and &quot;matching relative velocity&quot; is more the sort of complication that arises from Paradox or poorly-placed boundaries. The inside of a moving vessel is still the inside of a vessel.<br /> <br /> More prosaically, this is getting into the matter of creating your character in a way that allows them to be involved with the rest of the cast and interact with whatever other plot comes their way; &quot;guy who wants to take a decades-long journey into the great unknown&quot; tends to be more interesting in the preparatory phase (that needs outside assistance or hard study in a related field) or as an NPC who's most of the way there already (e.g. a lich who's bound their soul to a soul-stone in transit and is leveraging old or borrowed sympathies to relay information back to their collaborators). It's important not to get too caught up in the abstract and wind up producing something that doesn't interact with the rest of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, all this is very true. I guess I need to define the Obsession better then. There unlimited things to try and figure out in Physical Outer Space. Physical Outer Space in general seems to not be much of a concern for most Mages. And that makes it worth exploring on it\u2019s own. Who really knows what we might find. I mean, the Exarchs made probably want us to stay put on Earth, why not see what they don\u2019t want us to see? </div> </div> </div>This seems to be committing the cardinal mistake of assuming the Exarchs are responsible for every inconvenience humans have ever encountered, when the more probable explanation is that most terrestrial life emerged and/or adapted on Earth and does not perform well in an exposed vacuum with no gravity.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the bigger reason not as many mages (at least among the published example characters) are concerned with Physical Outer Space is because its conditions can be replicated with existing spells and the space program is people-intensive in a way that presents something of an obstacle to overt meddling. You can find vacuum and zero-gravity in nature (and if not, <s>store-bought</s> magically-produced is fine), and the shortcuts similar things from the Abyss or the Depths can take make them less of a shot in the dark to access if there's anything out there to look at personally (instead of by grabbing samples and sympathetic connections from the space program or reachable mage-astronomers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fair. If I\u2019m going to really devote chronical time to this, it seems interplanetary travel is my best bet for something that is both interesting to everyone and takes relatively little time. I think I can reasonably get that time down to about a month and a week round trip for Saturn, two weeks with a colocation back. That\u2019s reasonable for down time in a chronicle, right? Or a story? </div> </div> </div>I think developing the magical and/or mundane expertise needed to survive most aspects of space travel and/or extraterrestrial exploration can get you a decent daisy-chain of Obsessions to build along for a game; lord knows you wouldn't have too much trouble fitting into the Arrow's ethos of self-refinement, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T15:36:01-08:00","id":1469594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469589#post1469589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Long-Term Nimbus is a narrative convention for &quot;Path-appropriate supernatural phenomenon tend to be attracted to a mage's sympathetic connections based on their Wisdom and the maintenance of their Shadow Name. You can certainly have an effect target things a mage has a sympathetic connection to, but making effects that &quot;spread&quot; in general is the domain of Dynamics spells and thus limited to archmagic.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u201cIs the domain of Dynamics\u201d, so very much out of reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469589#post1469589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about what those experiments might be, but as mentioned, you're going to have to get to that point first, whether by having seen something in your Periphery in a photo or through a telescope or by being given a revelation during your Awakening; there's a reason one of the most evident long-term project-oriented mages is a type of barrow-lich that wakes up every few decades to do astronomy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Alright let\u2019s see, off the top of my head: is void a symbol -&gt; is void a material like shadow is for death -&gt; does the interstellar medium count as void (there is technically stuff in it)-&gt; can there be perfected void -&gt; do patches of it exist in the interstellar medium or galactic voids like perfected metals do sometimes in ore -&gt; what occult properties does perfected void have<br /> Is there resonance in the void between stars -&gt; is it plentiful because there is a lot of void, or is it thin because it\u2019s void resonance -&gt; is it possible that ley lines run between stars -&gt; are these lines tainted by void resonance or perhaps defined by it. -&gt; can Hallows or Nodes form from intersections of these ley lines and ( if so what kind)<br /> Is the interstellar medium a potent yantra -&gt; is there a difference between the yantra some of the Star Dust by itself produces and that of both the void and the dust<br /> what prevents the teleportation by telescope.-&gt; Do the threads of Sympathy get eroded by the void-&gt;<br /> <br /> Stuff like that. I\u2019m sure if I spent more time I could come up with more.<br /> Actually being a barrow-lich isn\u2019t a bad idea, if I can\u2019t manage to get a higher top speed. Maybe even if I can. I\u2019d be leaving everyone behind, or maybe almost everyone. But it would let me go very far indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469589#post1469589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Symbolically speaking, a place is a place, and &quot;matching relative velocity&quot; is more the sort of complication that arises from Paradox or poorly-placed boundaries. The inside of a moving vessel is still the inside of a vessel.</div> </div> </div> </div> This makes sense. At least I don\u2019t have worry about it being complicated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469589#post1469589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More prosaically, this is getting into the matter of creating your character in a way that allows them to be involved with the rest of the cast and interact with whatever other plot comes their way; &quot;guy who wants to take a decades-long journey into the great unknown&quot; tends to be more interesting in the preparatory phase (that needs outside assistance or hard study in a related field) or as an NPC who's most of the way there already (e.g. a lich who's bound their soul to a soul-stone in transit and is leveraging old or borrowed sympathies to relay information back to their collaborators). It's important not to get too caught up in the abstract and wind up producing something that doesn't interact with the rest of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will remember this. If I ever get to play Mage as a player, I will keep this mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469589#post1469589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems to be committing the cardinal mistake of assuming the Exarchs are responsible for every inconvenience humans have ever encountered, when the more probable explanation is that most terrestrial life emerged and/or adapted on Earth and does not perform well in an exposed vacuum with no gravity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh, I was thinking about how populations are easier to control if they all are in relatively the same space. I don\u2019t doubt that the Exarchs probably didn\u2019t cause the void between stars to be so big, but I\u2019m betting they benefited or are benefiting from it. There is probably \u201ca stay at home\u201d ministry. Probably extremely minor, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469589#post1469589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think the bigger reason not as many mages (at least among the published example characters) are concerned with Physical Outer Space is because its conditions can be replicated with existing spells and the space program is people-intensive in a way that presents something of an obstacle to overt meddling. You can find vacuum and zero-gravity in nature (and if not, <s>store-bought</s> magically-produced is fine), and the shortcuts similar things from the Abyss or the Depths can take make them less of a shot in the dark to access if there's anything out there to look at personally (instead of by grabbing samples and sympathetic connections from the space program or reachable mage-astronomers).</div> </div> </div> </div> True, but to see how things are outside of controlled conditions requires going there. Plus, look how mystery packed Earth is. I\u2019m sure there is plenty of crazy stuff just out of sight, even in the sky.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469589#post1469589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think developing the magical and/or mundane expertise needed to survive most aspects of space travel and/or extraterrestrial exploration can get you a decent daisy-chain of Obsessions to build along for a game; lord knows you wouldn't have too much trouble fitting into the Arrow's ethos of self-refinement, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div> hmm, the Arrow? Honestly, didn\u2019t really think of myself that way. I do like self refinement, but I\u2019m a pacifist, and dislike physical confrontation. I\u2019ve always seen myself happy in between the Silver Ladder, the Mysterium, and the Free Council. I believe, everyone, even people I disagree with should have the chance to awaken, if they want. I\u2019m no leader, and some of my worst nightmares are me being in command, but I\u2019d support someone who I\u2019d think would do a good job. I\u2019d also like to just be able to pursue my Obsessions and bring back information for what ever order I was in. Still, wouldn\u2019t be the first time I failed to account for some aspect of myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T16:04:50-08:00","id":1469595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469594#post1469594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u201cIs the domain of Dynamics\u201d, so very much out of reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can visit one of the Aeons of the Arcana in the Anima Mundi to petition for Auctoritas (Signs of Sorcery). One possible form of Auctoritas is a +1 dot in the Aeon's Arcanum for one single spell. The +1 dot trumps Gnosis and Path limits... I assume this means a Master (5-dot) can cast a Dynamics (6-dot) spell once.<br /> <br /> I glossed over the science parts of magical astronautics, but the main problem I see here is Paradox. IIRC, a sidebar in Dark Eras 2 mentioned the ocean's vicissitudes forcing extra Reach on certain uses of Fate, Time, and Space magic. I wouldn't be surprised to see the yawning gap of the void of outer space forcing similar, if not worse, Reach restrictions on certain Forces, Space, Time spells. Not to mention possibly having to use Advanced Scale and Advanced Duration on top of those.<br /> <br /> But hey, summoned Supernal Entities have infinite Reach, and another form of the Auctoritas is casting one single spell of the Arcanum without Paradox no matter what...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> hmm, the Arrow? Honestly, didn\u2019t really think of myself that way. I do like self refinement, but I\u2019m a pacifist, and dislike physical confrontation. I\u2019ve always seen myself happy in between the Silver Ladder, the Mysterium, and the Free Council. I believe, everyone, even people I disagree with should have the chance to awaken, if they want. I\u2019m no leader, and some of my worst nightmares are me being in command, but I\u2019d support someone who I\u2019d think would do a good job. I\u2019d also like to just be able to pursue my Obsessions and bring back information for what ever order I was in. Still, wouldn\u2019t be the first time I failed to account for some aspect of myself. </div> </div> </div>You could go straight to the Vidanti within the Arrows. I don't remember much of their 1E form, but for 2E they were mentioned off-hand out-of-book as a Nameless Order inside the Arrow, reserved for people who can't follow their tenets any more. It's more like a retirement program, though, so I suspect the Arrow would still put you in a magical boot camp at the least. (Or whatever their initiation is; I really need to reread the 1E orderbooks...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T16:37:39-08:00","id":1469596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469595#post1469595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can visit one of the Aeons of the Arcana in the Anima Mundi to petition for Auctoritas (Signs of Sorcery). One possible form of Auctoritas is a +1 dot in the Aeon's Arcanum for one single spell. The +1 dot trumps Gnosis and Path limits... I assume this means a Master (5-dot) can cast a Dynamics (6-dot) spell once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I think there's an implicit or explicit premise that granting somebody access to Imperial spells with the Auctoritas does not automatically convey understanding of the Quintessence required to cast them.<br /> <br /> That being said, there are Artifacts that can cast Imperial spells, and I've never seen any suggestion that those would require Quintessence. If the pirate Nameless of Nassau could use an Artifact that shut down all Yantras based on authority within a certain area, I'd say somebody could acquire an Artifact with a power that spreads out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I glossed over the science parts of magical astronautics, but the main problem I see here is Paradox. IIRC, a sidebar in Dark Eras 2 mentioned the ocean's vicissitudes forcing extra Reach on certain uses of Fate, Time, and Space magic. I wouldn't be surprised to see the yawning gap of the void of outer space forcing similar, if not worse, Reach restrictions on certain Forces, Space, Time spells. Not to mention possibly having to use Advanced Scale and Advanced Duration on top of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I find myself wondering if the Mysteries about such travel in that book are supposed to persist into the modern day; if mages did not find some way to resolve them at some point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could go straight to the Vidanti within the Arrows. I don't remember much of their 1E form, but for 2E they were mentioned off-hand out-of-book as a Nameless Order inside the Arrow, reserved for people who can't follow their tenets any more. It's more like a retirement program, though</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think they're more like a kind of tradition within the Order's systems then a separate embedded Order.<br /> <br /> ...Although calling them a Nameless Order within sounds vaguely like the kind of thing DaveB would say... I'll look back into it.<br /> <br /> For the time being though, I'd say that with the Order as written, the Adamantine Arrow would simply not accept avowed pacifists into their ranks. I think the corebook line about being willing to look upon peace as a greater challenge to achieve means that they can make some allowances for people who are highly reserved about the use of violence or dedicate themselves to resolution of conflicts without it, and the Order book itself talks about many aspects of what they do that are not strictly to do with fighting (one that I find interesting is the Arrow as element in a Consilium deadlocked by an excess of intrigue that gets people back on task), but they reject people who specifically not only reject all use of violence but view it as a moral wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T16:42:11-08:00","id":1469597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469582#post1469582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I feel inexplicably guilty about stealing momentum from the Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Steal it from space debris, man-made or natural. Forget about Earth or the redirection of your own speed vector, this is too much work for too little pay-off.<br /> <br /> Instead, just use fuel and then steal momentum from space rocks. You're trying to come up with the most complex answer by doing it with magic alone.<br /> <br /> Rockets use tonnes of fuel because they need to accelerate tonnes of fuel. You can magic the energy out of the fuel and not carry the weight. Asteroids are relatively common and high speed, and the big ones will be so many times your weight, vessel included, and you can guilty-free steal all their momentum. Plan your trip to pass through a few select targets and that's it, 1.000 Km/h stolen from a rock 100 times your mass will give you 100.000 Km/h because we're magicking physics out of the equation.<br /> <br /> Stripping energy/mass equivalence and other bits out of the equation simplifies your predicament immensely, and you can simply throw your excess momentum somewhere else when you arrive at your destination. There's no reason to think the trip will take more than a year with magic at your disposal.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> is right that you need to think through how this whole idea plays a role on the story. Unless it is a solo game or a novel/fiction you're writing, in which case you can enter suspended animation and don't care about the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T16:59:39-08:00","id":1469598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469596#post1469596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although I think there's an implicit or explicit premise that granting somebody access to Imperial spells with the Auctoritas does not automatically convey understanding of the Quintessence required to cast them.<br /> <br /> That being said, there are Artifacts that can cast Imperial spells, and I've never seen any suggestion that those would require Quintessence. If the pirate Nameless of Nassau could use an Artifact that shut down all Yantras based on authority within a certain area, I'd say somebody could acquire an Artifact with a power that spreads out.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026. Oops. Yeah, Quintessence might be an issue. An Artifact does sound easier, though likely perceived as more random in-universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T17:20:06-08:00","id":1469600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469598#post1469598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026. Oops. Yeah, Quintessence might be an issue. An Artifact does sound easier, though likely perceived as more random in-universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember the main villain of <i>The Soul Cage</i> found a loophole by asking about the Quintessence to an archmaster. So if you can get the information somehow, it could work, maybe. It would be incredibly Hubristic and, being an Imperial practice and it would probably require a ton of work to setup: negotiating with the Aeon, talking to or seeking out the information from the Invisible Masters, finding or producing the right Quintecense, selecting the optimal ritual site and doing it all in such a subtle way that no one stops it. It could be an entire chronicle's worth of work, but its theoretically possible. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T17:21:07-08:00","id":1469601,"title":"","content":"Accidentally tapped post before I was ready<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469595#post1469595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can visit one of the Aeons of the Arcana in the Anima Mundi to petition for Auctoritas (Signs of Sorcery). One possible form of Auctoritas is a +1 dot in the Aeon's Arcanum for one single spell. The +1 dot trumps Gnosis and Path limits... I assume this means a Master (5-dot) can cast a Dynamics (6-dot) spell once.</div> </div> </div> </div> No. Not for this. The Aeons are in my mind, a very last resort. I\u2019d love to visit them sometime, and speak to their servants, and learn from them. But their bargains will cost more, much more than a Dynamics spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469595#post1469595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could go straight to the Vidanti within the Arrows. I don't remember much of their 1E form, but for 2E they were mentioned off-hand out-of-book as a Nameless Order inside the Arrow, reserved for people who can't follow their tenets any more. It's more like a retirement program, though, so I suspect the Arrow would still put you in a magical boot camp at the least. (Or whatever their initiation is; I really need to reread the 1E orderbooks...)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026 can you tell me of them? I don\u2019t have the Arrow book, and they don\u2019t seem in 2e yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-04-2021, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T17:52:03-08:00","id":1469605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469601#post1469601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Accidentally tapped post before I was ready<br /> No. Not for this. The Aeons are in my mind, a very last resort. I\u2019d love to visit them sometime, and speak to their servants, and learn from them. But their bargains will cost more, much more than a Dynamics spell.<br /> <br /> \u2026 can you tell me of them? I don\u2019t have the Arrow book, and they don\u2019t seem in 2e yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Vidantus (meaning &quot;those who are to be shunned&quot;) are Arrows that have forsworn all conflict and embraced pacifism. Becoming one involves a ritual of renunciation, but some Caucuses levy the status as punishment for cowardice. Henceforth, they are no longer members of the Arrow, will not join any other Order and will not work against the Pentacle in any way. They are not allowed, under any circumstances, to council other Arrows or persuade them to join the Vidantus. While its expected for Arrows to shun them, its not an absolute and receiving magical (or mundane) tutelage from them could be accepted. In short, they are generally Arrows who experienced such traumas that they developed a fundamental, irreconcilable philosophical break with the core doctrine of the Arrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-04-2021, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T18:42:48-08:00","id":1469609,"title":"","content":"This was going to be part of my previous post, but accidents happened.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469596#post1469596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I find myself wondering if the Mysteries about such travel in that book are supposed to persist into the modern day; if mages did not find some way to resolve them at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even if they resolved it on Earth, doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s resolved in Space. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if it was mentioned that these problems still persist in remote environments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469596#post1469596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think they're more like a kind of tradition within the Order's systems then a separate embedded Order.<br /> <br /> ...Although calling them a Nameless Order within sounds vaguely like the kind of thing DaveB would say... I'll look back into it.<br /> <br /> For the time being though, I'd say that with the Order as written, the Adamantine Arrow would simply not accept avowed pacifists into their ranks. I think the corebook line about being willing to look upon peace as a greater challenge to achieve means that they can make some allowances for people who are highly reserved about the use of violence or dedicate themselves to resolution of conflicts without it, and the Order book itself talks about many aspects of what they do that are not strictly to do with fighting (one that I find interesting is the Arrow as element in a Consilium deadlocked by an excess of intrigue that gets people back on task), but they reject people who specifically not only reject all use of violence but view it as a moral wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don\u2019t know what they would think about me. I think violence is wrong, or at least a poor solution to problems. It tends to create even more problems and violence, which is not a bad thing to Arrow, since they believe in growing through struggle, but is not acceptable for me. I think that sometimes there aren\u2019t any other solutions, though. I guess I think of it like this, even if you do good by your actions, you still have all the wrongs you committed to get there. There isn\u2019t a balance, good doesn\u2019t make up for evil. You aren\u2019t absolved of your deeds, just because the good out weighed the bad. Everyone has a chance to become someone different, even if it isn\u2019t likely. Killing them tends to remove their ability to change. If someone tries to hurt or kill someone else, try resolve the situation or take away their ability to do harm, or shield the other. If you can\u2019t do anything else, if the only option truly is kill or let someone else be killed, well\u2026 do whatever you can live with. But no life is truly worth more than another. Not even mine. None of this will ever make it right. I don\u2019t know. I can\u2019t tell others how to live. Just thinking of the scenarios where I might be forced to kill has made me rather sad and slightly sick. I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d live through killing another. Nor letting someone die because I didn\u2019t act when I could have.<br /> I hope something of what I said makes sense, at least enough to place me in or out of the Arrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469597#post1469597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steal it from space debris, man-made or natural. Forget about Earth or the redirection of your own speed vector, this is too much work for too little pay-off.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, definitely should steal from space junk, that\u2019s going to be a problem for people later and it should just fall to Earth. Helping, kinda, with pollution and serving my own purposes, win-win. Even stealing from space rocks is fine, it\u2019s not like I need all of it, and even if I do the sun won\u2019t care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469597#post1469597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, just use fuel and then steal momentum from space rocks. You're trying to come up with the most complex answer by doing it with magic alone.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ha! Yes, I do that often. Thank you for stating the simple solution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469597#post1469597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rockets use tonnes of fuel because they need to accelerate tonnes of fuel. You can magic the energy out of the fuel and not carry the weight. Asteroids are relatively common and high speed, and the big ones will be so many times your weight, vessel included, and you can guilty-free steal all their momentum. Plan your trip to pass through a few select targets and that's it, 1.000 Km/h stolen from a rock 100 times your mass will give you 100.000 Km/h because we're magicking physics out of the equation.<br /> <br /> Stripping energy/mass equivalence and other bits out of the equation simplifies your predicament immensely, and you can simply throw your excess momentum somewhere else when you arrive at your destination. There's no reason to think the trip will take more than a year with magic at your disposal.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will do more calculations, but you are correct. Frankly, at this point, I am satisfied. Momentum and High Energy fuel would work wonders. Actually, I believe there is a way to store my excess if I every need it. It would require Space or Time though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469597#post1469597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBut <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> is right that you need to think through how this whole idea plays a role on the story. Unless it is a solo game or a novel/fiction you're writing, in which case you can enter suspended animation and don't care about the time.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is mostly a thought experiment, but I will use this if I ever make it into a Mage game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-04-2021, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T18:56:20-08:00","id":1469610,"title":"","content":"The Adamantine Arrow's perspective in violence is complicated (even apart from the book emphasizing variation in perspective). It could basically be summed up as them thinking it's not a thing to be yearned for, nor should it be shunned and demonised. It's not a grim necessity, or a thing you should be totally at peace with. It's an aspect of the universe and flowing along with it deepens your understanding of the universe and empowers you to remove things that ought to be removed, so you should embrace it but know the weight of it and be deliberate in where you point it.<br /> <br /> That goes particularly with killing, where a common attitude is that it can at times be necessary but never exactly what you'd call justified. Don't be crushed with guilt over it, but don't be at ease with it or treat it as a first resort, excepting cases where you judge no other resort will suffice.<br /> <br /> And at all times know there will be other Arrows to observe your use of violent and make their opinions of it known through their own martial skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T19:05:21-08:00","id":1469611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469594#post1469594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright let\u2019s see, off the top of my head: is void a symbol -&gt; is void a material like shadow is for death -&gt; does the interstellar medium count as void (there is technically stuff in it)-&gt; can there be perfected void -&gt; do patches of it exist in the interstellar medium or galactic voids like perfected metals do sometimes in ore -&gt; what occult properties does perfected void have</div> </div> </div> </div>There are void spirits, covered in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon, but I feel it's a reach to assume that turning a sensory phenomenon like shadows solid extends logically to turning the literal absence of any material at all into a substance through typical Awakened magic; attributing that kind of power to Death would let you move e.g. literal monetary debt around without the metaphor-handling equipment provided by the magic of changelings, demons, and other specialized systems.<br /> <br /> By the same token, it seems a stretch to assume you can perfect an absence when the vast majority of ordinary materials can't be perfected either, much less that perfected instances would occur in nature. (What would it even <i>do</i>?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there resonance in the void between stars -&gt; is it plentiful because there is a lot of void, or is it thin because it\u2019s void resonance -&gt; is it possible that ley lines run between stars -&gt; are these lines tainted by void resonance or perhaps defined by it. -&gt; can Hallows or Nodes form from intersections of these ley lines and ( if so what kind) </div> </div> </div>There's the aforementioned void spirits, but given how little there is to sustain them in their native environment, the <i>magath-</i>adjacent nature of many of them, and the desolate quality of the void, evidence suggests it's far from a feast of resonance out in the vacuum; most void-spirits are vacuum-spirits, with more stable specimens being light-spirits from distant stars and background radiation, and rarer beings born from psychic phenomena a mage might connect to the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> Ley lines are a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ley_line\" target=\"_blank\">landscape</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feng_shui\" target=\"_blank\">feature</a> that connect to each other through Nodes and transmit resonance along and between them; it would be very weird for ley lines to connect on Earth and in space but not together, barring some sort of plot-driving hidden connection point (like a beach-at-the-end-of-the-world where the Earth is actually flat), which would almost definitely be more about that magical phenomenon than space or ley lines themselves.<br /> <br /> Given the length of space between stars, it's pretty unlikely that there's any ley lines running several times the circumference of the Earth, and if there are, the resonance they'd be feeding into would almost certainly produce Nodes related to Time or Space, which\u2026 won't do anybody much good without a dramatic change in the landscape and population density of outer space.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the interstellar medium a potent yantra -&gt; is there a difference between the yantra some of the Star Dust by itself produces and that of both the void and the dust<br /> what prevents the teleportation by telescope.-&gt; Do the threads of Sympathy get eroded by the void-&gt; </div> </div> </div>Some of this seems founded in the assumption that Space Is Magic, which\u2026 available evidence suggests there's some nasty stuff Out There, but the universe Chronicles takes place in is not the dream of the Golden Age of Space Exploration. Reality is thin outside of the one we know, and often hungry, spiteful, and inhuman when we encounter it at all.<br /> <br /> Space dust is dust. If it has symbolic significance at all (rather than being effectively a mass of destroyed forms), it's going to have a normal amount of symbolic association with the place it came from.<br /> <br /> Sympathy is eroded by the things that erode sympathy, which is mostly time and the loss of memory or the waning of passions. Its connections aren't totally abstract \u2014 emotional phenomena are foundational in most magical matters to some degree, and Fate's got a spell that shows you sympathetic connections for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, I was thinking about how populations are easier to control if they all are in relatively the same space. I don\u2019t doubt that the Exarchs probably didn\u2019t cause the void between stars to be so big, but I\u2019m betting they benefited or are benefiting from it. There is probably \u201ca stay at home\u201d ministry. Probably extremely minor, though. </div> </div> </div>Mage is a game where if you want to affect an area larger than a small neighborhood with a single spell or change the minds of more than ten million people from the inside you need to approach the Godhead.<br /> <br /> The world mages occupy is one where:<br /> \u2022 An entire border-realm between Flesh and Spirit was destroyed and replaced by a barrier made of a non-place where werewolves' failed prototype forebears were imprisoned and fragments of totemic gods occasionally wreck shop, and now the world of spirits is overcrowded from lack of culling.<br /> \u2022 The ocean where ghosts go to dissolve has built up a case of cosmic plaque so extreme that cave systems and sham utopias pad out the space between the entryways and the shoreline, to say nothing of how most ghosts get sucked into the walls or are drinking the not-water.<br /> \u2022 The place where culture lives in the human soul is full of a thousand thousand conflicting idea-forms, engaged in literalized war with each other while on the other side of a metaphorical stone tunnel the world-soul dances to a tune of hunger and pain that can only sort of be blamed on the crashing waves of unreality at its farthest edge.<br /> <br /> People are welcome to customize the setting of their games however they like, but none of this really says to me &quot;Earth used to be part of a grander interstellar system&quot; besides raw speculation about the reach of Atlantis or the nature of the God-Machine. It looks more like the Fallen World is being kept creaking on past the point many of its systems were designed for by beings whose power and placement allows them to be comfortable while the world dies by inches.<br /> <br /> Which is to say: I don't think millennia of mountain-climbers, seafarers, forest-foragers, cave-delvers, and travelers to far-off lands are outweighed by the fact that humans haven't gone very far into space in the century in which we've seen what space is like for human bodies, had rigorous standards of safety and certainty in place even for unmanned exploration, and witnessed a number of highly visible examples of what happens when just the launch process goes wrong \u2014 most people are not mages, which means most people are not predisposed to throw caution to the winds when treating with a region hostile to human life at a scale many trillion times the size of the pale blue dot it comes from.<br /> <br /> I think the Exarchs aren't particularly threatened by the prospect of people going to space, especially when access to space travel is still tied up in matters of power and privilege as it is and those matters will have new avenues for oppression by the time it isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> hmm, the Arrow? Honestly, didn\u2019t really think of myself that way. I do like self refinement, but I\u2019m a pacifist, and dislike physical confrontation. </div> </div> </div>I'd mostly just been saying you wouldn't have much trouble finding volunteers from the Order that says Service is Mastery and prides itself on honing its members' nonmagical capabilities. Finding an Arrow or two who'd relish the physical and spiritual hardships of space travel as a crucible and the aid and protection of a researcher in a distant corner of the universe as a challenging oath to uphold surely wouldn't be impossibly hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-04-2021, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T21:16:10-08:00","id":1469623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are void spirits, covered in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon, but I feel it's a reach to assume that turning a sensory phenomenon like shadows solid extends logically to turning the literal absence of any material at all into a substance through typical Awakened magic; attributing that kind of power to Death would let you move e.g. literal monetary debt around without the metaphor-handling equipment provided by the magic of changelings, demons, and other specialized systems.</div> </div> </div> </div> What about cold then? It\u2019s an absence of heat. That\u2019s a physical absence Death covers. Also fire is a material, by the games logic, even though it\u2019s not in real life. I don\u2019t know, it seems like less of a reach because it\u2019s something lacking a gross arcanum. (Which seems to be something all the Death materials have in common, could be something I\u2019ve forgotten though) (On a side note, how would someone transfer debt through Supernal Magic, because that seems like a thing one should be able to do.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same token, it seems a stretch to assume you can perfect an absence when the vast majority of ordinary materials can't be perfected either, much less that perfected instances would occur in nature. (What would it even <i>do</i>?)</div> </div> </div> </div> \u2026I\u2019m not seeing a line saying that it\u2019s impossible to perfect other materials, just that Mages don\u2019t know much about them, and they are harder to make. It even gives the go ahead for the Storyteller to come up with their own stuff. As for properties, if I had to come up with something, I guess it would be like alkahest and dissolve everything into its smallest components and spread it it out. Maybe even destroy it, or destroy somethings magical properties. Or maybe it would be something like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/False_vacuum_decay\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's the aforementioned void spirits, but given how little there is to sustain them in their native environment, the <i>magath-</i>adjacent nature of many of them, and the desolate quality of the void, evidence suggests it's far from a feast of resonance out in the vacuum; most void-spirits are vacuum-spirits, with more stable specimens being light-spirits from distant stars and background radiation, and rarer beings born from psychic phenomena a mage might connect to the Anima Mundi.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oooo\u2026 direct connection to the Anima Mundi? From the Fallen World. That\u2019s interesting. Very interesting indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ley lines are a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ley_line\" target=\"_blank\">landscape</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feng_shui\" target=\"_blank\">feature</a> that connect to each other through Nodes and transmit resonance along and between them; it would be very weird for ley lines to connect on Earth and in space but not together, barring some sort of plot-driving hidden connection point (like a beach-at-the-end-of-the-world where the Earth is actually flat), which would almost definitely be more about that magical phenomenon than space or ley lines themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div> hmm, it might be interesting if it played into the celestial alignments trope, though that\u2019s more a Mummy thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the length of space between stars, it's pretty unlikely that there's any ley lines running several times the circumference of the Earth, and if there are, the resonance they'd be feeding into would almost certainly produce Nodes related to Time or Space, which\u2026 won't do anybody much good without a dramatic change in the landscape and population density of outer space.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, noted. The utility of Nodes isn\u2019t particularly high anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of this seems founded in the assumption that Space Is Magic, which\u2026 available evidence suggests there's some nasty stuff Out There, but the universe Chronicles takes place in is not the dream of the Golden Age of Space Exploration. Reality is thin outside of the one we know, and often hungry, spiteful, and inhuman when we encounter it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div> it\u2019s founded on the assumption that Yantras scale in strength based on how difficult it is to acquire them. Like I vaguely remember it saying somewhere. *shrugs* That being said, I think \u201cSpace being Magical\u201d is a great description for my style of doing things.<br /> I\u2019m fine for cosmic horror, it\u2019s part of what Mage is here for. Really, I\u2019d be surprised if I didn\u2019t meet some horrific thing from beyond the stars, that then tried to eat me or break my soul and mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space dust is dust. If it has symbolic significance at all (rather than being effectively a mass of destroyed forms), it's going to have a normal amount of symbolic association with the place it came from.</div> </div> </div> </div> A mass of destroyed forms seems intriguing in its own right, I mean, is there a pattern to the chaos? Secondly, depending on where the dust came from, it might have come from the creation of a solar system, nearly untouched since, despite the ages. That seems Magically potent to me. It would be grabbing a ember from a Forge, except the forge was cosmic in scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sympathy is eroded by the things that erode sympathy, which is mostly time and the loss of memory or the waning of passions. Its connections aren't totally abstract \u2014 emotional phenomena are foundational in most magical matters to some degree, and Fate's got a spell that shows you sympathetic connections for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I was suggesting the vast isolation of the void might wear those bonds, or maybe something like a mystery like those in the dark eras, but more directly pressing. I don\u2019t know, maybe that\u2019s not a good idea?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are welcome to customize the setting of their games however they like, but none of this really says to me &quot;Earth used to be part of a grander interstellar system&quot; besides raw speculation about the reach of Atlantis or the nature of the God-Machine. It looks more like the Fallen World is being kept creaking on past the point many of its systems were designed for by beings whose power and placement allows them to be comfortable while the world dies by inches.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m not really assuming there is some vast interstellar system, only positing that the Exarchs do nothing but benefit if we don\u2019t attempt to find out. There might, there might not be, but we could know if checked.<br /> <br /> Also that\u2019s a great description of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is to say: I don't think millennia of mountain-climbers, seafarers, forest-foragers, cave-delvers, and travelers to far-off lands are outweighed by the fact that humans haven't gone very far into space in the century in which we've seen what space is like for human bodies, had rigorous standards of safety and certainty in place even for unmanned exploration, and witnessed a number of highly visible examples of what happens when just the launch process goes wrong \u2014 most people are not mages, which means most people are not predisposed to throw caution to the winds when treating with a region hostile to human life at a scale many trillion times the size of the pale blue dot it comes from.<br /> <br /> I think the Exarchs aren't particularly threatened by the prospect of people going to space, especially when access to space travel is still tied up in matters of power and privilege as it is and those matters will have new avenues for oppression by the time it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div> Look, if there is a ministry for \u201croutine is the opiate of the masses\u201d I don\u2019t see one that says \u201cdon\u2019t explore anything new, stay at home where it is safe\u201d as being that far fetched. I\u2019m not saying it would be a big ministry, it might even fit in as a side branch of Horologion itself, but it seems like something the Seers would do. Have the Exarchs ever waited for something to actually be a threat, before they try to counter it? If something even infinitesimally increases the odds someone might possibly be in a position to one day oppose them, I pretty sure they would try to counter it. Especially if it improved their grip on reality. Keeping people from exploring means keeping people from finding something conflicting with their mental version of reality, and possibly awakening as a result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469611#post1469611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd mostly just been saying you wouldn't have much trouble finding volunteers from the Order that says Service is Mastery and prides itself on honing its members' nonmagical capabilities. Finding an Arrow or two who'd relish the physical and spiritual hardships of space travel as a crucible and the aid and protection of a researcher in a distant corner of the universe as a challenging oath to uphold surely wouldn't be impossibly hard.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh. Alright. Well, sure, crew could help lots! I will keep in mind the Arrow if I get do actually do this.<br /> We got a interesting discussion out of that misunderstanding, so I\u2019m glad it happened.<br /> <br /> I like to take a moment to say: Thank You Satchel. You always write such detailed responses. I wish I had more say in order to respond in kind.<br /> Thank You everyone for helping me with this thought problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-05-2021, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T11:02:13-08:00","id":1469654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469623#post1469623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What about cold then? It\u2019s an absence of heat. That\u2019s a physical absence Death covers. Also fire is a material, by the games logic, even though it\u2019s not in real life. I don\u2019t know, it seems like less of a reach because it\u2019s something lacking a gross arcanum. (Which seems to be something all the Death materials have in common, could be something I\u2019ve forgotten though)</div> </div> </div> </div>Cold is a sensory phenomenon (to the point where the human body has different nerves for detecting cold than for heat), and fire is <i>a thing</i>. The Elemental Masteries are Legacies corresponding to the modern elemental associations of the Paths, and the Tamers of the Void focus on Death with Attainments that use a particular form of ectoplasm.<br /> <br /> Again, this is not the realm of pure abstraction; Awakened magic below archmastery works with the tools provided by the Supernal being the place where the abstract and the concrete mix, but just as you're not going to be able to use Veiling spells to hide from Time Itself, you're not going to be able to Perfect the form of something that doesn't have a form. There's symbols for empty space and the sensory impact of vacuum, and you can move an empty space around in a way that shifts the stuff around it, but you Perfect the absence of anything by removing things from a space rather than by adding qualities to nothing; this is where using Unmaking spells to truck with the Lower Depths generally comes into play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (On a side note, how would someone transfer debt through Supernal Magic, because that seems like a thing one should be able to do.) </div> </div> </div>Shared Fate with the +1 Reach effect to shift it as it happens, Matter, Forces and/or Mind with the necessary placement or sympathies to change the indicators after the fact. Awakened magic runs on building-block logic instead of the rules provided by more established frames of reference, which is part of what Legacies push into to bend the rules like other monsters do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026I\u2019m not seeing a line saying that it\u2019s impossible to perfect other materials, just that Mages don\u2019t know much about them, and they are harder to make. It even gives the go ahead for the Storyteller to come up with their own stuff. </div> </div> </div>It also talks about compounds, alloys, and living materials rather than absences thereof or even magically-produced materials like solidified shadows or ephemera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oooo\u2026 direct connection to the Anima Mundi? From the Fallen World. That\u2019s interesting. Very interesting indeed. </div> </div> </div>Not really; that connection is me extrapolating for &quot;psychic phenomena from seemingly nothing&quot; from the fact that there's a long-established Legacy (the Dreamspeakers) that communicates with Dreamtime beings through their material correspondences \u2014 it's not inconceivable that a patch of outer space might match up with an invisible dreaming thing from the Whorl (Abode of Stars and Aeons), but that's an Astral being exerting rare worldly influence on its material counterpart in a way that happens to be in outer space.<br /> <br /> You'd get more material to go off of in a shorter time by starting from the Astral and building your findings from there, which is why that's the more common advice than leaping past aeronautics to comb the cosmic currents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it\u2019s founded on the assumption that Yantras scale in strength based on how difficult it is to acquire them. Like I vaguely remember it saying somewhere. </div> </div> </div>You get an extra die if you went through significant difficulty to get the right thing for the spell, bumping up to two extra dice if it's from outside the material realm, and this applies to <i>sacraments</i>, Yantras that you use by destroying or consuming them during casting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mass of destroyed forms seems intriguing in its own right, I mean, is there a pattern to the chaos? </div> </div> </div>I was being poetic about the fact that a thing that has ceased to be something is not that thing anymore; Mummy characterizes part of the role of Ammut the Devourer in the cosmology as releasing Sekhem (the stuff of manifest existence) from forms when it's destroyed.<br /> <br /> A clay figurine of a dog ceases to be a figurine of a dog when it's destroyed. Bread stops being bread when it's chewed and swallowed to make mast. Boiling seawater removes an amount of &quot;seawater&quot; from the world to make steam and salt. Space dust has stopped being the rocks it came from and started being one of the most reduced forms of matter in the visible universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have the Exarchs ever waited for something to actually be a threat, before they try to counter it? </div> </div> </div>Every time the Threshold Seeking happens. You don't usually get ochemata dispatched to assassinate you for researching archmastery until you're actually approaching the breakthrough that lets you establish a beachhead in Heaven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If something even infinitesimally increases the odds someone might possibly be in a position to one day oppose them, I pretty sure they would try to counter it. Especially if it improved their grip on reality. Keeping people from exploring means keeping people from finding something conflicting with their mental version of reality, and possibly awakening as a result. </div> </div> </div>The Ministries are charged to divide humanity and keep them trapped in spiritual infancy; they mostly accomplish that by fanning the flames of particular forms of fear or by propagating ways for Sleepers to be too preoccupied to investigate the Lie that keeps them ignorant of magic. Horologion's MO is dramatically more powerful in a fast-paced world where everything is scheduled down to the minute, Hegemony doesn't exist without The State, and the Nemesis's old Archigenitorship is built on the combination of privilege and deniability that cash and masks and such provide.<br /> <br /> There's almost certainly a &quot;stay at home&quot; Ministry or three \u2014 probably under the patronage of the Nemesis or a related Exarch \u2014 but that activity looks like more than just saying &quot;space is dangerous&quot; in a world where the Space Race happened; it's more likely to have its power base in Earthly concerns like insular ethnic neighborhoods or promoting anti-immigration sentiments (or both at once, ideally). Perhaps a different one covers pushing people to cling to stable urban living or engineering highly publicized accidents away from where most people live. Both are likely to run into conflict with a Ministry pushing people to be more afraid of losing their job than getting sick or injured, because the Exarchs play a deeply un-unified game with the Iron Pyramid and power takes many contradictory forms.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs occupy a place in the cosmology that's tied to humanity and doesn't especially care about distance, and the material universe is theoretically big enough that, were attempts to escape Earth's gravity to escape the Lie a credible threat to their power, those instances would be isolated enough that they can tackle them individually unless the individual is <i>also</i> seizing direct Supernal power a la Threshold Seekings or Imperium Rites. Distraction by mundane problems accomplishes much of the work of keeping people from going to space, which is part of why the go-to metaphor for the Awakened these days is to compare them to one-percenters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like to take a moment to say: Thank You Satchel. You always write such detailed responses. I wish I had more say in order to respond in kind. </div> </div> </div>I am a rambling curmudgeon and for that I apologize profusely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T14:02:07-08:00","id":1469662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cold is a sensory phenomenon (to the point where the human body has different nerves for detecting cold than for heat), and fire is <i>a thing</i>. The Elemental Masteries are Legacies corresponding to the modern elemental associations of the Paths, and the Tamers of the Void focus on Death with Attainments that use a particular form of ectoplasm.<br /> <br /> Again, this is not the realm of pure abstraction; Awakened magic below archmastery works with the tools provided by the Supernal being the place where the abstract and the concrete mix, but just as you're not going to be able to use Veiling spells to hide from Time Itself, you're not going to be able to Perfect the form of something that doesn't have a form. There's symbols for empty space and the sensory impact of vacuum, and you can move an empty space around in a way that shifts the stuff around it, but you Perfect the absence of anything by removing things from a space rather than by adding qualities to nothing; this is where using Unmaking spells to truck with the Lower Depths generally comes into play.</div> </div> </div> </div> Going to have concede this one. If anyone would be able to manipulate nothingness, the Tames of the Void would be able to. Still feel like you should be able to do something with something that is Nothing, but I am unable to present a coherent argument as to why I feel that way. So, I\u2019m going to let it rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shared Fate with the +1 Reach effect to shift it as it happens, Matter, Forces and/or Mind with the necessary placement or sympathies to change the indicators after the fact. Awakened magic runs on building-block logic instead of the rules provided by more established frames of reference, which is part of what Legacies push into to bend the rules like other monsters do.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, Fate was the missing piece. Thanks. Perfect spell for a Mammon Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also talks about compounds, alloys, and living materials rather than absences thereof or even magically-produced materials like solidified shadows or ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, but there is limited space in a book. They can\u2019t put everything in there. That\u2019s not strong argument that something cannot be a perfected material. I think. Frankly I would read a book on more random perfected Materials. I wonder if there is a material that is perfectly elastic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really; that connection is me extrapolating for &quot;psychic phenomena from seemingly nothing&quot; from the fact that there's a long-established Legacy (the Dreamspeakers) that communicates with Dreamtime beings through their material correspondences \u2014 it's not inconceivable that a patch of outer space might match up with an invisible dreaming thing from the Whorl (Abode of Stars and Aeons), but that's an Astral being exerting rare worldly influence on its material counterpart in a way that happens to be in outer space.</div> </div> </div> </div> Still worth investigating, I would think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd get more material to go off of in a shorter time by starting from the Astral and building your findings from there, which is why that's the more common advice than leaping past aeronautics to comb the cosmic currents.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah\u2026that\u2019s probably a better starting point for a chronicle anyways. Still, I think the trip is worth it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get an extra die if you went through significant difficulty to get the right thing for the spell, bumping up to two extra dice if it's from outside the material realm, and this applies to <i>sacraments</i>, Yantras that you use by destroying or consuming them during casting.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh. Whoops. This makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A clay figurine of a dog ceases to be a figurine of a dog when it's destroyed. Bread stops being bread when it's chewed and swallowed to make mast. Boiling seawater removes an amount of &quot;seawater&quot; from the world to make steam and salt. Space dust has stopped being the rocks it came from and started being one of the most reduced forms of matter in the visible universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026 I don\u2019t know, that still sounds like a pretty decent Yantra to me, but I suppose part of the point of Yantras is that they are subjective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time the Threshold Seeking happens. You don't usually get ochemata dispatched to assassinate you for researching archmastery until you're actually approaching the breakthrough that lets you establish a beachhead in Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do Seers get dispatched in that situation though? Because ochemata are technically breaking the agreement that archmages and ascended are under, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ministries are charged to divide humanity and keep them trapped in spiritual infancy; they mostly accomplish that by fanning the flames of particular forms of fear or by propagating ways for Sleepers to be too preoccupied to investigate the Lie that keeps them ignorant of magic. Horologion's MO is dramatically more powerful in a fast-paced world where everything is scheduled down to the minute, Hegemony doesn't exist without The State, and the Nemesis's old Archigenitorship is built on the combination of privilege and deniability that cash and masks and such provide.<br /> <br /> There's almost certainly a &quot;stay at home&quot; Ministry or three \u2014 probably under the patronage of the Nemesis or a related Exarch \u2014 but that activity looks like more than just saying &quot;space is dangerous&quot; in a world where the Space Race happened; it's more likely to have its power base in Earthly concerns like insular ethnic neighborhoods or promoting anti-immigration sentiments (or both at once, ideally). Perhaps a different one covers pushing people to cling to stable urban living or engineering highly publicized accidents away from where most people live. Both are likely to run into conflict with a Ministry pushing people to be more afraid of losing their job than getting sick or injured, because the Exarchs play a deeply un-unified game with the Iron Pyramid and power takes many contradictory forms.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nemesis\u2026 makes sense. I forget sometimes how much infighting the Iron Pyramid suffers, because that is a perfect example how even without meaning to, two Ministries might come into conflict. Going to use this minor Ministry, and Horologion as my go to minor Ministries, because both really exemplify the mundane nature of some of the Seers goals. Heh, maybe throw in the Cult of the Doomsday Clock. That would be interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469654#post1469654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a rambling curmudgeon and for that I apologize profusely.</div> </div> </div> </div> It\u2019s fine. Nobody is perfect. Anyways, your rambling is usually very helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-05-2021, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T14:41:11-08:00","id":1469667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469662#post1469662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Seers get dispatched in that situation though? Because ochemata are technically breaking the agreement that archmages and ascended are under, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pax Arcanum is an agreement <i>between</i> archmages and the Ascended, which is why the Threshold Seeking is generally the last chance to outright directly interfere with a prospective archmage; the Exarchs aren't the only ones who exploit this loophole, but they do get the most latitude by virtue of their position. Aspiring Tetrarchs don't necessarily get killed for their trouble, but their Ascended forebears in the Seers' vast hierarchy can put a stop to the Seeking if they don't meet their standards of loyalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T15:40:13-08:00","id":1469672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469662#post1469662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still feel like you should be able to do something with something that is Nothing</div> </div> </div> </div>You do every time you do something with something that is something.<br /> <br /> Or, to be precise for vacuum, with Matter (and Forces if you want to talk true vacuum).<br /> <br /> When you create content you destroy void, when you destroy content you create void.<br /> <br /> The key difference about Death here, though, is that we're not talking about deterioration or antithesis, but true absence. A corpse is opposed to Life because it is the deteriorating husk of the living. It is not mere absence, but a Symbol of degradation, destruction, end.<br /> <br /> But what about an empty room? This, not a corpse or ghost, is the Absence of Life. No lingering force, no memory or decaying husk, just nothing alive is there to begin with.<br /> <br /> Death is about the decaying and decayed, not about mere absence. It is about the ghost and the corpse, not about the empty room. That's why it isn't the Arcanum of void and vacuum, because those aren't the opposition of things, but just the absence of things.<br /> <br /> And absence you define by what is absent. You already deal with it with the other Arcana. So the question isn't what you do with vacuum, but what the complete absence of phenomena related to an Arcanum means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T16:07:01-08:00","id":1469675,"title":"","content":"As an answer to a stray question, the Exarchs didn't start sending influence to get mages to organise at a larger scale in their service until after the Diamond Orders were well on their way to being founded, and even then I get an impression it took a slow and subtle form rather than ochemata appearing to directly command them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T07:29:23-08:00","id":1469915,"title":"","content":"Wards and Signs cast over an area will mean that everything within that are can Withstand having spells cast on it, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T18:01:30-08:00","id":1469983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469915#post1469915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wards and Signs cast over an area will mean that everything within that are can Withstand having spells cast on it, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory yes, which means that technically it allows for an antimagic approach. Cast it over an area, send in a riot team and the mages will have mage armor at most. However, damaging spells are excluded from this, since they are not Withstood.<br /> <br /> On a related question, if one casts Possession over an area, does the mage act as the hive mind or genius loci ? By that I mean that, in theory, they should take control of every camera, every weapon, piece of furniture and individual that fails to Withstand, correct ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T19:13:14-08:00","id":1469987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469983#post1469983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, damaging spells are excluded from this, since they are not Withstood.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of spells that aren't Withstood, and the one in question makes no provision for them. All it says is that when the subject is the target of a spell, it is Withstood by the Potency of Wards and Signs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related question, if one casts Possession over an area, does the mage act as the hive mind or genius loci ? By that I mean that, in theory, they should take control of every camera, every weapon, piece of furniture and individual that fails to Withstand, correct ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel at best it could let you imbue your consciousness into an area such that it can flit around between discrete parts to effect its control, like it was a brain and body with no autonomous movement and required full concentration for everything, the regular human consciousness just not being able to handle governing something on a scope greater than a normal body without enhancement beyond normal Practices.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest though, I think there are some spells that don't quite fit comfortably into the usual factors system, some things that have logical limits to their targeting parameters or necessity in their casting. Like, I don't think there's any circumstance in which you can make use of Shifting Sands without reaching to make it Instant (possibly barring somebody at Gnosis 7 or higher and reaching to make it go back by scenes, and even then you're eating a decent chunk of the reclaimed time just in the ritual).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T23:26:09-08:00","id":1470014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469983#post1469983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, damaging spells are excluded from this, since they are not Withstood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Direct damage spells aren't normally Withstood by one of the subject's traits, but that doesn't mean they ignore Withstand ratings from other sources. They're still subject to Withstand if they're cast using Sympathetic Range or if cast on a subject that's subjected to Wards and Signs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T13:38:32-08:00","id":1470238,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to make durable platonic forms and eidolons by adding conjunctional Matter 3 to Weave in the durability and appearance of physical constructs ? If so, would it be viable to apply this to ectoplasm and solidified shadows as well ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T14:11:41-08:00","id":1470240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1470238#post1470238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible to make durable platonic forms and eidolons</div> </div> </div> </div>???<br /> <br /> Platonic Form: &quot;Potency may be allocated to the following effects: \u2022 Increase Durability by +1 [\u2026]&quot;<br /> <br /> Eidolon: &quot;They follow the Potency rules for Platonic Form (p.169) but Potency may also be allocated to grant dots of the Retainer Merit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T15:40:51-08:00","id":1470245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1470240#post1470240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">???<br /> <br /> Platonic Form: &quot;Potency may be allocated to the following effects: \u2022 Increase Durability by +1 [\u2026]&quot;<br /> <br /> Eidolon: &quot;They follow the Potency rules for Platonic Form (p.169) but Potency may also be allocated to grant dots of the Retainer Merit.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since every use of the created tool or weapon uses mana, I theorized it was part of the form being corroded by the Fallen World, since it only tass in solid form rather than a real mundane material. So would granting it the more real properties of Matter be a way to avoid the corrosion ? It mostly stems from thinking about alternative ways to replicate <i>Ex Nihilo</i> in such a way that more free Reach would be available to, for example, a Forge Master that dedicated herself to mastering both Arcana (and the associated higher Arcane XP investment).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T15:52:54-08:00","id":1470246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1470245#post1470245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since every use of the created tool or weapon uses mana, I theorized it was part of the form being corroded by the Fallen World, since it only tass in solid form rather than a real mundane material. So would granting it the more real properties of Matter be a way to avoid the corrosion ? It mostly stems from thinking about alternative ways to replicate <i>Ex Nihilo</i> in such a way that more free Reach would be available to, for example, a Forge Master that dedicated herself to mastering both Arcana (and the associated higher Arcane XP investment).</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly suspect it\u2019s a \u2018trade secret\u2019 kept by Forge Masters etc, be it via Attainments or jealously guarded magical items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T16:00:47-08:00","id":1470247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1470245#post1470245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since every use of the created tool or weapon uses mana, I theorized it was part of the form being corroded by the Fallen World, since it only tass in solid form rather than a real mundane material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure it's because it's Mana acting like tass and the primary usage of tass is to be consumed or to be a material that happens to have Mana in it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So would granting it the more real properties of Matter be a way to avoid the corrosion ? It mostly stems from thinking about alternative ways to replicate <i>Ex Nihilo</i> in such a way that more free Reach would be available to, for example, a Forge Master that dedicated herself to mastering both Arcana (and the associated higher Arcane XP investment). </div> </div> </div>This seems to be leaning into the old shenanigans where Weaving and Patterning are assumed to have only semantic limitations. You would have better luck ginning up a Perfecting spell that increases an object's equipment bonus and a Patterning spell that can turn a solid object into a different solid object than try to stretch what you can do to Platonic Forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T18:48:14-08:00","id":1470253,"title":"","content":"I like to think of the Platonic Form spell in more metaphysical terms; you're altering the Mana (which I can regard as an energy that kind of reinforces the reality of situations or subjects) into the form of a Supernal template of things, sans the gross material they would normally take the form of. The template can include a thing's properties (in the philosophical sense), and expenditure of Mana reinforces those properties through action; it does not require the Phenomenal thing (although conversely the Phenomenal thing does not require expenditures of Mana because it exists).<br /> <br /> I can see Matter spells that would reinforce its properties, but I'm thinking you can't make a Platonic Form physical enough that it's not spending Mana every time it does something, because by the point you've added enough matter that it doesn't need Mana anymore you've probably just supplanted the template with an actual thing. Like, it seems like the level of the Matter Arcanum where you're shaping some available instance of suitable substance into an actual object, which renders the template form a bit unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T09:49:01-08:00","id":1470285,"title":"","content":"I also don't think it makes that much sense to allow a short cut that would make being a Master of Matter kind of pointless. Yeah, there's probably more to it, but making stuff up out of nowhere is kind of a big part of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T10:46:30-08:00","id":1470535,"title":"","content":"In spell terms, how would one make a fake Grigori ? Effects I can see are a variation of Astral Projection that Patterns the mind into a Goetia with the Watching influence, with an extra Reach used to make them into Rank 2 beings and the whispering being built into the spell. Additional effects seem to include some variation of Shielding from entropy (Shielding of Death or Veil of Moments), something to keep them active via mana (Patterning of Prime and Mind perhaps) and maybe some weird variation of teleportation. Would that be accurate ?<br /> <br /> Lastly, does using Sever Oaths free the subject or is it still lethal ? Can it even dispel the Artifact's effects ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-15T12:05:56-08:00","id":1470541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1470535#post1470535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In spell terms, how would one make a fake Grigori ? Effects I can see are a variation of Astral Projection that Patterns the mind into a Goetia with the Watching influence, with an extra Reach used to make them into Rank 2 beings and the whispering being built into the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that a Patterning of Mind can transform your own unmoored consciousness into a Goetia sure, although I'd say the communication back would need to be a matter of an additional spell to communicate back information.<br /> <br /> Either that or it could be a Numen of the Goetia form. It looks to me like usual spells to create ephemeral entities don't inherently give you power to define things like Numina, so I'm thinking that would also be a case with magic to transform one thing into something ephemeral; an additional spell could be used to modify them. However, I'd also say that an ephemeral being assumes a form according to a general parameter that can include Numina useful for the intended function; not enough to mean the mage never has to cast such additional transformation, but enough to not be too inconvenient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additional effects seem to include some variation of Shielding from entropy (Shielding of Death or Veil of Moments), something to keep them active via mana (Patterning of Prime and Mind perhaps) and maybe some weird variation of teleportation. Would that be accurate ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shroud of Observation is an 8-dot Artifact, so I think its spell is just straight up Practice of Entity* of Mind to fully transform the Sleepwalker into a Grigori, where things like the bodily preservation or Resonance with and teleportation to a defined target are innate to the definition of what a Grigori is. I think the Mana cost could be regarded as a necessity of something casting an Imperial Practice, particularly if it's according to a recurring template.<br /> <br /> If it's an Imperial Practice, then Dispel magic won't work on it (it takes the Practice of Excision to end Imperial spells), and apart from the limited power I think the transformation could be regarded as going beyond the scope of what counts as a constraint on free will for Sever Oaths to be able to affect it.<br /> <br /> * I'd very much say that kind of magic or equivalent is the basis of all Seer servitors; the Tutor that creates Hollow Ones is a bit different, but I'd say any tetrarch who observes it would find the effect to follow the same basic principles as Excision, and could achieve the same effect on a subject themselves with that Practice (having a creature to do it is simply more efficient, and I suspect allows the creation of Hollow Ones on a much greater scale than Grigori, Myrmidons or the Hive-Souled).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, Entities is seven dots... I guess the Artifact could have two powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-15-2021, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-16T09:47:21-08:00","id":1470636,"title":"","content":"Fascinating, I had not thought that it would use an Imperial Practice. But it makes perfect sense, it does way too much for so few dots. Any mage who looks at that Artifact via a Knowing will probably start sweating cold.<br /> <br /> So it appears its too much trouble for a Banisher to make a red herring, causing conflict in a Consilia they can leverage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T01:19:11-08:00","id":1470829,"title":"","content":"With one Reach, the Serendipity spell allows a mage to substitute Skills of the same category, described as facilitated by quirks of fate.<br /> <br /> How might one make this work to be able to use Firearms in place of Drive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T20:59:35-08:00","id":1470906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1470829#post1470829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With one Reach, the Serendipity spell allows a mage to substitute Skills of the same category, described as facilitated by quirks of fate.<br /> <br /> How might one make this work to be able to use Firearms in place of Drive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the context, maybe a series of trick shots allow them to end a chase by blocking off the path of pursuers. It could make convenient alterations to the terrain that trivialize the driving, such as a bullet knocking down a lynchpin, causing a convenient landslide that fills in the space where they would have to drive through an old, narrow bridge. What kind of scenario is it being used for ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T12:51:53-08:00","id":1470942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1470906#post1470906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on the context, maybe a series of trick shots allow them to end a chase by blocking off the path of pursuers. It could make convenient alterations to the terrain that trivialize the driving, such as a bullet knocking down a lynchpin, causing a convenient landslide that fills in the space where they would have to drive through an old, narrow bridge. What kind of scenario is it being used for ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I wasn't really thinking of it in terms of using the gun itself to accomplish the goals that one would want out of applications of Drive so much as employing gun know-how to make up for lack of skill in vehicular handling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T13:01:59-08:00","id":1470944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1470942#post1470942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I wasn't really thinking of it in terms of using the gun itself to accomplish the goals that one would want out of applications of Drive so much as employing gun know-how to make up for lack of skill in vehicular handling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aim the car, hit the pedal like a trigger, correct your aim.<br /> <br /> This is just the worst bullet in the world and you're inside, but you're a pro!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T16:02:12-08:00","id":1471366,"title":"","content":"New question: I've been trying to figure out how to use a pocket dimension as a sanctum. <br /> <br /> A few things confused me, but mechanically, assuming you want to prevent the spell from being dispelled (and i haven't seen any examples of Making spells being lasting). <br /> <br /> The default withstand for dispelling pocket dimension would be 5, +2 for advanced potentcy, +1 for a Ward (prime 2 sheilding) = 8. (And a possible +1 for being withstood by sympathetic range?).<br /> <br /> Actually no, to dispell from outside of the pocket i am assuming you need to scry in and use two reach for a remote viewing to target the spell, which is not at sympathetic range. So a target of 8 withstanding, is that correct? <br /> <br /> The part i don't think is clear is without an iris, how hard is it to teleport into the pocket - the mage who casts the pocket can use their body as a material sympathic yantra, but do they also get a strong sympathetic connection (as the creator of the space?) Or do they need to build up sympathy over time (or with magic)? <br /> <br /> Other options I've considered are veiling the spell with prime (instead of earring), a space Ward, cut the threads to prevent sympathic connections... Am i missing anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T18:17:37-08:00","id":1471371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471366#post1471366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The default withstand for dispelling pocket dimension would be 5, +2 for advanced potentcy, +1 for a Ward (prime 2 sheilding) = 8. (And a possible +1 for being withstood by sympathetic range?).<br /> <br /> Actually no, to dispell from outside of the pocket i am assuming you need to scry in and use two reach for a remote viewing to target the spell, which is not at sympathetic range. So a target of 8 withstanding, is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either of these would work, though obviously the difficulties of getting an appropriate sympathy Yantra and borrowing the necessary connection is a bigger hurdle to clear than the coin toss between adding more Reach to the dispellation attempt or spending more Mana on the Attainment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The part i don't think is clear is without an iris, how hard is it to teleport into the pocket - the mage who casts the pocket can use their body as a material sympathic yantra, but do they also get a strong sympathetic connection (as the creator of the space?) Or do they need to build up sympathy over time (or with magic)? </div> </div> </div>A mage has a Medium sympathetic link to their own spells, per the chart. You would need to use magic or a lot of time; naturally-occurring Strong sympathies are a relatively narrow band of phenomena.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other options I've considered are veiling the spell with prime (instead of earring), a space Ward, cut the threads to prevent sympathic connections... Am i missing anything? </div> </div> </div>Ward is going to be your best bet for the simple reason that it adds another layer to circumvent and allows you to give yourself a backdoor to an already-secure space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T18:28:40-08:00","id":1471372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471371#post1471371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either of these would work, though obviously the difficulties of getting an appropriate sympathy Yantra and borrowing the necessary connection is a bigger hurdle to clear than the coin toss between adding more Reach to the dispellation attempt or spending more Mana on the Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually i was wondering how you could get a sympathy to the spell at all, a sympathy to the space (or anything in it) would be easier, assuming there are lots of things going in/out of this sanctum...<br /> <br /> Unless you spend lots of time examining it? Or borrow/steal a sympathy from the mage who cast it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mage has a Medium sympathetic link to their own spells, per the chart. You would need to use magic or a lot of time; naturally-occurring Strong sympathies are a relatively narrow band of phenomena. </div> </div> </div>Thank you i must have missed that bit!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ward is going to be your best bet for the simple reason that it adds another layer to circumvent and allows you to give yourself a backdoor to an already-secure space. </div> </div> </div>You mean a space Ward? <br /> <br /> Sorry i was confused there.<br /> <br /> Ok, so assuming the plan is to pay the willpower dot to release this spell. Is withstand of 8 against dispelling actually high (compared to the numbers ppl actually see in actual play? - which clearly i haven't done yet... This is more theory crafting so i get a good feel for the mechanics...)<br /> <br /> EDIT: i am neglecting the extreme option of developing a legacy to cast pocket dimension as an attainment instead of a spell, making dispell magic fail. But i am assuming that is even less practical than any of the above.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: quick back of the envelope calculations seems to actually give me a prime Ward of potentcy ~10 (+1 for spell withstanding) that would actually suggest a maximal dispell reaching 10 successes on average.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 12-27-2021, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T18:38:05-08:00","id":1471373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471366#post1471366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The default withstand for dispelling pocket dimension would be 5, +2 for advanced potentcy, +1 for a Ward (prime 2 sheilding) = 8. (And a possible +1 for being withstood by sympathetic range?)</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Prime Shielding has Potency lower than 8, then yes. Otherwise, it would take the priority with everything else being the slight modifier..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually no, to dispell from outside of the pocket i am assuming you need to scry in and use two reach for a remote viewing to target the spell, which is not at sympathetic range. So a target of 8 withstanding, is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages have medium sympathetic connections to their own spells, so spells are something that it is possible to have a connection to and then target directly with sympathetic magic. It wouldn't be necessary to have the live visual feed on the space to target it. Really, I think if you had sympathy to the space for scrying anyway, you could already cast the spell to try breaking it; would just need to have an idea of how big it is for the size factor.<br /> <br /> Scrying or similar visuals would help if the one with power to observe it doesn't have the Prime to dispel it, and needs to provide a visual for somebody who does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part i don't think is clear is without an iris, how hard is it to teleport into the pocket - the mage who casts the pocket can use their body as a material sympathic yantra, but do they also get a strong sympathetic connection (as the creator of the space?) Or do they need to build up sympathy over time (or with magic)?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage and her own spells is actually given as the first example of what a Medium sympathetic link might be. I think it's reasonable to say that when it comes to Making spells, the spell and the subject are indistinguishable for purposes of sympathy, and many other things besides. So if you use Making to create a living being, your Medium connection to the spell is simultaneously a connection to the creature.<br /> <br /> Hmm, has implications for how mages relate to what they bring forth whole cloth...<br /> <br /> Still, for a pocket with no Iris, I'd say getting sympathy to it is difficult enough; copying or stealing a connection from a Master of Space seems like a dicey proposition, so it might come down to getting and betraying their trust to enter (or acquiring it from some other person given that confidence).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other options I've considered are veiling the spell with prime (instead of earring), a space Ward, cut the threads to prevent sympathic connections... Am i missing anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a Veiling of Prime (or Space) would help to conceal any visual signifiers it might have (really only an Iris, I think; if it's totally detached from reality, there's nothing to observe).<br /> <br /> A Space Ward can make the Pocket Dimension harder to target remotely and lock down its Iris more firmly, but wouldn't make it harder to detect innately, if there's something to externally observe.<br /> <br /> Severing sympathy to a pocket dimension is possible, but that magic is Lasting. If it's a case of removing the connection from others to make it more exclusive that's fine, but if you sever it from yourself and have no Iris then the dimension is totally cut off, inaccessible to everybody. I think in a case where a pocket is so compromised, it might be more advisable to dismiss it and collect the contents from the hopefully more secure entry point.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose a powerful Wraith of Pandemonium or Dahlak, Aeon of Space (and Mind) could restore a sympathetic connection to something that cannot otherwise be interacted with to form them naturally or magically.<br /> <br /> Oh, here's a fun thing to consider; if a Seer Prelate with the Crown of Vision knows the pocket dimension exists and has a valid sympathy Yantra to it, it's impossible to make them unable to try targeting it with sympathetic spells. I'm suddenly imagining the mage who is manipulated into impulsively severing all ties to render the pocket and its contents inaccessible, only to realise that they've ceded access to it exclusively to Prelates of the Eye. Keep in mind, the Prelacy only allows somebody to cast <i>as though</i> they had a connection, it doesn't actually give them one, so you can't use other magic to sever a connection to prevent one from casting.<br /> <br /> (For consideration; a Seer with the Crown of Vision can be given a photograph of any random person, or learn any random name, and then target them sympathetically without knowing anything else about them or having ever personally encountered them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T20:13:42-08:00","id":1471375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471372#post1471372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you spend lots of time examining it? Or borrow/steal a sympathy from the mage who cast it...</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You mean a space Ward?<br /> <br /> Sorry i was confused there. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I mean the Space spell Ward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, so assuming the plan is to pay the willpower dot to release this spell. Is withstand of 8 against dispelling actually high (compared to the numbers ppl actually see in actual play? - which clearly i haven't done yet... This is more theory crafting so i get a good feel for the mechanics...) </div> </div> </div>It's at least a six-dice penalty on the dispellation pool for a Master of Prime, and more for any less experienced practitioner. Making up that difference is going to necessitate some potent Yantras or enough Gnosis to use a lot of smaller ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: i am neglecting the extreme option of developing a legacy to cast pocket dimension as an attainment instead of a spell, making dispell magic fail. But i am assuming that is even less practical than any of the above. </div> </div> </div>Gnosis 8, spend a scene to create a space the size of a large room that lasts for a year? There's worse things to put mastery of the Arcana towards, I suppose, but the limitations of Fixed Reach are such that there's also a number of better uses to put that limited resource toward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T20:19:37-08:00","id":1471376,"title":"","content":"Thanks, a lot of this maps to where my thinking was.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471373#post1471373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Prime Shielding has Potency lower than 8, then yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am assuming a master of Space with only a little Prime, so lower than 8. But maybe Prime Sheilding of 10 and above is realistic.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, for a pocket with no Iris, I'd say getting sympathy to it is difficult enough; copying or stealing a connection from a Master of Space seems like a dicey proposition, so it might come down to getting and betraying their trust to enter (or acquiring it from some other person given that confidence). </div> </div> </div>I am assuming that unforseen betrayal is not something you can protect against (obviously Fate might be able to prevent someone from passing an iris but for the sake of argument let's say our character has no dots in Fate). <br /> <br /> As for getting a sympathy: There is getting a sympathy to the spell itself (which i think is very hard, medium connection to the caster...which might weaken over time if it is indefinite duration and released with willpower?) And maybe a connection to someone who has scrutinised it a lot with focused mage sight?<br /> <br /> Whereas getting a connection to the space itself is much easier, just find someone who has visited. You don't have to turn them traitor, just scry on them while they are visiting the sanctum and get sensory (remote viewing) range on the spell. <br /> <br /> For context, i was thinking about severing connections to the space for visitors, or for object which may have been moved in (if your character is sleeping there, their bed doesn't need sympathy to the outside world). <br /> <br /> The thought of a lost space which no one can access leaves me with some fun possible story hooks. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, a Veiling of Prime (or Space) would help to conceal any visual signifiers it might have (really only an Iris, I think; if it's totally detached from reality, there's nothing to observe). </div> </div> </div> You veil the spell so visitors can't easily target it. Or remote viewing can't easily see it, not sure what veiling the space does - kinda covered severing the sympathic links, you Sheild the space to prevent unwanted scrying/remote viewing.<br /> <br /> Severing sympathy to a pocket dimension is possible, but that magic is Lasting. If it's a case of removing the connection from others to make it more exclusive that's fine, but if you sever it from yourself and have no Iris then the dimension is totally cut off, inaccessible to everybody. I think in a case where a pocket is so compromised, it might be more advisable to dismiss it and collect the contents from the hopefully more secure entry point.<br /> <br /> You might be better off using Time (and i am assuming our Character has time 2) to reacquire the sympathy... But also there are no seers. Or if there are the character doesn't know they can do that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, two other tangents. There is no paradox in a pocket dimension (though i don't think that should apply for spell control, just get the usual sanctum bonus to spell control at home). But assuming you have a scelestus or just a regular low wisdom mage casting sympatheticly out of the pocket dimension, can they accidentally* bring the abyss in and permanently mess things up?<br /> <br /> And second, if you do have the indefinite pocket dispelled (but you cast it from a different temp pocket which no longer exists) and everything returns to the non-existant temp pocket, does all the stuff get destroyed? ( I am half thinking of an easily dismissable entrance space - which is recast monthly or weekly - and most ppl or things actually enter from - the entrance i think needs Veil of Moments** rather than 'normal flow of time' but i think that should be an option for pocket dimension, a time 2 sheilding instead of the RAW time 2 ruling effect)<br /> <br /> *Or intentionally in the case of the scelestus.<br /> <br /> **Just to stop people bleeding out, so if they are fleeing they can wait in the entrance way until they aren't dying...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 12-27-2021, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T22:36:18-08:00","id":1471383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471376#post1471376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am assuming a master of Space with only a little Prime, so lower than 8. But maybe Prime Sheilding of 10 and above is realistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Master needs at least Gnosis 5 and Shielding needs at least Prime 2. I've calculated that a starting dice pool of 7 and the correct assembly of Yantras can readily cast a Potency 10 spell that can last for a month (provided it's a rote). <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942655-wards-and-signs-balance?p=1459191#post1459191\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...91#post1459191</a><br /> <br /> I think it should always be remembered that a mage with the luxury of time can get up to five extra dice just from making their ritual casting longer. Really, considering the miniscule pool and limited Yantra options of early mages, it's probably essential for the odd spell that needs decent factors; hence why Signs and Sorcery talks about what it takes to endure casting for eighteen hours straight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am assuming that unforseen betrayal is not something you can protect against (obviously Fate might be able to prevent someone from passing an iris but for the sake of argument let's say our character has no dots in Fate).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well any Iris can be given a Key to limit access. Still, most of your ways to prevent betrayal are in general conduct.<br /> <br /> I think it should always be kept in mind that a Master of Space casts sympathetic spells that overcome the Withstand of the weakest sympathy without having a name by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for getting a sympathy: There is getting a sympathy to the spell itself (which i think is very hard, medium connection to the caster...which might weaken over time if it is indefinite duration and released with willpower?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think there's an intimacy to even a relinquished spell that makes the link to it very enduring. Not forever, but for quite some time.<br /> <br /> That's if you cast it and walk away forever. I think there's no chance of you're regularly engaging with that pocket.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And maybe a connection to someone who has scrutinised it a lot with focused mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see naturally forming sympathy as requiring the subject to be a regular part of your life, something that forms part of the pattern of your activity. You can be given a summary of a person's entire life story, including all their secret hopes and crimes and dreams, and their person remains distant and disconnected, while you have a weak link to the barista you collect coffee from three times a week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas getting a connection to the space itself is much easier, just find someone who has visited. You don't have to turn them traitor, just scry on them while they are visiting the sanctum and get sensory (remote viewing) range on the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well scrying itself will need to be cast sympathetically there, so how is one's connection to the mage they're targeting? Do they need to touch that person along with a spell to have it? Do they need to steal yet another connection that somebody else has to the targeted mage?<br /> <br /> Scrying on a person only gives you a very limited range of vision on the space they inhabit or anything they interact with, mind. I think if one can cast sympathetically and dispel, they're still better off casting an area effect spell centered on the person they're connected to and make it big enough to encompass the pocket.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For context, i was thinking about severing connections to the space for visitors, or for object which may have been moved in (if your character is sleeping there, their bed doesn't need sympathy to the outside world).</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, although it can only ever have sympathy to the person who sleeps in it frequently. It's only a liability if somebody who can access a regular user can copy the connection unnoticed.<br /> <br /> Irregular visitors will not form a connection anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be better off using Time (and i am assuming our Character has time 2) to reacquire the sympathy...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the kind of Time magic needed to restore oneself to a state when they had sympathy to something would need at least three dots.<br /> <br /> There might be in-character stresses if it had to be regular, but I suppose once you had it you could get back into the pocket, drop the Time spell, and use Space to make a new connection to an area you can target directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, two other tangents. There is no paradox in a pocket dimension (though i don't think that should apply for spell control, just get the usual sanctum bonus to spell control at home). But assuming you have a scelestus or just a regular low wisdom mage casting sympatheticly out of the pocket dimension, can they accidentally* bring the abyss in and permanently mess things up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well anybody can cast to target outside of the pocket and risk that. If they have the traits to make long lasting Abyssal Environments, then sure those can form on a pocket dimension.<br /> <br /> If a Scelestus, those can have powers to store Paradox successes from other castings and just apply them directly to create Anomalies wherever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And second, if you do have the indefinite pocket dispelled (but you cast it from a different temp pocket which no longer exists) and everything returns to the non-existant temp pocket, does all the stuff get destroyed? </div> </div> </div> </div>It's an odd case, but I think it could qualify to leave the contents with nowhere to go.<br /> <br /> Your Time questions I'd have to be looking at the book to figure out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T07:37:53-08:00","id":1471389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Well anybody can cast to target outside of the pocket and risk that. If they have the traits to make long lasting Abyssal Environments, then sure those can form on a pocket dimension.<br /> <br /> If a Scelestus, those can have powers to store Paradox successes from other castings and just apply them directly to create Anomalies wherever. </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of adding an abyss so spells cast in the pocket dimension would cause paradox on their own. (I presume even Imperial practices of whatever causes the lie were not able to target pocket dimensions which didn't exist at the time, and which is why there is no paradox there... ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T07:55:47-08:00","id":1471390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, a Master needs at least Gnosis 5 and Shielding needs at least Prime 2. I've calculated that a starting dice pool of 7 and the correct assembly of Yantras can readily cast a Potency 10 spell that can last for a month (provided it's a rote). <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...91#post1459191\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...91#post1459191</a> </div> </div> </div>looking at your calculations, i think i would hit that number a different way. With Prime: use As Above, So Below to get a sacred tool (with 8-agains) and cast from a Grimoire* for Rote quality (or if you are a master casting your own rote). <br /> <br /> With Fate it would be: Exceptional Luck for 8-agains and Superlative Luck for Rote quality. <br /> <br /> Either way your expected success rate per dice is 0.7, which means you're better off rolling a large dice pool than taking penalties (for the primary spell factor).<br /> <br /> With Time 2 (which is required for a pocket dimension with normal time) you can also cast Choose the Thread to roll twice and pick the better result.<br /> <br /> Lots of reaching there, but inside a pocket dimension that is free.<br /> <br /> Gnosis 5 + prime 2 + yantras 5 + ritual time (160 minutes for +3) = 15 dice (with other yantras cancelling out the duration penalties) = 10.5 expected successes (not counting the effect of Choose the Thread).<br /> <br /> *Scribe Grimoire is only Prime 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 12-28-2021, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T08:17:48-08:00","id":1471391,"title":"","content":"Number of successes only matters for exceptional success, which can give you an extra Reach, a beneficial Condition, increase a factor by one step, or refund Mana.<br /> <br /> Also ignore Withstand, but that's irrelevant here.<br /> <br /> A spell's primary factor automatically gets stepped up based on caster's Arcanum rating. Masters casting Primary Potency get Potency 5 by default with one success. Increasing that requires taking penalties, same as any factor (or the bit from exceptional success). If cast with a level 2 Arcanum, it will be Potency 2.<br /> <br /> Effort to get a spell dice pool that rolls eleven successes has wasted six of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-28-2021, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T09:19:19-08:00","id":1471393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471391#post1471391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Number of successes only matters for exceptional success, which can give you an extra Reach, a beneficial Condition, increase a factor by one step, or refund Mana.<br /> <br /> Also ignore Withstand, but that's irrelevant here.<br /> <br /> A spell's primary factor automatically gets stepped up based on caster's Arcanum rating. Masters casting Primary Potency get Potency 5 by default with one success. Increasing that requires taking penalties, same as any factor (or the bit from exceptional success). If cast with a level 2 Arcanum, it will be Potency 2.<br /> <br /> Effort to get a spell dice pool that rolls eleven successes has wasted six of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell is withstood by a 10, the extra success cancel those out. No?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ok wait, so actually 5 success will dispell anything, no matter what the withstand is. (Or destroy any rank spirits...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 12-28-2021, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T09:52:56-08:00","id":1471394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471393#post1471393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the spell is withstood by a 10, the extra success cancel those out. No?</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting past Withstand is always a matter of raising Potency above it or using the effect of Exceptional Success to ignore it. Spells are something where rolling it is only ever normal success or exceptional success, number of dice that turn up in between or above that does not matter.<br /> <br /> Exceptional success on a dispel casting will affect any spell yes, although keep in mind that it takes 2 Reach to make that Lasting. Otherwise the spell effect will return when Duration expires.<br /> <br /> Annihilate Spirit... it's really dealer's choice between using Exceptional Success or regular Potency to overcome the target's Rank, because with Potency as primary factor it's always going to have enough to take out most spirits by default and will only need a -2 penalty to go after your Rank 5s (it can't hurt higher spirits anyway). That being said, that spell is an odd one when it not only provides Clash of Wills as an additional layer of protection, but gives it the unusual dice pool of Power + Finesse. Spirits that were already very powerful are going to fairly reliably be able to roll enough successes to not be disintegrated in one go.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, a few other things to consider about Annihilate Spirit:<br /> <br /> A rank 4 or 5 spirit is very likely to be bigger than size 5, and that's going to require some degree of additional penalty to cast on in the first place.<br /> <br /> You're only ever going to have one free Reach on the spell, and you're probably going to want to use that on making the casting instant. That means that making it something you can use at sensory range or going for advanced scale to ease the dice penalties for targeting on larger spirits is going to cost three Paradox dice each (more if you're the stronger kind of Master). I think that's not an inconsiderable portion of your Mana pool to mitigate it, and could delay the casting by a bit if you went for both and wanted to reduce to a chance die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-28-2021, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T10:14:38-08:00","id":1471396,"title":"","content":"Ok, so there is no point in making a spell harder to dispell than 5 (which is the default for pocket dimension without Warding or advanced potentcy etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T10:38:11-08:00","id":1471398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471396#post1471396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so there is no point in making a spell harder to dispell than 5 (which is the default for pocket dimension without Warding or advanced potentcy etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure why you think that is.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, dispelling only requires one dot of Prime and (in this case) Space. A spell with high Withstand will make things difficult for a large number of mages who cannot readily get high Potency or exceptional success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T11:32:51-08:00","id":1471399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471398#post1471398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not sure why you think that is.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, dispelling only requires one dot of Prime and (in this case) Space. A spell with high Withstand will make things difficult for a large number of mages who cannot readily get high Potency or exceptional success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because i was mistakenly misunderstanding that withstand reduced successes, so once you get 5 successes instead of overcoming more withstand you exceptional success and choose to ignore the withstand. <br /> <br /> But that isn't how it works at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T11:50:23-08:00","id":1471400,"title":"","content":"Yes, you could have a spell of whatever Potency with only one success. Withstand will subtract from Potency, unless exceptional success is rolled (if that option is chosen over things like Mana refund or a Condition to get an Arcane Beat).<br /> <br /> This has significance when you cast spells with effects tied to Potency on people. If a person has Resolve 4, it can be the difference between reducing an Attribute by 1 and by 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T12:02:06-08:00","id":1471401,"title":"","content":"Ok, so if someone cast withering (Death 4 unravelling - even though you are making them more dead) on a target with Wards and Signs (Prime 2 sheilding) of potency 3, the withering either gets 1-4 successes and applies (potency-3) damage, or 5 successes (3 for praxis) and does full potency damage (but damage spells normal are withstood so this benefits the defender a lot).<br /> <br /> EDIT: and thank you, too much 1st Ed thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 12-28-2021, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T13:01:31-08:00","id":1471404,"title":"","content":"Does the Familiar link always ping the Peripheral Sight ? If so, it seems to be a weird thing for the Guardians to have as a standard thing in Order Archives, since it seems like it would make it more difficult for the mage to blend in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T19:21:35-08:00","id":1471413,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471401#post1471401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so if someone cast withering (Death 4 unravelling - even though you are making them more dead) on a target with Wards and Signs (Prime 2 sheilding) of potency 3, the withering either gets 1-4 successes and applies (potency-3) damage, or 5 successes (3 for praxis) and does full potency damage (but damage spells normal are withstood so this benefits the defender a lot).</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471404#post1471404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Familiar link always ping the Peripheral Sight ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what do you mean by &quot;the Familiar link&quot;? Do you mean a Familiar walking into the presence of a mage? No; Peripheral Sight alerts mages to the activation of powers within their presence. If a person casts a dozen spells on themselves in the morning in their sanctum, they're not going to trigger the Sight of every mage they walk past.<br /> <br /> If you mean the sense sharing or Mana-Essence transfer, I'd say yes, those are active powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, it seems to be a weird thing for the Guardians to have as a standard thing in Order Archives, since it seems like it would make it more difficult for the mage to blend in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blend in with whom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T11:32:04-08:00","id":1471443,"title":"","content":"I just reviewed page 90 of the core book and the supplemental material on page 25 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>. The way its explained seems to suggest it detects all active supernatural effects nearby. But it doesn't draw a distinction between, for example, an active buff or the immediate activation of the effect. So technically both a Life increase to Dexterity cast at the beginning of the day and one cast impromptu should theoretically ping. Would there be perhaps a further source of clarification that I am missing ?<br /> <br /> By that train of thought, I imagined having things that would ping the Peripheral Sight while in your mundane persona would be a bad practice by Shadow Name standards, which would theoretically be something the Guardians would frown upon, even if it Familiars could provide a steady influx of intel while they go about their everyday lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T15:43:24-08:00","id":1471459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471443#post1471443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just reviewed page 90 of the core book and the supplemental material on page 25 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>. The way its explained seems to suggest it detects all active supernatural effects nearby. But it doesn't draw a distinction between, for example, an active buff or the immediate activation of the effect. So technically both a Life increase to Dexterity cast at the beginning of the day and one cast impromptu should theoretically ping. Would there be perhaps a further source of clarification that I am missing ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every published example of Peripheral Mage Sight triggering is based in an event happening or a record of an event happening, with the exceptions of the presence of Aedes, Ochemata, Lucid proto-mages, and Hallows/stored Mana/appropriate invisible entities with the modifications provided by the Mana Sensitivity Merit and the Lesser Utility Attainments for Death, Mind, and Spirit.<br /> <br /> The corebook's section on Active Mage Sight likewise says Peripheral Sight is triggered by supernatural events, and, of course, Signs clarified that Peripheral Mage Sight normally works through the lens of your mundane senses and leads with &quot;the casting of a spell&quot; rather than &quot;the presence of a spell&quot; as the mage-specific example of things that trigger Peripheral Sight.<br /> <br /> It's there to play the X Files theme when you witness a spooky phenomenon, and if something's mere presence is making your hair stand on end it's because it's especially potent and/or you've trained your sixth sense to that end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T16:13:51-08:00","id":1471461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471443#post1471443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just reviewed page 90 of the core book and the supplemental material on page 25 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>. The way its explained seems to suggest it detects all active supernatural effects nearby.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it uses the word &quot;active&quot; might seem to suggest that it responds to everything that is presently functional, the actual explanations specify that it means &quot;thing that has just been activated&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that train of thought, I imagined having things that would ping the Peripheral Sight while in your mundane persona would be a bad practice by Shadow Name standards, which would theoretically be something the Guardians would frown upon, even if it Familiars could provide a steady influx of intel while they go about their everyday lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the reasoning of carrying around something that might alert Peripheral Mage Sight causing the Shadow Name to intrude on mundane persona has a fault in its logic already. It's really mostly a thing concerned with who and what the mage deliberately casts their own spells on, and maybe also some other things happening to or arising from them that results in something actually... consequential happening to their mundane life. I could see an argument that a mage making trouble with spirits in a way that causes them to retaliate against Sleeper relatives undermines the Shadow Name, but not simply having a mystical connection to a single spirit.<br /> <br /> Even if your proposal was accurate, that could lead into the point that Guardians often discourage members from living by anything <i>but</i> a Shadow Name; depart completely from the life you had before and live exclusively for the Mysteries. Interact with Sleepers only in the persona of a cult manager or some form of shadowy figure that can fix things up for them or make their life hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T12:30:04-08:00","id":1471499,"title":"","content":"I see, that makes things much easier. Thank you both for the clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T17:12:44-08:00","id":1471694,"title":"","content":"Ok, some questions about the Eidolon spell (Prime 5 Making). It allows conjunctional Mind 5 (Making) to give it a mind of its own. 1) Would it also be reasonable to allow Goetic summons (Mind 3 Perfecting) to summon a part of one's own soul (possibly your virtue?) and have the Goetic Demon possess the mindless Eidolon (either conjunctionally or as a seperate spell).<br /> <br /> Assuming this is possible, 2) could you also use Forge Purpose (Prime 5 Making) to give the Eidolon/Goetic Demon one of your Obsessions? And essentially leave it to its own devices... (Maybe with some instruction...) <br /> <br /> And 3) what happens when your Goetic Demon returns to the Astral (again assuming you summoned it from your own Oneiros, not somewhere else). Would you be able to integrate its experience and gain any Arcane Experience it might have acquired while embodied. <br /> <br /> Similarly, 4) could you bind a ghost or spirit to an Eidolon (which is essentially an object, so might fit the requirements for making a fetish). <br /> <br /> For a ghost 5) could you make it look like the ghost's original body? <br /> <br /> For a spirit 6) could the Eidolon be a platonic ideal of whatever the spirit is resonant with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-02-2022, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T18:12:03-08:00","id":1471696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471694#post1471694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, some questions about the Eidolon spell (Prime 5 Making). It allows conjunctional Mind 5 (Making) to give it a mind of its own. 1) Would it also be reasonable to allow Goetic summons (Mind 3 Perfecting) to summon a part of one's own soul (possibly your virtue?) and have the Goetic Demon possess the mindless Eidolon (either conjunctionally or as a seperate spell).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think at that point you're just using Goetic Summons with conjunctional Prime 5 to give it a body made out of a complex Pattern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming this is possible, 2) could you also use Forge Purpose (Prime 5 Making) to give the Eidolon/Goetic Demon one of your Obsessions? And essentially leave it to its own devices... (Maybe with some instruction...) </div> </div> </div>Invisible Entities don't have Aspirations or Obsessions and goetia are arguably the least conceptually flexible of the lot, so probably not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And 3) what happens when your Goetic Demon returns to the Astral (again assuming you summoned it from your own Oneiros, not somewhere else). Would you be able to integrate its experience and gain any Arcane Experience it might have acquired while embodied. </div> </div> </div>Strong odds against, since they don't track Experiences and the nearest analog to what you're suggesting (ochemata) has the spending pull in the other direction (i.e. subsouls casting spells that cost Arcane Experience use their creator's pool).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, 4) could you bind a ghost or spirit to an Eidolon (which is essentially an object, so might fit the requirements for making a fetish). </div> </div> </div>Under the same logic as Golem's conjunctional use of Death or Spirit, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a ghost 5) could you make it look like the ghost's original body? </div> </div> </div>Per the visual limitations of Eidolon without conjunctional Forces, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a spirit 6) could the Eidolon be a platonic ideal of whatever the spirit is resonant with? </div> </div> </div>Unpack what this means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T18:26:03-08:00","id":1471697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unpack what this means </div> </div> </div>To use the example in the book, Eidolon fire (which does not burn) as a fetish object for a spirit of fire (which may gain essence from the usual fire related things and thus might like being in the platonic ideal of fire - and is not bleeding essence at least if i understand the possession rules). <br /> <br /> It might even influence the Eidolon fire to burn things using influence fire. <br /> <br /> It is the 'may imitate entire environments' part of the Eidolon spell i am thinking of. Ok you've got a fairly solid illusion going on, now can it be enhanced by a little spirit magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T18:37:55-08:00","id":1471699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Invisible Entities don't have Aspirations or Obsessions and goetia are arguably the least conceptually flexible of the lot, so probably not. </div> </div> </div> The forge purpose spell doesn't mention anything about needing to have aspirations. In fact it can explicitly force Obsessions onto sleepers (so they gain arcane experience where they normally could not). <br /> <br /> So to extend the question, can you cast forge purpose on anything with a mind? (Spirits, ghosts, vampires, changelings, a true fae?).<br /> <br /> Your counter point about Ochemata actually makes me think the opposite - shared souls/soul shards share a common pool of arcane experience - allowing Ochemata to cast some spells which require this cost.<br /> <br /> Goetic Summons specifically says <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Summoning aspects of one\u2019s own <br /> soul is dangerous, but rewarding </div> </div> </div>Which suggests this is like a non arch-mage version of creating an Ochemata (the Goeta can't cast supernal magic, so it isn't a full shard of your awakened soul... I don't know would making it a soul stone make it any more soul -like...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T19:04:35-08:00","id":1471701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471699#post1471699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which suggests this is like a non arch-mage version of creating an Ochemata (the Goeta can't cast supernal magic, so it isn't a full shard of your awakened soul</div> </div> </div> </div>Without going into too much detail about what the nature of the Astral Realms and Goetia are, Goetia from an Oneiros would be distinct from Ochemata in that they're not really formed from the stuff of the soul so much as constructs of personality traits. Like, they're aspects of the soul insofar as that's where the Oneiros in which they reside is found, but otherwise something like the Goetia of your wrath or your fear of spiders or the bad memory of your disastrous first date are far smaller entities. And it's dangerous because while they're summoned, those traits aren't in your head informing your behaviours.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T19:07:59-08:00","id":1471702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Under the same logic as Golem's conjunctional use of Death or Spirit, yes </div> </div> </div>Reading the Golden spell's conjugational options and <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Ok fine for mind 5 making or death/spirit 4 binding. But it does not suggest allowing the use of goetia as a controlling mind in a Golem at all (and by extension in an Eidolon).<br /> <br /> Is that an overly strict interpretation? And is there a reason Mind 5 is required for both Golem/Eidolon while Spirit/Death 4 is only mentioned for Golems? ( I note mind 5 is the only conjunctional for Create Life to give an animal its own mind - though that doesn't prevent you from binding a spirit/ghost/goetia into an animal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T19:13:53-08:00","id":1471703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471701#post1471701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without going into too much detail about what the nature of the Astral Realms and Goetia are, Goetia from an Oneiros would be distinct from Ochemata in that they're not really formed from the stuff of the soul so much as constructs of personality traits. Like, they're aspects of the soul insofar as that's where the Oneiros in which they reside is found, but otherwise something like the Goetia of your wrath or your fear of spiders or the bad memory of your disastrous first date are far smaller entities. And it's dangerous because while they're summoned, those traits aren't in your head informing your behaviours.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remembering more of that from 1st Ed now. And i presume if you summon a goetia of your virtue it prevents you from using your virtue's mechanical benefits, but is also a more powerful (rank 2?) Goetia?<br /> <br /> Still, doesn't have an awakened soul, so can't do what an Ochemata can do. Can it learn like a Psychic Genesis created mind presumably can (and thus gain beats)? Since both are treated as Goetia, should they both be able to have an Obsession forced into them with Prime Mastery?<br /> <br /> EDIT: and when i say non-archmage version of Ochemata, i mean, this is the closest awakened magic can get, and it doesn't produce something capable of connecting to the supernal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-02-2022, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T19:44:58-08:00","id":1471704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471697#post1471697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To use the example in the book, Eidolon fire (which does not burn) as a fetish object for a spirit of fire (which may gain essence from the usual fire related things and thus might like being in the platonic ideal of fire - and is not bleeding essence at least if i understand the possession rules).<br /> <br /> It might even influence the Eidolon fire to burn things using influence fire.<br /> <br /> It is the 'may imitate entire environments' part of the Eidolon spell i am thinking of. Ok you've got a fairly solid illusion going on, now can it be enhanced by a little spirit magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Eidolon that matches the description of one of a spirit's Influences may safely be considered to match the description of one of a spirit's Influences and thus possess the Resonant Condition for that spirit, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471699#post1471699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The forge purpose spell doesn't mention anything about needing to have aspirations. In fact it can explicitly force Obsessions onto sleepers (so they gain arcane experience where they normally could not).</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsessions grant Beats, grant Mana, penalize rolls from Acts of Hubris, none of which are traits goetia possess, and the effects of Forge Purpose on Sleepers are relevant primarily if they Awaken \u2014 which goetia cannot do, lacking souls or the natural capacity to hold one. The only mechanical impact it would have would be in the unlikely event that somebody tried to use Social Maneuvering on an invisible entity defined by what it represents in a way counter to that Obsession, in which case it puts one more Door in the way, and the goetia (as an NPC) gets a point of Willpower for pursuing the Obsession. That's it. You can accomplish that already with less fuss if you have enough Mind to be messing with goetia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So to extend the question, can you cast forge purpose on anything with a mind? (Spirits, ghosts, vampires, changelings, a true fae?). </div> </div> </div>If it normally tracks Aspirations, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your counter point about Ochemata actually makes me think the opposite - shared souls/soul shards share a common pool of arcane experience - allowing Ochemata to cast some spells which require this cost.<br /> <br /> Goetic Summons specifically says [quotation from the spell] </div> </div> </div>It <i>immediately clarifies what that means</i>, is the thing, and it doesn't mean anything like that, as Levi explains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471702#post1471702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the Golden spell's conjugational options and <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Ok fine for mind 5 making or death/spirit 4 binding. But it does not suggest allowing the use of goetia as a controlling mind in a Golem at all (and by extension in an Eidolon).<br /> <br /> Is that an overly strict interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And is there a reason Mind 5 is required for both Golem/Eidolon while Spirit/Death 4 is only mentioned for Golems? ( I note mind 5 is the only conjunctional for Create Life to give an animal its own mind - though that doesn't prevent you from binding a spirit/ghost/goetia into an animal). </div> </div> </div>The criteria for summoning any sort of goetia are dramatically more stringent than the criteria for summoning any sort of ghost or spirit, whereas with Mind 5 you can just construct a mind without having to pull it out of the Astral and deal with the necessities and consequences of doing so.<br /> <br /> The open development for Signs of Sorcery highlighted the fact that there wasn't space in the corebook to put especially complex spells and applications of conjunctive Arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471703#post1471703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, doesn't have an awakened soul, so can't do what an Ochemata can do. Can it learn like a Psychic Genesis created mind presumably can (and thus gain beats)?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to play a separate character from your mage, you are probably better off doing that instead of trying to bootstrap the system into letting you outsource your Experience gain to an offscreen character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T20:01:52-08:00","id":1471706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471694#post1471694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, some questions about the Eidolon spell (Prime 5 Making). It allows conjunctional Mind 5 (Making) to give it a mind of its own. 1) Would it also be reasonable to allow Goetic summons (Mind 3 Perfecting) to summon a part of one's own soul (possibly your virtue?) and have the Goetic Demon possess the mindless Eidolon (either conjunctionally or as a seperate spell).<br /> <br /> Assuming this is possible, 2) could you also use Forge Purpose (Prime 5 Making) to give the Eidolon/Goetic Demon one of your Obsessions? And essentially leave it to its own devices... (Maybe with some instruction...)<br /> <br /> And 3) what happens when your Goetic Demon returns to the Astral (again assuming you summoned it from your own Oneiros, not somewhere else). Would you be able to integrate its experience and gain any Arcane Experience it might have acquired while embodied.<br /> <br /> Similarly, 4) could you bind a ghost or spirit to an Eidolon (which is essentially an object, so might fit the requirements for making a fetish).<br /> <br /> For a ghost 5) could you make it look like the ghost's original body?<br /> <br /> For a spirit 6) could the Eidolon be a platonic ideal of whatever the spirit is resonant with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to backtrack this entire conversation and ask-<br /> <br /> Asides from being what I probably expect is an idea for an offscreen EXP generator, a concept an in-universe character will never think of, what's the <i>endgame</i> of this questions? What's the intention of this spell combination, what would a mage asking these questions really be trying to do?<br /> <br /> If it is an EXP generator thing, the outcome is that the GM probably twists player hubris against them in some for or fashion and makes it turn out terrible, or probably pulls the player asides and kindly asks them to stop trying to game the game if they'd like to keep playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-03T01:06:00-08:00","id":1471721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471706#post1471706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to backtrack this entire conversation and ask-<br /> <br /> Asides from being what I probably expect is an idea for an offscreen EXP generator, a concept an in-universe character will never think of, what's the <i>endgame</i> of this questions? What's the intention of this spell combination, what would a mage asking these questions really be trying to do?<br /> <br /> If it is an EXP generator thing, the outcome is that the GM probably twists player hubris against them in some for or fashion and makes it turn out terrible, or probably pulls the player asides and kindly asks them to stop trying to game the game if they'd like to keep playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely the players come across an unusual Eidolon which is trying to do something (possibly researching a mystery in a Sanctum or ancient ruins) - the mage who created it having died without reintegrating... And it being rather difficult to understand exactly what they are dealing with or how to negotiate with it. <br /> <br /> I think it would be hard to generate a useful amount of XP with it as a PC. Leaving it in your sanctum to do research while your character goes out to focus on other things seems less useful - as an aside can you use two thoughts, one mind to be in your own body and use possession on another target (possibly an Eidolon) at the same time, to largely do the same thing?<br /> <br /> The point is Eidolon seems rather underwhelming, (fate gets destinies, death/spirit/mind get ephemeral beings, Prime gets ? Truth?) And how do you make this 'Retainer' into something more interesting - and mage do acts of hibrid which may leave interesting mysteries behind for players (to possibly copy, giving them enough rope to hang...).<br /> <br /> In character, it is not &quot;oh i need an offscreen XP generator&quot; it is &quot;i have to do this frakking Consilium meeting/task, when i'd rather not be drawn away from my Obsession, i know I'll leave part of me behind...&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the point of using a Goetia instead of a Psychic Genesis is that Making is hard (not everyone has mastery) and using something which already exists but Weaving or Ruling it is almost always an easier option than pure Making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-03-2022, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-03T07:26:27-08:00","id":1471736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471721#post1471721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is Eidolon seems rather underwhelming, (fate gets destinies, death/spirit/mind get ephemeral beings, Prime gets ? Truth?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eidolon\u2019s are not Truth made manifest, that would be Mana (I think)\u2026 which you can just make with Prime making. And I don\u2019t mean as a Hallow. It wouldn\u2019t be lasting but I think the potential is clear. If you want destiny type stuff, you can give stuff a self sustaining Nimbus and have the same events play out again and again in the same place. Arguably you can even plant the initial seed for a Long Term Nimbus to form and grow. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471721#post1471721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how do you make this 'Retainer' into something more interesting - and mage do acts of hibrid which may leave interesting mysteries behind for players (to possibly copy, giving them enough rope to hang...).</div> </div> </div> </div> Make it completely independent from its creator, as a fusion of their mind and the mind of a rank 5 summoned Supernal being. Have it act as a autonomous store house of occult knowledge with a compulsion to seek out new mysteries to gain more knowledge, and give it the ability through imbuement to cast certain spells like the ability to transfer Mana and use Mage Sight. Heck, make it a Hallow, and veil it so other Mages don\u2019t interfere. If you really need a purpose for this thing, Ivy from the Dresden files is kinda in the same mental space, and acts as bastion for all written knowledge. The Mysterium probably has invested in the creation of such things regularly (kept safe and away from those unworthy to know the secrets the construct holds). If you want this this to be found in some ruin somewhere, have the construct refer to itself as its creator\u2019s child, and state it\u2019s purpose is to preserve it\u2019s creators legacy as more than dusty rotes and faint echos in soul stones. If you really want a weird Mystery, have it have it\u2019s creator\u2019s Legacy, and be able to use it.<br /> (As a side note, is it just me or wouldn\u2019t this be a fun character to play as in a deviant or promethean game? I\u2019d totally play a Eidolon Ivy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-03T10:14:53-08:00","id":1471742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eidolon\u2019s are not Truth made manifest, that would be Mana (I think)\u2026 </div> </div> </div> Not that this has to be Truth, just that truth is something Prime gets...<br /> <br /> And in a sense, a platonic form is the ideal (or True) version of the idea (made manifest from mana) - at least if you are familiar with Plato or where the spell gets its name (and an Eidolon does seem to be an advanced Platonic Form).<br /> <br /> Alternatively you can see it as the closest thing to a sentient spell non-Archmages can create (in that it is made of mana so presumably will seem similar enough to a spell to confuse some less well informed mages). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as a fusion of their mind and the mind of a rank 5 summoned Supernal being </div> </div> </div>Eh, what? I'm sorry lacking in info about Supernal beings, other than assuming they are not able to last for very long (outside of their summoning circle?/Demense/Verge?). What are their motivations? And how would you go about fusing their mind with your own (is that what your sentence means, you suggested it being independent of the creator, how is fusing the creator's mind independent?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-03-2022, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-03T12:12:06-08:00","id":1471745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471742#post1471742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, what? I'm sorry lacking in info about Supernal beings, other than assuming they are not able to last for very long (outside of their summoning circle?/Demense/Verge?). What are their motivations? And how would you go about fusing their mind with your own (is that what your sentence means, you suggested it being independent of the creator, how is fusing the creator's mind independent?)</div> </div> </div> </div> Supernal beings are Symbols made manifest. They don\u2019t have any one motivation, besides having to Challenge anyone who wants their help, and maybe trying not to fall into the Abyss. <br /> <br /> And no, that\u2019s not exactly what I meant. What I was suggesting as a interesting Eidolon was one that was created with fusion of the Knowledge of a Supernal being and a mind used to the Fallen World as it\u2019s mind. Presumably, the Mage involved will use their own mind, since you know, they are present for the spell. But don\u2019t let it just be a copy of the Mage, let it have its own will and wants. A new person. Like a child is based on it\u2019s parents. They might turn out like their parents, or they could be radically different.<br /> <br /> One could go about doing this by summoning a rank 5 Mind/Prime entity and asking for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-03T15:15:40-08:00","id":1471752,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for a mage just turned Archmage to hide his higher power and pass as a non-archmage mage and for a prolonged time (e.g. 3-4 years or so)?<br /> (Considering of course that his new obsessions somehow do not hinder this process, instead even enforcing it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-03T16:15:33-08:00","id":1471754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khalendas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471752#post1471752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for a mage just turned Archmage to hide his higher power and pass as a non-archmage mage and for a prolonged time (e.g. 3-4 years or so)?<br /> (Considering of course that his new obsessions somehow do not hinder this process, instead even enforcing it).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, with ease. With a Veiling of Prime, they can disguise their Nimbus, its strength and their Gnosis level. Since archmages automatically win Clash of Will with anything not equivalent to them or a Rank 6+ being (found in page 252 of the core book), it makes things very convenient for them. They are after all a post-human Gnostic horror, so since their spells cannot be countered or dispelled, even their use of the basic Practices is more powerful. So if a new archmage, for example, decided to send someone back via <i>Corridors of Time</i>, no one short of another archmage would be able to forcefully send the time traveler back. That might give them away, but who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-03-2022, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-03T18:27:42-08:00","id":1471758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471721#post1471721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most likely the players come across an unusual Eidolon which is trying to do something (possibly researching a mystery in a Sanctum or ancient ruins) - the mage who created it having died without reintegrating... And it being rather difficult to understand exactly what they are dealing with or how to negotiate with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's much more about your idea of using goetia than anything to do with Eidolons in particular This is much easier to manage with Life, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it would be hard to generate a useful amount of XP with it as a PC. Leaving it in your sanctum to do research while your character goes out to focus on other things seems less useful - as an aside can you use two thoughts, one mind to be in your own body and use possession on another target (possibly an Eidolon) at the same time, to largely do the same thing? </div> </div> </div>Considering the spell specifies that you're comatose and One Mind Two Thoughts specifies that the actions in question must be Mental or Social, I'd say not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is Eidolon seems rather underwhelming, (fate gets destinies, death/spirit/mind get ephemeral beings, Prime gets ? Truth?) And how do you make this 'Retainer' into something more interesting - and mage do acts of hibrid which may leave interesting mysteries behind for players (to possibly copy, giving them enough rope to hang...). </div> </div> </div>Eidolon lets you make <i>tass with no Mana in it</i> and shape it into <i>sets, actors, and </i><i>special effects</i>, and while being obviously magical is a problem for using magic in public it's incredibly striking as a thing to have floating around a place of power like you can make with the same Arcanum at the same level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In character, it is not &quot;oh i need an offscreen XP generator&quot; it is &quot;i have to do this frakking Consilium meeting/task, when i'd rather not be drawn away from my Obsession, i know I'll leave part of me behind...&quot; </div> </div> </div>Surely the solution there is to send a familiar or use something like Soul Windows or Co-Location to attend via telepresence or trade favors or foist it off on an apprentice instead of going yourself and leaving the interesting work to a manifest Obsession?<br /> <br /> Or, god forbid, taking the hit to your social capital and being late to or absent from your obligations?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: Also the point of using a Goetia instead of a Psychic Genesis is that Making is hard (not everyone has mastery) and using something which already exists but Weaving or Ruling it is almost always an easier option than pure Making. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Not everyone has mastery&quot; kind of falls flat when you're talking about Eidolons, but also: if you're at the level where you can mess with goetia, you're at the level where you can mess with people and animals. Make a raccoon smart enough to understand what it's looking at and give it a photographic memory. Rewire the neighbor kid to want to poke whatever weird shit you're keeping in your basement. Hell, acquire some cameras and magic the lenses.<br /> <br /> This whole thing feels like a billion-dollar answer to a thirty-dollar problem. Balancing pursuit of the Mysteries with other activities is the name of the game, and most characters manage it without needing Gnosis 5 and Astral soul-surgery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T03:51:20-08:00","id":1471771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471754#post1471754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, with ease. With a Veiling of Prime, they can disguise their Nimbus, its strength and their Gnosis level. Since archmages automatically win Clash of Will with anything not equivalent to them or a Rank 6+ being (found in page 252 of the core book), it makes things very convenient for them. They are after all a post-human Gnostic horror, so since their spells cannot be countered or dispelled, even their use of the basic Practices is more powerful. So if a new archmage, for example, decided to send someone back via <i>Corridors of Time</i>, no one short of another archmage would be able to forcefully send the time traveler back. That might give them away, but who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks, thought something like that ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12637-khalendas","name":"Khalendas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T09:39:03-08:00","id":1471783,"title":"","content":"I'll admit that Prime spells as yet published don't seem to have explored much of the angle of it being an Arcanum that engages with Truth, but for the moment I think the ideas of what each Path sees with it in Mage Sight can give some ideas. I've that stands out to me in particular is the Acanthus, and how Prime lets them see the driving purpose and motive of a narrative. I think if that's a thing that can be seen, then it should be valid as a basis for spell effects.<br /> <br /> As for being able to conjure up a Retainer that can be physical and probably easily disguised for most Masters of Prime, I think it's worth considering the full range of tasks a powerful mage might want covered seperately from themselves, and how an Eidolen might have more flexible circumstances to be applied than similar options like a zombie or animated statue. Even for the more simple undertakings that don't require additional Arcana or ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> And if not for oneself, then for somebody else. Masters aren't just advantaged in their own needs, but in what they can provide to incentivise other mages to assist them. Somebody with more prosaic needs might benefit from the Retainer you've conjured from nothing, and then they can act to use their capabilities to cover angles you cannot, or operate in a time and place you currently can't.<br /> <br /> I think such arrangements tend to be how mage hierarchies work in general. In particular, I think the idea that mundane Consilium business being a distraction from high level study of the Mysteries is mostly why the office of Provost exists, although I'd say that generally amounts to them engaging with most of the mundane administrative stuff, saving the Councillors for when important decisions need to be made.<br /> <br /> Although I'd also think that the Obsessions of powerful mages are also the kind of thing that need some larger management anyway. You've got to be conferring with peers and herding the juniors to keep the way clear or implement the large scale projects that answer your questions. Those kinds of projects can also be where you apply your servants of highly variable form conjured from nothing, even when their capabilities are simple. You're a Silver Ladder Obrimos, say, observing the symbols that indicate how the Ladder plays out across a particular society. Numerous Eidolens are called up and strategically placed; their individual tasks are simple, but aimed and coordinated to cause a sequence of events that shakes the society up a bit so you can observe how the Ladder of being and the Lesser Elemental Precepts hold up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T10:11:46-08:00","id":1471785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471783#post1471783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit that Prime spells as yet published don't seem to have explored much of the angle of it being an Arcanum that engages with Truth, but for the moment I think the ideas of what each Path sees with it in Mage Sight can give some ideas. I've that stands out to me in particular is the Acanthus, and how Prime lets them see the driving purpose and motive of a narrative. I think if that's a thing that can be seen, then it should be valid as a basis for spell effects.<br /> <br /> As for being able to conjure up a Retainer that can be physical and probably easily disguised for most Masters of Prime, I think it's worth considering the full range of tasks a powerful mage might want covered seperately from themselves, and how an Eidolen might have more flexible circumstances to be applied than similar options like a zombie or animated statue. Even for the more simple undertakings that don't require additional Arcana or ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> And if not for oneself, then for somebody else. Masters aren't just advantaged in their own needs, but in what they can provide to incentivise other mages to assist them. Somebody with more prosaic needs might benefit from the Retainer you've conjured from nothing, and then they can act to use their capabilities to cover angles you cannot, or operate in a time and place you currently can't.<br /> <br /> I think such arrangements tend to be how mage hierarchies work in general. In particular, I think the idea that mundane Consilium business being a distraction from high level study of the Mysteries is mostly why the office of Provost exists, although I'd say that generally amounts to them engaging with most of the mundane administrative stuff, saving the Councillors for when important decisions need to be made.<br /> <br /> Although I'd also think that the Obsessions of powerful mages are also the kind of thing that need some larger management anyway. You've got to be conferring with peers and herding the juniors to keep the way clear or implement the large scale projects that answer your questions. Those kinds of projects can also be where you apply your servants of highly variable form conjured from nothing, even when their capabilities are simple. You're a Silver Ladder Obrimos, say, observing the symbols that indicate how the Ladder plays out across a particular society. Numerous Eidolens are called up and strategically placed; their individual tasks are simple, but aimed and coordinated to cause a sequence of events that shakes the society up a bit so you can observe how the Ladder of being and the Lesser Elemental Precepts hold up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you meant Fate for the Acanthus example.<br /> <br /> Regarding Prime's purviews of Truth, one thing I theorize is that it would be very effective against anything of the Abyss. Either by making spells that are very effective against its manifestations or that create defenses that allow for a bit more safety when confronting it.<br /> <br /> I think its connection to the soul, as a subtle Arcanum that comprises it, could also be expanded upon. In a simplied overview, Fate has intent and choice, Death has endings and how the soul is attached, Mind has thought and consciousness, Spirit has emotions and instincts. But what role Prime plays in it all is still nebulous at the moment.<br /> <br /> I also believe its purview of revelation would be very interesting to explore. Combined with Fate, for example, would allow a mage to not only know a subject's current intended goals (Aspirations and Obsessions), but also reveal the ones they are working towards without being fully aware, such as the ones they are being manipulated towards (although not by whom) or what is the goal of a Fate/Doom that lies upon them. With Space, it would reveal what goals the subject had when creating those bonds and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-04-2022, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T13:47:10-08:00","id":1471795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eidolon lets you make tass with no Mana in it </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure the spell description explicitly says this is Mana, all mana all the time? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Surely the solution there is to... </div> </div> </div>Yes, zombies or living things or Golem, or indeed familiars, are all things mages with other Arcana can do. <br /> <br /> I'm explicitly asking what can a Prime mage do. Obviously the summon goetia (3 dot spell) added some mind, and could be bound into anything else. But my question boils do to, what makes Prime Mastery interesting (specifically focused on Eidlons, but broader answers are interesting).<br /> <br /> The 'obviously magic' line seems to be (as distinct from zombies/golems/life forms) to require that it create dissonance.<br /> <br /> The 'environment' aspect seems interesting, like some true fae powers to create environments, but i can't seem much use for it. Maybe a staff with eternal Eidolon flame (resonant to a fire spirit) would help, especially if you wanted a fire spirit as a familiar.<br /> <br /> Though honestly, i see making fetishes/spirit familiars as a fun way to do magic without paradox, and 2nd ed - with 1 dice of paradox (for sleeper witness) and 1 mana cost to mitigate it - seems to make overcoming paradox directly much easier.<br /> <br /> EDIT: actually it is the forge purpose spell which is unique to prime mastery... Maybe somehow related to truth, and i dunno, if you have to cast it on already sentient beings (which i presume is a wisdom sin) it seems much less fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-04-2022, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T14:03:21-08:00","id":1471799,"title":"","content":"Aside : mental magic<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering the spell specifies that you're comatose and One Mind Two Thoughts specifies that the actions in question must be Mental or Social, I'd say not </div> </div> </div>Then it might have to be creative thaumatergy'd in at a higher level. Though i will note One Mind, Two Thoughts says 'neither task can be solely physical' - suggesting you can do physical things as part of the task, but in 1st Ed i seem to recall your body was only able to do one thing, so you could allow one entirely physical task while the other mind did something else.<br /> <br /> Getting an effective way to be in two places at once (for a Master of Mind) seems like a great way to mirror the gross/subtle Arcana of the Mastigos, without breaking the game (as they should already be able to pull off similar feats with Space). <br /> <br /> But using possession/psychic projection, while physically able to control your own body would be a little powerful (psychic projection with a Goetic familar possessing your body would work though).<br /> <br /> EDIT: i note +2 reach for two thoughts does allow a physical action, but, oh wait it is clear that this is &quot;Physical&quot; in that it uses physical traits, but it is still Astral, not controlling your body while in the Astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-04-2022, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T14:23:58-08:00","id":1471800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471785#post1471785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you meant Fate for the Acanthus example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arcadian logic is based on free will. Fate and Time are the engines that drive reality, and they follow the decisions of the characters, not the plot of the story. Prime, then, is the imposi\u0002tion of the authorial voice, setting events in motion and fueling the engines. A story where nothing changes is a dull story, and Acanthus see Prime in every breeze through the Mists, in every shoot of moonsilver thorn that sprouts off in an unexpected direction. Prime dictates the terms of the story as surely as Fate dictates the events; it reveals the truths that drive the tale for\u0002ward, clears away the obstacles put in place by enemy mages, and provides the blessed artifact that brings the story to its climax </div> </div> </div>The Thorns show you where things came from and the varied options for where they're going. The Mists show you which things hold significance, the gravity that draw and bend events. It reads to me that Prime can let you observe these phenomena in terms of <i>why</i> they have that direction and importance, of how things begin and what gives them momentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T16:09:41-08:00","id":1471807,"title":"","content":"Ok, actual some question here: <br /> <br /> When would you use a sympathic yantra to gain +2 bonus (ie when not casting at sympathic range)? <br /> <br /> Would it be that any spell you cast in yourself you can use a lock of your hair (and possibly destroy it aswell for a +1 as a sacrament) - assuming you have no other better yantra options? <br /> <br /> It seems odd that the sympathic option works at all when you are in touch range, you have the body itself to apply as the 'who' the spell is targeting, why would you need a material sympathy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T20:56:42-08:00","id":1471823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471795#post1471795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm pretty sure the spell description explicitly says this is Mana, all mana all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an explicit point of difference from Platonic Form that Eidolons do not crumble when they run out of Mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 'obviously magic' line seems to be (as distinct from zombies/golems/life forms) to require that it create dissonance. </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't matter in any circumstance where Sleepers aren't present, as they shouldn't be in places like sancta, Hallows, or demesnes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 'environment' aspect seems interesting, like some true fae powers to create environments, but i can't seem much use for it. Maybe a staff with eternal Eidolon flame (resonant to a fire spirit) would help, especially if you wanted a fire spirit as a familiar. </div> </div> </div>I did not compare the spell's potential outputs to theatrical elements idly \u2014 an Eidolon can be manifested as a structure with physical presence and doesn't need extra Reach to produce complex systems. Its inability to make fire that burns or electricity that can power technology still leaves it with the capacity for harm through pure mechanical force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though honestly, i see making fetishes/spirit familiars as a fun way to do magic without paradox, and 2nd ed - with 1 dice of paradox (for sleeper witness) and 1 mana cost to mitigate it - seems to make overcoming paradox directly much easier. </div> </div> </div>The tradeoff, of course, being Dissonance and the allocation of Reach; instant-casting a spell at the limits of your skill with the Arcana means you're dipping into the unsafe Reach for any Advanced factors or side benefits, and no amount of Mana will make a crowd of Sleepers fail to vibrate an obvious long-term spell apart after a moderate exposure.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that doing so is an Act of Hubris for anyone above Falling Wisdom. You can mitigate that for Inured spells, but\u2026 well, at that point it's stopped being just 1 Mana to mitigate, and there's a pretty strict limit on how many spells you can do this with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471807#post1471807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, actual some question here:<br /> <br /> When would you use a sympathic yantra to gain +2 bonus (ie when not casting at sympathic range)?<br /> <br /> Would it be that any spell you cast in yourself you can use a lock of your hair (and possibly destroy it aswell for a +1 as a sacrament) - assuming you have no other better yantra options?<br /> <br /> It seems odd that the sympathic option works at all when you are in touch range, you have the body itself to apply as the 'who' the spell is targeting, why would you need a material sympathy?</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is a question of why you would use the bonus from a sympathetic Yantra instead of for Sympathetic Range, the answers are:<br /> <br /> \u2022 As long as you haven't destroyed it, you can use it for both the Sympathetic Range Attainment and the dice bonus; the cost is that this requires you to use it as a Yantra twice, just as you would for any other tool that counts as more than one type of Yantra.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Even if you're not using the Attainment, there is an entire middle ground between Touch Range and Sympathetic Range, and the cost of remote casting is different from the cost of the Attainment.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Even at Touch Range, material sympathy functions as a mnemonic for strengthening the spell's Imago just like any other Yantra does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T22:51:40-08:00","id":1471828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 As long as you haven't destroyed it, you can use it for both the Sympathetic Range Attainment and the dice bonus; </div> </div> </div>That is very much not something you can do by the RAW.<br /> <br /> &quot;In order to use a Yantra, a willworker has to recognize a specific symbolism in the tool....The more Yantras she uses \u2014 whether <b>different interpretations </b>of the same tool or different tools altogether \u2014 the more basis she has for her Imago, making it easier to form.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is one interpretation of the sympathic meaning of the item, which can't be used twice in a given spell. If the spell is at sympathetic range using a sympathic yantra gives 0 dice bonus (and takes up one of your yantra slots?) Because in both cases it is being interpreted as symbolising the &quot;who&quot; the spell is targeting.<br /> <br /> Just like you can't use the same path tool twice for the same meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even at Touch Range, material sympathy functions as a mnemonic for strengthening the spell's Imago just like any other Yantra does. </div> </div> </div>In my interpretation, if you are at touch range, it seems you can touch the actual subject and use their own body (or your own body) as a sympathic yantra to itself - for the easiest +2 i can think of.<br /> <br /> At least it makes very little metaphysical sense to me that a piece of the target can work as a yantra but their entire body can't - like why am i focusing on this lock of hair that i just cut when i could be focusing on the actual target i am also touching.<br /> <br /> So in my understanding, it would be really weird to use any sympathic yantra for touch range (as opposed to getting a free +2 yantras for touching them) and you can't get a bonus for using the attainment(s).<br /> <br /> At sensory/remote viewing ranges it makes more sense. But even then. Remote viewing 'live' is a stronger connection than a 'recent recording' - should you should still get an automatic +2 for using it as a sympathic yantra.<br /> <br /> Unless you think the player should be forced to make a hard copy recording of the remotely viewed item and then use it in the spell to get the yantra bonus (and cut a lock of their hair off before casting a touch range healing spell). <br /> <br /> I would end up either going with +2 for every spell that uses the target as a sympathic link to itself or not allowing any dice bonus for sympathic yantras (and only needing sympathic yantras with the attainments).<br /> <br /> The question being is an automatic +2 yantra too good (as it doesn't appear to be what the rules as written suggest), but comparing with the downsides of (say) Runes or Concentration, this seems too easy. It is equivalent to getting a +2 from being in a Demense - which is much harder to acquire and limited in what spells it can be cast with...<br /> <br /> I think my interpretation is too good for what is intended. But still, bring a polaroid camera and (mid-combat) take a photo of the and target and you get a +2 (material sympathy) to target them... And your players should be asking 'why does focusing on this photo of the target provide a better bonus than focusing on the actual target?'<br /> <br /> Using the targets blood as a sympathic attaintment and a +2 sacrement seems much more thematic and in-line with the difficult of acquiring other +2 yantra bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-05-2022, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T23:22:15-08:00","id":1471832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is an explicit point of difference from Platonic Form that Eidolons do not crumble when they run out of Mana. </div> </div> </div>I see, it does say that, it also says &quot;Eidolons are still made of solidified Mana&quot; - it doesn't crumble when it has run out of usable mana, but it is still made of mana.<br /> <br /> So you can make an Eidolon sword with X potency damage bonus and Y mana uses, and once it runs out of mana it become a 0 damage bonus? Improvised weapon? (Unless you spend your own mana to make it work - though that doesn't seem to be allowed for imbued items or fetishes, at least without word of command) <br /> <br /> That might actually be cool, though still somewhat underwhelming. A Retained with a magic sword protecting your sanctum.<br /> <br /> Actually on that, if you put 5 potency in retainer Merit with a field which include 'combat', then the Eidolon gets 10 dice pool for combat. But what does 10 dice for combat actually mean? 1 attack at 0 initiative bonus with a 10 dice pool and 0 defence (is that good?)it seems to be identical to a Golem, but strictly worse than a Zombie retained? (And less numerous, though you have to get actual bodies/statues for those other spells, and Eidolons just require mana...)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, can you use the Platonic Form reach to give your Eidolon tool 8-again (which i presume works for combat, but the wording on tools ba weapons in the spell seems confusing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-05-2022, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T23:25:21-08:00","id":1471833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471828#post1471828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is very much not something you can do by the RAW.<br /> <br /> &quot;In order to use a Yantra, a willworker has to recognize a specific symbolism in the tool....The more Yantras she uses \u2014 whether <b>different interpretations </b>of the same tool or different tools altogether \u2014 the more basis she has for her Imago, making it easier to form.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is one interpretation of the sympathic meaning of the item, which can't be used twice in a given spell. If the spell is at sympathetic range using a sympathic yantra gives 0 dice bonus (and takes up one of your yantra slots?) Because in both cases it is being interpreted as symbolising the &quot;who&quot; the spell is targeting.<br /> <br /> Just like you can't use the same path tool twice for the same meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven\u2019t fully read the discussion, but\u2026 I\u2019m pretty sure Sympathy Yantras by default represent <i>similarity</i>, not <i>proximity</i>. I don\u2019t have the book with me ATM, but I\u2019m pretty sure the Yantras section writes it as <i>Sympathy</i> Yantras and not <i>Sympathetic</i> Yantras, exactly because of this. Thus, two meanings and two Yantras can coexist on one object.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait a sec, just ignore me for a bit \u2014 I need to look up stuff again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-05-2022, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T00:40:23-08:00","id":1471835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471828#post1471828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And your players should be asking 'why does focusing on this photo of the target provide a better bonus than focusing on the actual target?'</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, you <i>always</i> have to focus on the target (except for Sympathetic Casting). The &quot;bonus&quot; you get for that is that you're able to cast a spell on them in the first place.<br /> Touching the target directly also grants you a &quot;bonus&quot;: The spell uses one less Reach than if you had cast at Sensory Range. As such, casting on yourself is already advantageous compared to casting on others.<br /> <br /> As for the +2 bonus; in my experience that's not unbalanced at all. If you prepare for a spell, you'll almost always be able to fill all your Yantra slots with Yantras that grant +2 or more dice anyway. If you're casting during stressed situations, the time pressure will limit the amount of Yantras used, so that you generally have multiple Yantras to choose between for your reflexive Yantra usage (and Mantra for almost all situations where you have time for a second Yantra unless you're packing both Mudra and Persona for this particular spell).<br /> And taking a photo of your opponent (or ally) mid combat means you've spent a turn preparing a Yantra while your enemies may spend that turn attacking or casting spells. If you have another reflexive Yantra to use (such as Persona, Concentration, Mudra, or any of the +1 Yantras), then you also need to spend <i>a second turn</i> using it as a Yantra for whatever spell you're about to cast. It will rarely, if ever, be worth it. And if it's during a niche situation actually worth it, then don't punish that player's ingenuity by removing their bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-05-2022, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T00:55:08-08:00","id":1471836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471828#post1471828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And your players should be asking 'why does focusing on this photo of the target provide a better bonus than focusing on the actual target?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, some of the metaphysics are concerned with the idea that representations of things are equivalent to them.<br /> <br /> I would say it can just be a matter of how even if you're providing the immediate sensory conception of your target's current state by touching them, the slot in the Imago that conceives of what your target is remains easier to form if focused on a smaller symbolic stand in. A photograph shrinks them down to an easier mental image of what the spell is going to target, whereas the actual subject has to be taken in with all its complexities; it relieves no mental space in forming the Imago.<br /> <br /> It would be like asking why you would use a lever to move something when you have perfectly good arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T05:04:58-08:00","id":1471839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471836#post1471836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, some of the metaphysics are concerned with the idea that representations of things are equivalent to them.<br /> <br /> I would say it can just be a matter of how even if you're providing the immediate sensory conception of your target's current state by touching them, the slot in the Imago that conceives of what your target is remains easier to form if focused on a smaller symbolic stand in. A photograph shrinks them down to an easier mental image of what the spell is going to target, whereas the actual subject has to be taken in with all its complexities; it relieves no mental space in forming the Imago.<br /> <br /> It would be like asking why you would use a lever to move something when you have perfectly good arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that description. I can kinda see it like a photo is a fixed representation, rather than the active moving (living breathing) target, so it is easier to focus on.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Aside, it seems that touching gives a connected sympathetic connection (&quot;Two subjects may become <br /> sympathetically linked when they share a strong emotional, <b>physical</b>, or mystical connection.&quot; And &quot;The two subjects are metaphysically one.&quot;)<br /> <br /> But it is even better than connected because touch range is one reach less than sensory, you don't need to spend a mana to activate the attainment and don't lose one potency if you don't know the target's sympathic name (ie withstand for sympathic range).<br /> <br /> Not really a question there. I can't think of any times when it would be relevant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T05:20:28-08:00","id":1471840,"title":"","content":"Quick one on Hung Spell, i think it just clicked in my head - so this is neither conjunctional nor combined.<br /> <br /> &quot;The subject must be a mage&quot; - so it just gives the mage the ability to trap other imagos while hung spell still has duration.<br /> <br /> In combat if you had (say) covering fire your cabal's apprentice of time could cast Hung spell on multiple targets at potency 3 (say) and then the entire cabal could spend 3 rounds of combat casting different spells before releasing them all in a sudden 'NOPE'.<br /> <br /> Or you could precast healing on connected targets (your cabal mates) and then end the hung spell to dish out a sudden boost to your side (even though you're not touching anymore...) - limited by the fact that all of the hung spells go off at once, so you can't only heal one injured person, it is all or nothing.<br /> <br /> Is that right? And can you combine multiple hung spell casting (with one potency each) to reduce spell control needs of the time apprentice? Or combine the hung spell and spell you trap in it (if casting on yourself)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T08:53:59-08:00","id":1471845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471832#post1471832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see, it does say that, it also says &quot;Eidolons are still made of solidified Mana&quot; - it doesn't crumble when it has run out of usable mana, but it is still made of mana.<br /> <br /> So you can make an Eidolon sword with X potency damage bonus and Y mana uses, and once it runs out of mana it become a 0 damage bonus? Improvised weapon? (Unless you spend your own mana to make it work - though that doesn't seem to be allowed for imbued items or fetishes, at least without word of command)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it drops to whatever damage the sword would normally have if it was a normal sword. It\u2019s still a sword. Just not Mana empowered at that moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471832#post1471832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might actually be cool, though still somewhat underwhelming. A Retained with a magic sword protecting your sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div> A retainer who doesn\u2019t need to eat or sleep, is absolutely loyal, who you effectively have Matter/Life 5 for, and is equivalent to one of the best mortals in their field. That field includes running, jumping, and people punching. And aiming, and firing a gun. (Depending on how you interpret \u201ccombat\u201d)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471832#post1471832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually on that, if you put 5 potency in retainer Merit with a field which include 'combat', then the Eidolon gets 10 dice pool for combat. But what does 10 dice for combat actually mean? 1 attack at 0 initiative bonus with a 10 dice pool and 0 defence (is that good?)it seems to be identical to a Golem, but strictly worse than a Zombie retained? (And less numerous, though you have to get actual bodies/statues for those other spells, and Eidolons just require mana...)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, can you use the Platonic Form reach to give your Eidolon tool 8-again (which i presume works for combat, but the wording on tools ba weapons in the spell seems confusing.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Remember that the Primary factor is Potency, so it easily gets retainer 5 unless you put all of the potency elsewhere. 10 dice means on average you get 3 successes. This also happens to be nearly the maximum possible base dice pool for Sleeper characters. (Max is 12 with a specialty and a merit, and only applies when using that specialty. Otherwise 10 is the max base dice pool for Sleepers.) I believe the Eidolon would have initiative equal to 10 or 5, it just wouldn\u2019t do anything until it was told to. Most characters only get one attack, so that\u2019s not particularly different from anyone else to matter. The 0 defense isn\u2019t good, but that represents the Eidolon not knowing to defend itself. Defense is normally only relevant to melee attacks. This means you have to rely on Durability and Structure as your primary defense. This can be high, if you put the potency into it. As for strictly worse than zombies, well that\u2019s a matter of perspective. Zombies are gross, and unsanitary. They also aren\u2019t exactly subtle either, especially after a few days, meaning you have to go through extra steps to hide what they are if you intend to go out in public with them. Corpses tend be rarer too, excepting certain circumstances. Golems are generally tougher than Zombies and Eidolons (depending on what they are made of), but way worse in subtlety as more durable materials tend to be heavier, and while someone might mistake a zombie for a living, if very ill, person if they don\u2019t look closely and stay at a distance, very few people are made of concrete. Golems can totally hide as statue though. While Matter in general is easy to come by, the best materials will take some time to acquire. Eidolon is pretty similar to Golem, as you noted, but is more fragile on average. However, Eidolon is best for for convenience and subtly as it can make anything that looks realistic enough for nobody to notice anything odd (with the Forces add on anyways.) Mana is cheap to a Master of Prime, as you can literally make more.<br /> <br /> All of that is just the base Eidolon though. The real power is having something you can buff. If you just use the rest of Prime, you can: Imbue the Eidolon with any spell you like, have it generate more Mana everyday, be able to see and interact with all forms of Twilight entities, have a higher dice pool by manipulating your nimbus on it, heal it, just normally increase it\u2019s dice pool, and so on. Arguably, you can even give the Eidolon the rote quality on potency actions for 2 reach and another mana. Or give the weapon rote quality. Other arcanum only increase your options. Heck, with Forces 3, you can totally make a 5 damage weapon plus assigned potency weapon, that is weaved with Regular or Perfected Fire to do even more damage as a side. It may use Mana per use, but with that much damage, you don\u2019t need to swing often. And you can make it produce Mana everyday.<br /> <br /> Edit: Grammar, and a weapon is a tool meant to be used to hurt someone. 8-again definitely applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-05-2022, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T09:14:30-08:00","id":1471846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471840#post1471840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In combat if you had (say) covering fire your cabal's apprentice of time could cast Hung spell on multiple targets at potency 3 (say) and then the entire cabal could spend 3 rounds of combat casting different spells before releasing them all in a sudden 'NOPE'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if these spells are being cast with only their reflexive Yantras, it may be their effects are weak. It's also a bit costly in Mana. It's a thing you could do, but I don't really see the advantage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could precast healing on connected targets (your cabal mates) and then end the hung spell to dish out a sudden boost to your side (even though you're not touching anymore...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Without being told how range works with Hung Spell, I'm inclined to think it leans towards requiring the appropriate range at the time the actual effect goes off; you can cast at Touch range in the absence of the target, but need contact or to throw the spell at the moment the suspension is ended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">limited by the fact that all of the hung spells go off at once, so you can't only heal one injured person, it is all or nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so. Awakened healing magic is fairly powerful, once you get the dots to acquire it; for Reach, a Disciple of Life can restore 3 Lethal by default, while the Adept can fix 8 (or 4 Aggravated; it costs Reach and Mana, but most get basically no acceleration on aggravated damage at all). I think it doesn't generally need to be Hung; maybe if one is worried about an overwhelming surprise attack.<br /> <br /> I'll think about the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T10:21:11-08:00","id":1471849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well if these spells are being cast with only their reflexive Yantras, it may be their effects are weak. It's also a bit costly in Mana. It's a thing you could do, but I don't really see the advantage. </div> </div> </div> Cool, my question was really about do i understand how the spell works, so glad to hear my understanding isn't completely off, and yeah the disadvantages are just that, if there is a tactical advantage to be had from loosing 3 spells at once, that is really down to the specifics of the situation and spells you hung. But the principle stands (more likely to leave a conditional trap on your sanctum... Maybe ban entry and as a second level defence if the ban is broken a hung quanentine of space is cast Unmaking the sanctum's connection to the rest of the world...) I think it is the one 1st Ed thing which didn't become an attainment. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without being told how range works with Hung Spell, I'm inclined to think it leans towards requiring the appropriate range at the time the actual effect goes off; you can cast at Touch range in the absence of the target, but need contact or to throw the spell at the moment the suspension is ended. </div> </div> </div> This one is harder - like the conversation about area of effect and what happens to my room full of zombies if they leave the room.<br /> <br /> But i think as written, you are hanging a spell not the imago for a spell. And rolling the dice for paradox and everything else (spending the mana and incorporating the hanging of the spell into the imago).<br /> <br /> I think allowing targets to be chosen at time of release is more broken. Like say you cast at sensory range on 'the area 5 meters in front of me', and then it hits whatever happens to be in front of you at that time... <br /> <br /> I think you have to encode the actual targets/range/spell factors at first. So maybe you're right and the spell fizzles if you're not touching the subject again (without sensory range). I just don't intuit that this is how magic works (it doesn't care where the target is because space is an illusion, unless it has changed dramatically and the temporal sympathy means that target no longer exists - maybe the cabal mate is already dead, so life magic can't heal them?). <br /> <br /> But being based on temporal sympathy makes more sense to me given that this is a time effect.<br /> <br /> And yes, maybe healing isn't the best use of hung spells, maybe you want a conditional incognito presence with high potency (+target the whole canal) so you can disengage from a fight if things go wrong.<br /> <br /> But again, the principle of 'hung spells work like this' is the essence of my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-05-2022, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-05T15:28:49-08:00","id":1471868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471828#post1471828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is very much not something you can do by the RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have pointed out, this is founded on the flawed assumption that being able to target a subject is the same interpretation of the Yantra as the one that allows a scaling benefit to your ability to conceptualize a spell. If you don't think a Sympathy Yantra should be usable for its bonus and the Attainment at the same time, you shouldn't be able to use the presence of the target as a Sympathy Yantra for itself, because the target's presence is what is allowing you to cast the spell rather than simply making it easier for you.<br /> <br /> Using a Sympathy Yantra for both its bonus and the Attainment takes up two Yantras, one of which specifically doesn't grant any bonus due to allowing an extension of the spell's range at reduced Reach. A Yantra with material sympathy to its intended subject is often something that has a sympathetic connection to the target that you can use Borrow Threads on to further circumvent Sympathetic Withstand, but that in turn puts another spell on your Spell Control load, which increases the chances that you'll overReach even with the shift in cost from Sympathetic Range.<br /> <br /> Sympathetic magic is a preparation-intensive process to use effectively, and much of that preparation relies on blurring the line between map and territory. That doesn't really work if you're trying to use the territory in place of a map.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T03:48:02-08:00","id":1471920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471868#post1471868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As others have pointed out, this is founded on the flawed assumption that being able to target a subject is the same interpretation of the Yantra as the one that allows a scaling benefit to your ability to conceptualize a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont know exactly what you are getting at, but i can see how one Yantra could have symbolic meaning to multiple things<br /> <br /> &quot;Rather than defining the \u201cwhat\u201d of a spell, sympathetic tools define the \u201cwho\u201d \u2014 the person, place, creature, or institution upon which the mage forces her will.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the spell will usually only be targeting one of these. Like maybe a work is badge could represent the person (or at least their work persona) and the institution... But you're not targeting both - so again, what 'different interpretations' are there for a tool to allow it he used as a second Yantra. <br /> <br /> You either use it to represent the subject to cast using sympathic range, OR to represent the subject 0-2 dice bonus (though you'd always he better off using anything else as a Yantra than the +0 Sympathy, it is only useful for use with an attainment). <br /> <br /> It is very clear for these attainments you &quot;must use a sympathetic Yantra&quot;<br /> <br /> And four paragraphs earlier where it defines sympathetic Yantra that they represent the &quot;who&quot; aka the subject.<br /> <br /> Being able to target is an extra ability granted by the attainment which just happens to require the use of a Yantra slot while giving no bonus.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If the rest of your argument was 'sympathetic magic is hard, so giving them a +2 bonus is only fair' - honestly getting a +2 yantra bonus isn't that difficult, just using a high speech Marta... Or some runes or a good sacrement (and a material sympathy is probably a good sacrement for most harmful spells...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't think a Sympathy Yantra should be usable for its bonus and the Attainment at the same time<br /> <br /> you shouldn't be able to use the presence of the target as a Sympathy Yantra for itself, because the target's presence is what is allowing you to cast the spell rather than simply making it easier for you </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying the presence of the target uses up a Yantra slot, it doesn't, but we both seem to agree that the sympathy attainments do use up a Yantra slot, and since you can't use the same yantra twice you've already used that meaning.<br /> <br /> Unless the attainment was only for targeting without taking up the Yantra slot, which would make it closer to sensory range.<br /> <br /> Basically the attainments say 'must use a sympathy yantra', sensory range only requires the reach for advanced range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-06-2022, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T05:43:49-08:00","id":1471926,"title":"","content":"New Question: can you have multiple Shadow names? (Buying the merit more than once?)<br /> <br /> I know Guardians can buy new merit if they have 5 dots in the Masque merit (immersion). But I'm wondering if you can create multiple magical identities for general use (in magical society and for persona yantras).<br /> <br /> And while I'm thinking of shadow name, in the chapter on storytelling it mentions <br /> <br /> 'To bring the Supernal down, through the Nimbus, and change the Fallen World, grounding is necessary. A grounded self, no longer adrift in the mess of the Fallen World, is necessary to do magic.'<br /> <br /> And 'It is possible to control a Shadow Name, over time... but the more famous the name, the more gravity attached to its meaning, the harder that feat is.'<br /> <br /> This seems to suggest the common collective human concept associated with your shadow name is important, and helps ground your magic in the fallen world.<br /> <br /> So presumably going to the astral and doing things to the representation of a mage's shadow name could change the symbology? (Possibly with great difficult, especially for ideas which many humans believe in cf: consensusal reality from Ascension).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T06:11:43-08:00","id":1471928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471920#post1471920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: If the rest of your argument was 'sympathetic magic is hard, so giving them a +2 bonus is only fair' - honestly getting a +2 yantra bonus isn't that difficult, just using a high speech Marta... Or some runes or a good sacrement (and a material sympathy is probably a good sacrement for most harmful spells...).</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument is that nothing particularly breaks from allowing a sympathetic Yantra to be used for its bonus and to target the Attainment, given that doing so requires using it as two Yantras \u2014 the specific bonus of +2 is irrelevant to the fact that Sympathetic Range already negates one bonus you could use targeting the spell without adding Sympathetic Withstand to the equation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T07:10:27-08:00","id":1471934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471868#post1471868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As others have pointed out, this is founded on the flawed assumption that being able to target a subject is the same interpretation of the Yantra as the one that allows a scaling benefit to your ability to conceptualize a spell. If you don't think a Sympathy Yantra should be usable for its bonus and the Attainment at the same time, you shouldn't be able to use the presence of the target as a Sympathy Yantra for itself, because the target's presence is what is allowing you to cast the spell rather than simply making it easier for you.<br /> <br /> Using a Sympathy Yantra for both its bonus and the Attainment takes up two Yantras, one of which specifically doesn't grant any bonus due to allowing an extension of the spell's range at reduced Reach. A Yantra with material sympathy to its intended subject is often something that has a sympathetic connection to the target that you can use Borrow Threads on to further circumvent Sympathetic Withstand, but that in turn puts another spell on your Spell Control load, which increases the chances that you'll overReach even with the shift in cost from Sympathetic Range.<br /> <br /> Sympathetic magic is a preparation-intensive process to use effectively, and much of that preparation relies on blurring the line between map and territory. That doesn't really work if you're trying to use the territory in place of a map.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book isn't exactly clear about what it means by &quot;different interpretations of the same tool&quot; so I can't say that your interpretation of gaining different bonuses counts as different uses is definitely wrong. However, I think it's much more reasonable to assume that it's the <i>symbolism</i> you draw from that can't be the same for multiple uses as a Yantra. Regardless of whether you use a Sympathy Yantra to gain bonus dice or to use the Sympathetic Range Attainment, the symbolism is the connection between the object and the subject, meaning you'd interpret the same symbolism from the object in both cases. I'm fairly confident that's the intended reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T08:24:54-08:00","id":1471939,"title":"","content":"There is nothing stopping you using two seperate yantras (blood and hair, say) in two yantra slots to give +2 each right**?<br /> <br /> So you could use a symbolic sympathy* (already a +0) for the attainment and a material sympathy (+2) for another yantra slot (and take the sympathic connection from the stronger one, i presume)<br /> <br /> *Maybe require the player to succeed in a craft art roll to make a drawing/caricature.<br /> <br /> **EDIT: had another look at this, and there seems to be no reason you can't do this according to RAW. But you could decide to run it that each Yantra needs to provide a different Symbolism, like a sentence eg: I (persona) of the Adamantine Arrows (Order tool) call upon the powers of Stygia (Verge, Demense, environment? path tools) to fray/rule/etc (sacrement/rod/etc) the subject (sympathy). Where you are only allowed to represent each part of the sentence with one Yantra.<br /> <br /> With (Runes/Concentration/Mantra) simply being repeating the sentence... <br /> <br /> EDIT2: infact i'd imagine this is kind of how you could describe the process of creating a rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-06-2022, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T10:12:58-08:00","id":1471940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471926#post1471926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Question: can you have multiple Shadow names? (Buying the merit more than once?)<br /> <br /> I know Guardians can buy new merit if they have 5 dots in the Masque merit (immersion). But I'm wondering if you can create multiple magical identities for general use (in magical society and for persona yantras).<br /> <br /> And while I'm thinking of shadow name, in the chapter on storytelling it mentions<br /> <br /> 'To bring the Supernal down, through the Nimbus, and change the Fallen World, grounding is necessary. A grounded self, no longer adrift in the mess of the Fallen World, is necessary to do magic.'<br /> <br /> And 'It is possible to control a Shadow Name, over time... but the more famous the name, the more gravity attached to its meaning, the harder that feat is.'<br /> <br /> This seems to suggest the common collective human concept associated with your shadow name is important, and helps ground your magic in the fallen world.<br /> <br /> So presumably going to the astral and doing things to the representation of a mage's shadow name could change the symbology? (Possibly with great difficult, especially for ideas which many humans believe in cf: consensusal reality from Ascension).</div> </div> </div> </div>This in itself makes me wonder how mages go about creating completely new Shadow Names. Its possible that building a Shadow Name from scratch is more difficult than using or reinterpreting a well known one, or one of its aspects. Should a mage use the name Ahura Mazda, for example, he would theoretically have access to all the 101 titles that come with it. But it would take considerable skill to manage that and the &quot;supernatural gravity&quot; (Long Term Nimbus) exerted by it could also be challenging to face. Taking on only the title/aspect of &quot;The Undefeated / Undistressed&quot; would allow the mage to have a more focused and predictable, if narrower set of symbolism to handle. Its certainly far easier than trying to wholesale redefine its meaning in the collective unconscious, a herculean task at the best of times.<br /> <br /> Building a Shadow Name and its symbolism from scratch allows the mage to more clearly define themselves on their own terms, but probably requires more forethought and work to do.<br /> <br /> In regards to obtaining multiple ones, page 92 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> states that the Shadow Name informs the Nimbus of the symbols that resonate for the mage alone. A carefully chosen and well understood one should provide all the yantras and occlusion benefits they could need. Given all that, plus the more detailed information on their nature presented in page 292 of the core book, I don't believe purchasing the merit multiple times is possible.<br /> <br /> Altering the Shadow Name, however, is very doable. It would probably require a Patterning of Space and Prime, like a lesser and more quick acting version of the <i>Unnaming</i> spell. Another option is to utilize <i>Rewrite History</i> to redefine the Shadow Name or repurpose another merit into it. Lastly, in much the same way that it can overwrite Aspirations and Obsessions, its arguable that <i>Forge Destiny</i> could redefine the symbolism of an existing Shadow Name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-06-2022, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T12:29:05-08:00","id":1471948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its possible that building a Shadow Name from scratch is more difficult than using or reinterpreting a well known one, or one of its aspects. </div> </div> </div> I would assume the opposite - as there is no momentum to push against, it should be easy to create a new shadow name from scratch - but it would hold less metaphysical weight and thus be valid only for 1 dot of shadow name merit... Whereas it should be easier to research Odin, and build up your persona to match his (possibly requiring a trip to the Astral to talk to Odin?) And thus easier to get a 3 dot shadow name (as you have a map to show you the way...).<br /> <br /> EDIT: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a Patterning of Space and Prime, like a lesser and more quick acting version of the Unnaming spell </div> </div> </div>What spell? All i can find is cut the threads with reach to remove a sympathic name (or the making to give a new sympathic name).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-06-2022, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T14:17:37-08:00","id":1471950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471948#post1471948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What spell? All i can find is cut the threads with reach to remove a sympathic name (or the making to give a new sympathic name).</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be found on page 94 of<i> Signs of Sorcery</i>, which overall is an incredible supplement that expands upon the metaphysics and mechanics, all the while presenting a lot of fascinating spells (the art is amazing as well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-06-2022, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T03:33:13-08:00","id":1471992,"title":"","content":"I'd address other points when I have a bit more ease, but I can start with a more direct one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1471948#post1471948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would assume the opposite - as there is no momentum to push against, it should be easy to create a new shadow name from scratch - but it would hold less metaphysical weight and thus be valid only for 1 dot of shadow name merit... Whereas it should be easier to research Odin, and build up your persona to match his (possibly requiring a trip to the Astral to talk to Odin?) And thus easier to get a 3 dot shadow name (as you have a map to show you the way...).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the first principle with the Shadow Name Merit is that it should not mandate what name you take on from how much of a bonus you want to get.<br /> <br /> When I think about Shadow Names and the Merit, I often think of the illustration accompanying the Carnival Melancholy Legacy, that guy's costuming and posture. It makes me think about how the extent of the Merit doesn't really need to be based on the depth of the symbols so much as in how much one commits to the persona while functioning as a mage.<br /> <br /> An Astral sojourn seems fairly unnecessary to knowing the motifs and traits you'd need to act according to a name &quot;Odin&quot;, the real challenge is more in how much you can immerse yourself in the act, which might well be more a case of not finding your dignity compromised and getting the proper sort of costume. Likewise, that Legacy member just needs to go hard into the right clothes, the right showy attitude, and a name that sounds like a stereotypical quack doctor, and he can readily get the +3 Yantra for spells arising from connotations of being a flamboyant con man.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Should also be kept in mind that a Shadow Name doesn't need to be a proper name. If a person names himself Solemn, his persona can be based on elements of being grave and quietly respectful. If he goes by Damascus based on the symbolism of the special and rare kind of steel, then it allows a persona following symbols of a kind of refinement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-07-2022, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T11:11:26-08:00","id":1472009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the first principle with the Shadow Name Merit is that it should not mandate what name you take on from how much of a bonus you want to get </div> </div> </div>My thinking was that a newly awakened mage would start with no shadow name.<br /> Then upon being introduced to the concept and adopt some minor trappings purchase 1 dot in the merit, and over time be able to develop their magical identity.<br /> <br /> And that i agree it should not matter what name you take, but how you develop that name could depend on the symbols already associated with the name.<br /> for example: Odin having a significant astral presence in the shared humanity bit, it would be easier to develop a persona - because there is a map for it, but harder to change the symbols...<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the opposite being the case for some name which holds much less significance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T11:48:09-08:00","id":1472014,"title":"","content":"Two questions:<br /> Abyssal entities, Gulmoth (spirit) and Acamoth (goetia) - i think Gulmoths enter the fallen world when you paradox enough or through a supernal verge, but if you do a supernal summoning is it still a Gulmoth or is there an Abyssal entity which operates on mana instead of essence (like a supernal being)?<br /> <br /> Or are abbysal entities inherent harmed by the supernal (as they are entities of non-existence, and Supernal is Truth, the truth of their existence is they shouldn't...)<br /> <br /> --<br /> It seems like imbued items work by creating an imago and embedding it in an item - which can then be cast repeatedly (with flexible subjects but spell factors are only flexible if the mage who created the items has maintained control*) for at least 1 mana - is there amount of mana in the item the limit in the number of 'charges' the imbued item has? Or can the caster (assuming they are a mage) spend their own mana to activate (ie without first channel mana into the item). If the imago is fixed what spell factors do you use? Is the reach set even if it is within the casting mage's spell control.<br /> <br /> If released from the mages spell control does this allow the casting of spells without anyone having spell control, and do they suffer from unsafely relinquished spell?<br /> <br /> If unrelinquished but the mage creator then dies without spending willpower to relinquish, does it remain (possible as an anchor for a ghost mage) with the imago but always cast spells as if they are unsafely relinquished?<br /> <br /> <br /> What spell factors do you use it the spell has been relinquished?<br /> <br /> I presume no Yantras can be used - the activation roll (Gnosis + spell arcanum) doesn't seem to be a spell casting roll - this would any spell factors would penalised the dice pool significantly, right (and free reach seems like it should be based on the creators arcanum rating, not the user's ie if they embedded an overreaching spell in the first place it will always risk paradox but with user's Gnosis).<br /> <br /> Or am I misreading this and it is a spell casting roll, which just happens to use the imbued item's arcanum and Imago to allow the user cast a spell which they wouldn't otherwise be able to cast?<br /> <br /> Lastly can it be a rote/praxis?<br /> <br /> *I just realised this is a lovely way to have more spell control. Though Prime 4 is expensive, I'm thinking of multiple pocket dimensions created and linked to each other, but only requiring 1 spell control slot; lack of indefinite duration would still suck...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T14:27:50-08:00","id":1472022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472009#post1472009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My thinking was that a newly awakened mage would start with no shadow name.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Then upon being introduced to the concept and adopt some minor trappings purchase 1 dot in the merit, and over time be able to develop their magical identity.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think this is approaching the mechanics a bit too much in terms of existing literally within the setting. While it's likely that the kind of person with a three-dot Shadow Name needs to develop it over time, the dot rating is generally there for the benefit of representing characters who have been Awakened for a while.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">for example: Odin having a significant astral presence in the shared humanity bit, it would be easier to develop a persona - because there is a map for it, but harder to change the symbols..</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I guess that's technically correct, but I find it an odd way to put it</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. Things that show up prominently in the Temenos are there because of how prominent they are in a culture, and I think that origin point among people is the thing to focus upon.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And I think mythic imagery as a basis for Shadow Names and other magic goes beyond the kind of cultural significance that places things in the Temenos.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions:<br /> Abyssal entities, Gulmoth (spirit) and Acamoth (goetia) - i think Gulmoths enter the fallen world when you paradox enough or through a supernal verge, but if you do a supernal summoning is it still a Gulmoth or is there an Abyssal entity which operates on mana instead of essence (like a supernal being)?</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, Abyssal things can be called by powerful Anomaly Paradoxes or enter through Abyssal Verges, but can also come through under their own circumstances, and might well do so more often than those other options. Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss talks about how things can slip in.<br /> <br /> For botched Supernal Summoning, I'd say you just get a straightforward Abyssal being (to the extent that they're ever straightforwards).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like imbued items work by creating an imago and embedding it in an item - which can then be cast repeatedly (with flexible subjects but spell factors are only flexible if the mage who created the items has maintained control*)</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note, Signs of Sorcery depicts mages as still arguing about how exactly imbued magic works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">for at least 1 mana - is there amount of mana in the item the limit in the number of 'charges' the imbued item has? Or can the caster (assuming they are a mage) spend their own mana to activate (ie without first channel mana into the item).</div> </div> </div> </div>Signs clarifies that an Awakened user can choose to spend their own Mana to activate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the imago is fixed what spell factors do you use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the imago question, users can decide on factors when activating. There's no option to use Yantras to get those dice back, although I presume that when casting with Ritual time the option remains to lengthen the casting for bonus dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the reach set even if it is within the casting mage's spell control.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation of items is that they aren't concerned with spell control limits. Apart from that, the creator decides on appropriate Reach when the item is made; by default, it only has as much as they assign to provide advanced factors or empowered effects, even if that places it high enough to risk Paradox. They can choose to allow for flexible Reach in exchange for making imbuing require more successes, but that only lets the user switch off some Reach benefits rather than adding them, and it doesn't reduce Paradox risks.<br /> <br /> Since I think of items as not having spell control limits, I think relinquising the spells they cast is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">this would any spell factors would penalised the dice pool significantly, right</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> <br /> My take on imbued items is that they provide the benefit of allowing mages who couldn't otherwise cast a spell do so, as well as letting the item cast its small number of spells frequently, at the cost of being much less flexible in terms of how much you can Reach with them or improve their factors. This would tend to mean that an item ends up requiring more surgical use.<br /> <br /> It also helps to distinguish them a bit from Artifacts; having their own Gnosis rating, it can be possible for them to have dice pools greater than what the user would get from their own Gnosis, carrying the potential to further improve factors. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly can it be a rote/praxis?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T14:30:20-08:00","id":1472023,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to to make a bold assumption and guess that you do not have Signs of Sorcery. The majority of your questions are answered on pg 67 which is titled: Imbued Items: Rules Clarification. SoS is very nice if you like magic items of all kinds, including my previous posts mention of Perfected Materials. You should acquire it if you can.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like imbued items work by creating an imago and embedding it in an item</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much. I come from a d&amp;d background so I like to think of it as adding a \u201cof\u201d to the item\u2019s pattern. Like eyeliner of true sight. Or the classic wand of fireballs. Oh and the definition of item can be stretched with the proper arcanum, you can imbue people with Life and Prime for example. Or Spaces with Space and Prime.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- which can then be cast repeatedly (with flexible subjects but spell factors are only flexible if the mage who created the items has maintained control*) for at least 1 mana</div> </div> </div> </div> Mostly correct, but you can double the require success to make the reach flexible for everyone, including after relinquishing it. In the circumstance where you didn\u2019t do that, only<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- is there amount of mana in the item the limit in the number of 'charges' the imbued item has?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, it defaults to having capacity of one mana. You can increase this with 2 successes per extra mana capacity.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or can the caster (assuming they are a mage) spend their own mana to activate (ie without first channel mana into the item).</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. It\u2019s a choice to do so when casting. I\u2019m sure you can alter the process with a Prime spell to exclude this option if you want.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the imago is fixed what spell factors do you use?</div> </div> </div> </div> Who says it\u2019s fixed? The next page (pg 68) goes into in theories on how the process of imbuing something works. Apparently even Mages don\u2019t all agree. The spell factors are whatever you want when casting. Since the spell casting pool changes from user to user, it doesn\u2019t make sense for the spell factors to be fixed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the reach set even if it is within the casting mage's spell control.</div> </div> </div> </div> The reach is set to anyone else using it, unless it\u2019s creator made it to have flexible reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If released from the mages spell control does this allow the casting of spells without anyone having spell control,</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and do they suffer from unsafely relinquished spell?</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess that depends on how the Mage relinquishes the imbued item.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If unrelinquished but the mage creator then dies without spending willpower to relinquish, does it remain (possible as an anchor for a ghost mage) with the imago but always cast spells as if they are unsafely relinquished?</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm\u2026sure? It automatically unsafely relinquishes upon death anyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What spell factors do you use it the spell has been relinquished?</div> </div> </div> </div> Whatever ones you want when you cast, as above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume no Yantras can be used</div> </div> </div> </div> Correct by default, but that can probably be fixed with some Prime if you want.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- the activation roll (Gnosis + spell arcanum) doesn't seem to be a spell casting roll</div> </div> </div> </div> Incorrect. It absolutely is.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- this would any spell factors would penalised the dice pool significantly, right</div> </div> </div> </div> What? I\u2019m sorry, I\u2019m am afraid I don\u2019t understand this part.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and free reach seems like it should be based on the creators arcanum rating, not the user's ie if they embedded an overreaching spell in the first place it will always risk paradox but with user's Gnosis).</div> </div> </div> </div> Completely correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or am I misreading this and it is a spell casting roll, which just happens to use the imbued item's arcanum and Imago to allow the user cast a spell which they wouldn't otherwise be able to cast?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly can it be a rote/praxis?</div> </div> </div> </div> No. A Rote uses a special type of Yantra and Praxis rely on a special and unique understanding of the spell. Use Prime for 8-9 again/ rote quality if you want it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472014#post1472014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*I just realised this is a lovely way to have more spell control. Though Prime 4 is expensive, I'm thinking of multiple pocket dimensions created and linked to each other, but only requiring 1 spell control slot; lack of indefinite duration would still suck...</div> </div> </div> </div> This is the secondary use of Imbued Items, yeah. Expense is subjective, but I will say that Prime both pays for itself and is a worthy secondary arcanum for any mage. As for the pocket dimensions, why would you lack Indefinite Duration? You can just reach for it, the primary spell factor already covers the dice penalty for duration, leaving the rest of the dice pool for scale. That\u2019s just one overreach, and another if you just have to have the biggest pocket dimension possible. Just be ready to pay the mana cost and/or accept that some of your pocket dimensions might come out \u2026 funny.<br /> <br /> Edit: Maybe I should start double checking if people have already answered the question while I write my answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-07-2022, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T15:36:26-08:00","id":1472026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . As for the pocket dimensions, why would you lack Indefinite Duration? </div> </div> </div>Correct, I don't have Signs.<br /> <br /> The attainment in the core book explicitly says the imbued spell may not have indefinite duration (while the imbuing of the spell is lasting). <br /> <br /> So you can have glasses of darkvision, which are activated whenever you put them on (costing 1 mana) and which last for a day (any duration which isn't indefinite).<br /> <br /> Then you spend 1 more mana to repeat the spell. But you can also take them off and give them to someone else to activate darkvision for that character... Also paying the mana and lasting the day.<br /> <br /> Taking off the imbued items doesn't automatically cancel the spell (it is unclear if spells can have deactivation options similar to the activation rules, I'm guessing they should if the creator decided).<br /> <br /> Obviously if these we're indefinite spells, you could use one imbued item to cast the same indefinite buff on everyone in the Consilium, and then sell the imbued item, or put it away... forcing the items to pay 1 mana for the spell every single time and not be indefinite balances things up a little (it becomes a 1 mana/duration/spell upkeep cost, rather than 1 mana forced and no upkeep).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess that depends on how the Mage relinquishes the imbued item </div> </div> </div>Of course, the relinquish is done by the creator.<br /> <br /> It takes one spell slot from the creator until it is relinquished (no matter how many times the spell is cast). And then it can be relinquished safely or unsafely and takes 0 spell slots (or the imbued item has a spell slot - kinda like a flag bearer)<br /> <br /> So basically you have no yantras, maybe spell factors, set reach, user's Gnosis* plus the Spell's Arcanum rating (optional on reducing the reach but still paradoxes).<br /> <br /> I am presuming the subject of the spell can't be locked, so in the glasses of darkvision example it doesn't automatically target the user, but if it is at touch range and the activation trigger is putting the glasses in your head, then it is pretty hard to target anyone else?? Whereas a 'Gun of Howl From Beyond', with the right reach(s) would target whoever the caster decided to (presumably, using 'point gun at the subject of your Spell's as the activation trigger if you can to make it intuitive - though there is no reason to assume the creator wanted that...)<br /> <br /> *Which may be zero if cast by a sleeper, werewolf or anyone without gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-07-2022, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T15:44:44-08:00","id":1472027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things that show up prominently in the Temenos are there because of how prominent they are in a culture, and I think that origin point among people is the thing to focus upon. </div> </div> </div>I guess it isn't an element of consensusal reality then, if the mage strongly identifies with their shadow name, it grounds them in the fallen whether other people understand the symbology or not.<br /> <br /> And thus a trip to the Temenos to understand* a rival may not be particularly useful. Though if their personal understanding of Odin differs greatly from the Temenos version, it still has the &quot;Don't expect to take the name Odin and not lose an eye&quot; - implying there is feedback as the world pushes its symbols onto the mages identity (perhaps you generated your own Fate?)<br /> <br /> *Or mess with the Temenos symbology, attempting to undermine them. You might aswell write a superhero comic featuring their shadow name as a character and hope it catches on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T15:56:31-08:00","id":1472028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although I presume that when casting with Ritual time the option remains to lengthen the casting for bonus dice </div> </div> </div>Very strange to think of the user having to do it a ritual time (presumably off of their own Gnosis, which might oreclude sleepers, of give them the same Gnosis 1 as for the paradox roll).<br /> <br /> But yes, if the reach for instant casting has not been taken, it must be at ritual time with the ritual effectively being the activation trigger.<br /> <br /> It just seems odd because in my head the imago is there (though obviously it's not all there as the subjects and spell factors can change) and it seems to be designed as a 'press button -&gt; generate effect'<br /> <br /> Doing a fairly long ritual (say for a sleepwalker) with a comparatively weak effect (though +5 for 18 hours does more than double the dice pool for a 5 dot spell) seems rather underwhelming. <br /> <br /> Still a Sleepwalker using a Making practice or Unmaking is a fairly impressive feat (even if the duration is limited... You can have a portable hallow generator which will then refill the manapool of the imbued item...)<br /> <br /> EDIT: though the cost of Create Truth is not something i had noticed until just now. Break even on mana would be fairly slow... Though making lasting Hallows with an imbued item is probably setting breaking - with standard scale, i presume that Hallow is 'arms lenght from a central point' in scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-07-2022, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T17:22:06-08:00","id":1472037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472026#post1472026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The attainment in the core book explicitly says the imbued spell may not have indefinite duration (while the imbuing of the spell is lasting).</div> </div> </div> </div> erm\u2026 I may be (metaphorically) blind and (actually) sick but I just reread the entire thing and it says nothing of the sort that I could find. Can you post a quote, please? (The closest thing I could find says spells \u201ca spell cast by using a imbued item <b>might </b>run out\u201d. That is a very different wording from no indefinite spells)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472026#post1472026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can have glasses of darkvision, which are activated whenever you put them on (costing 1 mana) and which last for a day (any duration which isn't indefinite).<br /> <br /> Then you spend 1 more mana to repeat the spell. But you can also take them off and give them to someone else to activate darkvision for that character... Also paying the mana and lasting the day.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, but you can make a version of them that has the spell as indefinite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472026#post1472026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking off the imbued items doesn't automatically cancel the spell (it is unclear if spells can have deactivation options similar to the activation rules, I'm guessing they should if the creator decided).</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s a Fate attainment. Otherwise it just stays active until the duration runs out, or the creator ends the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472026#post1472026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously if these we're indefinite spells, you could use one imbued item to cast the same indefinite buff on everyone in the Consilium, and then sell the imbued item, or put it away... forcing the items to pay 1 mana for the spell every single time and not be indefinite balances things up a little (it becomes a 1 mana/duration/spell upkeep cost, rather than 1 mana forced and no upkeep).</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. You can do that. Except extremely few mages would allow themselves to be buffed in that style. Because anyone who can make a imbued item can also hide spells and their effects, and unless you personally examine the imbued item, with the proper arcana, you can\u2019t know what exactly else is in the spell. Combined spells are a thing. Secondly, indefinite spells are offhandedly mentioned to sometimes cause people to go raptured. Not something most would want to risk, like radiation, people don\u2019t want to risk even a very safe dose. Same goes for most mages, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472026#post1472026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am presuming the subject of the spell can't be locked, so in the glasses of darkvision example it doesn't automatically target the user, but if it is at touch range and the activation trigger is putting the glasses in your head, then it is pretty hard to target anyone else?? Whereas a 'Gun of Howl From Beyond', with the right reach(s) would target whoever the caster decided to (presumably, using 'point gun at the subject of your Spell's as the activation trigger if you can to make it intuitive - though there is no reason to assume the creator wanted that...)</div> </div> </div> </div> In SoS, there is a \u201cCurse\u201d that has the imbued item only able to target whoever activated it. You can intentionally build that into your imbued item. Aside for that, aimed spells are the same spell factor as touch, so every item that is touch only can be aimed. Secondly, and I can\u2019t stress this enough, have someone skilled in Prime double check any imbued items you get, to at least to know if it works as it\u2019s supposed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T00:54:18-08:00","id":1472050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> erm\u2026 I may be (metaphorically) blind and (actually) sick but I just reread the entire thing and it says nothing of the sort that I could find. Can you post a quote, please? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imbued Item (\u2022+, Special)<br /> Effect: An Imbued Item is an item storing a spell that does not have an indefinite duration </div> </div> </div> Page 102<br /> <br /> I note there is no reference in the attainment section, and there is<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Enhanced Item (\u2022+, Special)<br /> Effect: Your character owns an item enhanced by indefinite Duration spells, which permanently modify the item\u2019s properties. </div> </div> </div>Page 101<br /> <br /> But i assume this refers to items with (for example) an indefinite alter integrity to enhance the item.<br /> <br /> And the Lexicon describes Matter as the arcanum which 'tools, machines, and enhanced items.' - so i take it that these two merits have nothing to do with each other, excepting that if you put the effort into imbuing an item you might want to enhance it with alter itegrity to make it harder to destroy (though that spell, not being an attainment, can be dispelled).<br /> <br /> Rereadind the attainment, the only bit i am confused by is &quot;The caster decides whether the spell imbued into the item is persistent (always active) or contingent (triggered by a word, gesture, or condition).&quot; - does the user need to do the spell roll for persistent effects? If they aren't indefinite then they can only last until their duration... It seems like you are supposed to be able to have an always on spell effect (like a Ward on your sanctum) which doesn't cost you spell control because it is imbued, and which can be dispelled (as usual, but with lower potentcy, because it is hard to gain large dice pools on imbued spells).<br /> <br /> I just like that narratively you could steal an item from someone's sanctum and disable its security system...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Contingent seems to mean my glasses of night vision could automatically switch off when they are taken off... Without using a fate attainment. But now I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: You could create a hammer of alter integrity, but without indefinite duration, you couldn't use it to produce unlimited enhanced items (even if you could, duration indefinite would be a -10 dice pool and pretty hard to do for lower Gnosis characters and Sleepwalkers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-08-2022, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T05:20:31-08:00","id":1472055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472050#post1472050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 102<br /> <br /> I note there is no reference in the attainment section, and there is</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b Wow, and first line too. I <b>am </b>blind, because I definitely reread that part. Hmm, so guess we have a choice now. Because it again doesn\u2019t mention anything about indefinite in the SoS attainment creation clarification. I used a word finder and everything. So you can interpret that has not being able to make such things, or you can interpret that as such items not being able to bought with merit points. To muddy things further, Imbued Ally, a new merit in SoS says: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your character has imbued a spell with a indefinite duration into a person or creature who is bound to her using the Prime Attainment, Imbue Item </div> </div> </div> Personally, I think that if such a restriction was completely intended, there would be a mention in the crafting rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472050#post1472050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 101<br /> <br /> But i assume this refers to items with (for example) an indefinite alter integrity to enhance the item.<br /> <br /> And the Lexicon describes Matter as the arcanum which 'tools, machines, and enhanced items.' - so i take it that these two merits have nothing to do with each other, excepting that if you put the effort into imbuing an item you might want to enhance it with alter itegrity to make it harder to destroy (though that spell, not being an attainment, can be dispelled).</div> </div> </div> </div> Your interpretation is seemingly correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472050#post1472050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rereadind the attainment, the only bit i am confused by is &quot;The caster decides whether the spell imbued into the item is persistent (always active) or contingent (triggered by a word, gesture, or condition).&quot; - does the user need to do the spell roll for persistent effects? If they aren't indefinite then they can only last until their duration</div> </div> </div> </div> Slightly expended on in SoS. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chosen by the creator on Imbuement. Persistent items are always active until their spell\u2019s duration expires, unless dispelled. Contingent Items are triggered by a word, gesture, or condition set by the creator. Only one spell in a item may be Contingent </div> </div> </div> Apparently once dispelled, you need Word of Command to reactivate the spell, which does require you to roll, twice in fact.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472050#post1472050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ... It seems like you are supposed to be able to have an always on spell effect (like a Ward on your sanctum) which doesn't cost you spell control because it is imbued, and which can be dispelled (as usual, but with lower potentcy, because it is hard to gain large dice pools on imbued spells).<br /> <br /> I just like that narratively you could steal an item from someone's sanctum and disable its security system...</div> </div> </div> </div> In the event of indefinite duration security systems, I\u2019d rule that the imbued item that created them would be a powerful yantra to effect or bypass them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472050#post1472050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Contingent seems to mean my glasses of night vision could automatically switch off when they are taken off... Without using a fate attainment. But now I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don\u2019t believe this to be the case as Contingent spells re defined properly above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472050#post1472050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT 2: You could create a hammer of alter integrity, but without indefinite duration, you couldn't use it to produce unlimited enhanced items (even if you could, duration indefinite would be a -10 dice pool and pretty hard to do for lower Gnosis characters and Sleepwalkers).</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s what primary spell factors are for. *realizes even with duration as the primary spell factor that\u2019s still a -4 penalty* Makes it more plausible anyways. Willpower goes a long way I guess. Or you could use the 2 reach option to make it Lasting in this specific example. Actually I\u2019m not seeing any mention of primary spell factors in the imbuement rules, I guess the default assumption would have the primary spell factor be linked to the spell\u2019s arcanum rating. It could also be equal the Creators, but that seems more complicated. Or I guess you could go with it having no primary spell factors, which is a strange thing to not mention in the item creation rules. This is starting to remind me of the Changeling \u201cfae twilight\u201d debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T07:55:59-08:00","id":1472057,"title":"","content":"I think what is being said in page 102 is that you cannot obtain an Imbued item with an indefinite duration spell via purchase alone, since most mages would not want to risk their client abusing it, Consilia or Order precedent might have ruled against it or people simply do not want to deal with the Paradox risk of stronger ones. In this way, it means the mage either needs to make it themselves, negotiate via some powerful boon or get incredibly lucky on the field. I believe that should reconcile what both sources are saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-08-2022, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T08:21:01-08:00","id":1472058,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the first line of the Imbued Item Merit was just a slightly awkward way of saying that the object is carrying the spell but it's not based on it having an indefinite duration.<br /> <br /> I'm observing now that the parameters of Enhanced Item are a bit broader than they were in First Edition, where it referred to something that had specifically had Durability, Structure, or Tool Bonus improved. The reading of it in the current rendition would be that you could have an object that has, say, been made to have acidic properties with what it touches and that would be Enhanced, but it would still be based on being an Indefinite duration spell that can be removed from it. The power of an Imbued Item cannot be extracted without breaking it.<br /> <br /> To be frank, I think there's a distinct lack of clarity about what Persistent Effects are, and the notes in Signs of Sorcery on them lasting for their Duration actually make it more confused. So you've got a choice between something that is &quot;always active&quot; (until it naturally runs out of time, and then needs to be manually activated in some fashion again) and something that can only be triggered by a set activity that also ends up with a limited duration. It ultimately ends up sounding like so-called Persistent Effects are just Contingent stuff that is more difficult to use. The more straight reading is that their effect really is active at all times, but that would end up clashing with a clear sense of what their factors actually are; even if they functionally amount to free indefinite effects, how are Potency and Scale determined? It actually makes me question the value of the distinction.<br /> <br /> Oh, to just follow that note about a Ward, spells don't Withstand being dispelled with their Potency, they do it with the Arcanum rating of the caster; a Ward cast by an Apprentice needs a Potency 3 dispellation to break it, that of a Master needs a 6. Although the Reach to increase that Withstand by 2 is used on Advanced Potency, that actual spell factor has no significance to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Indeed, because Ward is a spell based on providing a Clash of Wills, improved Potency is actually wasted on it... unless a Ward can only Clash as many space warping or sympathy targeting powers as it has Potency, per the guidelines on page 126-127. Hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T09:16:03-08:00","id":1472060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, to just follow that note about a Ward, spells don't Withstand being dispelled with their Potency, they do it with the Arcanum rating of the caster; </div> </div> </div>Of course, i keep forgetting this.<br /> <br /> It seems clear the imbued items use the Arcana rating from the item rather than the user (or indeed the creator) - at least this is the case for the dice pool. <br /> <br /> I am going to guess that the withstand is the arcanum rating of the spell (with a possible +2 for advanced potency). Does SoS clarify?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wow, and first line too. I am blind, because I definitely reread that part. </div> </div> </div>No your brain just filled in the details without reading because you've probably read it multiple times before... Human brains take shortcuts! Just look at your blind spots <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm not sure i like that 'you can't buy it with a merit'* or In Character explaination. I'd prefer to run a system which makes sense.<br /> <br /> Contingent imbued spells which turn on and off based on a simple user action (is not a spell roll) : indefinite duration, 0 mana to activate, can only be 'cast' once (unless dispelled with lasting) - as its imago is always in use - which would also prevent messing with spell factors.<br /> <br /> Persistent spells, which are always (at least) 1 mana and a spell roll to activate, and last until their duration is over. Can be cast multiple times, costing mana each time, but only one spell slot.<br /> <br /> This gives a reason for two different ways of casting, or types of spell.<br /> <br /> It is reminding me of 1st Ed (LARP) conversations i had about imbued items, i was firmly of the opinion that each spell you loaded into an item was a one use, and so a lasting damage spell was like loading a shotgun with one Shell. Whereas a hone the form spell with indefinite duration could be used only by one person at a time and could be switched on and off but would always be the same spell...<br /> <br /> *EDIT: I'm compiling a list of magical items; Imbued, Fetish, Enhanced are the ones with merits...just for quick reference. There are more types of items than you can buy as a merit, so sure, that seems fair. But i think a balance of permanent conditional vs non-indefinite 1 mana per activation works fine for my purposes (that is ignore the rule which doesn't seem to make sense and run something balanced and fun).<br /> <br /> EDIT2 : Actually the more i think about it, the more sense my persistent/contingent division makes sense. Eg: <br /> 1) Persistent Atheric Wind, effect lasting, cost 1 mana, roll Gnosis + 3 (Spell's Arcana), deal potency damage.<br /> 2) Contingent Wards and Signs, effect duration, once cast it may be switched on or off as needed (instant action?) Target withstands spells by potency","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-08-2022, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T10:26:34-08:00","id":1472063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472060#post1472060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contingent imbued spells which turn on and off based on a simple user action (is not a spell roll) : indefinite duration, 0 mana to activate, can only be 'cast' once (unless dispelled with lasting) - as its imago is always in use - which would also prevent messing with spell factors.<br /> <br /> Persistent spells, which are always (at least) 1 mana and a spell roll to activate, and last until their duration is over. Can be cast multiple times, costing mana each time, but only one spell slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got these backward, chief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T11:18:39-08:00","id":1472065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472063#post1472063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got these backward, chief.</div> </div> </div> </div>The names do seem back asswards.<br /> <br /> &quot;The caster decides whether the spell imbued into the item is persistent (always active) or contingent (triggered by a word, gesture, or condition)&quot;<br /> <br /> My thought is that the 'always active' spell is the one you want to be able to switch on and off with a condtion/trigger. Which is contingent... But i see how you are correct on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T11:33:32-08:00","id":1472066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472060#post1472060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, i keep forgetting this.<br /> <br /> It seems clear the imbued items use the Arcana rating from the item rather than the user (or indeed the creator) - at least this is the case for the dice pool.<br /> <br /> I am going to guess that the withstand is the arcanum rating of the spell (with a possible +2 for advanced potency). Does SoS clarify?</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope, but your reasoning makes plenty of sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472060#post1472060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No your brain just filled in the details without reading because you've probably read it multiple times before... Human brains take shortcuts! Just look at your blind spots <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I just wish I didn\u2019t have so many blind spots though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472060#post1472060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure i like that 'you can't buy it with a merit'* or In Character explaination. I'd prefer to run a system which makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s fair. Personally I find being able to put any spell on a imbued item to be more consistent with the rest of Mage, but you do whatever works for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T12:00:14-08:00","id":1472067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472065#post1472065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The names do seem back asswards.<br /> <br /> &quot;The caster decides whether the spell imbued into the item is persistent (always active) or contingent (triggered by a word, gesture, or condition)&quot;<br /> <br /> My thought is that the 'always active' spell is the one you want to be able to switch on and off with a condtion/trigger. Which is contingent... But i see how you are correct on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no, the literal definition of &quot;persistent&quot; is that it <i>persists,</i> whereas &quot;contingent&quot; means that it's not necessarily going to be happening at any given time, because depends on something happening.<br /> <br /> You can <i>want</i> it not to be that way, but the distinction is &quot;does this keep happening constantly&quot; versus &quot;does this happen when a trigger is applied,&quot; regardless of what you'd prefer it to be as someone who didn't make the decision about which way the item was made.<br /> <br /> Contingent items aren't toggled on and off, they're either in a state of having been activated or they aren't, with early termination being a function of normal spell control for the creator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-09T15:57:18-08:00","id":1472150,"title":"","content":"Seems a bit aggressive, but let me clarify two things.<br /> <br /> Firstly:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Contingent items aren't toggled on and off, they're either in a state of having been activated or they aren't, with early termination being a function of normal spell control for the creator. </div> </div> </div>My reading of this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> contingent (triggered by a word, <br /> gesture, or condition) </div> </div> </div>Is probably confused by the condtion part. My understanding is if the condition ends so does the spell (like the Conditional Duration Fate attainment).<br /> <br /> I am specifically saying, a pair of glasses which are trigger by putting them on, but have conditional duration ending the spell of you take them off (or the condition is being worn, and i interpret the rules to mean the spell ends if the condition is not satisfied).<br /> <br /> Secondly, i am saying the rules for indefinite spells in imbued items are not clear. With one paragraph explicitly forbidding them. <br /> <br /> I would house rule that as described above - to give two options both of which have advantages and disadvantages - and describe what are intuitive items for players to enjoy the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-09T16:22:11-08:00","id":1472152,"title":"","content":"New Question: i know this has been discussed before, (I'm only 230 pages into this thread, ok?) But two small things about Supernal Veil<br /> <br /> &quot;This spell wards its subject, which can be a <br /> spell, object, mage, supernatural creature, or any other active magical phenomenon, from detection&quot;<br /> <br /> Should this not be magical object? Object seems to be out of place in this spell.<br /> <br /> Second: whether or not the above uses Prime's purview of Truth and not Magic, could you creative thaumatergy a Veiling of the Truth (of subject's objectively true existence) to hide anything from everything (like various time spells that make the rest of the world simply act as if a subject with no history never existed - see Space 5 spell Quarentine).<br /> <br /> Probably CoW for supernatural detection, but essentially a more powerful than Incognito Presence (unless it is also withstood?)<br /> <br /> EDIT: on second thought, veiling the objective Truth of my existence should just make people question it, not fail to see it... Still makes witnesses to your actions have some reasonable doubts (in a legal sense). Eg: &quot;Witness1 i definitely saw him murder the Mayor<br /> Defence Lawyer: but are you sure he even exists?<br /> Witness1: i... Eh.. definitely saw someone who looked like him murder the Mayor.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-09-2022, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-09T19:06:24-08:00","id":1472156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472152#post1472152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Question: i know this has been discussed before, (I'm only 230 pages into this thread, ok?) But two small things about Supernal Veil<br /> <br /> &quot;This spell wards its subject, which can be a<br /> spell, object, mage, supernatural creature, or any other active magical phenomenon, from detection&quot;<br /> <br /> Should this not be magical object? Object seems to be out of place in this spell.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, they mean magical objects. You know, you can probably Veil Yantras too, so maybe ordinary objects from a Sleepers perspective can be veiled. That\u2019s possibly a different spell though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472152#post1472152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second: whether or not the above uses Prime's purview of Truth and not Magic, could you creative thaumatergy a Veiling of the Truth (of subject's objectively true existence) to hide anything from everything (like various time spells that make the rest of the world simply act as if a subject with no history never existed - see Space 5 spell Quarentine).<br /> <br /> Probably CoW for supernatural detection, but essentially a more powerful than Incognito Presence (unless it is also withstood?)</div> </div> </div> </div> It should be withstood, since this is effectively a reverse Words of Truth, and you are not changing the Truth itself, just hiding it. A non withstood version can be achieved through Patterning, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472152#post1472152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: on second thought, veiling the objective Truth of my existence should just make people question it, not fail to see it... Still makes witnesses to your actions have some reasonable doubts (in a legal sense). Eg: &quot;Witness1 i definitely saw him murder the Mayor<br /> Defence Lawyer: but are you sure he even exists?<br /> Witness1: i... Eh.. definitely saw someone who looked like him murder the Mayor.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> This is pretty much how it goes. Prime can\u2019t mess with any of the regular properties that go into detection like Mind or Life or Forces or most of the other arcanum, but the veiling Truth of your presence does technically work. It just produces some rather odd results. Let\u2019s say you veil the Truth of your identity, people who would recognize you could describe you in exact detail, even draw a perfect sketch of you, and recognize everything you are doing, and never realize it was you. Maybe they think it\u2019s a extremely well done costume, someone who likes like you, or that they are hallucinating or dreaming. When the spell ends, they will probably be able to recognize that it was you all along, (though they probably wouldn\u2019t come to that realization without some prompting,) but until then, even if you tell them exactly what\u2019s going to happen, they will <b>know</b> that it\u2019s not you. When compared to Veiling of Mind/Life etc, they can produce similar results, but they can outright make people fail to recognize that there is anything there at all. When Veiling the Truth of your existence, people will <b>know</b> that the person who shot the mayor doesn\u2019t exist. They mayor was shot, it was a murder, witnesses could describe the murderer perfectly, but the murderer is a person who doesn\u2019t exist. This doesn\u2019t protect your identity by the way, people will still recognize you. And they will <b>know</b> you don\u2019t exist. And if any sleepers think too hard about how someone who doesn\u2019t exist managed murder someone and shows up on cameras, you are going to have a huge problem with dissonance. And once the spell ends you are going to have problems. For example, your description is still plenty of evidence enough to make a case against you. This, on the whole, makes this a bad spell for not getting caught. Instead, look to enhance your lies with Veiling, and Veil your identity <b>and </b>specific parts of your identity (like your skin tone or tattoos or other major identifying features), and Veil the fact that you aren\u2019t where you belong. Maybe set up a scapegoat by Veiling your identity as someone else, so they take the fall and the case gets closed quickly. And accept that both memories, records, sketches, and cameras will potentially be problems in the long term. You probably will want to invest in a safely relinquished indefinite spell that Veils the fact you murdered the mayor. Also, other Mages will be able to figure out what you did pretty easily.<br /> <br /> Edit: Grammar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-09-2022, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-09T21:45:12-08:00","id":1472162,"title":"","content":"Page 123 states that Veiling cannot affect abstract concepts, you can hide the truth of a subject but not from truth itself (the subject does exist and has some truth). So you can use it to make everything you say sound genuine or everything someone else says sound like a lie. Mundane methods will be unable to pierce it and supernatural effects cause a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> So putting that together, it means you could, for example, change the contents of the piece of paper. So you could redact text, change a map into a picture or make it the color of the wall to hide a poster. But it would still have the tactile sensation, shape, weight and any other properties of the default paper.<br /> <br /> Regarding <i>Supernal Veil</i>, its main purpose is to hide anything under its purview from supernatural senses. This means casting it combined with a spell makes it not ping the Peripheral Sight, the mage register as a Sleeper or an Artifact as just an object.<br /> <br /> But the thing is, sometimes the important thing is just mundane. The journal that leads to a long lost temple is just ink on paper, its because it was written by a Sleepwalker that its contents are valuable. The special herbal candle is just a candle, but its also the ban of the ghost that is haunting the antique shop. Sure, they can still see it with their eyes, but hiding them from their supernatural abilities is already a big help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-10-2022, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T00:59:00-08:00","id":1472169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Page 123 states that Veiling cannot affect abstract concepts, you can hide the truth of a subject but not from truth itself (the subject does exist and has some truth). </div> </div> </div> Thanks for that, though that paragraph seems a bit off ( &quot;A target can be made to lose all sense of time (Time)&quot; but the counter example &quot;a mage can\u2019t Veil herself against death or hide from time&quot; - especially considering the written up veiling of time which prevent poisons, bleeding to death and natural healing).<br /> <br /> But yeah, i think this is veiling a concrete (objective truth) example of the abstract, not the abstract concept of truth itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding Supernal Veil, its main purpose is to hide anything under its purview from supernatural senses. This means casting it combined with a spell makes it not ping the Peripheral Sight, the mage register as a Sleeper or an Artifact as just an object. </div> </div> </div>That is exactly my interpretation, but not how it was agreed earlier in this thread. Hiding a spell hides the entire thing (but spells are hidden by default unless you decide for setting reason you want the world to have Display of Power always on - a la the magic in Doctor Strange). I presume this spell also hide an Eidolon, which is 'obviously magical' but it is entirely made of tasks, so like a spell, would it completely disappear? (I'm going back to my thoughts on Eidolons as retainer guardians, but using them as an environment which is not visible to sleepers - or conditionally dissapears when a sleeper walks by - would be cool).<br /> <br /> Unrelated Eidolon question, can they gain mana by performing a blood sacrifice? (I'm thinking a bird of prey - with a spirit appropriate to murdering small animals - refilling the Eidolon's mana pool by murdering small animals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-10-2022, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T03:21:38-08:00","id":1472172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472162#post1472162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding <i>Supernal Veil</i>, its main purpose is to hide anything under its purview from supernatural senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a common interpretation, but the text says nothing about hiding things <i>specifically from supernatural senses</i>. Other Veiling spells of the same kind tend to hide the subject (which is under the purview of the Arcanum) from any sort of detection, both magical and mundane. Nothing about Supernal Veil indicates it would work any different from its literal wording.<br /> Personally, I do favour that it merely hides the supernatural parts of the subject (even though that's technically not stated in the spell, but it's how it should work given the description for Veiling spells). So no casting Supernal Veil on yourself to become completely undetectable by direct means just because you're a mage and thus technically supernatural.<br /> <br /> You could definitely craft a spell that would hide its subject specifically from supernatural senses, but since the method of detection falls under the purview of Prime, the subject no longer needs to be and could theoretically be anything. In this case you could cast the spell on a mage to have the mage become undetectable to any supernatural senses, but you could also cast it on a Sleeper, or on that rock over there. Now you can't use Matter to gain info about the rock's mineral composition without winning a CoW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472169#post1472169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but spells are hidden by default</div> </div> </div> </div>Peripheral Mage Sight pings on all spells that aren't about concealment, and Active Mage Sight will reveal all spells from the Arcana of your Mage Sight (except for Prime which instead reveals all spells). Casting Supernal Veil on spells does a lot to keep those spells hidden from other mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T05:25:08-08:00","id":1472177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Peripheral Mage Sight pings on all spells that aren't about concealment, and Active Mage Sight will reveal all spells from the Arcana of your Mage Sight (except for Prime which instead reveals all spells). Casting Supernal Veil on spells does a lot to keep those spells hidden from other mages </div> </div> </div>thank you, always good for the reminder. I was talking about mundane senses, hence my bit about making spells look like they do in Dr. Strange (both the films and comics are very visual mediums, so it doesn't surprise me that they made this choice - mechanically you could have it as an option: -1 reach, make your spell visible to mundane senses, but practically in front of sleepers this gains you nothing, as they add 1 dice of paradox, and away from sleepers you would be making a choice between easier counter spelling for more power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T09:08:36-08:00","id":1472181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472169#post1472169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thanks for that, though that paragraph seems a bit off ( &quot;A target can be made to lose all sense of time (Time)&quot; but the counter example &quot;a mage can\u2019t Veil herself against death or hide from time&quot; - especially considering the written up veiling of time which prevent poisons, bleeding to death and natural healing).<br /> <br /> But yeah, i think this is veiling a concrete (objective truth) example of the abstract, not the abstract concept of truth itself.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you are referring to Veil of Moments, I think you will find that that particular spell is <b>Shielding</b> you from the effects of the passage of Time, not Time as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472169#post1472169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is exactly my interpretation, but not how it was agreed earlier in this thread. Hiding a spell hides the entire thing (but spells are hidden by default unless you decide for setting reason you want the world to have Display of Power always on - a la the magic in Doctor Strange). I presume this spell also hide an Eidolon, which is 'obviously magical' but it is entirely made of tasks, so like a spell, would it completely disappear? (I'm going back to my thoughts on Eidolons as retainer guardians, but using them as an environment which is not visible to sleepers - or conditionally dissapears when a sleeper walks by - would be cool).</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019ve read a post on the forum that explains this better, but Veiling can do 3 things. It can completely hide something from something under it\u2019s bailiwick, it can obscure one of the properties under it\u2019s bailiwick, or it can completely hide something that completely falls under it\u2019s bailiwick. Incognito Presence Is a example of the first one, it hides you from Minds. Supernal Veiling is a example of the second, it hides one of the properties of the subject. Lastly, Hidden Hoard is a example of there third that completely hides material objects from everyone and everything.<br /> <br /> So, yes, Prime Veiling can completely hide a Eidolon. I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s technically the same spell though, since Supernal Veiling is type 2 and this new one is a type 3. It would seem to me that you can hide a Eidolon\u2019s \u201cobviously magical nature\u201d with Supernal Veiling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472169#post1472169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated Eidolon question, can they gain mana by performing a blood sacrifice? (I'm thinking a bird of prey - with a spirit appropriate to murdering small animals - refilling the Eidolon's mana pool by murdering small animals).</div> </div> </div> </div> By default, no. You can only Channel Mana into it by default, I think. (I don\u2019t have the book on me right now.) That being said, you can probably Weave it in, as I recall, Mages can do something similar, and Mages a under the Purview of Prime. At the very worst, you can imbue it with Prime/Death spell that uses gives mana when you kill something.<br /> <br /> Edit: You absolutely can Veil stuff from just Sleepers with Prime. A spell that conditionally hides a thing or reveals itself based on who is nearby requires Archmastery. Note that there <b>is</b> a difference between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-10-2022, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T09:57:49-08:00","id":1472183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472181#post1472181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you are referring to Veil of Moments, I think you will find that that particular spell is <b>Shielding</b> you from the effects of the passage of Time, not Time as a whole.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve read a post on the forum that explains this better, but Veiling can do 3 things. It can completely hide something from something under it\u2019s bailiwick, it can obscure one of the properties under it\u2019s bailiwick, or it can completely hide something that completely falls under it\u2019s bailiwick. Incognito Presence Is a example of the first one, it hides you from Minds. Supernal Veiling is a example of the second, it hides one of the properties of the subject. Lastly, Hidden Hoard is a example of there third that completely hides material objects from everyone and everything.<br /> <br /> So, yes, Prime Veiling can completely hide a Eidolon. I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s technically the same spell though, since Supernal Veiling is type 2 and this new one is a type 3. It would seem to me that you can hide a Eidolon\u2019s \u201cobviously magical nature\u201d with Supernal Veiling.<br /> <br /> By default, no. You can only Channel Mana into it by default, I think. (I don\u2019t have the book on me right now.) That being said, you can probably Weave it in, as I recall, Mages can do something similar, and Mages a under the Purview of Prime. At the very worst, you can imbue it with Prime/Death spell that uses gives mana when you kill something.<br /> <br /> Edit: You absolutely can Veil stuff from just Sleepers with Prime. A spell that conditionally hides a thing or reveals itself based on who is nearby requires Archmastery. Note that there <b>is</b> a difference between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically you could give them a mana battery. Then modify a Hallow so it has Plentiful Tass and so one of the ley lines &quot;conducts&quot; the mana into a battery charge spot, which might require conjunctional Forces or Matter. Utilizing that and multiple batteries, you could technically have a self sustaining Eidolon, provided they periodically switch out their charged packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T11:23:21-08:00","id":1472192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472183#post1472183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Technically you could give them a mana battery. Then modify a Hallow so it has Plentiful Tass and so one of the ley lines &quot;conducts&quot; the mana into a battery charge spot, which might require conjunctional Forces or Matter. Utilizing that and multiple batteries, you could technically have a self sustaining Eidolon, provided they periodically switch out their charged packs.</div> </div> </div> </div> Quite true, this is probably more efficient for a self sufficient Eidolon, but I think the idea is that the Eidolon is going to be doing a number of tasks regularly to maintain its disguise as a normal creature. Might as well as get \u201cfood\u201d from the creatures it hunts, if it\u2019s going to be hunting regularly for no normal benefit besides disguise. It\u2019s not a bad idea, especially since with the proper spirit inside, it also gets fed with essence.<br /> Edit: Heck, if it has a spirit inside, you can probably Weave gaining mana to when the spirit produces essence in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-10-2022, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T11:34:27-08:00","id":1472193,"title":"","content":"First, apologies for the typos above, i didn't get a chance to edit them out.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: You absolutely can Veil stuff from just Sleepers with Prime. A spell that conditionally hides a thing or reveals itself based on who is nearby requires Archmastery. Note that there is a difference between the two </div> </div> </div>There is a difference, i was specifically thinking of the latter. But i thought it would be achievable (if risky) with the imbued item attainment. You imbue the veiling spell into the Eidolon, and give the spell a conditional trigger, now the item already has a mana pool, and would in theory be able to activate itself (without a mind I'm assuming it is no good at deciding when it should activate itself, but in terms of rolling it is equivalent to a sleeper (Gnosis 0) + Arcana dots of the spell) but with conditions... What are you able to do to automatically trigger the spell? (Admitted that a 2 dice pool without the option to spend willpower isn't great, plus every attempt to cast results in 1 mana used).<br /> <br /> And even then, if the condition was 'when a sleeper sees you' - assuming that is valid. I think it still triggers dissonance (infact possibly on both the veiling and the Eidolon, as that is two magical effects). Does that become a non-issue if the Eidolon kills the sleeper (who has invaded the sanctum and he now been attacked by a potentially 10 dice retainer combatant who is invisible)? That is can dead sleepers trigger dissonance?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, yes, Prime Veiling can completely hide a Eidolon. I\u2019m not sure if it\u2019s technically the same spell though, since Supernal Veiling is type 2 and this new one is a type 3. It would seem to me that you can hide a Eidolon\u2019s \u201cobviously magical nature\u201d with Supernal Veiling. </div> </div> </div>You may be right, i was thinking of a Eidolon as basically made of magic. Even if tass is Mana made solid, it is still under the purview of Prime... But normal tass just looks like a normal item (to mundane senses). So it should be possible to view an Eidolon so they don't trigger dissonance but are still visible to sleepers (not forcing them to fight an invisible retainer).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technically you could give them a mana battery. </div> </div> </div> I presume you mean with imbue item, but as they already have a mana pool, my thinking was they can naturally hold mana in their pattern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By default, no. You can only Channel Mana into it by default, I think. (I don\u2019t have the book on me right now.) </div> </div> </div>Looking up the Eidolon spell, it says &quot;A mage may \u201crefill\u201d the construct with the Channel Mana spell (p. 168) or similar effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> So here it my reasoning, you don't need Death spells to get mana from a death, so long as you do a blood sacrifice. And afaik, sleeper thaumatergy and vampire blood magic can both do similar effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Blood Sacrifice offers Mana. In an Act of Hubris, the mage kills a living being for Mana. Its death releases Mana from its Pattern. A small animal offers one Mana, while human sacrifices offer as much Mana as the person had Integrity dots remaining before the killing blow. The Mana gained from Sacrifice ignores the spend/Turn limits on Mana if the sacrifice is part of a spell\u2019s casting.&quot;<br /> <br /> I note, it can be done in a ritual way during a spell to add mana to pay for the spell, but a mage can simply kill a being, releasing mana from its pattern (is there some specific ruling about how the killer absorbs that mana? It doesn't require Death or Prime at least).<br /> <br /> So i am presuming anyone can do this, but most Patterns can't store mana by default. In which case the Eidolon has a unique advantage. Still it is unclear if it can be done this way. The spirit of murder birds will happily murder small animals without an act of hubris (it will likely generate resonance and possibly gain essence, right?) - i think it is also clear that an Eidolon without a mind can't do this complex of a job, maybe an Eidolon 'with its own mind' would be able to do it more effectively, since it can be given complex order to complete a ritual blood sacrifice - but blood sacrifice doesn't seem to need any ritual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That being said, you can probably Weave it in, as I recall, Mages can do something similar, and Mages a under the Purview of Prime. </div> </div> </div>Ah, so without an imbued spell? I think to weave that feature from the mage template you would have to study how blood sacrifice actually works (ie treat it as a mystery, which means watching a few? Probably using active mage sight (Death, Life and Prime) to see how it affects the Soul, how the life releases mana, and how the mage's pattern absorbs the mana.<br /> <br /> Is that fair? Or maybe a knowing spell of Prime would he enough to understand how it works?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you are referring to Veil of Moments, I think you will find that that particular spell is Shielding you from the effects of the passage of Time, not Time as a whole. </div> </div> </div>Of course, i think i am confusing the practice there. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-10-2022, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T11:48:29-08:00","id":1472194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heck, if it has a spirit inside, you can probably Weave gaining mana to when the spirit produces essence in general. </div> </div> </div>My assumption was that converting mana and essence was now much harder (they took out the spell which allowed it from 1st Ed.) I was presuming they wanted to make mana considerably harder to get (scouring wounds are now lethal, matter/prime i forget which can't use putting out the rubbish and dismantling its pattern to gain mana, no direct essence to mana transfer - except familiars- and channel essence allows a mage to have essence in their pattern which takes up mana pool space but isn't usable as mana). As a design goal, i approved, because limited resources makes for drama. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quite true, this is probably more efficient for a self sufficient Eidolon, but I think the idea is that the Eidolon is going to be doing a number of tasks regularly to maintain its disguise as a normal creature. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the idea that an Eidolon could be made self-sufficient was it. Choosing a spirit and form appropriately (to that task of killing) was the easy part. I don't have a problem with bird of prey killing small animals not causing a Act of Hubris - maybe creating this Eidolon killing machine would be an Act of Hubris for the mage who created it, but hell it is still fun.<br /> <br /> The hard part is making clear that they can be self sufficient. Having an AI type mind which returns to your sanctum and absorbs excess mana from the Hallow (assuming it would otherwise turn into tass anyway) or imbuing channel mana into it so it can take mana directly from the Hallow (or indeed death imbuement as you mentioned) all seem reasonable alternatives. <br /> <br /> None of them end up with a cute murder bird hunting for its mana. And they seem less elegant, this actually feels like the easiest to do (Arcana-wise it is Spirit 3, Prime 5 Vs Prime 5, Mind 5, Death 3/4?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-10-2022, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T13:50:35-08:00","id":1472198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, apologies for the typos above, i didn't get a chance to edit them out.</div> </div> </div> </div> No worries, I think you were clearly understood without much effort on our part, so all is well. Besides, if I went after you for typos, I\u2019d be a massive hypocrite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference, i was specifically thinking of the latter. But i thought it would be achievable (if risky) with the imbued item attainment. You imbue the veiling spell into the Eidolon, and give the spell a conditional trigger, now the item already has a mana pool, and would in theory be able to activate itself (without a mind I'm assuming it is no good at deciding when it should activate itself, but in terms of rolling it is equivalent to a sleeper (Gnosis 0) + Arcana dots of the spell) but with conditions... What are you able to do to automatically trigger the spell? (Admitted that a 2 dice pool without the option to spend willpower isn't great, plus every attempt to cast results in 1 mana used).</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah. I thought you meant as a single spell. This changes things. Yes, you can do this with imbued items, or a Eidolon in this case. As for the condition\u2026well I think it works. I\u2019m not certain though. There is a new type of Yantra in SoS called a Basilisk, that happens to cast spells when it is seen. It also requires Fate 2 to use, since it works by using that Attainment. I\u2019d personally would be happier if the creator of the imbuement also used Fate 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even then, if the condition was 'when a sleeper sees you' - assuming that is valid. I think it still triggers dissonance (infact possibly on both the veiling and the Eidolon, as that is two magical effects). Does that become a non-issue if the Eidolon kills the sleeper (who has invaded the sanctum and he now been attacked by a potentially 10 dice retainer combatant who is invisible)? That is can dead sleepers trigger dissonance?</div> </div> </div> </div> It most likely does. Things don\u2019t normally immediately vanish when you see them. No, the process is caused by a sleeper, sure, but after it starts it still does it\u2019s thing. Dead sleepers tend to not be able to perceive magic, and thus tend not to cause more dissonance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may be right, i was thinking of a Eidolon as basically made of magic. Even is tass is Mana made solid, it is still under the purview of Prime... But normal tass just looks like a normal item (to mundane senses). So it should be possible to view and Eidolon so they don't trigger dissonance but are still visible to sleepers (not forcing them to fight an invisible retainer).</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is much better than them straight up disappearing when spotted. Nothing magical about getting hacked to pieces. Strange and horrible, but not magical. A 10 dice combatant will still easily overpower most others especially since the majority of humans are not skilled fighters. The dissonance involved with being permanently invisible or disappearing when spotted isn\u2019t worth potential losing the spell guardian entirely. Depending on the circumstances, and what you are guarding and why, people seeing that you have a big and tough guardian prevents having to kill people as often.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume you mean with imbue item, but as they already have a mana pool, my thinking was they can naturally hold mana in their pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, there is a new spell in SoS called Mana Battery. It gives stuff a mana pool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking up the Eidolon spell, it says &quot;A mage may \u201crefill\u201d the construct with the Channel Mana spell (p. 168) or similar effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> So here it my reasoning, you don't need Death spells to get mana from a death, so long as you do a blood sacrifice. And afaik, sleeper thaumatergy and vampire blood magic can both do similar effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I guess this depends on wether anything with mana pool can preform Oblation. I\u2019m fairly certain only things with minds and a Supernal connection can. Vampire blood magic and sleeper thaumatergy are not relevant to Supernal magic, just because they can do something doesn\u2019t mean a mage can and visa-versa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Blood Sacrifice offers Mana. In an Act of Hubris, the mage kills a living being for Mana. Its death releases Mana from its Pattern. A small animal offers one Mana, while human sacrifices offer as much Mana as the person had Integrity dots remaining before the killing blow. The Mana gained from Sacrifice ignores the spend/Turn limits on Mana if the sacrifice is part of a spell\u2019s casting.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note, it can be done in a ritual way during a spell to add mana to pay for the spell, but a mage can simply kill a being, releasing mana from its pattern (is there some specific ruling about how the killer absorbs that mana? It doesn't require Death or Prime at least).</div> </div> </div> </div> I think normally it\u2019s supposed to just be absorbed by the Mage in question. I do know there is a Mysterium ritual to relies on preventing this and watching the mana spread out and dissolve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i am presuming anyone can do this, but most Patterns can't store mana by default. In which case the Eidolon has a unique advantage. Still it is unclear if it can be done this way. The spirit of murder birds will happily murder small animals without an act of hubris (it will likely generate resonance and possibly gain essence, right?) - i think it is also clear that a Eidolon without a mind can't do this complex of a job, maybe an Eidolon 'with its own mind' would be able to do it more effectively, since it can be given complex order to complete a ritual blood sacrifice - but blood sacrifice doesn't seem to need any ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div> The problem is that it might depend on there being a act of hubris. It might depend on it being a Mage doing the sacrifice. (Which was what my Prime Weaving spell tried to use). It might also depend on both. Or it could be something anyone can do. I think we both agree that a mindless Eidolon can\u2019t do it on it\u2019s own, but it\u2019s possible you can order a mindless Eidolon to kill stuff and gain mana as long as you do it for the mana. Good way to lose Wisdom quickly though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so without an imbued spell? I think to weave that feature of the mage template you would have to study how blood sacrifice actually works (ie treat it as a mystery, which means watching a few? Probably using active mage sight (Death, Life and Prime) to see how it affects the Soul, how the life releases mana, and how the mage's pattern absorbs the mana.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, imbuing it into the Eidolon is better, but it\u2019s not necessary. Sounds like a perfect set of mysteries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that fair? Or maybe a knowing spell of Prime would he enough to understand how it works?</div> </div> </div> </div> It\u2019s better than just fair, not only do you end up with a nifty new spell, you get arcane beats. Knowing would not help here, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472193#post1472193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, i think i am confusing the practice there. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div> It is fine, I\u2019m just amused at Veil of Moments being Shielding while Shield of Chronos is Veiling. Happens to also be Time\u2019s only example of a Veiling spell. Really, they had to do that on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T14:36:37-08:00","id":1472200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472194#post1472194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My assumption was that converting mana and essence was now much harder (they took out the spell which allowed it from 1st Ed.)I was presuming they wanted to make mana considerably harder to get (scouring wounds are now lethal, matter/prime i forget which can't use putting out the rubbish and dismantling its pattern to gain mana, no direct essence to mana transfer - except familiars- and channel essence allows a mage to have essence in their pattern which takes up mana pool space but isn't usable as mana). As a design goal, i approved, because limited resources makes for drama.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m going to assume that\u2019s because they didn\u2019t put any examples of Patterning something into another arcanum. You can turn stuff into Mana, it\u2019s just that it takes Prime 4 and the appropriate Arcanum 4 to do so. It\u2019s the same thing as turning flesh into stone. Heck, there is a Death spell that lets you pattern scour other people for mana. Mana isn\u2019t exactly rare, if you have Prime and know what you are doing. For example, with knowing you can locate Hallows, with perfecting you can just increase the amount you get out of pattern scouring, and with Making, you can make all the Mana you could need. Now it\u2019s not nearly enough for all the demand for mana, but it\u2019s not particularly rare. Basically, for the average mage, there is enough mana to do stuff, but not be terribly wasteful, with Prime, especially having Ruling Prime, you can afford to be a little wasteful now and then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472194#post1472194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the idea that an Eidolon could be made self-sufficient was it. Choosing a spirit and form appropriately (to that task of killing) was the easy part. I don't have a problem with bird of prey killing small animals not causing a Act of Hubris - maybe creating this Eidolon killing machine would be an Act of Hubris for the mage who created it, but hell it is still fun.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it\u2019s definitely a act of hubris for the mage that created it, but it\u2019s probably not anything particularly bad for the Eidolon or spirit. Heck, the spirit is probably thrilled, as this is pretty much a minor spirits dream job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472194#post1472194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hard part is making clear that they can be self sufficient. Having an AI type mind which returns to your sanctum and absorbs excess mana from the Hallow (assuming it would otherwise turn into tass anyway) or imbuing channel mana into it so it can take mana directly from the Hallow (or indeed death imbuement as you mentioned) all seem reasonable alternatives.<br /> <br /> None of them end up with a cute murder bird hunting for its mana. And they seem less elegant, this actually feels like the easiest to do (Arcana-wise it is Spirit 3, Prime 5 Vs Prime 5, Mind 5, Death 3/4?)</div> </div> </div> </div> Heck this version could just be Prime and a familiar. This one certainly has a certain style to it. Though, technically my Death one could use a ghost as it\u2019s mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T15:57:18-08:00","id":1472202,"title":"","content":"To clarify, a mana battery is an item that holds a certain amount of mana. While holding it, a user can transfer it into their pattern. More details can be found on page 70 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i><br /> <br /> I think it might make more sense to create a Supernal Knowledge spirit by utilizing a Patterning of Prime and Spirit (more details on page 124 of the core book) on an existing one. Modify them to gain sustenance from Supernal secrets. Now it has to do its job well in order to survive.<br /> <br /> Its naturally invisible in Twilight (unless someone has the Spirit 2 Attainment), can manipulate others and maintain a disguise by Fettering itself to them, can become better at its job by Claiming a host, can make quick exits via Discorporation. It has the flexibility of Influences and the Numina for more precise tasks. It also has an incentive to cultivate a spirit choir to help it be more efficient at its job, if not an entire Mystery Cult that flies under the radar of Awakened society by being a Nameless organization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T16:02:34-08:00","id":1472205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019d personally would be happier if the creator of the imbuement also used Fate 2. </div> </div> </div>That seems perfectly reasonable and another Mark against imbued items in my mind.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the rest of your comments, I've read them and laughed a few times.<br /> <br /> I suppose my only other question is, if an act of Hubris is required (as indeed the rules state) what Acranum's purview would that be under? Death for the Soul? Mind for the mind? Fate for the Intentions (like you don't just get mana for accidentally killing an animal or stepping on it, you have to intend to kill it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T16:19:30-08:00","id":1472206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472202#post1472202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify, a mana battery is an item that holds a certain amount of mana. While holding it, a user can transfer it into their pattern. More details can be found on page 70 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i></div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you, i thought i had seen the term used and presumed it was a reference to making imbued items with mana pools to carry around extra mana (while Eidolon already seem to have that). <br /> <br /> I suppose the advantage is how easy it is to access the mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it might make more sense to create a Supernal Knowledge spirit by utilizing a Patterning of Prime and Spirit (more details on page 124 of the core book) on an existing one. Modify them to gain sustenance from Supernal secrets. Now it has to do its job well in order to survive.<br /> <br /> Its naturally invisible in Twilight (unless someone has the Spirit 2 Attainment), can manipulate others and maintain a disguise by Fettering itself to them, can become better at its job by Claiming a host, can make quick exits via Discorporation. It has the flexibility of Influences and the Numina for more precise tasks. It also has an incentive to cultivate a spirit choir to help it be more efficient at its job, if not an entire Mystery Cult that flies under the radar of Awakened society by being a Nameless organization. </div> </div> </div>I completely misunderstood what you meant. So Patterning, like Living Pillar of Flame, you mean a spirit which has been transformed into the Purview of Prime? That i kinda like... (More than my wrong assumption about this just being a use of Shape Spirit, to change the spirit's fundamental nature into a spirit of Supernal Knowledge).<br /> <br /> I do think a full Patterning would also allow you to create something more like a supernal being, or also turn a Spirit into a Ghost/Goetia... Not sure what use that would be... Could you drag a spirit of Supernal Knowledge into your Onerious, and use it as an internal wikipedia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T16:33:24-08:00","id":1472207,"title":"","content":"I meant more along the lines of a being halfway between both Arcana. In essence I imagined a spirit which can act see Supernal magic, can affect all layers of Twilight and can manipulate either Essence or mana to fuel itself.<br /> <br /> Regarding extracting it into their Oneiros, sure its possible. A precedent exists, just modify the spell Goetic Evocation from page 90 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>. Sorry if I keep going back to that book, it just has that many interesting spells. Anyway, using that spell means you are placing a monomaniacal knowledge being into the part of your soul that defines your personality and emotions, so it wouldn't be exactly good for the subject's sanity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T18:16:26-08:00","id":1472212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472205#post1472205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems perfectly reasonable and another Mark against imbued items in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> Imbued items aren\u2019t bad, just mildly unwieldy. They are best for minions and allies who don\u2019t have the same capabilities you do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472205#post1472205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for all the rest of your comments, I've read them and laughed a few times.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then I have done well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472205#post1472205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose my only other question is, if an act of Hubris is required (as indeed the rules state) what Acranum's purview would that be under? Death for the Soul? Mind for the mind? Fate for the Intentions (like you don't just get mana for accidentally killing an animal or stepping on it, you have to intend to kill it).</div> </div> </div> </div> A tricky question, I think.<br /> <br /> Wisdom, in many ways, is a barrier between a Mage\u2019s Magic, and the Fallen World. This is best seen in the long term nimbus, which is free to wreak more havoc the lower one\u2019s Wisdom. Something comparable would be the Gauntlet, to the Shadow and the Fallen world. The Gauntlet falls under Spirit, and thus I think Wisdom falls under Prime. In fact, the only spell that I know of that interacts with Wisdom is Nimbus Tuning, which is Prime Knowing (in SoS). But I\u2019m not sure it completely falls under Prime. I think it has parts of it scattered throughout the Subtle Arcana, since in no uncertain terms, Wisdom is part of the Soul. After all, when Wisdom fails, Rapture follows. And Rapture is the Soul breaking under the strain of Obsession.<br /> <br /> But why does the act of sacrifice grant mana? If it relies on the Act of Hubris, other acts of Hubris do not grant mana. So then, why does this one in particular? Why does sacrifice generate power, not just for the Awakened, but certain Sleepwalkers and Vampires too? Is the important thing not the act of hubris, but the breaking point itself?<br /> <br /> I think we need definite answers to those questions before there can be a clear answer. Perhaps someone with more setting knowledge than me can give a better answer. That being said, if a player of mine wanted to do this, Prime and any of the other Subtle Arcana would work. Frankly, I have a hunch Mind or Death might be able to do it alone, depending on if the important thing is the damage to the mind or the soul, ie if a breaking point with any integrity like stat works.<br /> <br /> Edit: minor clarification<br /> Second edit: I adore the concept of that Prime Familiar. That\u2019s not really important, but I feel it must be said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-10-2022, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T00:27:14-08:00","id":1472227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I adore the concept of that Prime Familiar. That\u2019s not really important, but I feel it must be said </div> </div> </div>This raises another question, are supernal beings under the purview of Prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T00:51:24-08:00","id":1472228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472227#post1472227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This raises another question, are supernal beings under the purview of Prime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how the game bothers to categorize and name ten types of Supernal entities by Arcana, I\u2019d rule that you have to use the corresponding Arcanum. So Forces for Seraphim, Time for Anachronisms, etc. Gonna have to check if SoS said anything, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T04:24:45-08:00","id":1472235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472212#post1472212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Imbued items aren\u2019t bad, just mildly unwieldy. They are best for minions and allies who don\u2019t have the same capabilities you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are a lot of spells, and how much any given one of them can work within the limits of an imbued item will vary.<br /> <br /> If I'm a member of any Path other than Acanthus, and somebody hands me a coin that can answer questions about the future, I'm not turning it down even if getting it to work is a bit of a strain on two dice. Like, I'm not generally going to need to increase any of the factors, so I can just about get it going (maybe strain a bit with Willpower). Even if it wasn't given the Reach option to ask more sophisticated questions.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well why doesn't the character just learn the Time Arcanum?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because the XP that could go towards that is preferred for other things, and all they really want out of Time is the divination anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T15:02:47-08:00","id":1472268,"title":"","content":"Weird question time: Can Life by itself make alterations like weapons attached to the body? Like a bone sword, or spines that can be fired like a ranged weapon. If so, do those Brawl/Athletics or Weaponry/Firearms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T15:49:24-08:00","id":1472275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472268#post1472268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird question time: Can Life by itself make alterations like weapons attached to the body? Like a bone sword, or spines that can be fired like a ranged weapon. If so, do those Brawl/Athletics or Weaponry/Firearms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the limits of what's physically possible to achieve when using purely biological materials.<br /> The most relevant published spell, Transform Life, is exclusively concerned with traits that exist in other creatures, but there's really nothing that says you can't freely reshape a living subject. As long as it's a singular trait it should still be Weaving, but unlike Transform Life, a single spell should not be able to grant multiple different &quot;weapon&quot; traits that aren't based on a common base effect. I.e. a spell could have bone spikes for melee combat and a Reach option to make them launchable, but a spell could not grant both bone spikes and an acid spray.<br /> <br /> Now, what's actually possible to do, I don't know. I'm not an expert in biology. You can definitely make short blades or stingers that uses Brawl, but could you make a bone sword long enough to require Weaponry without it breaking on a hit? And how would you handle loss of biomass when launching projectiles? Would you take damage from losing part of your body's mass?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T19:33:48-08:00","id":1472288,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answer.<br /> I have new question, possibly weirder: What would it take to talk to someone who died in childbirth, as if they had lived instead? Is that even possible? (For context, I thought of a character who wanted to talk to a older sibling who didn\u2019t make it, and wanted to see the differences between them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T21:08:42-08:00","id":1472290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472268#post1472268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird question time: Can Life by itself make alterations like weapons attached to the body? Like a bone sword, or spines that can be fired like a ranged weapon. If so, do those Brawl/Athletics or Weaponry/Firearms?</div> </div> </div> </div>To supplement Tessie's answer, a general thing to keep in mind with Supernal magic as a narrative device is that, as-presented, it cannot be an exercise of pure abstraction to devise a new spell \u2014 some kernel of the concrete world and its symbolism should come into play as a grounding factor in the process of magical innovation, whether that's figuring out how to exploit the qualities of a Mystery or just spending a chapter or three Obsessing over how to get the shape of the Imago to work out and taking meaningful inspiration from the events accompanying that contemplation.<br /> <br /> Established biology supplemented by Perfecting spells can cover a lot of ground, but as mentioned, Life doesn't give you the tools to be exempt from the issues of physically using your new adaptations. Wonderful Machine probably isn't entirely required for replicating stuff at the level of the simple machines (the pulley and the wheel and axle notwithstanding), but I feel like if you're trying to create biological features that directly evoke tools that mankind devised (e.g. arm-blades that are clearly just swords grafted to your limbs instead of simple claws or sharp plates of armor) you're jumping into symbolism that entails Matter.<br /> <br /> The general focus of the Skills is such that Brawl is used for weapons that are an inseparable part of your body that don't reach much further than the part of the body that's moving them and Firearms is for weapons whose short range is nevertheless long enough that you'd basically have to be an Olympic athlete to cross the same distance in a single turn of running. They overwhelming majority of published powers representing a mode of attack that's part of the character's body use Brawl or Athletics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472288#post1472288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have new question, possibly weirder: What would it take to talk to someone who died in childbirth, as if they had lived instead? Is that even possible? (For context, I thought of a character who wanted to talk to a older sibling who didn\u2019t make it, and wanted to see the differences between them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Postcognition using Temporal Sympathy, cast as a combined spell with Prophecy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T21:16:38-08:00","id":1472291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472288#post1472288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your answer.<br /> I have new question, possibly weirder: What would it take to talk to someone who died in childbirth, as if they had lived instead? Is that even possible? (For context, I thought of a character who wanted to talk to a older sibling who didn\u2019t make it, and wanted to see the differences between them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there was a summonable Supernal Being in Summoners (1E supplement) that did something similar\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T04:43:20-08:00","id":1472302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472290#post1472290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Postcognition using Temporal Sympathy, cast as a combined spell with Prophecy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, the parameters for attaching spells to ones that call for Temporal Sympathy eludes me a bit, but it's in the Attainment description so I'm at least open to ideas for how it would work.<br /> <br /> Still,Prophecy as written wouldn't really provide a result like what has been asked for. It could provide insight into events that could happen to a subject out of the hypothetical scenario of still being alive (and only as many answers as the spell's Potency), but not model a person to the point of being able to converse with them. That to me sounds like Imperial Practice of Dynamics.<br /> <br /> So like, legendary Artifact, assistance from Aeon Glorianna, or summoning a suitable Anachronism seems necessary. I recall the one 21C Hermit is referring to as not quite being along the lines of the question, but close enough to suggest that the adjustment is within the possibilities of the Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T05:13:46-08:00","id":1472303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472291#post1472291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there was a summonable Supernal Being in Summoners (1E supplement) that did something similar\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, the Supernal being uses a temporal sympathy link to the imitate the person. Its almost perfect, but it always has a flaw that reminds you its not. Could be the voice, a personality trait, hair color, etc. It stays around until someone calls it out as a fake, whereupon it returns to the Supernal with the offered sympathetic thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T05:22:13-08:00","id":1472305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472302#post1472302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit, the parameters for attaching spells to ones that call for Temporal Sympathy eludes me a bit, but it's in the Attainment description so I'm at least open to ideas for how it would work.<br /> <br /> Still,Prophecy as written wouldn't really provide a result like what has been asked for. It could provide insight into events that could happen to a subject out of the hypothetical scenario of still being alive (and only as many answers as the spell's Potency), but not model a person to the point of being able to converse with them. That to me sounds like Imperial Practice of Dynamics.<br /> <br /> So like, legendary Artifact, assistance from Aeon Glorianna, or summoning a suitable Anachronism seems necessary. I recall the one 21C Hermit is referring to as not quite being along the lines of the question, but close enough to suggest that the adjustment is within the possibilities of the Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about using a custom spell mixing elements of Psychic Genesis and Prophecy. Using Temporal Sympathy, you lock on to the point of divergence. Then Time speculates on the timeline where they would have lived and Mind builds a personality based on those parameters. Its still just a copy of them, but I imagine its close enough to grant closure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-12-2022, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T13:34:50-08:00","id":1472324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472305#post1472305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about using a custom spell mixing elements of Psychic Genesis and Prophecy. Using Temporal Sympathy, you lock on to the point of divergence. Then Time speculates on the timeline where they would have lived and Mind builds a personality based on those parameters. Its still just a copy of them, but I imagine its close enough to grant closure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for a start, I'm thinking that Prophecy establishes a reasonable standard for the limits of Patterning an alternate or hypothetical future, and it seems far smaller than the scope of a human life.<br /> <br /> And Psychic Genesis is sufficient to bring up a Rank 1 Goetia, 2 at a Reach, and if Goetia are anything like spirits and ghosts then the first two Ranks constitute a consciousness less sophisticated than that of a human.<br /> <br /> I think the best such a spell could produce would be a snapshot of a subject's one opinion on one topic (per Potency). You're not making somebody you can converse with, you're staring through a keyhole to try and get some insight into them.<br /> <br /> I think short of archmastery, your most surefire way to get an idea of what a non-existant person would be like is to go back in time, alter the course of events so they lived, and then inhabit the timeline in which they exist for a while. Cancel the spell before the changes become Lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T17:12:17-08:00","id":1472333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472324#post1472324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Psychic Genesis is sufficient to bring up a Rank 1 Goetia, 2 at a Reach, and if Goetia are anything like spirits and ghosts then the first two Ranks constitute a consciousness less sophisticated than that of a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist's perspective on Rank 1 human ghosts is that they're still people, just massively hampered by being caught up in the circumstances of their death. Per Astral realms, the most common goetia that aren't just living scenery are Rank 1, have no Numina, and are largely indistinguishable from normal people aside from living in the collective unconscious; none of the treatment we've seen for the Astral in 2e appears to fully invalidate this presentation.<br /> <br /> Even setting aside the question of Rank 1, Rank 2 ghosts are used as the benchmark for &quot;ghosts largely indistinguishable from living people,&quot; described as &quot;intelligent&quot; in Mage and &quot;sapient&quot; in Geist. A Rank 2 ephemeral being is generally the approximate NPC equivalent of a basic supernatural PC in power and cognizance, even bearing in mind that that subset of ephemeral beings also includes its share of animalistic monsters and inanimate objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T19:14:23-08:00","id":1472341,"title":"","content":"In addition, unlike <i>Goetic Invocation</i>, which fills in the blanks using the symbolic information around the soul stone, the use of Temporal Sympathy allows a comprehensive and objective reference for the mind being duplicated. Now I feel like codifying this into a full spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T19:48:31-08:00","id":1472346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can turn stuff into Mana, it\u2019s just that it takes Prime 4 and the appropriate Arcanum 4 to do so. </div> </div> </div>Ok, so a mage who has studied how Changelings harvest glamour (mystery) could attempt to replicate the feat and then using Patterning to convert the energy into mana (Mind 4+ Prime 4). As an example (my other suggestions are copying vampire blood extraction, Life 4 + Prime 4 - which is close to blood sacrifice, but doesn't require killing the subject of an act of Hubris - though it may well be, and an equivalent of channel essence, drain vitae, Death 4 + Prime 4 to take blood points from a vampire and convert them i to mana).<br /> <br /> Edit: moving to a seperate post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-12-2022, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T19:52:32-08:00","id":1472347,"title":"","content":"Seperate question, just so i understand how advanced scale works (pushing it to its mechanical limits).<br /> <br /> i was looking at sensory range, mass subject spell (-20 dice pool penalty to target 5,120 subjects). And my thinking is that -20 isn't that hard (dice pool of Gnosis 5 + Arcana 5 + ritual timex6 3hours+ Mundras skill + persona + sacrament + mantra = dice pool of 29 (using a +3 sacrament, +4 persona (shadow name, cabal theme) enchance skill to 5 dots if you don't have the full Mundras skill...).<br /> <br /> The hardest thing seems to be keeping the 5,120 targets in sensory range for 3 hours - presumably you do something like go to a concert and target the audience members - but you can't keep sensing them all individually... Like you can focus on them one at a time or hear the noise they are generating...<br /> <br /> Alternatively this is 5,120 buildings of size 60 (which are arguably easier to target given that buildings don't tend to move about and are big enough to clearly make out at sensory range from some distance...)<br /> <br /> Is this (pushed to the limit) how advanced scale is supposed to work (and you can do that as an instant spell with 1 reach, 1 willpower and a loss of 2 dice...but you still have to build you imago around 5,120 targets, doing so in a few turns seems like the crowd of humans won't move around as much, but if you needed to focus on them it would take much more time...)<br /> <br /> Edit: to get a ritual with teamwork to up this dice pool allows indefinite duration spells, though with a spell which has duration as the primary factor, mastery means your default duration is 1 year, right? So 2 reach, 1 mana and -2 dice pool pentaly to turn this effect into an indefinite one.<br /> <br /> Or in total, sensory range, advanced scale, advanced duration, indefinite duration = 4 reach, +1 mana.<br /> Or 5 reach, 1 willpower and 1 mana for instant casting. With a 7 dice pool remaining... (EG: You could cast an indefinite soul armour on 5,120 people, without any paradox risk - at ritual time or 3 dice of paradox at instant time)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-12-2022, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T20:27:02-08:00","id":1472349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472347#post1472347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seperate question, just so i understand how advanced scale works (pushing it to its mechanical limits).<br /> <br /> i was looking at sensory range, mass subject spell (-20 dice pool penalty to target 5,120 subjects). And my thinking is that -20 isn't that hard (dice pool of Gnosis 5 + Arcana 5 + ritual timex6 3hours+ Mundras skill + persona + sacrament + mantra = dice pool of 29 (using a +3 sacrament, +4 persona (shadow name, cabal theme) enchance skill to 5 dots if you don't have the full Mundras skill...).<br /> <br /> The hardest thing seems to be keeping the 5,120 targets in sensory range for 3 hours - presumably you do something like go to a concert and target the audience members - but you can't keep sensing them all individually... Like you can focus on them one at a time or hear the noise they are generating...<br /> <br /> Alternatively this is 5,120 buildings of size 60 (which are arguably easier to target given that buildings don't tend to move about and are big enough to clearly make out at sensory range from some distance...)<br /> <br /> Is this (pushed to the limit) how advanced scale is supposed to work (and you can do that as an instant spell with 1 reach, 1 willpower and a loss of 2 dice...but you still have to build you imago around 5,120 targets, doing so in a few turns seems like the crowd of humans won't move around as much, but if you needed to focus on them it would take much more time...)<br /> <br /> Edit: to get a ritual with teamwork to up this dice pool allows indefinite duration spells, though with a spell which has duration as the primary factor, mastery means your default duration is 1 year, right? So 2 reach, 1 mana and -2 dice pool pentaly to turn this effect into an indefinite one.<br /> <br /> Or in total, sensory range, advanced scale, advanced duration, indefinite duration = 4 reach, +1 mana.<br /> Or 5 reach, 1 willpower and 1 mana for instant casting. With a 7 dice pool remaining... (EG: You could cast an indefinite soul armour on 5,120 people, without any paradox risk - at ritual time or 3 dice of paradox at instant time)</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds difficult to prepare, since you will need:<br /> <br /> - The spell as a rote, which means either requisitioning a grimmoire via Order status (doubling the casting time), finding one, borrowing one via a boon, finding a mentor or creating the rote yourself. It then needs to have a skill mudra that the caster has maximum proficiency in (which can be arranged with Mind).<br /> <br /> - A master level in that Arcana, meaning heavy Arcane XP investment <br /> <br /> - A safe space where they can commit for 6 hours of uninterrupted casting. This would grant a +7 bonus, which is compromised of a +5 from extended ritual time (core book page 114) and a +2 from using a ritual time cleansing yantra (Signs of Sorcery page 53). Reporters, enemies and local Sleepers can all cause interruptions and this is more likely in a largely populated target area.<br /> <br /> - Casting a mantra only takes a turn, so one might as well use it<br /> <br /> - Since the spell is taking ritual time, throw a +2 from a rune for free if casting on the area. Otherwise, they would need to paint runes in all 5000 subjects.<br /> <br /> With the mantra, mudra, cleansing and rune, all 4 yantra slots for a Gnosis 5 mage are taken. At that point, the easiest way to add more dice is probably to use a high Potency version of Exceptional Luck (core book page 135).<br /> <br /> Even then, provided the runes aren't used, the other alternatives require heavy investment. The +2 sacraments require the mage to go through extra effort to get the needed supernatural components and a Shadow Name may not necessarily symbollically resonate with the spell. The dedicated Shadow Name, the custom rote, the rare ingredients, this sounds like a cast conducted with ample preparation and investment, pulling it off is anything but simple.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Additional notes:</b><br /> <br /> The teamwork spell would require people who know the Arcanum to avoid a -3 penalty (core book page 119) and have rehersed the casting to avoid the -2 penalty (Signs of Sorcery page 55), adding more preparation time.<br /> <br /> Assuming all are Gnosis 5 masters, the instant spell would cause 9 paradox dice, since Gnosis 5 gets 3 dice per Reach. This is the bare minimum per caster, provided their Paradox pool is clean at that point. So preparing a lot of mana is necessary to avoid potentially summoning a Rank 6 Abyssal Invader (core book 116), which would not only cause cataclysmic harm, but also be near impossible for non-archmages to banish. Even if the casters managed to send the Invader back, the Lex Magicka would probably rule this as a crime worthy of Spiritual Oblivion (destroying the condemned's soul). <br /> <br /> Lastly, you would need to supplement it with a way for all participants to magically perceive all possible targets, otherwise sensory range will not be able to affect all subjects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-13-2022, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T01:21:12-08:00","id":1472353,"title":"","content":"I don't see how runes would help, 1) the need to be written in the subject - and take ritual time to compete - very hard with 5 thousand unwitting subjects.<br /> <br /> 2) for an indefinite spell, this is rather unwise as it will end as soon as the runes are disturbed.<br /> <br /> I am assuming you have a master at the centre of this casting (with or without teamwork) so they can create the rote - and teach it to all able to cast the spell for teamwork if that is necessary (and i just realised that can get a +1 from order rote specialisation, but I presume this doesn't allow you to go to +6 just like enhanced skill beyond normal human limits can't exceed the +5 mundras bonus).<br /> <br /> In this case for a sheilding spell, you get 4 free reach, and avoid any paradox roll. Probably worth the investment. <br /> <br /> Actually i think maintaining sensory range is the hardest. If someone leaves the area during casting to go to the toilet, or you turn around to pick something up, they go out of visual range. If you are using your hearing for sensory range, it seems much harder to pick out any individual subject. If using smell harder still touch is an odd sense to consider using for sensory range, but might be possible if everyone files past you and you don't have to keep touching them... (Taste is right out!)<br /> <br /> &quot;The Advanced Range factor is sensory, meaning that the mage must be able to directly see, hear, or sense her subject&quot;<br /> <br /> This does not specify that you must focus on the subject, or be able to see them directly for the entire ritual time... Using exceptional luck with a big bonus would do away with the need for either ritual or teamwork. Which makes everything much easier; though you have to find a someone to cast that spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T01:39:58-08:00","id":1472354,"title":"","content":"In fact, beyond sensory range, you can get touch range with a brawl or weaponry action. This suggests touch includes touching them with something the caster is holding.<br /> <br /> As such, for large groups can you have everyone hold hands and use touch range (this is assuming willing participants).<br /> <br /> EDIT: i am assuming they all have to be touching at the same time, and not allow them file past, shaking hands with the caster over the course of a ritual time period. Though that seems to be as reasonable as casting on 5,000 people at sensory range - as they may be moving around a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-13-2022, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T10:38:28-08:00","id":1472369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472353#post1472353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am assuming you have a master at the centre of this casting (with or without teamwork) so they can create the rote - and teach it to all able to cast the spell for teamwork if that is necessary (and i just realised that can get a +1 from order rote specialisation, but I presume this doesn't allow you to go to +6 just like enhanced skill beyond normal human limits can't exceed the +5 mundras bonus).</div> </div> </div> </div> I don\u2019t think there is a problem with going to +6, I think there would be a different arrangement of the sentences if they didn\u2019t want such a outcome to be possible. It would have been better to say that \u201chaving the order skill adds extra dot of skill for the purposes of the dice bonus\u201d if they wanted the cap at +5. Instead, they say, when using your orders skill, add a die. That doesn\u2019t suggest a cap at +5 to me. That being said, If you think it makes more sense to cap the total at +5, then by all means, do so.<br /> <br /> As for helping the spell, most arcanum can provide minor help, by causing certain yantras to be more convenient. Mind in particular can increase the dice gained by using Willpower, which will help with teamwork, and Prime can increase the spell dicepool directly like Exceptional Luck. (Requires +2 reach)<br /> <br /> Also, depending on the character, the first level of the Egregore merit really helps with teamwork spell casting. An automatic extra die per full participant is quite good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T10:49:07-08:00","id":1472372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472369#post1472369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don\u2019t think there is a problem with going to +6, I think there would be a different arrangement of the sentences if they didn\u2019t want such a outcome to be possible. It would have been better to say that \u201chaving the order skill adds extra dot of skill for the purposes of the dice bonus\u201d if they wanted the cap at +5. Instead, they say, when using your orders skill, add a die. That doesn\u2019t suggest a cap at +5 to me. That being said, If you think it makes more sense to cap the total at +5, then by all means, do so.<br /> <br /> As for helping the spell, most arcanum can provide minor help, by causing certain yantras to be more convenient. Mind in particular can increase the dice gained by using Willpower, which will help with teamwork, and Prime can increase the spell dicepool directly like Exceptional Luck. (Requires +2 reach)<br /> <br /> Also, depending on the character, the first level of the Egregore merit really helps with teamwork spell casting. An automatic extra die per full participant is quite good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even Egregore can be substituted and surpassed, especially since all participants must have it to get the benefit. All that is required is to find a Rank 2+ ephemeral being of Teamwork (I think a goetia might be easiest). Then have them use their Strengthen Influence to grant extra dice, with any used Essence being replenished via a use of Making. Requires a bit of diplomacy, but is still very viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T10:56:46-08:00","id":1472375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472372#post1472372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Even Egregore can be substituted and surpassed, especially since all participants must have it to get the benefit. All that is required is to find a Rank 2+ ephemeral being of Teamwork (I think a goetia might be easiest). Then have them use their Strengthen Influence to grant extra dice, with any used Essence being replenished via a use of Making. Requires a bit of diplomacy, but is still very viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, yeah that works much better. <br /> New but related question: is it possible to use Time or Mind (or both) to be able to spend more than one willpower per action?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T15:47:55-08:00","id":1472389,"title":"","content":"One thought on reapers, is it possible to wait until the point of death and then (if needed shifting sands back a turn) snatch the soul as it is about to leave the body?<br /> <br /> Is this a way to avoid acts of hubris while acquiring souls (whether it is still drowned upon by Consilium or not). I imagine Fate would make it relatively easy to find targets who are about to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T16:03:39-08:00","id":1472390,"title":"","content":"You could just cast Soul Jar on someone who's about to die. When they do, the soul remains stuck in the corpse rather than moving on.<br /> While it's certainly more ethical than taking a soul from someone who's using it, or worse, killing someone for their soul, Wisdom is not a measurement of ethics or morality. It's probably still an Act of Hubris due to the character hindering the soul from moving on without knowing what would've happened, and probably for whatever they want to use the soul for anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T16:23:20-08:00","id":1472391,"title":"","content":"At least you're not leaving a trail of soulless people behind...<br /> <br /> Unrelated question: can i extend a damage spell (saying fraying of mind) so if it has 3 potency and 3 turns duration, the damage is 1 bashing per turn?<br /> <br /> Or make it even slower with extended duration, slowly damaging them over the course of a day? (I'm thinking either a reach or a Creative thaumatergy spell). Just like a mild headache which gets more severe and the damage is drawn out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T16:27:29-08:00","id":1472392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472390#post1472390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wisdom is not a measurement of ethics or morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's not solely about that, but nor are those things incidental. I think the concerns of ethics in Wisdom aren't really abstract matters so much as a question of the attitude one cultivates in how they relate to other people from a position of power; the outcomes of use of power aren't just the domino effect but also how comfortable one is with using it to have licence over other people's lives. I'd say that's why losing Wisdom can give one an Obsession with dominating others and disable their capacity to empathise, and mages are going to look on that as a bad thing for reasons ranging from &quot;the uses of power emerging from that attitude are going to inevitably constitute further hubris&quot; to &quot;Gnosis gives us an awareness of the weight and interconnectedness of all things, and when that has the greatest clarity we're intimately aware of the value of other human lives and of our valuing those things&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T16:30:22-08:00","id":1472393,"title":"","content":"The creative thaumaturgy rules show how damage spells with long durations will periodically apply their Potency damage after intervals equal to the mage's ritual casting time. Make a Fraying spell last for a day, it will cause 3 bashing damage every 3 hours (if you're Gnosis 1). <br /> <br /> I'd say spells that do other forms of damage over time need to produce effects that would already cause that kind of damage, like how Forces can bring about a fire that harms over extended contact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T00:55:37-08:00","id":1472412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472393#post1472393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The creative thaumaturgy rules show how damage spells with long durations will periodically apply their Potency damage after intervals equal to the mage's ritual casting time. Make a Fraying spell last for a day, it will cause 3 bashing damage every 3 hours (if you're Gnosis 1). <br /> <br /> I'd say spells that do other forms of damage over time need to produce effects that would already cause that kind of damage, like how Forces can bring about a fire that harms over extended contact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not thinking about creating effects which then do damage over time (like using forces to create a fire which keeps burning, or presumably you could use life to burst a blood vessel in the brain).<br /> <br /> Just changing the instant Potency damage of a lasting effect direct damage spell into a slower Potency damage over spell duration(or over ritual time, i guess) so 3 bashing every 3 hours (say), but have it slowed to 1 bashing per hour (they would actually heal that naturally... So it would be like a really annoying pain in your head every hour... But i am thinking of an effect which feels like a constant pain).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T01:43:00-08:00","id":1472415,"title":"","content":"The rules do not allow for changing how ritual intervals work like that. Direct damage dealing spells are not meant to cause damage over time, or they would do so as part of their base effect.<br /> <br /> If the point isn't to inflict any actual damage and only cause pain, then that would be much better handled by a Condition.<br /> If you <i>do</i> want to cause damage but at a steady pace not dictated by your Gnosis, then a Tilt would be the best fit.<br /> In both cases the spell would be Withstood by the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T05:54:13-08:00","id":1472426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472415#post1472415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules do not allow for changing how ritual intervals work like that. Direct damage dealing spells are not meant to cause damage over time, or they would do so as part of their base effect.<br /> <br /> If the point isn't to inflict any actual damage and only cause pain, then that would be much better handled by a Condition.<br /> If you <i>do</i> want to cause damage but at a steady pace not dictated by your Gnosis, then a Tilt would be the best fit.<br /> In both cases the spell would be Withstood by the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't that i don't want to cause damage, it is just that dealing less that 1 point of bashing every 15 minutes would mean it keeps healing.<br /> <br /> I guess it is closer to a poisoned condition - though reading the rules on poisons, the tilt seems excessive. Applying a condition seems idealer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T06:58:14-08:00","id":1472432,"title":"","content":"With a Patterning of Life or Mind, you could inflict the Chronic Agony persistent condition. Its definitely painful, its very inconvenient since it can stun the target at a critical time and can be fine tuned so that the physical (or mental if cast using Mind) stimulus sends a message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T08:35:12-08:00","id":1472444,"title":"","content":"New question: we know from the counter spell attainment that you can mess with someone else's spell as they cast it* - and arguably this is also what is happening during teamwork spell casting - but just thinking of counterspell (not sure how it is described in 2e, i know in 1e it was pulling at the threads of the spell to cause it to come undone) can you instead try to push the spell to do something else - most destructively to draw down more paradox on the caster. <br /> <br /> I think subtle things like changing the subject, or messing with the spell factors should require co- operation (as in the teamwork rules), but just drawing more paradox down should be about as difficult as countering a spell - are there any written rules for this kind of effect (whether for scelesti or abyssal entities?) <br /> <br /> *Not after it is cast, as the only thing that can be done to a spell after it is cast is to reduce /dispell it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T10:38:03-08:00","id":1472455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472444#post1472444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question: we know from the counter spell attainment that you can mess with someone else's spell as they cast it* - and arguably this is also what is happening during teamwork spell casting - but just thinking of counterspell (not sure how it is described in 2e, i know in 1e it was pulling at the threads of the spell to cause it to come undone) can you instead try to push the spell to do something else - most destructively to draw down more paradox on the caster.<br /> <br /> I think subtle things like changing the subject, or messing with the spell factors should require co- operation (as in the teamwork rules), but just drawing more paradox down should be about as difficult as countering a spell - are there any written rules for this kind of effect (whether for scelesti or abyssal entities?)<br /> <br /> *Not after it is cast, as the only thing that can be done to a spell after it is cast is to reduce /dispell it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed describes adding Paradox to another\u2019s spell as one of the primary benefits of embracing your inverted Watchtower. Actually controlling the paradox involved is reserved to those who have successfully negotiated with the Old Man (ie the Aeon of the Abyss) or an Annuaki for power and privilege.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T14:26:03-08:00","id":1472474,"title":"","content":"Lets say a master of Fate casts Swearing an Oath on themselves with advanced duration (1 year) and advanced Potency. The oath is: &quot;I will not allow any of my spells to be dispelled or countered without my consent, may fear visit me should I fail&quot;. So they would be Charmed while under its effect and hexed by the Spooked condition upon failing to uphold it.<br /> <br /> This means any kind of counterspell or dispellation would automatically provoke a Clash of Wills where they would gain +5 bonus dice (+4 from duration and +1 from advanced Potency). This makes me wonder about 2 specific scenarios:<br /> <br /> 1- The mage is counterspelled without being aware, unlike Oaths Fullfilled, there is no restriction regarding whether the phenomenon could be perceived by Mage Sight or not, so would the Clash of Wills with a dice bonus automatically trigger before the counterspell could affect the Imago being made ?<br /> <br /> 2- A Supernal Dispellation is cast at the Sworn Oaths spell itself, what happens ? Does the Clash of Wills take precedence or does the suppression effect of the dispellation act first ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T23:02:21-08:00","id":1472490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472444#post1472444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think subtle things like changing the subject, or messing with the spell factors should require co- operation</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing a spell's subject strikes me as being far from subtle.<br /> <br /> Conventional magic cannot alter the parameters of spells. It requires archmastery.<br /> <br /> I think Nasnasi or Baalim powers can at least wield Paradox to force a spell to experience Dissonance, but that only ever breaks it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T01:20:18-08:00","id":1472496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472490#post1472490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing a spell's subject strikes me as being far from subtle.<br /> <br /> Conventional magic cannot alter the parameters of spells. It requires archmastery.<br /> <br /> I think Nasnasi or Baalim powers can at least wield Paradox to force a spell to experience Dissonance, but that only ever breaks it down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not after it is cast certainly. <br /> <br /> So yeah, dissonance is after the fact, or equivalent to dispellation. My thoughts go back to somewhere around page 285 of this thread where someone pointed out how counterspelling is reactive, but if successful it only uses up both of your actions for the turn leaving nothing happen. Therefore paradox is more interesting narratively.<br /> <br /> Adding paradox to their spell could force the spell to alter reach or change targets (but not in control of either player) or any other normal paradox effect controlled by the storyteller (or force a wisdom roll to take resistant damage into the caster's pattern).<br /> <br /> And it seems to at least be on par with Compelling practice (which is the level of the counter spell attainment) in that pulling paradox into the world is one of the normal things that spells do. Therefore should be relatively easy (if you know how to do it, no doubt the Guardians would consider this knowledge rather dangerous).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it could force the caster to spend mana to mitigate (assuming this is allowed) possibly delaying the spell.<br /> <br /> Which actually leads me to another question. Can a spell be countered at any point, if it takes a number of turns equal to the number of yantras being used and mana spending limits required to cast, is the Nimbus flaring for all of these turns and can you attempt to counter it each turn?<br /> <br /> What about multiple attempts to counter it from different sources? Do they get any bonus?<br /> <br /> And secondly, what about teamwork rituals, if someone wants to mess with your spell casting, can they intentionally fuck up, or attempt to alter the imago (change targets etc) when doing a ritual spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-15-2022, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T01:31:40-08:00","id":1472497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472474#post1472474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say a master of Fate casts Swearing an Oath on themselves with advanced duration (1 year) and advanced Potency. The oath is: &quot;I will not allow any of my spells to be dispelled or countered without my consent, may fear visit me should I fail&quot;. So they would be Charmed while under its effect and hexed by the Spooked condition upon failing to uphold it.<br /> <br /> This means any kind of counterspell or dispellation would automatically provoke a Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, my reading is that it would not offer a clash of wills, that would apply if someone we're to try to supernaturally compel you to break the Oath. Casting dispellation doesn't compel you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a supernatural power would force the subject to violate her oath \u2014 either by action or inaction \u2014 the mage may make a Clash of Wills against the effect </div> </div> </div>So if a mind spell attempted to force you to break your Oath you would cause a clash of will. Otherwise you are only failing to fulfill your Oath not being forced to.<br /> <br /> There will is no clash of wills if you swear an Oath to protect your cabal and someone shoots one of them. You have failed, but you we're not forced to fail your Oath by someone. This is equivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T08:42:50-08:00","id":1472501,"title":"","content":"The key word I am focusing on is inaction. If the mage is unable to perceive the supernatural power or counter it, then the power is forcing them to break their oath and provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> If your spell is being countered, you cannot counter that since you already used your cast for the round. Therefore, it would cause a violation of the oath.<br /> <br /> The main drawback is that a Clash of Wills is not as consistent as something like Wards &amp; Signs, which adds to the Withstand (or generates it in cases where it normally wouldn't apply). With this method, you are relying on lucky rolls to protect your spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T08:56:16-08:00","id":1472502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472496#post1472496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not after it is cast certainly. <br /> <br /> So yeah, dissonance is after the fact, or equivalent to dispellation. My thoughts go back to somewhere around page 285 of this thread where someone pointed out how counterspelling is reactive, but if successful it only uses up both of your actions for the turn leaving nothing happen. Therefore paradox is more interesting narratively.<br /> <br /> Adding paradox to their spell could force the spell to alter reach or change targets (but not in control of either player) or any other normal paradox effect controlled by the storyteller (or force a wisdom roll to take resistant damage into the caster's pattern).<br /> <br /> And it seems to at least be on par with Compelling practice (which is the level of the counter spell attainment) in that pulling paradox into the world is one of the normal things that spells do. Therefore should be relatively easy (if you know how to do it, no doubt the Guardians would consider this knowledge rather dangerous).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it could force the caster to spend mana to mitigate (assuming this is allowed) possibly delaying the spell.<br /> <br /> Which actually leads me to another question. Can a spell be countered at any point, if it takes a number of turns equal to the number of yantras being used and mana spending limits required to cast, is the Nimbus flaring for all of these turns and can you attempt to counter it each turn?<br /> <br /> What about multiple attempts to counter it from different sources? Do they get any bonus?<br /> <br /> And secondly, what about teamwork rituals, if someone wants to mess with your spell casting, can they intentionally fuck up, or attempt to alter the imago (change targets etc) when doing a ritual spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Paradox thing is part of Scelestus practices, expanded upon in Nameless &amp; Accursed. The lowest levels involve Befouling, trying to direct where the Paradox will strike. As the mage joins more with the Abyss, they gain more perks, but lose some freedom with each step. Its also an addictive practice and generally considered a violation of the Lex Magicka. Anyone who progressed far enough to control the nature of the Paradox has reached the point where both the Pentacle and Seers will cooperate to annihilate them.<br /> <br /> The only other way to alter another mage's spell is with archmastery, its normally far beyond the power of mages. The only &quot;exception&quot; are imbued items with flexible Reach, but those are built with more time and effort to accommodate that option. The nature of imbuements is different than conventional spells and is further explored in Signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> A spell can be counterspelled at any point before the Imago is released. Regardless of casting time and yantras used, counterspell is an instant action.<br /> <br /> Should a mage try to sabotage the team spellcast, it would impose a -3 penalty on all participants due to lack of cooperation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-15-2022, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T10:01:48-08:00","id":1472503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472496#post1472496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not after it is cast certainly.<br /> <br /> So yeah, dissonance is after the fact, or equivalent to dispellation. My thoughts go back to somewhere around page 285 of this thread where someone pointed out how counterspelling is reactive, but if successful it only uses up both of your actions for the turn leaving nothing happen. Therefore paradox is more interesting narratively.<br /> <br /> Adding paradox to their spell could force the spell to alter reach or change targets (but not in control of either player) or any other normal paradox effect controlled by the storyteller (or force a wisdom roll to take resistant damage into the caster's pattern).<br /> <br /> And it seems to at least be on par with Compelling practice (which is the level of the counter spell attainment) in that pulling paradox into the world is one of the normal things that spells do. Therefore should be relatively easy (if you know how to do it, no doubt the Guardians would consider this knowledge rather dangerous).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abyss doesn\u2019t fall under any of the arcanum. Manipulating paradox is the sole domain of the Scelesti, that\u2019s literally what the Scelesti are. The powers of Scelesti don\u2019t correspond to the practices, because the Abyss isn\u2019t a arcanum.<br /> Secondly, pulling paradox into the Fallen isn\u2019t a natural thing that spells do. The Abyss is a layer of oil and pollution that sits between the the Supernal and the Fallen, and it wasn\u2019t always there. The bigger, more complicated the spell, the more gunks gets stuck on the spell when it comes into the Fallen. Supernal Entities, who have a direct connection to the Supernal, don\u2019t risk paradox. They have the closest thing to a natural spell that can be found in the Fallen.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472496#post1472496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which actually leads me to another question. Can a spell be countered at any point, if it takes a number of turns equal to the number of yantras being used and mana spending limits required to cast, is the Nimbus flaring for all of these turns and can you attempt to counter it each turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, well the nimbus should be flaring, the Imago should be forming, and I don\u2019t see a mention of having to wait until the spell fully forms to counter it. So I guess you can do it whenever. Nothing says you can\u2019t try again, but I think there is a rule somewhere saying repeated attempts take a stacking -1 dice penalty on repeated actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472496#post1472496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about multiple attempts to counter it from different sources? Do they get any bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div> Other than being able to try? They could use teamwork, probably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472496#post1472496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And secondly, what about teamwork rituals, if someone wants to mess with your spell casting, can they intentionally fuck up, or attempt to alter the imago (change targets etc) when doing a ritual spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Teamwork spell casting isn\u2019t a equal partnership, someone has to take lead who also has the requirements to cast the spell. Teamwork spell casting merely uses another mage as a pseudo-yantra, kinda like willpower. Someone can refuse to play their part, but they can\u2019t significantly change the Imago.<br /> <br /> Edit: Grammar<br /> Edit 2: Supernal Entities don\u2019t have a direct connection to the Supernal, they are a piece of the Supernal pulled down to the Fallen world. Slight, but significant distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-15-2022, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T10:13:48-08:00","id":1472505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472501#post1472501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key word I am focusing on is inaction. If the mage is unable to perceive the supernatural power or counter it, then the power is forcing them to break their oath and provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> If your spell is being countered, you cannot counter that since you already used your cast for the round. Therefore, it would cause a violation of the oath.<br /> <br /> The main drawback is that a Clash of Wills is not as consistent as something like Wards &amp; Signs, which adds to the Withstand (or generates it in cases where it normally wouldn't apply). With this method, you are relying on lucky rolls to protect your spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>The benefit you gain from the Oath is the boon. Balanced by the hex if you break your Oath, whether by choice, inaction, or accident. <br /> <br /> Now if a smart opponent comes along and thinks, i will make them break their Oath so they suffer the bad stuff, and uses some kind of supernatural power (eg Vampire Dominate discipline) to force you to break your Oath, the spell offers a clash of wills* to protect you from that power. <br /> <br /> EDIT: for clarification, someone trying to dispel one of your spells doesn't force you to do or not do anything. It may result in your Oath being broken, that isn't the same as forcing you to break it (or allow it to be broken through forcing your inaction).<br /> <br /> It doesn't give you a clash of wills for anything else. This is like if you have sworn to protect someone it would not give you a clash to prevent them from being shot (or having a supernatural effect harm them). <br /> <br /> You have to fulfill your Oath all on your own, with only the advantage of the boon to help you.<br /> <br /> *It is unclear to me that this clash of wills benefit from the strength/duration of the Oath spell. The supernatural effect does not directly break the spell - ie prevent the boon/hex, which is the primary effect of the spell... If it was a mind shield which prevented being forced to do something, definitely you would get a clash based on the strength of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-15-2022, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T10:24:45-08:00","id":1472506,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a base principle of the setting's metaphysics would be that something like Paradox doesn't fall under the jurisdiction of the Arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472501#post1472501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key word I am focusing on is inaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's a word that's still in the context of power forcing a mage to do something contrary to the oath.<br /> <br /> Like, the whole thing is predicated on an assumption that people are swearing to do things. I think any interpretation of how its clauses work need to emerge from that, not unusual edge cases.<br /> <br /> You get to Clash Wills against powers that would compel you to the inaction of not trying to act against your spells being stopped or broken, nothing more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T10:31:50-08:00","id":1472507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472506#post1472506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get to Clash Wills against powers that would compel you to the inaction of not trying to act against your spells being stopped or broken, nothing more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go even further - I'm not convinced the clash would he afforded the extra strength from the duration/potency. It is not directly opposing the spell, if you are forced to break your Oath the Hex still applies, so the spell is still in effect. <br /> <br /> If you want a high potency protection against mind influence you would use a mind shield. The protections here are an incidental side effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T10:33:04-08:00","id":1472508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, a base principle of the setting's metaphysics would be that something like Paradox doesn't fall under the jurisdiction of the Arcana. </div> </div> </div>No, it is pure Gnosis which allows a mage to draw paradox from the Abyss, not any specific Arcana. The higher the Gnosis the more paradox.<br /> <br /> EDIT: sorry i missed this<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have the closest thing to a natural spell that can be found in the Fallen. </div> </div> </div>That and legacy attainments which are actually a natural part of the fallen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there is a rule somewhere saying repeated attempts take a stacking -1 dice penalty on repeated actions </div> </div> </div>That rule was definitely a thing, haven't seen it in this edition**. Also in combat i think if you miss a target and try to hit them again you don't suffer from the -1 for repeated actions. <br /> <br /> Not sure that is applicable here. But it seems relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Teamwork spell casting merely uses another mage as a pseudo-yantra, kinda like willpower. Someone can refuse to play their part, but they can\u2019t significantly change the Imago </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, i feel like they are doing more than being a pseudo yantra though. Sure, if they are a sleepwalker and are just going about the some ritual actions yes, that is all they are doing. But if they are a mage at all they are rolling their Gnosis + Arcana and doing spell casting (somehow helping with the imago formation) maybe a big complex spell can be divided up into parts which each helper is casting, and then the primary caster is using those partial imagos to make it easier to create the imago for the complete spell. Unlike a Yantra they can fail in their spell casting roll.<br /> <br /> Also: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each participant must roll for Paradox separately; if any one of the casters releases a Paradox instead of containing it, it affects the entire spell. </div> </div> </div>They can release paradox into the spell... Which kinda brings me back to my original question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So only acting like a Yantra in the sense that a Yantra makes it easier to form an imago.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this method of poluting a spell with paradox can only he done by having the spellcaster intentionally include the help. <br /> <br /> It can't be done either at instant time or without the spellcaster's cooperation. Though it does allow some amount of sabotage by the team mates.<br /> <br /> EDIT: i am going to assume a Scelesti can befoul their teamwork roll to intentionally draw down paradox, if you have accidentally included them.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: actually looking at the teamwork rules on page 214, if you fail a roll you get to make it a dramatic failure. And this gives the primary caster a -4 dice pool pentaly. If you can't cast the spell and are on a chance die (Gnosis -3) can you be more of a detriment than any help...<br /> <br /> **I'm wrong it is above the section on teamwork of 214. Not sure it applies to combat rolls though. You could argue that you're not trying to do the exact same thing, or that the fight is all effectively an extended contested action. Not repeating the exact same thing over and over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-15-2022, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T17:31:37-08:00","id":1472536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472508#post1472508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it is pure Gnosis which allows a mage to draw paradox from the Abyss, not any specific Arcana. The higher the Gnosis the more paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it is a consistent element of Paradox that, unless you are a Scelestus of sufficient initiation, you can't control how it manifests or directly inflict it on other people \u2014 the entire point of the Abyss dangling power over Paradox in front of its servants is that it leads to them trapping themselves in a world where they can't affect anything outside of the corrupted Mage Sight-induced nightmares that have replaced their reality.<br /> <br /> Higher Gnosis doesn't give you root access to another mage's expression of enlightened Will, and spells are discrete objects that don't positively or laterally alter their own parameters without a Quintessence going into their creation. If you want to mess with how a wizard's spells manifest, you mess with the wizard casting the spell to trick them into casting them that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T23:01:03-08:00","id":1472553,"title":"","content":"Supernal Beings are supposed to have Banes in the Mage 2E core. The Black Angels in SoS don't. Which would be the RAW in this case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T00:36:54-08:00","id":1472556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472536#post1472536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it is a consistent element of Paradox that, unless you are a Scelestus of sufficient initiation, you can't control how it manifests or directly inflict it on other people \u2014 the entire point of the Abyss dangling power over Paradox in front of its servants is that it leads to them trapping themselves in a world where they can't affect anything outside of the corrupted Mage Sight-induced nightmares that have replaced their reality.<br /> <br /> Higher Gnosis doesn't give you root access to another mage's expression of enlightened Will</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there are two ways to alter another mage's spell, pull it apart (Gnosis + Arcana/ Gnosis + Prime) and helping them build it (Gnosis + Arcana/Gnosis - 3) with their permission*. <br /> <br /> And given this <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mage can deliberately infect his spells with Paradox, increasing their power. No Order would admit the fact, but any mage can invite Paradox into his spells. </div> </div> </div>It seems likely that 'being Scelesti' just requires knowing that you can cause paradox if you try. (And roll Gnosis to control it).<br /> <br /> *And if your teamwork draws paradox into the fallen you can choose to let it into the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T00:57:57-08:00","id":1472558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472556#post1472556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, there are two ways to alter another mage's spell, pull it apart (Gnosis + Arcana/ Gnosis + Prime) and helping them build it (Gnosis + Arcana/Gnosis - 3) with their permission*.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that trying to litigate this based on citations of possibly comparable precedents isn't really the right way to approach it.<br /> <br /> It's really just a matter of altering the parameters of another mage's spells or forcing them to experience Paradox by means other than being a Scelestus not being on the table for reasons of gameplay and setting. The Counterspell Attainment or being able to participate in a ritual to provide bonus casting dice don't figure into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems likely that 'being Scelesti' just requires knowing that you can cause paradox if you try. (And roll Gnosis to control it).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are degrees of being Scelesti. Being able to Befoul your own spells (induce Paradox deliberately but have a bit of control over how it manifests) is the kind that any mage can do just by knowing the technique. The more elaborate stuff (including the forms where they can impose Paradox in the spells of other mages) requires one to be more transformed by the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T03:46:25-08:00","id":1472559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1203717#post1203717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3/3/2017, on 4chan's /tg/ board, DaveB answered a couple of questions on Shadow Names<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;&gt;DaveB, if you're still around, would it be possible for a mage to have 2 shadow names?<br /> Yeah, just buy the Merit multiple times<br /> <br /> &gt; How much Space would it be required to alter a Shadow Name and/or confer an additional one? Making? Dominions? Entities?<br /> Wouldn't say Space. A Shadow Name's just something you call yourself - the Merit represents it starting to resonante Supernally over time, such that you can use it as a Yantra. I would say Prime. Possibly archmaster-y.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, you can totally have 4, 3-dot merits for<br /> &amp;quot;The Angel of Destruction&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;The Wise Old Witch&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;She who waits in Shadows&amp;quot;, and &amp;quot;The Mystic Leader of Mankind&amp;quot;<br /> It's having at least one Shadow Name which grants your normal life protection from your Nimbus.<br /> Nothing says you can't cultivate multiple separate personas.<br /> I imagine many Guardians do, given the 5-dot Masque benefit can grant a Shadow Name.</div> </div> </div> </div>So multiple Shadow names are ok? Despite the book not explicitly saying so. What limits should there he? Like having to get into costume, prepare for some time... Like i presume this isn't a reflexive action between two spells... Though if it is just a mental tool to help you (a yantra) form an imago, does changing your clothes make a difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T04:09:55-08:00","id":1472561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1204305#post1204305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death Spell Devouring the Slain (Page 130) allows a mage to harvest willpower or mana (dealing damage in a ratio 1:1) for each potency from his target. With 1 reach a mage is allowed to cast this spell on a target that has not received damage. From what is written this seems like a superior version of a spell Rotting Flesh (page 132) or a Rank 4 spell Withering (page 133) allowing the mage to deal lethal damage with a 3 dot arcanum. Is this the intent of a design ? Personally I would rule that the target has to be stationary as the intent of the spell is not to deal damage, but to replenish the mages resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading this question makes me wonder. Pattern scouring can only be done for 1 (resistant) lethal damage per scouring.<br /> <br /> The sentence 'he may Scour the subject\u2019s Pattern for <br /> one point of Mana, dealing one lethal damage in the process, causing existing wounds to open and fester.' <br /> <br /> Would allow for the interpretation that this is 1 lethal total, not 1 lethal per potency of the spell (OR they can take 1 willpower per potency to a limit of the subject's available willpower).<br /> <br /> It doesn't say you can take 1 mana, dealing 1 lethal to the limit of the subjects health boxes... <br /> <br /> So (simple question) does this spell do 1 lethal or 1 lethal per potency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T04:50:57-08:00","id":1472562,"title":"","content":"The spell gives you two choices:<br /> A.) You steal [Potency] Willpower points<br /> OR<br /> B.) You Pattern Scour the subject which has the following effects: you deal <b>one</b> resistant lethal damage AND gain <b>one</b> Mana<br /> <br /> Since the second choice is a Pattern Scouring, it's also subject to your personal Gnosis derived limits for how often you can Pattern Scour. Unless the Reach option is used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T05:31:35-08:00","id":1472565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that trying to litigate this based on citations of possibly comparable precedents isn't really the right way to approach it. </div> </div> </div>Like many questions on this thread about practices and purview, this is about trying to understand the system and what makes sense based on what is already allowed. <br /> <br /> Call it litigating if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T06:46:34-08:00","id":1472566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472565#post1472565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like many questions on this thread about practices and purview, this is about trying to understand the system and what makes sense based on what is already allowed.<br /> <br /> Call it litigating if you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just find there's a difference between &quot;what can a Practice do&quot; and &quot;what if I use the standards of a Practice as a basis for this other unrelated but similar thing being allowed&quot;, and a point at which it keeps being argued on past the point of several people saying &quot;it doesn't really work like that&quot; gets to be a bit much.<br /> <br /> As for other questions:<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure even if Dave said that multiple Shadow Names are permissible, using the Merit or otherwise, considering what the Storytelling chapter has to say about the subject. If I was involved in that conversation, I would ask for the idea to be reconciled to the description of the intimacy of Shadow Names making them not an easy thing to adopt or leave, as well as how it would work with their capacity to shape your life. Like, if you have the names of the head gods of different pantheons, are you going to be afflicted with marks from all of them? Are you only vulnerable to losing an eye when you're acting and casting under the Odin name? It seems excessive.<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to read Devouring the Slain as yielding Mana and lethal damage fully equal to Potency. It comes out less efficient than Pattern Scouring in a way that can still push a mage towards more grievously damaging another person to get more Mana in a way that makes it an interesting affront to Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T07:35:08-08:00","id":1472567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472553#post1472553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal Beings are supposed to have Banes in the Mage 2E core. The Black Angels in SoS don't. Which would be the RAW in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div>My copy shows them having a Bane of indestructible materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T08:40:55-08:00","id":1472573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472553#post1472553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal Beings are supposed to have Banes in the Mage 2E core. The Black Angels in SoS don't. Which would be the RAW in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check that you've got the post-errata version of the book, because I remember reporting the same error for the Red Castellan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T15:34:02-08:00","id":1472589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm inclined to read Devouring the Slain as yielding Mana and lethal damage fully equal to Potency. It comes out less efficient than Pattern Scouring in a way that can still push a mage towards more grievously damaging another person to get more Mana in a way that makes it an interesting affront to Wisdom </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i think i agree. At one lethal (using up your limited pattern scouring) for one mana, not being at all efficient with the mana - compared with blood sacrifice which doesn't even require Death - this seems like a rather poor option.<br /> <br /> It was only the questions about why Death can do lethal at 3 dots that threw me. I think with the 2e 'different Arcana can do different things at different levels' it makes sense that Death of all Arcana would have lethal damage earlier (Not that forces can't rule lethal fire go burn someone at 2 dots...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-16-2022, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T15:36:03-08:00","id":1472590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I was involved in that conversation, I would ask for the idea to be reconciled to the description of the intimacy of Shadow Names making them not an easy thing to adopt or leave, as well as how it would work with their capacity to shape your life. </div> </div> </div>Indeed, all good questions. I think the fact that, where intended, merits say that you can buy them multiple times. Though i suppose an imbued item doesn't say that because it is obvious you could have more than one... So maybe that isn't the convincing argument i hoped for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-17T09:31:24-08:00","id":1472617,"title":"","content":"Do runic yantras have to be created while casting the spell?<br /> <br /> By my reading of the rules, there are two parts to the rules for Runes. One gives rules for how to use runes as a yantra (+2 dice, subject of the spell must have the runes on it, must be for a specific imago etc) and the other gives rules for scribing the runes (takes time equal to the mages ritual interval). While it seems like you could scribe runes as part of a ritual casting, nothing in the rules seems to actually require that to be the case.<br /> <br /> Are the runes themselves the yantra, and thus they can be pre-made, or is the act of inscribing the runes the yantra?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-17T10:00:35-08:00","id":1472619,"title":"","content":"The runes themselves are the Yantra. The rules for creating them are just listed so that there are rules for how long preparations would take. Once the runes are there, using them as a Yantra just requires a reflexive action, or an instant action if they're not the first Yantra you add to your casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-17T10:08:38-08:00","id":1472621,"title":"","content":"Ah, thank you. I thought that was it, but no other yantra has rules for creating it as part of the text so I wasn't sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-17T11:41:42-08:00","id":1472623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472621#post1472621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thank you. I thought that was it, but no other yantra has rules for creating it as part of the text so I wasn't sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not specifically, but I note that all of the Action Yantras have some little exception. Concentration greatly limits what else the mage can do, Mantras can't be used reflexively, Mudras only work with their rotes (and rotes can't be cast without using their Mudras). I think it's all a counterbalancing thing for the fact that these are Yantras that get to be a lot more impromptu than things like environments or tools. Runes aren't quite as versatile as the other Actions, once a rune is inscribed it can only enhance the kind of spell it describes (and also adds a vulnerability that methods lack), but as you say, it provides the opportunity to prepare something ahead of time or place a Yantra that can always be available thereafter.<br /> <br /> Plus, like, I think the main reason for there not to be rules for making the others is that the others aren't really things that get made, or at least where processes for making them are probably more understandable by virtue of what they are. Like, if you need a silver knife for casting, you're either using the usual item creation rules or some form of magic, and either method is self-evident and has its own challenges. Runes differ where they'd only ever be created, but on the face of things it may not be clear how much effort is supposed to be put into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T01:04:05-08:00","id":1472648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1233928#post1233928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very easy to bottle a ghost - you use Death to force them into the Fetter Manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This got me thinking.<br /> <br /> Can you fetter multiple ephemeral entities to the same subject? For example, fettering the ghosts of a mass murderer's victims to their killer? <br /> <br /> Same with possession? Can multiple entities possess the same target? For example a spirit and a ghost possessing the one body? Would they have to take turn? Wrest control from each other? Or can you push a possessing ghost out of a body by putting a spirit in?<br /> <br /> And a last question, the familiar merit says your spirit/ghost/goetia may be fettered. So you can have a cat spirit familiar and fetter it to an actual cat. How little use would this be? Does a cat with the urged condition do much? Or does it do whatever catly things it would have done anyway but with the urging to point it in a particular direction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T05:45:05-08:00","id":1472658,"title":"","content":"On hiding/protecting a spell.<br /> <br /> If you veil a spell (prime 2) and then try to shield it (also prime 2) does your shielding have to overcome the vieling Clash of Wills?<br /> <br /> And vica versa, if you shield it first, and then try to veil it, does the spell withstand being affected, right 'When the subject is the target of a spell, that spell is Withstood with the Potency of Wards and Signs.'?<br /> <br /> (Referring to Supernal Veil and Wards and Signs)<br /> <br /> And secondly, would you need to add subject to the veiling spell to hide both the Wards and Signs and the actual target spell you are protecting?<br /> <br /> Or would it make a difference if the Wards and original spell were cast as a combined spell* (actually perhaps you can't cast Wards and Signs as a combined spell on a target of the spell you are combining it with?)<br /> <br /> <br /> And lastly, would an area dispellation bypass the veiling entirely and dispell all valid spells in the area if possible? <br /> <br /> *Actually would this be the perfect choice for a combined spell, Veil and Shield the same target at the same time so neither spell is blocking the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T06:55:43-08:00","id":1472661,"title":"","content":"You would have to deal with a Clash of Wills to detect it via Unveiling, but winning would allow you to cast the Shielding with no further complications. The key is that Clashes of Wills occur when effects are acting at cross purposes. Another noteworthy detail is that the caster can choose to lose the Clash against the effect, so long as they still retain spell control. When the effect is relinquished, its treated as Clashing with a another caster, one that has the Gnosis + Arcanum pool of the mage at the time of casting.<br /> <br /> In the case of Wards and Signs, casting a Veiling after it would require it to either have enough Potency to power through or for the spell to be an exceptional success and the caster to choose to bypass Withstand.<br /> <br /> Should they be a combined spell, they are built specifically to work alongside one another, bypassing the problem entirely and Veiling the Wards and Signs at the same time<br /> <br /> Regarding dispellation, it would allow all effects to be bypassed and dispelled. However, the most widely encompassing option is Supernal Dispellation, which requires 2 Reach to permanently dispel rather than suppress the effects. That means that even a master would have to either cast with instant use and advanced duration, using yantras to adjust for the greatest cost benefit. A permanent solution would require ritual time (unless they can use Time In a Bottle) and additional work to get the AoE to the correct size, which means hoping that they will have enough time to do so or using either Stored Spell (Signs of Sorcery page 70) or Hung Spell (core book page 187) to setup beforehand. However, this would require more mana and spell control. Alternatively, they could use Dispel Magic, which grants a lot more free Reach, but requires the mage to hopefully have all the Arcana involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T07:41:18-08:00","id":1472666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472648#post1472648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This got me thinking.<br /> <br /> Can you fetter multiple ephemeral entities to the same subject? For example, fettering the ghosts of a mass murderer's victims to their killer?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. Spirits and Ghosts probably wouldn\u2019t do this normally, but it does happen. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472648#post1472648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same with possession? Can multiple entities possess the same target? For example a spirit and a ghost possessing the one body? Would they have to take turn? Wrest control from each other? Or can you push a possessing ghost out of a body by putting a spirit in?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, but again, Spirits and Ghosts probably wouldn\u2019t do this naturally. Again, it probably still happens. Wrest control, I should think, but I don\u2019t think there is a official ruling. After all, Hive-Claimed apparently naturally exist according to Werewolf. Plus there is Spiral. She is a Rapt who among other things forced multitudes of Spirits to claim her, while she maintains control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472648#post1472648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a last question, the familiar merit says your spirit/ghost/goetia may be fettered. So you can have a cat spirit familiar and fetter it to an actual cat. How little use would this be? Does a cat with the urged condition do much? Or does it do whatever catly things it would have done anyway but with the urging to point it in a particular direction?</div> </div> </div> </div> It\u2019s still a cat. It does what it wants. Occasionally, it might listen to the spirit, probably not the majority of the time, even when urged. At least, all the cats I\u2019ve met would never actually obey something willingly. Unless it suits them, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T08:35:10-08:00","id":1472671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472623#post1472623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and rotes can't be cast without using their Mudras)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not true. You <i>may</i> use the Mudra as a Yantra when casting a Rote from memory, but you are not required to do so. Additionally, you're unable to use Mudras for Rotes you cast from Grimoires instead of from memory, since you haven't learned the mnemonics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T09:39:22-08:00","id":1472674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472671#post1472671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not true. You <i>may</i> use the Mudra as a Yantra when casting a Rote from memory, but you are not required to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the mudras are the mnemonic techniques that allow the rote to be cast in a memorized form rather than read from a grimoire in the first place, how can it be possible to cast them without making use of the mnemonic?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T10:31:12-08:00","id":1472675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472674#post1472674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the mudras are the mnemonic techniques that allow the rote to be cast in a memorized form rather than read from a grimoire in the first place, how can it be possible to cast them without making use of the mnemonic?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Mudras <i>aren't</i> mnemonic techniques that allow the Rote to be cast from memory.<br /> <br /> &quot;When casting a Rote from memory, using an Order\u2019s recall techniques, the character may use dots in the associated Skill as a Yantra. The character must be free to make the mnemonic gestures to recall the Rote in order to benefit from the Skill bonus.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mudra is a mnemonic technique that makes it <i>easier</i> to cast Rotes from memory, but having learnt the Rote is enough to just cast it.<br /> Having Mudras both be a requirement <i>and</i> add a bonus would be a weird case of double dipping where you're not considered skilled enough to cast it as a Rote instead of an improvised spell without the mnemonic, but better at casting it as a Rote with the mnemonic than when casting it as an improvised spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T10:31:20-08:00","id":1472676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> additional work to get the AoE to the correct size </div> </div> </div>That raises a question, assuming i have a Nth scale area of effect spell (let's say it turns people into frogs) and someone casts and N-1th scale dispellation (whether Dispell magic or Supernal dispellation) would the spell be partially suppressed in the area of the dispellation (assuming potency exceeded the withstand) or would it be an all or nothing? <br /> <br /> Similarly if you cast a Nth scale area of effect dispellation, but only partially overlap the Nth scale Area of Frogs, does it fail (as the whole spell isn't inside the area?) - requiring N+1th scale area of effect to ensure you cover the whole thing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Should they be a combined spell, they are built specifically to work alongside one another, bypassing the problem entirely and Veiling the Wards and Signs at the same time </div> </div> </div> Is there something where it says a veiling spell is itself hidden from the purview that it is veiling/trigger peripheral mage sight - such that Supernal Veil doesn't need to be veiled from Prime (looking at page 123, i can't see it), but i am presuming this is the same?<br /> <br /> I like the autofail for the clash of wills. Does a mage consciously know what is being clashes with (in case they have multiple spells up)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T10:41:42-08:00","id":1472678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472666#post1472666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes. Spirits and Ghosts probably wouldn\u2019t do this normally, but it does happen. </div> </div> </div> </div>I am not assuming it is normal, hence my presumption that a mage could make it happen - perhaps as a punishment in the serial killer example<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but again, Spirits and Ghosts probably wouldn\u2019t do this naturally. Again, it probably still happens. Wrest control, I should think, but I don\u2019t think there is a official ruling. After all, Hive-Claimed apparently naturally exist according to Werewolf. Plus there is Spiral. She is a Rapt who among other things forced multitudes of Spirits to claim her, while she maintains control. </div> </div> </div>I am going to presume that they either existed as a hive entity before claiming, or collectively agreed to claim the subject together. <br /> <br /> If it is wresting control, you could summon a ghost (or ask your familiar) to possess someone who has a harmful spirit possessing them... At least as a temporary stopgap measure (possibly with one running out of essence before the other?) <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s still a cat. It does what it wants. Occasionally, it might listen to the spirit, probably not the majority of the time, even when urged. At least, all the cats I\u2019ve met would never actually obey something willingly. Unless it suits them, of course. </div> </div> </div>I do know of people who have trained their cats. How effective this is i couldn't tell you. But in general, having a cat with a cat spirit familiar fettered to it seems less than helpful... You could perhaps use the animal minion spell, and use the spirit's sensory input but otherwise it seems rather lackluster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T11:08:16-08:00","id":1472683,"title":"","content":"Can the Shattered Time environmental tilt (Dark Eras page 46) be created via an Unraveling of Time ? The effect itself is interesting, but it seems like it increases the Paradox dice pool, which makes me wonder if its even possible via Supernal magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T13:03:31-08:00","id":1472691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472678#post1472678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not assuming it is normal, hence my presumption that a mage could make it happen - perhaps as a punishment in the serial killer example</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that this is something that can happen without a mage, so it it doesn\u2019t conflict with a Mage being able to cause it. I intended no assumption into your idea of normalcy, since I have no way to know that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472678#post1472678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to presume that they either existed as a hive entity before claiming, or collectively agreed to claim the subject together.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe, all the sidebar says is that these things also exist naturally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472678#post1472678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is wresting control, you could summon a ghost (or ask your familiar) to possess someone who has a harmful spirit possessing them... At least as a temporary stopgap measure (possibly with one running out of essence before the other?)</div> </div> </div> </div> it\u2019s not a great plan, but it should work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472678#post1472678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do know of people who have trained their cats. How effective this is i couldn't tell you. But in general, having a cat with a cat spirit familiar fettered to it seems less than helpful... You could perhaps use the animal minion spell, and use the spirit's sensory input but otherwise it seems rather lackluster.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, you have a spirit that isn\u2019t leaking essence, that should be gaining lots of essence, and presumably has influence: cats. The sprit can really buff the cat and everything it does, and can talk to you. People don\u2019t really stop talking about stuff just because a cat is nearby, so you have nice little spy. That\u2019s not nothing. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T13:52:00-08:00","id":1472693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472675#post1472675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having Mudras both be a requirement <i>and</i> add a bonus would be a weird case of double dipping where you're not considered skilled enough to cast it as a Rote instead of an improvised spell without the mnemonic, but better at casting it as a Rote with the mnemonic than when casting it as an improvised spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>My response to that would be the idea that the Skill bonus is part of what makes a rote distinct from an improvised spell in the first place, and part of its value. Sure, even without that, you'd still have the benefits of extra Reach and not leaving your Signature. But I still think it's part of the definition and the value.<br /> <br /> However, I'll admit that my reading is prejudiced by certain things informed by First Edition. In that game, rotes definitely needed the mudra to cast, innately used Skills in the casting pool, and were... kind of lame. My reading is based both on a perspective of &quot;this is how they were possible to cast&quot; and &quot;I want their profile to be upped as much as possible&quot;, with the latter being counterbalanced a bit by requiring the mudra in all instances. Honestly, I kind of think even the extra Reach is good enough to make it necessary to use the mudra.<br /> <br /> In any event, we could agree that mudras as an Action Yantra are at least exceptional in being reserved for rotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T13:58:35-08:00","id":1472695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472683#post1472683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Shattered Time environmental tilt (Dark Eras page 46) be created via an Unraveling of Time ? The effect itself is interesting, but it seems like it increases the Paradox dice pool, which makes me wonder if its even possible via Supernal magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does look too \u2018big\u2019 to be just an Unraveling. Maaaaybe Unmaking. Or even some melange of Unmaking and Making. Either way, I\u2019d rather let that be an Artifact\u2019s power rather than a standard spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T15:40:43-08:00","id":1472700,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to find a distinction between an Imbued Item and an Enhanced Item. Can an Enhanced Item provide its &quot;enhancement&quot; to its wearer? For example, would an amulet with Gain Skill cast on it cause whomever is wearing it to be under said spell effect? <br /> <br /> I'm asking because I like the idea of a skill-monkey character who is constantly juggling a library of skill-amulets, and have to figure out if they'd be constantly casting on themselves or just swapping out their wardrobe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-18-2022, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T15:51:03-08:00","id":1472701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472700#post1472700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to find a distinction between an Imbued Item and an Enhanced Item. Can an Enhanced Item provide its &amp;quot;enhancement&amp;quot; to its wearer? For example, would an amulet with Gain Skill cast on it cause whomever is wearing it to be under said spell effect? <br /> <br /> I'm asking because I like the idea of a skill-monkey character who is constantly juggling a library of skill-amulets, and have to figure out if they'd be constantly casting on themselves or just swapping out their wardrobe</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e it was a clear distinction, the enhanced item had better durability/equipment bonus/similar. It was a strict limit of 3 or 4 matter spells which enhanced the item.<br /> <br /> In 2e this goes further, you could cast Veil of Moments (Time 2 sheilding) and enhance the item by prevent the normal ageing which occurs with time (is rusting/ normal wear and tear) or Ephemeral Enchantment (Prime 3 Weaving) to make it interact with ghosts, spirits and goetia. Any spell which enhanced the item itself.<br /> <br /> Enhance Skill doesn't do anything to an item as they don't have a skill rating, so that would be imbuing the item with a spell to cast on other subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T15:52:22-08:00","id":1472702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472700#post1472700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to find a distinction between an Imbued Item and an Enhanced Item. Can an Enhanced Item provide its &quot;enhancement&quot; to its wearer? For example, would an amulet with Gain Skill cast on it cause whomever is wearing it to be under said spell effect?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, by using Weaving to enchant the item with the effect.<br /> <br /> Regarding the distinction, enhanced items have been modified by spells. They do not cast spells, but are merely modified by spells actively affecting them. They cannot be turned off, they are constantly active and only affect themselves (like <i>Wonderful Machine</i>) or the users (like <i>Monkey's Paw</i>). So while you can make an item that makes someone have higher perception or a backpack that holds more items, you cannot make a lighter that casts fireballs or mind reading glasses.<br /> <br /> Imbued items are ones that had an Imago imprinted into their very nature. This allows users to cast using them and expending mana, in some cases even modify the Reach (if the crafter made them thus). Casting from an imbued item only takes one spell slot, no matter how many targets are affected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-18-2022, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T15:59:06-08:00","id":1472703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472691#post1472691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was that this is something that can happen without a mage, so it it doesn\u2019t conflict with a Mage being able to cause it. I intended no assumption into your idea of normalcy, since I have no way to know that.<br /> <br /> Maybe, all the sidebar says is that these things also exist naturally.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok, thanks i think i understand better now.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it\u2019s not a great plan, but it should work. </div> </div> </div>It might be your only option (eg if a ghost/spirit is possessing someone and you don't have access to Death/Spirit respectively, but have enough Mind to summon a powerful goetia...) And if you have an entity of high enough Rank (maybe 2 higher than currently possessing the subject) it should be able to take over, i think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, you have a spirit that isn\u2019t leaking essence, that should be gaining lots of essence, and presumably has influence: cats. The sprit can really buff the cat and everything it does, and can talk to you. People don\u2019t really stop talking about stuff just because a cat is nearby, so you have nice little spy. That\u2019s not nothing. </div> </div> </div>I guess i was comparing it to an unfettered familiar, which also isn't leaking essence, and can better spy by not being stuck to a cat. But your other points are well taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T16:01:09-08:00","id":1472704,"title":"","content":"So it sounds like there's some disagreement then - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> implied that Enhanced items can affect their wearer, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> emphatically stated that in 2e the spell only affects the item.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I understand the broad strokes difference between Enhanced and Imbued in 2e, but am trying to figure out if a skill monkey character would need to have a bunch of Imbued items they need to keep activating at regular intervals, or a bunch of wardrobe accessories that they throw on as needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T16:02:16-08:00","id":1472705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472695#post1472695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does look too \u2018big\u2019 to be just an Unraveling. Maaaaybe Unmaking. Or even some melange of Unmaking and Making. Either way, I\u2019d rather let that be an Artifact\u2019s power rather than a standard spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Unmaking would make events have jumpcuts, whereas this sounds like Unraveling inflicting severe damage to the forces of the Arcanum. I was thinking that conjunctionally applying Fate 4 could allow elements of <i>Chaos Mastery</i> to be mixed in, allowing it to be broken in more directed ways. Think of it as something similar to how safety equipment is designed to break in very specific ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T16:04:13-08:00","id":1472706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472704#post1472704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it sounds like there's some disagreement then - <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> implied that Enhanced items can affect their wearer, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27248_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27248\" data-vbnamecard=\"27248\">orathaic</a> emphatically stated that in 2e the spell only affects the item.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I understand the broad strokes difference between Enhanced and Imbued in 2e, but am trying to figure out if a skill monkey character would need to have a bunch of Imbued items they need to keep activating at regular intervals, or a bunch of wardrobe accessories that they throw on as needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it has a persistent imbued effect which targets the user, that is an imbued item. If it is a pair of binocculars which has a extremely good equipment bonus benefiting anyone who uses it, then it is an enhanced item... <br /> <br /> I'm not sure if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> disagrees with this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: so, both should be your answer. If you want an item which enhanced the user's skill rating, then Imbuing the item makes sense. Let's say a necklace which was imbued to enhance the wearer's weaponry. You could then use the enhanced weaponry with any relevant weapon.<br /> <br /> Alternatively a sword with a larger damage bonus/lower weight etc. Would be an enhanced item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-18-2022, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T16:06:26-08:00","id":1472707,"title":"","content":"I may have just misunderstood them then. Either way, sounds like my hypothetical skill-monkey would need to be continually activating items. Heavy investment in mana-batteries it is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T16:14:40-08:00","id":1472708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472707#post1472707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have just misunderstood them then. Either way, sounds like my hypothetical skill-monkey would need to be continually activating items. Heavy investment in mana-batteries it is!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> i think some imbued items don't need activating. They can be persistent, always on. So shouldn't need mana to activate each time. <br /> <br /> It is unclear if this means that whoever is wearing them at a given time becomes the subject of the effect (as that would be changing the Spell's subject...) But i think it is designed to work like that (and is similar to area of effect spells which affect anyone entering the area - or this would affect anyone who comes into touch range).<br /> <br /> But to avoid potential side effect of anyone being able to pick up the item and gain the benefit, i think that an activation roll/known (secret) trigger - along with the use of mana - is what you need.<br /> <br /> That said, you don't necessarily need seperate mana batteries as the imbued item(s) can have mana slots of its own to spend on its effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T16:35:02-08:00","id":1472710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 01-27-2019, 06:36 PM<br /> Originally posted by KaiserAfini View Post<br /> The big advantage is that your Oneiros guarantees it will be bug free forever.<br /> This is not the case.<br /> <br /> Although it utilizes the same systems, it has been clarified by the Dev that relinquished spells going haywire is not Paradox </div> </div> </div>So, this seems like the closest mages have to Dynamics without Archmastery. The Mysterium specifically like the idea of magic as being alive, so i can see one of them wanting to study the effects of a wild spell which mutated... What sort of spells seem likely to give the most interesting effects? Fate perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T16:37:00-08:00","id":1472711,"title":"","content":"The Imbued Item entry on 2e Mage's core book (page 102, I think) is pretty explicit that you're spending at least one point of mana to activate the spell, so you'll need to recast at least as often as the duration. I honestly read it kind of like a DnD Wand/Stave, or a Wheel of Time Ter'angreal - the item has one trick that any user can activate, so long as they pay the cost. That's also where I've been assuming the main use-distinction (as opposed to the crafting-distinction) is between Enhanced and Imbued is - Enhanced is permanent and self-contained, while effects generated by Imbued are temporary but flexible in their parameters.<br /> <br /> And while you can indeed have a pretty decently-sized mana reservoirs build into the item, you can get some pretty good milage out of multiple Indefinite castings Mana Battery on an item. Makes it easier to steal, true, but it means you can use it on more things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-18-2022, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T17:11:27-08:00","id":1472712,"title":"","content":"I remember asking about making items that enhanced users on this thread, wish I remembered a bit of the wording so I could find the reference.<br /> <br /> But in essence, every Path has a way to get mana at high tiers. With Prime you just win, since you can make and enhance Hallows. Resource intensive and time consuming, but has great gains too.<br /> <br /> Death, Mind and Spirit mages can use familiars, then generate Essence and instantly convert it to mana via the link. With a Perfecting spell, they could arguably even make the transfer more efficient.<br /> <br /> Fate is the easiest, just use Miracle to get a full mana reimbursement via exceptional successes. All the mana used on Attainments, Paradox mitigation and all other spell costs can just be recovered. With Time, using Temporal Pocket plus Veil of Moments with Reach effects lets you pattern scour and fully recover in the blink of an eye (plus get fully healed by chaining pattern restorations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-18-2022, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T17:18:59-08:00","id":1472713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472711#post1472711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Imbued Item entry on 2e Mage's core book (page 102, I think) is pretty explicit that you're spending at least one point of mana to activate the spell, so you'll need to recast at least as often as the duration. I honestly read it kind of like a DnD Wand/Stave, or a Wheel of Time Ter'angreal - the item has one trick that any user can activate, so long as they pay the cost. That's also where I've been assuming the main use-distinction (as opposed to the crafting-distinction) is between Enhanced and Imbued is - Enhanced is permanent and self-contained, while effects generated by Imbued are temporary but flexible in their parameters.<br /> <br /> And while you can indeed have a pretty decently-sized mana reservoirs build into the item, you can get some pretty good milage out of multiple Indefinite castings Mana Battery on an item. Makes it easier to steal, true, but it means you can use it on more things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It all depends on who you know. Have a master of Time make an enhanced item that grants a variation of Blink of an Eye that lets you change and reload equipment instantly. Then have a disciple of Space make a bag of holding. <br /> <br /> Now you can prepare a plethora of enchanted items and switch from Sleeper clothes to the optimal gear in literally no time at all. Its a lot less mana intensive than imbued items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T17:19:05-08:00","id":1472714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472710#post1472710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, this seems like the closest mages have to Dynamics without Archmastery. The Mysterium specifically like the idea of magic as being alive, so i can see one of them wanting to study the effects of a wild spell which mutated... What sort of spells seem likely to give the most interesting effects? Fate perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like anything that you fancy, personally Prime is mine for the least likely to accidentally cause nightmare fuel to making cool new stuff. ( Prime totally can cause nightmare fuel, but it has to work harder than\u2026let\u2019s say Life to be horrific) If you don\u2019t mind nightmare fuel, then Life + whatever is likely to make very fascinating results. And probably kill or whatever the spell was on, or make it wish it had died, but that\u2019s just details.<br /> <br /> Edit: so if spells going haywire isn\u2019t caused by paradox, can they create Abyssal Environmental Tilts, or summon a Abyssal Entity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-18-2022, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T17:40:05-08:00","id":1472715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472714#post1472714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like anything that you fancy, personally Prime is mine for the least likely to accidentally cause nightmare fuel to making cool new stuff. ( Prime totally can cause nightmare fuel, but it has to work harder than\u2026let\u2019s say Life to be horrific) If you don\u2019t mind nightmare fuel, then Life + whatever is likely to make very fascinating results. And probably kill or whatever the spell was on, or make it wish it had died, but that\u2019s just details.<br /> <br /> Edit: so if spells going haywire isn\u2019t caused by paradox, can they create Abyssal Environmental Tilts, or summon a Abyssal Entity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to suggest one source of Prime based nightmare fuel. Have you ever played Baten Kaitos: Origins ? There is this one village that has their essence consumed. They are visible as silhouettes going about their everyday life, heedless that the day has changed, just repeating it over and over. <br /> <br /> Eternally trapped in a Sysphian task, visible as naught but echoes in all layers of Twilight, unable to even acknowledge the new reality of their lives, supernaturally perceptible in all lens but hollowed out of all truth. That is one thing an Unmaking of Prime can do.<br /> <br /> I always thought it would be fun to make this into a plot hook. Like make this be the fate of Roanoke, creating this eerily all present city of oblivious people that only Sleepers cannot perceive (probably the result of a major conflict with the Paternoster).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T17:40:14-08:00","id":1472716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472713#post1472713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It all depends on who you know. Have a master of Time make an enhanced item that grants a variation of Blink of an Eye that lets you change and reload equipment instantly. Then have a disciple of Space make a bag of holding. <br /> <br /> Now you can prepare a plethora of enchanted items and switch from Sleeper clothes to the optimal gear in literally no time at all. Its a lot less mana intensive than imbued items.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exasperated Exarchs, it's Superman's phone-booth trick!<br /> <br /> Edit: for pedantry's sake, the Blink of and Eye item would still have to be Imbued, since it's an activated effect that causes a given roll to be performed in a much shorter time frame. Still a great way to play an infiltrator or spy though. Or a Magical Girl","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-18-2022, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T17:42:33-08:00","id":1472717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472716#post1472716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exasperated Exarchs, it's Superman's phone-booth trick!</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been caught, that is exactly what inspired it. A simple trick, but potentially very useful. I will probably post it in Creative Thaumaturgy in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T17:50:43-08:00","id":1472719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472715#post1472715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like to suggest one source of Prime based nightmare fuel. Have you ever played Baten Kaitos: Origins ? There is this one village that has their essence consumed. They are visible as silhouettes going about their everyday life, heedless that the day has changed, just repeating it over and over.<br /> <br /> Eternally trapped in a Sysphian task, visible as naught but echoes in all layers of Twilight, unable to even acknowledge the new reality of their lives, supernaturally perceptible in all lens but hollowed out of all truth. That is one thing an Unmaking of Prime can do.<br /> <br /> I always thought it would be fun to make this into a plot hook. Like make this be the fate of Roanoke, creating this eerily all present city of oblivious people that only Sleepers cannot perceive (probably the result of a major conflict with the Paternoster).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. That is amazing. I\u2019d so study that as Mage. And probably even if I wasn\u2019t a Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T18:25:55-08:00","id":1472724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Imbued Item entry on 2e Mage's core book (page 102, I think) is pretty explicit that you're spending at least one point of mana to activate the spell </div> </div> </div>I think this is where some of the confusion lies. Because the attainment also clearly says <br /> <br /> &quot;The caster decides whether the spell imbued into the item is persistent (always active) or contingent (triggered by a word, gesture, or condition)&quot;<br /> <br /> If it is contingent, then 1 mana per activation and a Gnosis+Arcana roll.<br /> <br /> But if it is persistent, then it seems like it only has to be activated once and is always on (which suggests indefinite duration to me, and is something the merit suggests imbued items can't do). <br /> <br /> The downside is that there is only ever one copy of the spell effect, whereas if you triggered it, you could cast the effect multiple times on different subjects (like giving honing the form to each member of your group one at a time for one mana each) with seperate durations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T18:39:31-08:00","id":1472726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472714#post1472714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: so if spells going haywire isn\u2019t caused by paradox, can they create Abyssal Environmental Tilts, or summon a Abyssal Entity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually studying a magically created disease as the spell making it mutates would be... Bad, queue zombie apocalypse.<br /> <br /> As for Abyssal it says &quot;Without maintenance from the caster, the spell may go awry if left for very long periods... the Storyteller rolls...success grants the Storyteller a Reach as though the spell had gained a Paradox; and an exceptional success ends the spell, canceling its remaining Duration.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sadly the exceptional success ends the spell. Otherwise i think it is just the reach. <br /> <br /> From paradox reach &quot;The Storyteller can use Paradox Reach to change the spell factors of the spell, to create Abyssal taint on the environment, or to summon an Abyssal entity.&quot; - so just change the spell factors... Add or remove subjects? Change scale of the effect? Change the actual target (so it could move from place to place?) Increase potency? <br /> <br /> I wonder could scrutinizing it (which involves releasing mana and watching how it dispersed into, in this case, the spell) power/trigger changes... <br /> <br /> I think a mind virus/meme would be interesting. Maybe a spell which creates a ideas, and then starts to spread...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T18:45:12-08:00","id":1472727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472724#post1472724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is where some of the confusion lies. Because the attainment also clearly says <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The caster decides whether the spell imbued into the item is persistent (always active) or contingent (triggered by a word, gesture, or condition)&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> If it is contingent, then 1 mana per activation and a Gnosis+Arcana roll.<br /> <br /> But if it is persistent, then it seems like it only has to be activated once and is always on (which suggests indefinite duration to me, and is something the merit suggests imbued items can't do). <br /> <br /> The downside is that there is only ever one copy of the spell effect, whereas if you triggered it, you could cast the effect multiple times on different subjects (like giving honing the form to each member of your group one at a time for one mana each) with seperate durations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went to Signs of Sorcery to check the more detailed layout - you are absolutely correct. During item creation you chose between Persistent or Contingent, with Persistent being permanent and Contingent being triggered. If a Persistent spell is disabled but the Imbued Item is still intact, you can use Words of Command to reactivate it.<br /> <br /> I'm still leery of it meaning I could make a Persistent Grant Skill amulet that grants the spell benefit as long as it's worn, but the reading of the rules could go either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T18:52:45-08:00","id":1472729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472726#post1472726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually studying a magically created disease as the spell making it mutates would be... Bad, queue zombie apocalypse.<br /> <br /> As for Abyssal it says &quot;Without maintenance from the caster, the spell may go awry if left for very long periods... the Storyteller rolls...success grants the Storyteller a Reach as though the spell had gained a Paradox; and an exceptional success ends the spell, canceling its remaining Duration.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sadly the exceptional success ends the spell. Otherwise i think it is just the reach.<br /> <br /> From paradox reach &quot;The Storyteller can use Paradox Reach to change the spell factors of the spell, to create Abyssal taint on the environment, or to summon an Abyssal entity.&quot; - so just change the spell factors... Add or remove subjects? Change scale of the effect? Change the actual target (so it could move from place to place?) Increase potency?<br /> <br /> I wonder could scrutinizing it (which involves releasing mana and watching how it dispersed into, in this case, the spell) power/trigger changes...<br /> <br /> I think a mind virus/meme would be interesting. Maybe a spell which creates a ideas, and then starts to spread...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or weaken the barriers between different\u2026 Oneiroes?\u2026Oneiri?\u2026 whatever plural Oneiros is so that people start merging into each other\u2019s minds. And still spreads.<br /> <br /> As for triggering specific changes, I bet that\u2019s a whole field of study, with servers competing theories, along with a dedicated legacy to at least one. I\u2019m imagining the Tamers of Roots watering their seed spells in specific resonances in their garden\u2026and now I want to add that as actual thing. Dang it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T18:59:42-08:00","id":1472731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472726#post1472726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually studying a magically created disease as the spell making it mutates would be... Bad, queue zombie apocalypse.<br /> <br /> As for Abyssal it says &quot;Without maintenance from the caster, the spell may go awry if left for very long periods... the Storyteller rolls...success grants the Storyteller a Reach as though the spell had gained a Paradox; and an exceptional success ends the spell, canceling its remaining Duration.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sadly the exceptional success ends the spell. Otherwise i think it is just the reach.<br /> <br /> From paradox reach &quot;The Storyteller can use Paradox Reach to change the spell factors of the spell, to create Abyssal taint on the environment, or to summon an Abyssal entity.&quot; - so just change the spell factors... Add or remove subjects? Change scale of the effect? Change the actual target (so it could move from place to place?) Increase potency?<br /> <br /> I wonder could scrutinizing it (which involves releasing mana and watching how it dispersed into, in this case, the spell) power/trigger changes...<br /> <br /> I think a mind virus/meme would be interesting. Maybe a spell which creates a ideas, and then starts to spread...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remember a really interesting one based on it from the 1001 story hooks thread. There was this Free Council mage who has sent a space probe and was using a constant Forces effect to make sure he always received the data instantly. However, he was killed and so the spell was unsafely relinquished. It then started to mutate. Rather than affecting his corpse, it attached to a random civilian. Instead of receiving electronic data, its sent their body heat to the probe. The result was a civilian who suddenly perished by hypothermia, with a layer of ice over them, killed by a supposedly dead mage and with a spell leading to outer space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T19:02:27-08:00","id":1472732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472727#post1472727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I went to Signs of Sorcery to check the more detailed layout - you are absolutely correct. During item creation you chose between Persistent or Contingent, with Persistent being permanent and Contingent being triggered. If a Persistent spell is disabled but the Imbued Item is still intact, you can use Words of Command to reactivate it.<br /> <br /> I'm still leery of it meaning I could make a Persistent Grant Skill amulet that grants the spell benefit as long as it's worn, but the reading of the rules could go either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if there was a custom Matter or Space spell to change the imbuement process like a curse to make the Amulet of Grant Skill effect only those who wear it? (And also create our previous hypothetical Sunglasses of Night Vision)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T19:27:59-08:00","id":1472736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472727#post1472727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went to Signs of Sorcery to check the more detailed layout - you are absolutely correct. During item creation you chose between Persistent or Contingent, with Persistent being permanent and Contingent being triggered. If a Persistent spell is disabled but the Imbued Item is still intact, you can use Words of Command to reactivate it.<br /> <br /> I'm still leery of it meaning I could make a Persistent Grant Skill amulet that grants the spell benefit as long as it's worn, but the reading of the rules could go either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>My takeaway is that the Imbued Item Merit talking about not having indefinite duration is an error or miscommunication, because that restriction is mentioned literally nowhere else in 2e's discussion of Imbued Items, Signs of Sorcery's clarification negates the Merit's implicit limitation of one imbued spell per item, and Signs of Sorcery's treatment on Enhanced Items makes it pretty clear that Enhanced Items are still items with spells that affect their own qualities cast on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T19:42:32-08:00","id":1472739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472732#post1472732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if there was a custom Matter or Space spell to change the imbuement process like a curse to make the Amulet of Grant Skill effect only those who wear it? (And also create our previous hypothetical Sunglasses of Night Vision)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's /kinda of/ a variation on the Primary Subject Prime 3 spell in the curse section of Signs of Sorcery... doesn't help with the Relinquishment, but you might be able to finagle it into meaning that Persistents affect the user.<br /> <br /> Or just ST fiat it one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T19:47:17-08:00","id":1472740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472727#post1472727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still leery of it meaning I could make a Persistent Grant Skill amulet that grants the spell benefit as long as it's worn, but the reading of the rules could go either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am now wondering can you change which skill it grants of it is triggered? Or is that a different imbuement of the same spell?<br /> <br /> For the sake of my headcannon, I'm assuming it works the same way as area of effects, anything within touch range being the 'area', so the subject is always the wearer (and only one wearer at a time...).<br /> <br /> Now if this was unsafely relinquished...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> constant Forces effect to make sure he always received the data instantly. </div> </div> </div> The physicist in me says, nope, that is clearly Space or Time...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The result was a civilian who suddenly perished by hypothermia, with a layer of ice over them, killed by a supposedly dead mage and with a spell leading to outer space </div> </div> </div> The physics of this is really cool though. That said, with a reach, changing spell factors, I'm not sure it should change the transmit information to transmit heat - unless 'spell factors' is taken to include, hmm, i don't have a word for it. Other parts of the imago that you can't usually take a -2 dice penalty or reach for advanced? If that makes sense?<br /> <br /> Living destiny spells would also be interesting. Forge Destiny changing the number of subjects or scale and granting a Doom or Supernatural merit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T19:54:21-08:00","id":1472741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472740#post1472740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am now wondering can you change which skill it grants of it is triggered? Or is that a different imbuement of the same spell?<br /> <br /> For the sake of my headcannon, I'm assuming it works the same way as area of effects, anything within touch range being the 'area', so the subject is always the wearer (and only one wearer at a time...).</div> </div> </div> </div>The lazy/permissive/munchkin part of me says the skill is chosen with each casting, but there is a part of me that thinks the Imago of the spell contains the link to the part of the Tenemos you're pulling the skill-knowledge from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472740#post1472740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Living destiny spells would also be interesting. Forge Destiny changing the number of subjects or scale and granting a Doom or Supernatural merit...</div> </div> </div> </div>Contagious Dooms!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T20:07:59-08:00","id":1472743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472740#post1472740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am now wondering can you change which skill it grants of it is triggered? Or is that a different imbuement of the same spell?</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on how you make it, honestly. I could see both in different items.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472740#post1472740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the sake of my headcannon, I'm assuming it works the same way as area of effects, anything within touch range being the 'area', so the subject is always the wearer (and only one wearer at a time...).</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that works for me, but I personally would have it as whoever wore the thing, so if two people hooked a amulet around their heads, it works for both at the cost of being awkward to move.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472740#post1472740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The physicist in me says, nope, that is clearly Space or Time...</div> </div> </div> </div> The amateur Obrimos in me says that\u2019s most likely a persistent Forces Knowing with possible secondary Prime suppression spell cast before the launch, but you do you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472740#post1472740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The physics of this is really cool though. That said, with a reach, changing spell factors, I'm not sure it should change the transmit information to transmit heat - unless 'spell factors' is taken to include, hmm, i don't have a word for it. Other parts of the imago that you can't usually take a -2 dice penalty or reach for advanced? If that makes sense?</div> </div> </div> </div> It\u2019s a Ruling (I think, could be Compelling) Forces to treat a object as though it was touching another for heat transfer even when they aren\u2019t touching. Then Physics makes the two equalize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T20:10:49-08:00","id":1472744,"title":"","content":"New (possibility silly) question: If a spell is withstood, is the Signature Nimbus still left on the target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T20:21:15-08:00","id":1472746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472744#post1472744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New (possibility silly) question: If a spell is withstood, is the Signature Nimbus still left on the target?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. The spell's still <i>there</i>, Withstand just makes it not <i>do</i> anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T20:28:37-08:00","id":1472747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</