ainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472743#post1472743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that works for me, but I personally would have it as whoever wore the thing, so if two people hooked a amulet around their heads, it works for both at the cost of being awkward to move.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, i'd only allow this if the spell factors allowed two subjects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The amateur Obrimos in me says that\u2019s most likely a persistent Forces Knowing with possible secondary Prime suppression spell cast before the launch, but you do you. </div> </div> </div>I was assuming it was based off of Transmission (Forces 2 Ruling) - which i think is the most misunderstood Forces spell and should have a conjunctional mind option for encryption.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s a Ruling (I think, could be Compelling) Forces to treat a object as though it was touching another for heat transfer even when they aren\u2019t touching. Then Physics makes the two equalize. </div> </div> </div>Ok, so assuming all of the magic works. My question is can paradox/unsafely relinquished spells change their practice - in this case from Knowing to Compelling/Ruling?<br /> <br /> ie is the practice consider a spell factor for the purposes of &quot;The Storyteller can use Paradox Reach <br /> to change the spell factors of the spell&quot;<br /> <br /> Actually looking more closely at the anomolies:<br /> <br /> &quot;1 Reach Undo or apply a single Reach from <br /> the Common Reach Effects list on p. <br /> 112 except Casting Time.<br /> 1 Reach Impose a Condition on the subject of <br /> the spell.<br /> 2 Reach Change the subject of the spell&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems like none of what i would consider changing the spell factors... But even assuming a liberal reading of: changing the reach effects, changing the subject, or changing the spell factors are all possible. Does that include changing the practice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T01:29:08-08:00","id":1472759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472746#post1472746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. The spell's still <i>there</i>, Withstand just makes it not <i>do</i> anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the strength of the signature Nimbus, or shall we say, how easy it is to read, depend on the Spell's pote? And if so is it the effective potency after withstanding or before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T08:59:59-08:00","id":1472784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472758#post1472758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, i'd only allow this if the spell factors allowed two subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, it\u2019s aoe of touch, that means it\u2019s not using subjects. But you do you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472758#post1472758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was assuming it was based off of Transmission (Forces 2 Ruling) - which i think is the most misunderstood Forces spell and should have a conjunctional mind option for encryption.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s a perfectly valid way to communicate with the craft, but that doesn\u2019t change the fact that a combined Forces Knowing and Compelling spell to receive information and send instructions instantly is way better than the delay from the speed of light.<br /> <br /> Why would it need Mind? You don\u2019t need Mind to understand encrypted transmissions with Tune In. You are simply creating a more complicated message, which doesn\u2019t require any other Arcana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472758#post1472758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so assuming all of the magic works. My question is can paradox/unsafely relinquished spells change their practice - in this case from Knowing to Compelling/Ruling?<br /> <br /> ie is the practice consider a spell factor for the purposes of &quot;The Storyteller can use Paradox Reach<br /> to change the spell factors of the spell&quot;<br /> <br /> Actually looking more closely at the anomolies:<br /> <br /> &quot;1 Reach Undo or apply a single Reach from<br /> the Common Reach Effects list on p.<br /> 112 except Casting Time.<br /> 1 Reach Impose a Condition on the subject of<br /> the spell.<br /> 2 Reach Change the subject of the spell&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems like none of what i would consider changing the spell factors... But even assuming a liberal reading of: changing the reach effects, changing the subject, or changing the spell factors are all possible. Does that include changing the practice?</div> </div> </div> </div> Looks like a no, unless storyteller wishes to go against that for a better story. Since it can\u2019t create abyssal environments nor summon entities, I would personally put warping what the spell does, but staying in practice at 3 reach and 4 reach to potentially change practice. But that is just me, and others might think that system is silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T09:03:29-08:00","id":1472785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472759#post1472759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the strength of the signature Nimbus, or shall we say, how easy it is to read, depend on the Spell's pote? And if so is it the effective potency after withstanding or before?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Signature Nimbus? No. Higher Gnosis makes it clearer, but not Potency.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T10:15:49-08:00","id":1472790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, it\u2019s aoe of touch, that means it\u2019s not using subjects. But you do you. </div> </div> </div> I was (mistakenly?) treating it like a 1 subject spell still.<br /> <br /> AOE starts at arms reach (sphere); which is fine so long as nobody has an issue with portable AOEs. But it does touch on my question about AOE dispelling, and whether you need to cover the whole area of a subject or is partial overlap is acceptable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472785#post1472785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Signature Nimbus? No. Higher Gnosis makes it clearer, but not Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that is what i was thinking of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T10:29:14-08:00","id":1472792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> that doesn\u2019t change the fact that a combined Forces Knowing and Compelling spell to receive information and send instructions instantly is way better than the delay from the speed of light. </div> </div> </div>No, that may be the case. Feels odd for some reason, having me ask whether knowing is a lasting effect like damage and should repeat every ritual interval or if Compelling is even less intuitive than the knowing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would it need Mind? You don\u2019t need Mind to understand encrypted transmissions with Tune In. You are simply creating a more complicated message, which doesn\u2019t require any other Arcana </div> </div> </div>Mind has the purview of communication and language. Old Timey AM radio signals can be converter directly from one form to another (radio waves to sound waves) with Forces alone. Modern digital signals need a computer/Mind to decode.<br /> <br /> Forces just happens to not have anything to do with translation of languages in its purview. This is the edgecase for mind with electronics, with true AI being the that is clearly mind. (With Forces still able to affect the purview like Life can still affect the mental state of a person, but really you want Mind to do more subtle effects).<br /> <br /> But basically. If anyone can intercept the signal and read it without any effort (or without passing it through a computer) then that is fine. Anything digital is messy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: now that i think about it, you should he able to change the subject and have your smart phone be the target of a Knowing spell and have it decode a signal... Probably perfectly normal for a Free Council Obrimos, might not be taught by the Diamond Orders. (You can normally have others gain the knowing or unveiling effects, does it require an extra subject?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-19-2022, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T11:59:03-08:00","id":1472799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472792#post1472792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that may be the case. Feels odd for some reason, having me ask whether knowing is a lasting effect like damage and should repeat every ritual interval or if Compelling is even less intuitive than the knowing.</div> </div> </div> </div> It should be a persistent effect, if you do it right. Look, it\u2019s simply accessing the information on the computer, and being able to influence it. The spells involved are Influence Electricity and \u201cRead Device\u201d. (I made up \u201cRead Device\u201d, but it should be a easy Knowing.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472792#post1472792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind has the purview of communication and language. Old Timey AM radio signals can be converter directly from one form to another (radio waves to sound waves) with Forces alone. Modern digital signals need a computer/Mind to decode.</div> </div> </div> </div> Unveiling/Knowing Spells automatically translate the symbolic information into whatever a target will recognize. Tune In explicitly works with wireless modems. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472792#post1472792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces just happens to not have anything to do with translation of languages in its purview. This is the edgecase for mind with electronics, with true AI being the that is clearly mind. (With Forces still able to affect the purview like Life can still affect the mental state of a person, but really you want Mind to do more subtle effects).</div> </div> </div> </div> Unless I\u2019m quite mistaken, Forces covers the mediums of communication in Sound, Light, and Electricity. Communication has 3 parts, the meaning of the sender, the medium of the message, and the understanding of both by the receiver. Knowing/Unveiling, as long as it can use any part of the message, will translate the message. Life, for example, has Speak With Beasts. This works with Humans, so Life can act as a universal translator, as long as the message comes through a person. Mind is the best in this regard, as you can know any language that humanity knows, or ever has known, read the mind of the sender, or impress your intended meaning on the receiver. Probably can do even more stuff with communication.<br /> <br /> You can use Matter to read a book that is in another language. After all, a book is usually made of paper, with strange markings made from ink that represent concepts and symbols. It is intended to be store and communicate knowledge. Craftsman\u2019s Eye with the first reach option will translate the book for you. (I\u2019d argue you can get the translation effect with a Creative Thaumaturgy Matter Unveiling, but I want to prove my point, not make unbacked assertions.) This doesn\u2019t give you the ability to speak the language the book is in, since sound and language isn\u2019t under Matters purview. Now just apply the same concept to Forces, but with Light and Electricity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472792#post1472792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: now that i think about it, you should he able to change the subject and have your smart phone be the target of a Knowing spell and have it decode a signal... Probably perfectly normal for a Free Council Obrimos, might not be taught by the Diamond Orders. (You can normally have others gain the knowing or unveiling effects, does it require an extra subject?)</div> </div> </div> </div> The phone is just a Yantra for most circumstances, I should think, unless you need the information stored on the phone for some reason. Also the Diamond Orders totally do technomagic, they as a group just don\u2019t think it\u2019s anything special vs any other kind of magic. Mysterium probably has quite a few random members studying it, just not anywhere close to the Free Councils numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T12:23:13-08:00","id":1472803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472799#post1472799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It should be a persistent effect, if you do it right. Look, it\u2019s simply accessing the information on the computer, and being able to influence it. The spells involved are Influence Electricity and \u201cRead Device\u201d. (I made up \u201cRead Device\u201d, but it should be a easy Knowing.)<br /> <br /> Unveiling/Knowing Spells automatically translate the symbolic information into whatever a target will recognize. Tune In explicitly works with wireless modems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah-ha. I am indeed rather wrong.<br /> <br /> Except what you said about unveiling. Knowing explicitly delivers awareness of Supernal truth (like what you said).<br /> <br /> Unveiling does not. Merely allowing you to sense things which your brain has to process normally. So while i feel I'm only half wrong. I am still very very wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless I\u2019m quite mistaken, Forces covers the mediums of communication in Sound, Light, and Electricity. Communication has 3 parts, the meaning of the sender, the medium of the message, and the understanding of both by the receiver. Knowing/Unveiling, as long as it can use any part of the message, will translate the message. Life, for example, has Speak With Beasts. This works with Humans, so Life can act as a universal translator, as long as the message comes through a person. Mind is the best in this regard, as you can know any language that humanity knows, or ever has known, read the mind of the sender, or impress your intended meaning on the receiver. Probably can do even more stuff with communication.<br /> <br /> You can use Matter to read a book that is in another language. After all, a book is usually made of paper, with strange markings made from ink that represent concepts and symbols. It is intended to be store and communicate knowledge. Craftsman\u2019s Eye with the first reach option will translate the book for you. (I\u2019d argue you can get the translation effect with a Creative Thaumaturgy Matter Unveiling, but I want to prove my point, not make unbacked assertions.) This doesn\u2019t give you the ability to speak the language the book is in, since sound and language isn\u2019t under Matters purview. Now just apply the same concept to Forces, but with Light and Electricity. </div> </div> </div>I wonder if they are consistent about distinguishing between knowing and unveiling across those arcanum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The phone is just a Yantra for most circumstances, I should think, unless you need the information stored on the phone for some reason. Also the Diamond Orders totally do technomagic, they as a group just don\u2019t think it\u2019s anything special vs any other kind of magic. Mysterium probably has quite a few random members studying it, just not anywhere close to the Free Councils numbers. </div> </div> </div>I think i get your point about the Free Council. And infact i am wrong in suggesting a knowing spell should be used on your phone - minds can interpret symbolic truths. I don't know that phones can. Unveiling might work... Letting your phone record twilight if you cast the right unveiling on the camera before hand? <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how a digital device can record 'direct awareness of supernal truth' As that is not a data stream.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Regardless, thank you so much for the effort clarifying things for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T12:30:23-08:00","id":1472805,"title":"","content":"Ok, new question.<br /> <br /> I had a thought about unlimited reach, and how it kinda breaks things with spells like shifting sands (supernal beings).<br /> <br /> In a Pocket Dimension, if you cast unlimited reach shifting sands to go back, i presume that the point where you go back to before you entered the pocket dimension you are no longer protected by the zero paradox effect. Alternatively you could use Shifting Sands to go back as far in time as the Pocket has existed?<br /> <br /> Does that seem appropriate? What else breaks with limited reach? (I'm going to treat extra reach beyond spell control limits like unsafely relinquished spells, ie make the spell go wild but not paradoxical).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T12:54:43-08:00","id":1472806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472803#post1472803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah-ha. I am indeed rather wrong.<br /> <br /> Except what you said about unveiling. Knowing explicitly delivers awareness of Supernal truth (like what you said).<br /> <br /> Unveiling does not. Merely allowing you to sense things which your brain has to process normally. So while i feel I'm only half wrong. I am still very very wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> Language translation still seems like something Unveiling can do, since it\u2019s revealing information hidden by language. I mean, you still have to read it. If said or gave that impression that you didn\u2019t, I was very wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472803#post1472803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if they are consistent about distinguishing between knowing and unveiling across those arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don\u2019t thinks so, Tune In is Knowing, despite having an effect I\u2019d swear was Unveiling. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472803#post1472803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think i get your point about the Free Council. And infact i am wrong in suggesting a knowing spell should be used on your phone - minds can interpret symbolic truths. I don't know that phones can. Unveiling might work... Letting your phone record twilight if you cast the right unveiling on the camera before hand?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how a digital device can record 'direct awareness of supernal truth' As that is not a data stream.</div> </div> </div> </div> SoS has a Prime Weaving spell called Camera Obscura that allows one to record \u201cSupernal Energies\u201d allowing on to make a recording that one can use AMS or FMS on to examine like the photo was the thing it recorded. I would allow any other Arcanum to do the same with their respective Twilights and such, possibly as a Forces + whatever combined spell to detect the thing, and record it. There is probably a easier way to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472803#post1472803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Regardless, thank you so much for the effort clarifying things for me.</div> </div> </div> </div> No problem, I really enjoy Mage, and the technical parts of it. And helping people with something is something I like doing when I can.<br /> <br /> I\u2026 have not had a great last few days, and I hope that none of my frustration with life bled through into my posts. If it did so, I apologize.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T14:40:01-08:00","id":1472813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472806#post1472806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Language translation still seems like something Unveiling can do, since it\u2019s revealing information hidden by language. I mean, you still have to read it. If said or gave that impression that you didn\u2019t, I was very wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> I may have misunderstood what you said, but yes, unveiling a text in a foreign language might be very useful if you can stick it into google translate later... I was thinking purely in the example of Tune in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t thinks so, Tune In is Knowing, despite having an effect I\u2019d swear was Unveiling. </div> </div> </div>Tune in needs to be knowing to get meaning... Does active mage sight let you sense radio waves, or should you have some unveiling spell aswell?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> SoS has a Prime Weaving spell called Camera Obscura that allows one to record \u201cSupernal Energies\u201d allowing on to make a recording that one can use AMS or FMS on to examine like the photo was the thing it recorded. I would allow any other Arcanum to do the same with their respective Twilights and such, possibly as a Forces + whatever combined spell to detect the thing, and record it. There is probably a easier way to do it. </div> </div> </div>So you can get a dynamic view of the symbols of a spell as it mutates (to bring it back to the previous conversation) hmm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No problem, I really enjoy Mage, and the technical parts of it. And helping people with something is something I like doing when I can.<br /> <br /> I\u2026 have not had a great last few days, and I hope that none of my frustration with life bled through into my posts. If it did so, I apologize. </div> </div> </div>It has not. These have been very helpful answers and lines of enquiry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T15:21:55-08:00","id":1472817,"title":"","content":"Ok, on the question of observing spells go wonky.<br /> <br /> There is a science experiment where you take white blood cells from two people, dye them so you can see which is which, and them mix them and watch under a microscope to see which ones kill the other first.<br /> <br /> Multiple castings of Dispell magic, AOE with indefinite duration, without the reach to make their effect lasting. All with overlapping areas, and keyed to dispell Prime. <br /> <br /> Different nimbuses? Conjunctional Prime Wards? Varying potency? Survival of the fittest, kinda...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T15:34:21-08:00","id":1472818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472813#post1472813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tune in needs to be knowing to get meaning... Does active mage sight let you sense radio waves, or should you have some unveiling spell aswell?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sadly, Forces AMS doesn\u2019t let you see radio waves on it\u2019s own, unless it\u2019s strong enough to count as a tilt. You do need Unveiling to see other frequencies besides the visible of light.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472813#post1472813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can get a dynamic view of the symbols of a spell as it mutates (to bring it back to the previous conversation) hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh! That\u2019s a great use for it! (I feel like the spells allowed to grow and change need a fancy name, but I\u2019m terrible with giving stuff names.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472813#post1472813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has not. These have been very helpful answers and lines of enquiry.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T20:18:50-08:00","id":1472843,"title":"","content":"The 2e core books says Totems can &quot;provide mages with material components for spells and magical items that can\u2019t be found anywhere on Earth&quot;. Should that be interpreted as having to rip the fangs out of a Supernal Sabertooth's skull, or more like bargaining with a Supernal Koi for one of its scales? There's room for both interpretations in a setting, obviously, but murdering a supernal being for some reagents seems more the domain of Exalted than Mage. Or at least a Wisdom sin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-19-2022, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T20:29:07-08:00","id":1472845,"title":"","content":"Who says you have to murder a thing for it\u2019s eyes? But seriously, both are just different variations of the Trial, involving different skills than each other, obviously. There is even a Boon of Life Beasts (not just Atavisms) can grant healing/mana potions by ripping the thing apart with your bare hands. Your call if that\u2019s a Wisdom sin, but it\u2019s something some Supernal Entities allow.<br /> <br /> Edit: spelling, though Bear hands is accidentally amusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-19-2022, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T20:52:57-08:00","id":1472852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472845#post1472845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says you have to murder a thing for it\u2019s eyes? But seriously, both are just different variations of the Trial, involving different skills than each other, obviously. There is even a Boon of Life Beasts (not just Atavisms) can grant healing/mana potions by ripping the thing apart with your bare hands. Your call if that\u2019s a Wisdom sin, but it\u2019s something some Supernal Entities allow.<br /> <br /> Edit: spelling, though Bear hands is accidentally amusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I shall use my BEAR HANDS, which I claimed from the Supurnal Bear, to tear you apart, Supernal Salmon! Raaaaar!<br /> <br /> Could you point me in the direction of that Boon you mentioned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T20:58:28-08:00","id":1472855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472852#post1472852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I shall use my BEAR HANDS, which I claimed from the Supurnal Bear, to tear you apart, Supernal Salmon! Raaaaar!<br /> <br /> Could you point me in the direction of that Boon you mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Signs of Sorcery pg 42 \u201cFlesh of the Prey\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T05:17:35-08:00","id":1472869,"title":"","content":"Its also expanded upon on page 103 of <i>Summoners</i>.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the mage is conducting the Supernal version of &quot;I hunt this prey for the resources I need to survive&quot;. If the Supernal Entity is fine with it, I would say its unlikely to be an Act of Hubris. A clean kill or one where you need to win via combining lots of dirty tricks? Sure, hunts are messy, you can't be perfect every time, but you are not intentionally trying to prolong their suffering. <br /> <br /> Its also being conducted inside a summoning area that is probably prepared to minimize risks to others and without risking the summon being lost to the Abyss upon &quot;death&quot;. So its probably ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-20-2022, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T06:04:06-08:00","id":1472870,"title":"","content":"New Question, what would a Death spell of Making Absence do?<br /> <br /> My thoughts are Absence of heat and light, health and energy (possibly only limited amounts of these).<br /> <br /> Those are the obvious choices (as it is making Cold, Darkness, decay and Enervation, respectively) as they are all in the purview of Death. <br /> <br /> Could you fill a room with this Absence? (AOE stops these things from functioning). <br /> <br /> Would it need to be seperate spells?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, can you unmake Absence. So take someone suffering grief and unmake the Absence the feel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T06:07:52-08:00","id":1472871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472818#post1472818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh! That\u2019s a great use for it! (I feel like the spells allowed to grow and change need a fancy name, but I\u2019m terrible with giving stuff names.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, but i think a mage who 'feeds*' the spell(s) should be called a zookeeper.<br /> <br /> *By using focused mage sight and paying mana to see how it interact a with the Spell's pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T08:01:03-08:00","id":1472875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472870#post1472870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Question, what would a Death spell of Making Absence do?<br /> <br /> My thoughts are Absence of heat and light, health and energy (possibly only limited amounts of these).<br /> <br /> Those are the obvious choices (as it is making Cold, Darkness, decay and Enervation, respectively) as they are all in the purview of Death. <br /> <br /> Could you fill a room with this Absence? (AOE stops these things from functioning). <br /> <br /> Would it need to be seperate spells?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, can you unmake Absence. So take someone suffering grief and unmake the Absence the feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe creating a vacuum? Either a vacuum that persists by keeping other matter out, or a vacuum space that immediately fills with the surrounding matter with all the consequences that implies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T08:49:10-08:00","id":1472882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472871#post1472871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, but i think a mage who 'feeds*' the spell(s) should be called a zookeeper.<br /> <br /> *By using focused mage sight and paying mana to see how it interact a with the Spell's pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a gardener. This whole concept is right up the Tamers of Roots alley. I can just imagine them planting the Spell Seed in their garden, watering it with resonance, and waiting for it to bloom! I wonder how that approach changes the spells, as compared to actively feeding the spell mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T08:54:06-08:00","id":1472883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472875#post1472875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe creating a vacuum? Either a vacuum that persists by keeping other matter out, or a vacuum space that immediately fills with the surrounding matter with all the consequences that implies.</div> </div> </div> </div> This may be relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469672#post1469672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do every time you do something with something that is something.<br /> <br /> Or, to be precise for vacuum, with Matter (and Forces if you want to talk true vacuum).<br /> <br /> When you create content you destroy void, when you destroy content you create void.<br /> <br /> The key difference about Death here, though, is that we're not talking about deterioration or antithesis, but true absence. A corpse is opposed to Life because it is the deteriorating husk of the living. It is not mere absence, but a Symbol of degradation, destruction, end.<br /> <br /> But what about an empty room? This, not a corpse or ghost, is the Absence of Life. No lingering force, no memory or decaying husk, just nothing alive is there to begin with.<br /> <br /> Death is about the decaying and decayed, not about mere absence. It is about the ghost and the corpse, not about the empty room. That's why it isn't the Arcanum of void and vacuum, because those aren't the opposition of things, but just the absence of things.<br /> <br /> And absence you define by what is absent. You already deal with it with the other Arcana. So the question isn't what you do with vacuum, but what the complete absence of phenomena related to an Arcanum means.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T11:01:41-08:00","id":1472891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472883#post1472883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And absence you define by what is absent. You already deal with it with the other Arcana. So the question isn't what you do with vacuum, but what the complete absence of phenomena related to an Arcanum means.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why Cold, and Darkness make sense, they are defined by absences. Area of effects with some duration would affect any valid target, but i suppose that doesn't really apply to a Making spell? You are not making it from a subject which can enter and then leave the area... <br /> <br /> My thought was that as light entered the area it would become darkness, absent itself, so by the time you get to the center it would be completely dark. That at least makes a distinct effect from a space 3 Weaving's Ban spell.<br /> <br /> But the more i think about it that doesn't really fit. It isn't targeting the incoming light and transforming it. It is making an Absence...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T11:03:43-08:00","id":1472892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472882#post1472882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a gardener. This whole concept is right up the Tamers of Roots alley. I can just imagine them planting the Spell Seed in their garden, watering it with resonance, and waiting for it to bloom! I wonder how that approach changes the spells, as compared to actively feeding the spell mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see a legacy splitting now, between the gardener faction and the zookeeper faction...<br /> <br /> EDIT: I really like the resonance angle not something i would have thought of... And combining the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-20-2022, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T11:19:55-08:00","id":1472894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472891#post1472891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why Cold, and Darkness make sense, they are defined by absences. Area of effects with some duration would affect any valid target, but i suppose that doesn't really apply to a Making spell? You are not making it from a subject which can enter and then leave the area...<br /> <br /> My thought was that as light entered the area it would become darkness, absent itself, so by the time you get to the center it would be completely dark. That at least makes a distinct effect from a space 3 Weaving's Ban spell.<br /> <br /> But the more i think about it that doesn't really fit. It isn't targeting the incoming light and transforming it. It is making an Absence...</div> </div> </div> </div>This <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1373121#post1373121\">spell</a> may also be relevant to the discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T21:04:50-08:00","id":1472931,"title":"","content":"Signs of Sorcery provides a bit more information on the topic. Mastigos see abscence as the cessation of self, whereas Thyrsus see it as an absence of life, light and warmth.<br /> <br /> The main issue happens when asking &quot;absence of what ?&quot; , it seems like it requires other Arcana for context and even then, how is it different from using Unmaking with that Arcanum ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T21:21:06-08:00","id":1472934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472931#post1472931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main issue happens when asking &quot;absence of what ?&quot; , it seems like it requires other Arcana for context and even then, how is it different from using Unmaking with that Arcanum ?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is precisely that Vacuum and Absence are precisely just the result of a thorough Unmaking, and defined by the other Arcana, not Death (unless you want to Unmake Death, evidently).<br /> <br /> You could add some other effect to ward off the entry of new instances of that Arcana, but otherwise Making Void is just a fallacy, not an actual spell.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that the Void so created can't contain its own Mysteries, as you can learn a lot about something by examining complete absence of it, especially if this absence is rare or non-existent in nature. It can have its own weird effects and so on. But isn't a Supernal Symbol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T07:16:32-08:00","id":1472964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1369434#post1369434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's using Patterning to rewrite the Gnosis potential/Gnosis retention of another mage's soul/soul stone into your own effective Gnosis in the same fashion as teleportation uses Patterning to &quot;rewrite&quot; a subject's physical location.<br /> <br /> Given that most things that aren't soul stones and mage souls don't have any direct impact on your Gnosis, probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. I see what this question was answering. (Ie can you graft a spirit into your Gnosis with Patterning of spirit+prime). And i think i agree with Satchel.<br /> <br /> However it gets another question, can you graft a Spirit into your soul to gain their (non-gnosis) related power. Possibly Spirit + Death, since you don't have a Spirit normally?<br /> <br /> Maybe gain access to 1 numina/influence per potency of the spell? (My thinking here is that you can shape your soul using legacies to gain supernatural abilities... So can you graft other things onto your soul to gain supernatural effects...) <br /> <br /> Of course being able to power them with essence may be an issue... But i suppose if you have Spirit 4 gaining essence isn't too hard.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and thinking about it, you should he able to find a path in your Onerios to the Anima Mundi related to the spirit you have granted on, and probably be worse as preventing the Anima Mundi from damaging your soul (as your soul has a hole in it that lets the Ecstatic Wind right in)... And also dying from Ecstatic wind is probably way worse (as instead of just being soul shocked, you have a spirit ready to fill up your soul)<br /> <br /> Of course if you're going to go the whole way, graft the soul of a werewolf onto your soul, you end up with a bunch of pissed off werewolves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-21-2022, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T08:12:37-08:00","id":1472969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472931#post1472931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Signs of Sorcery provides a bit more information on the topic. Mastigos see abscence as the cessation of self, whereas Thyrsus see it as an absence of life, light and warmth.<br /> <br /> The main issue happens when asking &quot;absence of what ?&quot; , it seems like it requires other Arcana for context and even then, how is it different from using Unmaking with that Arcanum ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Death is clear, cold and darkness are not real physical things*, they are absences of heat and light (Forces Arcanum), but Absence is the purview of Death so metaphysically this arcanum can treat them as positive actual things.<br /> <br /> Likewise decay is close to an absence of growth, enervation is an absence of energy. Are ghosts an absence of the soul/life? - the twilight 'echos' of buildings are only there as the absence of the original building (are they made of Ectoplasm?) <br /> <br /> Everything Death can Make, is an absence (notable the Soul and the Underworld are under the purview of Death but can't be made).<br /> <br /> The spell Empty Presence: &quot;The mage destroys the subject\u2019s presence in the world, removing any evidence of her life or existence. &quot; Should probably be a Making practice not Unmaking.<br /> <br /> That at least is my understanding of Making Absence. You can't simply Unmake thing in other Arcanum's purview. Unmaking a person (Life) doesn't create a Ghost, but a Making of Death can.<br /> <br /> *At least according to our physics.<br /> <br /> EDIT: to put this in the form of a question, can you Make the absence of a child in the mind of someone who has never had children (grief), it is touching on the Purview of Mind, but you are allowed to have the same effect coming from two different Arcana...<br /> <br /> EDIT2: Or the feeling of an empty chair at a party, like someone is missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-21-2022, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T08:17:09-08:00","id":1472971,"title":"","content":"Looking at the other purview of Death that i haven't mentioned, can you use endings to end a spell? Like trigger the condition for a conditional duration spell? Can you dispell any spell by Making an ending for it? (Probably the same effect as Supernal Dispellation), i think i recall seeing that somewhere...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T10:11:58-08:00","id":1472977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472971#post1472971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the other purview of Death that i haven't mentioned, can you use endings to end a spell? Like trigger the condition for a conditional duration spell? Can you dispell any spell by Making an ending for it? (Probably the same effect as Supernal Dispellation), i think i recall seeing that somewhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition gave ending a spell as part of Death's roster, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T13:54:38-08:00","id":1472993,"title":"","content":"The Duel Arcane appears to have been simplified, which is nice, but does that mean that the variants like Shadow Chess are now thematic decisions? I liked the idea of some Consilli turning the whole thing into a children's card game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T14:54:20-08:00","id":1472994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472971#post1472971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the other purview of Death that i haven't mentioned, can you use endings to end a spell? Like trigger the condition for a conditional duration spell? Can you dispell any spell by Making an ending for it? (Probably the same effect as Supernal Dispellation), i think i recall seeing that somewhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>Signs of Sorcery gives us \u2018Death of Magic\u2019 as an example Boon for Angels with the Death Arcanum. Considering how Death is the Inferior Arcanum of the Obrimos, and what other \u2018Inferior Arcanum Boons\u2019 look like, I suspect using Death to end spells etc is \u201cNot The Intended Use, but hey it works\u201d approach here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T14:57:55-08:00","id":1472995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1472993#post1472993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Duel Arcane appears to have been simplified, which is nice, but does that mean that the variants like Shadow Chess are now thematic decisions? I liked the idea of some Consilli turning the whole thing into a children's card game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The default assumption for 1E-2E translation seems to be that, unless it was explicitly axed away or otherwise changed, it\u2019s still there. Just without official mechanical support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-22T02:22:31-08:00","id":1473025,"title":"","content":"The question came up on page 430 of this thread about copying or stealing temporal sympathies.<br /> <br /> I want to know, could you take or Make a weak temporal sympathy to someone else in the past - 'the subject is vastly different', seems an appropriate level of sympathy to maintain... And is it fair to presume similar impacts that you would expect from spatial sympathies (how they affect emotional connection). So perhaps a temporal sympathy would give a sense of deja vu for things that never happened to you. Or push you towards creating a future/destiny which would be appropriate for your sympathic past (like how shadow names can affect you narratively)? <br /> <br /> Can you unmake your own temporal sympathy to you past? (Making any remaining sympathies more significant?) Could you use Perfecting to make yourself more like someone else's past? And use this as a subtle form of identity theft?<br /> <br /> Seperately but definitely related, by Unmaking a person's temporal sympathies to their past, can you make them free-er to pursue new aspirations unrelated to their past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-22-2022, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-22T10:50:38-08:00","id":1473036,"title":"","content":"Using the Transmute Numen, is it possible for ghost engineers to build a high tech boat ? What difficulty category would the materials and alloys be ? Would they need to work the materials into shape or does the Numen already do that for them ?<br /> <br /> Similarly, would the ghost of a famous blacksmith be able to use the maximum Rank of Transmute to make perfected metals ? Since they can occur in nature, the should be under its purview, albeit at the highest difficulty (I think alloys are way out of its purview). But it might allow weapons of &quot;meteoric iron&quot; made with lost techniques to suddenly show up. Both could be interesting Mysteries for a Forge Master to pursue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-22T20:45:03-08:00","id":1473056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473036#post1473036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, would the ghost of a famous blacksmith be able to use the maximum Rank of Transmute to make perfected metals ? Since they can occur in nature, the should be under its purview, albeit at the highest difficulty (I think alloys are way out of its purview). But it might allow weapons of &quot;meteoric iron&quot; made with lost techniques to suddenly show up. Both could be interesting Mysteries for a Forge Master to pursue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd vote that ghosts of Craftsmen can &quot;use themselves up&quot; creating a perfected item. It would have to be a ghost who lingers because of something crafting-related, like an unfinished masterwork or regret over never mastering a family specialty. In the act of fulfilling that Anchor, they pour themselves into the craft to trigger the refinement.<br /> <br /> __________<br /> <br /> Reading Temporal Sympathy, I can't just take Supernal Fire or Thunderbolt and slap TS on it to recreate Balefire from The Wheel of Time. A Time Disciple can still delete someone from history with Temporal Sympathy and Rend Lifespan though, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-22-2022, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-22T21:08:27-08:00","id":1473057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473056#post1473056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading Temporal Sympathy, I can't just take Supernal Fire or Thunderbolt and slap TS on it to recreate Balefire from The Wheel of Time. A Time Disciple can still delete someone from history with Temporal Sympathy and Rend Lifespan though, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that getting Lasting effects out of Temporal Sympathy requires actually engaging with the mechanics for time travel, given that otherwise the exercise amounts to either &quot;this is uncontestably completely broken&quot; or &quot;it is entirely up to the Storyteller what happened in the time between that point in history and the present&quot; with no guidance presented for anything in-between.<br /> <br /> &quot;Time spells that call for it&quot; means &quot;Time spells that say you can use Temporal Sympathy.&quot; You can do all sorts of stuff on a temporary basis with Rewrite History, but making it a persistent fact that Master Entomologos was eaten by radioactive fire-ants thirty years ago is going to require the legwork of making that actually happen in experienced history for it to be real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-22T22:06:25-08:00","id":1473058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473056#post1473056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> __________<br /> <br /> Reading Temporal Sympathy, I can't just take Supernal Fire or Thunderbolt and slap TS on it to recreate Balefire from The Wheel of Time. A Time Disciple can still delete someone from history with Temporal Sympathy and Rend Lifespan though, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cult of the Doomsday Clock, a Legacy from 1E, does something like that; erasing the reality of the Fallen World, one past event by another. They do that using 'Doomsday Clocks,' a special magical item that creatively combines the Time 4 spell &quot;Erase History&quot; (1E; not in 2E) and other destructive spells (the given example being &quot;Annihilate Matter&quot;). Notably, &quot;Erase History&quot; is only supposed to conceal information - it's the combined destructive spells <i>and</i> its maker &amp; users' Abyssal power that enables this feat.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to flirt with the Abyss, an Archmage using what 1E calls Time 7 Excision spells should work. Or a sufficiently powerful Time Artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T09:54:44-08:00","id":1473082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473058#post1473058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably, &quot;Erase History&quot; is only supposed to conceal information</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, between that and being Lasting, I'd say that spell as written doesn't really translate very well to Second Edition. It's got an effect that belongs to Veiling (or Unmaking), and is out of the usual bounds for what Lasts.<br /> <br /> That being said, we do have the Space Unmaking Spell &quot;Quarantine&quot;, that can include Mastery of Time to render its subject retroactively non-existent alongside being thrown outside of the universe, removing or reassigning all of its effects for the spell's Duration. It still kind of establishes a precedent for the idea that erasing something from the past requires much greater power than a Disciple.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, I think if the Cult of the Doomsday Clock was going to be adapted, I'd say they should make more use of Paradox Anomalies in their history erasure efforts, and the Clocks themselves would be modelled as more direct Artifacts through what we know now about the power of archmastery (and items that can emulate it) rather than moulding together a bunch of other effects.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T11:35:02-08:00","id":1473090,"title":"","content":"Aye, the Ticktock Men not having frequently used their time-bombs was assumed to be from difficulty in manufacturing. That would imply Quintessence, or at least some Abyssal equivalent. <br /> <br /> No balefire then. Probably for the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T12:21:16-08:00","id":1473094,"title":"","content":"Siderite is capable of slicing through just about anything. Mechanically this means ignoring Durability, which is basically saying &quot;if you want to make an Excalibur, this is probably a good way to start&quot;.<br /> <br /> By the same logic, would it be reasonable to assume that siderite bullets ignore armor from all mundane protective gear ?<br /> <br /> On a side note, maybe a spell that utilizes a different configuration of perfected metals can be used to create an offensive version of thaumium, thus creating bullets that Clash to pierce magical armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-23-2022, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T13:05:15-08:00","id":1473102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473094#post1473094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siderite is capable of slicing through just about anything. Mechanically this means ignoring Durability, which is basically saying &quot;if you want to make an Excalibur, this is probably a good way to start&quot;.<br /> <br /> By the same logic, would it be reasonable to assume that siderite bullets ignore armor from all mundane protective gear ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Extremely reasonable, I should think. It\u2019s basically a extremely Metal Jacketed Round. I don\u2019t know if that has mechanics, but as I understand, armor piercing is what FMJ rounds do. I think. I don\u2019t know guns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473094#post1473094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side note, maybe a spell that utilizes a different configuration of perfected metals can be used to create an offensive version of thaumium, thus creating bullets that Clash to pierce magical armor.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds fine to me. Maybe the proportions would be different much like real world alloys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T14:57:06-08:00","id":1473114,"title":"","content":"How do exceptional successes work with extended actions? Do you have to exceed the target successes by five?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T15:35:18-08:00","id":1473118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473114#post1473114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do exceptional successes work with extended actions? Do you have to exceed the target successes by five?</div> </div> </div> </div>They work as normally for rolls, giving you the set of options listed on page 213; specific rolls will say if there is something special that occurs when you exceed the target success number by five or more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T16:14:06-08:00","id":1473119,"title":"","content":"When can Blood, Sweat, Tears, etc be targeted by Matter spells, if ever?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T16:29:04-08:00","id":1473121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473119#post1473119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When can Blood, Sweat, Tears, etc be targeted by Matter spells, if ever?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe its after a few minutes from being separated from the source. When they become symbolically dead, transitioning from Life to Matter, then they can be affected. This is building upon the theory upon which perfected living material is made, which is presented on page 64 of Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-23-2022, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T16:42:51-08:00","id":1473122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473121#post1473121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe its after a few minutes from being separated from the source. When they become symbolically dead, transitioning from Life to Matter, then they can be affected. This is building upon the theory upon which perfected living material is made, which is presented on page 64 of Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I had forgotten they specified that. Guess you need Life to kill with a kiss. (Was thinking of a Prime/Matter legacy devoted to lies and poison. Probably not going to make it, since I don\u2019t have time, but fun to speculate about.) <br /> Oh, had a idea, is it possible to make resistant damage with a Prime + whatever by Weaving that property of Pattern Scourging into it? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T17:23:16-08:00","id":1473125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473122#post1473122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, I had forgotten they specified that. Guess you need Life to kill with a kiss. (Was thinking of a Prime/Matter legacy devoted to lies and poison. Probably not going to make it, since I don\u2019t have time, but fun to speculate about.) <br /> Oh, had a idea, is it possible to make resistant damage with a Prime + whatever by Weaving that property of Pattern Scourging into it? <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think all you need is to use Hone the Perfected form to make perfected poison. I would call it Cantarella (to reference the near mythical toxin of the Borgias), make it odorless, tasteless, colorless, undetectable and incurable by mundane medicine, with [Potency] toxicity.<br /> <br /> Then just have ready some perfected antipoison, which I would call Mithridate in reference to the poison king and his legendary formula. Alternatively, the mage could use Alchemist's Touch to gain immunity to the Cantarella before coating her lips in the poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T17:27:29-08:00","id":1473126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473122#post1473122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, had a idea, is it possible to make resistant damage with a Prime + whatever by Weaving that property of Pattern Scourging into it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Separately from Devouring the Slain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T18:14:45-08:00","id":1473128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473126#post1473126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Separately from Devouring the Slain?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I mostly was thinking on how to poison a Life Mage and actually pose a interesting threat. Resistant damage can\u2019t be healed by magic, and causing resistant damage is a property of pattern scouring. If you can make your damage resistant, then the Life Mage has to think around the problem rather simply heal themselves and move on. On second thought, Mages having access to resistant damage outside of Devouring the Slain opens a problematic can of worms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-23-2022, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T18:38:34-08:00","id":1473132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473128#post1473128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, I mostly was thinking on how to poison a Life Mage and actually pose a interesting threat. Resistant damage can\u2019t be healed by magic, and causing resistant damage is a property of pattern scouring. If you can make your damage resistant, then the Life Mage has to think around the problem rather simply heal themselves and move on. On second thought, Mages having access to resistant damage outside of Devouring the Slain opens a problematic can of worms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe \u2018Attribute damage\u2019 via a really clingy version of Degrade the Form? Life magic can still offset it, but hey at least it forces Spell Control.<br /> <br /> Also, your poisoner Legacy idea inspired me to do idly wonder about the Sichuan Tang-men of wuxia trope fame in the CofD, Mage or otherwise <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T23:55:38-08:00","id":1473148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473102#post1473102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> as I understand, armor piercing is what FMJ rounds do. I think. I don\u2019t know guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most modern bullets consist of lead in a full metal jacket (typically copper based), to get the best of lead's high density while also letting it leave the gun barrel smoothly. Armour-piercing bullets consist of a core of harder metal, often a steel, to force its way through the armour. Bullets might not be fully jacketed if they're intended to expand on impact.<br /> <br /> For simplicity's sake, I'd say a bullet with siderite components would readily pierce armour.<br /> <br /> I think mages should have fairly limited options to inflict resistant damage specifically because the utility of the Life Arcanum would lend itself to a scenario where that's the only kind of damage worth inflicting. Also some of the issues with the general principle of &quot;here's the one thing your cool powers straight up don't work on&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think a mage can poison a Life mage with something they can't fix at all if they extract it from some Mystery or the Abyss, and poison of their own generation has to sustain itself against healing magic with Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T13:12:38-08:00","id":1473191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473148#post1473148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think mages should have fairly limited options to inflict resistant damage specifically because the utility of the Life Arcanum would lend itself to a scenario where that's the only kind of damage worth inflicting. Also some of the issues with the general principle of &quot;here's the one thing your cool powers straight up don't work on&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it\u2019s not worth the problems it causes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473148#post1473148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a mage can poison a Life mage with something they can't fix at all if they extract it from some Mystery or the Abyss, and poison of their own generation has to sustain itself against healing magic with Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div> I seem to remember there being some kind of benefit for Clashes of Wills originating from a Legacy Attainment, but I can\u2019t seem to find it. Am I misremembering something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-24-2022, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T13:28:17-08:00","id":1473193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473191#post1473191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it\u2019s not worth the problems it causes.<br /> <br /> I seem to remember their being some kind of benefit for Clashes of Wills originating from a Legacy Attainment, but I can\u2019t seem to find it. Am I misremembering something?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe its based on the Automatic Activation subsection on page 198, which then lead to the way the Eleventh Question's first optional Attainment pierces concealment (page 201)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T13:39:10-08:00","id":1473197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473193#post1473193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe its based on the Automatic Activation subsection on page 198, which then lead to the way the Eleventh Question's first optional Attainment pierces concealment (page 201)</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks, I\u2019m blind, and I was losing my mind for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T13:43:51-08:00","id":1473198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473191#post1473191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to remember there being some kind of benefit for Clashes of Wills originating from a Legacy Attainment, but I can\u2019t seem to find it. Am I misremembering something?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473193#post1473193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe its based on the Automatic Activation subsection on page 198, which then lead to the way the Eleventh Question's first optional Attainment pierces concealment (page 201)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAutomatic successes on activation rolls doesn't affect Clash of Wills. They are rolled normally. This is something the community has repeatedly gotten wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T13:52:03-08:00","id":1473199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473198#post1473198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bAutomatic successes on activation rolls doesn't affect Clash of Wills. They are rolled normally. This is something the community has repeatedly gotten wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, when it says \u201c\u2026Active Mage Sight (Matter) upon arrival. If it must pierce any form of supernatural concealment, it automatically scores successes equal to the mage\u2019s Matter dots.\u201d, it isn\u2019t referring to the Clash of Wills, or isn\u2019t a precedent for Automatic successes applying to the Clash of Wills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T14:10:36-08:00","id":1473201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473199#post1473199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, when it says \u201c\u2026Active Mage Sight (Matter) upon arrival. If it must pierce any form of supernatural concealment, it automatically scores successes equal to the mage\u2019s Matter dots.\u201d, it isn\u2019t referring to the Clash of Wills, or isn\u2019t a precedent for Automatic successes applying to the Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Eleventh Question\u2019s Attainment? It seems \u2018automatic Clash\u2019 there <i>is</i> the Attainment\u2019s (Optional) effect, since the Option doesn\u2019t do anything else otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T15:02:36-08:00","id":1473207,"title":"","content":"I can't tell you why it breaks the rules (alternatively, why it nonsensically would reference activation successes for Mage Sight that is normally never rolled), nor can I tell you why activating Mage Sight is deemed worthy of being an Attainment, but I can <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/881992-mage-the-awakening-2nd-edition-errata-thread?p=889508\">link</a> the dev clarification regarding Legacy Attainment CoWs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T15:08:55-08:00","id":1473208,"title":"","content":"\u2026well, guess that definitively answers that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T09:57:21-08:00","id":1473273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1419755#post1419755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tl;dr the vast majority of spells will succeed, either because they're simply not Withstood or because it's very easy to just compensate if needed. The only spell I remember casting that failed because of spell factors was when I failed to take Size into account</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of size. Is there any concensus on how Mind affect large animals/monsters? <br /> <br /> Eg: a size 7 horse, does it require extra scale for large target? Does Life and Mind treat it differently? <br /> <br /> Likewise, do Zombies, Golems, Eidolons and similar have no mind (without the addition of a mind 5 conjunctional effect) and are thus impervious to Mind effects (with the possible except of possession)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-25-2022, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T10:04:42-08:00","id":1473274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473273#post1473273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of size. Is there any concensus on how Mind affect large animals/monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. If it has a mind, Mind works on it. You can use Mind on dogs, elephant and claimed houses all the same. Well, except for scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473273#post1473273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eg: a size 7 horse, does it require extra scale for large target? Does Life and Mind treat it differently?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. Other than affecting the body or the mind, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473273#post1473273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, do Zombies, Golems, Eidolons and similar have no mind (without the addition of a mind 5 conjunctional effect) and are thus impervious to Mind effects (with the possible except of possession)?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, no mind, nothing to affect. You can cast the spell mind you, it just won\u2019t do anything.<br /> <br /> Edit: Giving it a mind with Making is another example of something it\u2019s not impervious to. Possession works fine, since you are just moving the vessel you mind is in. You can possess a rock if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-25-2022, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T10:06:17-08:00","id":1473275,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473273#post1473273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of size. Is there any concensus on how Mind affect large animals/monsters?<br /> <br /> Eg: a size 7 horse, does it require extra scale for large target? Does Life and Mind treat it differently?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a spell is cast on a subject, it needs to have enough Scale factor steps to accomodate for the subject's Size.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473273#post1473273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, do Zombies, Golems, Eidolons and similar have no mind (without the addition of a mind 5 conjunctional effect) and are thus impervious to Mind effects (with the possible except of possession)?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, nothing has an outright immunity to any single Arcanum. It's all about the specific spell effects. Most Mind spells won't have any effect at all on those as long as they don't have any minds, but some Mind spells doesn't affect the subject's mind and can affect those just as well as a human subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T10:49:18-08:00","id":1473279,"title":"","content":"How does spellcasting account for targeted attacks ? Should a target be so big that you can only reasonably make a quick attack on its leg or when trying to snipe the wings of a flying being, if both cases use sensory range, does that impose a specified target penalty ? Does a similar penalty apply only when trying to hit with an aimed spell ? Similarly, if only part of a giant target is hit by an area of effect, are only those specific limbs attacked or is the subject entirely unaffected ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:11:57-08:00","id":1473281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473275#post1473275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> If a spell is cast on a subject, it needs to have enough Scale factor steps to accomodate for the subject's Size.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think that is in question. The only question is what size is the subject's mind.<br /> <br /> Eg: does an elephant have an elephant sized mind?\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In general, nothing has an outright immunity to any single Arcanum. It's all about the specific spell effects. Most Mind spells won't have any effect at all on those as long as they don't have any minds, but some Mind spells doesn't affect the subject's mind and can affect those just as well as a human subject. </div> </div> </div>Can you give an example? <br /> <br /> Like take Psychic assault &quot;A living mind is a delicate thing, easily broken... The subject takes bashing damage equal to Potency.&quot;<br /> <br /> As read, the Elephant Zombie with no mind, as a subject of this spell requires Scale and takes bashing damage. Or their mind is the Subject, in which case it has none and can't be affected, (or perhaps with conjunctional mind/ghost possession - it has a kind but it is this ghost/goetia which is the subject* and it doesn't necessarily have the scale of an elephant?)<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Can you cast grant skill on a Golem to give them new &quot;fields&quot;? I can't think of any other listed Mind spell which you could use on a mindless Zombie...<br /> <br /> *This seems like a distinct case, where the possessing ephemeral entity has their own health track. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:12:37-08:00","id":1473282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473279#post1473279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does spellcasting account for targeted attacks ? Should a target be so big that you can only reasonably make a quick attack on its leg or when trying to snipe the wings of a flying being, if both cases use sensory range, does that impose a specified target penalty ? Does a similar penalty apply only when trying to hit with an aimed spell ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no reason to ever do a targeted attack with aimed spells. If the spell hits, it affects the subject. An aimed spell hitting the subject's arm would still inflict a Leg Wrack if that's the effect of the spell.<br /> Targeted sensory range spells doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473279#post1473279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, if only part of a giant target is hit by an area of effect, are only those specific limbs attacked or is the subject entirely unaffected ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Book doesn't say how to handle subjects that are both inside and outside an AoE. But for subjects that are so large that you can't cover them with an AoE, they'd absolutely not be valid subjects since they obviously outclass the Scale factor. (Spells like &quot;fill this AoE with fire&quot; still fills the area with fire which may affect anyone who's wholly or partly within the area.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:15:07-08:00","id":1473283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473279#post1473279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does spellcasting account for targeted attacks ? Should a target be so big that you can only reasonably make a quick attack on its leg or when trying to snipe the wings of a flying being, if both cases use sensory range, does that impose a specified target penalty ? Does a similar penalty apply only when trying to hit with an aimed spell ? Similarly, if only part of a giant target is hit by an area of effect, are only those specific limbs attacked or is the subject entirely unaffected ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the targeted body part its own supernal symbol which can be used to target that precise thing? <br /> <br /> Like does a 'wing' have a meaning which allows it to be targeted by a spell? <br /> <br /> Are there any spells which use part of a target as the subject?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:17:52-08:00","id":1473284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473282#post1473282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book doesn't say how to handle subjects that are both inside and outside an AoE. But for subjects that are so large that you can't cover them with an AoE, they'd absolutely not be valid subjects since they obviously outclass the Scale factor. (Spells like &quot;fill this AoE with fire&quot; still fills the area with fire which may affect anyone who's wholly or partly within the area.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this answer my question from a few pages back on AOE dispellation? If you only partially cover the area of a targeted spell does it do nothing (rather than suppressing part of the spell in the area targeted)?<br /> <br /> EDIT: i realise i am assuming here that area of effect spells have a scale factor which dispellation needs to overcome to affect. Or alternatively this could only apply to AoE dispellation, and a targeted spell would be able to dispell without accounting for scale...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-25-2022, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:19:47-08:00","id":1473285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473281#post1473281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only question is what size is the subject's mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the thing. The Size of the subject's mind doesn't matter. The Size of the <i>subject</i> does.<br /> <br /> If the mind was the subject, then you could never affect the mind with touch range or sensory range spells without somehow boosting yourself (by, say, using Mind Sight) because normally it's 100% impossible to directly touch or perceive someone's mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473281#post1473281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you give an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can give you three:<br /> Knowing/Veiling will easily tell you that the subject has no mind.<br /> Incognito Presence will hide the subject from other minds.<br /> Mental Shield will protect the subject from Goetia and Mind spells.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> A fourth example that <i>requires</i> the subject to not have a mind: A Making spell that grants the subject a mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-25-2022, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:24:42-08:00","id":1473286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473285#post1473285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the mind was the subject, then you could never affect the mind with touch range or sensory range spells without somehow boosting yourself (by, say, using Mind Sight) because normally it's 100% impossible to directly touch or perceive someone's mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no. You don't need to directly touch things, you can extend your touch with a weapon, for example, and you still count as effectively connecting for the purpose of casting a touch spell.<br /> <br /> Likewise touch the body, and their mind is connected to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can give you three:<br /> Knowing/Veiling will easily tell you that the subject has no mind.<br /> Incognito Presence will hide the subject from other minds.<br /> Mental Shield will protect the subject from Goetia and Mind spells. </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:25:49-08:00","id":1473287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473281#post1473281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Eg: does an elephant have an elephant sized mind?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473281#post1473281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you give an example?<br /> <br /> Like take Psychic assault &quot;A living mind is a delicate thing, easily broken... The subject takes bashing damage equal to Potency.&quot;<br /> <br /> As read, the Elephant Zombie with no mind, as a subject of this spell requires Scale and takes bashing damage. Or their mind is the Subject, in which case it has none and can't be affected, (or perhaps with conjunctional mind/ghost possession - it has a kind but it is this ghost/goetia which is the subject* and it doesn't necessarily have the scale of an elephant?)<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Can you cast grant skill on a Golem to give them new &quot;fields&quot;? I can't think of any other listed Mind spell which you could use on a mindless Zombie...</div> </div> </div> </div> Grant them a Mind? Bury memories in them? Make them invisible to everything with a Mind? Possess them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473281#post1473281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*This seems like a distinct case, where the possessing ephemeral entity has their own health track. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div> With possession, sure. That\u2019s explicitly how it works. If the possessing entity has a different size, then it requires a different scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:38:10-08:00","id":1473289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473283#post1473283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the targeted body part its own supernal symbol which can be used to target that precise thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026No? Depends on what you mean. You have to target the whole subject. Now you can mess with specific things after you do that. If you want to give someone a unusual eye color, you need to target the whole person, not the eye. Unless the eye is separated from the body, I guess.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:44:44-08:00","id":1473290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473289#post1473289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026No? Depends on what you mean. You have to target the whole subject. Now you can mess with specific things after you do that. If you want to give someone a unusual eye color, you need to target the whole person, not the eye. Unless the eye is separated from the body, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are going to make me come up with metaphysics to make this the case, aren't you?<br /> <br /> So if it is connected, (ie a connected sympathic link in the physical sense) then it is one subject. Presumably then a person and all their clothes/items they are carrying are one subject - for the purposes of scale - and while a life spell will not affect their clothes, and matter spell will, all with them as the subject? (ie the abstraction we use playing the game corresponds to the 'supernal symbology' relevant for the imago?)<br /> <br /> EDIT: actually this seems fine, until i consider something like a building, it would mean i can't target the windows without taking into account the entire scale of the building... Which is counter intuitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-25-2022, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T12:45:53-08:00","id":1473293,"title":"","content":"So, I checked and I don\u2019t think the Core rule book ever defines <i>subject</i>, which makes this difficult. My quick fix would be to ask if breaking the thing will reduce the Health/Structure of the thing, if so they are part of the subject. If not, then they are not part of the thing. Usually, breaking a window doesn\u2019t really affect the overall structure of a building. Secondly, I don\u2019t know how spells spread to clothes when cast on a person. Spells don\u2019t automatically spread to soul stones, even though they are Connected, without Sympathetic magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T14:07:37-08:00","id":1473295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473293#post1473293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I checked and I don\u2019t think the Core rule book ever defines <i>subject</i>, which makes this difficult. My quick fix would be to ask if breaking the thing will reduce the Health/Structure of the thing, if so they are part of the subject. If not, then they are not part of the thing. Usually, breaking a window doesn\u2019t really affect the overall structure of a building. Secondly, I don\u2019t know how spells spread to clothes when cast on a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption was that a subject was anything which you could easily define in English as the subject of the spell. Or to put it another way, a subject would be something which we have symbols for.<br /> <br /> A cell, organ, limb or body could all be subjects of a Life spell. Proteins might be valid targets for Life or Matter, Chemical/Molecules and Atoms would be valid subjects for Matter - but you might want to try AoE effects on matter at that scale, as modifying a single atom isn't going to be particularly useful (even assuming you can get sensory range).<br /> <br /> Other Arcana don't have English words for subjects in the same level of detail... But i think you would allow anything be a subject, so long as the character can understand what they are using as the subject to form the imago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spells don\u2019t automatically spread to soul stones, even though they are Connected, without Sympathetic magic. </div> </div> </div>Yes, i think magically connected and physically connected are treated differently, they are only the same for sympathy. Physically connected things can easily be seperated (like dropping a cup), whereas metaphysically connected items require considerably more effort to form / destroy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: i will say, the touching with a weapon thing makes me think you should be able to cast a spell at touch range on a circle of people holding hands. So long as everyone in the cicrle is taking part, a ritual cast by holding hands...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-25-2022, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T14:39:36-08:00","id":1473296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473295#post1473295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My assumption was that a subject was anything which you could easily define in English as the subject of the spell. Or to put it another way, a subject would be something which we have symbols for.<br /> <br /> A cell, organ, limb or body could all be subjects of a Life spell. Proteins might be valid targets for Life or Matter, Chemical/Molecules and Atoms would be valid subjects for Matter - but you might want to try AoE effects on matter at that scale, as modifying a single atom isn't going to be particularly useful (even assuming you can get sensory range).<br /> <br /> Other Arcana don't have English words for subjects in the same level of detail... But i think you would allow anything be a subject, so long as the character can understand what they are using as the subject to form the imago.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect there\u2019s an implicit difference in the symbolic intuitions for Life and Matter. So an organ is a part of the body (unless explicitly removed), but an aperture etc is not a part of the building (unless explicitly reinforced and integrated).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T14:56:35-08:00","id":1473298,"title":"","content":"The problem with allowing an infinite (or near infinite) reduction of the subject is that it would be completely disconnected from the rules for Withstand. Any spell that is Withstood by the subject uses the character's stats for the Withstand rating. A spell that inflicts an Arm Wrack is not Withstood by the arm's Stamina because the arm doesn't have Stamina; it's Withstood by the character's Stamina so the character is the subject. We simply do not track separate stats for subunits of characters so applying the spellcasting rules system on such subunits doesn't really work. Maybe the character is a pro arm wrestler (having a Specialty on &quot;arm wrestling&quot; and/or &quot;right arm&quot;), or maybe their arm has just become useable after previous injuries but is still severely weakened (which would be represented through a persistent Condition); the character's Stamina is still the same and it's the character's Stamina that is used for the Withstand rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T16:20:03-08:00","id":1473303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473298#post1473298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with allowing an infinite (or near infinite) reduction of the subject is that it would be completely disconnected from the rules for Withstand. Any spell that is Withstood by the subject uses the character's stats for the Withstand rating. A spell that inflicts an Arm Wrack is not Withstood by the arm's Stamina because the arm doesn't have Stamina; it's Withstood by the character's Stamina so the character is the subject. We simply do not track separate stats for subunits of characters so applying the spellcasting rules system on such subunits doesn't really work. Maybe the character is a pro arm wrestler (having a Specialty on &amp;quot;arm wrestling&amp;quot; and/or &amp;quot;right arm&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, or maybe their arm has just become useable after previous injuries but is still severely weakened (which would be represented through a persistent Condition); the character's Stamina is still the same and it's the character's Stamina that is used for the Withstand rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely fair abstractions for the purpose of a game. And as stated, you can remove the arm and then perform magic with it as the subject (possibly Death at that stage). Will it still have no withstand?<br /> <br /> But it still seems like an abstraction for gameplay, rather than a description of how the magic works. Still it answers my question regarding how people play...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T00:10:41-08:00","id":1473323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473303#post1473303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entirely fair abstractions for the purpose of a game. And as stated, you can remove the arm and then perform magic with it as the subject (possibly Death at that stage). Will it still have no withstand?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the spell. Some would be Withstood by Durability, which the arm wouldn't have before it was separated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it still seems like an abstraction for gameplay, rather than a description of how the magic works. </div> </div> </div>Magic is described and understood through rules systems and only experienced through gameplay. For all practical purposes that <i>is</i> how magic works, even if the characters in-setting might never use gameplay terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T01:37:09-08:00","id":1473324,"title":"","content":"I think magic as it works and is experienced within the setting is a bit more than the game rules that can represent it, but I'd also say that discussion of how to target discrete parts of certain subjects is not on the right track because the magic is largely functioning on metaphysics of things being what they're typically experienced as.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T10:11:03-08:00","id":1473342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473324#post1473324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think magic as it works and is experienced within the setting is a bit more than the game rules that can represent it, but I'd also say that discussion of how to target discrete parts of certain subjects is not on the right track because the magic is largely functioning on metaphysics of things being what they're typically experienced as.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you would say ppl normally experience a door and a window as a distinct targetable parts of a building, but not the eye, heart or arm of a person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T16:51:14-08:00","id":1473365,"title":"","content":"I don't think i have seen this asked.<br /> <br /> Where are spells <u>once</u> cast*? If you cast on a person, it follows them around, right? So then if you can see the spell (active prime mage sight) you can target it (with Wards/dispellation) at sensory range.<br /> <br /> Can you touch the subject of the spell and attempt to dispell at touch range? For multiple subject spells i think it is clear the one dispellation is enough to suppress the effect for all targets, but an AoE dispellation effect may have different results... <br /> <br /> So importantly, for AoE effects, can you activate prime mage sight and touch any point in the area to attempt a dispell at touch range? (Or sensory range of you can't get touch range by touching the subject of a spell).<br /> <br /> Actually, that implies you could cast a dispell on yourself to remove a debuff spell without active mage sight (if the spell is touching you then you don't need sensory range... Of course if only prime users can dispell, they can always use active mage sight with prime, but costs a mana for 4/5th of characters, and another mana per attempt to dispell). <br /> <br /> *I guess my original thoughts on this came from Pocket Dimension, as there location of the Spell's subject doesn't exist until the spell is cast... Without going to the pocket dimension, presumably you could dispell on an iris which was created by spell. So if it was actually in your pocket it could be dispelled by someone looking at you... Actually with sensory range can you only see spells where you can sense the subject?<br /> <br /> So you wouldn't know someone had a pocket dimension in their pocket (with active mage sight on) unless you could see their pocket? Or the subject of their spell is the item of clothing itself, thus you can sense the spell if you can see any part of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-26-2022, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T17:23:13-08:00","id":1473366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473365#post1473365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are spells <u>once</u> cast*? If you cast on a person, it follows them around, right? So then if you can see the spell (active prime mage sight) you can target it (with Wards/dispellation) at sensory range.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> *I guess my original thoughts on this came from Pocket Dimension, as there location of the Spell's subject doesn't exist until the spell is cast... Without going to the pocket dimension, presumably you could dispell on an iris which was created by spell. So if it was actually in your pocket it could be dispelled by someone looking at you... Actually with sensory range can you only see spells where you can sense the subject?<br /> <br /> So you wouldn't know someone had a pocket dimension in their pocket (with active mage sight on) unless you could see their pocket? Or the subject of their spell is the item of clothing itself, thus you can sense the spell if you can see any part of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells are objects that occupy the physical space and time required for a spell with their factors to affect the targets or areas they affect. As Pocket Dimension is a Master-level Space spell that is not required to be anchored to a physical space, it can sidestep the vulnerability this entails, but accessing the Made space presents a window in which it can be accessed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you touch the subject of the spell and attempt to dispell at touch range? For multiple subject spells i think it is clear the one dispellation is enough to suppress the effect for all targets, but an AoE dispellation effect may have different results... </div> </div> </div>For multiple-target spells you need to target all the targets to suppress the whole spell. If you have Fate you can suppress less than the whole spell, but that doesn't imply that it's easier to stop ten people from being frogs than it is to stop two of ten people from being frogs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So importantly, for AoE effects, can you activate prime mage sight and touch any point in the area to attempt a dispell at touch range? (Or sensory range of you can't get touch range by touching the subject of a spell). </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind the possible consequences of touching an area-effect spell, yes. The Scale of the dispellation still needs to encompass the whole of the spell's subjects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T18:37:48-08:00","id":1473371,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone! Can someone explain where in the books a full set of rules for familiars, how they work, and what they do? My &quot;speaker of the dead&quot; has invested points to gain one of the ghosts he has helped out along the way to be a familiar for him, so gaining an understand of how the systems work would be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T18:47:07-08:00","id":1473372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473371#post1473371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone! Can someone explain where in the books a full set of rules for familiars, how they work, and what they do? My &quot;speaker of the dead&quot; has invested points to gain one of the ghosts he has helped out along the way to be a familiar for him, so gaining an understand of how the systems work would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for the Familiar Merit are on page 101 of the Mage 2e core rulebook.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Familiar&quot; spell can be found on page 183 of the Mage 2e core rulebook.<br /> <br /> The rules for Invisible Entities (which familiars are a subset of) start on page 252 of the Mage 2e core rulebook, with a sidebar on familiars on page 253; the Familiar Manifestation Condition is described on page 260.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T02:20:56-08:00","id":1473385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473365#post1473365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>A non-AoE spell is a singular thing with no Size. To target it with a non-AoE spell of your own, you only need to perceive one subject of the spell, and you don't need any Scale increases to dispel the spell from all subjects.<br /> If you want to dispel it selectively from multiple subjects (by adding Fate 1), you need Scale enough to cover each subject you wish to dispel, and implicitly also cast the spell on those subjects (meaning you need to touch/perceive those subjects or cast remotely/sympathetically on them).<br /> <br /> <br /> For AoE spells, it's unclear. We simply do not know if an AoE spell that partially overlaps a subject affects that subject.<ul><li>Either it does, and then you don't need to increase Scale on your AoE spell to affect the entirety of the other spell spell.</li> <li>Or it doesn't, and you need to cover the other spell with your own AoE.</li> <li>In either case, a non-AoE Dispel Magic/Supernal Dispellation should still be able to affect an entire AoE spell. It depends on whether an AoE spell can be considered to have size that you need to account for with your Scale factor or not.</li> <li>In <i>neither</i> case would an AoE Dispel Magic/Supernal Dispellation only affect the overlapping parts. A spell either affects the subject or it doesn't. The other spell is the subject. <i>However</i>, we know that you can cast the spell on each individual subject instead of on the spell itself if you use the Fate option. I would personally allow adding Fate 1 (or Space 1) to only suppress the spell from subjects in the overlapping area, with the rationale that the subjects of the first spell would be the subjects of your spell rather than the spell directly. But it's not the default behaviour of the published dispellation spells.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-27-2022, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T03:13:14-08:00","id":1473388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473366#post1473366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells are objects that occupy the physical space and time required for a spell with their factors to affect the targets or areas they affect. As Pocket Dimension is a Master-level Space spell that is not required to be anchored to a physical space, it can sidestep the vulnerability this entails, but accessing the Made space presents a window in which it can be accessed.</div> </div> </div> </div> That was the conclusion i came to.<br /> <br /> I think having an Iris - which is allowed, is it 1 reach per iris, either as part of the spell or you can create a portal as a seperate spell - gives you a downside, people who can see the Iris can see the spell which creates it and thus attempt to dispell it. <br /> <br /> If that is a seperate spell from the pocket dimension (ie not made with the reach option) then you don't lose the whole space just the connection. But it costs an extra spell control/willpower...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For multiple-target spells you need to target all the targets to suppress the whole spell. </div> </div> </div>I can't see anything in the rules which suggests this. Can you provide a page reference?<br /> <br /> My understanding is that, without fate, you have to either completely suppress the spell or not affect any it (AoE effects may differ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bearing in mind the possible consequences of touching an area-effect spell, yes. The Scale of the dispellation still needs to encompass the whole of the spell's subjects. </div> </div> </div>This would make area of effect spell very difficult to dispell. Withstand by potency (plus Wards) plus an additional scale factor. Interesting if correct as i was asking in my first question how to make a pocket dimension for a sanctum as impenetrable as possible.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473385#post1473385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A non-AoE spell is a singular thing with no Size. To target it with a non-AoE spell of your own, you only need to perceive one subject of the spell, and you don't need any Scale increases to dispel the spell from all subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my understanding, i think the question is, can you touch the subject of the spell to cast at touch range (and i think you've answered it, with a yes. Even touch their clothes or with a weapon you are holding).<br /> <br /> This would also apply to veiling the spell, touch one target and veil the spell where ever it is visible...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to dispel it selectively from multiple subjects (by adding Fate 1), you need Scale enough to cover each subject you wish to dispel, and implicitly also cast the spell on those subjects (meaning you need to touch/perceive those subjects or cast remotely/sympathetically on them). </div> </div> </div>This seems much clearer as it is what i would expect from the description of the Fate spell. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For AoE spells, it's unclear. </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that, unclear is fine so long as it is clear that nobody knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-27-2022, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T03:31:08-08:00","id":1473390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In neither case would an AoE Dispel Magic/Supernal Dispellation only affect the overlapping parts. A spell either affects the subject or it doesn't. </div> </div> </div>Interesting, that is exactly the opposite of what i would expect.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to 'dispel' an effect in this way, you would have to Ward targeting the subject not the spell (adding to their withstand) and thus create an AoE which targets the people in the area making the original effect cease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T09:52:48-08:00","id":1473411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473366#post1473366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells are objects that occupy the physical space and time required for a spell with their factors to affect the targets or areas they affect. </div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, assuming this is the case (and targeting a spell requires taking into account its size). Do spells recheck their spell factors as they do with withstand?<br /> <br /> Two possibilities, one yes. In which case you can increase the size of a subject and all spells on them will either be suppressed or fizzle (unless they have extra scale).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, no. In which case you can expand the area inside an AoE effect (with Space) and get effective extra spell factors on the spell.<br /> <br /> I don't find either of these possibilities particularly compelling.<br /> <br /> I was leaning towards no, until i realised that spell do indeed keep checking their duration has expired. And so you can push a spell into the future (with time) or perhaps the past (though i think it can only exist in its own past ..) pulling a spell from its past should give it extra duration, aging it should reduce duration...<br /> <br /> Is that right?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Tangentially related. Can you cast an Aimed spell in a co-located space and throw it through to the other side? I guess the spell effect would appear as if from nowhere?<br /> <br /> EDIT2:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bearing in mind the possible consequences of touching an area-effect spell, yes. </div> </div> </div> And just to be clear, i am presuming you can walk up to a Ban which prevent you from entering an area, lay hands on it to touch the area, and attempt to dispell it (Without being 'inside' the area).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-27-2022, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T10:08:59-08:00","id":1473412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And so you can push a spell into the future (with time) or perhaps the past (though i think it can only exist in its own past ..) pulling a spell from its past should give it extra duration, aging it should reduce duration... </div> </div> </div>So our Gardener/Zookeeper legacy should use Time to age indefinite spells faster so you can see them mutate faster... <br /> <br /> This might require a Temporal Pocket (Time Making). But can you do it with lowerlevel practices of aging? I mean, i presume a shielding of time can not extend the duration of any spells...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T11:23:20-08:00","id":1473414,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473412#post1473412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So our Gardener/Zookeeper legacy should use Time to age indefinite spells faster so you can see them mutate faster...</div> </div> </div> </div> Time works, you could use the growth angle to justify Life as well. Kinda like how movement falls under Forces, Space, and Time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473412#post1473412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might require a Temporal Pocket (Time Making).</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably more like Time Unmaking to delete the time between changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473412#post1473412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But can you do it with lowerlevel practices of aging?</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019d accept Acceleration decreasing the time between intervals, it already lowers the time to do extended actions with a reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473412#post1473412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, i presume a shielding of time can not extend the duration of any spells...</div> </div> </div> </div> Why not? Spells aren\u2019t particularly special, you can totally age them to dust with Time. I don\u2019t see why preserving them with Veil of Moments wouldn\u2019t extend the duration of a spell.<br /> <br /> Edit:You can totally increase the rate of change in a spell with Prime by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-27-2022, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T11:50:32-08:00","id":1473415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Probably more like Time Unmaking to delete the time between changes. </div> </div> </div> Clearly i may be confused, not very good at Time spells, but i know if you cast Temporal Pocket (Making) on an area it experiences duration time and (for anyone outside the area) it appears almost instantaneously to have aged/prepared by that duration.<br /> <br /> Corridors of Time (Unmaking) unmakes the subject's past, which could extend a Spell's duration... I suppose my confusion is Unmaking your future which is the opposite of Unmaking your past?<br /> <br /> Though really Blink of an Eye and Temporal Pocket can achieve the same thing, with different spell factors, the Temporal Pocket allows you spend the actual time casting a ritual (or doing an extended action) without taking the +2 reach (but you need area of effect and duration...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t see why preserving them with Veil of Moments wouldn\u2019t extend the duration of a spell </div> </div> </div>I don't think duration of a spell is a time effect. I think it is a conditional effect. The spell doesn't age, it simply is over a certain area/subject(s) and a certain time. There is definitely an argument for spell duration not being affected except when the spell is cast within a Temporal Pocket (or similar). <br /> <br /> Either way, you get some funky effects. Either you can Temporal Pocket as a way to end any spell which isn't indefinite in duration - and indefinite spells which are unsafely relinquished. Or you get more time under the effect of a limited duration spell by casting a Temporal Pocket on the spell plus the subject of the spell.<br /> <br /> Either the spell duration counts down time in the Temporal Pocket or it waits until relative time outside the pocket has passed and has extra duration for being in the pocket.<br /> <br /> I suppose having Masters of Time able to end spells like this isn't particularly game breaking.... But Veil of Moments is different i think. RAW the subject is protected only from things which worsen with time. Not instant effects (like taking damage from a lethal attack). Which i think would include the Spell's duration ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T11:55:49-08:00","id":1473416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Time works, you could use the growth angle to justify Life as well. Kinda like how movement falls under Forces, Space, and Time. </div> </div> </div>Interesting, Life has growth mentioned in the Lexicon, but not under it purview on p.148 (are there other discrepancies?) <br /> <br /> Are you suggesting a Making growth within the Spell's pattern?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T12:05:11-08:00","id":1473417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473416#post1473416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, Life has growth mentioned in the Lexicon, but not under it purview on p.148 (are there other discrepancies?)<br /> <br /> Are you suggesting a Making growth within the Spell's pattern?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m suggesting that a legacy treating spells as alive and growing things is the perfect place to make that sentiment very literal. ie, the spells can be alive if you want them to be. The practice to just do that is Weaving.<br /> Edit: I suppose Spirit could work too.<br /> Edit 2: Metamorphosis isn\u2019t growth? Anyways, growth is just part of Life, same as healing as healing is just regrowth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-27-2022, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T12:33:11-08:00","id":1473418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473415#post1473415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think duration of a spell is a time effect. I think it is a conditional effect. The spell doesn't age, it simply is over a certain area/subject(s) and a certain time. There is definitely an argument for spell duration not being affected except when the spell is cast within a Temporal Pocket (or similar).</div> </div> </div> </div> If the condition is Time, then Time can mess with it. It\u2019s the same thing as Space messing with aoe spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473415#post1473415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose having Masters of Time able to end spells like this isn't particularly game breaking.... But Veil of Moments is different i think. RAW the subject is protected only from things which worsen with time. Not instant effects (like taking damage from a lethal attack). Which i think would include the Spell's duration ending.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe. Time isn\u2019t my best arcanum either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T12:56:10-08:00","id":1473421,"title":"","content":"I think its worth pointing out that using Time instead of Death has a downside. Basing the approach on Temporal Pocket means that everything the spell would do will happen. So lets say a Gnosis 5 master used a lethal damage spell that lasts a day. That means [Arcana] damage will be inflicted at [Ritual casting time]. So for one day it would be, with a 30 minute ritual time, 48 intervals * Potency 5 = 240 damage taken in one go. Unless you can Make the interval and Unmake the consequences of the spell activating, so the question is if it can be done.<br /> <br /> With Time 4 you could theoretically protect them from negative change, as per the Arcanum's purview. In such a case, a Clash of Wills might be required sometime or maybe for the spell to beat the Potency of the Time effect. Incorporating elements of that idea into this spell might be doable. Following that train of thought, I hypothesize that a Making of Time used for dispellation purposes would need to match or beat the duration of the spell (which might be very difficult for indefinite effects).<br /> <br /> <b>Observation:</b> The fact all that damage can be inflicted at once is why a high Potency <i>Blink of an Eye</i> with the +2 Reach effect (making Ritual intervals into a minute or less) is one of the most horrifyingly powerful sources of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-27-2022, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T14:45:20-08:00","id":1473427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> match or beat the duration of the spell (which might be very difficult for indefinite effects). </div> </div> </div>That had occured to me. There is this odd issue where the Master of Time gets to use an indefinite duration spell, but after one round it does not count against spell control, because it has either ended or never will, whatever was the subject of the spell is now permanently in that temporal Pocket.<br /> <br /> Notably if it is a person and they can 'not physically move, consume, or injure anything \u2014 any at-<br /> tempt to do so immediately ends the spell, but returns the subject to the timeline having just completed the action he attempted.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I presume for a spell trapped in a Temporal Pocket (without it's subject) it will do nothing until ritual time has elapsed and then trigger its effect, exiting the Pocket.<br /> <br /> If the spell has a continuous effect it may not ever break free from the pocket, even if indefinite... It may be considered to be out of spell control (unless the caster is also in the Temporal Pocket) and i could imagine it growing wild... But i think indefinite duration spells trapped for an indefinite duration inside a Temporal Pocket just blink out of existence.<br /> <br /> I think some of this logic transfers well over to Space and manipulating the scale of an AoE spell (like casting Secret Room at advanced scale to shrink a large warehouse down two steps. Then cast you intended spell on the smaller area, slow the Secret Room to lapse, and then possibly recast it to grow the area two steps.<br /> <br /> You now have a city block sized area affected by a spell cast at the smallest advanced scale.<br /> <br /> But better is if you cast an area of effect on the largest scale, and then grow the area inside, and nobody can dispell the large area of effect because it is bigger than largest scale factor (without first dispelling the Secret room(s) which is making it bigger).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T18:49:10-08:00","id":1473437,"title":"","content":"So, while browsing the forum for poison spells, I came across a old post saying Platonic Form can be used to make cyanide and other poisons. I actually wasn\u2019t aware Platonic Forms carried any material properties besides shape and form. Is this a valid use of the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T19:14:40-08:00","id":1473438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473437#post1473437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, while browsing the forum for poison spells, I came across a old post saying Platonic Form can be used to make cyanide and other poisons. I actually wasn\u2019t aware Platonic Forms carried any material properties besides shape and form. Is this a valid use of the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say its possible to make a platonic drug that makes the subject Addicted to the mage and their Nimbus, but otherwise it seems outside its purview. Platonic Forms are mana that was shaped into the forms it takes while inhabiting tass, so their properties should be the same as those that tass may have.<br /> <br /> In addition, the spell Phantasm from page 227 of the 1ed book, from which Platonic Form appears to be based, states: &quot;These objects do not and cannot possess qualities such as conductivity, magnetism or the like. Phantasmal wood does not float in water and it does not fuel a fire (though it can still be destroyed by such, it does not sustain the flame on its own)&quot;. So it appears that the intent is for them to be discartable tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T19:24:30-08:00","id":1473440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473437#post1473437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, while browsing the forum for poison spells, I came across a old post saying Platonic Form can be used to make cyanide and other poisons. I actually wasn\u2019t aware Platonic Forms carried any material properties besides shape and form. Is this a valid use of the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>If solely using Prime magic, I\u2019d rather make a spell that changes properties of Tass so that it becomes poisonous, or add a Reach option to Create Truth so that the created Hallow has a Feature (<b>Signs of Sorcery</b>) where it generates poisons that happen to be Tass\u2026 Doubtful of using Platonic Form and/or Eidolon, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T19:52:11-08:00","id":1473443,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473438#post1473438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say its possible to make a platonic drug that makes the subject Addicted to the mage and their Nimbus, but otherwise it seems outside its purview. Platonic Forms are mana that was shaped into the forms it takes while inhabiting tass, so their properties should be the same as those that tass may have.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, it may not be lethal, but this is so much better than lethal for a social legacy. Prime/Matter was so the right combo for the legacy. While we are on the topic of mind bending poisons, I\u2019ve heard of certain chemicals that have used to keep people\u2026pliable and open to manipulation. Like the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_wXcqC6vwvM\" target=\"_blank\">zombie</a>. Think it\u2019s possible to combine Prime and Matter to add the effects of certain poisons on a victim who have been addicted in this way?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473440#post1473440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If solely using Prime magic, I\u2019d rather make a spell that changes properties of Tass so that it becomes poisonous, or add a Reach option to Create Truth so that the created Hallow has a Feature (<b>Signs of Sorcery</b>) where it generates poisons that happen to be Tass\u2026 Doubtful of using Platonic Form and/or Eidolon, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, do you think it\u2019s Weaving to invest one point of mana into a thing in order to make it Tass, with a reach to add one of the properties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T20:05:35-08:00","id":1473444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473443#post1473443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it may not be lethal, but this is so much better than lethal for a social legacy. Prime/Matter was so the right combo for the legacy. While we are on the topic of mind bending poisons, I\u2019ve heard of certain chemicals that have used to keep people\u2026pliable and open to manipulation. Like the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_wXcqC6vwvM\" target=\"_blank\">zombie</a>. Think it\u2019s possible to combine Prime and Matter to add the effects of certain poisons on a victim who have been addicted in this way?<br /> <br /> So, do you think it\u2019s Weaving to invest one point of mana into a thing in order to make it Tass, with a reach to add one of the properties?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have you considered using a Weaving of Prime and Matter to make actual poisonous words ? Make the truth poisonous to a subject, in such a way that they lie to themselves and others simply to get respite from the thing that affects them with a Toxicity of [Potency]. Now only you know when they speak the truth and what they mean. They will self destruct as they become known as pathological liars, if they do not start to believe the lies themselves. The mage will be the only confidant that reliably understands their situation, which places them in a position of trust where the final &quot;accident&quot; can be setup. Sounds like something the Seers would try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T20:29:53-08:00","id":1473445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473444#post1473444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered using a Weaving of Prime and Matter to make actual poisonous words ? Make the truth poisonous to a subject, in such a way that they lie to themselves and others simply to get respite from the thing that affects them with a Toxicity of [Potency]. Now only you know when they speak the truth and what they mean. They will self destruct as they become known as pathological liars, if they do not start to believe the lies themselves. The mage will be the only confidant that reliably understands their situation, which places them in a position of trust where the final &quot;accident&quot; can be setup. Sounds like something the Seers would try.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had mostly been focusing on actual lies and poisons...but this is a fun idea! It is nicely subtle, just like what this legacy wants in it's attainments. Probably one of the higher attainments, which I'm short of. Going to use it if I ever actually write this legacy down. I actually had planned on them being a rather annoyingly survivable nameless order that works with pretty much everyone (yes, even the Lower Depths, and individual Scelesti), with members only being truly loyal to the order...hypothetically anyways. They are probably more of a mess than the Seers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-27-2022, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T20:38:57-08:00","id":1473446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473444#post1473444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered using a Weaving of Prime and Matter to make actual poisonous words ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how that works. There is no reason for Matter to be involved in this spell unless you are actually turning something into physical poison, and historically that's entailed using actual material phenomena as the raw material, not Truth.<br /> <br /> Setting negative consequences for a particular circumstance or course of action is a Fate trick, possibly with a side of Time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T21:13:50-08:00","id":1473447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473443#post1473443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, do you think it\u2019s Weaving to invest one point of mana into a thing in order to make it Tass, with a reach to add one of the properties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I was thinking of using Prime Weaving to make already-existing Tass poisonous, and adding a Reach option to the official Create Truth (Prime Making) spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T21:26:21-08:00","id":1473449,"title":"","content":"While that\u2019s certainly one way to do things, I was wondering how one could produce Tass without a Hallow needing to be involved. Since it\u2019s like a weird offshoot of Channel Mana and Mana Battery, I figured it would be Weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T22:18:38-08:00","id":1473451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473449#post1473449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that\u2019s certainly one way to do things, I was wondering how one could produce Tass without a Hallow needing to be involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble here being that the closest published equivalent to the 1e Create Tass spell in 2e is Platonic Form. Tass is otherwise formed based on the environment around a Hallow; Hallows are consistently part of the described process of tass formation outside of mimicking the property of &quot;putting Mana into material form&quot; through Platonic Form and Eidolon, and there's even some bits of text that suggest loose Mana <i>goes to Hallows</i> to become tass.<br /> <br /> Platonic Form doesn't give its creations Resonance keywords or other special properties and can't create things that are edible in more than the physical-mechanical sense (and I'm doubtful that it can manage potability, either). This is one of those things where the semantic purviews of the Arcana don't fully extend to their actual capabilities so that the setting can remain coherent and resource scarcity can drive character motivations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T06:15:46-08:00","id":1473460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473440#post1473440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If solely using Prime magic, I\u2019d rather make a spell that changes properties of Tass so that it becomes poisonous, or add a Reach option to Create Truth so that the created Hallow has a Feature (<b>Signs of Sorcery</b>) where it generates poisons that happen to be Tass\u2026 Doubtful of using Platonic Form and/or Eidolon, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how the Signs of Sorcery Features work, but could you feed poisonous resonance to the Hallow and expect the tass to be imbued with that? Or is this essentially a more direct result of the same effect? (Maybe tapping a leyline associated with toxic effulent from an industrial plant... Not poison, but still going to hurt anyone who consumed it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T06:36:52-08:00","id":1473461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473460#post1473460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure how the Signs of Sorcery Features work, but could you feed poisonous resonance to the Hallow and expect the tass to be imbued with that? Or is this essentially a more direct result of the same effect? (Maybe tapping a leyline associated with toxic effulent from an industrial plant... Not poison, but still going to hurt anyone who consumed it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hallow Features described in SoS seem to assume that a Hollow will be naturally found with such features; it doesn\u2019t mention at all the idea of any mage \u2018hacking\u2019 such features into a Hallow. Which is why I went with the \u2018just create a new one from scratch\u2019 spell idea.<br /> <br /> AFAIK, you can manipulate ley lines/Resonances to imbue ley lines/Nodes with a Resonance of \u2018Poisonous,\u2019 and if that Node is placed on a Hallow, that Hallow\u2019s Mana will indeed gain the Poisonous Resonance\u2026 but this won\u2019t exactly be the same thing as making toxic Tass. You\u2019d just get Mana that\u2019s Resonant with Poison, that you could use as a Yantra for casting poison magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T07:20:29-08:00","id":1473462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by TempleBuilder View Post<br /> Can Space unlock most irises without a key? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1446872#post1446872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> I think only if it traverses space within the same realm. I can't really buy Space opening an Avernian Gate or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason i thought this required Fate, not Space. But i can't find it anywhere.<br /> <br /> The closest is Fate 2 Veiling &quot;Fabricate Fortune&quot; allows you to trick conditional durations or triggers, i somehow associated this with triggering keyed Irises aswell. <br /> <br /> Is this how anyone else plays Fate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-28-2022, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T07:34:03-08:00","id":1473464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473461#post1473461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hallow Features described in SoS seem to assume that a Hollow will be naturally found with such features; it doesn\u2019t mention at all the idea of any mage \u2018hacking\u2019 such features into a Hallow. Which is why I went with the \u2018just create a new one from scratch\u2019 spell idea.<br /> <br /> AFAIK, you can manipulate ley lines/Resonances to imbue ley lines/Nodes with a Resonance of \u2018Poisonous,\u2019 and if that Node is placed on a Hallow, that Hallow\u2019s Mana will indeed gain the Poisonous Resonance\u2026 but this won\u2019t exactly be the same thing as making toxic Tass. You\u2019d just get Mana that\u2019s Resonant with Poison, that you could use as a Yantra for casting poison magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that the precise form Tass takes depends on the resonance of the Hallow. But RAW this is neither necessary nor sufficient. <br /> <br /> The tass depends on the Hallow's physical and symbolic characteristics.<br /> <br /> Which are things you can change mundanely (or magically, like the spell you described). Locating a Hallow in waste disposal area of an industrial chemical plant for example (either building a plant on top of a known Hallow or creating a Hallow in an existing plant...).<br /> <br /> Resonance likely draws spirits, and they can create/influence things, but resonant mana is different from poisonous tass. <br /> <br /> Edit:What are the benefits/drawbacks of resonant mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-28-2022, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T08:38:59-08:00","id":1473467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473464#post1473464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would assume that the precise form Tass takes depends on the resonance of the Hallow. But RAW this is neither necessary nor sufficient.<br /> <br /> The tass depends on the Hallow's physical and symbolic characteristics.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, and it can get weird. One example in SoS is little homunculi that you have to catch, cook, and eat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473464#post1473464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resonance likely draws spirits, and they can create/influence things, but resonant mana is different from poisonous tass.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. Resonance is \u201cmerely\u201d the supernatural and symbolic impressions a action or thing leaves on the world. On it\u2019s own it\u2019s about as effective as wall paint at effecting things. Poison resonating Tass merely has the symbolism of the bit of Mana directed towards poison. Poisonous Tass by contrast can have any resonance, but either addicts you to harvesting it, or gives you a curse. The only real guidelines for the curse option are to be weird curses and not lots of aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473464#post1473464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit:What are the benefits/drawbacks of resonant mana?</div> </div> </div> </div> Having a +1 yantra for spells relating to the resonance in your mana pool, and having something spirits like to hang around. It\u2019s not the most impressive thing, but it\u2019s extremely common since Ley Lines that feed into Hallows bestow their resonance, and most Hallows have attached Ley Lines as I recall.<br /> <br /> Edit: note, when I say wall paint, I don\u2019t mean in a sarcastic way, since aesthetics have a very impact to people choosing and using a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-28-2022, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T08:55:36-08:00","id":1473469,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Signs of Sorcery <i>does</i> have an offhand reference to the idea that mages can channel mana to create their own tass. I'd assume such a thing is three dots, but then that would be the same level as the Mana Battery spell...<br /> <br /> I guess they'd still be distinguished by the fact that the latter doesn't actually cost any Mana, it just makes an object that functions as a store for it... also, you don't need to use the Channel Mana spell to extract any of its Mana, just need to be a mage or Proximus and touch it, so that puts it one over Tass. Although I don't know, it still seems to come out generally superior to converting Mana into tass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473451#post1473451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of those things where the semantic purviews of the Arcana don't fully extend to their actual capabilities so that the setting can remain coherent and resource scarcity can drive character motivations.</div> </div> </div> </div>But <i>would</i> it reduce the scarcity of tass? If it still requires the mage to provide their own Mana to its substance? There would still need to be an origin point to the Mana, you just externalize it from yourself as a reserve. Plus, if you don't have Prime as Ruling and make it indefinite, it's costing some Mana that doesn't get saved (although I'd have a notion to give such a spell a Reach option to be Lasting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T09:18:17-08:00","id":1473472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473469#post1473469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess they'd still be distinguished by the fact that the latter doesn't actually cost any Mana, it just makes an object that functions as a store for it... also, you don't need to use the Channel Mana spell to extract any of its Mana, just need to be a mage or Proximus and touch it, so that puts it one over Tass. Although I don't know, it still seems to come out generally superior to converting Mana into tass.</div> </div> </div> </div> In this one case, creating tass is necessary, because I want to make use of one of the cursed tass options, which I doubt carries over to Mana Batteries, at least without some impressive amounts of reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T12:21:36-08:00","id":1473488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473472#post1473472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In this one case, creating tass is necessary, because I want to make use of one of the cursed tass options, which I doubt carries over to Mana Batteries, at least without some impressive amounts of reach.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I remember correctly, the Banishers book presented two options. One was to taint mana so that it would be &quot;sluggish&quot;, it was unable to be used for Pattern Restoration and, so long as at least one point of tainted mana remained in their Pattern, the mage unable to use more than one mana per turn. Another spell created poisonous mana, which would inflict a point of lethal damage once it was spent by the mage. Perhaps those could work as a basis for an updated spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T13:01:52-08:00","id":1473494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473488#post1473488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, the Banishers book presented two options. One was to taint mana so that it would be &quot;sluggish&quot;, it was unable to be used for Pattern Restoration and, so long as at least one point of tainted mana remained in their Pattern, the mage unable to use more than one mana per turn. Another spell created poisonous mana, which would inflict a point of lethal damage once it was spent by the mage. Perhaps those could work as a basis for an updated spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fun. I\u2019ll see if I can make that and add the SoS options alongside\u2026but I don\u2019t have Banishers. Was there anything special about how they accomplished making this tainted Mana in the description of the spell?<br /> Edit: unless you planned on making the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T14:16:46-08:00","id":1473500,"title":"","content":"There doesn't seem to be anything in particular with the metaphysics. For both spells, the amount of mana affected is equal to rolled successes (which translates to Potency in 2ed). In the Poisoned Mana one, it says that with Prime 5 it can do aggravated damage, which can be translated to it requiring a Reach and a mana in 2ed.<br /> <br /> Currently I am focusing on breaking down some of the abilities Regulus Corneas has in Re: Zero, there is a lot of fascinating and useful stuff (the series overall is fantastic), so it would take a while before I would get to the poisoned mana ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T02:46:19-08:00","id":1473518,"title":"","content":"So &quot;darkness&quot; and &quot;cold&quot; are under the purview of Death. Usually this is portrayed as more mystical and abstract than the more accurate-to-Fallen-science Forces. But what actually happens when you Fray/Pattern/Unravel/Unmake darkness or cold? What happens when I Pattern the darkness of a lightless room into cold? Will the room be extremely cold but lit up (or rather &quot;undarkened&quot;) without a visible source of light? What happens when I Unmake the cold of a room? Does the temperature jump to a theoretical maximum and immediately incinerate the room and everything in it like a sun just popped up in it? Or are we to assume that coldness and darkness are infinite wells (and thus Death Patterning could basically always Pattern something Death-related out of the environment, as some reservoir of darkness or cold would be just about everywhere)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T08:05:35-08:00","id":1473524,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473518#post1473518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So &quot;darkness&quot; and &quot;cold&quot; are under the purview of Death. Usually this is portrayed as more mystical and abstract than the more accurate-to-Fallen-science Forces. But what actually happens when you Fray/Pattern/Unravel/Unmake darkness or cold?</div> </div> </div> </div> It would tends toward to a median than people would call average. Cold would become warmer (but never warm), and Darkness would become brighter (but never bright). This is the same as how Death works with in general with stuff only technically in it\u2019s purview thanks to decay, like when healing or restoring a memory, it can bring the thing back up to normal, but it can\u2019t make it better or higher than normal.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473518#post1473518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when I Pattern the darkness of a lightless room into cold? Will the room be extremely cold but lit up (or rather &quot;undarkened&quot;) without a visible source of light?</div> </div> </div> </div> I would say it\u2019s just enough to see by, not enough for anyone to say it was bright. Twilight, or Gloom might be appropriate words. And yes, it would be very cold. You can probably reuse the Forces chart to figure out just how cold it can get.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473518#post1473518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when I Unmake the cold of a room? Does the temperature jump to a theoretical maximum and immediately incinerate the room and everything in it like a sun just popped up in it?</div> </div> </div> </div> No. it just becomes \u201cnot cold\u201d. Death doesn\u2019t have the ability to create heat. The room would be lukewarm, neither hot nor cold.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473518#post1473518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or are we to assume that coldness and darkness are infinite wells (and thus Death Patterning could basically always Pattern something Death-related out of the environment, as some reservoir of darkness or cold would be just about everywhere)?</div> </div> </div> </div> Whatever works for you. Normally, we can find a scenario in which one arcanum doesn\u2019t have much that it can use. Generally speaking, you will always have your shadow, meaning you will have something to work with, but it might not be very much if you are in a super bright and hot room. Remember, the amount of shadow is proportional to the amount of stuff you can get when you work with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-29-2022, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T12:10:54-08:00","id":1473539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473518#post1473518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So &quot;darkness&quot; and &quot;cold&quot; are under the purview of Death. Usually this is portrayed as more mystical and abstract than the more accurate-to-Fallen-science Forces. But what actually happens when you Fray/Pattern/Unravel/Unmake darkness or cold?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26736_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26736\" data-vbnamecard=\"26736\">TempleBuilder</a> said.<br /> <br /> Treat cold and darkness as if there we're positive real substances, metaphysically that is what Death is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T17:20:02-08:00","id":1473612,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Dispel Magic. In the description of the spell, it states:<br /> <br /> 'In addition, the mage must include all Arcana involved<br /> in the casting of the subject spell at one dot.'<br /> <br /> Does this mean that the caster of Dispel Magic needs to have a dot in the Arcana of the spell they are trying to dispel?<br /> <br /> Thanks<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26970-blu44","name":"Blu44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T17:26:11-08:00","id":1473613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blu44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473612#post1473612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Dispel Magic. In the description of the spell, it states:<br /> <br /> 'In addition, the mage must include all Arcana involved<br /> in the casting of the subject spell at one dot.'<br /> <br /> Does this mean that the caster of Dispel Magic needs to have a dot in the Arcana of the spell they are trying to dispel?<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly seems so. You\u2019d need Supernal Dispellation (Prime 4) to use solely Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T14:53:46-08:00","id":1473699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473613#post1473613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Certainly seems so. You\u2019d need Supernal Dispellation (Prime 4) to use solely Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than that, you need to know what Arcana they are using (maybe you can guess?). You are taking advantage of your own knowledge of the Arcana being cast to pull apart the spell as it is being cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T17:19:11-08:00","id":1473707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473699#post1473699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More than that, you need to know what Arcana they are using (maybe you can guess?). You are taking advantage of your own knowledge of the Arcana being cast to pull apart the spell as it is being cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dispellation and Counterspell are separate things and Counterspell requires you to have Active Mage Sight of the appropriate Arcanum to counter the spell. For Dispellation you can just Reveal the spell with any Focused Mage Sight to identify the Arcana it uses per the notes in Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T17:37:44-08:00","id":1473709,"title":"","content":"What happens when the Mind of a subject is outside of the body (like with Psychic Projection or Possession), and the body dies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T17:47:23-08:00","id":1473710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473709#post1473709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when the Mind of a subject is outside of the body (like with Psychic Projection or Possession), and the body dies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing official IIRC. I\u2019d say the norm is that it just dies, likely right after the spell ends.<br /> <br /> \u2026 So obviously, a Mystery could form around exceptions where the minds become wandering ghost-Goetia hybrid thingies or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T17:58:54-08:00","id":1473712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473710#post1473710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing official IIRC. I\u2019d say the norm is that it just dies, likely right after the spell ends.<br /> <br /> \u2026 So obviously, a Mystery could form around exceptions where the minds become wandering ghost-Goetia hybrid thingies or something.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m fairly sure of the answer, but the soul disappears when the body dies, right? How does that affect our hypothetical Mind only creature? Especially Mages? Do they experience the effects of soul loss, and the extra rote paradox on spells?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T19:08:25-08:00","id":1473716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473712#post1473712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I\u2019m fairly sure of the answer, but the soul disappears when the body dies, right? How does that affect our hypothetical Mind only creature? Especially Mages? Do they experience the effects of soul loss, and the extra rote paradox on spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the leftover creature is a Lich, we probably won\u2019t have to worry about them.<br /> <br /> If it <i>is</i>!a Lich\u2026 hmm, I don\u2019t think we have 2E rules yet for \u2018proper\u2019 Ghost Liches etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T19:54:33-08:00","id":1473717,"title":"","content":"Well, now I want to see a ghost-spirit-goetia hybrid. Surely some 3rd Degree Master out there was feeling abominable. <br /> <br /> Unrelated, how difficult would it be to pull off a &quot;rod of god&quot; strike using Co-Location or a Forces spell? You'd need a big enough tungsten rod to work with, but I could see using Contol Gravity to put the thing in orbit with Conditional Duration set to expire once it's on-target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T20:21:57-08:00","id":1473718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473717#post1473717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now I want to see a ghost-spirit-goetia hybrid. Surely some 3rd Degree Master out there was feeling abominable.<br /> <br /> Unrelated, how difficult would it be to pull off a &quot;rod of god&quot; strike using Co-Location or a Forces spell? You'd need a big enough tungsten rod to work with, but I could see using Contol Gravity to put the thing in orbit with Conditional Duration set to expire once it's on-target.</div> </div> </div> </div> That where you get a satellite into orbit, and just drop a heavy and durable rod from it, right? You just time it so it falls where you want it to? Some basic orbital dynamics, calculus, money, and Control Gravity is all you need. Not hard at all, a starter character could do it. You don\u2019t need Conditional duration if you do the Math, and keep a timer. I\u2019m also fairly sure you can just set up the duration to end after a specific time has past so a timer is irrelevant. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T20:37:19-08:00","id":1473719,"title":"","content":"Orbital mechanics: for when you absolutely must vaporize the local Seer nexus from a distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T20:37:43-08:00","id":1473720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473716#post1473716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it <i>is</i>!a Lich\u2026 hmm, I don\u2019t think we have 2E rules yet for \u2018proper\u2019 Ghost Liches etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e Core describes them as retaining their ability to use magic with reference to the systems for Supernal beings. We don't know how to determine their Ranks besides back-converting from their highest Arcana, but &quot;give a ghost/spirit/goetia Arcana and let it cast like a Supernal being&quot; seems intuitive enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473717#post1473717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now I want to see a ghost-spirit-goetia hybrid. Surely some 3rd Degree Master out there was feeling abominable.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those things where you're going to have to step outside of the abstraction and think practically, because otherwise you just end up with a goetia manifested through spiritual ephemera and slathered in ectoplasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T20:42:25-08:00","id":1473721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473720#post1473720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of those things where you're going to have to step outside of the abstraction and think practically, because otherwise you just end up with a goetia manifested through spiritual ephemera and slathered in ectoplasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geists are effectively spirit-ghost magaths, aren't they? Even if not, I could see a creature able to hop between Twilight frequencies becoming a very dangerous predator","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T20:52:13-08:00","id":1473722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473720#post1473720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e Core describes them as retaining their ability to use magic with reference to the systems for Supernal beings. We don't know how to determine their Ranks besides back-converting from their highest Arcana, but &quot;give a ghost/spirit/goetia Arcana and let it cast like a Supernal being&quot; seems intuitive enough.</div> </div> </div> </div> While very intuitive, a Master taking this route to Lichdom will become very scary due to the power boost of using Power + Finesse instead of Gnosis + Arcana.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T20:56:19-08:00","id":1473723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473721#post1473721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Geists are effectively spirit-ghost magaths, aren't they? Even if not, I could see a creature able to hop between Twilight frequencies becoming a very dangerous predator</div> </div> </div> </div> Nah, pure ghost. Granted the Geist has become more chthonic than it once was, and has left some of it\u2019s humanity behind, but that doesn\u2019t make it any more spirit.<br /> Edit: as for Twilight hopping\u2026I guess you could end up with a creature that does that, but I think it more likely that you end up with it in all of them at once. Which is useful in it\u2019s own way, since it can probably use Irises to the Shadow, Astral, and Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-31-2022, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T21:49:06-08:00","id":1473726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473721#post1473721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geists are effectively spirit-ghost magaths, aren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're ghosts who functionally treat a type of deathly Resonance as a much less limited form of Anchor, which, combined with their immunity to Essence bleed, allows them much more mobility than most ghosts, but they only interact with spirits insofar as they have anything to do with death. Ostracism from the choirs for being an abomination and ostracism by other ghosts for being a terrifying and incomprehensible specter are separate types of solitary, and the former doesn't enter into ghostly existence.<br /> <br /> You could certainly try some sort of long-term project to make something that inhabits an interstitial frequency of Twilight between Shadow ephemera and Astral ideaform, but established lore alone is just going to get you ways to give spirit qualities to ghosts or ghost qualities to goetia rather than declare that this thing is three wildly different things at the same time without thinking about what that means \u2014 remember that forming an Imago entails coming up with a mental representation of the spell's end result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T21:49:27-08:00","id":1473727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473723#post1473723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nah, pure ghost. Granted the Geist has become more chthonic than it once was, and has left some of it\u2019s humanity behind, but that doesn\u2019t make it any more spirit.<br /> Edit: as for Twilight hopping\u2026I guess you could end up with a creature that does that, but I think it more likely that you end up with it in all of them at once. Which is useful in it\u2019s own way, since it can probably use Irises to the Shadow, Astral, and Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>My headcanon is now that it would be a demon from the Bartimaeus Trilogy; interacting with reality on multiple planes of existence simultaneously, and being really damn snarky while doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-01-2022, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T22:11:24-08:00","id":1473729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473726#post1473726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're ghosts who functionally treat a type of deathly Resonance as a much less limited form of Anchor, which, combined with their immunity to Essence bleed, allows them much more mobility than most ghosts, but they only interact with spirits insofar as they have anything to do with death. Ostracism from the choirs for being an abomination and ostracism by other ghosts for being a terrifying and incomprehensible specter are separate types of solitary, and the former doesn't enter into ghostly existence.<br /> <br /> You could certainly try some sort of long-term project to make something that inhabits an interstitial frequency of Twilight between Shadow ephemera and Astral ideaform, but established lore alone is just going to get you ways to give spirit qualities to ghosts or ghost qualities to goetia rather than declare that this thing is three wildly different things at the same time without thinking about what that means \u2014 remember that forming an Imago entails coming up with a mental representation of the spell's end result.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd see it as a mad (possibly Rapt?) Free Councilor's interpretation of a &quot;4th dimensional being&quot;. Or, possibly, a sentient Verge. <br /> <br /> My personal envisioning of the imago is of a twisted mass of inchoate matter, like the depictions of something from the Far Realms in DnD. Something so aberrent and warped that it feels wrong just looking at it. Not in the unclean, thing-that-must-not-exist way of an acamoth, just the slighly less horrifying feeling of The Flood. <br /> <br /> Or, on the opposite side of the spectrum, a black hole-esque &quot;gravity&quot; that twists and compresses Twilight frequencies around it into a single contiguous plane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T22:21:17-08:00","id":1473730,"title":"","content":"\u2026aren\u2019t humans 4th dimensional beings? We have length, width, height, and duration. We just can only see 3 dimensions. Sorry, minor nitpick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T22:25:32-08:00","id":1473732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473730#post1473730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026isn\u2019t humanity 4th dimensional beings? We have length, width, height, and duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you are academically correct, I was more thinking of the scifi &quot;alien geometries&quot; or &quot;additional spacial dimensions&quot; tropes. Things that are to us as we are to a 2D drawing, that sort of thing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T22:36:38-08:00","id":1473733,"title":"","content":"Tangentially related Spirit question: does the spirit of an object have sympathy to said object for the purposes of Space magic? I assume yes, and can envision some interesting uses in the hands of a Space-Thrysus or Spirit-Mastigos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T22:39:20-08:00","id":1473734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473733#post1473733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially related Spirit question: does the spirit of an object have sympathy to said object for the purposes of Space magic? I assume yes, and can envision some interesting uses in the hands of a Space-Thrysus or Spirit-Mastigos</div> </div> </div> </div>Connected sympathy, probably. They do have a mystical bond, after all. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T00:47:13-08:00","id":1473737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473716#post1473716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the leftover creature is a Lich, we probably won\u2019t have to worry about them.<br /> <br /> If it <i>is</i>!a Lich\u2026 hmm, I don\u2019t think we have 2E rules yet for \u2018proper\u2019 Ghost Liches etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure the leftover creature doesn't become a Lich, unless perhaps they attempted a ritual casting where they used their own body as a sacrament... At which point Lichdom may be a possible result.<br /> <br /> Warning: do not try this at home.<br /> <br /> There is a fallen magic ritual* in Immortals (1e) for turning into a spirit being - with a immortal body which reforms when killed like a spirit reforming their corpus.<br /> <br /> But i imagine they have no soul (as spirits don't have souls) so a mage doing that likely result in losing their Gnosis/Arcana. A modified ritual may work...<br /> <br /> *If the ritual fails it become an elaborate form of suicide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T05:49:30-08:00","id":1473747,"title":"","content":"My understanding of how orbit works would mean that taking away the spell keeping the subject from falling just means that it will fall in a circle around the Earth. It would need a different kind of force to act upon it to set it back to the Earth's surface.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I would understand that the main point of a kinetic orbital strike is that you need that distance and starting off in the frictionless environment for the object to build sufficient velocity, and at the level of Forces magic that would be required to do so in the first place, going from orbit is a tad unnecessary. A simple Perfecting spell will double an object's velocity for every level of Potency, so start off with something fast enough and add enough dice to a pool dedicated to just one factor...<br /> <br /> Like, start with an object that can accelerate on its own to 50mph, and at Potency 10 it will be speeding at... 51,200mph.<br /> <br /> And that spell still says that velocity affects damage from collisions, so...<br /> <br /> Of course, at that point (and several steps before it), you're basically performing drone strikes in crowded neighbourhoods, so there's a concern from Wisdom drops and being reprimanded by other mages; I think Guardians of the Veil would very sternly suggest that there were more precise ways you might have tried to disrupt a Seer base.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473737#post1473737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a fallen magic ritual* in Immortals (1e) for turning into a spirit being - with a immortal body which reforms when killed like a spirit reforming their corpus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, given the way the core book sidebar on Weird Stuff references Immortals, I think they're in much the same boat as Supernatural Merits, incompatible with the state of being Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T08:11:18-08:00","id":1473754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473747#post1473747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of how orbit works would mean that taking away the spell keeping the subject from falling just means that it will fall in a circle around the Earth. It would need a different kind of force to act upon it to set it back to the Earth's surface.</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe you will find that the rod never actually achieves orbit as that would require a distance past the orbit of the moon to accomplish if Control Gravity is straight up. Even if it isn\u2019t, it will be a long time falling sideways before it achieves the velocity necessary to say in orbit. But once it is in orbit, you would be correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473747#post1473747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I would understand that the main point of a kinetic orbital strike is that you need that distance and starting off in the frictionless environment for the object to build sufficient velocity, and at the level of Forces magic that would be required to do so in the first place, going from orbit is a tad unnecessary. A simple Perfecting spell will double an object's velocity for every level of Potency, so start off with something fast enough and add enough dice to a pool dedicated to just one factor...<br /> <br /> Like, start with an object that can accelerate on its own to 50mph, and at Potency 10 it will be speeding at... 51,200mph.<br /> <br /> And that spell still says that velocity affects damage from collisions, so...<br /> <br /> Of course, at that point (and several steps before it), you're basically performing drone strikes in crowded neighbourhoods, so there's a concern from Wisdom drops and being reprimanded by other mages; I think Guardians of the Veil would very sternly suggest that there were more precise ways you might have tried to disrupt a Seer base.</div> </div> </div> </div> Technically, all you need is Apprentice to get the necessary height, but yes, you can get those speeds from simply perfecting the velocity. Of course you can also get way higher velocity than the either two methods by combining both. Requires only Forces 3, Arcana wise, but here is where Fate and Space help. As for Wisdom, I\u2019m having trouble thinking of something more hubristic. It\u2019s flashy, unsubtle, hard to control, and it will have enormous collateral damage, most likely including civilians, and is easily countered by simply not being in the office that day. Only way it could be worse is if it wasn\u2019t planned in advance, or done out of rage. Oh, and the Seers would absolutely retaliate in kind, probably worse even. Yeah, I can see everyone besides the Free Council facepalming at the use use of this tactic. And the Free Council is probably torn about the issue, depending on how zealously a particular voter feels about destroying followers of the lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T11:27:12-08:00","id":1473761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473747#post1473747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of how orbit works would mean that taking away the spell keeping the subject from falling just means that it will fall in a circle around the Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if it has sufficient horizontal velocity. <br /> <br /> If it just goes up (from antigravity) then it will come straight down... But it will be hard to predict exactly where it will hit, because the earth is spining underneath it, wind may even be a problem, and it isn't going as fast as an orbiting object/meteor so I'm not convinced it will burn up. Plus air resistance will slow it down, losing a lot of the energy it does have... Unless it is incredibly dense i suppose.<br /> <br /> EDIT: won't this also provoke preemptive action from Seers as their prophecies sees a terrible destruction rein down upon them?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, given the way the core book sidebar on Weird Stuff references Immortals, I think they're in much the same boat as Supernatural Merits, incompatible with the state of being Awakened. </div> </div> </div>Yes, i would assume that this method transforms your soul into a spirit, so when your body dies instead of a soul which dissapeares, your spirit hibernates and act just like a spirit (albiet one with a naturally occurring physical body, rather than ephemeral corpus... ). I think you become not human in the sense that immortals of this type shouldn't contribute to the Temenos. <br /> <br /> I am presuming that Awakened Liches don't use this kind of Fallen Sorcery, and have better methods of retaining their Gnosis. But this presents a baseline of what is possible (if you are willing to give up being human).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-01-2022, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T12:07:59-08:00","id":1473766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473761#post1473761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: won't this also provoke preemptive action from Seers as their prophecies sees a terrible destruction rein down upon them?</div> </div> </div> </div> Why? Just shunt the building into twilight or something, \u201caccidentally\u201d forget to include some rivals into your twilight bunker, let the collateral damage do it\u2019s thing to the sleepers all around you, and then use the political capital this attack fosters to force the Diamond to make tons of concessions to avoid all out war. Then let the Diamond lynch the idiot who did it. Maybe earn a promotion. Twirl your clip on mustache. Or your real one if you can grow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T12:51:25-08:00","id":1473769,"title":"","content":"You could conceivably set it up to look like it was another Pylon who did the deed. I could totally see it being played off as a malfunction from a secret Orbital weapons system (which opens up a whole other can of political worms). Do any of the Supernaturals have influence over world governments and/or militaries, come to think of it? I remember the Four Awful Old Men from Seers, and Project NIGHTFALL from Guardians, but that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-01-2022, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T21:12:58-08:00","id":1473794,"title":"","content":"Fairly mundane question, but would a spell granting you a Language merit be a 2-dot, 3-dot, or 4-dot mind spell? It's closest to Gain Skill, since you're manufacturing the understanding somewhat wholesale, but the argument could be made that your just filtering your own understanding of language through a supernal medium, which is Enhance Skill. But it's also a merit, so you could also argue it falls under the &quot;Ruling&quot; spell description.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Tangentially related, would being under the effect of skill-enhancing or skill-adding spells be plausible training time for learning a skill? You'd still have to spend XP to gain dots, obviously, but as an in-character explanation it kinda makes sense. <br /> &quot;I've spent the last three months under the near-continuous influence of my mathematics-assisting Mind spell, balancing TELM's books. It... it's started to rub off on me, even when I don't have the spell up!&quot;<br /> <br /> The argument against would be that it's information artificially tacked onto your psyche - does its influence vanish entirely once the spell runs out? You still have memories of what it's like being under the effect, but you're diminished in the now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T21:51:36-08:00","id":1473801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473794#post1473794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fairly mundane question, but would a spell granting you a Language merit be a 2-dot, 3-dot, or 4-dot mind spell? It's closest to Gain Skill, since you're manufacturing the understanding somewhat wholesale, but the argument could be made that your just filtering your own understanding of language through a supernal medium, which is Enhance Skill. But it's also a merit, so you could also argue it falls under the &amp;quot;Ruling&amp;quot; spell description.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Universal Language spell is Mind 3, so Mind 2 or 3 looks good enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Tangentially related, would being under the effect of skill-enhancing or skill-adding spells be plausible training time for learning a skill? You'd still have to spend XP to gain dots, obviously, but as an in-character explanation it kinda makes sense. <br /> &amp;quot;I've spent the last three months under the near-continuous influence of my mathematics-assisting Mind spell, balancing TELM's books. It... it's started to rub off on me, even when I don't have the spell up!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The argument against would be that it's information artificially tacked onto your psyche - does its influence vanish entirely once the spell runs out? You still have memories of what it's like being under the effect, but you're diminished in the now. </div> </div> </div>Sure, I\u2019d allow it. After all, even the Awakening itself could be described as \u201cFor a moment I was one with the universe and understood its secrets, but now I must work to recapture that brilliance.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T21:56:47-08:00","id":1473802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473794#post1473794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fairly mundane question, but would a spell granting you a Language merit be a 2-dot, 3-dot, or 4-dot mind spell? It's closest to Gain Skill, since you're manufacturing the understanding somewhat wholesale, but the argument could be made that your just filtering your own understanding of language through a supernal medium, which is Enhance Skill. But it's also a merit, so you could also argue it falls under the &quot;Ruling&quot; spell description.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same metric as gaining Skills wholesale needing Patterning instead of Perfecting, I'd say gaining new &quot;internal&quot; Merits wholesale is a Perfecting or Weaving effect instead of Ruling.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tangentially related, would being under the effect of skill-enhancing or skill-adding spells be plausible training time for learning a skill? You'd still have to spend XP to gain dots, obviously, but as an in-character explanation it kinda makes sense.<br /> &quot;I've spent the last three months under the near-continuous influence of my mathematics-assisting Mind spell, balancing TELM's books. It... it's started to rub off on me, even when I don't have the spell up!&quot;<br /> <br /> The argument against would be that it's information artificially tacked onto your psyche - does its influence vanish entirely once the spell runs out? You still have memories of what it's like being under the effect, but you're diminished in the now. </div> </div> </div>ChroD explicitly doesn't worry about training times. If you've been holding onto enough Experiences to buy multiple dots of a Trait that doesn't have an explicit limit on when you can raising it like Gnosis or Wisdom, go nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T22:46:38-08:00","id":1473804,"title":"","content":"I would argue you don't do any learning while under the influence of a spell like that. Usually learning comes from failure and/or trying hard to overcome your limits...for either in this case you are just breezing through on magic.<br /> <br /> That said, tangential question, if you were at (say) occult 2 and under the influence of a +2 occult spell for months of duration, and then you buy up 2 dots of occult, does the spell now only give you +1 because you have hit the cap on skills?<br /> <br /> Also, despite Universal Language, i'd say this is Patterning. Yes there are multiple ways of doing some things, and adding a brand new language like this may seems inefficient compared to Universal language (though that spell say nothing about speaking or writing the language, only understanding and translating it... So maybe the merit is strictly better).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-02-2022, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T00:09:49-08:00","id":1473809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473804#post1473804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, tangential question, if you were at (say) occult 2 and under the influence of a +2 occult spell for months of duration, and then you buy up 2 dots of occult, does the spell now only give you +1 because you have hit the cap on skills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, sans Reach, the cap should still be taken into account.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T05:52:40-08:00","id":1473819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473761#post1473761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, i would assume that this method transforms your soul into a spirit, so when your body dies instead of a soul which dissapeares, your spirit hibernates and act just like a spirit (albiet one with a naturally occurring physical body, rather than ephemeral corpus... ). I think you become not human in the sense that immortals of this type shouldn't contribute to the Temenos.<br /> <br /> I am presuming that Awakened Liches don't use this kind of Fallen Sorcery, and have better methods of retaining their Gnosis. But this presents a baseline of what is possible (if you are willing to give up being human).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well transforming into a spirit is already offered as one of the possibilities for liches, so it's within the bounds of Awakened power. When I say incompatible, I'm proposing that the method that Sleepers can use just won't work for them at all along similar lines to why gaining Gnosis will cause you to lose telekinesis that you might have had or whatever. That the state of being Awakened hardwires you into something that would override any attempt to use a ritual of existing spirit magic to transform yourself.<br /> <br /> Mostly this is from a point of view that Immortals and Awakened liches are best reconciled in the same setting with the idea that the former can, at best, function as the subject of Obsessions to provide Arcane Experience towards whatever a lich might do to make themselves into something that doesn't die, rather than the idea that the answer to their dilemma lies outside of their game line. That and a general attitude for how the Awakened relate to other forms of supernatural power, even ones that are technically weaker; that the Supernal is elemental in a way that doesn't function well along with more messy, complicated forms of supernatural power (with some of those complications lending themselves to particular results that a Supernal spell doesn't quite come to as easily).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T10:16:16-08:00","id":1473837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473819#post1473819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">function as the subject of Obsessions to provide Arcane Experience towards whatever a lich might do ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that using them as a mystery makes perfect sense. And that trying their method at worst doesn't work (and you die) and at best you die, lose your awakening and the become a Purified 'Spirit' Immortal. Which is considerable worse off than being a Spirit Lich.<br /> <br /> Likewise, i don't have an object to a vampire killing/embrace a mage and leave them without awakened magic (amongst the other things that suck about being a vampire). Whether that is RAW or not.<br /> <br /> Seperate question: <br /> Assuming you cast and area of effect Devouring the Slain (scouring targets pattern for mana) without the reach for not counting towards your daily scouring limit, probably with the reach for hitting healthy subjects, do you get one mana per valid target within the area? And does it count as 1 scouring for the purpose of your daily limit? <br /> <br /> Similarly if you target multiple subjects with dice pool penalties for extra subjects. <br /> <br /> Even with the reading (i think we discussed previously) that the scouring is not 1 mana/lethal damage per potency of the spell, this seems to grant a <i>lot</i> of mana...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T11:17:15-08:00","id":1473844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473837#post1473837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seperate question:<br /> Assuming you cast and area of effect Devouring the Slain (scouring targets pattern for mana) without the reach for not counting towards your daily scouring limit, probably with the reach for hitting healthy subjects, do you get one mana per valid target within the area? And does it count as 1 scouring for the purpose of your daily limit?<br /> <br /> Similarly if you target multiple subjects with dice pool penalties for extra subjects.<br /> <br /> Even with the reading (i think we discussed previously) that the scouring is not 1 mana/lethal damage per potency of the spell, this seems to grant a <i>lot</i> of mana...</div> </div> </div> </div> The way I\u2019m reading it, seems to be that for each subject, you get Potency after Withstand Scourings, which grant 1 Mana and deal 1 Lethal each. Casting the spell itself seems to be what uses up the Scouring, not the individual Scourings\u2026so yeah, you can gain lots of Mana very quickly if you are willing to hurt a lot of people for it. Which is probably not good for your wisdom. But if you don\u2019t have a high potency or many subjects you won\u2019t get much, possibly less than a normal Scouring and then passing the damage onto someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T13:59:37-08:00","id":1473857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473844#post1473844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The way I\u2019m reading it, seems to be that for each subject, you get Potency after Withstand Scourings, which grant 1 Mana and deal 1 Lethal each. Casting the spell itself seems to be what uses up the Scouring, not the individual Scourings\u2026so yeah, you can gain lots of Mana very quickly if you are willing to hurt a lot of people for it. Which is probably not good for your wisdom. But if you don\u2019t have a high potency or many subjects you won\u2019t get much, possibly less than a normal Scouring and then passing the damage onto someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading is that it allows 1 willpower per potency, or 1 mana and health level (it even says there is a limit of the willpower which can be stolen, but no limit of the number of health levels converted to mana -which it doesn't need if it is only 1).<br /> <br /> But that aside. With extra targets it clearly does multiple damage and gives multiple mana. The withstand does make it difficult to get many targets and high potency, though with high Gnosis and a large group you could fill a large mana pool instantly (at the agreed wisdom risk).<br /> <br /> The only way to reduce the risk would be with consent, i image a low wisdom mage with a cult of fanitcal devotees could be persuaded to take the damage as part of some kind of prayer. Have to make it a legacy attainment though - no withstand if they consent, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-02-2022, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T14:55:59-08:00","id":1473865,"title":"","content":"Yes, withstand is lowered if they consent. Maybe study vampire bites and replicate some of their effects to make it a easier sell. Actually, any legacy that has this spell in it is probably a little vampiric in theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T15:18:32-08:00","id":1473869,"title":"","content":"Can you weave damage (say resistant damage) to move it from one subject to another? And is it Death to do so? Or possibly either Death/Life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T15:28:00-08:00","id":1473871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469546#post1469546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New questions:<br /> 1)Is damage done to a living creature under Deaths purview?<br /> 1.5)Can I move the damaged area, like changing Leg Wrack to Arm Wrack?<br /> 2)If I have damage to my pattern, would it be possible to transfer that damage to someone or something else, effectively healing the damage? Kinda like transferring charges between batteries, if damage was charge.<br /> 2.5)Can I do that with just Death?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1469552#post1469552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Yep, entropy and endings are within its purview<br /> 1.5) It would probably require a Reach, but the Condition would end when with the duration does<br /> 2) You can with a Weaving of Death<br /> 2.5) Yes, by transfering Potency damage to the target, withstood by Stamina. You can arguably do it with Weaving of Life as well, or transfer the lastest Potency turns of damage via Time's purview of change (resisted by Composure)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think messing with resistant damage is not possible, though. Otherwise, why not just heal it with Life? It amounts to the same thing. I think resistant damage even ignores time spells that age you the requisite two days in a instant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-02-2022, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T16:23:25-08:00","id":1473875,"title":"","content":"It would mainly be a way to get around the inability to heal - ie &quot;the reason i didn't heal this, is i couldn't, sa i moved it somewhere more convienant&quot; - seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> I do not think resistant damage ignored Time magic. The healing is a side effect, time magic - like Temporal Pocket - would let you rest for the amount of time needed, and healing would occur naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T16:35:21-08:00","id":1473876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473875#post1473875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think resistant damage ignored Time magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resistant damage explicitly uses the standard healing times, per the sidebar on page 223.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T17:39:55-08:00","id":1473878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473876#post1473876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resistant damage explicitly uses the standard healing times, per the sidebar on page 223.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Temporal Pocket will still allow more time to pass. Life can accelerate healing times, Time can actually make that time pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T17:50:01-08:00","id":1473879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473878#post1473878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Temporal Pocket will still allow more time to pass. Life can accelerate healing times, Time can actually make that time pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resistant damage is, by definition, resistant to magic. It's damage that follows the base rules set by the Fallen World, and is not subject to the imposition of will, regardless of how roundabout or environmental it goes.*<br /> <br /> *Though that said, I do need to double check the book's specific wording on the subject-it goes against the spirit of the purposes for that kind of cheat, but the specific wording might be argued.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T17:59:32-08:00","id":1473881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473878#post1473878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Temporal Pocket will still allow more time to pass. Life can accelerate healing times, Time can actually make that time pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>My copy says:<br /> <i>They cannot be healed by magic, <b>or have their healing times accelerated by magic \u2014 only recovery at the rates on this page will work</b> </i><br /> <br /> Emphasis on \u2018only.\u2019 So RAI seems to be \u2018No.\u2019<br /> <br /> (\u2018Accelerated by Time magic\u2019 is still \u2018accelerated by magic,\u2019 unless we get an official ruling where the Time Arcanum trumps this wording, similar to what happened with Siderite and fairies.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait a sec, Temporal Pocket? Hmm\u2026 yeah, I could see a table deciding to rule this one away without much issue. Or present this as something Awakened magic can\u2019t do\u2026 but Artifacts and Supernal Entities can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 02-02-2022, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T18:25:10-08:00","id":1473883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473881#post1473881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My copy says:<br /> <i>They cannot be healed by magic, <b>or have their healing times accelerated by magic \u2014 only recovery at the rates on this page will work</b> </i><br /> <br /> Emphasis on \u2018only.\u2019 So RAI seems to be \u2018No.\u2019<br /> <br /> (\u2018Accelerated by Time magic\u2019 is still \u2018accelerated by magic,\u2019 unless we get an official ruling where the Time Arcanum trumps this wording, similar to what happened with Siderite and fairies.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait a sec, Temporal Pocket? Hmm\u2026 yeah, I could see a table deciding to rule this one away without much issue. Or present this as something Awakened magic can\u2019t do\u2026 but Artifacts and Supernal Entities can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... you still age while in the pocket, right? Time is moving at a &quot;normal&quot; rate both inside and outside the pocket, but not in sync with one-another? So it's a question of if the pocket is magic-affecting-the-area or magic-altering-the-individual","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T19:57:34-08:00","id":1473886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473883#post1473883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So it's a question of if the pocket is magic-affecting-the-area or magic-altering-the-individual</div> </div> </div> </div>Its description is closer to Quarantine than Pocket Dimension, so I\u2019d say the latter or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T20:32:10-08:00","id":1473887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473886#post1473886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its description is closer to Quarantine than Pocket Dimension, so I\u2019d say the latter or both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I almost see it as a bubble, extending not far from the targets outermost layer. As soon as the target tries to interact with anything else, the bubble &quot;pops&quot;. Maybe it depends on how the caster conceptualized the Imago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T00:23:51-08:00","id":1473889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473887#post1473887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I almost see it as a bubble, extending not far from the targets outermost layer. As soon as the target tries to interact with anything else, the bubble &quot;pops&quot;. Maybe it depends on how the caster conceptualized the Imago?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why you want to cast it as an area of effect, so you can eat and drink things inside the pocket without time resuming... Ideally there will also be enough air to breath - if you intend to survive for (say) a week.<br /> <br /> EDIT: similarly, if you Temporal Stutter someone into the future, they don't experience any time, and so no damage heals (despite these healing times).<br /> <br /> EDIT2: further the rules say:<br /> &quot;Mages can speed healing times, and even close wounds with a single spell given enough mastery of the Arcana, but absent any supernatural effects recovery takes time.&quot; - obviously a spell to heal resistant damage doesn't work, but a spell to experience time would fit the definition of 'recovery takes time'. RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-03-2022, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T07:24:37-08:00","id":1473896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473889#post1473889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is why you want to cast it as an area of effect, so you can eat and drink things inside the pocket without time resuming... Ideally there will also be enough air to breath - if you intend to survive for (say) a week.<br /> <br /> EDIT: similarly, if you Temporal Stutter someone into the future, they don't experience any time, and so no damage heals (despite these healing times).<br /> <br /> EDIT2: further the rules say:<br /> &amp;quot;Mages can speed healing times, and even close wounds with a single spell given enough mastery of the Arcana, but absent any supernatural effects recovery takes time.&amp;quot; - obviously a spell to heal resistant damage doesn't work, but a spell to experience time would fit the definition of 'recovery takes time'. RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't considered the air prospect. Dunno if it was intended to be weaponized like Ban, but it sure has the possibility now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T10:50:15-08:00","id":1473908,"title":"","content":"I normally consider <i>Temporal Pocket</i> to be able to allow you to heal the damage from scouring Attributes, but not the effect of scouring Paradox Conditions or health. It seems that symbolically speaking, you require actual Fallen time for the Pattern to fix itself. The most interference I think is acceptable is to use either a medicine roll or spell to stabilize the character from bleeding out. This means that, for example, the cabal's Sanctum within a <i>Temporal Pocket</i> may help them rest up, plan and prepare between missions in very intense scenarios. However, they will still be in significant discomfort in the meantime and the damage will possibly become a liability that needs to be accounted for in case there is not enough downtime between their actions. Ultimately, this makes it so that when this shows up, its a tool to drive up the risks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T10:53:37-08:00","id":1473909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473896#post1473896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hadn't considered the air prospect. Dunno if it was intended to be weaponized like Ban, but it sure has the possibility now!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is unclear. The spell is written as if it should affect one person. If they interact with food or water, it ends, but it doesn't suggest breathing is a problem.<br /> <br /> However, as an AoE spell, any air which exists within the area would no longer be in the time pocket as soon as it hits the edge, so would appear to be freeze. With no fresh air entering (as no time is passing outside - no air should he able to move).<br /> <br /> But weaponising it may be difficult, as the target only has to walk out of the area (or interact with something)... Now if they are bleeding on the ground you can freeze them in place until they are dead, and nobody has a chance to stabilise/heal them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-03-2022, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T10:58:08-08:00","id":1473910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473908#post1473908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I normally consider <i>Temporal Pocket</i> to be able to allow you to heal the damage from scouring Attributes, but not the effect of scouring Paradox Conditions or health. It seems that symbolically speaking, you require actual Fallen time for the Pattern to fix itself. The most interference I think is acceptable is to use either a medicine roll or spell to stabilize the character from bleeding out. This means that, for example, the cabal's Sanctum within a <i>Temporal Pocket</i> may help them rest up, plan and prepare between missions in very intense scenarios. However, they will still be in significant discomfort in the meantime and the damage will possibly become a liability that needs to be accounted for in case there is not enough downtime between their actions. Ultimately, this makes it so that when this shows up, its a tool to drive up the risks.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no distinction in the rules between 'fallen time' and Making Time, just as a sword creating with a Making of Matter is treated exactly the same in the rules as a normal sword (except it ceases to exist when the Spell's duration ends).<br /> <br /> Similarly you can use Shifting Sands to go back in Time, rest and encounter or avoid all the things which injured you in the first place (or Temporal Stutter your way past the things) - it is just strictly worse, because when you do the healing is before you we're injured, so you are liable to be injured again...<br /> <br /> Likewise Temporal Summoning explicitly says it can bring a healed version of yourself to the present. But as it is removing damage not healing it, this is a stop-gap measure at best.<br /> <br /> Basically Time can happily less with health as a side effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-03-2022, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T15:28:05-08:00","id":1473936,"title":"","content":"We know what a mana battery is, a Forces battery is probably just a Supernally efficient battery and fetishes are Essence batteries. <br /> <br /> Following that train of thought, Mind can probably create Willpower batteries. Fate can create luck batteries that allow you to degrade exceptional success to normal ones in order to store them for later (I might make those into spells shortly).<br /> <br /> But what would a time battery be ? What would it be used for and how can it be charged ? Any ideas ?<br /> <br /> I can't help but imagine a scene with a hubristic Libertine saying &quot;What most people don't know is that the real secret to getting the most out of time batteries is to charge them with the premium source of high density time in existence: black holes. You see, normally nothing in the Tapestry can escape them. However, Supernal magic imposes its will on reality and overwrites it, making it the only thing that can safely manipulate them.<br /> <br /> All you need is this hyperlink to the camera of our satellite in orbit, enhaced with an Unveiling of Forces and algorithmically programmed to find singularities of optimal size for remote view casting. Lets see, this is the list of the ones available, you can use that one. <br /> <br /> What is that ? Taking time from it will make the event horizon expand much quicker ? Meh, we checked, its maximum size before collapsing is Prophesied to be nowhere near Earth, feel free to harness away.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T15:42:24-08:00","id":1473937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473936#post1473936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know what a mana battery is, a Forces battery is probably just a Supernally efficient battery and fetishes are Essence batteries. <br /> <br /> Following that train of thought, Mind can probably create Willpower batteries. Fate can create luck batteries that allow you to degrade exceptional success to normal ones in order to store them for later (I might make those into spells shortly).<br /> <br /> But what would a time battery be ? What would it be used for and how can it be charged ? Any ideas ?</div> </div> </div> </div>We already have a Time spell that rends someone\u2019s lifespan to inflict harm. Might as well go a step further and steal it.<br /> <br /> In fact, wasn\u2019t there a movie where a dystopian society had people trading time/lifespan as money? A mage could replicate that, at the risk of not-so-inaccurately being accused of being a Lich (though, beware the Chancellor\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T16:09:31-08:00","id":1473938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't help but imagine a scene with a hubristic Libertine saying &quot;What most people don't know is that the real secret to getting the most out of time batteries is to charge them with the premium source of high density time in existence: black holes. You see, normally nothing in the Tapestry can escape them. However, Supernal magic imposes its will on reality and overwrites it, making it the only thing that can safely manipulate them. </div> </div> </div>I think Time barely exists at the edge of a black hole... As you look at something falling it, it's time clock slows down to eventually freeze when it gets to the event horizon, and then it never crosses.<br /> <br /> I mean, from an observer's perspective. From the thing going down you just pass right across... Maybe, we've never actually tested it. <br /> <br /> Make of that what you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T16:15:54-08:00","id":1473939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473937#post1473937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We already have a Time spell that rends someone\u2019s lifespan to inflict harm. Might as well go a step further and steal it.<br /> <br /> In fact, wasn\u2019t there a movie where a dystopian society had people trading time/lifespan as money? A mage could replicate that, at the risk of not-so-inaccurately being accused of being a Lich (though, beware the Chancellor\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The question is how would that translate mechanically. What could you be able to do with stolen time ? How much would be taken by each level of Potency ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T17:07:42-08:00","id":1473942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473939#post1473939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The question is how would that translate mechanically. What could you be able to do with stolen time ? How much would be taken by each level of Potency ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026 Just throwing something, without fine-tuning things;<br /> <br /> Extract Lifespan (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> Rote: Occult, Science, Persuasion<br /> Extract (Potency) hours of lifespan from subject into a silvery wisp. Can be injected into a living creature to extend its lifespan for the same length, or incorporated as a Yantra for spells that affect life and lifespans.<br /> Lifespan returns to original owner when Duration expires, reversing any life-extensions and instantly dispelling spells that incorporated it. If the subject to whom the lifespan was injected has died, or the spell that incorporated it has expired/been destroyed, the spent lifespan is gone for good.<br /> Lifespan is a stubborn but flexible thing; avoiding dangers and harm can extend it, and vice-versa. This spell thus can result in net gain of lifespan when cast judiciously, or net loss for the unwise.<br /> This spell cannot cause immediate death, always leaving a sliver of time. Similarly, this spell cannot reverse death, nor affect the dead.<br /> +1 Reach: (Potency) days.<br /> Add Prime \u2022\u2022: Spell that used the extracted lifespan as a Yantra is not dispelled when lifespan is returned.<br /> Add Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: The grafted lifespan can be used to accelerate natural healing instead of extending lifespan. Treat as if time equal to injected length passed for the injury. Can cure Physical Tilts and Conditions. Cannot affect resistant damage. This consumes the spent lifespan for good.<br /> Add Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Can reverse death for the injected length. Revived target is soulless, does not necessarily know anything about the afterlife or whatever their state was during the interim, and returns to death after the injected lifespan is spent or returned. This consumes the spent lifespan for good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 02-03-2022, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T05:55:53-08:00","id":1473966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473942#post1473942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm\u2026 Just throwing something, without fine-tuning things;<br /> <br /> Extract Lifespan (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> Rote: Occult, Science, Persuasion<br /> Extract (Potency) hours of lifespan from subject into a silvery wisp. Can be injected into a living creature to extend its lifespan for the same length, or incorporated as a Yantra for spells that affect life and lifespans.<br /> Lifespan returns to original owner when Duration expires, reversing any life-extensions and instantly dispelling spells that incorporated it. If the subject to whom the lifespan was injected has died, or the spell that incorporated it has expired/been destroyed, the spent lifespan is gone for good.<br /> Lifespan is a stubborn but flexible thing; avoiding dangers and harm can extend it, and vice-versa. This spell thus can result in net gain of lifespan when cast judiciously, or net loss for the unwise.<br /> This spell cannot cause immediate death, always leaving a sliver of time. Similarly, this spell cannot reverse death, nor affect the dead.<br /> +1 Reach: (Potency) days.<br /> Add Prime \u2022\u2022: Spell that used the extracted lifespan as a Yantra is not dispelled when lifespan is returned.<br /> Add Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: The grafted lifespan can be used to accelerate natural healing instead of extending lifespan. Treat as if time equal to injected length passed for the injury. Can cure Physical Tilts and Conditions. Cannot affect resistant damage. This consumes the spent lifespan for good.<br /> Add Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Can reverse death for the injected length. Revived target is soulless, does not necessarily know anything about the afterlife or whatever their state was during the interim, and returns to death after the injected lifespan is spent or returned. This consumes the spent lifespan for good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a fascinating idea, I really like how lifespans can be extended with clever use as well. A few questions come to mind:<br /> <br /> 1- What kind if yantra does it count as, how much of a bonus does it give ?<br /> <br /> 2- How does it interact with those dying or bleeding out without conjunctional Life ?<br /> <br /> 3- What is the benefit of using lifespan with the conjunctional effects, such as Body Control for healing or Deny The Reaper for resurrection? <br /> <br /> 4- Can it be incorporated into spells to extend their lifespan/duration ?<br /> <br /> 5- What is the difference between taking one day from a rat rather than from a human ? How does it affect spirits (I guess vampires are possibly immune), who are theoretically immortal? Does it act on potential lifespan or fated one ?<br /> <br /> 6- In 1ed core book, there was a Steal Lifespan spell that granted years of lifespan, although it did not grant restored youth, healing or any kind of reprieve from aging or disease, so its usefulness was very questionable. Would there be any Reach options or variations that would tempt a prospective lich or a hubristic mage ?<br /> <br /> 7- Would it be possible for a variation of the spell to store the unspent potential lifespan of an individual at the moment of death ? Similar to how Merlin's protection spell affects Chas Chandler in the Constantine tv show ? Maybe that is the purview of Fate ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T06:38:22-08:00","id":1473967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473966#post1473966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its a fascinating idea, I really like how lifespans can be extended with clever use as well. A few questions come to mind:<br /> <br /> 1- What kind if yantra does it count as, how much of a bonus does it give ?<br /> <br /> 2- How does it interact with those dying or bleeding out without conjunctional Life ?<br /> <br /> 3- What is the benefit of using lifespan with the conjunctional effects, such as Body Control for healing or Deny The Reaper for resurrection? <br /> <br /> 4- Can it be incorporated into spells to extend their lifespan/duration ?<br /> <br /> 5- What is the difference between taking one day from a rat rather than from a human ? How does it affect spirits (I guess vampires are possibly immune), who are theoretically immortal? Does it act on potential lifespan or fated one ?<br /> <br /> 6- In 1ed core book, there was a Steal Lifespan spell that granted years of lifespan, although it did not grant restored youth, healing or any kind of reprieve from aging or disease, so its usefulness was very questionable. Would there be any Reach options or variations that would tempt a prospective lich or a hubristic mage ?<br /> <br /> 7- Would it be possible for a variation of the spell to store the unspent potential lifespan of an individual at the moment of death ? Similar to how Merlin's protection spell affects Chas Chandler in the Constantine tv show ? Maybe that is the purview of Fate ?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Tools. <br /> 4. Being a Yantra already sorta heads into increased Duration.<br /> 5. The base should work only on humans, and between species with either Reach of Life add-on, and flat-out impossible with the undead and the ephemeral.<br /> 6. Youth I would imagine be a separate spell effect, and Lichdom another separate (but likely related) endeavor.<br /> <br /> Anything I don\u2019t answer above, 1) I haven\u2019t thought of it yet, or 2) I\u2019m not confident about it being good idea to continue in this topic.<br /> <br /> Those whose imaginations were poked by the above, may have better answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T07:08:32-08:00","id":1473970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473942#post1473942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell thus can result in net gain of lifespan when cast judiciously</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want it to be a spell that can be cast judiciously then it needs to be either Lasting by default or have an option to be made so. If the effect is tied to a Duration then it isn't stackable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T08:29:02-08:00","id":1473976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473970#post1473970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want it to be a spell that can be cast judiciously then it needs to be either Lasting by default or have an option to be made so. If the effect is tied to a Duration then it isn't stackable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, there is no way to append it to an existing person's. I believe another, more benign and difficult intended use is to see it as an investment. The caster or subject whose lifespan was borrowed could have it returned with a net gain or loss, provided it wasn't used up. This means that mages who understand how to expand it and avoid shortening it could arguably create a slowly stacking buildup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T16:43:37-08:00","id":1474011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473976#post1473976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe another, more benign and difficult intended use is to see it as an investment. The caster or subject whose lifespan was borrowed could have it returned with a net gain or loss, provided it wasn't used up. This means that mages who understand how to expand it and avoid shortening it could arguably create a slowly stacking buildup.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't make heads or tails of this.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay, the best I can figure is that it's reading 21C Hermit's spell as saying that the quantity of stolen lifespan can depend in some unclear fashion on lifestyle, so is suggesting that a mage could steal a lifespan, live in a way that makes it last longer, give it back, and then steal it again to live a bit longer.<br /> <br /> While also saying that the stolen lifespan has a quantity measured by Potency, which would be more consistent with usual magic rules.<br /> <br /> Mind, the idea that a lifespan whose extension or detraction) is measured in hours, or even days, has its own issues. It really only seems worth doing for a mage who is already dying of old age looking to get time enough for one last activity in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-04-2022, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T17:10:22-08:00","id":1474013,"title":"","content":"If I wished to grant a Mage the various High Speech merits with a spell, that's Prime, right? or do I need the Mind components?<br /> <br /> Edit: Can I do this without the Prerequires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-04-2022, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T17:45:26-08:00","id":1474014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474013#post1474013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wished to grant a Mage the various High Speech merits with a spell, that's Prime, right? or do I need the Mind components?<br /> <br /> Edit: Can I do this without the Prerequires?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd read it as Mind primarily, although you could definately argue Prime. Conjunctive, maybe?<br /> <br /> As to the prerequisites... my gut says this circumvent the prerequisite since it only lasts as long as the spell does.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> This may be a worn-out question, but my casual search turned up nothing. Can a Mage use Forces- or Matter-Conjunctive Ban to protect themselves from bullets? &quot;No objects above X velocity&quot; or &quot;No objects of lead (or whatever material your current enemy favors)&quot; respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-04-2022, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T18:00:11-08:00","id":1474015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474014#post1474014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd read it as Mind primarily, although you could definately argue Prime. Conjunctive, maybe?<br /> <br /> As to the prerequisites... my gut says this circumvent the prerequisite since it only lasts as long as the spell does.</div> </div> </div> </div> The spell that allows sleepers to understand High Speech is Prime + Mind, but according to the Core rulebook High Speech is under Prime's purview, while it says nothing directly about High Speech in Mind's purview. So I'm uncertain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474014#post1474014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a worn-out question, but my casual search turned up nothing. Can a Mage use Forces- or Matter-Conjunctive Ban to protect themselves from bullets? &quot;No objects above X velocity&quot; or &quot;No objects of lead (or whatever material your current enemy favors)&quot; respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. It's probably a pretty common use of Ban.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-04-2022, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T18:26:07-08:00","id":1474017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474015#post1474015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The spell that allows sleeper to understand High Speech is Prime + Mind, but according to the Core rulebook High Speech is under Prime's purview, while it says nothing directly about High Speech in Mind's purview. So I'm uncertain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only say Mind because it's implanting knowledge and/or understanding. Words of Truth and Universal Language are both similar spells in concept, one is just making it so Truth is conveyed perfectly, while the other is conveying meaning with near-perfect clarity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-04-2022, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T18:51:07-08:00","id":1474020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474013#post1474013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wished to grant a Mage the various High Speech merits with a spell, that's Prime, right? or do I need the Mind components?<br /> <br /> Edit: Can I do this without the Prerequires?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say either Prime 3 (because its within its purview) or a Perfecting of Mind. Because at the end of the day, all mages return from the Supernal with High Speech. Learning to use it to describe an Imago is a trained skill that the Orders teach, therefore using Mind to gain the skill should be valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-04-2022, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T20:55:36-08:00","id":1474027,"title":"","content":"How would you work a matter-to-energy spell? Scale of the matter to the Level (p146) of the energy, and vice-versa?<br /> <br /> Basically, if one were to try to make a sunlight grenade... actually, since that wouldn't be Lasting, what happens when the spell ends? Energy-to-matter just results in a sudden burst of the original energy, but matter-to-energy either makes a fine powder or effectively deletes the original matter from existence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 02-04-2022, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-05T06:06:10-08:00","id":1474037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474027#post1474027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you work a matter-to-energy spell? Scale of the matter to the Level (p146) of the energy, and vice-versa?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think scale is going to allow the size of the targeted object, and Potency will effect how strongly it lasts.<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to think that it would work a lot like trying to turn a living thing into a creature of pure fire, that in most cases the transformed state retains the shape of the material object it was. You turn a rock into sunlight then it doesn't expand outwards, it becomes a little ball of light that can change back to its original form when the spell ends.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-05T06:41:31-08:00","id":1474038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474037#post1474037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think scale is going to allow the size of the targeted object, and Potency will effect how strongly it lasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be misunderstanding, but wont Duration effect how strongly it lasts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474037#post1474037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to think that it would work a lot like trying to turn a living thing into a creature of pure fire, that in most cases the transformed state retains the shape of the material object it was. You turn a rock into sunlight then it doesn't expand outwards, it becomes a little ball of light that can change back to its original form when the spell ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's a little opaque ball that will burn a vampire on contact? And possibly do horrible things to their insides if forced to swallow it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T20:24:36-08:00","id":1474249,"title":"","content":"The spellcasting pool of an imbued item is [spell's Arcanum rating]+[user's Gnosis, if any]. This means a master of Forces or an initiate imbuing Nightvision into an item will always result in a dice pool if 1+[user's Gnosis, if any].<br /> <br /> But does the same apply to Reach ? I always thought it was also fixed by the spell's rating, meaning only one free Reach, but the existence of flexible Reach in Signs makes me wonder if they have the same amount of Reach as the creator's Arcanum rating at the time would allow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T20:32:00-08:00","id":1474250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474249#post1474249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spellcasting pool of an imbued item is [spell's Arcanum rating]+[user's Gnosis, if any]. This means a master of Forces or an initiate imbuing Nightvision into an item will always result in a dice pool if 1+[user's Gnosis, if any].<br /> <br /> But does the same apply to Reach ? I always thought it was also fixed by the spell's rating, meaning only one free Reach, but the existence of flexible Reach in Signs makes me wonder if they have the same amount of Reach as the creator's Arcanum rating at the time would allow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect it\u2019s fixed at what level it was when it was \u2018cast\u2019 at the moment of Imbuing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T00:43:25-08:00","id":1474262,"title":"","content":"Does flexible reach not allow paradox risks rather than extra free reach?<br /> <br /> Also, i noticed something last night. Imbued items explicitly state that sleepers can use them. Am i correct that Artifacts require the user to be a mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T05:16:16-08:00","id":1474280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474262#post1474262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does flexible reach not allow paradox risks rather than extra free reach?<br /> <br /> Also, i noticed something last night. Imbued items explicitly state that sleepers can use them. Am i correct that Artifacts require the user to be a mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Flexible Reach allows a user of the item to modify the Reach to be less than what the creator set, but never more. Doing so does not modify or mitigate any Paradox Risk the item already had. (SoS page 67).<br /> <br /> Artifacts can only be used by a mage, who must use the activation key (or Word of Command) in order to cast (core book page 99).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T08:06:40-08:00","id":1474284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474249#post1474249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But does the same apply to Reach ? I always thought it was also fixed by the spell's rating, meaning only one free Reach, but the existence of flexible Reach in Signs makes me wonder if they have the same amount of Reach as the creator's Arcanum rating at the time would allow.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's there under the Paradox Risk section in the Imbued Item rules in Signs; it states that the spell can risk Paradox if the Reach imbued exceeds the free Reach of the item's creator at the time it is made. To me that very much reads that the creator gets to use their free Reach as it would normally apply; if you're an Adept of Forces, you can imbue an item with Nightvision that can be instant cast at range and with advanced duration and scale without risking Paradox.<br /> <br /> Flexible Reach then becomes allowing the item's users to choose if they wanted to downgrade any of those factors for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> It also means that if you're an Initiate of Forces, you can make an item that has all the same factors, it's just going to count as three Reach over for anybody using it (and it's only if they have flexible Reach that they have the option to bring it down to safe levels).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T10:33:44-08:00","id":1474298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also means that if you're an Initiate of Forces, you can make an item that has all the same factors, it's just going to count as three Reach over for anybody using it (and it's only if they have flexible Reach that they have the option to bring it down to safe levels).</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense. If flexible reach doesn't allow you reduce to prevent risking paradox, and can't increase the reach anyway, it seems kinda ... trivial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T10:56:20-08:00","id":1474302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474280#post1474280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts can only be used by a mage, who must use the activation key (or Word of Command) in order to cast (core book page 99).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that is what i thought. It seems backwards. <br /> <br /> Imbued items (effectively) give the user access to Arcana dots they don't have. And can be used without gnosis.<br /> <br /> Artifacts can give the user both Arcana and Gnosis which they don't have access to, but can't be used without gnosis.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Artifacts can trigger themselves, and thus a sleeper could be using one without knowing it if the happen to satisfy the &quot;different circumstances, <br /> determined when you create the Artifact&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T14:28:50-08:00","id":1474326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474302#post1474302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, that is what i thought. It seems backwards. <br /> <br /> Imbued items (effectively) give the user access to Arcana dots they don't have. And can be used without gnosis.<br /> <br /> Artifacts can give the user both Arcana and Gnosis which they don't have access to, but can't be used without gnosis.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Artifacts can trigger themselves, and thus a sleeper could be using one without knowing it if the happen to satisfy the &amp;quot;different circumstances, <br /> determined when you create the Artifact&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also a Sleepwalker merit that allows them to use Artifacts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T00:39:08-08:00","id":1474355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474298#post1474298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would make sense. If flexible reach doesn't allow you reduce to prevent risking paradox, and can't increase the reach anyway, it seems kinda ... trivial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say there can be enough circumstances where one wants to reduce the factors from advanced, and perhaps also use the versions of spell effects when they're not Reaching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T02:48:47-08:00","id":1474359,"title":"","content":"Ok, i saw someone mention this on Reddit and i thought it was wrong, now i am confused.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notAnExactQuote</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Words of Command allows you 'cheat' the imbued item activation roll - the spell say it activates exactly as it it we're triggered normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if the 'normal' spell had spell factors for (say) indefinite duration - putting you on a chance die without Yantras - Word of Command seems to let you activate it with a normal Prime + Gnosis roll without negative modifier.<br /> <br /> This seems rather broken. Am i reading it wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T03:27:42-08:00","id":1474362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474359#post1474359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, i saw someone mention this on Reddit and i thought it was wrong, now i am confused.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So if the 'normal' spell had spell factors for (say) indefinite duration - putting you on a chance die without Yantras - Word of Command seems to let you activate it with a normal Prime + Gnosis roll without negative modifier.<br /> <br /> This seems rather broken. Am i reading it wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn\u2019t Word of Command get you [Potency] successes on the activation roll? Even better than rolling Prime + Gnosis.<br /> <br /> The balancing factor here would be actually finding Items Imbued with Indefinite spells in the first place, or finding &amp; convincing someone who can make them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T04:40:00-08:00","id":1474363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474362#post1474362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn\u2019t Word of Command get you [Potency] successes on the activation roll? Even better than rolling Prime + Gnosis.<br /> <br /> The balancing factor here would be actually finding Items Imbued with Indefinite spells in the first place, or finding &amp; convincing someone who can make them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, [Potency] successes, but for a spell you only usually care about the 1st success. So I'm just ignoring that - might be important for Werewolf fetishes, or Changeling something, or maybe a Ghost shaped into an object can have their numina activated... (I don't know about sin-eaters, i think I'm remembering Exalted).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T06:26:51-08:00","id":1474370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474359#post1474359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, i saw someone mention this on Reddit and i thought it was wrong, now i am confused.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So if the 'normal' spell had spell factors for (say) indefinite duration - putting you on a chance die without Yantras - Word of Command seems to let you activate it with a normal Prime + Gnosis roll without negative modifier.<br /> <br /> This seems rather broken. Am i reading it wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think this is a place where the rule that the spell cannot be cast if its dice penalty puts the pool five below zero would come into play. Depending on the Arcanum of the item's spell and the Gnosis of the caster, that gives a very limited range of possibilities for casting at a -10 penalty with no Yantras.<br /> <br /> I mean, so long as Duration isn't the primary factor, although even then if it's using the spell's Arcanum then the leg up against the penalty still might not be enough.<br /> <br /> Although I wonder... it may be that Imbued items typically can't cast indefinite spells anyway. Indefinite duration requires Reach, so if the creator didn't imbue the spell with Reach already assigned to it then it would make sense to not have the option.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm thinking that this function of Word of Command relieves the burden of having a means of casting spells without being able to alleviate the penalties a bit. Not to a huge extent, as you still only have so many penalties you can apply without the option to boost the pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T08:18:46-08:00","id":1474375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depending on the Arcanum of the item's spell and the Gnosis of the caster, that gives a very limited range of possibilities for casting at a -10 penalty with no Yantras. </div> </div> </div>I think that a weaving spell (Arcanum 3) plus Gnosis 2 gives you -5. And words of command making that an automatic success for any character with Prime 1 seems very strong. <br /> <br /> And if it is the primary factor, that is even easier. But i realised the merit does say indefinite spells can't be imbued - so i think limiting it to -8 (1 year) will still be very powerful and available to starting characters. (I was assuming the 2 reach being applied).<br /> <br /> That said, persistent spell effects seem like they should be indefinite and i know this is ground that has been discussed elsewhere, so i will leave that point alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to a huge extent, as you still only have so many penalties you can apply without the option to boost the pool. </div> </div> </div>I take it you are talking about the -5 dice pool (which isn't being rolled). So yes, assuming a [Arcana 5] imbued item and Gnosis 1 starting character (with a dot in prime) - 11 (so 5 steps worth of factors) plus any free steps of primary factors (do you get those from the imbued Item's Arcana rating?)<br /> <br /> I don't think that is too broken, but it seems far more powerful than a normal imbued item. With slim justification for the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-10-2022, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T11:20:01-08:00","id":1474380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474375#post1474375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that a weaving spell (Arcanum 3) plus Gnosis 2 gives you -5. And words of command making that an automatic success for any character with Prime 1 seems very strong.<br /> <br /> And if it is the primary factor, that is even easier. But i realized the merit does say indefinite spells can't be imbued - so i think limiting it to -8 (1 year) will still be very powerful and available to starting characters. (I was assuming the 2 reach being applied).<br /> <br /> That said, persistent spell effects seem like they should be indefinite and i know this is ground that has been discussed elsewhere, so i will leave that point alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I take it you are talking about the -5 dice pool (which isn't being rolled). So yes, assuming a [Arcana 5] imbued item and Gnosis 1 starting character (with a dot in prime) - 11 (so 5 steps worth of factors) plus any free steps of primary factors (do you get those from the imbued Item's Arcana rating?)<br /> <br /> I don't think that is too broken, but it seems far more powerful than a normal imbued item. With slim justification for the power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Word of Command</i> is arguably one of if not the best 1 dot spell to be made into a Legacy Attainment. Since those have automatic activation, it means any imbued item that you have will be able to be reliably cast. No matter how tense the combat or how dire the situation, you have 100% chance of casting it and with an exceptional success at Prime 5. So a mage that has a lot of skill negotiating with crafters or is one themselves can arguably be ready for anything, so long as they have the mana. But Prime mages will likely have the mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T17:33:16-08:00","id":1474402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474375#post1474375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that is too broken, but it seems far more powerful than a normal imbued item. With slim justification for the power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that if a person invested most of their starting dots in an Imbued Item capable of a Master spells, there's this really cool thing they want to be able to pull off without needing to be running it on chance dice a lot of the time.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I'm going to look at it again and decide if Words of Power needs to have its Duration matched to the item it's keeping active.<br /> <br /> Also, for most mages who aren't Obrimos, that's compounding their Mana costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T04:41:23-08:00","id":1474425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474402#post1474402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say that if a person invested most of their starting dots in an Imbued Item capable of a Master spells, there's this really cool thing they want to be able to pull off without needing to be running it on chance dice a lot of the time.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I'm going to look at it again and decide if Words of Power needs to have its Duration matched to the item it's keeping active.<br /> <br /> Also, for most mages who aren't Obrimos, that's compounding their Mana costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can buy an Imbued item with merit dots. Is that what you mean?<br /> <br /> It does not need duration, the spell effect is to trigger the Item's normal trigger without knowing what that it. Then the spell ends and the Item's effect takes over. And yes, 1 mana for those who don't have it as a ruling Arcana , or choose it as a Praxis (which i just leanred bypasses that cost). Definitely worth considering if you use a lot of imbued items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T18:30:21-08:00","id":1474464,"title":"","content":"How do direct damage spells interact with the Resilience Discipline ? Would the damage be reduced or do spells bypass that to always inflict the intended damage ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-11-2022, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T19:31:54-08:00","id":1474469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474464#post1474464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do direct damage spells interact with the Resilience Discipline ? Would the damage be reduced or do spells bypass that to always inflict the intended damage ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Resilience \u2018feels\u2019 like Armor, so I feel it should work on damage spells too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T01:18:43-08:00","id":1474483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474464#post1474464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do direct damage spells interact with the Resilience Discipline ? Would the damage be reduced or do spells bypass that to always inflict the intended damage ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Resilience works against all sources of damage unless specified otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T20:48:55-08:00","id":1474597,"title":"","content":"Would Fate alone be enough to make an attack be an &quot;universal frailty&quot; for changelings ? What about a &quot;universal bane&quot; for vampires ? I can see the possibility of it requiring, respectively, conjunctional Mind or Death. However, I also imagine it being interpreted as it not affecting their supernatural body, but just intensifying an aspect of their curses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T21:02:42-08:00","id":1474598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474597#post1474597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Fate alone be enough to make an attack be an &quot;universal frailty&quot; for changelings ? What about a &quot;universal bane&quot; for vampires ? I can see the possibility of it requiring, respectively, conjunctional Mind or Death. However, I also imagine it being interpreted as it not affecting their supernatural body, but just intensifying an aspect of their curses.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the level of Traveler spells? Absolutely not. All the published spells involve rewriting the banes of specific entities, making an object the bane of specific entities, or circumventing the rules of specificity for banes that fit within the umbrella category of an existing substance. Hardwiring the quality of being globally ruinous to an entire category of being is the domain of archmastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T08:27:36-08:00","id":1474625,"title":"","content":"Just reading the first dot of the Mysterium merit Egregore, and i realise i don't know how to construct the dice pool. <br /> <br /> It says to use the teamwork rules, so &quot;assemble dive pool as normal&quot; - this can be a minimum of -5 with spell factors, and then successes from the ritual casters add to that dice pool?<br /> <br /> So RAW it seems you don't add their dice first and then spell factor down to -5, is that a correct reading? <br /> <br /> (With everyone involved having the Mysterium merit, you just go to -5 and add a single an automatic success, or if you want to get an extraordinary success, bring 4 Mysterium members and cast as a Praxis or 6 members... Automatic exceptional success seems broken, but i guess you can pretty much guarantee it with Rites+prime+sacred tools, or Fate, either way, you still have to roll dice for those)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T09:44:58-08:00","id":1474631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474625#post1474625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just reading the first dot of the Mysterium merit Egregore, and i realise i don't know how to construct the dice pool.<br /> <br /> It says to use the teamwork rules, so &quot;assemble dive pool as normal&quot; - this can be a minimum of -5 with spell factors, and then successes from the ritual casters add to that dice pool?<br /> <br /> So RAW it seems you don't add their dice first and then spell factor down to -5, is that a correct reading?<br /> <br /> (With everyone involved having the Mysterium merit, you just go to -5 and add a single an automatic success, or if you want to get an extraordinary success, bring 4 Mysterium members and cast as a Praxis or 6 members... Automatic exceptional success seems broken, but i guess you can pretty much guarantee it with Rites+prime+sacred tools, or Fate, either way, you still have to roll dice for those)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be beneficial to also read the expanded details on teamwork casting in Signs of Sorcery page 55. But to summarize how every caster is affected:<br /> <br /> * <i>Secondary participants with no dots in the Arcana used:</i> can be used as environmental yantra<br /> <br /> * <i>Secondary participants with some dots in the Arcana used, but not enough to cast the spell: </i>Roll Gnosis-3 and add successes as a dice bonus to the leader. If everyone has Egregore, they just roll Gnosis.<br /> <br /> * <i>Secondary participants who can cast the spell:</i> roll Gnosis + Arcanum, adding successes to the leader's dice pool. If everyone has Egregore, they gain one automatic successes, meaning they guarantee at least a +1 bonus to the leader<br /> <br /> * All of this is modified by rehearsal bonuses and penalties<br /> <br /> In addition, each Path probably has a way to gain exceptional successes. Acanthus and Obrimos are easy, Mastigos just use a high powered Ritual focus spell and high Willpower bonuses. Thyrsus could arguably intensify and alter the Resonance of a Hallow, making the bonus from Resonant mana much greater. Moros can probably intensify the bonus from a sacrificial yantra and provide perfected metals to the casters, giving a much higher chance of an exceptional success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-14-2022, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T10:36:09-08:00","id":1474635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474631#post1474631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If everyone has Egregore, they gain one automatic successes, meaning they guarantee at least a +1 bonus to the leader</div> </div> </div> </div>Can i just clarify. 'at least a +1 bonus to the leader' is to the leader's successes, not to the leader's dice pool.<br /> <br /> Re-reading the merit, it appears that full participants gain only +1, and don't have to roll. Rather than rolling and adding 1 more than that number of successes to the leader's dice pool.<br /> <br /> Auto-success on any ritual attempt seems excessive, but that is the only way i can see to read the merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T11:13:55-08:00","id":1474636,"title":"","content":"I know this is from another thread (I'm trying to avoid necro-thread every interesting thing i see) but it gave me a simple time travel question (I've snippets the bits which are clear to me).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1457340-time-arcanum-and-people-travelling-back?p=1457358#post1457358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>might</i> be complications on occasions with a mage with <i>no</i> sympathy to the period in question, although even that might be overcome with other spells (although I think creating sympathy wholecloth to the past should be a slightly more tricky proposition than doing it for spatial sympathy).</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption would (now) be that you can only have Temporal sympathy to yourself, if you could Make Temporal sympathy wholesale then that should allow you to go back in time into someone else's body, and i don't know that this was intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Keep in mind that when going back in time, the present still exists and the space where you departed retains a signature where the spell can be dispelled, preventing any changes to the past from taking hold. Travelling back with the intention of doing something with widespread changes will create a lot of ripples to warn mages, who may be very motivated to find out where this person travelled back from. </div> </div> </div>This just seems wrong, the Time arcanum makes clear the CofD present remains at a fixed time until you catch up (at which point changes become lasting). And once it is lasting dispelling the spell (assuming it continues to exist) doesn't undo anything.<br /> <br /> &quot;the present is frozen at the moment they left \u2014 if they \u201ccatch up\u201d to it, anything they changed becomes real, and the normal flow of time resumes.&quot;<br /> <br /> So if there is a duration spell ongoing it is frozen in the present at a single location. Dispelling it should be done in the past, by using Time sight to notice somebody is a time traveller... But folks in the past aren't invested in your subjective future... So really it would be people with Time spells protecting them from any changes to the timeline noticing you did a thing (clash of wills to not be changed) and trying to go back and undo your changes/counter your spell in the past?<br /> <br /> Ok, two questions.<br /> <br /> Is this a form is Lichdom? You travel back to your younger body, you cast it as an indefinite spell, which you then cancel once you arrive at the 'present', then return to your past to live out your life again... 'the groundhog lich'?<br /> <br /> And secondly, as that thread was comparing shifting sands to corridors of time, i realised shifting sands says nothing about inhabiting your past self, my interpretation would be that there are now two of you. The original and the time traveller (it is also not withstood by Temporal sympathy, because you are not using the Temporal sympathy attainment, so it doesn't matter how changed your past body might have been). Is this correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-14-2022, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T11:14:14-08:00","id":1474637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474635#post1474635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can i just clarify. 'at least a +1 bonus to the leader' is to the leader's successes, not to the leader's dice pool.<br /> <br /> Re-reading the merit, it appears that full participants gain only +1, and don't have to roll. Rather than rolling and adding 1 more than that number of successes to the leader's dice pool.<br /> <br /> Auto-success on any ritual attempt seems excessive, but that is the only way i can see to read the merit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looking at Egregore, it says in the description on page 101: <i>&quot;She does not suffer the \u20133 penalty to contribute without the necessary Arcanum rating, and adds an automatic success if a full participant.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Then looking at the teamwork rules in page on page 119: <i>&quot;Any secondary caster who meets the Arcanum requirements rolls her own casting and adds her successes as bonus dice to the leader.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So the wording can be a bit vague, but I think the merit benefits both leader and full secondary casters. The leader gets one automatic success by default. The full secondary participants also get a single success, which becomes a bonus dice for the leader. Since the merit says &quot;adds&quot; rather than something like &quot;substitutes the roll&quot;, it would suggest you still roll but receive the additional efficiency as a bonus. Secondary casters with partial qualification do not suffer the dice penalty and secondary unqualified casters act as environmental yantra as usual. That would be the intent I felt from that specific wording.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T11:59:06-08:00","id":1474639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474636#post1474636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is from another thread (I'm trying to avoid necro-thread every interesting thing i see) but it gave me a simple time travel question (I've snippets the bits which are clear to me).<br /> <br /> My assumption would (now) be that you can only have Temporal sympathy to yourself, if you could Make Temporal sympathy wholesale then that should allow you to go back in time into someone else's body, and i don't know that this was intended.<br /> <br /> <br /> This just seems wrong, the Time arcanum makes clear the CofD present remains at a fixed time until you catch up (at which point changes become lasting). And once it is lasting dispelling the spell (assuming it continues to exist) doesn't undo anything.<br /> <br /> &quot;the present is frozen at the moment they left \u2014 if they \u201ccatch up\u201d to it, anything they changed becomes real, and the normal flow of time resumes.&quot;<br /> <br /> So if there is a duration spell ongoing it is frozen in the present at a single location. Dispelling it should be done in the past, by using Time sight to notice somebody is a time traveller... But folks in the past aren't invested in your subjective future... So really it would be people with Time spells protecting them from any changes to the timeline noticing you did a thing (clash of wills to not be changed) and trying to go back and undo your changes/counter your spell in the past?<br /> <br /> Ok, two questions.<br /> <br /> Is this a form is Lichdom? You travel back to your younger body, you cast it as an indefinite spell, which you then cancel once you arrive at the 'present', then return to your past to live out your life again... 'the groundhog lich'?<br /> <br /> And secondly, as that thread was comparing shifting sands to corridors of time, i realised shifting sands says nothing about inhabiting your past self, my interpretation would be that there are now two of you. The original and the time traveller (it is also not withstood by Temporal sympathy, because you are not using the Temporal sympathy attainment, so it doesn't matter how changed your past body might have been). Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since Shifting Sands moves you across Time, but not space, you inhabit your past self. Think of it as a Temporal Summoning of the present self upon the past one, you are rewriting the properties of the past self with those of the current self. Having two mages at the same time would require Patterning or perhaps even Making. In regards to Time Liches, I recommend you look at the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e/page25\">Eternal Soul Sentinels</a>, this is what they specialize in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T14:02:19-08:00","id":1474644,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll have to reread the book to be 100% confident, but my memory suggests\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474636#post1474636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, two questions.<br /> <br /> Is this a form is Lichdom? You travel back to your younger body, you cast it as an indefinite spell, which you then cancel once you arrive at the 'present', then return to your past to live out your life again... 'the groundhog lich'?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? Keep in mind though, the label \u201cLich\u201d is only really applied to those who fall from humanity in their pursuit of immortality. It <i>could</i> be used as an in-universe slander, like the label \u201cLeft-Handed,\u201d but thematically that\u2019s the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And secondly, as that thread was comparing shifting sands to corridors of time, i realised shifting sands says nothing about inhabiting your past self, my interpretation would be that there are now two of you. The original and the time traveller (it is also not withstood by Temporal sympathy, because you are not using the Temporal sympathy attainment, so it doesn't matter how changed your past body might have been). Is this correct? </div> </div> </div>Inhabiting your past self is the <i>default</i> form for time travel to the past, at least for \u2018Traveler\u2019 spells i.e. anything below Archmastery (\u2018Seeker\u2019 spells), whether you use Temporal Sympathy or not.<br /> <br /> You need to create/find an Iris to the past to make your present self and past self coexist together at a given point in the past. Archmages of Time can create them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T14:36:57-08:00","id":1474647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474637#post1474637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Looking at Egregore, it says in the description on page 101: <i>&amp;quot;She does not suffer the \u20133 penalty to contribute without the necessary Arcanum rating, and adds an automatic success if a full participant.&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> Then looking at the teamwork rules in page on page 119: <i>&amp;quot;Any secondary caster who meets the Arcanum requirements rolls her own casting and adds her successes as bonus dice to the leader.&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> So the wording can be a bit vague, but I think the merit benefits both leader and full secondary casters. The leader gets one automatic success by default. The full secondary participants also get a single success, which becomes a bonus dice for the leader. Since the merit says &amp;quot;adds&amp;quot; rather than something like &amp;quot;substitutes the roll&amp;quot;, it would suggest you still roll but receive the additional efficiency as a bonus. Secondary casters with partial qualification do not suffer the dice penalty and secondary unqualified casters act as environmental yantra as usual. That would be the intent I felt from that specific wording.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems fair. Only i didn't think the main caster got any benefit... 'participating in' as opposed to 'leading'. It is slightly unclear. <br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T15:00:48-08:00","id":1474652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474644#post1474644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll have to reread the book to be 100% confident, but my memory suggests\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe? Keep in mind though, the label \u201cLich\u201d is only really applied to those who fall from humanity in their pursuit of immortality. It <i>could</i> be used as an in-universe slander, like the label \u201cLeft-Handed,\u201d but thematically that\u2019s the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, i don't have a problem with that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I think reliving the same day over and over (or week or month) will eventually drive you crazy. <br /> <br /> Developing a legacy to do just that does seem like the way to go to avoid dispellation... But that just makes one more committed to the insanity. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Inhabiting your past self is the <i>default</i> form for time travel to the past, at least for \u2018Traveler\u2019 spells i.e. anything below Archmastery (\u2018Seeker\u2019 spells), whether you use Temporal Sympathy or not.<br /> <br /> You need to create/find an Iris to the past to make your present self and past self coexist together at a given point in the past. Archmages of Time can create them. </div> </div> </div>See that would have been my initial assumption, until i compared the two spells, and now I'm wondering why i thought that? (Just re-read the Time arcanum... Maybe it is discussed somewhere else). <br /> <br /> Shifting Sands seems to explicitly send your current body back, as you keep all your injuries etc. Whereas Corridors is really clear about not doing that. <br /> <br /> It's seems if that was the default then &quot;The Past can be Rewritten&quot; section on p. 185/6 would be where it would be. <br /> <br /> I do like that the two bodies would immediately crash i to each other, if the haven't move location. There is even a space spell which does that. I could totally see a Time version of that spell working as direct damage... But i digress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T15:05:22-08:00","id":1474653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474652#post1474652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shifting Sands seems to explicitly send your current body back, as you keep all your injuries etc. Whereas Corridors is really clear about not doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what Hermit means is that altering your Time Pattern normally moves you along the axis of your own position in the world over time, such that Shifting Sands puts you where you were a turn/minute/scene ago in the state you're in in the present rather than duplicating you in your current position with the clock turned back however many intervals \u2014 there's a reason the sample archmaster of Time is where we most prominently see temporally-displaced doppelgangers of a character in the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T16:28:17-08:00","id":1474658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474652#post1474652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, i don't have a problem with that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I think reliving the same day over and over (or week or month) will eventually drive you crazy. <br /> <br /> Developing a legacy to do just that does seem like the way to go to avoid dispellation... But that just makes one more committed to the insanity. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> See that would have been my initial assumption, until i compared the two spells, and now I'm wondering why i thought that? (Just re-read the Time arcanum... Maybe it is discussed somewhere else). <br /> <br /> Shifting Sands seems to explicitly send your current body back, as you keep all your injuries etc. Whereas Corridors is really clear about not doing that. <br /> <br /> It's seems if that was the default then &amp;quot;The Past can be Rewritten&amp;quot; section on p. 185/6 would be where it would be. <br /> <br /> I do like that the two bodies would immediately crash i to each other, if the haven't move location. There is even a space spell which does that. I could totally see a Time version of that spell working as direct damage... But i digress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah what Satchel said.<br /> <br /> So for example, let\u2019s say you walked out of a room where all your friends were\u2026 and then got shot. You rewind time. You are now back in the room\u2026 and freak out your friends, because as far as <i>they</i> can tell, your body spontaneously bursted out gunfire wounds out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> Even if Corridors doesn\u2019t specify this, I\u2019m pretty sure the assumption stays the same. I mean, I don\u2019t see any immediate reason it shouldn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> It could be that the writers were thinking of immediate action-filled short flashes to the past when writing Shifting, so they felt the need to reiterate the stuff about injuries there, but were thinking of big prepared rituals when writing Corridors, so it kinda slipped their minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T16:39:53-08:00","id":1474659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474653#post1474653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">altering your Time Pattern normally moves you along the axis of your own position in the world over time</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, i can see that now. Is usually spells like Postcognition and Temporal summoning follow the subject's timeline. But it definitely looks open to interpretations. <br /> <br /> Side note, Shifting sands is lasting by default, like it was modelled on other fraying spells. Sure the changes you make aren't immediately lasting until you reach the present again, but the spell has no duration - so can't be dispelled. The only defence is constant presence (ie winning a clash of wills). How does the duration so of constant presence work? When do you have to cast it to be protected? I am very confused...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T16:48:33-08:00","id":1474661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474658#post1474658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah what Satchel said.<br /> <br /> So for example, let\u2019s say you walked out of a room where all your friends were\u2026 and then got shot. You rewind time. You are now back in the room\u2026 and freak out your friends, because as far as <i>they</i> can tell, your body spontaneously bursted out gunfire wounds out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> Even if Corridors doesn\u2019t specify this, I\u2019m pretty sure the assumption stays the same. I mean, I don\u2019t see any immediate reason it shouldn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> It could be that the writers were thinking of immediate action-filled short flashes to the past when writing Shifting, so they felt the need to reiterate the stuff about injuries there, but were thinking of big prepared rituals when writing Corridors, so it kinda slipped their minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as i can tell Corridors doesn't work like that. you go back to your body when you were a child and now you (the awakened soul and mind of adult you) is living in your child body (for the Spell's duration - unless it is dispelled*) - which does not spontaneously develop wounds or grow older. (Child you has a withstand rating especially if pre-awakening - an example of withstand 3 is pre-awakening - which unless you cast corridors with reach to change primary factors to duration, and that is desirable, you will always have the potency to go back that far).<br /> <br /> This being strictly better than shifting sands seems fine given the lack of reach available...<br /> <br /> *Which is not the case for Shifting Sands, as it doesn't need any duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T16:56:57-08:00","id":1474662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474661#post1474661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as i can tell Corridors doesn't work like that. you go back to your body when you were a child and now you (the awakened soul and mind of adult you) is living in your child body (for the Spell's duration - unless it is dispelled*) - which does not spontaneously develop wounds or grow older. (Child you has a withstand rating especially if pre-awakening - an example of withstand 3 is pre-awakening - which unless you cast corridors with reach to change primary factors to duration, and that is desirable, you will always have the potency to go back that far).<br /> <br /> This being strictly better than shifting sands seems fine given the lack of reach available...<br /> <br /> *Which is not the case for Shifting Sands, as it doesn't need any duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, gonna have to reread later the parts about body states and Durations. (For now, all we can be sure is that both Shifting Sands and Corridors of Time do not allow one person to exist simultaneously at one point.)<br /> <br /> But before that; I\u2019m not sure why you thought the Withstand rating here is important? Once it\u2019s overcome, it\u2019s overcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T17:20:12-08:00","id":1474664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474659#post1474659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side note, Shifting sands is lasting by default,</div> </div> </div> </div>Shifting Sands lasts one turn by default. It works like time travel works, which is that you jump back to the present when the Duration runs out if you didn't catch up already.<br /> <br /> Constant Presence triggers a Clash once the subject's history would be altered, and if Constant Presence wins the Clash then the subject &quot;jumps&quot; from its pre-altered present to the altered present in its pre-altered state, thus preserving it against temporal meddling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T20:22:41-08:00","id":1474697,"title":"","content":"So lets say you are using Corridors of Time, how much control does the caster have over it ? Do you always need to live your way back to the present ? Should mid trip the situation become worse, can you dispel the effect and not allow the changes to set in ? Similarly, if you are at prima facie satisfied with the changes, can you end the trip and set them (alongside any consequences of history filling in the blanks) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-14-2022, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T00:24:41-08:00","id":1474710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474697#post1474697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So lets say you are using Corridors of Time, how much control does the caster have over it ? Do you always need to live your way back to the present ? Should mid trip the situation become worse, can you dispel the effect and not allow the changes to set in ? Similarly, if you are at prima facie satisfied with the changes, can you end the trip and set them (alongside any consequences of history filling in the blanks) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do not need to live your way to the present. If it only lasts 3 turns, when the Spell's ends you are back in the present and changes set.<br /> <br /> The difference if the spell is dispelled is significant, as all changes are undone (i guess you retain knowledge of an alternative past... But not any injuries sustained). <br /> <br /> It is unclear whether ending the spell prematurely behaves like it finished normally (setting the changes) or like it was dispelled. But i would lean towards the former.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shifting Sands lasts one turn by default. It works like time travel works, which is that you jump back to the present when the Duration runs out if you didn't catch up already. </div> </div> </div>'It works like time travel' suggests there is a set way that time travel works. But there isn't, there are clearly two spells which have different effects, and a set of rules which explain time travel in general.<br /> <br /> Only in one place does it explain that time travel works like that, and it is in corridors of time, not the general time travel rules.<br /> <br /> As far as i can tell Shifting Sands, with one reach, sends you back a scene (regardless of the potency) and you live out the whole scene again, even without adding duration. <br /> <br /> This is like teleportation - which is lasting despite Patterning spells (in creative thaumatergy) normally never being lasting.<br /> <br /> But also like all fraying spells which do direct damage. If you cast it with 3 potency and go back 3 turns (the default for primary factors) why would you expect to need to add three turns of duration aswell? <br /> <br /> Whereas Corridors explicitly says you remain back in time for spell duration (despite being a potency spell which it is because you have to overcome Temporal sympathy withstand - unless you only go back to unchanged).<br /> <br /> But if I'm wrong it seems pretty annoying to roleplay, eg: by default it is potency 3, sending you back 3 turns (9 seconds) and 1 duration (3 seconds). If done in combat you go back 3 turns, at one turn, and then have the Storyteller handwave what happens in the other 2 turns? Or just play them out with everyone playing past versions of themselves as the time traveller is gone?<br /> <br /> It seems to make more sense to just play all 3 turns again, with one character having future knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For now, all we can be sure is that both Shifting Sands and Corridors of Time do not allow one person to exist simultaneously at one point.)<br /> <br /> But before that; I\u2019m not sure why you thought the Withstand rating here is important? Once it\u2019s overcome, it\u2019s overcome. </div> </div> </div>Yes, i think i have been convinced that you remain in your own body - even though in one case you bring your older body with you.<br /> <br /> It is only notable because with potency primary and 5 dots of time, you, by default have overcome the highest withstand from Temporal sympathy (unless the target is warded i guess). I guess it is still important because you need sensory range, a yantra slot and 1 mana to go back. But the relevance here was the examples of what a weak sympathic connection is.<br /> <br /> While for shifting sands, you're fraying time. Not using Temporal sympathy at all... You go back in your own timeline with your whole body as it is in the 'present'. <br /> <br /> That part seemed relevant when i was interpreting it as allowing - no requiring - body doubling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-15-2022, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T05:55:14-08:00","id":1474729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474710#post1474710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'It works like time travel' suggests there is a set way that time travel works.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/902581-questions-about-temporal-sympathy-and-time-magic?p=904306#post904306\">Because there is</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T09:01:09-08:00","id":1474740,"title":"","content":"This question is really seperate, so new post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474664#post1474664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Constant Presence triggers a Clash once the subject's history would be altered, and if Constant Presence wins the Clash then the subject &amp;quot;jumps&amp;quot; from its pre-altered present to the altered present in its pre-altered state, thus preserving it against temporal meddling.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the 'once the subject's history is altered' is the only unclear bit. Is that the point in the 'present' when the other spell becomes lasting? Or for Corridors of time, the point in the 'past' where their spell duration ends? <br /> <br /> Or can you cast it earlier, when they first detect Timey windy nonsense going on? So they would be constantly in a different timeline and unable to interact with the time traveller (as they constantly updated to bring in their original timeline location/state) - that one seems wrong, but otherwise we have A goes back in time and B notices something is different. B casts Constant Presence and nothing happens, time still seems different to B, who can still see weird alternative timeline Shenanigans going on. A's spell ends but is not lasting yet? A is gone so B is sitting there with a constant presence on waiting for the timeline to settle... <br /> <br /> Or B cancels her spell and uses prophecy to determine when would be the right time to cast it again in order to avoid being affected? B lives in the altered timeline for a few years and decided she doesn't want to risk losing all she has lived through and decided not to cast constant presence.<br /> <br /> Very strange...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T09:11:49-08:00","id":1474741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474729#post1474729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a pity that is not what is written <b>in the book</b> (or the FAQ). Especially when there is a section describing how time travel works at the start of the Time Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Also, Dave appears to be wrong when he says <br /> &quot;It's just that most people, when using Shifting Sands, will hit the present before the spell runs out of Duration&quot; - because by default the potency is 3-5 turns back on time and the duration is 1 turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-15-2022, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T17:38:21-08:00","id":1474764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474741#post1474741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It's just that most people, when using Shifting Sands, will hit the present before the spell runs out of Duration&quot; - because by default the potency is 3-5 turns back on time and the duration is 1 turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>By default the spell does nothing for you if you're Giant thanks to how Scale factors work, but mages who're really big will ostensibly still use the spell if they have the need for it. More to the point, by default the Potency is 1 and you get optional freebies that let you bump that up as high as 3-5 before you need to take penalties, which you don't have to use.<br /> <br /> Most mages use spell factors beyond the freebies. There are plenty of spells in the corebook, especially from Practices at or above Disciple-level, whose &quot;default&quot; factors will result in very little practical benefit.<br /> <br /> I am not interested in arguing this point with you and this is not the thread for it. Run it how you like if you both don't want to negotiate turn-by-turn outcomes and don't want players to take penalties or use less than the maximum effect of the spell, but the way time travel works is established in the Arcanum writeup and it's sufficiently non-analogous to teleportation that it's clearly a reach to assume Shifting Sands' base effect is Lasting just because you find it inconvenient to run its minimal uses a particular way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T18:17:33-08:00","id":1474765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474740#post1474740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the 'once the subject's history is altered' is the only unclear bit. Is that the point in the 'present' when the other spell becomes lasting? Or for Corridors of time, the point in the 'past' where their spell duration ends?<br /> <br /> Or can you cast it earlier, when they first detect Timey windy nonsense going on? So they would be constantly in a different timeline and unable to interact with the time traveller (as they constantly updated to bring in their original timeline location/state) - that one seems wrong, but otherwise we have A goes back in time and B notices something is different. B casts Constant Presence and nothing happens, time still seems different to B, who can still see weird alternative timeline Shenanigans going on. A's spell ends but is not lasting yet? A is gone so B is sitting there with a constant presence on waiting for the timeline to settle...<br /> <br /> Or B cancels her spell and uses prophecy to determine when would be the right time to cast it again in order to avoid being affected? B lives in the altered timeline for a few years and decided she doesn't want to risk losing all she has lived through and decided not to cast constant presence.<br /> <br /> Very strange...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oukronia the Master Enchanter is training a couple of Disciples and wards her Sanctum against historical revision to keep its contents in order, casting Constant Presence on the area before the exercise begins. Her students travel back in time a scene or two to play time-detective with each other's alterations to the past and see if they can track each other down by following their respective breadcrumb trails, potentially drastically changing the nature of the building. Once their spells' Duration runs out and/or they catch up to the present, history begins to settle and a Clash of Wills ensues; if Oukronia wins the Clash, her Sanctum reverts to the state it would have been in in the present where its history was not altered \u2014 it's effectively picked up and re-placed following the ripple effect of finalized time alteration.<br /> <br /> Alternately, Unicorn the 5D Chess Champ walks into Oukronia's Sanctum knowing her students plan to ambush him in the past, and so he casts Constant Presence on himself to keep them from looping their way into a tactical coup once they've seen him establish his route into the main hall. One of the Disciples casts Shifting Sands and snipes him from a far window, mortally wounding him, and when they return to the present, if Unicorn wins the Clash he doesn't have a bullet in his head.<br /> <br /> &quot;Travelers are insulated against the alterations of history&quot; is the quality Constant Presence is leveraging in its return; as long as the spell's Duration is running, the present version of the subject is the version of it that will exist when someone alters its history and then returns to the present. The talk about the tell-tale signs of disruption in the spell's initial description seems to be more about the fact that Time mages can spot the work of time travelers and like to have insurance against it \u2014 past versions of a character pulling themselves forward in response to meddling would seem to be the opposite of the spell's intent, in addition to functionally being a bootleg version of Temporal Stutter with free Duration.<br /> <br /> There is nothing to indicate any sort of alternate timeline shenanigans are the intended reading of the mechanics; spells to read the future cast in the past show the &quot;future&quot; as it unfolded into the present the time-traveler came from, but unless you're looking at an event with Time Sight there's no sign that it's any different from what was going to happen other than any foreknowledge you already had, which is normally imperfect on account of the way magical precognition works in the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T12:33:26-08:00","id":1474819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474765#post1474765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oukronia the Master Enchanter is training a couple of Disciples and wards her Sanctum against historical revision to keep its contents in order, casting Constant Presence on the area before the exercise begins. Her students travel back in time a scene or two to play time-detective with each other's alterations to the past and see if they can track each other down by following their respective breadcrumb trails, potentially drastically changing the nature of the building. Once their spells' Duration runs out and/or they catch up to the present, history begins to settle and a Clash of Wills ensues; if Oukronia wins the Clash, her Sanctum reverts to the state it would have been in in the present where its history was not altered \u2014 it's effectively picked up and re-placed following the ripple effect of finalized time alteration.<br /> <br /> Alternately, Unicorn the 5D Chess Champ walks into Oukronia's Sanctum knowing her students plan to ambush him in the past, and so he casts Constant Presence on himself to keep them from looping their way into a tactical coup once they've seen him establish his route into the main hall. One of the Disciples casts Shifting Sands and snipes him from a far window, mortally wounding him, and when they return to the present, if Unicorn wins the Clash he doesn't have a bullet in his head.<br /> <br /> &quot;Travelers are insulated against the alterations of history&quot; is the quality Constant Presence is leveraging in its return; as long as the spell's Duration is running, the present version of the subject is the version of it that will exist when someone alters its history and then returns to the present. The talk about the tell-tale signs of disruption in the spell's initial description seems to be more about the fact that Time mages can spot the work of time travelers and like to have insurance against it \u2014 past versions of a character pulling themselves forward in response to meddling would seem to be the opposite of the spell's intent, in addition to functionally being a bootleg version of Temporal Stutter with free Duration.<br /> <br /> There is nothing to indicate any sort of alternate timeline shenanigans are the intended reading of the mechanics; spells to read the future cast in the past show the &quot;future&quot; as it unfolded into the present the time-traveler came from, but unless you're looking at an event with Time Sight there's no sign that it's any different from what was going to happen other than any foreknowledge you already had, which is normally imperfect on account of the way magical precognition works in the present.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One question please, wouldn't Unicorn only be protected from the first attempt at altering his history. Whether he wins the Clash of Wills or not, Shielding spells only protect against the first [Potency] supernatural attempts to cause effects under the Arcanum's purview, correct ? So in theory sheer attrition could shatter the Shield, meaning that, if they have a second Hung version of <i>Shifting Sands</i>, then they would be defenseless against the rewrite unless they had cast <i>Constant Presence</i> with a higher Potency ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T14:00:19-08:00","id":1474823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474819#post1474819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shielding spells only protect against the first [Potency] supernatural attempts to cause effects under the Arcanum's purview, correct ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The mention of using Potency that way in the book is a leftover from an earlier version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T14:01:49-08:00","id":1474824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474823#post1474823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. The mention of using Potency that way in the book is a leftover from an earlier version.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So its just fully applicable until the duration elapses ? Cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T16:06:48-08:00","id":1474826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474765#post1474765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oukronia the Master Enchanter is training a couple of Disciples and wards her Sanctum against historical revision to keep its contents in order, casting Constant Presence on the area before the exercise begins. Her students travel back in time a scene or two to play time-detective with each other's alterations to the past and see if they can track each other down by following their respective breadcrumb trails, potentially drastically changing the nature of the building. Once their spells' Duration runs out and/or they catch up to the present, history begins to settle and a Clash of Wills ensues; if Oukronia wins the Clash, her Sanctum reverts to the state it would have been in in the present where its history was not altered \u2014 it's effectively picked up and re-placed following the ripple effect of finalized time alteration.<br /> <br /> Alternately, Unicorn the 5D Chess Champ walks into Oukronia's Sanctum knowing her students plan to ambush him in the past, and so he casts Constant Presence on himself to keep them from looping their way into a tactical coup once they've seen him establish his route into the main hall. One of the Disciples casts Shifting Sands and snipes him from a far window, mortally wounding him, and when they return to the present, if Unicorn wins the Clash he doesn't have a bullet in his head.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Travelers are insulated against the alterations of history&amp;quot; is the quality Constant Presence is leveraging in its return; as long as the spell's Duration is running, the present version of the subject is the version of it that will exist when someone alters its history and then returns to the present. The talk about the tell-tale signs of disruption in the spell's initial description seems to be more about the fact that Time mages can spot the work of time travelers and like to have insurance against it \u2014 past versions of a character pulling themselves forward in response to meddling would seem to be the opposite of the spell's intent, in addition to functionally being a bootleg version of Temporal Stutter with free Duration.<br /> <br /> There is nothing to indicate any sort of alternate timeline shenanigans are the intended reading of the mechanics; spells to read the future cast in the past show the &amp;quot;future&amp;quot; as it unfolded into the present the time-traveler came from, but unless you're looking at an event with Time Sight there's no sign that it's any different from what was going to happen other than any foreknowledge you already had, which is normally imperfect on account of the way magical precognition works in the present.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally have no idea what your point is with half of these examples. Is it just, you cast constant presence, then someone else changes time within the duration of your spell, and you clash to be unaffected by the effects (which become lasting at the point from their perspective - when the duration of their spell ends, or they catch up to the present - which from your perspective is the same instant as they cast the spell).<br /> <br /> Is that what you're trying to say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T16:19:07-08:00","id":1474827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474824#post1474824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So its just fully applicable until the duration elapses ? Cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the way all of the sheilding spells are written.<br /> <br /> It is only in a dangling paragraph on page 127 which probably contributed to it being overlooked.<br /> <br /> I think it is only Fate spells granting certain effects [potency] times within the duration of the spell. Whereas most Arcana grant a [potency] level effect for the whole duration of the spell. <br /> <br /> Cuts down on a lot of bookkeeping of you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T17:48:13-08:00","id":1474829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1473372#post1473372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for the Familiar Merit are on page 101 of the Mage 2e core rulebook.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Familiar&quot; spell can be found on page 183 of the Mage 2e core rulebook.<br /> <br /> The rules for Invisible Entities (which familiars are a subset of) start on page 252 of the Mage 2e core rulebook, with a sidebar on familiars on page 253; the Familiar Manifestation Condition is described on page 260.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So if you have a Rank 2 Ghost familiar, is there somewhere that explains stats and/or Numina? Or a baseline of how/what exactly you can do with said familiar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T18:57:55-08:00","id":1474832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474826#post1474826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I literally have no idea what your point is with half of these examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote exactly two, so that's a promising rate of success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it just, you cast constant presence, then someone else changes time within the duration of your spell, and you clash to be unaffected by the effects (which become lasting at the point from their perspective - when the duration of their spell ends, or they catch up to the present - which from your perspective is the same instant as they cast the spell).<br /> <br /> Is that what you're trying to say? </div> </div> </div>The present is the present \u2014 it is a fixed point in time for time travelers, to which they return once they have stopped being able to make changes to the past, which means if Constant Presence's Duration is active at the point in the present that somebody casts a spell to travel back in time, and the subject(s) of Constant Presence have their history altered, a successful Clash roll causes the subject(s) to remain as they were at the point that the time travel spell was cast.<br /> <br /> The spell preserves the subject's present state against being altered by time travel for the Duration of the spell, which is exactly what it says it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474829#post1474829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you have a Rank 2 Ghost familiar, is there somewhere that explains stats and/or Numina?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for Invisible Entities (which familiars are a subset of) start on page 252 of the Mage 2e core rulebook.<br /> <br /> The rules for Invisible Entities' Traits begin on page 253, starting with Rank and Essence/Mana, then moving on to Attributes and (lack of/alternatives to) Skills, Advantages, and Other Traits (Corpus, Willpower, Initiative, Defense, Speed, Size, and Languages) on page 254. A discussion of Influence can be found on pages 257-258, in addition to the reference chart for Influence effects on page 256. Manifestations can be found on pages 258-261; sample Numina can be found on pages 261-263.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or a baseline of how/what exactly you can do with said familiar? </div> </div> </div>It is a being with whom you have a sufficiently positive relationship that it is not cutting off the connection afforded to the pair of you that relies on neither of you deciding to end that connection, and it has supernatural powers, at least partial intangibility to most of the world, and functional invisibility to the average person on the street, in addition to allowing you to see through its senses and thereby use its presence to cast spells on remote targets without needing to negotiate the limits of sympathetic range.<br /> <br /> If you have a Rank 2 ghost as a familiar, you have an invisible person with three to five discrete supernatural powers and the ability to at least Strengthen one category of thing, if not Manipulate that category of thing or Strengthen more than one category of thing, as well as at least two forms of inhabiting the world besides its default state of being able to walk through most walls and only being visible to people who can see ghosts. You can look through its eyes and hear through its ears and, with a little extra risk, cast on things it can perceive as though you were there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-16-2022, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T01:26:01-08:00","id":1474840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474832#post1474832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and functional invisibility to the average person on the street,</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one addition, the merit explicitly allows a variation where the familiar is fettered to an item or animal - though i suppose the familiar is still visible, and while fettered a spirit can only urge their animal, not directly control it.... But i sort of see that as the 'permanently visible' version of a familiar.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the familiar gets protection against essence bleed, and i thought a ghost would be freed to move around beyond it's anchors (or at least near to the mage) but i can't see that in the rules... Basically both the mage and the familiar gain some benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-17-2022, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T01:55:04-08:00","id":1474841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474832#post1474832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if Constant Presence's Duration is active at the point in the present that somebody casts a spell to travel back in time, and the subject(s) of Constant Presence have their history altered, a successful Clash roll causes the subject(s) to remain as they were at the point that the time travel spell was cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, very clear. I think it is very weak, but then 'having no way of knowing' - when it might be needed - may not be an issue for any Mage with a few dot in the Time arcanum...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-17-2022, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T03:50:31-08:00","id":1474842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474840#post1474840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one addition, the merit explicitly allows a variation where the familiar is fettered to an item or animal - though i suppose the familiar is still visible, and while fettered a spirit can only urge their animal, not directly control it.... But i sort of see that as the 'permanently visible' version of a familiar.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the familiar gets protection against essence bleed, and i thought a ghost would be freed to move around beyond it's anchors (or at least near to the mage) but i can't see that in the rules... Basically both the mage and the familiar gain some benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being fettered does not make an ephemeral entity visible. Not even to what it's fettered to.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are already free to move beyond their anchors. What's notable about the Anchor Condition is that it protects against Essence bleed, unlike both the Resonant and Infrastructure Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T11:26:49-08:00","id":1474858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474842#post1474842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being fettered does not make an ephemeral entity visible. Not even to what it's fettered to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but i think it becomes a bit blurry, if your pet cat has your cat spirit familiar fettered to it (and urging it) you can now imagine you are looking through your cat's eye. <br /> <br /> It mimics that familiar trope, and you may even refer your pet as your familiar - even if mechanically that is not the case. And the eyes you are seeing through are in the spirit twilight, and thus able to see things which a cat's eye can not...<br /> <br /> Not sure what happens if this kind of familiar tries to manifest, or indeed if they can't because they are fettered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ghosts are already free to move beyond their anchors. What's notable about the Anchor Condition is that it protects against Essence bleed, unlike both the Resonant and Infrastructure Conditions. </div> </div> </div>Of course, i had forgotten, thank you for that. So ghost familiars can move beyond their anchors without worrying about essence bleed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-17-2022, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T16:34:47-08:00","id":1474877,"title":"","content":"Should a mage take a vial of Underworld River water, would they require a Weaving for it to be used in the material side ? In addition, would Endless Bounty require conjunctional Death 4 to produce an infinite supply of it ? An example is to always have a stock of Lethe water to answer questions in an emergency or Seers using water from the Ocean of Fragments to brainwash Pentacle mages into serving their Order, all the while profiteering from the valuable memories they extract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T16:54:29-08:00","id":1474878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474877#post1474877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a mage take a vial of Underworld River water, would they require a Weaving for it to be used in the material side ? In addition, would Endless Bounty require conjunctional Death 4 to produce an infinite supply of it ? An example is to always have a stock of Lethe water to answer questions in an emergency or Seers using water from the Ocean of Fragments to brainwash Pentacle mages into serving their Order, all the while profiteering from the valuable memories they extract.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t see why a Weaving would be needed simply to make it usable (as opposed to altering it). Was there anything specifically saying that River water loses its potency outside the Underworld?<br /> <br /> For Endless Bounty, I wouldn\u2019t say River water counts as a \u2018small expendable item\u2019 whose value can be represented easily via Resources. To get an infinite supply, I\u2019d probably do something like open a sympathetic Co-Located portal to a River. Hey, nothing could go wrong with wedging open a constant aperture between life and death, right\u2026?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T17:11:23-08:00","id":1474879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474878#post1474878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t see why a Weaving would be needed simply to make it usable (as opposed to altering it). Was there anything specifically saying that River water loses its potency outside the Underworld?<br /> <br /> For Endless Bounty, I wouldn\u2019t say River water counts as a \u2018small expendable item\u2019 whose value can be represented easily via Resources. To get an infinite supply, I\u2019d probably do something like open a sympathetic Co-Located portal to a River. Hey, nothing could go wrong with wedging open a constant aperture between life and death, right\u2026?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was guessing that perhaps taking the water back could place it in Death Twilight, but maybe its not a problem.<br /> <br /> I think that Endless Bounty just being able to replicate any water could have terrifying implications. Should any mage get one from the waters of Anahita, The River of Life, that would grant unlimited resurrections, healing and the cure to all diseases. It would probably be an incredibly dangerous quest, but might be worth it. I would also imagine particularly Wise archmages would make water jugs that endlessly and secretly resupply it, far away from any mages, just to prevent the scenario where the waters run dry and the Material collapses into the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T17:12:03-08:00","id":1474880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474878#post1474878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t see why a Weaving would be needed simply to make it usable (as opposed to altering it). Was there anything specifically saying that River water loses its potency outside the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a substance from the Underworld created from trickles of ghostly ephemera and Essence, it's almost certainly unusable for the vast majority without altering its Twilight property with Weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T17:27:20-08:00","id":1474881,"title":"","content":"I think making a supernatural substance function beyond its natural boundaries fits more under Perfecting. Depending on the usual rules for River water, taking it to the living world might require more Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T18:44:28-08:00","id":1474883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474880#post1474880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a substance from the Underworld created from trickles of ghostly ephemera and Essence, it's almost certainly unusable for the vast majority without altering its Twilight property with Weaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026 Yeah for some reason I completely forgot about Twilight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474881#post1474881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think making a supernatural substance function beyond its natural boundaries fits more under Perfecting. Depending on the usual rules for River water, taking it to the living world might require more Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, seeing how summoning spirits etc is Perfecting, \u2018summoning\u2019 a River could be too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T18:46:17-08:00","id":1474884,"title":"","content":"Arrgh, dam multi quote<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474879#post1474879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was guessing that perhaps taking the water back could place it in Death Twilight, but maybe its not a problem.<br /> <br /> I think that Endless Bounty just being able to replicate any water could have terrifying implications. Should any mage get one from the waters of Anahita, The River of Life, that would grant unlimited resurrections, healing and the cure to all diseases. It would probably be an incredibly dangerous quest, but might be worth it. I would also imagine particularly Wise archmages would make water jugs that endlessly and secretly resupply it, far away from any mages, just to prevent the scenario where the waters run dry and the Material collapses into the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still not sure about allowing Endless Bounty specifically, but all this sounds like something a Legacy and/or Nameless Order could be built out of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T01:10:12-08:00","id":1474891,"title":"","content":"I'm not really on board with Endless Bounty being able to make fonts of supernatural substance anyway, but even with its natural subjects I feel as though there should be certain limits to the viability of what it replicates. I'm not quite okay with the idea that you could take an enhanced gun clip and just slide the bullets out and hand them around. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking something like a ruling that it only really carries substance through the function of the container that it would be issued from. So it all holds together if you're using that magazine to constantly shoot bullets, but if you remove them to set aside for storage or sale, they won't last very long beyond the container.<br /> <br /> If it was something that worked on the water of the Ocean of Fragments, the vessel containing it would be the exclusive treasure of the pylon that ventured all the way down there to collect it and safely returned. It wouldn't be something they could distribute.<br /> <br /> Mind, Seers probably wouldn't share freely even if they could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T03:03:31-08:00","id":1474892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474891#post1474891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking something like a ruling that it only really carries substance through the function of the container that it would be issued from. So it all holds together if you're using that magazine to constantly shoot bullets, but if you remove them to set aside for storage or sale, they won't last very long beyond the container.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems perfectly reasonable ruling, for making your game more fun. But how would you describe it in terms of the rules for the magic system, for game consistenty?<br /> <br /> Like if it we're a Making effect over an area, anything leaving the area should cease to exist... Seems close to what you are describing, but not exactly. <br /> <br /> This spell is, what, ruling on the container (to not run out)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T07:17:21-08:00","id":1474899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474892#post1474892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems perfectly reasonable ruling, for making your game more fun. But how would you describe it in terms of the rules for the magic system, for game consistenty?<br /> <br /> Like if it we're a Making effect over an area, anything leaving the area should cease to exist... Seems close to what you are describing, but not exactly.<br /> <br /> This spell is, what, ruling on the container (to not run out)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Endless Bounty is a published spell in Signs of Sorcery, a Patterning Practice cast on containers of &quot;small, expendable items&quot; that ensures that they never run out for the Duration (with the initial item's value being Availability equal to Potency).<br /> <br /> I'd think of it as a transformation of the subject's nature as a container, both for simplicity and a basis for that idea to focus it on the stored item being expended according to intuitive functions. There's a bit of wiggle room, but not to excessive degrees; you could drown a person by putting an endless water bottle over their mouth, but try tipping it over to flood a room and you'll find a puddle of water that just kind of fades into nothing at the edges.<br /> <br /> This is the kind of thing I have in mind as an answer to that question in the other thread about explaining magic. I think something like making a dispenser endless is both a bit complicated and very simple; that is to say that complicated things might technically be happening to uphold the spell's effects, but the spell itself is very direct, and the caster does not need to account for all the details. You're not casting a spell to replicate the molecular structure of bullets, you're casting a spell that's making an adjustment to a magazine's property of &quot;containerness&quot;.<br /> <br /> And I think it's the kind of approach to the subject that would manage to be balanced and reasonably intuitive, while still ending up just arbitrary enough for some mages to be challenged with figuring out quite how spells work and what implications they might have for the nature of the Supernal and reality itself. Plus the occasional source of minor Mystery; you might not be able to bury somebody in hundred dollar bills flowing in a torrent from your wallet, but as long as you spend them naturally your supply is still inexhaustible and those bills might continue circulating around the economy, indistinguishable to anybody but a mage whose Sight can reveal the oddity of their origin. I'm suddenly thinking that a minor but interesting project for some mage might be gathering up all the bills that originated from the same enchanted wallet, long after the original spell ended, and seeing if anything happens if they're all placed together or put to a function that would have been outside the spell's parameters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T10:08:47-08:00","id":1474910,"title":"","content":"Thank you, lots of interesting ideas to chew through.<br /> <br /> The only minor quible is whether 100$ bills are expendable (as they retain their value after being used...). But i do wonder how much you could Rule an item to have similar effect, and what arcanum it would be (Matter i presume or is it another Arcanum's purview not the shaping/crafting/transmutation/alchemy of Matter?)- Could it also he a shielding against endings? Maybe stasis/change? Really hard to see how the 'container'-ness of an object dots any arcanum purivew... Could you use prime conjunctaively to use a magical container (like a soul jar?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T11:36:15-08:00","id":1474916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474910#post1474910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, lots of interesting ideas to chew through.<br /> <br /> The only minor quible is whether 100$ bills are expendable (as they retain their value after being used...). But i do wonder how much you could Rule an item to have similar effect, and what arcanum it would be (Matter i presume or is it another Arcanum's purview not the shaping/crafting/transmutation/alchemy of Matter?)- Could it also he a shielding against endings? Maybe stasis/change? Really hard to see how the 'container'-ness of an object dots any arcanum purivew... Could you use prime conjunctaively to use a magical container (like a soul jar?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not sure if the same effect could be accomplished with a Ruling. However, I did make <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1408432#post1408432\">a spell </a>some time ago leveraging Time and Fate to make a variation of a container that could accomplish this in an different manner, mixing an unlimted container with the capacity to use Schrodinger's items multiple times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T16:39:13-08:00","id":1474926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474916#post1474916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am not sure if the same effect could be accomplished with a Ruling. However, I did make <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1408432#post1408432&quot;]a</a> spell [/URL]some time ago leveraging Time and Fate to make a variation of a container that could accomplish this in an different manner, mixing an unlimted container with the capacity to use Schrodinger's items multiple times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Ruling could, nor should, be able to do the same, but how close it can come is my question. Like perhaps a Space Ruling to give a container more capacity - kinds like ground eater, but a more than Compelling.<br /> <br /> I like your haversack. Almost matched by pocket dimension (without any time) which you can use to pull items from Nowhere... Though as a Making spell it is pretty ludicrous to pull off - also doubles as an excellent holding cell/prison. And mimics a Temporal Stutter (which is what your haversack is conditionally using?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-20-2022, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T16:49:31-08:00","id":1474927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474926#post1474926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Ruling could, not should, be able to do the same, but how close it can come is my question. Like perhaps a Space Ruling to give a container more capacity - kinds like ground eater, but a more than Compelling.<br /> <br /> I like your haversack. Almost matched by pocket dimension (without any time) which you can use to pull items from Nowhere... Though as a Making spell it is pretty ludicrous to pull off - also doubles as an excellent holding cell/prison. And mimics a Temporal Stutter (which is what your haversack is conditionally using?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, its the result of asking the question &quot;how would an Acanthus make something like a bag of holding&quot; ? The answer I arrived at was they move the contents back and forth from the future, which could combo with the precision of Fate to make it even more convenient and discrete than a normal bag of holding. The Fate 4 ability is basically thinking of it as &quot;the box of Schrodinger's Cat&quot;, with both Arcana setting the result in an unusual way, allowing the mage to carry a huge amount of mundane utility (gas masks, food, duct tape, plastic bags, glowsticks, ammo, flare gun, changes of clothes, medicine and much more). The main constraint is that the item needs to fit inside the bag/backpack/trenchcoat, which means that asking a Mastigos to cast <i>Optimal Container</i> on it might be a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-18-2022, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T01:37:49-08:00","id":1474952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474927#post1474927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer I arrived at was they move the contents back and forth from the future</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very much not how the future works in this cosmology. The future doesn't exist until the present catches up with it, which is why traveling there requires removing yourself from time until the point you want to be in arrives.<br /> <br /> Also, the Schr\u00f6dinger's cat thought experiment isn't about the probability of a thing even being inside of the box, it's about uncertainty concerning the state of things that have already been verified to be inside of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T07:52:17-08:00","id":1474978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474952#post1474952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's very much not how the future works in this cosmology. The future doesn't exist until the present catches up with it, which is why traveling there requires removing yourself from time until the point you want to be in arrives.<br /> <br /> Also, the Schr\u00f6dinger's cat thought experiment isn't about the probability of a thing even being inside of the box, it's about uncertainty concerning the state of things that have already been verified to be inside of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I explained that poorly, its actually moving the contents out of the timeline and back in depending on what the user wants to store or retrieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:18:26-08:00","id":1474985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474978#post1474978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I explained that poorly, its actually moving the contents out of the timeline and back in depending on what the user wants to store or retrieve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that not just the basic Temporal Stutter spell being selectively switched off?<br /> <br /> Mind, I think your application would require the spell to have a mobility that they're not usually afforded, and I'm not sure there's a way to use the Time Arcanum to enchant a container that really makes sense with that effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:58:22-08:00","id":1474995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1474985#post1474985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that not just the basic Temporal Stutter spell being selectively switched off?<br /> <br /> Mind, I think your application would require the spell to have a mobility that they're not usually afforded, and I'm not sure there's a way to use the Time Arcanum to enchant a container that really makes sense with that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of it as a combination of altering the properties of a container (Weaving) to interact with the Arcanum by temporaly stuttering the contents (Patterning) and then using Fate's ability to read intentions (Unveiling) to decide what content is stuttered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T08:04:06-08:00","id":1475320,"title":"","content":"I think i know the answer to this, but I've searched the forums and i can't seem to find a clear answer.<br /> <br /> Temporal Sympathy (the attainment not the sympathy) says it needs :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the subject as it exists now, cast at sensory range, use a sympathy Yantra, and spend one Mana. </div> </div> </div>Contrasted by Sympathic Range which swaps the subject in the present for a sympathic connection to the subject.<br /> <br /> In both cases the attainments go on to say the spell is withstood by the strength of the sympathic connection (one spatial, one Temporal). <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the fragility of the temporal sympathy (p. 186) between the mage and her subject </div> </div> </div>Ok, makes sense, your spell uses that connection.<br /> <br /> Do i need a Temporal Sympathy between &quot;the mage and her subject&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T10:00:45-08:00","id":1475327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475320#post1475320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do i need a Temporal Sympathy between &quot;the mage and her subject&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is most probably erroneously copy-pasted from the Sympathetic Range Attainment. The mage does not require temporal sympathy between themselves and the subject because temporal sympathy can only exist between a subject and its own past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T12:44:13-08:00","id":1475348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475327#post1475327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This part is most probably erroneously copy-pasted from the Sympathetic Range Attainment. The mage does not require temporal sympathy between themselves and the subject because temporal sympathy can only exist between a subject and its own past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is my preferred understanding. The temporal sympathy section does discuss strengthen and destroy temporal sympathies, (like WebWeaver) and the emotional effects. <br /> <br /> This didn't come up in the FAQ? (I didn't re-read the thread to check).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T08:58:31-08:00","id":1475537,"title":"","content":"Conversation on another thread* makes me wonder about the inherent nature of ghosts. And practically iif Making a Ghost of a specific person should require a sympathic connection to the actual person.<br /> <br /> That said, my question, if a gun (say) has a strong sympathic connection to its owner, who dies, can you still use that connection to identify the owner (perhaps while investigating the death).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475536#post1475536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*From here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 02-27-2022, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T11:33:07-08:00","id":1475544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475537#post1475537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversation on another thread* makes me wonder about the inherent nature of ghosts. And practically iif Making a Ghost of a specific person should require a sympathic connection to the actual person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's reasonable enough for a sympathetic connection to provide relevant information or links to a deceased subject, although I think it would need to be done quickly. I'd say one side being dead is reasonable enough for the connection to start fading rapidly due to lack of engagement (barring cases where the connection is the result of something such as the item having itself been used to kill them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T11:50:34-08:00","id":1475547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475544#post1475544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's reasonable enough for a sympathetic connection to provide relevant information or links to a deceased subject, although I think it would need to be done quickly. I'd say one side being dead is reasonable enough for the connection to start fading rapidly due to lack of engagement (barring cases where the connection is the result of something such as the item having itself been used to kill them).</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems fair, an ancient relic buried with its owner probably has no connection? Or maybe after a few days in a museum collection it will have developed new connections to whoever found it, bought/sold it...<br /> <br /> Whereas a recently deceases person's wedding ring might hold onto its connection for how long?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T17:17:28-08:00","id":1475562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475547#post1475547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas a recently deceases person's wedding ring might hold onto its connection for how long?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an example such as that should vary according to numerous factors (such as what the nature of the marriage was) that are hard for an observing mage to effectively measure, and even then find that when comparing similar situations the links fade at different rates. Still, I think it would be reasonable for something like that to not generally hold the connection for longer than a year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T12:33:20-08:00","id":1475925,"title":"","content":"I can't seem to find this anywhere - how do you calculate the Merit rating of a Fetish if a mage wants one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T12:39:17-08:00","id":1475926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475925#post1475925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't seem to find this anywhere - how do you calculate the Merit rating of a Fetish if a mage wants one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetishes aren't dot rated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T14:04:27-08:00","id":1475935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475925#post1475925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't seem to find this anywhere - how do you calculate the Merit rating of a Fetish if a mage wants one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, an item with a Indefinite duration Fetish spell is just a four dot Enhanced Item.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T15:22:18-08:00","id":1475946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475926#post1475926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fetishes aren't dot rated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. So no way by RAW to get a Fetish at game start w/ sanctity of merits applied...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 03-06-2022, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T23:03:02-08:00","id":1475968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475946#post1475946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. So no way by RAW to get a Fetish at game start w/ sanctity of merits applied...</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The closest would be Enhanced Item at four dots as mentioned, but that's technically incorrect as it's supposed to be cast on existing items to enhance their properties, not on spirits to turn them into items with supernatural effects. Enhanced Item also has the problem that it doesn't say anything about Potency, which is the difference between a single dot Influence fetish and a fetish with a five dot Influence and up to 11 Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T00:49:30-08:00","id":1475972,"title":"","content":"In 1e you were allowed to buy a fetish as a merit. I would presume that you can use the merit from Werewolf if your storyteller agrees.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure though if they changed exactly how fetishes work in werewolf, or if mage's can still produce them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T01:34:44-08:00","id":1475974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1475972#post1475972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure though if they changed exactly how fetishes work in werewolf, or if mage's can still produce them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf fetishes have always worked different than mages. Mages just create items to harness some of the spirit's own powers, werewolves use spirits as a basis for creating objects with powers of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T14:38:18-08:00","id":1476001,"title":"","content":"So, maybe one merit dot per point of spell potency that would be required for the fetish would be workable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T14:44:40-08:00","id":1476228,"title":"","content":"How does Reach work on combined spells? You you get reach on each of them separately or all at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T15:19:18-08:00","id":1476230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476228#post1476228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Reach work on combined spells? You you get reach on each of them separately or all at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA 2e Core, p118-119</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free Reach is determined as normal. Reach to alter spell factors applied to all spells, but additional Reach effects in a spell's listing must be bought separately. Multiple spell effects must use the same scale unless the mage uses a Reach to separate the effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA 2e Core, p112</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character receives a <i>free</i> Reach \u2014 which does <i>not</i> add Paradox dice \u2014 per dot of her highest-rated Arcanum that meets or exceeds the spell's requirement. For example a mage with four dots of the Mind Arcanum gains two free Reaches when casting a spell that requires Mind 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T17:32:03-07:00","id":1476349,"title":"","content":"<br /> How could a mage find a meteor, asteroid or comet? Assuming he could only use Forces (or others arcanas). If it's not possible this way, how could it be done?<br /> Assuming he can't have mundane help (like technology). Only magical means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27342,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","user":"werikscs","date":". 03-13-2022, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T19:04:51-07:00","id":1476353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476349#post1476349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How could a mage find a meteor, asteroid or comet? Assuming he could only use Forces (or others arcanas). If it's not possible this way, how could it be done?<br /> Assuming he can't have mundane help (like technology). Only magical means.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Find as in detecting them in space? I'm not sure they could; they're probably not subjects in visual range to have spells cast on them, and they're further than the distance Forces enhanced vision can effectively see out to.<br /> <br /> I think a mage's best bet for knowing where distant cosmic objects are is to go to the Sidereal Wastes in the Astral Anima Mundi and find beings that can inform them, or journey about looking for their targets manually; they'll experience the journey as though it was taking as long as it would to traverse such distance, but time in reality will pass much more conveniently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T20:52:51-07:00","id":1476356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476353#post1476353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Find as in detecting them in space? I'm not sure they could; they're probably not subjects in visual range to have spells cast on them, and they're further than the distance Forces enhanced vision can effectively see out to.<br /> <br /> I think a mage's best bet for knowing where distant cosmic objects are is to go to the Sidereal Wastes in the Astral Anima Mundi and find beings that can inform them, or journey about looking for their targets manually; they'll experience the journey as though it was taking as long as it would to traverse such distance, but time in reality will pass much more conveniently.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I disagree. People have found such things with the naked eye. Forces enhanced sight, and maybe a unveiling to clear out distortions caused atmospheric conditions, and it could happen. Depends on the Mage\u2019s knowledge of physics, to recognize what they should look for, and how many nights they are willing to look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T21:15:08-07:00","id":1476359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476356#post1476356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, I disagree. People have found such things with the naked eye. Forces enhanced sight, and maybe a unveiling to clear out distortions caused atmospheric conditions, and it could happen. Depends on the Mage\u2019s knowledge of physics, to recognize what they should look for, and how many nights they are willing to look.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would also depend a lot on the object's size and distance, so while it is possible I would say <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> is right in practice more than not.<br /> <br /> Either way, one option is to use Fate and Time to examine a region you think may be affected by a meteor somehow in the future. Easier for those actually hitting Earth, but still possible to do if you predict visible passing through an area in the sky or some gravitational interference on something you can target more easily. But then, again, actual knowledge in astrophysics would help a lot to have ideas on what to look for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T07:47:52-07:00","id":1476379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476356#post1476356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have found such things with the naked eye. Forces enhanced sight, and maybe a unveiling to clear out distortions caused atmospheric conditions</div> </div> </div> </div>An additional spell isn't strictly necessary, Zoom In has a Reach condition to remove the penalties from atmospheric conditions. <br /> <br /> However, at best it can provide clear vision only up to five miles, so past that you're no better off looking with the naked eye than any Sleeper would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Either way, one option is to use Fate and Time to examine a region you think may be affected by a meteor somehow in the future. Easier for those actually hitting Earth, but still possible to do if you predict visible passing through an area in the sky or some gravitational interference on something you can target more easily.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Hmm, I think the description of sensory range ends up being a bit ambiguous about being able to cast spells on regions of the universe that are technically visible in the night sky. For me it becomes a question of whether such an area so distant can be regarded as being viewed directly. Plus, area factors would still apply; you might be able to divine the future of a cube of empty space the size of a few city blocks several million miles away, but that's such a small section of the whole, the odds that you've targeted somewhere that anything will ever pass through still become rather small. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T10:42:30-07:00","id":1476387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476379#post1476379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An additional spell isn't strictly necessary, Zoom In has a Reach condition to remove the penalties from atmospheric conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Whoops, forgot about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476379#post1476379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, at best it can provide clear vision only up to five miles, so past that you're no better off looking with the naked eye than any Sleeper would be.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is there a particular reason why we can\u2019t make a lens with Forces that has a arbitrary great resolving power and magnification? It should just be a wide area Control Light.<br /> <br /> Edit: or maybe just allow further reach on Zoom In to grant further resolving power, like maybe +2 or +3 reach for light seconds, then another reach for light minutes and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-14-2022, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T18:11:03-07:00","id":1476405,"title":"","content":"<br /> Is it possible to use forces to translate one heard language into another? Could it be the weaving practice to change the sound waves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T18:26:00-07:00","id":1476409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476405#post1476405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to use forces to translate one heard language into another? Could it be the weaving practice to change the sound waves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean by \u2018translating\u2019. If you know both Language A and Language B, then you should be able to use Control Sounds (Forces 2 Ruling) to change words spoken in A to B (and vice-versa)\u2026 But in this case, you are the one who\u2019s doing the actual translation of meaning here.<br /> <br /> To make the spell do live translation on demand, Mind or Prime would be needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T20:31:18-07:00","id":1476414,"title":"","content":"Could someone give me a valid example of Action Yantra to be the target that will receive the 9-again effect with the spell As Above, So Below? Is it possible to use Concentration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T22:45:14-07:00","id":1476416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476414#post1476414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone give me a valid example of Action Yantra to be the target that will receive the 9-again effect with the spell As Above, So Below? Is it possible to use Concentration?</div> </div> </div> </div> Pouring holy water on the subject, giving a blessing in High Speech, knighting them with a sword. For less Obrimos examples, perhaps anointing with a admixture of silver and holly, or a giving a wreath of lilac. Generally, go for symbolism that is positive, like a gift or a blessing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476414#post1476414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to use Concentration?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. I believe everything with a duration past instant works with Concentration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-15-2022, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T00:28:48-07:00","id":1476419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476379#post1476379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I think the description of sensory range ends up being a bit ambiguous about being able to cast spells on regions of the universe that are technically visible in the night sky. For me it becomes a question of whether such an area so distant can be regarded as being viewed directly. Plus, area factors would still apply; you might be able to divine the future of a cube of empty space the size of a few city blocks several million miles away, but that's such a small section of the whole, the odds that you've targeted somewhere that anything will ever pass through still become rather small.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is ambiguous, quite the opposite.<br /> <br /> The thing is, while thinking it in terms of distance is intuitive, it not only isn't necessarily true for the Supernal, it also isn't interesting from the perspective of game design.<br /> <br /> What you accomplish by setting this limitation? You just define an entire set of phenomena as outside the purview of the game entirely. While mundane astronomers derive huge amounts of data about the universe at large out of puny instruments barely suited for the task (and that's basically their own opinion), Mages are stuck with astrological maps at the best of days.<br /> <br /> So the definition is actually very practical: if you can perceive something, you can investigate it with magic and bring it to the game. The great distances only make space work as a parallel to other worlds, you need specific forms of interaction to deal with it, but that's all.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of the fiction, to see something is to see an aspect of its supernal Truth. You glimpse Supernal Symbols of all kinds in every thing you see around you, why it would be different with the distant lights in the night sky? Specially, again, when mundane humans are so capable of deriving truth and meaning from them that astronomy is possibly the oldest science, with ancient societies developing calendars, sometimes even predicting eclipses, before they learned how to write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T01:54:27-07:00","id":1476423,"title":"","content":"I think the best way to find astronomical (and astrological) phenomena is to use Fate.<br /> In general, spells can only grant knowledge about specific subjects or within limited areas (which is why scanning the sky bit by bit is required with most Arcana) or impart knowledge to specific subjects. Fate is great for imparting knowledge about things you haven't or can't target with a spell, and I'd definitely put astronomy and astrology under Fate due to their age old connotations with fates, destinies, predictions, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476419#post1476419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[..]with ancient societies developing calendars, sometimes even predicting eclipses, before they learned how to write.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before they invented writing, is a more fair way to put it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T04:42:56-07:00","id":1476426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476416#post1476416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Pouring holy water on the subject, giving a blessing in High Speech, knighting them with a sword. For less Obrimos examples, perhaps anointing with a admixture of silver and holly, or a giving a wreath of lilac. Generally, go for symbolism that is positive, like a gift or a blessing.<br /> <br /> Yes. I believe everything with a duration past instant works with Concentration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I didn't make it clear what I meant. I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> On page 167, and in the spell (As Above, So Below) description, it says:<br /> <br /> For every level of Potency, she chooses a single Yantra (and it must be a specific example of a Yantra, not just a category: \u201cthe Crypt of the Mariner,\u201d not just \u201cEnvironment\u201d).<br /> <br /> The book classifies Yantra into categories. The main categories are Place, Actions, Tools and Dedicated Tools.<br /> <br /> The Yantra used in the spell description As Above, So Below, Environment, is of category Place. But as the spell says, it need to be more specific.<br /> <br /> So, I would like to know specific actions for Yantras from Action category. Like: Concentration, Mantras, Mudras and Runes. I would like to use them as target of the mentioned spell, but I can't think of anything specific to fulfill the spell requirement.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your patience, guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27342,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","user":"werikscs","date":". 03-15-2022, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T06:14:26-07:00","id":1476427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476419#post1476419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is ambiguous, quite the opposite.<br /> <br /> The thing is, while thinking it in terms of distance</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about distance, it's about levels of resolution. If you observe the Earth from the moon, can you cast a spell on any building that technically lies within your line of sight, even if it's not even small enough to be a speck?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you accomplish by setting this limitation? You just define an entire set of phenomena as outside the purview of the game entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Opening portals to stars millions of light years away is a bit of silliness it's better to put the kibosh on so that everybody can stay focused rather than trying to stretch things to clever edge cases. Avoid more conversations like conjuring up Hemingway books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While mundane astronomers derive huge amounts of data about the universe at large out of puny instruments barely suited for the task (and that's basically their own opinion), Mages are stuck with astrological maps at the best of days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortal long distance communication isn't dependant on deep personal relationships either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the definition is actually very practical: if you can perceive something, you can investigate it with magic and bring it to the game. The great distances only make space work as a parallel to other worlds, you need specific forms of interaction to deal with it, but that's all.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of the fiction, to see something is to see an aspect of its supernal Truth. You glimpse Supernal Symbols of all kinds in every thing you see around you, why it would be different with the distant lights in the night sky? Specially, again, when mundane humans are so capable of deriving truth and meaning from them that astronomy is possibly the oldest science, with ancient societies developing calendars, sometimes even predicting eclipses, before they learned how to write.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even apart from the question of whether looking at something in the night sky makes it valid to cast at, the game already introduces cases where magic doesn't work properly. In just the core book there are Tokyo's anshos and the fleeting worlds. Dark Eras 2 had Mysteries around complications in casting transportation magic on Caribbean islands or across North America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T06:20:43-07:00","id":1476429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476426#post1476426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I would like to know specific actions for Yantras from Action category. Like: Concentration, Mantras, Mudras and Runes. I would like to use them as target of the mentioned spell, but I can't think of anything specific to fulfill the spell requirement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit uncertain if an action can be a target for the spell in the first place, it's not really a pre-existing subject to enchant. Still:<br /> <br /> High Speech incantation that could only apply to some specific set of spells; you can get a few applications out of saying the equivalent of &quot;fire walk with me&quot;, but you're not turning a dog into a slightly different breed of dog with it.<br /> <br /> Concentration and runes are just slight variations on that.<br /> <br /> Designate a particular set of mudras and the kinds of rotes that they're encoded to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T07:02:46-07:00","id":1476432,"title":"","content":"I remember something from Werewolf, about how the planetary angels (spirits serving the great planets) are more like spirits of <i>light</i> reflected from the planets, not derived from the planet\u2019s aspects per se. Related to that, we already know via modern science how distances measured in outer space tend to be messy with \u201cAre we really seeing it, not just the light from it a few ages ago?\u201d<br /> <br /> And as mentioned above, Dark Eras show us something relatively \u2018small\u2019 as the Ocean can mess with magic.<br /> <br /> With all those points, directly casting spells on celestial bodies/phenomena we observe may be impossible, even for simple spells\u2026 impossible via <i>normal</i> magic, of course. Until future canon says something otherwise, I suggest \u2018locking\u2019 these feats behind Artifacts, Archmastery, Ascended grace, and maybe Legacy Attainments. (Hey, the Thrice-Great are supposed to major in Forces according to DaveB if IIRC\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T07:21:40-07:00","id":1476434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476427#post1476427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about distance, it's about levels of resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>A spell that targets a planet or star without better defining a place within it doesn't need better resolution than seeing the entire star as a spec itself. The example that set this tangent was to simply locate a meteor.<br /> <br /> Some cases are absurd by themselves. You can't affect an star planet with an area spell just because it looks like a spec for you, and you can't pinpoint a target you can't perceive just because you can see the planet or the area in space your target is in. In such instances, you're just arguing things no one said.<br /> <br /> But if a spell can target a place without specifying a location in that place, then it logically works as normal. Locating where in your visible field a specific spec of light will appear isn't that much of a stretch, and the fact the spec itself is astronomically far and big is meaningless for the task.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476427#post1476427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. Opening portals to stars millions of light years away is a bit of silliness it's better to put the kibosh on so that everybody can stay focused rather than trying to stretch things to clever edge cases. Avoid more conversations like conjuring up Hemingway books.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's a valid approach, I don't think it is the intent of the system, at least not in this manner. Keeping the game from ever dealing with space because you think it is silly seems a little too far, it's an overreaction to overblown expectations on what players will do with such things.<br /> <br /> Mage is about people that focus on their own Obsessions all the time, you're simply pre-determining one such obsession as off-limits, because?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476427#post1476427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal long distance communication isn't dependant on deep personal relationships either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't got the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476427#post1476427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even apart from the question of whether looking at something in the night sky makes it valid to cast at, the game already introduces cases where magic doesn't work properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that has no relation to the question. It just means you're on your right to define it, or anything else, as an exclusion case.<br /> <br /> No book defined space or the sky as an exclusion case (or said it isn't), and your argument was that targeting space seemed like lack of clarity on the rules. It isn't lack of clarity, it enables working anything in the game if the group wants to. If the ST don't want to, then you just define it as an exclusion case.<br /> <br /> While I usually agree with you, and also dealt with silly questions from people in the forum wanting to explore material space in the game, the notion that the game <b>should</b> write off the possibility, or that it is somehow implied, just isn't in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T09:38:24-07:00","id":1476438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476426#post1476426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I didn't make it clear what I meant. I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> On page 167, and in the spell (As Above, So Below) description, it says:<br /> <br /> For every level of Potency, she chooses a single Yantra (and it must be a specific example of a Yantra, not just a category: \u201cthe Crypt of the Mariner,\u201d not just \u201cEnvironment\u201d).<br /> <br /> The book classifies Yantra into categories. The main categories are Place, Actions, Tools and Dedicated Tools.<br /> <br /> The Yantra used in the spell description As Above, So Below, Environment, is of category Place. But as the spell says, it need to be more specific.<br /> <br /> So, I would like to know specific actions for Yantras from Action category. Like: Concentration, Mantras, Mudras and Runes. I would like to use them as target of the mentioned spell, but I can't think of anything specific to fulfill the spell requirement.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your patience, guys!</div> </div> </div> </div> Ooooh. Yeah, sure, why not? Just use yourself as the subject for action yantras, since you would be performing the action. It\u2019s a bit like targeting the book, when the important part is the words.<br /> <br /> Edit: Forget to check if anyone else had answered, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-15-2022, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T18:44:13-07:00","id":1476484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476434#post1476434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Locating where in your visible field</div> </div> </div> </div>At least some of this is based on a question of whether certain things coherently count as being within somebody's visible field.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage is about people that focus on their own Obsessions all the time, you're simply pre-determining one such obsession as off-limits, because?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, questions about applying magic to space have come up before, and the very salient point has been made that it's a pretty messy thing to make a game about just on the basis of how it's very far removed from engagement with setting or dramatic systems. I think it would be a bit like how there's a Science Skill, but Chronicles of Darkness is not really set up to tell stories of characters spending five years doing the kind of research that entails meticulously gathering slight variations in data and recalibrating instruments to develop their models.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm not really saying that mages with Obsessions about the cosmos should be off limits, just that it might require more steps than looking up into the night sky and being able to cast spells on anything up there.<br /> <br /> That and I do think the premise has some more practical applications that should be curtailed. I don't think a mage should be able to freely cast on anything that might be within their line of sight from the top of a skyscraper even if they can't make it out individually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't got the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic has rules that impose some limits on it, things that Sleepers can make without it don't do much as a standard to measure against.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T19:37:13-07:00","id":1476488,"title":"","content":"A Bay City Marshal who is friendly with a Changeling Court besides the Leafless Tree would represent that through what merit, if any? Say, a Marshal has a good reputation with the Court of Favors, would that be Ally 1 (Court of Favors)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T20:00:00-07:00","id":1476491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476488#post1476488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Bay City Marshal who is friendly with a Changeling Court besides the Leafless Tree would represent that through what merit, if any? Say, a Marshal has a good reputation with the Court of Favors, would that be Ally 1 (Court of Favors)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the primary salient benefit of having a dot of Court Goodwill with a changeling court, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T21:51:18-07:00","id":1476818,"title":"","content":"Can there be such a thing as a spirit of a specific linage? (Perhaps what is commonly referred to as a ancestor spirit?) (I understand there is no such thing as a human spirit, but apparently spirits of nations exist?)<br /> Assuming they do exist, would there be anything special about those spirits who resonate with Proximi?<br /> On a somewhat related note, are there any Death/Spirit focused Thyrsus legacies? I\u2019m interested in seeing how the path understands ghosts in the context of their relation to spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T22:34:07-07:00","id":1476822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476818#post1476818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can there be such a thing as a spirit of a specific linage? (Perhaps what is commonly referred to as a ancestor spirit?) (I understand there is no such thing as a human spirit, but apparently spirits of nations exist?)<br /> Assuming they do exist, would there be anything special about those spirits who resonate with Proximi?<br /> On a somewhat related note, are there any Death/Spirit focused Thyrsus legacies? I\u2019m interested in seeing how the path understands ghosts in the context of their relation to spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even if there were, I suspect they'll go <i>magath</i> pretty quick. And to begin with, I'd say the lineage in question will need some 'public weight' for spirits to form around them, as it seems to be the case for cities and nations. So a super important and powerful lineage that also happens to be super secret likely won't have a spirit representing them. You'll have better luck looking for Goetia, or spirits of certain aspects that the lineage involves themselves with. (A lineage of assassins may be long-term allies with a Murder spirit, for instance.)<br /> <br /> By anything special, would you be thinking about Influences? &quot;Magic&quot; is one of those things that are too diverse and broad to be represented as a single purview, I think. It'll be like having a spirit of Emotions. So Proximus-lineage-spirits shouldn't have something like &quot;Magic&quot; as an Influence, not even &quot;Acanthus Magic&quot; or &quot;Curse Magic&quot;, for example. But say, a spirit aligned with the Sisters of the Mountain for instance should have Influences over Hills, Herbs, Healing, etc.<br /> <br /> Oh, but then again, IIRC Dark Eras had a case of allowing Countermagic as a Numen, so spirits who had extensive relationships with mages could develop Numina that roughly interact with Awakened magic.<br /> <br /> Dunno about ghost/Death-focused Thyrsus. Seems like an unexplored space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Clarity 03-21-2022, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T06:06:29-07:00","id":1476839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476818#post1476818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can there be such a thing as a spirit of a specific linage? (Perhaps what is commonly referred to as a ancestor spirit?) (I understand there is no such thing as a human spirit, but apparently spirits of nations exist?)</div> </div> </div> </div>They were a recurring thing in Werewolf 1e, though 2e hasn't really mentioned them all that much. Nation-spirits have likewise gone relatively unremarked-upon since the earlier days of 1e.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming they do exist, would there be anything special about those spirits who resonate with Proximi? </div> </div> </div>Like any spirit, that would depend heavily upon the history of the thing. Some could be little more than ordinary spirits who've lent their patronage to a family, others could be pulling something similar to reaping the benefits of a pack bond, still others could be the spiritual reflection of an influential family in their entirety. The Shadow gets weird, but for the most part it deals in resonances that aren't people or subtypes thereof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T08:34:10-07:00","id":1476846,"title":"","content":"I think you could put spirits in for ancestral lineages, but they'd be an uncommon thing that probably mostly get involved with families that already have particular ties to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Although I think like... the Werewolf: the Forsaken ones were kind of supposed to be something that Uratha actually turned into? It looks to me like an artefact of a time when Forsaken was going a bit more for retaining the idea of consolidated and cultivated family lines of werewolves, which I find Second Edition to have all but dropped completely (there's still a hereditary aspect, it just doesn't seem to be given any wider impact beyond &quot;sometimes your kids or grandkids might also be werewolves&quot; and made small placed alongside additional reasons why somebody might undergo the First Change).<br /> <br /> And interaction with Proximi I think is the kind of thing that needs to engage with them not exactly being normal families above and beyond having hereditary magical powers; the notion that a lot of those lines trace back to Imperial spells, refugees from Emanations, possibly ancestry with some kind of actual god.<br /> <br /> Mind, in Mage terms I can't help but feel like it becomes a bit of a square peg for a round hole when the Temenos is there. A personification for a family lineage feels like a much more organic fit as a Goetia under the circumstances, and family identities with greater or lesser prominence are definitely part of that realm. It's less accessible than the Shadow, but that might be for the best, and one could possibly work in that they're a type with a little bit more leeway than most of them get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T11:36:38-07:00","id":1476862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476818#post1476818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a somewhat related note, are there any Death/Spirit focused Thyrsus legacies? I\u2019m interested in seeing how the path understands ghosts in the context of their relation to spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476822#post1476822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno about ghost/Death-focused Thyrsus. Seems like an unexplored space.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Devourers of the Flesh from the Adamantine Arrow book are Death-Primary and Thyrsus, but they're cannibals with no mentioned interest in ghosts. The reverse version of the original Illumined Path (who were Thyrsus) from Keys to the Supernal Tarot <i>are</i> actually Death and Spirit-focused, but again have no explicit relation to ghosts, though they do use spirits for spooky effects. There's also an unnamed Legacy mentioned in a sidebar in Left-Hand Path that was created by a Thyrsus and can be reasonably inferred to be Death-Primary since its purpose is to resurrect the dead, but that also is not directly related to ghosts.<br /> In Signs of Sorcery, the section describing how the Paths approach non-Ruling Arcana gives some insight into how Thyrsus view ghosts, which are seen as little different from spirits since both are invisible entities that must be appeased to avoid their harm to the living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T13:18:30-07:00","id":1476875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476862#post1476862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Signs of Sorcery, the section describing how the Paths approach non-Ruling Arcana gives some insight into how Thyrsus view ghosts, which are seen as little different from spirits since both are invisible entities that must be appeased to avoid their harm to the living.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that actually kind of makes me think that a focused Legacy of Thyrsus might be better suited to engaging with the Underworld than Moros are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T19:17:16-07:00","id":1476913,"title":"","content":"I couldn't find anywhere in the book if it is explicitly prohibited to have more than one familiar.<br /> Can you only have one familiar?<br /> <br /> I have an NPC Mage planned from the Thrice-Great and I want her to have 2 spirits each fettered on snakes, and I wanted to know if this is possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T19:37:01-07:00","id":1476914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LunaLupa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476913#post1476913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't find anywhere in the book if it is explicitly prohibited to have more than one familiar.<br /> Can you only have one familiar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. There was a Merit specifically for having multiple familiars very early in 1e, where its only effect was allowing you to buy more, and 2e has generally moved past that type of cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T19:42:31-07:00","id":1476915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LunaLupa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1476913#post1476913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you only have one familiar?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem like it. I think the only obstacle would be the story sense of not wanting too many spirits to manage or take responsibility for, and that's a fairly soft one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T20:00:07-07:00","id":1476916,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T10:22:07-07:00","id":1477099,"title":"","content":"Would targets of the same casting of Incognito Presence be able to interact with each other as normal, or are they as incapable of perceiving each other as everyone else? Invisibility has a similar drawback, only you can at least hear each other and remember doing so","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T10:29:46-07:00","id":1477100,"title":"","content":"Would targets of the same casting of Incognito Presence be able to interact with each other as normal, or are they as incapable of perceiving each other as everyone else? Invisibility has a similar drawback, only you can at least hear each other and remember doing so","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T13:18:27-07:00","id":1477114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1477100#post1477100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would targets of the same casting of Incognito Presence be able to interact with each other as normal, or are they as incapable of perceiving each other as everyone else? Invisibility has a similar drawback, only you can at least hear each other and remember doing so</div> </div> </div> </div> I could see both options, honestly. I don\u2019t think the spell causes the subject to forget themselves, so there is some shielding from its effects. I believe it mostly depends how a mage sets up the spell, different rotes might have the drawback or not, depending on who made them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T13:56:23-07:00","id":1477117,"title":"","content":"I think if people are under the effect of a Veiling, they're Veiled from everybody it would naturally apply to, even if they were separate targets of the same spell. If nothing else, I'd put it under the same logic as how individual targets within a single spell get to Withstand separately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T16:13:28-07:00","id":1477129,"title":"","content":"I imagine a +1 Reach option to allow Incognito Presence subjects to perceive each other would be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T02:58:54-07:00","id":1477427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1477100#post1477100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would targets of the same casting of Incognito Presence be able to interact with each other as normal, or are they as incapable of perceiving each other as everyone else? Invisibility has a similar drawback, only you can at least hear each other and remember doing so</div> </div> </div> </div>The simplest solution i have seen was to give the targets a telepathic connection first.<br /> <br /> Letting them communicated silently, and possibly share each other's senses (though i wonder whether they can see themselves through the other's eyes...)<br /> <br /> Alternatively, i think you can exempt them from effect of the spell using Fate (even though they aren't subjects of the spell).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T03:51:55-07:00","id":1477429,"title":"","content":"The individual subjects are likely fully aware of themselves even though they're subjects of the spell. As such I think it's reasonable to be able to designate all subjects combined as a single unit, making the unit still aware of itself as if it was a single subject. At the very most this would cost a Reach, but I'd personally allow it to be a free choice because the subjects being aware of each other feels more natural even though it's technically not RAW.<br /> <br /> I would not, as someone suggested above, lock that choice in when turning the spell into a Rote. Rotes allow you to cast a single spell, but leave all types of choices and factors up to the caster, not the creator of the Rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T07:44:39-07:00","id":1477440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1477429#post1477429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The individual subjects are likely fully aware of themselves even though they're subjects of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the spell does use the phrase &quot;onlookers&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As such I think it's reasonable to be able to designate all subjects combined as a single unit, making the unit still aware of itself as if it was a single subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what does that mean for the prospect of dispelling it?<br /> <br /> Invisibility of various kinds is pretty strong, I think it's reasonable enough for those benefiting to deal with the complication of being unable to perceive one another. Besides, a bit of planning to coordinate beforehand can deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T08:53:17-07:00","id":1477951,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone! Could a time mage change the frequency that physical events occur but that have the time variable in their representations?<br /> <br /> Some examples:<br /> <br /> - change the rate at which a subject accelerates (for example, a subject experiencing the effects of gravity from 9.8m/s^2 -&gt; 9.8m/(10s)^2<br /> <br /> - change the rate at which a subject travels a distance (for example, a subject traveling at 10m/s -&gt; 10m/(10s)<br /> <br /> - or in the case of a collision, increasing the time it would take a subject to go from a speed x to 0 (maybe the same way as above examples), thus decreasing the damage the subject would suffer (Example 9.2 on link: <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-2-impulse-and-collisions\" target=\"_blank\">https://openstax.org/books/universit...and-collisions</a>)<br /> <br /> I know these ideas could easily be done with Forces but I'm playing with Time and I would like to know if it's possible to accomplish these kind of effects with this Arcana. And Time is still a bit abstract for me, I'm trying to come up with ideas on how to improve usage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T09:29:33-07:00","id":1477952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1477951#post1477951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone! Could a time mage change the frequency that physical events occur but that have the time variable in their representations?<br /> <br /> Some examples:<br /> <br /> - change the rate at which a subject accelerates (for example, a subject experiencing the effects of gravity from 9.8m/s^2 -&gt; 9.8m/(10s)^2<br /> <br /> - change the rate at which a subject travels a distance (for example, a subject traveling at 10m/s -&gt; 10m/(10s)<br /> <br /> - or in the case of a collision, increasing the time it would take a subject to go from a speed x to 0 (maybe the same way as above examples), thus decreasing the damage the subject would suffer (Example 9.2 on link: <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-2-impulse-and-collisions\" target=\"_blank\">https://openstax.org/books/universit...and-collisions</a>)<br /> <br /> I know these ideas could easily be done with Forces but I'm playing with Time and I would like to know if it's possible to accomplish these kind of effects with this Arcana. And Time is still a bit abstract for me, I'm trying to come up with ideas on how to improve usage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is accomplished through the Disciple level spells Acceleration and Chronos' Curse, on pages 188 and 189 of the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T09:42:56-07:00","id":1477953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> change the rate at which a subject accelerates (for example, a subject experiencing the effects of gravity from 9.8m/s^2 -&gt; 9.8m/(10s)^2 </div> </div> </div>I think the answer is no. Even though it disagrees with my sense of physics, you can slow a person's movement through time, but gravity would remain the same (from their perspective). Everyone else would see them falling at half the rate - but in the time frame they are travelling in they would still hit the ground just as hard.<br /> <br /> F = ma =&gt; a = F/m you can either change the force with Forces, or change the mass with Matter, but i think Time only affects the relative motion through time... At least that would be my interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is accomplished through the Disciple level spells Acceleration and Chronos' Curse, on pages 188 and 189 of the corebook. </div> </div> </div>I was going to reference these two spells, but reading them through, i don't think they accomplish what is being asked.<br /> <br /> Mechanically those spells allow you change your speed and possibly add potency to your defence.<br /> <br /> But reducing the impulse (time over which a force is applied) would be more like armour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 04-03-2022, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-04T12:09:24-07:00","id":1478015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1477951#post1477951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone! Could a time mage change the frequency that physical events occur but that have the time variable in their representations?<br /> <br /> Some examples:<br /> <br /> - change the rate at which a subject accelerates (for example, a subject experiencing the effects of gravity from 9.8m/s^2 -&gt; 9.8m/(10s)^2<br /> <br /> - change the rate at which a subject travels a distance (for example, a subject traveling at 10m/s -&gt; 10m/(10s)<br /> <br /> - or in the case of a collision, increasing the time it would take a subject to go from a speed x to 0 (maybe the same way as above examples), thus decreasing the damage the subject would suffer (Example 9.2 on link: <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-2-impulse-and-collisions\" target=\"_blank\">https://openstax.org/books/universit...and-collisions</a>)<br /> <br /> I know these ideas could easily be done with Forces but I'm playing with Time and I would like to know if it's possible to accomplish these kind of effects with this Arcana. And Time is still a bit abstract for me, I'm trying to come up with ideas on how to improve usage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also agree that the first two applications sound like Acceleration and Chrono's Curse.<br /> <br /> Regarding the third one, the same amount of forces would apply, magic simply overwrites the phenomenon its applied to, without altering anything else. Which means that using Matter to change the state of a rock to liquid will create a room temperature liquefied rock rather than lava. Applying the same principle can create ice vapor or a room temperature water block.<br /> <br /> The Time effect you are looking for sounds like Mage Armor. Regarding different applications of Time, I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473214#post1473214\"> a detailed post about it</a>, hopefully that can be a useful starting point. Since they are based on spells I previously wrote in Creative Thaumaturgy, if there is anything that looks interesting, please let me know and I will provide the reference for more details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-04-2022, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-04T12:45:21-07:00","id":1478016,"title":"","content":"I feel as though changing rates at which something occurs would be valid as something that the Time Arcanum could do, but mostly as a narrative subject. I don't think the system particularly has the granularity to effectively display the difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T11:16:58-07:00","id":1478395,"title":"","content":"Does a Legacy's first attainment get 2 Reach or just 1 if it's emulating a 1-dot spell using its Primary Arcanum? The wording in the corebook could be read as allowing 2 Reach (&quot;Attainments receive only the Paradox-free Reach for meeting and exceeding <i>Arcanum</i> requirements&quot;) since the attainment requires the Primary Arcanum at 2 dots, but I see that most fanmade Legacies go for the just 1 Reach interpretation, while a few official Legacies actually get 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T12:15:13-07:00","id":1478404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1478395#post1478395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Legacy's first attainment get 2 Reach or just 1 if it's emulating a 1-dot spell using its Primary Arcanum? The wording in the corebook could be read as allowing 2 Reach (&quot;Attainments receive only the Paradox-free Reach for meeting and exceeding <i>Arcanum</i> requirements&quot;) since the attainment requires the Primary Arcanum at 2 dots, but I see that most fanmade Legacies go for the just 1 Reach interpretation, while a few official Legacies actually get 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>The example immediately following &quot;meeting and exceeding Arcanum requirements&quot; is a three-dot Attainment made from a two-dot spell having two free Reach. The first Attainment has one free Reach \u2014 the Eleventh Question's Undisturbed Scene puts it toward instant use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T13:49:53-07:00","id":1478424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1478404#post1478404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The example immediately following &quot;meeting and exceeding Arcanum requirements&quot; is a three-dot Attainment made from a two-dot spell having two free Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no issue with second-to-fifth attainments since their Primary Arcanum requirement matches their attainment level. I'm talking specifically about first attainments since their Primary Arcanum requirement exceeds their attainment level by default.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1478404#post1478404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Attainment has one free Reach \u2014 the Eleventh Question's Undisturbed Scene puts it toward instant use.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the Tyrian Archons and the Reality Stalkers from Nameless and Accursed have 2 Reach for their first attainments. Probably just fringe cases, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T15:11:54-07:00","id":1478432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1478424#post1478424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no issue with second-to-fifth attainments since their Primary Arcanum requirement matches their attainment level. I'm talking specifically about first attainments since their Primary Arcanum requirement exceeds their attainment level by default.On the other hand, the Tyrian Archons and the Reality Stalkers from Nameless and Accursed have 2 Reach for their first attainments. Probably just fringe cases, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arcanum prerequisites for Legacy Initiation (which is always 2), and the Minimum Legacy Ruling Arcanum requirement for Legacy Attainments (which equals Attainment rank), seem to be <i>separate</i> factors.<br /> <br /> So, a First Attainment\u2019s primary Arcanum requirement (and thus the Arcanum dot rating its Fixed Reach is calculated by), which is the same thing as the Minimum Legacy Ruling Arcanum requirement as described above, is still 1 \u2014 even if mages will have long met the criterion due to Initiation.<br /> <br /> Strange, I know, but the fine letters do seem to work out.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The First Attainments of the Tyrian Archons and the Reality Stalkers as described in N&amp;A have the extra Reach at a condition or cost, so I\u2019d say that they\u2019re exceptions that prove the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-09-2022, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T18:14:43-07:00","id":1478453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1478424#post1478424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no issue with second-to-fifth attainments since their Primary Arcanum requirement matches their attainment level.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be a one-dot spell for a two-dot Attainment and the math would be the same. Legacy Attainments calculate their Reach by the level of the Arcanum required for the Attainment, not the level of the Arcanum the character possesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T04:16:37-07:00","id":1478478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1478424#post1478424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking specifically about first attainments since their Primary Arcanum requirement exceeds their attainment level by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. The specified &quot;Minimum Legacy Ruling Arcanum&quot; for the first Legacy Attainment is clearly listed as 1 on page 199 in <s>black</s>dark blue on <s>white</s>bright blue.<br /> <br /> The <i>practical</i> prerequisite is 2 because you need two dots for initiation, but that is not the same as the listed Arcanum requirement, which is what the text on Free Reach directly refers to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T05:17:22-07:00","id":1478674,"title":"","content":"<br /> Does spell Veil of Moments (Corebook, p.188) prevent the subject from needing to meet basic needs (hunger, thirst, sleep, fatigue, etc)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T05:52:04-07:00","id":1478675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1478674#post1478674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does spell Veil of Moments (Corebook, p.188) prevent the subject from needing to meet basic needs (hunger, thirst, sleep, fatigue, etc)?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Immune to things that worsen with time&quot; and &quot;New Conditions and Tilts cannot be imposed on the subject while the spell remains in effect&quot; would seem indicate this is the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T06:24:24-07:00","id":1478677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1478675#post1478675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Immune to things that worsen with time&quot; and &quot;New Conditions and Tilts cannot be imposed on the subject while the spell remains in effect&quot; would seem indicate this is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> These conditions were not very clear to me in the spell description. Could the need to breathe also be affected? Sometimes I can't discern if a spell from one arcana is entering the area of \u200b\u200banother. In the case of breathing and eating, I would mistake it as being from the Life arcana only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T09:51:01-07:00","id":1478697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1478677#post1478677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> These conditions were not very clear to me in the spell description. Could the need to breathe also be affected?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're breathing comfortably at the time the spell is cast, your pattern will be frozen into that state sure.<br /> <br /> To the extent that being distinguished from the Life Arcanum matters, I think the fact that Reach is required to be able to heal wounds, regain Willpower or acquire Mana is relevant. I'd also say that if a person whose stomach was full when the spell was cast can be forced to throw it up then they'll be in a perpetual state of uncomfortable hunger.<br /> <br /> Still, don't forget that there's a sidebar talking about how it's fine for there to be some intersections between the Arcana. Time might have some things that can hold off hunger, aging, even fix up a wounded individual, but you can't do things like change appearances or give somebody adhesive hands with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T10:11:18-07:00","id":1479346,"title":"","content":"I have a question that harkens back to the days of the Bene Ashmedai and the Clavicularius. At what point does a Legacy become it's own thing? Or, to approach it from a different direction, what makes a Legacy into a group identity?<br /> <br /> Say a Free Council Obrimos was refused entry to the Pure Sovereigns, so they go off on their own and self initiate into a personal legacy that is, for all intents and purposes, identical to the Sovereigns. Are they now a Pure Sovereign, and subject to the Sympathy laws? <br /> <br /> The rules imply that you stay Connected even if you divorce yourself from the Legacy's community, so is it lines of inheritance etched into the soul and tracing back to the founder that makes you Connected?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T11:11:57-07:00","id":1479353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479346#post1479346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say a Free Council Obrimos was refused entry to the Pure Sovereigns, so they go off on their own and self initiate into a personal legacy that is, for all intents and purposes, identical to the Sovereigns. Are they now a Pure Sovereign, and subject to the Sympathy laws?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the way to answer this that is most straightforward and in line with the general intent of Legacies is that it's not actually possible to found a Legacy that is truly identical independently. The Attainments might function in the same way, but there are going to be at least changes in the nuances of the ethos that forms the process of Legacy indoctrination and what that lends to things like the oblations and yantras that the Legacy bestows.<br /> <br /> If your alt-Pure Sovereign was rejected on grounds of incompatibilities in the outlook, those are almost certainly going to find their way into what the new founder creates. Even if it was arbitrary denial to somebody who would otherwise be a viable candidate, I'd say they can be assumed to lack insufficient knowledge to truly recreate the ethos, rituals, and priority and approach to Mysteries of the original Legacy.<br /> <br /> Hell, not just outlook. It's explicit that the process of founding a Legacy requires exploration of a Mystery key to its ethos through direct action. You might be looking for Attainments of improved bodily function, even towards an ethos of a perfected body signifying a right to authority, but you're probably not going to be able to engage with the same kinds of mystical expressions of and insights into those ideas that the original Pure Sovereign did. Not in an age where practical examples of kingship are not really available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules imply that you stay Connected even if you divorce yourself from the Legacy's community, so is it lines of inheritance etched into the soul and tracing back to the founder that makes you Connected?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there may be some wires crossed here.<br /> <br /> There are two ways Legacy is relevant to sympathy. Legacy members function as high level sympathetic Yantras to other members and components of their Legacy, which can alternately enhance the dice pools for casting on those things or provide the means of sympathetic casting at them without needing some external prop or intimate information. Actual sympathetic connections are still necessary, so a given member does not automatically have the means to cast on somebody that they've never met.<br /> <br /> Mentors and students form Strong sympathetic bonds as a matter of course, which can tend to lead to one high ranking member of the Legacy having a good connection to several other mages, and the means to cast on them without needing anything that represents them. An enterprising mage might use a sequence of other spells to acquire bonds your student or master has that you do not, but you aren't innately bonded to any other Legacy member, although these two details together could be leveraged into allowing several members of the Legacy to regularly congregate, which would allow formation of natural bonds.<br /> <br /> It does seem to me that it's possible for people to receive tutelage from mages other than the one who initially initiated them without complication, so over the course of your development you might form such bonds with additional mages, but that's never going to lead to more than five of them.<br /> <br /> A true outsider is going to have no bond if they have not actually had the experience of direct interaction and shared ritual that a tutor and student have, nor are hey going to function as a sympathetic Yantra because they lack the properly calibrated alignment of shared refinement of Gnosis.<br /> <br /> The purported common history of the Clavicularius and Bene Ashmedai is an edge case an actual Mystery. If there's any truth to the idea that they have a common lineage, and particularly to the idea that an initiate of one Legacy managed to become another, it's probably not going to be something applicable across other Legacies, and might owe a lot to the specifics of those ones being concerned with the inner realms of the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T11:15:44-07:00","id":1479354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479346#post1479346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question that harkens back to the days of the Bene Ashmedai and the Clavicularius. At what point does a Legacy become it's own thing? Or, to approach it from a different direction, what makes a Legacy into a group identity?<br /> <br /> Say a Free Council Obrimos was refused entry to the Pure Sovereigns, so they go off on their own and self initiate into a personal legacy that is, for all intents and purposes, identical to the Sovereigns. Are they now a Pure Sovereign, and subject to the Sympathy laws?<br /> <br /> The rules imply that you stay Connected even if you divorce yourself from the Legacy's community, so is it lines of inheritance etched into the soul and tracing back to the founder that makes you Connected?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if it is an existing Legacy, then they need some way to be initiated. A rogue mentor or a sympathetic one in the Legacy's astral realm are the least controversial. They could also find a Daimonomica or soul stone of the Legacy, but those raise heavy questions, since it can be argued that the mage essentially stole its teachings. But as soon as they obtain the full first Attainment, the ties of Sympathy are binding, no matter how they feel about the ones that refused them.<br /> <br /> Should those not be the case, then they could start half initiated or with a general idea, then diverge as they make it their own. A Legacy is more than a set of abilities, its a philosophical view on how the mage chooses to specialize their magic, with corresponding symbols, practices and traditions. The Reality Makers are one of the most prominent examples. The founder was left half initiated as a member of the Sisterhood of the Blessed. He diverged by focusing on using their Arcana to focus on solving problems with minimal effort, rather than seeking a glamorous accumulation of political power from behind the scenes. He became a Reality Maker on the first Attainment, with no sympathetic ties to the Sisterhood. Everything follows the standard rules for Legacy creation afterwards, they must either make a Daimonomica or develop the third Attainment in order to pass it onto others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T11:48:16-07:00","id":1479357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479353#post1479353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, not just outlook. It's explicit that the process of founding a Legacy requires exploration of a Mystery key to its ethos through direct action. You might be looking for Attainments of improved bodily function, even towards an ethos of a perfected body signifying a right to authority, but you're probably not going to be able to engage with the same kinds of mystical expressions of and insights into those ideas that the original Pure Sovereign did. Not in an age where practical examples of kingship are not really available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I'd forgotten about the Mystery aspect. Yes, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479353#post1479353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there may be some wires crossed here.<br /> <br /> There are two ways Legacy is relevant to sympathy. Legacy members function as high level sympathetic Yantras to other members and components of their Legacy, which can alternately enhance the dice pools for casting on those things or provide the means of sympathetic casting at them without needing some external prop or intimate information. Actual sympathetic connections are still necessary, so a given member does not automatically have the means to cast on somebody that they've never met.<br /> <br /> Mentors and students form Strong sympathetic bonds as a matter of course, which can tend to lead to one high ranking member of the Legacy having a good connection to several other mages, and the means to cast on them without needing anything that represents them. An enterprising mage might use a sequence of other spells to acquire bonds your student or master has that you do not, but you aren't innately bonded to any other Legacy member, although these two details together could be leveraged into allowing several members of the Legacy to regularly congregate, which would allow formation of natural bonds.<br /> <br /> It does seem to me that it's possible for people to receive tutelage from mages other than the one who initially initiated them without complication, so over the course of your development you might form such bonds with additional mages, but that's never going to lead to more than five of them.<br /> <br /> A true outsider is going to have no bond if they have not actually had the experience of direct interaction and shared ritual that a tutor and student have, nor are hey going to function as a sympathetic Yantra because they lack the properly calibrated alignment of shared refinement of Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 197's sidebar gave me the impression that all Legacy members (and Daimonomika/Soulstones) were Connected, but that that utility was limited by any caster's knowledge of who was actually in the Legacy. Much like how Seers with the Panopticon Crown are terrifying... if they know about you. If that's not the case, then it does change how I look at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479353#post1479353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The purported common history of the Clavicularius and Bene Ashmedai is an edge case an actual Mystery. If there's any truth to the idea that they have a common lineage, and particularly to the idea that an initiate of one Legacy managed to become another, it's probably not going to be something applicable across other Legacies, and might owe a lot to the specifics of those ones being concerned with the inner realms of the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479354#post1479354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should those not be the case, then they could start half initiated or with a general idea, then diverge as they make it their own. A Legacy is more than a set of abilities, its a philosophical view on how the mage chooses to specialize their magic, with corresponding symbols, practices and traditions. The Reality Makers are one of the most prominent examples. The founder was left half initiated as a member of the Sisterhood of the Blessed. He diverged by focusing on using their Arcana to focus on solving problems with minimal effort, rather than seeking a glamorous accumulation of political power from behind the scenes. He became a Reality Maker on the first Attainment, with no sympathetic ties to the Sisterhood. Everything follows the standard rules for Legacy creation afterwards, they must either make a Daimonomica or develop the third Attainment in order to pass it onto others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both these lead well into a tangential question - Core mentions about Mages creating novel attainments for their Legacy; &quot;A mage may either develop Attainments according to the orthodox teachings of her Legacy, or invent novel Attainments based on her personal approach to the Legacy\u2019s doctrine.&quot; <br /> <br /> At what point do you diverge enough from the root Legacy to become a new one? Can you have only your First Attainment be the same as the rest of your peers, and still be one of them? The Threnodists in 1E touched on that briefly in regards to their secondary arcana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T12:03:06-07:00","id":1479359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479357#post1479357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At what point do you diverge enough from the root Legacy to become a new one? Can you have only your First Attainment be the same as the rest of your peers, and still be one of them? The Threnodists in 1E touched on that briefly in regards to their secondary arcana</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't initiate another mage into a Legacy until you've gotten your Third Attainment, so I'd say that if there's a distinction drawn between variants of a Legacy it's no sooner than that point; if you've managed to instruct another mage to the point where they've learned one of your Novel Attainments as an Orthodox Attainment, you might still qualify as a branch of the same Legacy, but the point of separation feels like it's narratively determined by changes in the focal theory and Mystery of your group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T22:57:34-07:00","id":1479400,"title":"","content":"I think Bluewinds' <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1308179-sisterhood-of-the-blessed-a-time-prime-take-on-the-1e-legacy\">Sisterhood of the Blessed</a> is a great example of this in practice.<br /> <br /> The ethos of accumulating political power via subtle manipulation and &quot;lucky&quot; coincidences remains, but this branch focuses on proactively seizing authority rather than becoming the power behind the crown. <br /> <br /> The culture, yantras and oblations still cleave to the original philosophy, but the unorthodox Attainments and approach quality it as a variation. In this case, I believe the sympathetic connection remains, but a soul stone or Daimonomika created by such a mage would teach this version of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T00:56:42-07:00","id":1479406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479357#post1479357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you have only your First Attainment be the same as the rest of your peers, and still be one of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes. I think the shared process of initiation, the Yantras and oblations, and the parameters under which an Attainment must be developed remain common enough to still be identifiable as the same Legacy.<br /> <br /> I think it's enough for an orthodoxy to predominate rather than riddling the Legacy with variations through a combination of the incentive of greater ease, a bit of insistence by peers, and coming to a Legacy generally out of sincere investment in what it's about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T11:12:58-07:00","id":1479719,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">The spell <i><b>Choose the Thread (Time \u2022\u2022)</b> </i>(pag 187, Core), says<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The subject\u2019s player rolls twice for her next mundane dice roll...</i> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">does that mean that after using the effect, the spell ends?<br /> <br /> that is, is the spell only for the next roll and not for rolls made within the spell's duration? </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T11:50:55-07:00","id":1479723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479719#post1479719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The spell <i><b>Choose the Thread (Time \u2022\u2022)</b> </i>(pag 187, Core), says<br /> <br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">does that mean that after using the effect, the spell ends?<br /> <br /> that is, is the spell only for the next roll and not for rolls made within the spell's duration? </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the spell only affects the subject's next roll. However, I will note that the text is ambiguous on whether its effect is Lasting (such as Knit, which is to say the spell ends as soon as it's cast unless Advanced Duration is applied), or if the spell has a normal Duration (in which case even after its power is used, the spell would still technically be active until dismissed or its timer runs out).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T11:55:55-07:00","id":1479725,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to decrease the time needed for the brain to &quot;think&quot; with <b>Time</b>?<br /> <br /> The idea is to react more quickly to external events and possibly think faster. Something like what Flash can do. If so, would you have any idea how to do this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T12:09:51-07:00","id":1479728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479725#post1479725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible to decrease the time needed for the brain to &quot;think&quot; with <b>Time</b>?<br /> <br /> The idea is to react more quickly to external events and possibly think faster. Something like what Flash can do. If so, would you have any idea how to do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tipping the Hourglass and Acceleration both more or less cover that angle, at least from a more abstracted point of view. For long-term pondering, there's Blink of an Eye, or potentially a new, lower-level spell that reduces the intervals for extended actions.<br /> <br /> Outside that, if you wanted to represent the subject's brain processing information and sensory input faster, I think there's probably justification for representing such as a Time Perfecting spell that increases the subject's Wits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T13:08:08-07:00","id":1479734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479725#post1479725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible to decrease the time needed for the brain to &quot;think&quot; with <b>Time</b>?<br /> <br /> The idea is to react more quickly to external events and possibly think faster. Something like what Flash can do. If so, would you have any idea how to do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wits is the speed at which you take in and process information. Dexterity is your ability to antecipate and adjust your fine motion control for given tasks. With a Perfecting of Time, you could increase either by [Potency]. By spending a Reach and a mana, you could go beyond trait limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-29-2022, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T13:43:14-07:00","id":1479738,"title":"","content":"Think there is room for a legacy about embracing one\u2019s mortality and getting the most out of what time they do have? Wanted a thematic opposite to a Prime/Mind Lich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T14:50:13-07:00","id":1479747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479738#post1479738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think there is room for a legacy about embracing one\u2019s mortality and getting the most out of what time they do have? Wanted a thematic opposite to a Prime/Mind Lich.</div> </div> </div> </div>A possible conundrum to a Legacy embracing mortality is that the Psychopomp blocks the way for souls trying to move beyond the Fallen world. So making the most of life probably requires addressing the fear of doom after death.<br /> <br /> Regarding Arcana, I think Life and Fate would make for a good combination. Life ensures you are always in peak condition, well fed, fully healed and able to adapt to whatever curveballs an intensely proactive lifestyle throws at you. Fate ensures there are new opportunities, small pleasures and lucky breaks to keep you motivated even in the darkest moments, to make beacons of hope for yourself and others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T03:47:10-07:00","id":1479800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479725#post1479725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible to decrease the time needed for the brain to &amp;quot;think&amp;quot; with <b>Time</b>?<br /> <br /> The idea is to react more quickly to external events and possibly think faster. Something like what Flash can do. If so, would you have any idea how to do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you envision that working out in play terms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479738#post1479738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think there is room for a legacy about embracing one\u2019s mortality and getting the most out of what time they do have? Wanted a thematic opposite to a Prime/Mind Lich.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Tamers of the Void in Legacies: the Ancient might be like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T05:55:03-07:00","id":1479803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479800#post1479800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you envision that working out in play terms?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The main ideia is to use <b>Hung Spell</b> (pag 187, Core) with <b>Shifting Sands </b>(pag 189, Core), to create something like <a href=\"https://naruto.fandom.com/wiki/Izanagi\" target=\"_blank\">Izanagi</a>. <br /> When the subject is injured in some way, she cancels Hung Spell and Shifting Sands start.<br /> <br /> The objective of heightening the subject's 'senses' is to realize that she is being hurt and to be able to cancel Hung Spell before it is too late.<br /> <br /> I know I probably could do the same with Fate 2 but I don't have Fate. In our game, we can choose the arcana you want to start with (homebrew).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T08:11:02-07:00","id":1479810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479803#post1479803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main ideia is to use <b>Hung Spell</b> (pag 187, Core) with <b>Shifting Sands </b>(pag 189, Core), to create something like <a href=\"https://naruto.fandom.com/wiki/Izanagi\" target=\"_blank\">Izanagi</a>.<br /> When the subject is injured in some way, she cancels Hung Spell and Shifting Sands start.<br /> <br /> The objective of heightening the subject's 'senses' is to realize that she is being hurt and to be able to cancel Hung Spell before it is too late.<br /> <br /> I know I probably could do the same with Fate 2 but I don't have Fate. In our game, we can choose the arcana you want to start with (homebrew).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well... cancelling spells is already a reflexive action, it can be done at will regardless of any other considerations of timing. A person could be injured and then immediately will the Hung Spell to end, so is this a case of wanting some option where a person perceives incoming harm before it connects or is damaged lethally but is able to end the spell before falling unconscious? What are the particulars of wanting an option that can respond to harm before some threshold has been passed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T08:33:32-07:00","id":1479812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479810#post1479810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well... cancelling spells is already a reflexive action, it can be done at will regardless of any other considerations of timing. A person could be injured and then immediately will the Hung Spell to end, so is this a case of wanting some option where a person perceives incoming harm before it connects or is damaged lethally but is able to end the spell before falling unconscious? What are the particulars of wanting an option that can respond to harm before some threshold has been passed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea is to notice the event that will injure the target as soon as it starts (assuming the target hasn't seen it coming). Like a sword touching the skin moments before taking an arm off, or a bullet touching the forehead moments before going through the head. But as a last resort, cancel the Hung Spell before the subject falls unconscious. The less the subject is injured, the better it would be.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T12:09:36-07:00","id":1479825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479812#post1479812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The idea is to notice the event that will injure the target as soon as it starts (assuming the target hasn't seen it coming). Like a sword touching the skin moments before taking an arm off, or a bullet touching the forehead moments before going through the head. But as a last resort, cancel the Hung Spell before the subject falls unconscious. The less the subject is injured, the better it would be.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Using time to avoid damage like this is effectively how the Time armour attainment works.<br /> <br /> That may be an aside to what you are asking, but i thought it worth mentioning. Getting higher initiative using acceleration or similar gives some nice advantages. <br /> <br /> Doing something like Choose the Threads to see what the best action to take next will be also seems appropriate - maybe having it as a legacy attainment so you could activate it without having to roll dice... <br /> <br /> Basically, yes, Time has loads of ways of doing this, most seem to be ruling/perfecting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T20:07:24-07:00","id":1479925,"title":"","content":"Ground Eater (pag 173, Core) and Acceleration (pag 188, Core) could they work together or did they fall under the spell stacking rule? <br /> <br /> Ground Eater adds/reduces Potency to/from Speed and Acceleration multiply Speed by Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-01T21:08:42-07:00","id":1479927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1479925#post1479925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ground Eater (pag 173, Core) and Acceleration (pag 188, Core) could they work together or did they fall under the spell stacking rule?<br /> <br /> Ground Eater adds/reduces Potency to/from Speed and Acceleration multiply Speed by Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe they do not stack, since they affect the same stat, in this case speed. What would stack with those individual spells would be something like Levitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T05:32:12-07:00","id":1480525,"title":"","content":"I remember &quot;something&quot; about living beings reasserting their pattern and making it hard to have a lasting effect on them, outside of healing, damage and transform life. Can anyone tell me where that is or if that was a 1e thing or was it likely just specific to my old ST?<br /> <br /> Edit: found the side bar that goes over this, the one that talks about turning people into frogs, life 4 patterning cannot do the types of lasting changes that I was thinking it couldnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 05-09-2022, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T11:02:46-07:00","id":1480561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1480525#post1480525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember &quot;something&quot; about living beings reasserting their pattern and making it hard to have a lasting effect on them, outside of healing, damage and transform life. Can anyone tell me where that is or if that was a 1e thing or was it likely just specific to my old ST?<br /> <br /> Edit: found the side bar that goes over this, the one that talks about turning people into frogs, life 4 patterning cannot do the types of lasting changes that I was thinking it couldnt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lasting effects in 2e are those with ontological inertia, if the magic is removed the effect persists.<br /> <br /> I think you're partially conflating this with the 1e rule for indefinite duration:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw1e p120</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The spell is permanent until cancelled or dispelled.<br /> Living targets, however, grow, change and heal. Spells with<br /> an indefinite Duration cannot be cast upon a living creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e a spell with an indefinite duration <i>can</i> be cast on a living creature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T12:10:53-07:00","id":1481943,"title":"","content":"Looking at page 111 of <i>Astral Realms</i>, there is the Platonic Element numen, which is used to create Platonic Exemplar. Both that term and the item's ability to safely relinquish spells share a similarity with Eidoforms, which appear on page 102 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>. Within that entry, it is mentioned that there are no known reliable methods of creating them. However, the Platonic Element numen's entry suggests this is a way to achieve this, one which smiths, alchemists and other mages that craft (using fire for the given example of a salamander) would have a higher likelihood of finding. It does not allow one to create Plastic Eidoforms (I imagine that requires an additional boon from a crafting Supernal summon or crafting the item entirely from Platonic Exemplars), but even then it still sounds remarkably useful.<br /> <br /> Does that mean that in 2ed that numen does not exists ? Would it be perhaps act as a gateway to studying the Mystery of the process, using a different ephemeral entity based on the crafting method (a member of the Forge Master or Lords of the Inanimate would be very interested) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T19:36:06-07:00","id":1481970,"title":"","content":"I have a quick question about Ghost/Goetic Summons. Using the reach to give the summoned a one word spell, in theory, would always cause a breaking point as you are forcing a being to do something. Why wouldn't the act of summoning them and forcing them to come to you not also cause a breaking point?<br /> <br /> P.S. Is there a good resource for learning about Goetia outside of the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","user":"Hyuse","date":". 05-25-2022, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T20:39:18-07:00","id":1481978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1481970#post1481970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a quick question about Ghost/Goetic Summons. Using the reach to give the summoned a one word spell, in theory, would always cause a breaking point as you are forcing a being to do something. Why wouldn't the act of summoning them and forcing them to come to you not also cause a breaking point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless answering the summons is counter to the spirit's interests, there is no reason to assume that would be the case.<br /> <br /> That being said, yes, mages who do a lot of summoning and binding will either inure their tools of trade, conduct their work sparingly and/or Virtuously, or make their peace with not being especially Wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> P.S. Is there a good resource for learning about Goetia outside of the book? </div> </div> </div><i>Astral Realms</i> still has a lot of generally-usable information as well as a great number of example Astral denizens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T09:48:55-07:00","id":1482005,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to think that it isn't an Act of Hubris to use magic to put a spirit on a task that it would already be inclined to do anyway; it's already the kind of thing it does, you just specify. That's the kind of thing that helps if you've spent time familiarising yourself with the local ecology, knowing the natures and interests of spirits so that you can match being to activity.<br /> <br /> You might lose a bit of flexibility, as I think there are a number of useful tasks that you could assign just about any spirit to do otherwise (like, tell one to follow somebody and report on what they're doing), but many a practiced shaman thinks it's a worthwhile tradeoff in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T00:30:48-07:00","id":1482135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1482005#post1482005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to think that it isn't an Act of Hubris to use magic to put a spirit on a task that it would already be inclined to do anyway; it's already the kind of thing it does, you just specify. That's the kind of thing that helps if you've spent time familiarising yourself with the local ecology, knowing the natures and interests of spirits so that you can match being to activity.<br /> <br /> You might lose a bit of flexibility, as I think there are a number of useful tasks that you could assign just about any spirit to do otherwise (like, tell one to follow somebody and report on what they're doing), but many a practiced shaman thinks it's a worthwhile tradeoff in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was already inclined to do the thing, you are safer not using magic. Summon the entity, then negotiation for them to do the thing ( and no binding spell will be left to trace back to you or be dispelled ).<br /> <br /> That still requires summoning though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T01:01:34-07:00","id":1482137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1482135#post1482135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it was already inclined to do the thing, you are safer not using magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am putting forward an argument where it can be safe for the mages to do something with magic. I like the Wisdom system, but would be averse to the idea of something that seems elementary to a character concept innately taking hits to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T06:35:07-07:00","id":1482148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1482137#post1482137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am putting forward an argument where it can be safe for the mages to do something with magic. I like the Wisdom system, but would be averse to the idea of something that seems elementary to a character concept innately taking hits to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was my understanding that that is what Inuring spells is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T07:11:20-07:00","id":1482153,"title":"","content":"Simple question: what could happen if one of the Bound (Supernal Being) is released?<br /> <br /> My understanding is the Supernal Beings are symbols (or parts of Symbols) and that Ascending Archmasters become symbols. So would returning a Bound to the Supernal be equivalent to Ascension - or perhaps easier as you aren't creating a new Supernal Symbol.<br /> <br /> And seperately, are there good reasons why you would want to keep them bound in the Phenomenal, rather than sending them to the Abyss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T08:59:25-07:00","id":1482159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1482153#post1482153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple question: what could happen if one of the Bound (Supernal Being) is released?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Suspire has a debatably-true account of one outcome, and the Seers keep the ravens of the Tower of London happy to keep another one from somehow causing the fall of England, but on a smaller scale<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My understanding is the Supernal Beings are symbols (or parts of Symbols) and that Ascending Archmasters become symbols. So would returning a Bound to the Supernal be equivalent to Ascension - or perhaps easier as you aren't creating a new Supernal Symbol. </div> </div> </div>That's the particular work of the Alienated entente of archmasters \u2014 the Bound have smaller prisons that they could ostensibly be freed from before the prospect of returning them to the heavens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And seperately, are there good reasons why you would want to keep them bound in the Phenomenal, rather than sending them to the Abyss? </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters, that would mean the Abyss has them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T09:16:17-07:00","id":1482161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1482153#post1482153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple question: what could happen if one of the Bound (Supernal Being) is released?<br /> <br /> My understanding is the Supernal Beings are symbols (or parts of Symbols) and that Ascending Archmasters become symbols. So would returning a Bound to the Supernal be equivalent to Ascension - or perhaps easier as you aren't creating a new Supernal Symbol.<br /> <br /> And seperately, are there good reasons why you would want to keep them bound in the Phenomenal, rather than sending them to the Abyss?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bound are symbols that were cast out of the Supernal by the Exarchs, eventually degrading into thaumavores in order to survive their forced existence in the Phenomenal.<br /> <br /> The process of returning them to the Supernal is a type of Ascension and the Alienated entente of archmastersuse that as a gateway for their own one. Sometimes via bargaining, merging with the being, tying their fates together and more. <br /> <br /> The Bound are symbols that were either dangerous to the Exarchs or just not helpful in creating a humanocentric cosmos. An example would be a fate where the world ends, not necessarily badly, but it does. Since this opposes the eternal rule of the Throne, it was exiled. There could be Bound who embody compassion and empathy, a powerful weapon against the Tyrants. They coud also have sealed Typon, who could father new Idigam. <br /> <br /> Regarding why not feed them to the Abyss, it doesn't eliminate the problem and increases the Void's encroachment on reality, there is a reason letting Supernal beings be consumed is an act of Falling Wisdom. It corrupts the symbols in ways that are not possible, which then can be weaponized against reality. The kraken is incredibly dangerous, but would you rather go through the trouble of creating highly complex containment procedures or would you prefer throwing it into non-reality, watch it become Cthulu and spend the rest of your life hoping it never awakens from its slumber ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T12:21:20-07:00","id":1482186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1482148#post1482148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was my understanding that that is what Inuring spells is for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, my statement probably requires the specificity of &quot;the character concept of harnessing spirits&quot;.<br /> <br /> Inuring works, but I think it leans a lot into the subject of how the character is doing something messed up. Like, I've no reservations about the idea of somebody needing to be Inured to not be jeopardizing their wisdom whenever they mind control somebody, even if that is assumed to be central to what they're doing.<br /> <br /> Although part of what contrasts with that is that I'd feel the Mind Arcanum still has a lot that it can do besides the mind control, which makes the decision for that to be central carry a statement, whereas I feel the Spirit Arcanum does not offer so much around the act of directing spirits with it. That would be one where I think general use of the Arcanum gets undermined if its spine mostly puts you between the places of constantly risking Wisdom or Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">are there good reasons why you would want to keep them bound in the Phenomenal, rather than sending them to the Abyss?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I mean, mages are hardly comfortable with sending Supernal beings to the Abyss even in the event of doing so being necessary to save themselves or anything else. Per Signs of Sorcery, there are only a few Consilia who are even willing to make allowances for killing in self defence if they're beings in the service of the Throne that have been targeted at them. Golden Law and the sense of their own Gnosis as expressed through Wisdom would seem to agree on the idea that if you see one even doing something highly atrocious and your only option for prevention is killing it, you walk away.<br /> <br /> While there might be some greater metaphysical arguments for that in terms of gradually feeding reality into the Abyss, I think its foundation can be something as simple as intuitively coming across as something deeply transgressive and profane. The Supernal might not be moral, but there is a certain innate rightness to it and its components, and feeding that into the horror of the Abyss can only ever be a terrible shock.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T13:28:53-07:00","id":1482190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1482186#post1482186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> While there might be some greater metaphysical arguments for that in terms of gradually feeding reality into the Abyss, I think its foundation can be something as simple as intuitively coming across as something deeply transgressive and profane. The Supernal might not be moral, but there is a certain innate rightness to it and its components, and feeding that into the horror of the Abyss can only ever be a terrible shock.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, because, of course your Gnosis would say that destroying supernal is bad, otherwise the universe wouldn't be so stable...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T17:00:10-07:00","id":1483085,"title":"","content":"How long do bodily samples (blood, hair, etc) remain Strong Sympathetic connections, and could you use Veil of Moments to extend that duration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:17:15-07:00","id":1483134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483085#post1483085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long do bodily samples (blood, hair, etc) remain Strong Sympathetic connections</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the point where it seems to have broken down enough to not be what it was at the time it was separated would be a good rule of thumb. Blood that has coagulated, hair that has become brittle and falling apart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">could you use Veil of Moments to extend that duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Veil of Moments prevents anything that progresses naturally over time. If you want something to not break down in natural decay, it will prevent that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:43:07-07:00","id":1483142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483134#post1483134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Veil of Moments prevents anything that progresses naturally over time. If you want something to not break down in natural decay, it will prevent that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say even mundane preservation would do the trick. Keeping a lock of hair pressed in a book, storing the blood in a vial. Both the act and the intention behind it should be able to preserve the sympathetic connection for a really long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T19:18:45-07:00","id":1483200,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, thanks!<br /> <br /> Side tangent, does blood Perfected maintain the Connection to the donor, or is it wiped of that Sympathy by being attuned to the Supernal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T12:54:27-07:00","id":1483244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483200#post1483200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense, thanks!<br /> <br /> Side tangent, does blood Perfected maintain the Connection to the donor, or is it wiped of that Sympathy by being attuned to the Supernal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why it should not retain the connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T17:22:03-07:00","id":1483262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483244#post1483244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why it should not retain the connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering if theres a difference between a vial of &quot;Perfect blood&quot;, and a vial of &quot;Person X's Perfect Blood&quot;. Which is probably just a meaningless distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T17:31:45-07:00","id":1483263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483262#post1483262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if theres a difference between a vial of &amp;quot;Perfect blood&amp;quot;, and a vial of &amp;quot;Person X's Perfect Blood&amp;quot;. Which is probably just a meaningless distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Temporal</i> sympathy could weaken, similar to how the Awakening weakens temporal sympathy between pre- and post-Awakening selves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T18:27:56-07:00","id":1483265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483263#post1483263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Temporal</i> sympathy could weaken, similar to how the Awakening weakens temporal sympathy between pre- and post-Awakening selves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... is a really good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T16:13:55-07:00","id":1483928,"title":"","content":"Cross-Splat question: A Changeling's Fetch supposedly has a piece of their soul in it. Would the two count as Connected for the purposes of Space Sympathy? The Fetch has a lot of obfuscation inherent to their creation, and the Lost as a spalt exemplify being unbound and adrift, which might interfear with the connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T17:03:19-07:00","id":1483932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483928#post1483928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross-Splat question: A Changeling's Fetch supposedly has a piece of their soul in it. Would the two count as Connected for the purposes of Space Sympathy? The Fetch has a lot of obfuscation inherent to their creation, and the Lost as a spalt exemplify being unbound and adrift, which might interfear with the connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're definitely not Connected, if only because the fetch and the changeling exist on opposite ends of a metaphysical change at least equivalent to the Awakening in intensity, and having a piece of their soul used to make it doesn't make the fetch the same being as the changeling any more than an Eidolon created using a person's soul as a sacrament would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T17:09:07-07:00","id":1483933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483928#post1483928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross-Splat question: A Changeling's Fetch supposedly has a piece of their soul in it. Would the two count as Connected for the purposes of Space Sympathy? The Fetch has a lot of obfuscation inherent to their creation, and the Lost as a spalt exemplify being unbound and adrift, which might interfear with the connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say &quot;yes&quot; with two caveats:<br /> <br /> Since the Fetch has, indeed, some inherent obfuscation, some of them <i>may</i> interfere with the spell. It wouldn't be a rule, though.<br /> <br /> And a Lost could be beyond the spell's reach just by being on the Hedge. In this case, Space wouldn't be enough.<br /> <br /> Themes aren't rules, and there's no reason to think the Lost would jeopardize Space magic in any particular way. And Fetches are the <b>most intimate connection</b> most people can imagine for a Lost, specially when you consider that the Fetch itself also has innate perceptions about their Lost arising from their intrinsic connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T17:27:19-07:00","id":1483935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483932#post1483932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're definitely not Connected, if only because the fetch and the changeling exist on opposite ends of a metaphysical change at least equivalent to the Awakening in intensity, and having a piece of their soul used to make it doesn't make the fetch the same being as the changeling any more than an Eidolon created using a person's soul as a sacrament would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I interperated it more as the sliver of soul being used to create a soulstone, than as a sacremental consumption of the sliver. The details may have changed a bit between editions, but Lost 1E gave the option of reintergrating the Fetch, which definately sounds more like a soulstone parallel to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483933#post1483933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say &quot;yes&quot; with two caveats:<br /> <br /> Since the Fetch has, indeed, some inherent obfuscation, some of them <i>may</i> interfere with the spell. It wouldn't be a rule, though.<br /> <br /> And a Lost could be beyond the spell's reach just by being on the Hedge. In this case, Space wouldn't be enough.<br /> <br /> Themes aren't rules, and there's no reason to think the Lost would jeopardize Space magic in any particular way. And Fetches are the <b>most intimate connection</b> most people can imagine for a Lost, specially when you consider that the Fetch itself also has innate perceptions about their Lost arising from their intrinsic connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. I'd argue that while themes aren't rules, they're definately symbols, and symbols have power in the Awakened world. Like Obfuscation and Shadow Names muddying a Mage's connections to the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T18:15:26-07:00","id":1483938,"title":"","content":"I think something like the creation of a changeling and its fetch is operating under unique enough circumstances and with some of what is kind of god-tier power in the mix that it should be taken as playing by its own rules when regarding the application of something like sympathetic magic, rather than extrapolated by analogy.<br /> <br /> Which is to say that a person has carte blanche to come up with whatever outcome they please for how they wish the scenario to play out.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd lean towards a distinct separation. That the Wyrd gets to mark this one being as everything about yourself that got taken away, such that they're essentially a stranger down to a metaphysical level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T18:25:58-07:00","id":1483941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483935#post1483935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I interperated it more as the sliver of soul being used to create a soulstone, than as a sacremental consumption of the sliver. The details may have changed a bit between editions, but Lost 1E gave the option of reintergrating the Fetch, which definately sounds more like a soulstone parallel to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>And 2e goes through the various options for resolving the matter of the fetch, has actual literal pieces of a changeling's soul as ludonarrative devices, and crucially <i>does not consistently provide these things from any form of dissolution of the fetch.</i><br /> <br /> The Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle specifies that changelings have Connected sympathy to their Icons. Reclaiming the fetch requires a process of understanding that would take up at least the length of a story and killing it does the opposite of improve a changeling's Clarity, while doing what an Icon does is only one suggested outcome of reintegrating the shadow.<br /> <br /> Demons who've called in a soul pact functionally own the soul that forms the basis of their cover, and the pacts that support that give the parties of the first and second parts Strong sympathy to each other; considering that most characters won't get Strong sympathy with each other without a lifelong or life-altering relationship, that's plenty.<br /> <br /> Perhaps most crucially, there's a Merit for having a particularly deep connection to your fetch, which lets the two of you share senses not unlike a mage and their familiar can, and it simply doesn't make sense for fetches to be considered Connected to their changelings by default if that is an abnormal state of affairs.<br /> <br /> It's a Strong connection. It's something made from a piece of you, not a child you're bearing or a spirit mystically bound to the low-level Bedlam spilling out of your soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T22:58:00-07:00","id":1483960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1483938#post1483938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think something like the creation of a changeling and its fetch is operating under unique enough circumstances and with some of what is kind of god-tier power in the mix that it should be taken as playing by its own rules when regarding the application of something like sympathetic magic, rather than extrapolated by analogy.<br /> <br /> Which is to say that a person has carte blanche to come up with whatever outcome they please for how they wish the scenario to play out.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd lean towards a distinct separation. That the Wyrd gets to mark this one being as everything about yourself that got taken away, such that they're essentially a stranger down to a metaphysical level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but outside of analogy, my reason for assuming the link by default stems from two other considerations:<br /> <br /> 1 - What it means to get your hands on a Fetch in the first place. To even try this scenario the Mage has to figure out its possibility and then get hold of an actual Fetch in some significant fashion. Not even just noticing their physical similarity (if it still exists) is enough, as a Mage without some awareness of the nature of the Fetch wouldn't have reason to expect such level of sympathetic connection. At the very least the Mage would have to solve the Mystery in a Fetch.<br /> <br /> That way, exploring the possibility of this connection existing means an investment in the story beyond simply asking the question, and it being true will give an adequate payoff more often than not, unless you have a better use for it in a particular case, that being the reason why I don't think the answer should be consistent (other than this inconsistent making sense for the Symbols and tropes at play).<br /> <br /> 2 - As for the nature and theme of the Fetch, its most important feature is the Confrontation with the Changeling. The Fetch is aware of the Changeling in some way as soon as the Lost arrive in the Material world. For the Changeling, how they decide to deal with the Fetch, or what they accomplish in this regard, is one of the most important questions regardless of being about a very specific relationship. The answers and possible outcomes are extremely varied, but the weight of the question is so monumental that even the decision to ignore the Fetch altogether isn't meaningless. And the Fetch is frequently equipped to force this confrontation in terms the Changeling doesn't expect.<br /> <br /> So making the Fetch a Sympathetic Link explores this characteristic of the entity and its purpose on the story, which is both an aspect of the Fetch as a game element and an in-game aspect of the Fetch as Arcadian magic. They are intertwined by Fate and Time already in one of the most close fashions. They're meant to affect each other. In a sense, giving the Mage access to this Space Sympathy isn't so much the Mage making use of a passive property of the Fetch, but the Mage being used as an instrument by the active Fate of them both, Lost and Fetch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T21:36:11-07:00","id":1484084,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this question came from my love of the Bay City Marshals. I feel like the first thing any Space-savvy Mage would ask upon hearing about the Fetch is &quot;Does this thing have Sympathy to my posse-mate?&quot; followed closely by &quot;Can I capture it for study?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T08:42:28-07:00","id":1484615,"title":"","content":"Can Time Sight perceive supernatural effects, highlighting only the duration ? An example would be that that they see the subject is affected by some kind of supernatural power that lasts a year and a day, but would have no way of knowing if its a Pledge, an Awakened spell, Promissory Pact or something else with only Time Sight. In case it can see them, would that be sufficient to target those effects with Time magic ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-21-2022, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T14:52:36-07:00","id":1484653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484615#post1484615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Time Sight perceive supernatural effects, highlighting only the duration ? An example would be that that they see the subject is affected by some kind of supernatural power that lasts a year and a day, but would have no way of knowing if its a Pledge, an Awakened spell, Promissory Pact or something else with only Time Sight. In case it can see them, would that be sufficient to target those effects with Time magic ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that remaining duration on a spell is a piece of example Deep Information, I should think the obvious answer is &quot;no.&quot;<br /> <br /> It could almost definitely provide that information through Scrutiny, but Active Time Sight just uniquely highlights supernatural effects that mess with Time, not any supernatural effect with a duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T04:23:40-07:00","id":1484691,"title":"","content":"Do you think a Knowing of Time would be able to tell how long something temporary has left?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T10:05:32-07:00","id":1484708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484691#post1484691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think a Knowing of Time would be able to tell how long something temporary has left?</div> </div> </div> </div>For things with set durations like spells and egg timers, I'd say yes.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of Surface Information, does &quot;Awakened magic&quot; include spells cast from Artifacts, Supernal entities, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T13:26:08-07:00","id":1484723,"title":"","content":"In page 61 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i>, it mentions that Kassiterum has no inclusions or weak points, plus that Siderite It is the hardest and strongest of all the Perfected metals. What does that mean in terms of creating armor ? Orichalcum's Durability cannot be reduced by nonmagical means, perfected leather grants immunity from crushing and bashing damage, perfected glass does not suffer damage from anything short of diamonds or perfected materials.<br /> <br /> But what about those two perfected metals ? While page 60 states &quot;<i>An item created with a Perfected metal still functions as its mundane counterpart, though it is created from partially-Supernal material. It has the same properties and equipment bonuses as any other mundane object of the same kind.</i>&quot;, their properties seem to imply otherwise. Would not having weaknesses or inclusions would mean that mundane means could not affect their Structure and Durability (since they are supposedly more resilient than Orichalcum) ? Perhaps that they are perfect defenses against most physical attacks (meaning fire and radiation could bypass them) ? Blacksmithing is not my forte, so I am wondering if a melee oriented mage could make higher quality armor from perfected metals (probably with extensive research to account for weight and concealment).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-22-2022, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T14:24:32-07:00","id":1484726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484708#post1484708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For things with set durations like spells and egg timers, I'd say yes.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of Surface Information, does &amp;quot;Awakened magic&amp;quot; include spells cast from Artifacts, Supernal entities, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd lean towards anything that ultimately originates from the Supernal (and to a lesser extent, the Abyss) falls under the purview of Awakened Magic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T04:53:25-07:00","id":1484766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484723#post1484723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would not having weaknesses or inclusions would mean that mundane means could not affect their Structure and Durability (since they are supposedly more resilient than Orichalcum) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the mundane means to reduce Durability anyway?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps that they are perfect defenses against most physical attacks (meaning fire and radiation could bypass them) ? Blacksmithing is not my forte, so I am wondering if a melee oriented mage could make higher quality armor from perfected metals (probably with extensive research to account for weight and concealment).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in the event that a person is wearing full plate armour, damage that gets through to them is assumed to be striking a necessarily uncovered point like part of the face anyway. Some kinds of blows damage by means of transmission of force rather than penetrating tissue, you can still be hurt like that no matter how indestructible armour is (and I don't think Siderite comes across as quite that hard).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T13:58:16-07:00","id":1484805,"title":"","content":"This will very much be a vanity question. You can't make lasting permanent changes to your appearance with Life, but can heal damage and expunge health aberrations like illness or parasites. Could you target and permanently remove moles? Moles are caused when cells in the skin called melanocytes grow in clusters, and VERY prone to becoming... abnormal. Or cancerous. Could you Fray moles away or Rule the cells into dispersing? <br /> <br /> Likewise, could you straighten someone's teeth? We do it the mundane way with pressure and time, so could you conceivably make a Lasting change using Arcana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 06-23-2022, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T09:02:00-07:00","id":1484970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484805#post1484805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This will very much be a vanity question. You can't make lasting permanent changes to your appearance with Life, but can heal damage and expunge health aberrations like illness or parasites. Could you target and permanently remove moles? Moles are caused when cells in the skin called melanocytes grow in clusters, and VERY prone to becoming... abnormal. Or cancerous. Could you Fray moles away or Rule the cells into dispersing?<br /> <br /> Likewise, could you straighten someone's teeth? We do it the mundane way with pressure and time, so could you conceivably make a Lasting change using Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically it feels more appropriate for such changes to be non-Lasting as the direct effect of a spell; you could replicate and enhance mundane methods by e.g. healing the damage involved in breaking and re-setting bones, accelerating the time in which they heal, etc, but symbolically moles that haven't turned into malignant tumors don't feel like something that the likes of Purge Illness should catch in a single casting. Regular use of magic to supplement or simulate healthy living, sure, but the things that spells make Lasting tend to be knock-on consequences like &quot;you burned that chair&quot; or &quot;that wound has healed,&quot; not &quot;you're more conventionally attractive.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T09:39:19-07:00","id":1484971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484766#post1484766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are the mundane means to reduce Durability anyway?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think in the event that a person is wearing full plate armour, damage that gets through to them is assumed to be striking a necessarily uncovered point like part of the face anyway. Some kinds of blows damage by means of transmission of force rather than penetrating tissue, you can still be hurt like that no matter how indestructible armour is (and I don't think Siderite comes across as quite that hard).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a powerful acid could reduce Durability. <br /> <br /> I was more wondering if a golem with a siderite outer shell could easily deal with explosions, melee weapons, armor piercing rounds and so on. Since siderite is stated to be the hardest perfected metal, that would mean its more durable than perfected lead, which is incredibly resilient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T13:07:33-07:00","id":1484981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484970#post1484970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically it feels more appropriate for such changes to be non-Lasting as the direct effect of a spell; you could replicate and enhance mundane methods by e.g. healing the damage involved in breaking and re-setting bones, accelerating the time in which they heal, etc, but symbolically moles that haven't turned into malignant tumors don't feel like something that the likes of Purge Illness should catch in a single casting. Regular use of magic to supplement or simulate healthy living, sure, but the things that spells make Lasting tend to be knock-on consequences like &amp;quot;you burned that chair&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;that wound has healed,&amp;quot; not &amp;quot;you're more conventionally attractive.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How about straightening teeth? Maybe a Forces spell to apply pressure as if you were wearing braces? Add in Time to accelerate the rate of change, and maybe Life to keep the teeth from shattering?<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, an Awakened dentist might make for an interesting minor NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T14:48:28-07:00","id":1484990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484981#post1484981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about straightening teeth? Maybe a Forces spell to apply pressure as if you were wearing braces? Add in Time to accelerate the rate of change, and maybe Life to keep the teeth from shattering?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the sort of thing I meant by replicating and enhancing mundane methods, yeah. The key thing is that the spell itself isn't directly producing the outcome \u2014 accelerating time may make the process of letting your flesh and bone adjust go faster, but the spell isn't built with an Imago of &quot;my teeth are straighter&quot; just because that's what you're using the secret laws of Time to facilitate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T16:12:41-07:00","id":1484998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484971#post1484971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a powerful acid could reduce Durability. <br /> <br /> I was more wondering if a golem with a siderite outer shell could easily deal with explosions, melee weapons, armor piercing rounds and so on. Since siderite is stated to be the hardest perfected metal, that would mean its more durable than perfected lead, which is incredibly resilient.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd still worry about the joints, unless the outer layer is some kind of seamless, flexible coating","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T19:49:40-07:00","id":1485004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1484998#post1484998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd still worry about the joints, unless the outer layer is some kind of seamless, flexible coating</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, doing it with siderite alone would be though. A solution could be to use a Weaving to transfer the properties of an MR fluid to it, then apply a light coating, increasing defense without sacrificing flexibility. But that might lead to the golem being paralyzed if it was dispelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T23:01:36-07:00","id":1485016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485004#post1485004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, doing it with siderite alone would be though. A solution could be to use a Weaving to transfer the properties of an MR fluid to it, then apply a light coating, increasing defense without sacrificing flexibility. But that might lead to the golem being paralyzed if it was dispelled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, cover the joints in Siderite chainmail. It'll stop the worst of the melee attacks, but you'll still run into problems with impact-based damage. Which would be a problem with Siderite skin anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T14:16:07-07:00","id":1485142,"title":"","content":"What Practices would the spells Forge Godsend and Forge Doom from 1ed fall under ? Can they be translated to 2ed ? I imagine maybe Patterning, as a variation of Chaos Mastery perhaps ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T19:38:17-07:00","id":1485159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485142#post1485142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Practices would the spells Forge Godsend and Forge Doom from 1ed fall under ? Can they be translated to 2ed ? I imagine maybe Patterning, as a variation of Chaos Mastery perhaps ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Godsend reads like 2e's Miracle, but you could probably get away with Chaos Mastery. For Forge Doom, you could spoof it with a Condition, so probably a Patterning-hex.<br /> <br /> Tangentially-related question - Say I Befuddle someone's resistance stat down enough to affect them with a Potency-dependent spell like Grave Misfortune. If Grave Misfortune was cast to last longer than Befuddle, and the target's resistance stat reverts to normal while the Grave Misfortune is still active, is Grave Misfortune's effective Potency propotionally decreased? Or do dampening effects of Withstand only impact initial casting? The &quot;overcome Withstand at full Potency&quot; effect from the Exceptional Success table could be read either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 06-27-2022, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T19:57:06-07:00","id":1485162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485159#post1485159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially-related question - Say I Befuddle someone's resistance stat down enough to affect them with a Potency-dependent spell like Grave Misfortune. If Grave Misfortune was cast to last longer than Befuddle, and the target's resistance stat reverts to normal while the Grave Misfortune is still active, is Grave Misfortune's effective Potency propotionally decreased? Or do dampening effects of Withstand only impact initial casting? The &quot;overcome Withstand at full Potency&quot; effect from the Exceptional Success table could be read either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a spell's subject's Withstand rating changes, the effective Potency is recalculated accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T20:26:40-07:00","id":1485163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485162#post1485162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a spell's subject's Withstand rating changes, the effective Potency is recalculated accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind pointing me to the relevant book page? The Withstand section was a bit ambiguous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T05:38:47-07:00","id":1485184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485159#post1485159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Godsend reads like 2e's Miracle, but you could probably get away with Chaos Mastery. For Forge Doom, you could spoof it with a Condition, so probably a Patterning-hex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Grave Misfortune already Forge Doom's (better) successor? Which would make a 2e Godsend spell probably Weaving?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T06:43:17-07:00","id":1485186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485184#post1485184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Grave Misfortune already Forge Doom's (better) successor? Which would make a 2e Godsend spell probably Weaving?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, <i>Grave Misfortune</i> is target specific. But a doom makes all sources of damage worse for those that qualify for it that are in its presence. So the Banisher's Bane, for example, would make it so anyone who had killed a mage would take more damage from everything in its presence. Punches, falling rocks, explosions, poison, etc. I see it like the difference between the <i>Give Me That</i> spell (adding the property of &quot;this item makes people obsessed&quot;) and applying the Obsessive condition with a Patterning of Mind (this person is obsessed with a given thing). That is how I understand it, based on the 1ed text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-28-2022, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T20:21:26-07:00","id":1485249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485186#post1485186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of, <i>Grave Misfortune</i> is target specific. But a doom makes all sources of damage worse for those that qualify for it that are in its presence. So the Banisher's Bane, for example, would make it so anyone who had killed a mage would take more damage from everything in its presence. Punches, falling rocks, explosions, poison, etc. I see it like the difference between the <i>Give Me That</i> spell (adding the property of &amp;quot;this item makes people obsessed&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and applying the Obsessive condition with a Patterning of Mind (this person is obsessed with a given thing). That is how I understand it, based on the 1ed text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting <i>Give Me That</i> on a <i>person</i> sounds like a recipe for a miserable day. Especially if you're in a city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T21:05:48-07:00","id":1485252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485249#post1485249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Casting <i>Give Me That</i> on a <i>person</i> sounds like a recipe for a miserable day. Especially if you're in a city.</div> </div> </div> </div>When targeting a specific person, another option is to Weave the property <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e7JbMWvPhGY\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;this is the most dangerous person in the world&quot;</a>. <br /> <br /> I imagine it would be the equivalent of living under the permanent effect of Disquiet or a Blood Hunt, which all things considered would be one of the most horrible curses to inflict on anyone, because it escalates by isolating the target from their everyday life, and becomes exponentially worse if any supernaturals they meet can't make the save.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T22:08:38-07:00","id":1485258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485252#post1485252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When targeting a specific person, another option is to Weave the property <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e7JbMWvPhGY&amp;quot;]&amp;quot;this</a> is the most dangerous person in the world&amp;quot;[/URL]. <br /> <br /> I imagine it would be the equivalent of living under the permanent effect of Disquiet or a Blood Hunt, which all things considered would be one of the most horrible curses to inflict on anyone, because it escalates by isolating the target from their everyday life, and becomes exponentially worse if any supernaturals they meet can't make the save.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you were to make the connotation positive (&quot;This is a desirable mate&quot;) you'd still have a bad day. There was an Episode of Eureka like that, and a comic or two. Or the ending of Perfume! God that was a wierd book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T06:16:28-07:00","id":1485279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485186#post1485186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of, <i>Grave Misfortune</i> is target specific. But a doom makes all sources of damage worse for those that qualify for it that are in its presence. So the Banisher's Bane, for example, would make it so anyone who had killed a mage would take more damage from everything in its presence. Punches, falling rocks, explosions, poison, etc. I see it like the difference between the <i>Give Me That</i> spell (adding the property of &quot;this item makes people obsessed&quot;) and applying the Obsessive condition with a Patterning of Mind (this person is obsessed with a given thing). That is how I understand it, based on the 1ed text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forge Doom is also target specific, though:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While in direct confrontation with a doom or while acting within or being targeted by the parameters of a doom (being struck in the wounded leg or getting in trouble with a woman\u2019s large boyfriend while hitting on her in a club), any damage dice suffered by <b>the subject</b> are increased by the spell\u2019s successes. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T09:19:37-07:00","id":1485294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485279#post1485279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forge Doom is also target specific, though:</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I am very confused, I was thinking of the Artifact spear from page 221 of the <i>Adamantine Arrow</i> book, which is the Doom of anyone with Morality 5 or less, or the user's Doom if they attack someone of Morality 8 or higher. Even when accounting that Artifacts do weird things, I thought it made sense to use the spell like that. The bull headed staff was the doom of Zahak and his followers, or a blade can exist that is the Doom of all who rule tyrannically. It sounded like something resonant with Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-29-2022, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T18:01:08-07:00","id":1485580,"title":"","content":"Signs of Sorcery mentions in passing that experts can tell if a spell was relinquished safely or unsafely. I'm assuming then that it's also possible to discern the method of safe Relinquishment used, such as Sacrificial Relinquishment, Broken Relinquishment, Willpower dot sacrifice, etc. If that's the case, how do y'all intemperate the general signs? Imago stained with ephemeral blood on a Sacrificial Relinquishment, for example?<br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelated rabbit hole-ramble - what would Perfected or Crucible-affected food be like? If you used Hone The Perfected Form or Crucible on ingredients before, say, making a batch of cookies, are the resulting cookies Perfected Cookies? Eidoforms? Something else entirely? If you let the duration on said spell-affected ingredients lapse once the baking is complete, would the resulting cookie be better than if no spells had been cast at all? Can the spells even survive the mixing and baking process, or is their subject too changed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-01-2022, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T20:10:36-07:00","id":1485586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485580#post1485580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Signs of Sorcery mentions in passing that experts can tell if a spell was relinquished safely or unsafely. I'm assuming then that it's also possible to discern the method of safe Relinquishment used, such as Sacrificial Relinquishment, Broken Relinquishment, Willpower dot sacrifice, etc. If that's the case, how do y'all intemperate the general signs? Imago stained with ephemeral blood on a Sacrificial Relinquishment, for example?<br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelated rabbit hole-ramble - what would Perfected food be like? If you used Hone The Perfected Form on ingredients before, say, making a batch of cookies, are the resulting cookies Perfected Cookies? Eidoforms? Something else entirely? If you let the duration on said Perfected ingredients -or just Crucible-affected ingredients- lapse once the baking is complete, would the resulting cookie be better than if no spells had been cast at all? Can the spells even survive the mixing and baking process, or is their subject too changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine there are multiple interpretations, since how a mage experiences magic is subjective, but here are some ideas, alongside ones for Surface Information under Focused Sight:<br /> <br /> <b>Sacrificial Relinquishment:</b> The Imago appears to be made of materials used in tombstones, with cryptic words for the means of death incribed as a bizzare epitaph (tecpatl, breath drinker, the thorned plume cuts, moon scented maw, etc). Under Focused Sight, observers see shadows near the Imago form into a stylized shadow puppet show of the moment.<br /> <br /> <b>Reaping Relinquishment:</b> The Imago writhes as something beneath the surface tries to get out. Sometimes a face jumps at observers, trying to convey a message desperately, its jaw too mangled for their lips to be read. Under Focused Sight the Imago cracks, flooding the senses of observers with the scent of brine, revealing a tortured humanoid shadow trying to flee, only to be pulled back in by what looks like an animated wall of the Great Below, before it seals itself back perfectly.<br /> <br /> <b>Broken Relinquishment:</b> The Imago sometimes tears to reveal a mouth, screaming the unfiltered, incohesive internal thoughts of the victim, in their mother tongue (since its something people can default to it when under extreme emotional stress), at the moment of trauma. Under Focused Sight an eye tears open through the Imago, its gestures replicating the ones in the moment, other times a hand reaches out, desperately reacting to the looping trauma that piece of soul is bound to.<br /> <br /> I think perfected food would always be fresh, cooked perfectly, last indefinitely, maximize nutritional value and invalidate drawbacks. Perfected fugu does not poison you, perfected bread never molds, perfected fruits will taste as if just picked at the peak of the season and will even become ripe if it wasn't before, meat will be smoked or aged perfectly to maximize umami, fish will become as fresh as if it was just caught, etc.<br /> <br /> I imagine the perfecting spell would correct anything that made no sense to the mage, like removing any Coca-Cola a madman used as &quot;cooking water&quot; for sphagetti, a highly traditional chef's spell might remove pineapple from pizza, make pasta al dente or the pasta not too dry (yellow to orange colored pasta has been speedily and excessively dried to hasten the production process), remove chili jam from egg fried rice and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-02-2022, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T09:40:12-07:00","id":1485696,"title":"","content":"Would it be possible to use a Weaving of Time to allow scouring of a subject's history ? Essentially it would diminish a skill by each dot scoured, if it goes beneath zero, you also temporarily forget any rotes with that skill mudra. Each scoured dot would &quot;heal&quot; at the same rate as lethal damage. A comparative effect is how the creations of the Watchmaker from <i>Summoners</i> are fueled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T21:55:38-07:00","id":1485744,"title":"","content":"I believe this is a simple question: <b>With what Arcana and what Practice you can create a illusion of something?</b> I have a player that wants to create a illusionist, creating fake images and fake bridges.<br /> <br /> He [and I for that matter] don't care for more efficient or useful practices or uses of arcanas (&quot;if you can create a bridge with Matter Five, why would you create a fake bridge?&quot;), and Mind don't convince me enough because you can create a Illusion for a specific target (or Scale of target) but not a fake image that exist in the world but is not solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T23:01:40-07:00","id":1485747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485696#post1485696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be possible to use a Weaving of Time to allow scouring of a subject's history ? Essentially it would diminish a skill by each dot scoured, if it goes beneath zero, you also temporarily forget any rotes with that skill mudra. Each scoured dot would &quot;heal&quot; at the same rate as lethal damage. A comparative effect is how the creations of the Watchmaker from <i>Summoners</i> are fueled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally lean towards having to Temporally target the points where the subject learned the skills - their days playing a sport for Atheletics, for example. I would NOT allow it to affect rotes tho - you can have a rote you have no skill dots in, it just means you dont get the benefit of the Mudra Yantra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485744#post1485744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe this is a simple question: <b>With what Arcana and what Practice you can create a illusion of something?</b> I have a player that wants to create a illusionist, creating fake images and fake bridges.<br /> <br /> He [and I for that matter] don't care for more efficient or useful practices or uses of arcanas (&quot;if you can create a bridge with Matter Five, why would you create a fake bridge?&quot;), and Mind don't convince me enough because you can create a Illusion for a specific target (or Scale of target) but not a fake image that exist in the world but is not solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>For making an ephemeral illusion in the vein of DnD-style Illusion spells, Mind is your go-to for things that only the targets can see, while Forces would be a good candidate for visual-but-intangible phenomena. A Forces spell could make some heat-haze bending of light - call it &quot;Mirage&quot;. Prime was the illusion Arcana in 1e, but 2e doesnt have a specified purview for holograms. Since it's the domain of &quot;truth&quot;, I'd personally say that either Prime is incapable of produceing holograms, or it's a Fraying/Unraveling Practice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T03:43:33-07:00","id":1485758,"title":"","content":"Shadow Name can be used as a Yantra. As Above So Below can be used to enhance a targeted Yantra. Assuming you &quot;targeted&quot; a Shadow Name with As Above So Below, can the spell be observed? That is, Spells cast on a target can be viewed and analyzed by Prime Mage Sight, but where is &quot;Shadow Name&quot; located? <br /> <br /> Would it be you, since you <i>are</i> your Shadow Name, so long as you work under it's auspices? If so, does it mean that the spell becomes occluded whenever you shift into your Fallen identity?<br /> <br /> Would it be some piece of your Onieros, since the Shadow Name is a part of your identity, and plausibly has a manifestation in your psyche?<br /> <br /> Would it just be some nebulous &quot;target&quot;, that can't be studied beyond maybe strange whisps that you can spot in the corner of your Mage Sight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-05-2022, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T07:04:17-07:00","id":1485767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485758#post1485758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow Name can be used as a Yantra. As Above So Below can be used to enhance a targeted Yantra. Assuming you &quot;targeted&quot; a Shadow Name with As Above So Below, can the spell be observed? Spells cast on a target can be viewed and analyzed by Prime Mage Sight, but where is &quot;Shadow Name&quot; located?<br /> <br /> Would it be you, since you <i>are</i> your Shadow Name, so long as you work under it's auspices? If so, does it mean that the spell becomes occluded whenever you shift into your Fallen identity?<br /> <br /> Would it be some piece of your Onieros, since the Shadow Name is a part of your identity, and plausibly has a manifestation in your psyche?<br /> <br /> Would it just be some nebulous &quot;target&quot;, that can't be studied beyond maybe strange whisps that you can spot in the corner of your Mage Sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the rote removal is excessive, but I thought it was an interesting property the summoned entity had.<br /> <br /> Looking at page 122 of the core book, the Shadow Name generally falls under the Persona yantra. Which means the mage (or cabal if applied to the Cabal Theme merit), plus any trappings or tools related to the Shadow Name are brought metaphysically closer to that particular symbolism. So if Vulcan has a hammer he brought closer to his Shadow Name, its going to be great for spells that shape, craft and manipulate flame. But if someone tries to use it in a spell to channel lightning or one to magically control its trajectory, it only provides the normal bonus, with no dice trick, because those are outside of Vulcan's symbolic portfolio and are closer to Thor's.<br /> <br /> Based on the information on page 292, it location seems to be widely encompassing. You walk as that symbolic persona until the Supernal acknowledges it and then they start to walk like you, which is when you gain the benefit of the merit and can build upon (or create, in case of an original one) its legend. Its in your sympathetic network, since it separates mundane persona from the shadow persona, plus Space can erase it entirely via <i>Unnaming</i>. It can be found in the Astral, because it must be deeply ingrained in your Oneiros to affect self perception and it has your correspondences outside of it (like in the Temenos). Its in your Fate pattern, drawing mythological correspondences towards you and rewards you for playing out your own spin on the legend. Its part of your Prime pattern, becoming part of your true magical self, shaping your Nimbus (and Long Term Nimbus) just as much as your personality, magical style and Legacy do.<br /> <br /> So the answer seems to be that its located on the mage and exists even when in their mundane persona, because its drawing a metaphysical line to distinguish the two. You can use it as a yantra when in the persona, so long as you stick to your mage identity's behavior, but its probably Wiser to be minimalistic and discrete to keep in line with its symbolic purpose. All the mage's spells are just as easy to see as before, its just that anything that connects them to their mundane persona or tries to see them while in that persona becomes more difficult.<br /> <br /> More information on how this extra level of secrecy translates mechanically and how it interacts with Occultation can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1256484#post1256484\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-04-2022, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T08:07:57-07:00","id":1485775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485744#post1485744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe this is a simple question: <b>With what Arcana and what Practice you can create a illusion of something?</b> I have a player that wants to create a illusionist, creating fake images and fake bridges.<br /> <br /> He [and I for that matter] don't care for more efficient or useful practices or uses of arcanas (&quot;if you can create a bridge with Matter Five, why would you create a fake bridge?&quot;), and Mind don't convince me enough because you can create a Illusion for a specific target (or Scale of target) but not a fake image that exist in the world but is not solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Weaving of Forces should permit &quot;hologram&quot; type illusions, basically an advanced version of Control Light and Control Sound combined. I wrote up a spell to this effect in the Creative Thaumaturgy thread a little while back.<br /> <br /> The Mind Patterning spell Hallucination puts an image into the mind of the subject; if you cast it with Advanced Scale and have it affect everyone in the Area, for most purposes it would be a stand-alone illusion that anyone can see, so long as they're not too far away.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T10:15:13-07:00","id":1485780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485747#post1485747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime was the illusion Arcana in 1e, but 2e doesnt have a specified purview for holograms. Since it's the domain of &amp;quot;truth&amp;quot;, I'd personally say that either Prime is incapable of produceing holograms, or it's a Fraying/Unraveling Practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e Prime can make use of the Truth to create platonic forms. The supernal ideal of an object (And Eidolons with mastery). The are solid, and really exist, until they run out of mana... Or in the case of the Eidolon the Spell's duration runs out.<br /> <br /> So it may not qualify for what most of us might consider an illusion (kinda green lantern powers) but might work for what altidiya was askig for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485744#post1485744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Mind don't convince me enough because you can create a Illusion for a specific target (or Scale of target) but not a fake image that exist in the world but is not solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the answer, Mind can give hallucinations, Forces can give intangible illusion, Prime can give solid magical constructs which eventually vanish (Prime + forces can make these magical constructs not appear obviously magical).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T16:10:25-07:00","id":1485805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>altidiya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485744#post1485744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe this is a simple question: <b>With what Arcana and what Practice you can create a illusion of something?</b> I have a player that wants to create a illusionist, creating fake images and fake bridges.<br /> <br /> He [and I for that matter] don't care for more efficient or useful practices or uses of arcanas (&quot;if you can create a bridge with Matter Five, why would you create a fake bridge?&quot;), and Mind don't convince me enough because you can create a Illusion for a specific target (or Scale of target) but not a fake image that exist in the world but is not solid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1416788#post1416788\">this </a>is the spell that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23730_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23730\" data-vbnamecard=\"23730\">Scriptorian</a> mentioned, creative use of Forces can make good illusions and its necessary to make Platonic constructs appear realistic. I second the idea of Prime as a nice avenue for a master of illusions. The Reality Stalkers in 1ed has a interesting spell where they could do a Veiling of an object, similar to printing over it. Combined with some platonic items and some lucky breaks using Fate made them very good at improvising and being charlatans. A good example would be Hisoka from <i>Hunter X Hunter</i>, since all his abilities could be replicated with that Legacy. Another recent one that uses Prime in that way would be the expanded version of the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded?p=1447704#post1447704\">Nighthawks</a>.<br /> <br /> Mind has a lot of interesting things that a trickster can leverage. With a Weaving you can connect different ideas, such as connecting joy to doing a task the mage wants or shame for a topic they want the subject to hide (the <i>Passion Link</i> spell found on page 195 of <i>Guardians of the Veil</i>). <i>Memory Hole</i> and <i>Read the Depths</i>' Reach effect allow you to control how a subject perceives or remembers details of a situation. With a Patterning you can impose the Delusion condition, making them unshakingly convinced of anything, which can lead them to turn on their allies (using a capgras delusion) or even pursue a goal you set (<i>Psychic Reprogramming</i>). Depending on how much focus and resources are dedicated, a mage can achieve a more powerful version of Hallucination earlier. Put the target to sleep, control their dreams and make them forget they were put to sleep. Now use <i>One Mind, Two Thoughts</i> to continually manage their Lotus Eater Machine prison to temporarily remove them from the board, kill them via starvation or keep the powerful being in a containment it will not even want to escape.<br /> <br /> Merit wise, I would recommend the Familiar merit so they can get a Waxman (<i>Astral Realms</i> page 104) or an equivalent, like a spirit of hallucinations or a ghost with such a portfolio, like a stage magician. A Retainer with a field like special effects, practical magic or conning could also be interesting. If they really want to go all in with the theme, they could use mundane misdirection to make the Awakened magic even easier or more believable, in which case Professional Training in Subterfuge, Larceny and Stealth could be useful in setting up their trickery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-04-2022, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T16:30:27-07:00","id":1485808,"title":"","content":"Dave Brookshaw has often said that Forces effectively took over the purview of what would generally be called illusions. I don't really think it needs qualifiers such as working like a mirage, any more than the Invisibility spell needs to work on a basis of bending light waves in some fashion that could be exploited to reveal itself. Invisibility simply proceeds directly to the idea of becoming unseen under a purview of the medium for seeing stuff falling under Forces, so I should think creating a non-existent source of image comes under much the same logic. Weaving transforms ambient light into the image you want it to be, and there it is.<br /> <br /> I do think illusions in any form under Awakening's systems are going to be a bit limited by a lack of innate capacity to respond or perform complex actions. I think a mage might be able to cast an additional spell upon their illusion to puppet it directly, but it's not really a construct that can be left alone and expected to, say, have a conversation with somebody. In this setting, that level of adaptability in a spell belongs to archmastery (although you might get close if you have the Arcana to, say, conjure up a mind that can be attached to your illusory construct to puppet it on your behalf).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T17:21:30-07:00","id":1485866,"title":"","content":"What do Proximi use to determine the increase in primary factor for their Blessings ? Do they receive no bonus by default ? Space Blessings have no access to sympathetic range, correct ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T20:42:56-07:00","id":1485877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485866#post1485866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do Proximi use to determine the increase in primary factor for their Blessings ? Do they receive no bonus by default ? Space Blessings have no access to sympathetic range, correct ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read the details on page 307 as meaning they have their Willpower as a dice pool, but no &quot;free&quot; advances along any primary factors like a Mage would. I also read it as not granting Attainments, since they don't actually have any Arcana dots. House Rules might override that for more interesting retainers, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T23:22:01-07:00","id":1485889,"title":"","content":"Is Words of Truth supposed to be cast on &quot;Mage plus any designated targets they want to affect&quot;? Or is it a radius-affecting spell that radiates from the target, like Incognito Presence?<br /> <br /> The way it reads in the Core book is the former; only designated targets can hear and understand you perfectly, or be affected by the Reach effect. But the Attainment entry for the Tyrian Archons in Nameless and Accursed reads as the latter; anyone in a reasonable proximity is affected, like a Mage waking around with Incognito Presence up.<br /> <br /> Edit: OK, Tessie's logic makes sense. Ouch for the Archons tho - Words of Truth as a normal Scale-targeting spell is weak for a Legacy that implies powerful oration. Plus, the Reach effect for their subordinates is kinda pointless. You can only affect one person you can touch, and it only lasts around a turn. You could bump up either scale or duration -or both- a step or two at higher Prime, but it still means that the Inspired/Guilty condition will be fleeting, at best. You could move it to the third Attainment to get another Reach to play with, although the Apprentice Attainment doesn't have an easy replacement.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, The Chronologues have the same issue. That seems to be an issue with most of the published Legacy Attainments that affect other people - most of them either don't last long enough to have a real impact, don't have enough Potency to affect most people, or affect too small a scale compared to their stated purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-06-2022, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T23:35:17-07:00","id":1485890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1485889#post1485889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Words of Truth supposed to be cast on &amp;quot;Mage plus any designated targets they want to affect&amp;quot;? Or is it a radius-affecting spell that radiates from the target, like Incognito Presence?<br /> <br /> The way it reads in the Core book is the former; only designated targets can hear and understand you perfectly, or be affected by the Reach effect. But the Attainment entry for the Tyrian Archons in Nameless and Accursed reads as the latter; anyone in a reasonable proximity is affected, like a Mage waking around with Incognito Presence up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the spell and the attainment calls those who are affected subjects, meaning they have had the spell/attainment cast on them.<br /> Also, unlike Words of Truth, Incognito Presence has a Mana cost to balance out that it affects everyone around the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T08:10:48-07:00","id":1486040,"title":"","content":"Could a Supernal entity with the appropriate manifestations theoretically Claim a sleepwalker? I'm thinking it'd take multiple summonings to get the necessary repeated possessions, but once it does, do you suppose it'd be safe from the corpus damage of being in the Fallen world in the same way other ephemeral entities are safe from essence bleed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27146-elifloof","name":"EliFloof","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T08:31:18-07:00","id":1486043,"title":"","content":"Supernal entities aren't ephemeral entities and don't have Manifestations. The Invisible Entities section is very careful about when it uses the word &quot;ephemeral.&quot;<br /> <br /> There probably are other forms of intrusion into the Fallen World than traditional supernal summonings, though they're unlikely to look like an ephemeral entity using Manifestations like Claim. Ochemata, for example, are detailed in Signs of Sorcery as extruded avatars of supernal gods.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T09:32:50-07:00","id":1486046,"title":"","content":"I remember there was one in <i>Summoners</i> that could survive the Fallen World. You offered a temporal sympathy &quot;strand&quot; of the time of death of a person as its trial, then it would take the person's appearance and mannerisms, acting as a surrogate. There always would be a flaw, like a different eye color, hair color, a new habit, a different voice, etc. It was protected from Fallen corrosion while doing its job and would remain until someone pointed out they were not the original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T11:29:48-07:00","id":1486052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486043#post1486043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There probably are other forms of intrusion into the Fallen World than traditional supernal summonings, though they're unlikely to look like an ephemeral entity using Manifestations like Claim. Ochemata, for example, are detailed in Signs of Sorcery as extruded avatars of supernal gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Verges can naturally have Supernal entities appear within them, and Signs also details a variety that can have cause to venture out of them to pursue an agenda. I recall that they're still subject to breaking down in the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Ochemata are modelled using Supernal entity rules, but are technically a different form of being that comes with their own metaphysical premises.<br /> <br /> Barring something weird like the Time doppleganger, I think the general principle is that Supernal beings don't really get an out from the Abyss yawning over them. An ephemeral entity can stave off decay via possession because being housed in flesh provides something it otherwise lacks that makes it soluble in material reality, but a mortal body (and I think not anything else) isn't going to help a Supernal being around the fact that its natural environment is perfect level and you're dragging it out into where everything's crooked, reality is poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T11:30:54-07:00","id":1486054,"title":"","content":"Also, the Bound are explicitly supernal Beings who can (and indeed must) stay in the fallen world. <br /> <br /> Of course they starve and may be driven crazy by hunger, to the point of performing (effectively) blood sacrifice on the first living thing they come across. <br /> <br /> I would assume that the change in their circumstances significantly changes their behaviour, if not also their essential being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 07-08-2022, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T13:15:11-07:00","id":1486065,"title":"","content":"I think at least they wouldn't be able to move about without a drawback. An example is the Tall Blue Man, who swore an oath to find an original tale and was protected by the Hedge when he entered the Fallen. He has diminished powers and is effectively exiled until he completes the mission, but he can exist in the Fallen. I imagine an Arcadian entity could exist that works on a similar logic, a Stygian warrior, an Aethereal lawbringer, etc.<br /> <br /> An interesting thing is that the Bound need not only be creatures. The kraken can be a Bound, but so can the Darkhold, a ritual site or a bubble of an alternate timeline. They can even be beings that are just concepts anathema to the Exarchs, like saying that in truth Chiyou is a being embodying enlightened war. There a lot of interesting things that can be done with them, even as players content with the danger their thaumavoric needs pose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-08-2022, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T16:37:04-07:00","id":1486075,"title":"","content":"I do assume that, given the references to how drained Bound are forced to return to their prison or site of their Fall, that something essential was changed within them, more than just being Supernal entites who might be stuck somewhere. This idea that exile perversely made them natural inhabitants of the Fallen World, even if in most respects they experience that as though they had to live wrapped in sand paper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T17:58:21-07:00","id":1486076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486052#post1486052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring something weird like the Time doppleganger, I think the general principle is that Supernal beings don't really get an out from the Abyss yawning over them. An ephemeral entity can stave off decay via possession because being housed in flesh provides something it otherwise lacks that makes it soluble in material reality, but a mortal body (and I think not anything else) isn't going to help a Supernal being around the fact that its natural environment is perfect level and you're dragging it out into where everything's crooked, reality is poison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes me wonder if a Supernal entity could extend its time in the Fallen World by consuming souls. Could be an interesting plot hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T08:02:27-07:00","id":1486096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486075#post1486075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do assume that, given the references to how drained Bound are forced to return to their prison or site of their Fall, that something essential was changed within them, more than just being Supernal entites who might be stuck somewhere. This idea that exile perversely made them natural inhabitants of the Fallen World, even if in most respects they experience that as though they had to live wrapped in sand paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i can't remember if it is just headcannon or not, but does the supernal not manifest the gross Arcana, so Supernal Beings would normally be outside the time stream.<br /> <br /> I'd say being force to experience time, space, forces, matter and life, might not be great for an entity not designed for them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T08:54:16-07:00","id":1486100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486096#post1486096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, i can't remember if it is just headcannon or not, but does the supernal not manifest the gross Arcana, so Supernal Beings would normally be outside the time stream.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a way I've heard <i>some</i> people talk about it, but I don't think it really fits with how the books tended to portray things, and certainly not with the greater elaboration that Second Edition has provided. There are symbols that denote Time in the Supernal, there is Fate in the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> I'd think of it as being like... your native experience of a triangle is the Platonic triangle, mathematically perfect. If you're force into contact with a real triangle, your sensitivity to the slight deviations in its angles and its lines creates a friction that is like being cut by a knife.<br /> <br /> Apply that to everything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T09:56:43-07:00","id":1486104,"title":"","content":"Aside: there being no gross Arcana expressed in the supernal doesn't mean there are no subtle Arcana expressed in the fallen. <br /> <br /> And alternatively, there being symbols to represent Time in the supernal doesn't mean Time flows in the supernal, with alternative future seperate timelines or anything that we would use to describe our understanding of time. That would coorelated with the 1e idea about retconning the Universe when an Archmaster Ascends, that their supernal symbol was always part of the supernal... I don't know if this is applicable to 2e. <br /> <br /> But i agree on the principle that Bound Supernal Entities are intrinsically different, because of their condition (whatever the nature of the Supernal is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T11:01:35-07:00","id":1486106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486104#post1486104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And alternatively, there being symbols to represent Time in the supernal doesn't mean Time flows in the supernal, with alternative future seperate timelines or anything that we would use to describe our understanding of time. That would coorelated with the 1e idea about retconning the Universe when an Archmaster Ascends, that their supernal symbol was always part of the supernal... I don't know if this is applicable to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very definitely applicable in 2e. Signs of Sorcery has a whole section on how Awakenings can produce similar retroactive changes to reality through interactions with the Lustrum generated by the Watchtower.<br /> <br /> Time and Space are experienced in the Supernal when they're imposed through a Lustrum, but otherwise the Supernal's main state of time is Now; it doesn't matter if the underpinnings of the world &quot;used to be&quot; different, they're as they are now and that informs the world they describe backwards into history, albeit with the hiccups one would expect from fiddling with fundamental forces of description via the Art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T11:23:43-07:00","id":1486107,"title":"","content":"Does that make a Lustrum the reverse of a supernal verge? Imposing something of the fallen into the supernal? (And by equivalence, one could theorize, that the function of a supernal verge was to allow Supernal Entities experience the fallen directly... Though they don't have watchtowers to sign... )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 07-09-2022, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T14:52:55-07:00","id":1486115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486107#post1486107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that make a Lustrum the reverse of a supernal verge? Imposing something of the fallen into the supernal? (And by equivalence, one could theorize, that the function of a supernal verge was to allow Supernal Entities experience the fallen directly... Though they don't have watchtowers to sign... )</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more like Focused Mage Sight perceptible to more than one person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery, Introduction, p14-15, &quot;Advanced Supernal Cosmology&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages often speak of one Supernal World and five Supernal Realms defined by Path. Others of five Worlds and one Realm. In truth, there\u2019s as many Worlds as mages and only one Realm, but both can be divided into five parts. The Supernal Realm is all the symbols of everything that can exist. Each of the five Paths reveals a large set of those symbols, which are then experienced by a mage looking into the Supernal World with her Sight and viewing phenomena they define. It\u2019s easy to think of Pandemonium as separate to the Aether, Arcadia, Primal Wild, and Stygia based on the experiences of mages in the Fallen World, but there\u2019s absolutely no evidence to suggest that the Supernal Realm is so subdivided, and lots of implication from archmasters and Exarchal sources that it isn\u2019t. Those sources instead refer to individual symbolic landscapes classed by barely understood criteria: <u>Dhatus, Exarchates, Cintamani</u>, and other, rarer terms. <b>The best known, thanks to the Corpus Mysteriorum using it, is <u>Lustrum</u>, defined in its pages as the translation of a single Supernal symbol into a phenomenon a Fallen being can interact with. Awakened theoreticians describe Lustrums as the reverse of more familiar things like Shadow Names and Yantras \u2014 while the Awakened spend great effort putting themselves and their work in Supernal terms, a Lustrum is the Supernal Realm putting on a mask of being a place, thing, or being. The only ones most mages will ever encounter are their Watchtowers, during their Awakenings. Outside of bizarre Mysteries involving deep Emanation Realms, mages only glimpse other Lustrums in Awakenings gone terribly wrong or in the actions of extremely powerful Supernal Entities.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lustrums first showed up under that name in Imperial Mysteries, as things archmasters needed to impose on the Supernal through an act of will to navigate it for any length of time and things that Supernal Gods could create as shelter for guests, should they feel the inclination; being in the Supernal without the protection of a Lustrum will cause it to annihilate and/or absorb you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-09-2022, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T15:15:11-07:00","id":1486117,"title":"","content":"The Lustrum is like a filter. In the Supernal, if you cannot find yourself amidst the symbols of everything, then you dissolve into everything. Think of it as a more extreme version of the Ecstatic Winds. Its also the reason that while Emanations can have direct entrances to the Supernal at their very depths, no one tries to use them, because regular mages have no clue how to survive that.<br /> <br /> Normally you require at least an archmage candidate who is starting to grok the idea of Imperial magic to create one. The Watchtowers have a Lustrum that acts as generic filter, allowing the Lucid to understand and connect to certain specific sets of symbols. The downside is that they are not as personalized as a proper archmage's Lustrum, so they provide consistent results rather than optimal ones for the person (which is why every Arcanum is Ruling for an archmage and they are far stronger in Clashes of Wills).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-09-2022, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T15:20:06-07:00","id":1486118,"title":"","content":"Ok, so it is in the Supernal, it is described like the opposite of a Yantra/shadow name, and it does create an area around which you can survive.<br /> <br /> Is there a different name for the area around a Lustrum? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486115#post1486115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more like Focused Mage Sight perceptible to more than one person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean. When someone awakens, do other mages who happen to be there see the Lustrum and interact with the space?<br /> <br /> I think i am more confused now, since the Supernal in 2e is more an overlay on reality than actual physical realm (like Emanation Realms...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T15:46:22-07:00","id":1486120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486118#post1486118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a different name for the area around a Lustrum?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lustrum <i>is</i> the area. Every part of the directly-experienced Supernal that's not being interpreted as a Lustrum is just the Supernal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure what you mean. When someone awakens, do other mages who happen to be there see the Lustrum and interact with the space? </div> </div> </div>Focused Mage Sight sees the Supernal through the object being Scrutinized, in contrast to seeing the object in the context of the Supernal; a Lustrum is the Supernal interpreted as a scene. Mages can describe what they see in their Focused Sight to other mages, or convey it through their memory, but Opacity is tracked separately for every mage observing a Mystery and Mage Sight is a personal experience.<br /> <br /> A Lustrum is the same place for everybody occupying it, whether it's the Cintamani of a collaborating archmaster (for which the characters must deliberately seek to align their experience, else they will merely be interpreting the same Supernal symbol in different ways), the foyer of a hospitable True God, or the Adyton of an Awakening being intruded upon by another mage who shares the Prospect's potential Path through very lucky uses of Focused Mage Sight (it requires an exceptional success on a Revelation roll for what counts as an Opacity 6 Mystery).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T12:24:42-07:00","id":1486174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486118#post1486118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think i am more confused now, since the Supernal in 2e is more an overlay on reality than actual physical realm</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in a sense, but it's also still supposed to be distinct enough that Ascension matters.<br /> <br /> I mean, in the very rare cases where it matters at all to mages who are not archmasters (Irises in the heart of Emanations are rare and difficult enough to find and approach as it is), the question of &quot;where&quot; you might end up, whether it be some totally disconnected distant place or something immediately corresponding to where you were a moment before, is going to be rendered a bit moot by the fact that there's nothing you can do to keep from being annihilated to the point that you might never have existed if you go through.<br /> <br /> Still, I think it's a bit of an error to look at what Active Mage Sight reveals and think of the Supernal as being like the Shadow. When you look at that level upon something and see, say, a spiralling dance of fair folk, you're not seeing something that is literally happening in that exact spot on the other side of the Abyss, you're getting information about the essence of what is at work there conveyed through symbols.<br /> <br /> I also think some ways in which the Supernal might be seen as overlaying the Phenomenal are complicated by something like what all five Realms say about Space, namely that distance is really more of a perceptual thing emerging out of a sense of intimacy. With that in mind, is a fairy circle seen in New York really something like 3000 Supernal miles away from the same symbol perceived in Los Angeles? Can you really say if it isn't the actual same Supernal process that is applying to two (or more) Phenomenal places simultaneously?<br /> <br /> In any case, the Lustrum mostly matters for archmasters, who don't really travel to the Supernal as though it was a distinct physical place so much as they tune the frequency of their existence until it functions on the more abstract level of the Supernal (even if many of them experience this in terms of walking along their Golden Road, because the symbolism matters). It's just that once an archmaster does so, it becomes necessary to engage with one's reality by grasping for relevant concepts and willing them to assume a comprehensible symbolic form, and where engagement with the Supernal over a period of time tends to require creating a chain of Lustrums.<br /> <br /> The very idea of an area immediately surrounding the Lustrum is complicated by the fact that experiencing space in terms of physical distinctions is really only something that takes place inside the Lustrum. Beyond the boundaries of the scene that the archmaster has created, there is everything and nothing all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T02:00:22-07:00","id":1486209,"title":"","content":"Question for your subjective opinions - in your vision of the Fallen World, how widespread is it for members of one Order to learn the Order-specific merit of another? Say, a Silver Ladder learning Adamant Hand, or a Mystagog learning Techn\u00e9?<br /> <br /> As written, it's possible to do so by working closely with one Order, and attaining Order Status 1. You can't go any higher, but that's all you need. In terms of theme though, you might run into symbolic issues with everything but Adamant Hand - the other merits are based deeply in Order-dependent philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T05:11:33-07:00","id":1486214,"title":"","content":"The First Edition Mysterium book outright said that not being part of the Order anymore disconnected one from the egregore. It was part of a sense of... you need to be immersed in the lifestyle and rituals to have the kind of resonance that connects you into these things. For Lex Magica, I think there would be the added matter of having rescinded some of the symbolic authority that is the basis by which you can leverage those laws anyway (much like how, even if you stay in the Order, you couldn't use the Merit without an appropriate title).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T05:30:38-07:00","id":1486215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486214#post1486214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Lex Magica, I think there would be the added matter of having rescinded some of the symbolic authority that is the basis by which you can leverage those laws anyway (much like how, even if you stay in the Order, you couldn't use the Merit without an appropriate title).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but Lex Magica can also run off of Consillium Status. It seems like the kind of thing the Ladder would actually encourage - &quot;See, if you play by our rules, magic just works better for you!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T07:40:08-07:00","id":1486224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486209#post1486209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for your subjective opinions - in your vision of the Fallen World, how widespread is it for members of one Order to learn the Order-specific merit of another? Say, a Silver Ladder learning Adamant Hand, or a Mystagog learning Techn\u00e9?<br /> <br /> As written, it's possible to do so by working closely with one Order, and attaining Order Status 1. You can't go any higher, but that's all you need. In terms of theme though, you might run into symbolic issues with everything but Adamant Hand - the other merits are based deeply in Order-dependent philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it can be thought if there is enough of a philosophical understanding between the mage and the Order that normally teaches the merit.<br /> <br /> A Guadian could have a track record of solving things diplomatically, trying to vote as fairly as possible. But when there is trouble, they are the first to investigate and the most methodical in rooting out those that threaten the Pentacle. Such a mage might have enough respect with the Silver Ladder to be taught the Lex Magicka.<br /> <br /> A Mystagogue could have become known for facilitating the containment of dangerous lore or artifacts in the Censorea. Maybe he has a reputation as the voice of reason that keeps other Mystagogues from going off the deep end, but recognizes that doing that can be just as much a burden as a necessity. Such a mage might be taught a Masque.<br /> <br /> There needs to be enough good blood between the person being taught and the Order. The student respects and resonates enough with their principles, even when they don't commit as deeply as with their main Order.<br /> <br /> An analogy is that you are a competent enough martial artist, you are mindful of their philosophy and integrate it into your own. You are not a grandmaster or willing to dedicate a lifetime pondering its depths, but you are earnest and dedicated enough to be taught some exclusive techniques.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-11-2022, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T08:33:16-07:00","id":1486228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486224#post1486224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mystagogue could have become known for facilitating the containment of dangerous lore or artifacts in the Censorea. Maybe he has a reputation as the voice of reason that keeps other Mystagogues from going off the deep end, but recognizes that doing that can be just as much a burden as a necessity. Such a mage might be taught a Masque.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a Masque isn't like some one-off formula you can be taught, nor is it related to the part of the Guardians that is specifically within the containment or advocacy. It is mystically emergent from the philosophy and lifestyle in which Guardians of the Veil <i>constantly lie</i>. Like, their original Order book talks about how a lot of the time Guardians will even lie about unimportant things, just to maintain the practice. It's that in combination with the degree to which they sacrifice of themselves, become detached from their own wants in favour of a greater good.<br /> <br /> Of all Orders to suggest getting in on that... the Mysterium have severe proscriptions against lying about magical subjects (and kind of discourage doing it in any event), and are all about the personal life journey of finding and developing what resonates with you specifically. There's too much ego in there for the dissolution of self that allows one to be replaced by a Masque, and the kinds of practices that is likely to entail anyway are the sort other mystagogues will often find abhorrent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T17:15:27-07:00","id":1486244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486215#post1486215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but Lex Magica can also run off of Consillium Status. It seems like the kind of thing the Ladder would actually encourage - &quot;See, if you play by our rules, magic just works better for you!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the reason for that is because the Consilium is a Ladder innovation. The writeup for Order Status describes it as unlocking Merits and advantages <i>unique to</i> that group; it then goes on to specify that characters can normally only have Status in one order and that the rare exception only allows access to the first dot, which doesn't even allow them the prosaic benefits of requisition privileges.<br /> <br /> Anti-widespread verging on nonexistent, in other words, with the possible exception of deep-cover Guardian characters running high-level Masques.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T05:21:46-07:00","id":1486511,"title":"","content":"If I understand the spell correctly, an Eidolon consumes a point of Mana whenever it's used for a Retainer roll/given task. If you gave it a Mind with the conjunctional effect, and give it the same free reign you'd give a normal person, is it consuming Mana at a regular pace? Story-wise you could explain topping them up with Mana as payment for services rendered, but it also starts to butt up on indentured servitude. Great for storytelling purposes, but morally unsettling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T06:43:44-07:00","id":1486516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486511#post1486511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand the spell correctly, an Eidolon consumes a point of Mana whenever it's used for a Retainer roll/given task. If you gave it a Mind with the conjunctional effect, and give it the same free reign you'd give a normal person, is it consuming Mana at a regular pace? Story-wise you could explain topping them up with Mana as payment for services rendered, but it also starts to butt up on indentured servitude. Great for storytelling purposes, but morally unsettling.</div> </div> </div> </div>It possible the mage might try to anticipate the issue and spellcast around it. Psychic Genesis lets you design the mind, so they can be made to think of themselves as a sophisticated coin operated machine, there to wake up, do a job and fall asleep. But that is worse, identured servitude plus brainwashing. <br /> <br /> I think the less disturbing use of this ability is as a temporary vessel for a mind or ephemeral entity while the cabal finds someone who can make a proper body or golem. <br /> <br /> Regarding the rules for adding the mind to the Eidolon, by default Psychic Genesis lets you design a mind equivalent to a Rank 1 goetia (so average to below average skill). This means all skill penalties outside its theme still apply. So if the mage is making something durable or if they have two compatible Dedicated Tools for Paradox mitigation, or is an Egregore that does the same by mixing the 4 dot benefit with their normal Dedicated tool, then making a Rank 2 mind might be worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T12:28:15-07:00","id":1486543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486516#post1486516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It possible the mage might try to anticipate the issue and spellcast around it. Psychic Genesis lets you design the mind, so they can be made to think of themselves as a sophisticated coin operated machine, there to wake up, do a job and fall asleep. But that is worse, identured servitude plus brainwashing. <br /> <br /> I think the less disturbing use of this ability is as a temporary vessel for a mind or ephemeral entity while the cabal finds someone who can make a proper body or golem. <br /> <br /> Regarding the rules for adding the mind to the Eidolon, by default Psychic Genesis lets you design a mind equivalent to a Rank 1 goetia (so average to below average skill). This means all skill penalties outside its theme still apply. So if the mage is making something durable or if they have two compatible Dedicated Tools for Paradox mitigation, or is an Egregore that does the same by mixing the 4 dot benefit with their normal Dedicated tool, then making a Rank 2 mind might be worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, Casting the two spells separately makes more sense, but I'm actually trying to figure out the rate of consumption of the Mana - is the Eidolon using up Mana for every <i>assigned</i> task, or is simply going about daily life going to consume Mana? Is it reasonable to assume that, barring an assignment or extraneous circumstance, it only consumes a fixed amount? Like a point per day/week/month?<br /> <br /> As a side note, I'm a fan of having Broad Dedication and Profligate Dedication - dedicate a Perfected item of your path, your Shadow Name, and High Speech, and relinquish an indefinite As Above So Below one of the above. Gotcha a nice spread of tools that are difficult to take away, and you can spam Mana to eliminate even Chance Paradox. Granted, there's the downside of only being able to use two on a given spell, but the tool and Shadow Name aren't always going to apply to a spell, and sometimes you just can't use High Speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-15-2022, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T15:20:27-07:00","id":1486556,"title":"","content":"I am dissapointed it doesn't mention anything about mana use for Eidolons (other than listing the differences from Platonic forms). <br /> <br /> If you use an Eidolon to create an environment including fire which does not burn, it seems like it uses no mana. But since it can be used to make functioning objects, i'd rather the environment was able to do damage perhaps with a mana cost. (Also, combined with Create Truth, you could have a Hallow which automatically refilled the Environment, or an Eidolon environment which absorbed mana from the Hallow it is part of...but per the rules environmental Eidolons don't seem to use any mana)<br /> <br /> Aside: i have half written up a legacy which turns a mage into an Eidolon, and require spending one mana each day to remain active (and regain a willpower - which you don't get from sleeping, because that is what happens when you pattern your Life into Prime)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T16:03:16-07:00","id":1486557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486556#post1486556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am dissapointed it doesn't mention anything about mana use for Eidolons (other than listing the differences from Platonic forms).</div> </div> </div> </div>Even Platonic Form is written kinda oddly - it implies that Mana is only used when the &quot;equipment bonus&quot; potency allocation was used. So you could make yourself a nice suit out of Mana, Indefinite but with no Potency into equipment bonuses, and the spell would never end.<br /> (I know that's not the spirit of the spell, but that's how I parse the text as-written)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486556#post1486556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use an Eidolon to create an environment including fire which does not burn, it seems like it uses no mana. But since it can be used to make functioning objects, i'd rather the environment was able to do damage perhaps with a mana cost. (Also, combined with Create Truth, you could have a Hallow which automatically refilled the Environment, or an Eidolon environment which absorbed mana from the Hallow it is part of...but per the rules environmental Eidolons don't seem to use any mana)</div> </div> </div> </div>A stop-gap would be to grab the rules on Temple Guardians from the Signs of Sorcery. Not perfect, but it can be adjusted to fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486556#post1486556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside: i have half written up a legacy which turns a mage into an Eidolon, and require spending one mana each day to remain active (and regain a willpower - which you don't get from sleeping, because that is what happens when you pattern your Life into Prime)</div> </div> </div> </div>My question partially stemmed from a similar Legacy idea. By default it feels like the less evil version of a Timori - at worst you're being a mana-vampire to keep your Eidolon-form fueled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-15-2022, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T16:23:20-07:00","id":1486559,"title":"","content":"Nothing stops the mage from making a person or object into a Hallow. They could then produce their own fuel at the expense of being a walking Resonance cascade. With a Patterning of Prime they could make an existing Hallow portable by moving it into a vessel. <br /> <br /> Speaking of an Eidolon humanoid, I also had an idea for such a Legacy, but didn't fully flesh it out. They got around the refueling downside by using a Patterning of Life and Prime to become beings halfway between a Platonic ideal and living being, with all the benefits of both and none of the downsides. The general concept was inspired by the xianxia genre, with them being cultivators that used <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1413312#post1413312\">very dubious methods inspired by Chinese alchemy</a> to become superhuman immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-15-2022, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T19:26:40-07:00","id":1486571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486559#post1486559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing stops the mage from making a person or object into a Hallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that a Hallow is a place stops the mage from making a person or object into a Hallow. Even Werewolf's Waystone Tell doesn't make a person a locus for the purposes of generating Essence, so a spell allowing a mage to make a portable Hallow is not going to work without extenuating circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T19:53:23-07:00","id":1486573,"title":"","content":"While the text of the spell could be construed as the Hallow radiating out from a point designated by the Caster, which could be something you could move, I'm with Satchel on that being out-of-bounds.<br /> <br /> Seems like a good Legacy capstone tho - become a walking Hallow with Potency equal to your dots in Prime. Put the Reach into Advanced Duration; the character engages in a bizarre ritual at regular intervals, but suddenly Tass is just randomly occuring wherever they go. Great storytelling potential there; anything from Seers to Banishers to Timori suddenly gunning for the individual, or Bound/Supernal creatures mistaking them for a safe haven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T21:28:21-07:00","id":1486582,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it could also be done with Forces (purview of movement) or Space (purview of separation). The capstone of the Stewards of the Celestial Orrery, found on page 178 of the <i>Silver Ladder</i> book, allowed them to generate mana like a Hallow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T22:44:57-07:00","id":1486590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486582#post1486582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it could also be done with Forces (purview of movement) or Space (purview of separation). The capstone of the Stewards of the Celestial Orrery, found on page 178 of the <i>Silver Ladder</i> book, allowed them to generate mana like a Hallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Space/Prime Legacy maybe, with the capstone Master Attainment letting you co-locate with a chosen Hallow? Meditate in said Hallow for the activation ritual, then the area around you is treated as being within that Hallow wherever you go.<br /> <br /> I have a harder time justifying Forces, since that deals with Fallen energy rather than Supernal Energy (Prime), or location (Space)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-16-2022, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T23:26:40-07:00","id":1486592,"title":"","content":"Swinging back momentarily to created entities - what level of Conditional Duration would &quot;The Creation Knowingly Betrays Me&quot; get, if used to create a Goetia/Spirit/Ghost/Intelligent Automata? Improbable, since the entity is a &quot;loyal servant&quot;? Or Infrequent, since it's always possible to alienate servants and blackmail works on anything with free will?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T06:27:08-07:00","id":1486612,"title":"","content":"For a goetia, depends if you gave them the option. Could be improbable if not, infrequent by default. Spirits and ghosts are far more obsessive, so unless the spirit feels very tempted by an opportunity to harness Essence or gain Rank, it should theoretically be loyal if treated well, so I would say infrequent. <br /> <br /> A created ghost has whatever Anchors the mage sets, so they have a deep care for protecting and interacting with them, if not Resolving them somehow. This could be the mage or their cabal, so the nature of the created pre-death memories and personality will color those interactions. Combining those with them having free will to resent the mage, I would say infrequent by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-16-2022, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:38:00-07:00","id":1486688,"title":"","content":"Can a mage use their own dedicated tool in addition to the free one granted by Egregore to gain the Paradox cancelation benefits of using two while avoiding the drawbacks ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T16:23:14-07:00","id":1486693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486688#post1486688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a mage use their own dedicated tool in addition to the free one granted by Egregore to gain the Paradox cancelation benefits of using two while avoiding the drawbacks ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes... to an extent. RAW, you have to cast spells using both tools for a month (while not benefiting from them at all) to achieve a dual dedication. I'd rule that having Egregore means you can avoid the lack-of-one-tool penalty as long as you declare one of the other Yantras used as being affected by Mysteriorum Calamitas","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-16-2022, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T16:28:46-07:00","id":1486694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486693#post1486693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say yes... with caveats. You have to cast spells using both tools for a month (while not benefiting from them at all) to achieve a dual dedication. I'd rule that having Egregore means you can avoid the lack-of-one-tool penalty as long as you declare one of the other Yantras used as being affected by Mysteriorum Calamitas</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't consider using Mysteriorum Calamitas as a replacement for when your second Dedicated tool is missing, which is interesting. What I meant was, if you use Mysteriorum Calamitas for your first yantra to make it Dedicated, then use your actual Dedicated tool next, what happens ? Would it allow it to count as using two Dedicated tools and therefore gain the Paradox cancelation effect ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T16:33:01-07:00","id":1486696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486694#post1486694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't consider using Mysteriorum Calamitas as a replacement for when your second Dedicated tool is missing, which is interesting. What I meant was, if you use Mysteriorum Calamitas for your first yantra to make it Dedicated, then use your actual Dedicated tool next, what happens ? Would it allow it to count as using two Dedicated tools and therefore gain the Paradox cancelation effect ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I lean on the side of &quot;no&quot;, since the month-long dedicating process implies you have to become practiced at using both tools as reflections of one-another. The spontaneous use is a nice idea, and RAW doesn't specifically disallow it, but my personal opinion is it wouldn't work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T12:53:18-07:00","id":1486790,"title":"","content":"My reading is the same as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a>. The preamble states that...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Your character has been granted secrets of techniques which decouple physical objects from magic.&quot; </div> </div> </div>To me that suggests that your character drops the need for a specific tool to gain the effect, rather than allowing them to both use any tool in addition to a specific tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T18:54:52-07:00","id":1486823,"title":"","content":"Lets say a sniper uses the Marksmanship maneuver <i>Through the Crosshairs</i> to spend the maximum amount of turns aiming, then uses <i>Precision Shot</i> to attack the hand of his target. The target uses Forces armor and, being a Prelate of Fury, instinctively counters all dots of the fighting style. So maximum Aim bonus would be reduced to +3, then the called shot would apply a -4 penalty, resulting in an attack modifier of -1 before applying defense, correct ? But the aiming time remains the same, since the mage only reacted reflexively when shot, would that be accurate ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-17-2022, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T20:09:40-07:00","id":1486833,"title":"","content":"Do Legacy Attainments add to -or have their own- spell control limit? I assume &quot;no&quot;, since it doesn't seem to come up anywhere in RAW.<br /> <br /> I'm also assuming that means you can't Relinquish an attainment &quot;spell&quot;. Not that you'd want or need to if they don't have an associated control limit, but it's a point I want to clarify if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T20:14:53-07:00","id":1486834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486833#post1486833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Legacy Attainments add to -or have their own- spell control limit? I assume &quot;no&quot;, since it doesn't seem to come up anywhere in RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They have none, its one of the best things about them. A Bokor can animate as many zombies as he has time to spare and for as long as the Attainment allows, a technomancer can have as many gadgets as they want under <i>Remote Control</i> (including all its defenses and computers) and a chronomancer can perfect the temporal sympathy of as many people as they want before sending them through time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T22:05:22-07:00","id":1486841,"title":"","content":"If you cast Quarantine on a subject, does the spell end when they die? They aren't protected from the passage of time like the default Pocket Dimension, so they can starve, suffocate, or age as normal.<br /> <br /> If it DOESNT end on their death, then the Time conjunctive effect becomes rather terrifying. It's like the offensive hammer to the cooperative scalpel of Corridors of Time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T22:54:00-07:00","id":1486843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486841#post1486841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you cast Quarantine on a subject, does the spell end when they die? They aren't protected from the passage of time like the default Pocket Dimension, so they can starve, suffocate, or age as normal.<br /> <br /> If it DOESNT end on their death, then the Time conjunctive effect becomes rather terrifying. It's like the offensive hammer to the cooperative scalpel of Corridors of Time</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to this; does <i>any</i> spell end when its subject dies, for that matter? Nothing seems to suggest so\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T23:01:08-07:00","id":1486844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486843#post1486843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Adding to this; does <i>any</i> spell end when its subject dies, for that matter? Nothing seems to suggest so\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mend or Knit spell cast with indefinite duration will re-apply healing at every ritual interval. If it doesn't stop even once the subject is dead....<br /> <br /> Well, probably no zombie apocalypse, since a corpse is the domain of Death, not Life. But the spell will probably just sit there until the corpse gets sufficiently broken down.<br /> <br /> I imagine any spell whose subject dies just keeps existing until dispelled or the duration runs out, or the subject's body degrades into component pieces. It becomes effectively innert for as long as it can't apply its intended effects under that logic. Makes for a kind of morbid Grimoire, honestly.<br /> <br /> On the same note, how many corpses are just hanging in no-space, where Space-Time Masters chucked them? Is there a way to find them, short of the Master's personal diary or Archmage intervention?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-18-2022, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T04:32:58-07:00","id":1486860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486844#post1486844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Mend or Knit spell cast with indefinite duration will re-apply healing at every ritual interval. If it doesn't stop even once the subject is dead....<br /> <br /> Well, probably no zombie apocalypse, since a corpse is the domain of Death, not Life. But the spell will probably just sit there until the corpse gets sufficiently broken down.<br /> <br /> I imagine any spell whose subject dies just keeps existing until dispelled or the duration runs out, or the subject's body degrades into component pieces. It becomes effectively innert for as long as it can't apply its intended effects under that logic. Makes for a kind of morbid Grimoire, honestly.<br /> <br /> On the same note, how many corpses are just hanging in no-space, where Space-Time Masters chucked them? Is there a way to find them, short of the Master's personal diary or Archmage intervention?</div> </div> </div> </div><i><br /> <b> \u201cAh, so I should combine-cast Knit/Mend with Quicken Corpse then!\u201d </b><br /> \u2014 The last and only eligible sentence salvaged from a known Neceomancer\u2019s correspondences to an unknown ally. Requires preservation as evidence.<br /> </i><br /> <br /> <br /> For the original question; so the implied answer seems to be that, yes the Quarantine sticks around\u2026 assuming the caster made it so (Advanced Duration).<br /> <br /> If it was not relinquished safely, the Quarantined area likely mutates into some hideous interstitial Mystery that we see all the time in indie horror games. It may tear Irises into itself to allow more victims access.<br /> <br /> Even if it was relinquished safely, who knows if the Quarantine would <i>remain</i> so after long years without supervision, considering all the Weird Shit that happens in the CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T04:53:56-07:00","id":1486864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486860#post1486860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <i><b>\u201cAh, so I should combine-cast Knit/Mend with Quicken Corpse then!\u201d </b><br /> \u2014 The last and only eligible sentence salvaged from a known Neceomancer\u2019s correspondences to an unknown ally. Requires preservation as evidence.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For the original question; so the implied answer seems to be that, yes the Quarantine sticks around\u2026 assuming the caster made it so (Advanced Duration).<br /> <br /> If it was not relinquished safely, the Quarantined area likely mutates into some hideous interstitial Mystery that we see all the time in indie horror games. It may tear Irises into itself to allow more victims access.<br /> <br /> Even if it was relinquished safely, who knows if the Quarantine would <i>remain</i> so after long years without supervision, considering all the Weird Shit that happens in the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe that's where the Prince of 10,000 Leaves came from originally - a Time-conjunctive Quarantine that erroded to Paradox.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelated question - Spirits (and Goetia, with help) can Materialize. The body is nominally made out of ephemera/ectoplasm. Esoteric entities will have odd physiology, but does a humanoid creature have phaux organs? Or are they like slime creatures in DnD, only having a general outer shell defined by their archetype? Do they need to simulate bodily functions like sweating or eating? Can they digest food, and if so, do Materialized entities need to poop?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-18-2022, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T05:23:12-07:00","id":1486867,"title":"","content":"When you Quarantine a target, you are setting them afloat in a bubble outside of space. When the spell ends, the chains of sympathy can exert their pull once again. Whether its a corpse, complex machine or live individual is irrelevant, the piece is slotted back into the jigsaw puzzle when duration ends. <br /> <br /> Which means unscrupulous mages probably use the conjunctional Time effect to hide bodies they still need to investigate for information on Mysteries or search for magical items. I imagine Banishers use it so no one even knows they kidnapped one of their victims, Timori would favor it to reap a bountiful harvest of Gnosis.<br /> <br /> In regards to the spells, they are all automatically relinquished unsafely when the caster dies (deatils on page 118 of the core book), which means lots of possible spell mutations and Mysteries emerging from it. This is one reason why killing a mage is not done lightly, the possibile domino effect can be remarkably dangerous.<br /> <br /> Materialized ephemeral entities are more like 40k daemons, they have no internal organs, they are just ephemera made solid. So they don't need any biological functions, since they only process Essence. But I would argue that perhaps one with the Mortal Mask numen could fake sweating, crying or eating (with no nutritional benefit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-18-2022, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T10:33:49-07:00","id":1486887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486867#post1486867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which means unscrupulous mages probably use the conjunctional Time effect to hide bodies they still need to investigate for information on Mysteries or search for magical items. I imagine Banishers use it so no one even knows they kidnapped one of their victims, Timori would favor it to reap a bountiful harvest of Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be regarding the spell of a Master (possibly of the second degree) a bit flippantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T10:51:52-07:00","id":1486890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486887#post1486887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems to be regarding the spell of a Master (possibly of the second degree) a bit flippantly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking more along the lines of a veteran Banisher, one that has the power and experience to be more discrete. But yeah, it requires high Gnosis and double mastery at the very least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T12:35:10-07:00","id":1486895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486694#post1486694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't consider using Mysteriorum Calamitas as a replacement for when your second Dedicated tool is missing, which is interesting. What I meant was, if you use Mysteriorum Calamitas for your first yantra to make it Dedicated, then use your actual Dedicated tool next, what happens ? Would it allow it to count as using two Dedicated tools and therefore gain the Paradox cancelation effect ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also say no.<br /> <br /> Calamitas is about divorcing the magical benefits from the object, i would assume this is the opposite of dedicating two magical tools (wherein you marry yourself even more to the objects rather than divorcing the relationship). <br /> <br /> It has the main benefit of not being without a tool if someone steals it. Or leaving a sympathic connection behind if someone steals the tool.<br /> <br /> I think the trade off of only being able to benefit from Calamitas OR having two dedicated magical tools is a good choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T12:46:22-07:00","id":1486898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486867#post1486867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the spells, they are all automatically relinquished unsafely when the caster dies (deatils on page 118 of the core book), which means lots of possible spell mutations and Mysteries emerging from it. This is one reason why killing a mage is not done lightly, the possibile domino effect can be remarkably dangerous.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that only applies to unrelinquished spells. If a Mage cast an Indefinite spell, then relinquished it safely, by default it wouldn't go haywire.<br /> <br /> That being said, the game is usually on a timescale where long-term degradation doesn't set in. It's wholey possible that spells fail given enough time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-18-2022, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T13:28:48-07:00","id":1486904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the same note, how many corpses are just hanging in no-space, where Space-Time Masters chucked them? Is there a way to find them, short of the Master's personal diary or Archmage intervention? </div> </div> </div>The spell description says 'the are essentially in a pocket dimension' - which would usually mean you just have to use a sympathic connection to find them. But the way Quarentine works, all sympathic connections are unmade - on the subject of the spell.<br /> <br /> This suggests using a key to enter the Quarentined area will remove your sympathic connections.<br /> <br /> As a result, no. Temporal Sympathy is also impossible with the Time 5 conjunction. You might be able to use prophecy to see if they exist in any possible futures. Or any of the usual plot devices (talk to the Aeon of Space, a rank 5 supernal entity of Space and Time, an Archmaster, etc.) <br /> <br /> I'd like to say time sight looking at the altered past would see it. Because the effect isn't lasting... I also think the spell effect would be visible as Space itself has been reshaped to accommodate the alteration (unless you cast it on a person as the subject...) - though finding a spatial anomoly and Dispelling the spell inside it, are two seperate issues.<br /> <br /> You can't go to the astral to find them because everything in the fallen has been retconned, so, again Archmastery to go to the supernal, but summoning a supernal entity is your best bet (as you can do it at space 3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T14:43:07-07:00","id":1486909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486904#post1486904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless you cast it on a person as the subject...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was assuming a person-target by default - much fewer spell factors to worry about. Also kills quickly, assuming this was someone the Mage hated -or pitied- enough to want them retconned out of history with no chance of escape.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Supernal entities, an Imp of Time or a Anachronism of Space would be your best bets. The Imp if you focus on finding Quarantine spacial anomalies, the Anachronism if you want to look for anchors of alternate history.<br /> <br /> Spiraling further down the rabbit hole, heres a causality question. Say a son gets indefinitely Quarantined, and thus never existed. In this new timeline, his mother coincidentally also gets Quarantined, and thus never existed. Does the son still exist in his little pocket? If not, does his pocket reappear when the mothers Quarantine ends?<br /> <br /> Does a Mage who casts Quarantine even remember why they suddenly have a filled control slot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-18-2022, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T19:46:33-07:00","id":1486936,"title":"","content":"On the subject of the mage's memory, the answer lies with another question: did the mage cast Constant Presence? They do remember the spell, they have to keep making adjustments to the Imago to keep it stable.<br /> <br /> On the mother and son quandary, depends on the casters. The caster has the options of either having the subject's actions never have happened or have been done by someone else. So the mother could have had another son, or adopted one, maybe their sibling did everything or she never had one. <br /> <br /> When she is Quarantined, there are no historical ties to her son, so he stays unaffected. When he returns and she doesn't, he could, depending on the spell cast on the mother, either have a different mother or be left without a past as Time magic adjusts causality.<br /> <br /> This sounds like it would make for a fascinating Mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-18-2022, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T21:03:50-07:00","id":1486951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486936#post1486936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of the mage's memory, the answer lies with another question: did the mage cast Constant Presence? They do remember the spell, they have to keep making adjustments to the Imago to keep it stable. On the mother and son quandary, depends on the casters. The caster has the options of either having the subject's actions never have happened or have been done by someone else. So the mother could have had another son, or adopted one, maybe their sibling did everything or she never had one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Working similar to Rewrite History, I suppose, which tracks with the Arcana level. Come to think of it, can you declare someones &quot;death&quot; as their divergence point for Rewrite Histroy? Would they stay dead once the spell ends? I assume not based on the text, but...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486936#post1486936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When she is Quarantined, there are no historical ties to her son, so he stays unaffected. When he returns and she doesn't, he could, depending on the spell cast on the mother, either have a different mother or be left without a past as Time magic adjusts causality.<br /> <br /> This sounds like it would make for a fascinating Mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, for the sake of clarity and my sanity, here's a shorthand for the various timelines -<br /> <br /> Timeline 1 - The original timeline<br /> Timeline A - The timeline that results from Quarantining the son<br /> Timeline B - The timeline that results from Quarantining the mother<br /> Timeline C - The timeline potentially resulting from the son's Quarantine losing it's caster<br /> <br /> Assuming the Mage in Timeline 1 didn't cast Constant Presence for whatever reason -quite an oversight for a second degree Master, but bear with me- then the Mage who cast the son's Quarantine in Timeline 1 may not exist in Timeline B. This means that either the son's Quarantine is now unmoored (Unsafely relinquished?), stops existing, or exists purely as a self-sustaining Mystery that can only be accessed by higher Supernal powers.<br /> <br /> If it stops existing, the son either<br /> 1. pops into Timeline C with memories of Timeline 1 but no past in Timeline C. He is now a Mystery. And a decent candidate for Awakening, all things considered.<br /> 2. pops into Timeline B and is immediately retconned into having been born through different avenues, and thus no memory of Timeline 1, resulting in Timeline C<br /> 3. Disapears with the rest of Timeline 1 and A leaving Timeline B as the only thread that matters. He'll reappear with Timeline 1 when the mother's Quarantine ends, since her not existing is the lynchpin causing Timeline B to exist. Once Timeline B goes, Timeline 1 reasserts itself.<br /> 4. pops into Timeline 1, the Quarantine that started all of this being the lynchpin that takes presidence over the mother's Quarantine.<br /> <br /> Even with Constant Presence up, there's still the chance that the Mage from Timeline 1 loses the Clash of Wills with the Mage from Timeline A (Assuming it isn't the same mage). In which case the same conundrum pops up. All of this also assumes that the son's Quarantine is an unrelinquished spell - a relinquished spell probably avoids all of this by existing wholey independent of any timeline.<br /> <br /> Goddamn, Time magic is trippy. I'm quite fond of the theory that Atlantis existed, but history keeps getting retconned and the wildly different ruins left behind are where reality couldn't fully compensate for the overlapping changes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">If I were a mage, I'd learn Adept of Pime and every Arcana's Shielding practice, for the express purpose of making a Persistent Imbued Item that layers every single general Shielding spell. Probably master Matter too, so I could make it a Thaumium amulet with the &quot;no-sell most supernatural powers for mana&quot; schtick. Wouldn't be too dangerous a combatant, admittedly, but I'd be hard to touch through supernatural means.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-19-2022, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T22:41:40-07:00","id":1486962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486951#post1486951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">If I were a mage, I'd learn Adept of Pime and every Arcana's Shielding practice, for the express purpose of making a Persistent Imbued Item that layers every single general Shielding spell. Probably master Matter too, so I could make it a Thaumium amulet with the &amp;quot;no-sell most supernatural powers for mana&amp;quot; schtick. Wouldn't be too dangerous a combatant, admittedly, but I'd be hard to touch through supernatural means.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that\u2019s a pretty sizable obsession and a long career to fuel it.<br /> <br /> I kind of have a similarly intense goal in one of my NPC mages. She became an initiate in 8 arcana (all but Matter and Forces) so that she could study - and paint - as much of a person\u2019s Pattern as possible.<br /> Then she wanted the same view from the other 4 Paths, so became an Adept in Prime and sought out 4 other mages similarly trained mages (or ones who were willing to be), and exchanged imbued items with Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> A different terrible generalist NPC is obsessed with using every Arcana to make a sympathetic yantra that maps an entire city and can at least dig up a clue on just about any supernatural event within it. \u2026 She draws a lot of heat: the Assembly kind of uses her as bait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T22:45:51-07:00","id":1486963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> then the Mage who cast the son's Quarantine in Timeline 1 may not exist in Timeline B. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem to be likely given how the spell described the retcon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">Any influence it, or anyone inside, had on the world is either undone or was caused by someone else.</pre> </div>Only removes the mage if they were a consequence of the mother's actions.<br /> <br /> Also for AoE effects, if you create a Quarentine with a key, the mage can enter and will be erased from existence (perhaps temporarily).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T23:13:32-07:00","id":1486965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486962#post1486962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that\u2019s a pretty sizable obsession and a long career to fuel it.<br /> <br /> I kind of have a similarly intense goal in one of my NPC mages. She became an initiate in 8 arcana (all but Matter and Forces) so that she could study - and paint - as much of a person\u2019s Pattern as possible.<br /> Then she wanted the same view from the other 4 Paths, so became an Adept in Prime and sought out 4 other mages similarly trained mages (or ones who were willing to be), and exchanged imbued items with Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> A different terrible generalist NPC is obsessed with using every Arcana to make a sympathetic yantra that maps an entire city and can at least dig up a clue on just about any supernatural event within it. \u2026 She draws a lot of heat: the Assembly kind of uses her as bait.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a career that would take quite a while and a lot of favors - I like Mastigoi and the Pure Sovereigns, so that Inferior Matter trek would be a slog. On the other hand, my self-imposed rule is that I only increase Gnosis upon gaining the Initiate or Mastery levels of an Arcana, or acheive any level of the character's Inferior Arcana. Feels like the expanded Mage sight would be an effective gnostic trigger, as would the understanding of how to create phenomena whole-cloth or comprehending your Path's weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Both those NPCs sound fun<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486963#post1486963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't seem to be likely given how the spell described the retcon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">Any influence it, or anyone inside, had on the world is either undone or was caused by someone else.</pre> </div>Only removes the mage if they were a consequence of the mother's actions.<br /> <br /> Also for AoE effects, if you create a Quarentine with a key, the mage can enter and will be erased from existence (perhaps temporarily).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I phrased that poorly. &quot;Mage 1&quot; may still exist, but without Constant Presence they would be &quot;Mage 1a&quot; in Timeline A, since they now have no memory of casting the spell in the first place. And potentially never cast it in the first place through grandfather paradox, although I think that was addressed as not being a thing in one of the books.<br /> <br /> Or, if we're more lenient and assume the imago has a build-in clause to protect &quot;Mage 1&quot;, then consider how &quot;Mage 2&quot; casting Quarantine on the mother changes reality again - we're two timelines away from where &quot;Mage 1&quot; cast their spell, with the original target and one of their progenetors not existing.<br /> <br /> To put it another way - Timeline A only exists because &quot;Mage 1&quot; is willing it to be so. If Timeline B is brought into being, then &quot;Mage 2&quot; is at the helm, and unless they know about &quot;Mage 1&quot; they're unlikely to have accounted for the son.<br /> <br /> Granted, this has become a snarl of my trying to express an interpretation of temporal mechanics that I don't have the eloquence to bring outside of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T05:33:49-07:00","id":1486988,"title":"","content":"An item that has been Imbued with even one Shielding from each Arcanum is going to require forty successes to pull off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T07:30:37-07:00","id":1487007,"title":"","content":"I would just create an antimagic field by using a spell combining a Knowing of Prime to determine what is Supernal magic with a Making of Death. Then use a Reach to exclude spells with my Nimbus. If I didn't want to have that constantly up or deal with the Paradox from over Reaching, I would start trading at a Goblin Market for Hedgespun equipment, maybe sorting through antiquaries and auctions for Mementos. After all, it would be terrifying if only you had the magic weapons that work. <br /> <br /> The XP for getting all Shieldings would be the same required to be a Adept in one Arcanum (Prime) and a quadruple master, which would me much more worth it, since you could build very complex and powerful spells using all those Arcana, including an elaborate defense. Shielding is an amazing Practice, it allows mages to no sell anything mundane in the Arcanum's purview (what are knifes, guns and explosives before a Forces Shielding against kinetic energy attacks ?) and can make a mage a veritable juggernaut, but more advanced Practices can offer a lot as well.<br /> <br /> The Clash of Wills only works if the spells are at cross purposes. If the timeline can be retconned further without compromising the main effect (&quot;this person does not influence history&quot;), then causality will naturally adjust.<br /> <br /> The only way the spell could be undone would be if either the mage had no reason to cast it in the revised timeline or if they had a reason to end the spell early, in which case no Clash of Wills happens since the mage is historically making a different choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-19-2022, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T12:32:49-07:00","id":1487041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only way the spell could be undone would be if either the mage had no reason to cast it in the revised timeline or if they had a reason to end the spell early, in which case no Clash of Wills happens since the mage is historically making a different choice. </div> </div> </div>In this example, i am presuming at first the mage knows they cast a spell to remove someone from the timeline. But then someone else removes the mother and the first mage wouldn't have needed to remove the son of he never existed (which he can't if his mother never existed) so now without a reason to have cast the spell you are saying he didn't? But there is no son coming back out of quarentine because he never existed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T13:29:02-07:00","id":1487050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1486988#post1486988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An item that has been Imbued with even one Shielding from each Arcanum is going to require forty successes to pull off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Walking around with ten charms hanging off your belt isn't a bad alternative. Alternatively, make friends with a Fate mage and have them hit you with a ton of lucker spells before you start crafting.<br /> <br /> Even if you never succeed, Seraph Kitty made a good point about it being a good Obsession. And if you succed, a great Quintessence for becoming an Archmage!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487007#post1487007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just create an antimagic field by using a spell combining a Knowing of Prime to determine what is Supernal magic with a Making of Death. Then use a Reach to exclude spells with my Nimbus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space Ban with the Reach effect to exclude Prime-related effects (i.e. most spells), plus an extra Reach to Key it to your nimbus. Or a Keyed Wards and Signs. Requires maybe Disciple level in Space and Prime, so not too XP intensive. Magic that isn't marked with your Nimbus provokes a Clash of Wills for the first, and gets Withstood by the spell's Potency for the second.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487041#post1487041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this example, i am presuming at first the mage knows they cast a spell to remove someone from the timeline. But then someone else removes the mother and the first mage wouldn't have needed to remove the son of he never existed (which he can't if his mother never existed) so now without a reason to have cast the spell you are saying he didn't? But there is no son coming back out of quarentine because he never existed...</div> </div> </div> </div>Time shenanigans! Really makes you wonder who is real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-19-2022, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T15:27:52-07:00","id":1487063,"title":"","content":"I really like those two antimagic options, a cabal could perhaps use both as layered defenses. Another one is a <i>Sworn Oath</i> of &quot;I will not be affected by any spells/supernatural effects that I do not wish to be&quot;, no Key needed (Fate has the purview of intentions) and anything outside of that scope provokes a Clash of Wills. With mastery, advanced duration and potency, it gets a +5. If spell control is maintained, the mage will always know when they are Clashing and be able to add another +3 from Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T15:55:22-07:00","id":1487066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487063#post1487063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like those two antimagic options, a cabal could perhaps use both as layered defenses. Another one is a <i>Sworn Oath</i> of &quot;I will not be affected by any spells/supernatural effects that I do not wish to be&quot;, no Key needed (Fate has the purview of intentions) and anything outside of that scope provokes a Clash of Wills. With mastery, advanced duration and potency, it gets a +5. If spell control is maintained, the mage will always know when they are Clashing and be able to add another +3 from Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure Sworn Oath would be able to provide that kind of protection - I read it as a slightly more powerful version of Warding Gesture, in which case it only covers a geas, a supernatural compulsion to act against her will, or having her fate manipulated by Fate magic or similar supernatural effects. So if it's a spell that directly manipulates your behavior, sure, but I don't think a lightning bolt being chucked at you would qualify...<br /> <br /> Granted, Warding Gesture can be Reached into protecting a target from AoE spells, so it's possible I'm reading Sworn Oaths too narrowly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T16:03:17-07:00","id":1487068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487063#post1487063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like those two antimagic options, a cabal could perhaps use both as layered defenses. Another one is a <i>Sworn Oath</i> of &amp;quot;I will not be affected by any spells/supernatural effects that I do not wish to be&amp;quot;, no Key needed (Fate has the purview of intentions) and anything outside of that scope provokes a Clash of Wills. With mastery, advanced duration and potency, it gets a +5. If spell control is maintained, the mage will always know when they are Clashing and be able to add another +3 from Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh\u2026 won\u2019t Sworn Oaths just end up hexing you for daring to let a spell affect you, then? As opposed to actually stopping the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T16:43:16-07:00","id":1487070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487068#post1487068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh\u2026 won\u2019t Sworn Oaths just end up hexing you for daring to let a spell affect you, then? As opposed to actually stopping the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why you add the clause &quot;that I do not wish to be affected by&quot;, meaning any spells you cast and anyone else uses spells on you, with your approval, will not trigger the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> Plus if you maintain spell control, you can simply end the effect if you lose the Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T16:57:38-07:00","id":1487071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487070#post1487070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is why you add the clause &amp;quot;that I do not wish to be affected by&amp;quot;, meaning any spells you cast and anyone else uses spells on you, with your approval, will not trigger the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> Plus if you maintain spell control, you can simply end the effect if you lose the Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iir, Clashes happen when two supernatural abilities have opposing or otherwise incompatible effects.<br /> <br /> The effect of a Sworn Oaths in this context seems to be \u201cI won\u2019t let myself be affected by spells.\u201d<br /> <br /> A supernatural effect that Clashes with this would be \u201cI want you to be left vulnerable and exposed to spells.\u201d Not \u201cSpells.\u201d<br /> (Or was this the intention all along? Sorry if it was, cuz I haven\u2019t followed the recent argument too closely)<br /> <br /> For a more poetic/mythic example; when C\u00fa Chulainn swore (okay, got Geasa\u2019ed) to not eat dog meat, the Oath did nothing to prevent dog meat from reaching his mouth, whether he wanted it or not. Similarly, a Sworn Oath to not let unwanted spells affect me would do nothing to prevent spells from affecting me, whether I want it or not; just punish me for it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Warding Gestures probably does the Say No To Spells! thing better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T17:03:31-07:00","id":1487072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487070#post1487070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is why you add the clause &quot;that I do not wish to be affected by&quot;, meaning any spells you cast and anyone else uses spells on you, with your approval, will not trigger the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> Plus if you maintain spell control, you can simply end the effect if you lose the Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed the bit about swearing oaths not giving you magical protection. You have to uphold the oath in order to gain the boon. If you are hit by a spell (withstood by whatever other defences you have) and it harms you, then you failed to uphold your oath and the (oath) spell hexes you with the bad stuff you included.<br /> <br /> At least the way I've seen it used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 07-20-2022, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T17:03:56-07:00","id":1487073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487071#post1487071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, Warding Gestures probably does the Say No To Spells! thing better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed - it Clashes to prevent behavior- or Destiny-altering magic from affecting the subject, and with Reach can cause them to Clash against being affected by AoE spells. It's a good layer for the hypothetical uber-Shielding this discussions spawned from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T17:10:26-07:00","id":1487074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487071#post1487071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Iir, Clashes happen when two supernatural abilities have opposing or otherwise incompatible effects.<br /> <br /> The effect of a Sworn Oaths in this context seems to be \u201cI won\u2019t let myself be affected by spells.\u201d<br /> <br /> A supernatural effect that Clashes with this would be \u201cI want you to be left vulnerable and exposed to spells.\u201d Not \u201cSpells.\u201d<br /> (Or was this the intention all along? Sorry if it was, cuz I haven\u2019t followed the recent argument too closely)<br /> <br /> For a more poetic/mythic example; when C\u00fa Chulainn swore (okay, got Geasa\u2019ed) to not eat dog meat, the Oath did nothing to prevent dog meat from reaching his mouth, whether he wanted it or not. Similarly, a Sworn Oath to not let unwanted spells affect me would do nothing to prevent spells from affecting me, whether I want it or not; just punish me for it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Warding Gestures probably does the Say No To Spells! thing better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Warding Gesture</i> only protects targets from your own spells, as well as ones that would affect their free will. With a Reach, it protects from AoE spells only.<br /> <br /> The text for <i>Sworn Oaths</i> in page 137 mentioned that &quot;If a supernatural power would force the subject to violate her oath \u2014 either by action or inaction \u2014 the mage may make a Clash of Wills against the effect.&quot;. So I understood that, in theory, an oath could be used to enter a Banned building or protect themselves from spells, depending on how the oath is worded. Violating it will hex them, but they can just cancel the punishment by ending the spell, either via spell control or conditional duration. The gambit is how long can you make it last and, once the oath is broken, you are vulnerable until you make a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-19-2022, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T17:13:33-07:00","id":1487076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487074#post1487074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text for Sworn Oaths in page 137 mentioned that &quot;If a supernatural power would force the subject to violate her oath \u2014 either by action or inaction \u2014 the mage may make a Clash of Wills against the effect.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's meant to be read as &quot;If the supernatural power is compelling you to action or inaction&quot;, as opposed to &quot;If the mere act of a supernatural power taking effect on you would violate your Oath&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T17:22:25-07:00","id":1487079,"title":"","content":"I also visualized a medieval example of a paladin swearing something like &quot;I shall rescue my comrade from that abominable Seer lair and I swear that none of their foul sorcery shall stop me, may my sword arm fail me if I give them any ground&quot;, forging ahead by upholding the commitment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T18:10:54-07:00","id":1487081,"title":"","content":"That would still only protect you from being compelled to stray from your quest - otherwise, the sorcery only &quot;stops&quot; you when you're dead.<br /> <br /> You <i>might</i> be able to swing using it to resist Ban, but even that isn't stopping you, just hindering you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-19-2022, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T19:58:16-07:00","id":1487096,"title":"","content":"I checked against the closest 1ed spell, <i>Swearing an Oath</i>, found on page 153 of that core book. Seems like the intent was that it would activate on <br /> circumstances that would forbid action, so arguably it could be used to break in or out of a Ban or Pocket Dimension if whatever was related to the oath was on the other side. Maybe even very specific ones like &quot;I will not leave this city until the the stolen Grimoire is recovered&quot; could allow you to Clash against being teleported away.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated question, what would qualify as breaking a rune inscribed on a weapon, cloth or armor ? A called shot to it, certain amounts of continuous damage (fire, electricity, etc) or an explosion ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-19-2022, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T20:24:34-07:00","id":1487100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487096#post1487096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated question, what would qualify as breaking a rune inscribed on a weapon, cloth or armor ? A called shot to it, certain amounts of continuous damage (fire, electricity, etc) or an explosion ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Destruction of the main &quot;structure&quot; of the rune. Snapping a sword blade wouldn't affect the Rune inscribed on the pommel, but scoring the rune in the course of hitting someone with the pommel would. So it's mostly at the STs disgression as to what particular effect does the rune in. A called shot that hits likely would, as would setting a flamable example alight, assuming it hasn't been warded against flames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T01:05:29-07:00","id":1487123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487096#post1487096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I checked against the closest 1ed spell, <i>Swearing an Oath</i>, found on page 153 of that core book. Seems like the intent was that it would activate on <br /> circumstances that would forbid action, so arguably it could be used to break in or out of a Ban or Pocket Dimension if whatever was related to the oath was on the other side. Maybe even very specific ones like &amp;quot;I will not leave this city until the the stolen Grimoire is recovered&amp;quot; could allow you to Clash against being teleported away.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think everyone else agrees that this reading is wrong.<br /> <br /> A vampire using Dominate or Presence to make you teleport yourself away would clash. But a mage teleporting you would not. <br /> <br /> The clash is to prevent a loophole and give you more free will in decisions relating to the Oath. It does not prevent someone binding you into a car and driving you off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T07:38:52-07:00","id":1487191,"title":"","content":"Yep, agreed. Can a Shielding of Mind fully protect against the Ecstatic Wind or would a Perfecting of the Amnion be required ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T17:13:55-07:00","id":1487282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487191#post1487191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Shielding of Mind fully protect against the Ecstatic Wind or would a Perfecting of the Amnion be required ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A sensible reading of the setting would indicate this is one of those things you simply can't manage as a Traveler, because the alternative is that the Whorl is a non-issue for any mage with sub-Adept levels of Mind and Time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T18:13:51-07:00","id":1487293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487282#post1487282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sensible reading of the setting would indicate this is one of those things you simply can't manage as a Traveler, because the alternative is that the Whorl is a non-issue for any mage with sub-Adept levels of Mind and Time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, how that was phrased was a bit confusing, so I need to clarify. The first part seemed to suggest that only archmages can explore an area where the Ecstatic Wind is present for a considerable length of time.<br /> <br /> But the second part stated that ruling otherwise would make exploring the Whorl a non-issue for anyone with less than 4 dots in Mind or Time. But that would imply that mages could possibly solve the issue with Adept level spells, which contradicts the first statement.<br /> <br /> I think you implied that because the Amnion is a specialized type of mage armor for the Astral, which is why a Perfecting spell would not be able to reinforce it, would that be accurate ? <br /> <br /> However, that also made me think that there is nothing preventing the activation of Mage Armor in the Astral, correct? Does that mean a Mind armor or another subtle Arcanum's armor could work as an additional buffer against the Ecstatic Wind in, for example, a combat scene in the Dreaming Earth ? Not necessarily an efficient solution, but maybe give just enough breathing room against giant predators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T20:21:32-07:00","id":1487308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487293#post1487293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, how that was phrased was a bit confusing, so I need to clarify. The first part seemed to suggest that only archmages can explore an area where the Ecstatic Wind is present for a considerable length of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Being immune to the Ecstatic Wind&quot; is presently an obscure template feature for werewolves and demons out of Cover. Archmasters can mess with that, but at present the Awakened handle the specific form of damage to Dream Health from the Ecstatic Wind \u2014 the world-soul attempting to break down the barriers of their selfhood \u2014 with a fixed amount of effective Armor based on Traits they can't boost with spells that don't require a credible run at godhood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the second part stated that ruling otherwise would make exploring the Whorl a non-issue for anyone with less than 4 dots in Mind or Time. But that would imply that mages could possibly solve the issue with Adept level spells, which contradicts the first statement. </div> </div> </div>Of course it contradicts the first statement. The second statement is stating an implication of the first statement not being true as an argument for why it makes more sense for the first statement to be true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you implied that because the Amnion is a specialized type of mage armor for the Astral, which is why a Perfecting spell would not be able to reinforce it, would that be accurate ? </div> </div> </div>The Amnion is the mage leveraging spiritually-backed controlled egocentrism to buttress their identity against the soul of the universe trying to resorb it. It doubles as a general Armor rating for the Astral in 2e because the Ecstatic Wind works through Dream Health damage instead of intermittent Resolve + Composure rolls, but its primary effect in this discussion is not analogous to Mage Armor just because it now also works against Astral attacks that appear physical.<br /> <br /> Without touching the Godhead, there is no spell that is going to give you more Gnosis or more dots in Prime/Spirit/Fate/Death/Mind to fortify your soul against the yawning tide of unreality at the shores of the dreaming universe that yanks at your coherence while astrally venturing among the lands before language.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, that also made me think that there is nothing preventing the activation of Mage Armor in the Astral, correct? </div> </div> </div>The Amnion's Armor rating explicitly stacks with spells and Attainments, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does that mean a Mind armor or another subtle Arcanum's armor could work as an additional buffer against the Ecstatic Wind in, for example, a combat scene in the Dreaming Earth ? Not necessarily an efficient solution, but maybe give just enough breathing room against giant predators. </div> </div> </div>In the Dreaming Earth the Wind does not blow frequently enough to come into play during a combat scene, and even less so in the Anthropic Redoubts. The Whorl is the only part of the Anima Mundi where the Ecstatic Wind is a concern within the duration of a scene, and the way time works there is why I mentioned Time in addition to Mind.<br /> <br /> You may reasonably guess that if a spell idea would completely trivialize or circumvent the systems the game presents for an aspect of magical reality as it is inhabited by a society of wizards that have been plugging away at Understanding The Supernatural for multiple millennia, and that spell does not trade one complication for another or have an exceptional force or circumstance backing it, it's not going to work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T01:52:02-07:00","id":1487335,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, a spell to repair your Dream Health would probably be reasonable. Perfecting or Weaving Mind, likely. You might be able to make a case for any of the subtle Arcana, but Mind is the best candidate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T03:24:47-07:00","id":1487343,"title":"","content":"Is an ephemeral entity that enters the Fallen World through a Gateway manifestation tangible by default, or are they coming through directly into Twilight? If they are tangible, Gateway seems like a better version of Materialize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T04:33:09-07:00","id":1487354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487343#post1487343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is an ephemeral entity that enters the Fallen World through a Gateway manifestation tangible by default, or are they coming through directly into Twilight? If they are tangible, Gateway seems like a better version of Materialize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight is the natural state of ephemera present in the matetial/physical/living world, so I\u2019d say, no just Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T13:58:14-07:00","id":1487417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487343#post1487343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is an ephemeral entity that enters the Fallen World through a Gateway manifestation tangible by default, or are they coming through directly into Twilight? If they are tangible, Gateway seems like a better version of Materialize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gateway says it allows one to cross between worlds. Materialize says it gives something Materialized. Page 253 says the state of ephemeral entities without Manifestations is Twilight. Only one of those two Manifestations says it grants the Materialized Condition, which states that it makes the subject physical and no longer subject to the conditions of Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-21-2022, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T16:10:12-07:00","id":1487423,"title":"","content":"If you kill a spirit(or ghost or goetia) by filling their corpus with lethal damage, but they still have essence they go into hibernation.<br /> <br /> I always assumed you couldn't harm them again (directly) until they reform their corpus (after regaining corpus points of essence). <br /> <br /> I was assuming they have no body to harm anymore so you can't deal damage... But i have seen others assume you can just hit them (if you can find them).<br /> <br /> And further that more lethal will roll over into agg and cause them to lose essence so actually be killable. <br /> <br /> What happens in 2e? Probably doesn't matter for Goetia as most of them can reform if conditions which created them persist, but for ghosts and spirits in particular...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T16:41:49-07:00","id":1487425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487423#post1487423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you kill a spirit(or ghost or goetia) by filling their corpus with lethal damage, but they still have essence they go into hibernation.<br /> <br /> I always assumed you couldn't harm them again (directly) until they reform their corpus (after regaining corpus points of essence).<br /> <br /> I was assuming they have no body to harm anymore so you can't deal damage... But i have seen others assume you can just hit them (if you can find them).<br /> <br /> And further that more lethal will roll over into agg and cause them to lose essence so actually be killable.<br /> <br /> What happens in 2e? Probably doesn't matter for Goetia as most of them can reform if conditions which created them persist, but for ghosts and spirits in particular...</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is found on page 257 of the core book, so long as they have at least one point of Essence, they reform in a hibernating state on a location with a suitable Condition. So the simplest way to make sure they die is to use their Ban to pull them away from it, hurt them to near death and wait for a few hours until you are relatively sure they are out of Essence (probably check with an Occult roll), then deliver the finishing blow with the Ban. This is incredibly easy since, unless someone steps in to defend them, you have the time to get a Killing Blow. However, be careful because spirits that hibernate in Twilight at zero Essence start drifting back to the Shadow, so leaving one unattended could make them the meal that empowers another, and then you have a bigger problem.<br /> <br /> After they reform from being Discorporated, they are in a vegetative state while recovering Essence, but fully there and the same rules as normal apply. The far easier approach is to entreat someone with the right subtle Arcanum or recruit ephemeral entities of the same type. In the case of ghosts, probably a mix of Investigation and Empathy can be used to uncover their past and figure out their Anchors, at which point smashing them consigns them to a literal fate worse than death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-21-2022, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T18:16:31-07:00","id":1487431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487423#post1487423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you kill a spirit(or ghost or goetia) by filling their corpus with lethal damage, but they still have essence they go into hibernation.<br /> <br /> I always assumed you couldn't harm them again (directly) until they reform their corpus (after regaining corpus points of essence).<br /> <br /> I was assuming they have no body to harm anymore so you can't deal damage... But i have seen others assume you can just hit them (if you can find them).<br /> <br /> And further that more lethal will roll over into agg and cause them to lose essence so actually be killable.<br /> <br /> What happens in 2e? Probably doesn't matter for Goetia as most of them can reform if conditions which created them persist, but for ghosts and spirits in particular...</div> </div> </div> </div>A discorporated ephemeral being with Essence in its system tends to reform in a Conditioned location that is also a safe place, where possible \u2014 spirits have the easiest time of this thanks to running on Resonance instead of Anchors and being pulled into the Shadow when they enter hibernation, where the things that are theoretically most able to get at them while they're vulnerable are also part of a pseudo-cultural system that incentivizes against wasteful destruction or particularly careless consumption, but even ghosts can reform out of sight if Anchored to sufficiently large and/or complex location.<br /> <br /> Given that the newer presentations of the mechanics in Geist and Changeling 2e specify, respectively, that ghosts awaken from hibernation with all Corpus boxes empty and Hedge ghosts reform in the Hedge &quot;once enough time has passed for them to recover Glamour equal to Corpus,&quot; and given that Mage 1e's description of the mechanic ran &quot;spirit recovers Essence equal to its Corpus, then starts recovering Corpus,&quot; <i>and</i> given that Rouse Spirit specifies that waking a spirit with that spell prematurely means it awakens with less than its full Corpus track empty, I think it's safe to say that an invisible entity in the process of hibernating due to discorporation is not subject to damage to its Corpus \u2014 you can steal Essence from it and forestall its return to activity if you've got the tools to do so, but it's already effectively at 0 Corpus and in the place it goes when it breaks down; it hasn't booted its ephemeral body back into a solid enough state to be meddled with in that fashion yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T22:27:48-07:00","id":1487451,"title":"","content":"Summoning a goetia out of a person's mind deprives them of that aspect of their personality for the duration. Does anything similar happen with entities summoned from the Tenemos or Anima Mundi? The 1e book Astral Realms has an entry for Blights, which are festering wounds that can result from an Astral object being summoned out, but that's the closest description I could find at a glance.<br /> <br /> For example, if you summon a minor pop-culture character goetia to be your Familiar, are you impacting humanity's interactions with that character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-22-2022, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T02:04:59-07:00","id":1487463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487451#post1487451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summoning a goetia out of a person's mind deprives them of that aspect of their personality for the duration. Does anything similar happen with entities summoned from the Tenemos or Anima Mundi? The 1e book Astral Realms has an entry for Blights, which are festering wounds that can result from an Astral object being summoned out, but that's the closest description I could find at a glance.<br /> <br /> For example, if you summon a minor pop-culture character goetia to be your Familiar, are you impacting humanity's interactions with that character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely not full deprivation, but yes it does seem to have an impact. Mage 2e mentions how you can kill off a tv show\u2019s protagonists to attempt to get that show cancelled \u2014 the mechanics of doing so expanded in one of the Beast supplements (which one, I forgot atm). While such manipulations are cases of working \u2018within\u2019 the Temenos, summoning and \u2018locking\u2019 Goetia out of the Astral could work too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Clarity 07-22-2022, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T02:28:59-07:00","id":1487465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487463#post1487463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Likely not full deprivation, but yes it does seem to have an impact. Mage 2e mentions how you can kill off a tv show\u2019s protagonists to attempt to get that show cancelled \u2014 the mechanics of doing so expanded in one of the Beast supplements (which one, I forgot atm). While such manipulations are cases of working \u2018within\u2019 the Temenos, summoning and \u2018locking\u2019 Goetia out of the Astral could work too.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><i>Note to Self: Hold the Astral cast of a show/band you hate hostage to get it canceled.</i></b><br /> <br /> Flip side, does boosting a goetia through magic improve the associated concept's influence on humanity? Could I, say, increase the Rank of the goetia of an obscure show to turn said show into a cult classic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-22-2022, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T03:08:59-07:00","id":1487469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487465#post1487465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><i>Hold the Astral cast of a show/band you hate hostage to get it canceled.</i></b><br /> <br /> Noted. Flip side, does boosting a goetia through magic improve the associated concept's influence on humanity? Could I, say, increase the Rank of the goetia of an obscure show to turn said show into a cult classic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps? Not clear on that.<br /> <br /> Although my personal preference is to rule that it does so only indirectly \u2014 that is, the goetia still has to manually do whatever long-term project it has to do to increase its influence, but it can do so more easily with improved Rank/Attributes/Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T17:38:01-07:00","id":1487666,"title":"","content":"If a mage that is being affected by <i>Terrorize </i>spends a Willpower and uses pattern restoration to heal the condition, does it provoke a Clash of Wills (probably Gnosis+4 since the effect is Lasting and has no set Arcanum) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T17:50:25-07:00","id":1487668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487666#post1487666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage that is being affected by <i>Terrorize </i>spends a Willpower and uses pattern restoration to heal the condition, does it provoke a Clash of Wills (probably Gnosis+4 since the effect is Lasting and has no set Arcanum) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd say it's a Clash using Gnosis+Mind or Gnosis+Resolve/Composure. <br /> <br /> For the first, it's because Life enhances the physiological aspects of Pattern Restoration, which means Mind isn't too outlandish a choice to assist in resolving a mental condition. <br /> <br /> For the second, it's because you're wrenching your emotions back into place with your Resistance stat, assisted by your Gnosis. Like a lever and fulcrum (which is which I leave up to you). That being said, Gnosis+(Attribute) is... not normal, so I doubt it'd fly with most STs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T19:03:40-07:00","id":1487673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487666#post1487666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage that is being affected by <i>Terrorize </i>spends a Willpower and uses pattern restoration to heal the condition, does it provoke a Clash of Wills (probably Gnosis+4 since the effect is Lasting and has no set Arcanum) ?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Player\u2019s Guide to the Contagion Chronicle</b> has unrated abilities (such as a vampire\u2019s blood bond) roll relevant Attribute + Supernatural Potency.<br /> <br /> A mage\u2019s Pattern Restoration would be such a case. For Terrorize specifically, likely Composure + Gnosis.<br /> <br /> EDIT: On second thought, having it just work without Clashing may probably be the original intention, as Satchel\u2019s answer below. Healing spells work that way anyway; PR might as well too. M","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 07-24-2022, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T22:08:38-07:00","id":1487691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487666#post1487666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage that is being affected by <i>Terrorize </i>spends a Willpower and uses pattern restoration to heal the condition, does it provoke a Clash of Wills (probably Gnosis+4 since the effect is Lasting and has no set Arcanum) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no reason to involve the Clash mechanics here. The character is spending a not-insignificant amount of their Mana capacity to end the Broken Condition as part of a power that ends Conditions, and the spell applies its effect until the spell or the Condition ends.<br /> <br /> If the mention of spending Willpower is referring to the Insensate Tilt, then we've run into a different reason for the same outcome, which is &quot;Insensate generated by a Mind spell is neither a Condition nor a physical Tilt.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T22:12:59-07:00","id":1487692,"title":"","content":"Can you have more than one Professional Training merit track?<br /> <br /> Say your character has Professional Training (Author) 1. You later take dots in a Mystery Cult that grants a dot of a different Professional Training. Do you now have two PT tracks? Should you just add the new dot to your original PT track? Should you just gain the value of the dots, as MtAw core recommends for ineligible MC merits?<br /> <br /> Professional Training 3 (Breadth of Knowledge) would be the best place to &quot;merge&quot; multiple tracks, but that's a somewhat narrow window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T22:17:29-07:00","id":1487693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1487692#post1487692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you have more than one Professional Training merit track?<br /> <br /> Say your character has Professional Training (Author) 1. You later take dots in a Mystery Cult that grants a dot of a different Professional Training. Do you now have two PT tracks? Should you just add the new dot to your original PT track? Should you just gain the value of the dots, as MtAw core recommends for ineligible MC merits?<br /> <br /> Professional Training 3 (Breadth of Knowledge) would be the best place to &amp;quot;merge&amp;quot; multiple tracks, but that's a somewhat narrow window.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if Professional Training is ruled as something you can\u2019t take multiple instances of, I feel one granted by MCI should be an exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T14:54:43-07:00","id":1488216,"title":"","content":"Say you want to enchant your Sanctum with Incognito Presence, but leave your Cabal unaffected. Or make your ally immune to all magic but your own via Wards and Signs. Would that exclusion clause be a Key, via a conjunctive Space effect along the lines of Secret Door? Or a conjunctive Fate effect, \u00e0la Warding Gesture's exclusion ability? Or would both be viable avenues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T15:15:26-07:00","id":1488217,"title":"","content":"All 3 are viable. Utilizing Space 2 with a Reach could apply a Key (or Space 3), conjunctional Prime 3 could let it be seen by those marked with the cabal's Nimbuses (which means imprinting the Signature Nimbus on guests) or conjunctional Fate 3 to allow entrance based on certain conditions. I think another possible option would be to make a Reach option for <i>Incognito Presence</i> to add mental Keys, things like only those who know its there and are searching for it with no ill emotions can find it.<br /> <br /> In general terms, it will either an Arcana 2 effect with a Reach or a Weaving of the given Arcana.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T03:38:11-07:00","id":1488250,"title":"","content":"Can you use the Hidden High Speech merit to disguise Mantra Yantras? It costs a point of Willpower, but it could come in useful when pretending to be a Sleeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T15:35:29-07:00","id":1488286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488250#post1488250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use the Hidden High Speech merit to disguise Mantra Yantras? It costs a point of Willpower, but it could come in useful when pretending to be a Sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be its main intended use, so I\u2019d say sure. Useful for Libertines, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T16:24:47-07:00","id":1488289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488250#post1488250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use the Hidden High Speech merit to disguise Mantra Yantras? It costs a point of Willpower, but it could come in useful when pretending to be a Sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, which is good if you are taking multiple turns to cast, giving the benefit of a mantra amidst a conversation. <br /> <br /> One of its coolest benefits is that it's like Thieves Cant, you can tell objectively true information or intent to another mage in a highly secure way, even in mundane settings. <br /> <br /> It also pairs well with Sleepwalkers with High Speech Perception, allowing information to be given to them in a way no other Sleepers could detect, especially Hunters. The Szary Straznik Legacy in my signature gives the merits to high enough members of the associated Mystery Cult, reinforcing their theme as the secret agents of the glyphs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:55:15-07:00","id":1488310,"title":"","content":"What kind of aesthetic do you imagine for Mage, in general? Vampires are modern gothic, Changelings are creepy whimsical Neil Gaiman-esque trash gothic, Promethean has some very striking imagery with alchemical equipment and Prometheans getting hit with big electric currents, etc. Mage seems a bit all over the place (or maybe flexible is a better way of putting it). A little pulpy, a lot &quot;ceremonial&quot; with masks and robes and strange costumes, some crystal-spires-and-togas influence? I'm just having a harder time visualizing it than most of the game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T20:54:13-07:00","id":1488314,"title":"","content":"Depends on the type of game and theme of the chronicle I am going for. But in general terms, anything street level probably has a Dresden Files style urban fantasy feel<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/image/jpeg;base64, PRICLpNMpWghzhfs8uafAkqbUjQd1GwjG0uzpmqekhGmWTB9Nha16CNOnCpUr41pcf43 e8VTcWQgMkP1NvlA e/wBKHLD480welwEC6vzBMwyZfUjz  SX bRZNw9SHVmY6BwCA9yTZjaw79ITKlsfFmHdP9wwoZ60/Cu3B HzCrQajfsLrLXyC1GBOolCgxuBw z9Oe0MaGiWadUn SVZk9RZ0jsRpBaZqVahKVch8p8/4/Pyi0LXLIJ02O3rBeK9hbuvczDFJtrDnDcTSvwTT0So6joeQeYZV GS5wzjwq3I2P 4biM7VUC5SvFdOxF/nv5wny8X P9iiWsi0 wbGMFUlZABINwfpFtBg/izL29LD o0FNO97IO65Ycbunvv/AEITTK5zdTcfSJfUT7r3LvS1vartB/v0oDJ7P OIU1WJKV8Gmh5BhfU