"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T02:34:51-07:00","id":1488344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488342#post1488342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i right in assuming that you should be able to specify a key for Create Avernian gate? (With +1 reach, and a number of requirements equal to the spell's potency)</div> </div> </div> </div>Death with Space conjunctive, probably. Space 2, since a Key barrier is effectively a Shielding effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T16:30:59-07:00","id":1488504,"title":"","content":"Familiars - I just noticed that the description for the familiar merit indicates that the familar could be &quot;wholly in twilight or fettered to an item or animal&quot;. What would be the point of the latter choice? An ephemeral entity using the fetter manifistation can't use numina and can only use influences on the thing to which it is fettered. Since essence bleed is not a problem for a familiar, I don't see any reason. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 07-30-2022, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T17:14:27-07:00","id":1488508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488504#post1488504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Familiars - I just noticed that the description for the familiar merit indicates that the familar could be &quot;wholly in twilight or fettered to an item or animal&quot;. What would be the point of the latter choice? An ephemeral entity using the fetter manifistation can't use numina and can only use influences on the thing to which it is fettered. Since essence bleed is not a problem for a familiar, I don't see any reason. Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe the ephemeral just wants to partly interact with the material world, or the mage wants it to (without full-on Materialization). <br /> <br /> A Fettered entity can't use its Numina, but it can still use its Influence (on its fetter) at a discount. That, and a Familiar by definition has a cooperative relationship with a being who can potentially do things better than its own Numina, so the loss likely isn't felt anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T17:25:03-07:00","id":1488509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488504#post1488504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Familiars - I just noticed that the description for the familiar merit indicates that the familar could be &quot;wholly in twilight or fettered to an item or animal&quot;. What would be the point of the latter choice? An ephemeral entity using the fetter manifistation can't use numina and can only use influences on the thing to which it is fettered. Since essence bleed is not a problem for a familiar, I don't see any reason. Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Narratively, modeling animal familiars and such. Mechanically, having a familiar whose body/control of a host doesn't require Essence to maintain by the hour.<br /> <br /> Also, Fettered entities can still use Numina, just not on things that aren't their Fetter. It's a minor distinction, but it's not nothing, especially given the breadth of options Numina can potentially cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T02:34:58-07:00","id":1488544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488344#post1488344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death with Space conjunctive, probably. Space 2, since a Key barrier is effectively a Shielding effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is conjunctive space Shielding. 1) it is more like conditional affect, so if it was conjunctional it would be fate. And 2) Spirit spells which open portals don't require conjunctional Space to add a key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T06:07:36-07:00","id":1488559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488544#post1488544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it is conjunctive space Shielding. 1) it is more like conditional affect, so if it was conjunctional it would be fate. And 2) Spirit spells which open portals don't require conjunctional Space to add a key.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space is the primary source of Key effects. To the degree that it's the chapter of the book that specifically describes them and their uses.<br /> <br /> Like most effects, you can replicate a Key effect with other Arcana, the sticking point becomes how you interpret it. I can't see Fate barring an open portal like Space can, but I could see it causing a portal to open when conditions are fulfilled. <br /> <br /> Similarly, if Spirit gives precedence, go for it. I only recommended Space because it's the sure-fire way to make Keys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T09:53:33-07:00","id":1488576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488509#post1488509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Fettered entities can still use Numina, just not on things that aren't their Fetter. It's a minor distinction, but it's not nothing, especially given the breadth of options Numina can potentially cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>After all, if you have a spirit of the thing that it is fettered to, it can still be using its Influences to do things with that fetter. Like, attach a rat spirit to a rat that it can Strengthen. <br /> <br /> I would assume that the mage is mostly the one pushing for the familiar to be fettered, for reasons of giving it a form of physical presence without the obviousness of being materialized and being able to keep a bit of a leash on it, and still able to use some powers that it couldn't if it was possessing.<br /> <br /> Heh, it occurs to me that with a fettered familiar, you really have a relationship with two entities; the animal remains its own being even if the spirit can push it a bit, and on top of being able to engage with it in its own right it kind of acts like something that can drag the spirit around as needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T11:28:15-07:00","id":1488586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488559#post1488559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Space is the primary source of Key effects. To the degree that it's the chapter of the book that specifically describes them and their uses.<br /> <br /> Like most effects, you can replicate a Key effect with other Arcana, the sticking point becomes how you interpret it. I can't see Fate barring an open portal like Space can, but I could see it causing a portal to open when conditions are fulfilled. <br /> <br /> Similarly, if Spirit gives precedence, go for it. I only recommended Space because it's the sure-fire way to make Keys.</div> </div> </div> </div>1.) Space is not the primary source of keys, the section basically says, since space includes lots of spells dealing with portals... It is only natural that many Space spells allow specifying a key.<br /> <br /> Spirit just lets you include a key (with the same method discussed in the Space section, one extra reach to key an Iris, though in Spirit Manse it allows you to do this without the extra reach - it is +1 reach for an Iris, with an optional free Key)<br /> <br /> 2.) My reading of Fabricated Fortune (fate veiling) is that you can use it to fake the conditions requried to staisfy a key, or prevent the correct key from being noticed and opening the iris.<br /> <br /> I presume Fate scrutiny or knowing should allow a player to reveal the key to a given mystery/spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T14:36:43-07:00","id":1488598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488586#post1488586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1.) Space is not the primary source of keys, the section basically says, since space includes lots of spells dealing with portals... It is only natural that many Space spells allow specifying a key.<br /> <br /> Spirit just lets you include a key (with the same method discussed in the Space section, one extra reach to key an Iris, though in Spirit Manse it allows you to do this without the extra reach - it is +1 reach for an Iris, with an optional free Key)<br /> <br /> 2.) My reading of Fabricated Fortune (fate veiling) is that you can use it to fake the conditions requried to staisfy a key, or prevent the correct key from being noticed and opening the iris.<br /> <br /> I presume Fate scrutiny or knowing should allow a player to reveal the key to a given mystery/spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, I'm not disagreeing that a Keys could be made without Space, just that Space is the primary Arcana for Keys. Without Space, the spell will need to be something that only affects their purview, like Avernian Gate. Spirit and Death are capable of fully Keying their portals because everything that passes through them is under their purview - converting things to ephemera, and placing them in a realm that resonates entirely with their themes. They also have the benefit of being able to affect Resonance and Manifestation Conditions, which would be an even more appropriate explanation of how they are denying access to certain swathes of transit.<br /> <br /> Fate can spoof you to meet the requirements of a given Key, but Space is the Arcana that defines boundaries. Fate has intent, which could be argued into a Key fairly easily, but thats not its primary use. There's no reason you <i>can't </i> make a Fate Key, but in terms of purview Space has precedence.<br /> <br /> For a rough analogy using Fabricate Fortune, Space is installing a sieve, Fate is using pressure to force something through that sieve. <br /> <br /> Fate can definately detect the requirements of a Key, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-31-2022, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T02:17:13-07:00","id":1488956,"title":"","content":"I'm hammering out an astronaut Legacy, with the third Attainment being protection against general space hazards like radiation or no atmosphere. What level of Extreme Environment would hard vacuumed be?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Current plan is to merge Environmental Shield with either Colocation (to create a self-contained environmental bubble around you identical to the other end of the Colocation) or Veil of Moments (ignore the environment outright, as long as you can avoid directed attacks. And don't mind being stagnant for the duration)<br /> <br /> The Colocation has the advantage of being able to support other people, but Veil of Moments is a simpler spell to convert into a workable Attainment</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-03-2022, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T07:25:36-07:00","id":1488972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488956#post1488956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hammering out an astronaut Legacy, with the third Attainment being protection against general space hazards like radiation or no atmosphere. What level of Extreme Environment would hard vacuumed be?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Current plan is to merge Environmental Shield with either Colocation (to create a self-contained environmental bubble around you identical to the other end of the Colocation) or Veil of Moments (ignore the environment outright, as long as you can avoid directed attacks. And don't mind being stagnant for the duration)<br /> <br /> The Colocation has the advantage of being able to support other people, but Veil of Moments is a simpler spell to convert into a workable Attainment</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Lets see, an extreme environment of 1 is exemplified by things like light snow or heavy rain, whereas a 4 (the maximum normally achievable) are tsunamis and tornadoes.<br /> <br /> The vaccum of space would suck out the air from your lungs, making you faint in 10 seconds, according to a NASA estimate. Your blood would boil, probably denaturing proteins and causing The Bends (from the air bubbles). Then the muscle swelling from the expanding liquids would cut off circulation to the heart and lungs. Eventually the blood vapor would be pulled off by the vaccum, taking your body heat with it (since the boiling process had to absorb thermal energy from somewhere). This would leave a semi frozen corpse with cooked internal organs. All of this would happen over the course of a minute. So I would say its tier 4, albeit one of the most horrific ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-03-2022, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T01:28:50-07:00","id":1489456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1488956#post1488956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hammering out an astronaut Legacy, with the third Attainment being protection against general space hazards like radiation or no atmosphere. What level of Extreme Environment would hard vacuumed be?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Current plan is to merge Environmental Shield with either Colocation (to create a self-contained environmental bubble around you identical to the other end of the Colocation) or Veil of Moments (ignore the environment outright, as long as you can avoid directed attacks. And don't mind being stagnant for the duration)<br /> <br /> The Colocation has the advantage of being able to support other people, but Veil of Moments is a simpler spell to convert into a workable Attainment</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I would not say Veil of Moments is enough to protect against hard vaccum. It prevents conditions which get worse with time, it doesn't prevent you from taking damage in an extreme environment (like being hit by lightening). <br /> <br /> Matter/Forces shielding might be better. Or a space ban to prevent energy and matter from leaving your body (protecting against the effect of low pressures, though you still have to cool down.... ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T02:58:12-07:00","id":1489460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489456#post1489456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would not say Veil of Moments is enough to protect against hard vaccum. It prevents conditions which get worse with time, it doesn't prevent you from taking damage in an extreme environment (like being hit by lightening). <br /> <br /> Matter/Forces shielding might be better. Or a space ban to prevent energy and matter from leaving your body (protecting against the effect of low pressures, though you still have to cool down.... ).</div> </div> </div> </div>I ended going with a combination of Colocation and Ban (Forces). The premise is that you anchor yourself to a specific point in space, and carry a bubble of that atmosphere with you. Check out the Extraterrestrial Seekers Legacy I posted for specific details, if it interests you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T12:52:57-07:00","id":1489498,"title":"","content":"What are acceptable limits for Rewrite History with only temporal sympathy ? The spell says that, with Temporal Sympathy, it may change any detail of the subject's history, so long as its possible. But then we have Reach options for skills, attributes and backgrounds. But shouldn't the default use allow that, provided you have temporal sympathy that goes back far enough ?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't that mean the Reaches are more of a brute force approach that doesn't require temporal sympathy ? If yes, then it feels thematically inconsistent. If no, then why all the extra Reach requirements? I can understand the inertia of moving things related to supernatural templates, but moving skills and merits seems like a driving thematic use, like becoming a well established member of a Mystery Cult or gaining some Status in a suspicious organization (like becoming a high clearance guard or researcher) when infiltrating them. <br /> <br /> So does that mean that by default, the spell with temporal sympathy could only rewrite minor things ? If Rewrite History only affects the subject, what could those things be ? How does it account for social merits, like Contacts, Allies or Resources ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T13:02:02-07:00","id":1489499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489498#post1489498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are acceptable limits for Rewrite History with only temporal sympathy ? The spell says that, with Temporal Sympathy, it may change any detail of the subject's history, so long as its possible. But then we have Reach options for skills, attributes and backgrounds. But shouldn't the default use allow that, provided you have temporal sympathy that goes back far enough ?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't that mean the Reaches are more of a brute force approach that doesn't require temporal sympathy ? If yes, then it feels thematically inconsistent. If no, then why all the extra Reach requirements? I can understand the inertia of moving things related to supernatural templates, but moving skills and merits seems like a driving thematic use, like becoming a well established member of a Mystery Cult or gaining some Status in a suspicious organization (like becoming a high clearance guard or researcher) when infiltrating them. <br /> <br /> So does that mean that by default, the spell with temporal sympathy could only rewrite minor things ? If Rewrite History only affects the subject, what could those things be ? How does it account for social merits, like Contacts, Allies or Resources ?</div> </div> </div> </div>My take is that baseline Rewrite History allows the player specify changes they want to make (Person X failed their AP History exam), and the ST choses how those changes affect the nitty-gritty of resultant timeline. By default, I assume this means the new timeline deviates as little as possible, adjusting much like one affected by Time-conjunctive Quarentine. The Reach effects then are the player exerting fine control over the changes (Person X failed their AP History exam, and thus never got into their first choice college, so they never joined that Mystery Cult)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-08-2022, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T14:05:40-07:00","id":1489502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489499#post1489499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My take is that baseline Rewrite History allows the player specify changes they want to make (Person X failed their AP History exam), and the ST choses how those changes affect the nitty-gritty of resultant timeline. By default, I assume this means the new timeline deviates as little as possible, adjusting much like one affected by Time-conjunctive Quarentine. The Reach effects then are the player exerting fine control over the changes (Person X failed their AP History exam, and thus never got into their first choice college, so they never joined that Mystery Cult)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So could conjunctional Fate 4 be used to be able to make these specific edits without Reaching ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T15:08:58-07:00","id":1489505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489502#post1489502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So could conjunctional Fate 4 be used to be able to make these specific edits without Reaching ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Under the premise that Chaos Mastery, Divine Intervention, and Strings of Fate could provide suitable templaes, I personally would allow it. Fate is decreeing that in this timeline, Person X's attempts to join the Mystery Cult were doomed to fail.<br /> <br /> Plus the XP investment into double-Adept seems like an acceptable trade-off.That's just me though, I could completely understand an ST shooting it down.<br /> <br /> Tangentially related, would someone who Awakened in a rewritten history remain Awakened when the spell ended? Not just the targets of the spell, but anyone in that alternate timelne? They'd need to have Constant Presence up, probably...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-08-2022, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T15:32:21-07:00","id":1489507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489505#post1489505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Under the premise that Chaos Mastery, Divine Intervention, and Strings of Fate could provide suitable templaes, I personally would allow it. Fate is decreasing that in this timeline, Person X's attempts to join the Mystery Cult were doomed to fail.<br /> <br /> Plus the XP investment into double-Adept seems like an acceptable trade-off.That's just me though, I could completely understand an ST shooting it down.<br /> <br /> Tangentially related, would someone who Awakened in a rewritten history remain Awakened when the spell ended? Not just the targets of the spell, but anyone in that alternate timelne? They'd need to have Constant Presence up, probably...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They remain permanently Awakened, no additional magic needed. <i>Signs of Sorcery </i>page 130 (and perhaps<i> Imperial Mysteries</i>) describe an Awakening as an Imperial spell cast by the Watchtowers, one that writes itself into the source code of existence <i>Ad Aeternum, </i>making the change always true from that moment. So if you look at someone's destiny before they Awakened, they were destined to remain Sleepers. If you go back to the past to examine it, you will be certain they were always destined to Awaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T21:04:47-07:00","id":1489527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489507#post1489507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They remain permanently Awakened, no additional magic needed. <i>Signs of Sorcery </i>page 130 (and perhaps<i> Imperial Mysteries</i>) describe an Awakening as an Imperial spell cast by the Watchtowers, one that writes itself into the source code of existence <i>Ad Aeternum, </i>making the change always true from that moment. So if you look at someone's destiny before they Awakened, they were destined to remain Sleepers. If you go back to the past to examine it, you will be certain they were always destined to Awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a hard time thinking of Rewrite History as anything other than a &quot;What If&quot; simulation playing out in the minds of the caster and target. Like, the only proof that it happened once it ends is the memories in those parties. Unless you're, say, using it on a supernatural to remove their template. Elder Vampires are much easier to kill if they aren't vampires at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-09-2022, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T09:15:28-07:00","id":1489554,"title":"","content":"New Q:<br /> <br /> As a storyteller, I'm toying with the idea that one of the PCs, upon Awakening, has literally moved to a new timeline/Universe (my overarching story will be about the cult of the Doomsday Clock merging timelines/universes to cause so much Paradox that it will end everything).<br /> <br /> Assuming that can happen, how would you apply post-cognition? <br /> <br /> Would his timeline 'start' when he came to this reality, would looking further into his past need to overcome a greater withstand rating it would it function as normal with the caster being left to ponder any differences he spots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26816-john-courage","name":"John Courage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T09:36:54-07:00","id":1489559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Courage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489554#post1489554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming that can happen</div> </div> </div> </div>It can, and the supplement Signs of Sorcery even talks about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Courage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">how would you apply post-cognition?</div> </div> </div> </div>By the usual way that this works, Postcognition is going to reveal a past as though the person always existed in the same universe as everybody else, even if they have no memory of those events. Sometimes it may look at things as though the person's existence only even started when they Awakened.<br /> <br /> I think sometimes the easiest way to manage the whole thing is to say that their Awakening is such a profound transformation that it severs most or all of their temporal sympathy to their Sleeper life at all, which can leave some mages wondering if they might not have had a previous life they're just highly deluded about.<br /> <br /> Still, I think it's okay to occasionally have an instance where a person can be examined to find that they have an impossible past. I'm sure there would be locations where the Mystery is that is how Postcognition works on everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T09:52:18-07:00","id":1489562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Courage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489554#post1489554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Q:<br /> <br /> As a storyteller, I'm toying with the idea that one of the PCs, upon Awakening, has literally moved to a new timeline/Universe (my overarching story will be about the cult of the Doomsday Clock merging timelines/universes to cause so much Paradox that it will end everything).<br /> <br /> Assuming that can happen, how would you apply post-cognition?<br /> <br /> Would his timeline 'start' when he came to this reality, would looking further into his past need to overcome a greater withstand rating it would it function as normal with the caster being left to ponder any differences he spots?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait a second, John Courage, I know that Shadow Name.....Technocrat on board, notify the Hierarch, call an Adamant Sage ! If a NWO agent made it here, it means one of those Void Engineer spaceships is docked somewhere nearby, normally near somewhere associated with a Verge.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness though, it would depend on the role I wanted him to play. If he would be a minor key to it, I would make Postcognition show two timelines overlapping in the same scene. Anomalies and inconsistencies would create frame skips in their history, or one scene leading others that make no sense &quot;spatially&quot;, which when overlapped with the previous effect would make things incredibly weird. Paradox environmental effects around them would be more likely to cause Shattered Time (found on page 46 of <i>Dark Eras</i>) and they would always look like a temporally displaced being under Time Sight, even if no spells were active.<br /> <br /> If players were really invested in them, if they wanted to harness this anomaly into something powerful or if I wanted to hint they were sent there as an unknowing pawn of a more powerful being, then I would give them the option of becoming a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1244944-homebrew-legacy-the-kalachakra-feedback-wanted\">Kalachakra</a>. Then I would recommend Re:Zero as a source of inspiration, ultimately giving the cabal the goal of aiming for the optimal timeline that fixed or reversed the goals of the Tick-Tocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-09-2022, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T11:00:10-07:00","id":1489569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Courage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489554#post1489554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Q:<br /> <br /> As a storyteller, I'm toying with the idea that one of the PCs, upon Awakening, has literally moved to a new timeline/Universe (my overarching story will be about the cult of the Doomsday Clock merging timelines/universes to cause so much Paradox that it will end everything).<br /> <br /> Assuming that can happen, how would you apply post-cognition? <br /> <br /> Would his timeline 'start' when he came to this reality, would looking further into his past need to overcome a greater withstand rating it would it function as normal with the caster being left to ponder any differences he spots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you are not retconning the new timeline (where the mage is awakened) and want seperate interaction timelines, then post cognition on the mage should let the caster see back into the other timeline with a withstand of 3 (for the weakest Temporal Sympathy).<br /> <br /> But i would also be very limited in what the caster can see, (see the limitations on scrying through a sympathic connection...) Making it fairly hard to actually determine that you've got a seperate timeline...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T01:11:38-07:00","id":1489613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489562#post1489562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait a second, John Courage, I know that Shadow Name.....Technocrat on board, notify the Hierarch, call an Adamant Sage ! If a NWO agent made it here, it means one of those Void Engineer spaceships is docked somewhere nearby, normally near somewhere associated with a Verge.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I used to post quite regularly as Courage (on WW forums...possibly here in the very early days) but after a very lengthy absence had to create a new account last year. I've been lurking since! He was a favourite from Ascension. In a campaign I ran I 'borrowed' the idea of Archetypes from Unknown Armies; Courage was essentially the Masterless Man.<br /> <br /> Back to the point about the PC, I think I may combine the answers posted so far as I like a lot of the ideas.<br /> <br /> My reading of Signs of Sorcery wasn't that a Transformative/External awakening literally moved you to an alternative Universe as <b>Isator</b> suggests; I took it that the person's Awakening literally changed this Universe but they were the only one that knew.<br /> <br /> However, going with the original idea, I like the idea from <b>Isator</b> that the Awakening is so profound that it severs ties to the previous life. The player's base idea was, like Richard Mayhew from Neverwhere, the world had forgotten him; so he is taking Occultation, Anonymity and Shadow Name as merits. I don't want the player to know at the start of the game that he has 'moved' between timelines, so I can just say that his Awakening changed the world around him.<br /> <br /> How the truth of the situation manifests could be a combination of the ideas from <b>KaiserAfini</b> and <b>orathaic</b>; As a Thrysus his nimbus could give a syncopated/displaced rhythm with Shattered Time paradox effects (I'll need to read Dark Eras) and always looking out of place. Anyone trying to scroll into his past would have a Withstand rating of 3 with limits on what they can see. I might make the Withstand rating higher as - undecided as of yet - the hand of an Archmaster/Exarch/Otherworld Force may have played a part.<br /> <br /> Thanks folks. Away to read Signs of Sorcery again...and to read Dark Eras!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26816,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26816-john-courage","user":"John Courage","date":". 08-10-2022, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26816-john-courage","name":"John Courage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T10:03:52-07:00","id":1489647,"title":"","content":"At Archmastery i would probably allow the Temporal Sympathy to be broken completely, which should be an interesting mystery. Like if someone specifically altered their past to break it a) they must have had a reason and b) they must have left some signs.<br /> <br /> For that approach, i would look at some of the advanced rules for mysteries in SoS it is Mysteries as Clues and Clues as Mysteries...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T15:00:50-07:00","id":1489793,"title":"","content":"Say you use a Creative Thaumaturgy Life spell to artificially inseminate an egg with normally incompatible parents - two of the same sex, a sterile couple, more than two parents, etc. Is that a Lasting effect? Or would the spell need to be sustained? If sustained, until the offspring is born?<br /> <br /> Mutable Mask can do something similar in that the new form can be made fertile, but I have to imagine that if its the &quot;mother&quot; that's being affected, the effects of the spell ending before delivery is... unfortunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-11-2022, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T15:38:23-07:00","id":1489799,"title":"","content":"I would speculate that should the effect be cast on the egg, then its subject to duration. Should it be a result of the parents being affected by Transform Life, then I would say its Lasting, since things like poison that were deployed by a mutation don't vanish. However, if the carrier is not suitable, then a magical effect would be needing. The effect being dispelled or ending before birth would result in some form of miscarriage, with possible health risks for the parent as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T16:16:15-07:00","id":1489807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489799#post1489799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would speculate that should the effect be cast on the egg, then its subject to duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the resultant child in that scenario only exists as long as the spell does, ala Create Life? And would it have a soul?<br /> <br /> (I must specify I mean this in game terms only)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-11-2022, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T16:41:43-07:00","id":1489809,"title":"","content":"I think the resulting child would be subject to some kind of withering effect when the spell ends, like when <i>Regeneration </i>expires. But would they have a soul ? No clue. It likely they won't, since they only exist due to the magic, so they would be affected by soulessness from birth. But if they do, that in itself could constitute a Mystery.<br /> <br /> Magic is weird and full of edge cases, so maybe exposure to certain phenomenon during gestation could make them be born with a soul. Maybe something happens after they are born. Perhaps some NPC bargained with a pylon composed of members of Peirasmon and Mammon, who pride themselves in being able to sell anything to a customer, for the right price, and now they are the first link in a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Needful_Things\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Needful Things</i></a> styled domino effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T19:32:26-07:00","id":1489825,"title":"","content":"Quicken Corpse has two Reach effects.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> +1 Reach: The mage may create a zombie suitable for combat. It uses its dot-rating as a dice pool for attacks, and has a Defense 3, Initiative 1, and Speed 6.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: The mage may spend a point of Mana to imbue the zombie with exceptional physical prowess. zombie has Defense 5, Initiative 3, and Speed 8. </div> </div> </div>Is the second Reach effect supposed to be read as a direct upgrade to the first? Or would you have to take both to get the best defense and the &quot;dot rating to dice pool&quot; effect? I assume it's a linear upgrade that got cut down for word count purposes, since a non-combat Retainer largely won't benefit from the higher defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T19:55:25-07:00","id":1489828,"title":"","content":"I think its meant as a linear upgrade, regular zombie battle butlers at 1 Reach, Thriller dancing zombie warriors for another Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T23:51:19-07:00","id":1489845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489793#post1489793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say you use a Creative Thaumaturgy Life spell to artificially inseminate an egg with normally incompatible parents - two of the same sex, a sterile couple, more than two parents, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, while I usually think magic is working on a more holistic level than a physiological one, I feel as though this is a question that calls for follow ups about the processes behind each of the suggestions.<br /> <br /> Like, I find infertility in particular to be a very strange thing to refer to &quot;normally incompatible parents&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or like, fertilizing an egg with the sperm of two fathers, is the notion there that the egg's nucleus is removed from the equation entirely, or that the two sperm samples are merged together in some fashion, or what?<br /> <br /> In a lot of those cases, I think one probably is holding together a lot of things that wouldn't be sustained without magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T04:12:59-07:00","id":1489867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489845#post1489845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, while I usually think magic is working on a more holistic level than a physiological one, I feel as though this is a question that calls for follow ups about the processes behind each of the suggestions.<br /> <br /> Like, I find infertility in particular to be a very strange thing to refer to &quot;normally incompatible parents&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might have been poor phrasing. I just meant any pair of individuals who are incapable of conceiving a child without external intervention, if at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489845#post1489845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or like, fertilizing an egg with the sperm of two fathers, is the notion there that the egg's nucleus is removed from the equation entirely, or that the two sperm samples are merged together in some fashion, or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you transform one sperm sample into an egg (ignoring a slew of chromosome issues there), at which point a question I've asked before comes up - at what point does the target of a spell change so much that the spell no longer applies to them? Once the transmuted egg is fertilized and reaches... let's say the germinal or embryonic phase, is the egg its own thing now? It's gone beyond what the original Imago likely encompassed. The original cells are long gone, and the cells that have developed <i>should</i> be stable and self-sustaining enough to progress a normal pregnancy, assuming it has a suitable gestation environment. It's not even like Create Life, which is an organism created whole cloth.<br /> <br /> I'd also note that two sperm fertilizing one egg <i>can</i> happen, but is a roughly 1% chance of occuring.<br /> <br /> Edit: actually, side tangent. The offspring of a Create Life creature and a normal creature is implied to be a Lasting entity. What about the offspring of a pair of Created Life entites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-12-2022, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T11:58:35-07:00","id":1489908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489793#post1489793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mutable Mask can do something similar in that the new form can be made fertile, but I have to imagine that if its the &quot;mother&quot; that's being affected, the effects of the spell ending before delivery is... unfortunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that is how mutabke mask works. It is a veiling practice. It doesn't change the underlying biology (which probably requires weaving).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutableMask</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">subject\u2019s apparent features, albeit only<br /> cosmetically and temporarily</div> </div> </div> </div>The other veiling example which comes to mind, is Corpse Mask - when used on a living target. I think it should impose a penalty on any medicine check if someone tries to heal your 'wound' (say you are hiding a magical injury from a sleeper family member... ) They can't see what your actual injury looks like, so i presume the veiling makes it harder to perform any medical treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:56:31-07:00","id":1489928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489908#post1489908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that is how mutabke mask works. It is a veiling practice. It doesn't change the underlying biology (which probably requires weaving).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The other veiling example which comes to mind, is Corpse Mask - when used on a living target. I think it should impose a penalty on any medicine check if someone tries to heal your 'wound' (say you are hiding a magical injury from a sleeper family member... ) They can't see what your actual injury looks like, so i presume the veiling makes it harder to perform any medical treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I misspoke- I meant Many Faces:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Many Faces</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than an illusion as with \u201cMutable Mask,\u201d the transformation caused by this spell is entirely physical and functional \u2014 subjects can be made fertile in their new forms</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-12-2022, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T16:28:20-07:00","id":1489971,"title":"","content":"Lets say a mage is using <i>Psychic Projection</i> to inspect a building before entering it, but then they discover it has a <i>Ban </i>that blocks beings in Mind Twilight from exiting it. When the mage cancels the spell, does their mind return to their body normally ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T16:40:26-07:00","id":1489974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489971#post1489971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say a mage is using <i>Psychic Projection</i> to inspect a building before entering it, but then they discover it has a <i>Ban </i>that blocks beings in Mind Twilight from exiting it. When the mage cancels the spell, does their mind return to their body normally ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd either give them Soul Shock, or throw them into a coma until either the body is brought into the building or the Ban is brought down. Leaning more towards the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T16:45:00-07:00","id":1489975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489971#post1489971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say a mage is using <i>Psychic Projection</i> to inspect a building before entering it, but then they discover it has a <i>Ban </i>that blocks beings in Mind Twilight from exiting it. When the mage cancels the spell, does their mind return to their body normally ?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, I\u2019m not sure if a psychic projection counts as a Twilight \u2018being\u2019 though. Although the Ban could\u2019ve made to specifically contain thoughts too\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T16:47:53-07:00","id":1489977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489971#post1489971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say a mage is using <i>Psychic Projection</i> to inspect a building before entering it, but then they discover it has a <i>Ban </i>that blocks beings in Mind Twilight from exiting it. When the mage cancels the spell, does their mind return to their body normally ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Ban is two-way, so if they can't get out they shouldn't have been able to get in in the first place, and &quot;ceasing to exist in Mind Twilight&quot; is distinct from crossing the spatial demarcations of the Ban in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T00:25:54-07:00","id":1490002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1489977#post1489977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Ban is two-way, so if they can't get out they shouldn't have been able to get in in the first place, and &quot;ceasing to exist in Mind Twilight&quot; is distinct from crossing the spatial demarcations of the Ban in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ban would be two-way, but it could also be setup as a trap (if that is what KaiserAfini is imagining). Hung spell with a conditional duration to activate the Ban once a mind enters...<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that ceasing to exist in that state is the same as teleporting out... In fact i think it is liable to kill you -mind can't return to the life support of its body, but can no longer exist as an psychic projection (supported by the spell). <br /> <br /> Though that would be a particularly harsh interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-13-2022, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T05:30:37-07:00","id":1490015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490002#post1490002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The B\u00e1n would he two-way, but it could also be setup as a trap (if that is what KaiserAfini is imagining). Hung spell with a conditional duration to activate the Ban once a mind enters...<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that ceasing to exist in that state is the same as teleporting out... In fact i think it is liable to kill you -mind can't return to the life support of its body, but can no longer exist as an psychic projection (supported by the spell).<br /> <br /> Though that would be a particularly harsh interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychic Projection lets you project yourself into a person's dreams in addition to the ability to just project your senses into Twilight, which is sufficiently distinct from &quot;magic that manipulates space&quot; that I don't believe it engages with the Ban in either the described fashion or the Clash it triggers with such powers. The worst-case scenario if the Ban somehow &quot;kills&quot; the projection is just that the mage becomes Soul-Shocked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T07:45:33-07:00","id":1490024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490015#post1490015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psychic Projection lets you project yourself into a person's dreams in addition to the ability to just project your senses into Twilight, which is sufficiently distinct from &quot;magic that manipulates space&quot; that I don't believe it engages with the Ban in either the described fashion or the Clash it triggers with such powers. The worst-case scenario if the Ban somehow &quot;kills&quot; the projection is just that the mage becomes Soul-Shocked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Teleportation out causes a clash, so i'd probably rule a clash here too and give the soul shocked condition if they lost the clash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T09:34:59-07:00","id":1490033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490024#post1490024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleportation out causes a clash, so i'd probably rule a clash here too and give the soul shocked condition if they lost the clash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna point out again that &quot;ceasing to exist&quot; is not teleportation.<br /> <br /> Switch the particulars of this scenario to locking in a goetia instead of a projected consciousness; would you propose that a goetia within the Ban cannot be discorporated and is therefore immortal?<br /> <br /> Ban is a Spatial process, not a spiritual one, so if the means of egress don't involve physically crossing the boundaries of the spell or manipulating space to leave it, it should logically not affect those methods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-13-2022, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T12:43:39-07:00","id":1490048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490033#post1490033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna point out again that &quot;ceasing to exist&quot; is not teleportation.<br /> <br /> Switch the particulars of this scenario to locking in a goetia instead of a projected consciousness; would you propose that a goetia within the Ban cannot be discorporated and is therefore immortal?<br /> <br /> Ban is a Spatial process, not a spiritual one, so if the means of egress don't involve physically crossing the boundaries of the spell or manipulating space to leave it, it should logically not affect those methods.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ceases to exist&quot; sounds more like artistic prose than a specific description. As to the Goetia, I'd argue that they're either permanently destroyed, or discorperate to the nearest source of semi-appropriate Resonance within the bounds of the spell. Or possibly Clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-13-2022, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T13:13:28-07:00","id":1490050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490048#post1490048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Ceases to exist&quot; sounds more like artistic prose than a specific description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discorporation is the consequence of an invisible entity being destroyed. In certain circumstances they reform elsewhere, but the starting point is &quot;there was a ghost here, it's gone now,&quot; not &quot;the ghost has gone to a better place.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to the Goetia, I'd argue that they're either permanently destroyed, </div> </div> </div>Shortcutting past the entire function of ephemeral beings losing all their Corpus with Essence in their system, which feels out of keeping with the existing lethal uses of the spell (e.g. the sidebar on the same page).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or discorperate to the nearest source of semi-appropriate Resonance within the bounds of the spell. </div> </div> </div>Discorporated entities reform in an area that is described as a safe place first and a Conditioned location optionally. A Banned area below a certain Scale functionally has no safe places in it if something is able to Discorporate it therein.<br /> <br /> Different comparison to further highlight the way in which this does not work: adding Death to a Ban to only forbid souls from crossing it should logically not prevent souls from vanishing at the point of death just on the strength of incorporating Death into the Ban, because that is a different thing from preventing souls from entering or leaving the Ban. This isn't an Exorcism/Banishment/Familiar/Bind [Ephemeral Being] situation \u2014 Ban is a Space spell that works on Spatial effects, not the normal consequences of killing something. It would be like Banning liquids from crossing the Ban somehow translating to not being able to boil water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T13:33:58-07:00","id":1490054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490033#post1490033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna point out again that &quot;ceasing to exist&quot; is not teleportation.<br /> <br /> Switch the particulars of this scenario to locking in a goetia instead of a projected consciousness; would you propose that a goetia within the Ban cannot be discorporated and is therefore immortal?<br /> <br /> Ban is a Spatial process, not a spiritual one, so if the means of egress don't involve physically crossing the boundaries of the spell or manipulating space to leave it, it should logically not affect those methods.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of Discorporation (then manifestation effect) does not require any motion. Their corpus can be destroyed without them crossing a ban (whether by that manifestation or by direct damage). <br /> <br /> Which then causes it to hibernate, and pushed back its home realm. It is at this point that the ban may be able to prevent normal movement, whether sports, ghost, or goetia. <br /> <br /> I think a mage can trap them using Space alone. You can add Mind to a ban to make it only block mental projections or Goetia. Which i think definitely prevents them from being pushed back to their body/the astral.<br /> <br /> But they are not immortal in that case. They can be forced into hibernation and lacking a source of essence, they will never wake up.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and reading your other comments, i still disagree.<br /> <br /> The comparison is with Spirits banned from entering an area (without adding spirit they can be banned) you would argue they can cross the gauntlet because it is a spiritual transition, not a spatial one. Is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-13-2022, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T13:43:18-07:00","id":1490056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490050#post1490050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discorporation is the consequence of an invisible entity being destroyed. In certain circumstances they reform elsewhere, but the starting point is &quot;there was a ghost here, it's gone now,&quot; not &quot;the ghost has gone to a better place.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You used &quot;cease to exist&quot; to describe the Psychic Projection, unless I misunderstood the post. Which I don't find to make a lot of sense in the context of said projection - you're still connected to your body, so its plausable that you need a clear path to &quot;snap back&quot; to your body. That's also why I lean towards it putting you into a coma until the Ban comes down - your mind is trapped in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490050#post1490050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shortcutting past the entire function of ephemeral beings losing all their Corpus with Essence in their system, which feels out of keeping with the existing lethal uses of the spell (e.g. the sidebar on the same page).</div> </div> </div> </div>The black humor text about how long it will take to suffocate a person? That honestly seems to support the case for them not being able to reform in a safe space - anyone inside the Ban is limited by any environmental concerns that the Ban limits. Heck, Ban reads like a way to build ghost traps and salt circles, which traditionally have been ways to trap and permenantly destory a captured ghost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490050#post1490050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discorporated entities reform in an area that is described as a safe place first and a Conditioned location optionally. A Banned area below a certain Scale functionally has no safe places in it if something is able to Discorporate it therein.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which gives even more credence to them not being able to reform, similar to a human drowning because they can't reach the surface, but possibly finding pockets of air to prolong their life. If you want to give the entity a chance to survive, I reiterate my suggestion of it forcing a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490050#post1490050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Different comparison to further highlight the way in which this does not work: adding Death to a Ban to only forbid souls from crossing it should logically not prevent souls from vanishing at the point of death just on the strength of incorporating Death into the Ban, because that is a different thing from preventing souls from entering or leaving the Ban. This isn't an Exorcism/Banishment/Familiar/Bind [Ephemeral Being] situation \u2014 Ban is a Space spell that works on Spatial effects, not the normal consequences of killing something. It would be like Banning liquids from crossing the Ban somehow translating to not being able to boil water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Souls are not a good comparison to any kind of standard behavior, since they're one of the most persistent mysteries for Mages. No-one knows where they go when an entity dies, or how they make that transition. Similarly, Soul Jar provides an example of a spell containing a soul, something you coud potentially extrapolate into a Death Ban to keep a soul from exiting. Not something I'd allow in a game, but it's not unreasonable.<br /> <br /> Also, an anti-Mind ban will require dots in Mind to cast... Meaning it's also targeted specifically to that &quot;frequency&quot; of entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-13-2022, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T15:40:07-07:00","id":1490072,"title":"","content":"The issue I'm seeing is with the idea that cancelling the spell causes the projected mind to &quot;return&quot; to the body as though it is crossing a space to do so that it can be blocked from. What I think of as the baseline for how Supernal magic works would mean that doesn't really make sense.<br /> <br /> It reads to me that there's no transitional process between states when a spell is involved; it's more like a binary state to reality where things change discretely between &quot;normal&quot; and &quot;effect defined by imago present&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you cast a spell to have a longer limb, it's not creating a process that allows it to grow, it's changing the essence of how long it is; you couldn't hold it in a vice to keep it from getting shorter when the spell ends.<br /> <br /> So you can't put a mental projection into a space where it would matter that the originator switched off the state of reality where their mind can be separate from their body.<br /> <br /> Now, I do think that you can trap somebody's mental projection, but it's not based in creating a boundary for them (at least not at first), but making it so that their projected state is based on <i>your</i> spell, not theirs. Cast that spell on them while they're in your clutches, and it won't matter that they shut off their spell, their state is now defined by yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T19:38:36-07:00","id":1490085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490056#post1490056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I don't find to make a lot of sense in the context of said projection - you're still connected to your body, so its plausable that you need a clear path to &quot;snap back&quot; to your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not plausible at all, given that there are a number of supernatural powers based around projecting your senses that <i>do</i> maintain enough of a residual awareness to allow/force you to maintain the projection if your body is disturbed and Psychic Projection is not one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That honestly seems to support the case for them not being able to reform in a safe space - anyone inside the Ban is limited by any environmental concerns that the Ban limits. Heck, Ban reads like a way to build ghost traps and salt circles, which traditionally have been ways to trap and permenantly destory a captured ghost. </div> </div> </div>You can do that with Death by itself. Space is still not the primary building block to use for depriving an ephemeral being of Essence any more than it is the thing to look to for opening an Avernian Gate or linking a spirit to a material actor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which gives even more credence to them not being able to reform, similar to a human drowning because they can't reach the surface, but possibly finding pockets of air to prolong their life. If you want to give the entity a chance to survive, I reiterate my suggestion of it forcing a Clash of Wills. </div> </div> </div>Your suggestion entails a ghost or spirit rolling Rank against Gnosis + Space for something that is supposed to happen when they lose all their Corpus to continue to happen normally in the face of a spell designed to keep phenomena inside or outside a region of space, when the thing that is happening is the phenomenon in question being destroyed, or, in the case of a Psychic Projection, a person waking up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Souls are not a good comparison to any kind of standard behavior, since they're one of the most persistent mysteries for Mages. No-one knows where they go when an entity dies, or how they make that transition. </div> </div> </div>The implication you are making here is that discorporation <i>is</i> a spatial process despite the fact that spirits don't need sympathy to a location to reform in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, Soul Jar provides an example of a spell containing a soul, something you coud potentially extrapolate into a Death Ban to keep a soul from exiting. Not something I'd allow in a game, but it's not unreasonable. </div> </div> </div>The way Mage constructs spells is very distinctly not based on extrapolation \u2014 a spell does the thing it is made to do, and doing something else entails a different spell. &quot;Stop a spirit from discorporating or a soul from moving on&quot; are in the same conceptual neck of the woods as &quot;stop a life from ending,&quot; which is a distinctly different phenomenon from &quot;stop living/spiritual beings from entering or leaving this space.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, an anti-Mind ban will require dots in Mind to cast... Meaning it's also targeted specifically to that &quot;frequency&quot; of entity. </div> </div> </div>And in the case of Psychic Projection the &quot;entity&quot; in question is literally your senses. I don't agree with the reading that supposes a Mind Ban causes people passing through it to be knocked out, either, while we're on the subject.<br /> <br /> Archmasters' Golden Roads potentially separating visitors' minds from their bodies is supposed to be an aberrant circumstance, and that doesn't really work out too well if it's something any Mastigos who's put any amount of study into their Path can accomplish as a side-effect of setting up a perimeter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-13-2022, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T00:56:18-07:00","id":1490102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490085#post1490085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">our suggestion entails a ghost or spirit rolling Rank against Gnosis + Space for something that is supposed to happen when they lose all their Corpus to continue to happen normally in the face of a spell designed to keep phenomena inside or outside a region of space, when the thing that is happening is the phenomenon in question being destroyed, or, in the case of a Psychic Projection, a person waking up</div> </div> </div> </div>No. What happens when a emphemeral entity loses all it's corpus is clear. <br /> 1) The corpus explodes (possibly showering the area in a harvestable resource - plasm equalling the size of a ghost in that case)<br /> 2) they fall into hibernation<br /> And 3) they reform in a safe place (effectively teleporting there)<br /> <br /> It is only this last step which is blocked by a ban.<br /> I think the best comparison is teleporting into the Shadow, to do it you need both Space and Spirit. You can mundanely do it by substituting walking for the spatial movement and a spirit iris (Locus) for the spirit part.<br /> <br /> If either part is missing you can't cross into (or out of) the shadow. No Iris, you can walk whereever you want, not going to cross the gauntlet, no ability to walk? You can lie beside a locus all day, you're not going to go anywhere ..<br /> <br /> Ban (and to a greater extent Quarentine) prevent the spatial component. And for supernatural effect which would bypass it provokes a clash of wills (it literally says as much in the spell description).<br /> <br /> I don't think Souls are particularly illustrative, because we don't know what happens to them or how. I think they may be on Archmastery level and thus auto-win any clash of wills; though a soul jar can still prevent them moving on, so I'm unsure... <br /> <br /> Psychic projection i think i would allow a clash of wills to return to your body without the soul shocked condition (again based on the spell description).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way Mage constructs spells is very distinctly not based on extrapolation \u2014 a spell does the thing it is made to do, and doing something else entails a different spell. &quot;Stop a spirit from discorporating or a soul from moving on&quot; are in the same conceptual neck of the woods as &quot;stop a life from ending,&quot; which is a distinctly different phenomenon from &quot;stop living/spiritual beings from entering or leaving this space&quot; </div> </div> </div>This is generally called a straw man, because nobody is claiming that a ban should stop Discorporation (either an emphemeral entity using the manifestation or their corpus being destroyed). They question is where the discorporated entity ends up. Which in this case should still be inside the ban (if it fails a clash of wills).<br /> <br /> That is precisely what the spell Ban does, and only that.<br /> <br /> Likewise a person can die within a Ban (starved of oxygen) and their body and ghost will remain trapped there until the spell ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-14-2022, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T02:04:49-07:00","id":1490107,"title":"","content":"Objects can have Sympathetic ties to each other, right? Like, if a Mage is trying to locate other copies of a book, could they use Sympathy? Probably just Weak connections, I'd imagine...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I'm planning a Legacy based around collecting books. Using Correspondence to find sequels and related texts seems like a neat Initiate power.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T03:47:38-07:00","id":1490111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490107#post1490107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objects can have Sympathetic ties to each other, right? Like, if a Mage is trying to locate other copies of a book, could they use Sympathy? Probably just Weak connections, I'd imagine...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px 