 (which i don't see as a problem, just extra leg work...)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> For a legacy you could make it a special version of the spell which automatically finds the right connection to follow...</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Connection to the author, and from the author to their other works, maybe? The first Reach effect from Correspondence would work for that, although it begs the question of if you have a Connection to text you <i>publish</i>, even if you don't physically write it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-14-2022, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T05:13:12-07:00","id":1490120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490107#post1490107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objects can have Sympathetic ties to each other, right? Like, if a Mage is trying to locate other copies of a book, could they use Sympathy? Probably just Weak connections, I'd imagine...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I'm planning a Legacy based around collecting books. Using Correspondence to find sequels and related texts seems like a neat Initiate power.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026\u2026. While nothing IIRC says two objects <i>can\u2019t</i> have sympathy with each other, <i>every instance of sympathetic connection described in Mage material</i> (again, iirc) assumes at least one end be capable of feeling. So\u2026 perhaps Not.<br /> <br /> This is broadly similar to the Ban &amp; Psychic Projection query above I believe. Magical stuff sometimes just skips the \u2018logical\u2019 step between results.<br /> <br /> Of course, since we\u2019re talking about Legacies and Attainments, you can always slip in a clause that says \u201cIt works this way for these guys!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T09:41:29-07:00","id":1490139,"title":"","content":"I think it could be logical for objects to have sympathetic connections to other objects that were of significance to creating their state of being; a sculpture connected to the tools used to carve it, for instance. I don't think such connections would ever be stronger than Medium, and I don't think they would last very long, there's not much to maintain the association.<br /> <br /> Even then I feel a bit tentative. I read sympathy in terms of the game's overall metaphysics for the Space Arcanum, and the basic axiom of that Arcanum is &quot;actual distance is an illusion, the truth is a matter of perception&quot;, which I would say privileges sympathy as a property of conscious beings. My main reservation is in thinking about how objects can be targeted and it feels as though it should be possible to do so with something like a piece of it taken away; a sliver of brick taken out of a building's wall, for instance.<br /> <br /> But sympathy isn't really a matter of abstract, conceptual associations, nor are such things generally possible to target with spells.<br /> <br /> I think the best bet for that sort of thing is not in Space but in Fate. That's the Arcanum with a basis for giving things certain qualifiers; conditional duration pegs spell length to particular circumstances, Oaths Fulfilled allows you to give yourself awareness of some particular outcome befalling a subject (it could alert you if a person writes a book that is a sequel to a previous work of theirs), Serendipity guides you towards desired objectives, and Strings of Fate allows you to just kind of declare some wanted result will be. I feel those give it a certain purview over abstract relationships.<br /> <br /> Either way, I think this is a Legacy where in the early stages you can give yourself some of the diagnostic tools, but are still going to have to put in a lot of the legwork.<br /> <br /> I mean, depending on how much legwork there is. Looking for book sequels doesn't exactly imply searching for rare tomes, in which case I'd feel as though a lot of the searching and acquisition would be relatively mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T11:14:42-07:00","id":1490154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490139#post1490139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best bet for that sort of thing is not in Space but in Fate. That's the Arcanum with a basis for giving things certain qualifiers; conditional duration pegs spell length to particular circumstances, Oaths Fulfilled allows you to give yourself awareness of some particular outcome befalling a subject (it could alert you if a person writes a book that is a sequel to a previous work of theirs), Serendipity guides you towards desired objectives, and Strings of Fate allows you to just kind of declare some wanted result will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, looking at the example unveiling spell Interconnections (fate 1), it can detect sympathetic connections between the subjects, aswell as the main effect of detecting the marks of fate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But sympathy isn't really a matter of abstract, conceptual associations, nor are such things generally possible to target with spells. </div> </div> </div>I am 90% sure you are describing the Temenotic connections there. Definitely no sympaties, vaguely Mind rather than Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:24:47-07:00","id":1490172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490139#post1490139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, depending on how much legwork there is. Looking for book sequels doesn't exactly imply searching for rare tomes, in which case I'd feel as though a lot of the searching and acquisition would be relatively mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sequel&quot; here including sequential journals or other notebooks, but I take your point. Thanks for the detailed rational, it was interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T17:04:29-07:00","id":1490200,"title":"","content":"What about using Prime and Space to find the Eidoforms of a specific media or collection ? It also makes looking for Grimoires easier and safer as well.There are Grimoires that are seeded with false and dangerous information on purpose, the Guardians and Abyss did so with the Codex of Lies and Tome of Power, respectively. Knowing objective fact from lies is important, distinguishing warped and corrupted rotes from normal ones can be a lifesaver. <br /> <br /> In addition, if you find the English Literature Eidoform, for example, then you added infinite valuable sources of information to the collection. So it makes each acquisition all the more meaningful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-14-2022, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T02:59:47-07:00","id":1490236,"title":"","content":"Can you use Create Life to create sacrificial stock? That is, could I walk up to the local Life Master and request a couple of cows to sacrifice for Mana and Sacrificial Relinquishment? If so, does that spell need to have been safely relinquished, or could they have just unsafely relinquished it?<br /> <br /> And was there ever an answer as to what level Wisdom sin sacrificing animals for mana was?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T03:23:48-07:00","id":1490238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490236#post1490236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use Create Life to create sacrificial stock? That is, could I walk up to the local Life Master and request a couple of cows to sacrifice for Mana and Sacrificial Relinquishment? If so, does that spell need to have been safely relinquished, or could they have just unsafely relinquished it?<br /> <br /> And was there ever an answer as to what level Wisdom sin sacrificing animals for mana was?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is a life then you should be able to sacrifice it. I doubt a master will be using create life for you, least of all with an indefinite/relinquished spell - since the effort required for it seems greater than you get benefit from the sacrifice - but that seems like an rp limitation rather than a mechanical one (imo it is not wise to ask a master to make you a magic cow, when you can ask a farmer, they are far more common).<br /> <br /> As for the act of hubris itself. I haven't seen an answer. I guess it depends on the mage in question. Some may see it as equivalent to murder... For others it might be understanding.<br /> <br /> But since it is always an act of hubris that tmeans a wisdom 1 mage should have to roll, and since they don't roll for understanding would you A) infer that it is falling (1 die) act for all mages, or B) it is an act of hubris, but understanding (3 die) and thus doesn't require a roll for lower wisdom mages?<br /> <br /> Edit: actually reading the example spell may lead to conclude that Irish an act of hubris against enlightened wisdom <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreateLifeExampleSpell</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the spell\u2019s Duration expires, so does the created organism, which may count as an Act of Hubris against Enlightened Wisdom. Simply creating the living creature knowing this may also count as an Act of Hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-15-2022, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T04:13:18-07:00","id":1490242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490236#post1490236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use Create Life to create sacrificial stock? That is, could I walk up to the local Life Master and request a couple of cows to sacrifice for Mana and Sacrificial Relinquishment? If so, does that spell need to have been safely relinquished, or could they have just unsafely relinquished it?<br /> <br /> And was there ever an answer as to what level Wisdom sin sacrificing animals for mana was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing seems to stop that. And if you\u2019re nigh-immediately killing the animals, relinquishment won\u2019t be an issue. Just keep in mind that finding a Master who\u2019d actually do all that for you is going to be troublesome all by itself.<br /> <br /> I mean, someone who can and will casually create life for the sole purpose of killing it probably isn\u2019t someone you\u2019d want to hang out with, even by mages\u2019 standards. Who knows what that Master will charge you as a price, or what shenanigans you\u2019d get entangled in by associating with that Master (especially considering what kind of Shadow Name and Long-Term Nimbus this Master likely has developed\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T04:41:20-07:00","id":1490243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490242#post1490242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(especially considering what kind of Shadow Name and Long-Term Nimbus this Master likely has developed\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div>Should we be <i>more</i> or <i>less</i> worried if it's a prophetic Thrysus who uses the Shadow Name Haruspex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T05:33:19-07:00","id":1490249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490243#post1490243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should we be <i>more</i> or <i>less</i> worried if it's a prophetic Thrysus who uses the Shadow Name Haruspex?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there was this Left-Handed Legacy back in 1e called Haruspices, so Yes Worry? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T06:00:46-07:00","id":1490251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490243#post1490243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should we be <i>more</i> or <i>less</i> worried if it's a prophetic Thrysus who uses the Shadow Name Haruspex?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it's the Left-Handed Legacy that gains an eerily precise notion of the future via sacrificial yantra, then probably worry. But if its just their Shadow Name and you notice they are starting to behave like Artemy Burakh, its probably a good idea to keep an eye on them, but it might be very enlightening to see what they figure out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T13:55:41-07:00","id":1490286,"title":"","content":"If you have Tune In active, do you need to have Transmission set to Sensory Range in order to affect signals you're receiving?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T14:24:08-07:00","id":1490293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490286#post1490286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have Tune In active, do you need to have Transmission set to Sensory Range in order to affect signals you're receiving?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sometimes, the description for <i>Tune In</i> states &quot;<i>Satellite internet and TV programming, closed walkie-talkies, CB broadcasts, and radio transmissions all become <b>open to her senses</b>, as well as wireless communications.</i>&quot;, meaning that the mage can see data being transmitted in the area they are inside (like satellite internet, radio or a wifi network) or things they can observe rather than touch (such as data being sent over cables). So if your phone can manipulate it, so can you. Which also means <i>Tune In</i> is more likely to be an Unveiling (uncover phenomena via sensory information) rather than Knowing (receive information on the thing being examined).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T14:47:12-07:00","id":1490296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490249#post1490249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there was this Left-Handed Legacy back in 1e called Haruspices, so Yes Worry? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Prospective Left-Handed. It would depend on whether or not doing that shit to actual people pans out.<br /> <br /> Animal sacrifice is something that mages are kind of dubious about, but is also something that literally every initiated member of the Mysterium has done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-15-2022, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T14:48:07-07:00","id":1490297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490293#post1490293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sometimes, the description for <i>Tune In</i> states &quot;<i>Satellite internet and TV programming, closed walkie-talkies, CB broadcasts, and radio transmissions all become <b>open to her senses</b>, as well as wireless communications.</i>&quot;, meaning that the mage can see data being transmitted in the area they are inside (like satellite internet, radio or a wifi network) or things they can observe rather than touch (such as data being sent over cables). So if your phone can manipulate it, so can you. Which also means <i>Tune In</i> is more likely to be an Unveiling (uncover phenomena via sensory information) rather than Knowing (receive information on the thing being examined).</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is weird, because knowing spells let you understand the Supernal meaning - so it doesn't matter how the signal is encrypted/what language it is in; whereas unveiling spells would make the info available to your sense (but you should need a conjunctional mind effect to translate... Unless it is unencrypted and in a language you speak).<br /> <br /> But i don't think that is how the the spells are written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T04:19:53-07:00","id":1490367,"title":"","content":"I know Invisible Runes is listed as being primarily used as... what, Mage tags? A way to mark territory and pass messages, at any rate. Have any of you -or your players- used them as Rune-Yantras-In-A-Can?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T05:29:16-07:00","id":1490374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490367#post1490367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Invisible Runes is listed as being primarily used as... what, Mage tags? A way to mark territory and pass messages, at any rate. Have any of you -or your players- used them as Rune-Yantras-In-A-Can?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's possible to use them like that, but would require the usual ritual time to write them. Should they be dispelled, then so would the spell they are related to, so they do carry that extra risk. An alternative for mages that want to use discrete runes is to write them using UV paint and look for them via a black light flashlight. This would allow them to mark key places and locations with runes for later use in sympathetic casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T08:48:25-07:00","id":1490400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490367#post1490367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Invisible Runes is listed as being primarily used as... what, Mage tags? A way to mark territory and pass messages, at any rate. Have any of you -or your players- used them as Rune-Yantras-In-A-Can?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure Sanctum &amp; Singil (1e) goes into great depth on the kind of territory markings cabals make with invisible runes, thing like right of crossing or right of hospitality... I haven't read it, but it goes into great depth as far as i know.<br /> <br /> Marking a subject with invisible runes (instead of say a tattoo) would he insteresting, but again, to make valid runes for a yantra you require ritual time... Might be better off making real runes and then casting a supernal veil to make them hidden...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T13:37:01-07:00","id":1490435,"title":"","content":"I read the spell as letting you spontaneously generate text- if you use Instant Cast and Sensory Range then whatever runes you wanted to write manifest on the target. Under that assumption, you could use it to mark a target, then use the runes as a Yantra to hit them with another spell. Including another Instant spell, using the runes as a bullseye.<br /> <br /> It makes Invisible Runes an interesting choice for an Attainment - you can manifest effectively unbreakable runes, which can't be dispelled either. <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, can Invisible Runes be written independent of a surface? Just hanging in midair, for example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-16-2022, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T14:18:16-07:00","id":1490440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490435#post1490435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read the spell as letting you spontaneously generate text- if you use Instant Cast and Sensory Range then whatever runes you wanted to write manifest on the target. Under that assumption, you could use it to mark a target, then use the runes as a Yantra to hit them with another spell. Including another Instant spell, using the runes as a bullseye.<br /> <br /> It makes Invisible Runes an interesting choice for an Attainment - you can manifest effectively unbreakable runes, which can't be dispelled either.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, can Invisible Runes be written independent of a surface? Just hanging in midair, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, but it will trigger the Peripheral Sight since its not a Veiling and it still requires ritual time to figure out how to describe the spell in a High Speech rune. Doing it instantly would probably require a custom spell utilizing elements of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1175514#post1175514\">Hasten Symbolism</a> to make the process much faster.<br /> <br /> <i>Invisible Runes</i> can, however, generate all other types of texts and scripts on the fly, provided the mage knows them. Which means another application is to create a quick or covert summoning area. Lets say the mage wants to summon some kind of lightning Angel, using <i>Invisible Runes</i> they could make a summoning circle containing a Triangle of Solomon, elder Futhark runes, Enochian script and a binding seal to represent controlling the destructive elements of lightning. With that they could improvise a summoning area that looked like nothing out of the ordinary by mundane senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-16-2022, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T14:29:02-07:00","id":1490442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490440#post1490440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it still requires ritual time to figure out how to describe the spell in a High Speech rune.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you've never done so before, I would think. If it's a Mantra that you use all the time, or if you have Fluent High Speech, I don't think it would take longer to scribe than using spoken High Speech as a Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T17:11:37-07:00","id":1490458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490367#post1490367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have any of you -or your players- used them as Rune-Yantras-In-A-Can?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to go out on a limb here and suppose the fact that making a Rune Yantra normally takes your ritual interval to do precludes a spell's effects being described in anything that could reasonably be described as &quot;a short message,&quot; particularly given that the spell already makes the message in question invisible to anyone without Mage Sight and explicitly allows a Clash to attempts to overwrite them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T18:08:13-07:00","id":1490465,"title":"","content":"Perfect Recall (Mind 1) is an unveiling spell with a potency primary. It says that the subject can recall one memory per level of potency.<br /> It makes no special mention of duration of the memories, and since the practice is unveiling, it seems like the perfectly recalled memories are shrouded one turn later.<br /> That doesn't seem like the intent of the spell but does seem to be how the spell ought to work, according to the rules as written.<br /> Am I missing some element that makes the rules as written match the seeming intent OR do I just need to stop being such a needless pedant and chalk this up to mild error?<br /> <br /> Related question: If the memory is crisp for only for a turn, would the correct ruling be to treat it as if one were exposed to a picture briefly and then attempted to recall the memory of seeing the picture? In other words, is the spell Lasting insofar that you have a memory of the memory, and depending upon circumstance, itself dependent on an intelligence roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T18:39:01-07:00","id":1490469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490465#post1490465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect Recall (Mind 1) is an unveiling spell with a potency primary. It says that the subject can recall one memory per level of potency.<br /> It makes no special mention of duration of the memories, and since the practice is unveiling, it seems like the perfectly recalled memories are shrouded one turn later.<br /> That doesn't seem like the intent of the spell but does seem to be how the spell ought to work, according to the rules as written.<br /> Am I missing some element that makes the rules as written match the seeming intent OR do I just need to stop being such a needless pedant and chalk this up to mild error?<br /> <br /> Related question: If the memory is crisp for only for a turn, would the correct ruling be to treat it as if one were exposed to a picture briefly and then attempted to recall the memory of seeing the picture? In other words, is the spell Lasting insofar that you have a memory of the memory, and depending upon circumstance, itself dependent on an intelligence roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>My take is that it &quot;refreshes&quot; the memory to how it would be if you had just experienced it, with the quality of the recall begining to degrade from there as normal. So you'd have a window (one the ST should decide, but I'd recommend leaning on leniency for the sake of the narrative) in which the recall is photo-perfect for you to analyze.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Can you spend a Reach to change the Primary Factor to Scale, or does that only work for switching Potency and Duration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-16-2022, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T19:13:31-07:00","id":1490473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490469#post1490469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you spend a Reach to change the Primary Factor to Scale, or does that only work for switching Potency and Duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is only switching potency and duration. Can I access advanced duration without switching the primary factor?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T19:18:57-07:00","id":1490475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490473#post1490473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe that is only switching potency and duration. Can I access advanced duration without switching the primary factor?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, it just costs a Reach. Having it be the Primary Factor just gives you free steps along the track","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T02:20:53-07:00","id":1490496,"title":"","content":"1 reach for swapping primary factor to duration<br /> 1 reach for advanced duration <br /> Both for free steps in advanced duration which (in the above example) would kept your perfect recall for at least an hour, if not a full week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T12:31:21-07:00","id":1490642,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Storyteller can use Paradox Reach to change the spell factors of the spell, <b>to create Abyssal taint on the environment, or to summon an Abyssal entity.</b>&quot;<br /> Where can I find information on bolded text in the book? I got one success for my Paradox roll and I want to know what sort of entity I summoned or effect on the environment I've caused.<br /> <br /> Edit: I found a side-box that gives examples at the top of page 116.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  Answer. 08-18-2022, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T12:44:36-07:00","id":1490644,"title":"","content":"Page 116 and 117","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T12:47:20-07:00","id":1490646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490644#post1490644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 116 and 117</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be misreading them. I thought they were just for containing the Paradox. I released it into the world.<br /> <br /> I'd like to summon an Abyssal Entity, as it seems the most interesting. How do I do that with one Paradox success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  Added a specific question 08-18-2022, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T13:20:04-07:00","id":1490649,"title":"","content":"Psychic Domination doesn't explicitly impose a condition in the spell description. Is the broader idea of conditions to reflect such anomalies of character grounds to grant it or am I presuming too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T13:27:53-07:00","id":1490651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490646#post1490646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be misreading them. I thought they were just for containing the Paradox. I released it into the world.<br /> <br /> I'd like to summon an Abyssal Entity, as it seems the most interesting. How do I do that with one Paradox success?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't, each success on a Paradox roll becomes a Paradox Reach, which can be applied based on the table on page 116. 1 Reach allows you to undo or reassing an existing Reach effect. It takes 5 Reach to summon anything.<br /> <br /> This is by design, dealing with over Reach is cheap and easy for a starting mage. By the time their Gnosis is higher, each over Reach gives more Paradox dice, consumes more resources to compensate and consequently more spellcasting time.<br /> <br /> Since Paradox is normally a problem the mage creates, the system is designed in such a way as to build complacency, raising the danger constantly, until they eventually hang themselves with their own rope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T13:45:05-07:00","id":1490652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490649#post1490649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psychic Domination doesn't explicitly impose a condition in the spell description. Is the broader idea of conditions to reflect such anomalies of character grounds to grant it or am I presuming too much?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are completely different. <i>Psychic Domination</i> can be described as someone seizing the remote control of your brain and you will be pulled along for the ride, lucidly knowing those were not your thoughts. A Wise mage will use it discretely, in a situation where its easy to rationalize the command away. You froze because you were terrified, you ducked just in time for the bullet to miss due to survival instinct, you turned left instead of right because you were tired. But that does not mean it caused any feelings, its like Command Spirit, its using an admin command to tell the brain to execute a task.<br /> <br /> Regarding conditions, more information can be found on page 126. Temporary conditions and tilts can be inflicted with a Ruling, whereas Permanent conditions require a Patterning. So with Mind 2 they can make someone feel Guilty, but not become Delusional. They can make a subject Frightened, but only with Mind 4 can they make them Mesmerized (similar to the effects of a vampire's Majesty Discipline). They can force a surrender by making them feel Beaten Down with 2 dots, but not enter a Fugue state when a preprogrammed stimulus is used.<br /> <br /> Hope that proved helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-18-2022, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T13:19:26-07:00","id":1490732,"title":"","content":"How/Can you maintain spells?<br /> <br /> Eg: Mage casts spell with One Week duration. Six days pass, and they want to renew the Week long investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T13:25:16-07:00","id":1490733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490732#post1490732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How/Can you maintain spells?<br /> <br /> Eg: Mage casts spell with One Week duration. Six days pass, and they want to renew the Week long investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once cast, a spell runs its course and then dissipates. You can't &quot;refresh&quot; it, unfortunately - once the duration elapses, you have to cast it again. It's what makes Indefinite Duration so desirable. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, maintaining a spell takes up one of your [gnosis] spell-control slots. That means you should relinquish any long-term spells if you can, so you don't drown in the &quot;charged an extra Reach for every spell over your control limit&quot; effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-19-2022, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T13:53:54-07:00","id":1490735,"title":"","content":"That being said, its important to be careful as how you relinquish. Safe relinquishing costs a Willpower dot, which translates into a XP cost to buy it back.<br /> <br /> Unsafe relinquishing costs a Willpower point, but makes the spell mutate after a while. So you probably want to have someone with skill in dispellation end it before that happens. <br /> <br /> There are alternative relinquishment costs, but they can come with a cost (high mana fee, requiring someone to suffer a breaking point, etc) or dabbling in Left-Handed practices (killing a sentient being, destroying a soul, etc). However, its something mages are constantly researching, so there is plenty of room for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1472584#post1472584\">unusual approaches</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-19-2022, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T14:09:36-07:00","id":1490738,"title":"","content":"Thank you both. Opinion sought: Would using Mind's Know Nature to gain the person's name instead of their social and mental dice pools be an acceptable substitution?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T14:26:46-07:00","id":1490739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490738#post1490738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you both. Opinion sought: Would using Mind's Know Nature to gain the person's name instead of their social and mental dice pools be an acceptable substitution?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its reasonable to learn their name (part of how they define their identity) and Shadow Name (how they see their Supernal identity). Its part of knowing someone's nature to understand what names have the most emotional connection to who they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T14:27:15-07:00","id":1490741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490738#post1490738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you both. Opinion sought: Would using Mind's Know Nature to gain the person's name instead of their social and mental dice pools be an acceptable substitution?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually throw that under Mental Scan, or <i>maybe</i> Correspondence's &quot;detailed context&quot; Reach effects. Or a Fate variation - fey steal true names, after all. Know Nature is a bit more about sensing your personality, which I could see being a good excuse to reveal the target's <i>Shadow</i> name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-19-2022, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T05:30:49-07:00","id":1490778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490741#post1490741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a Fate variation - fey steal true names, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The logic underlying how most other supernatural beings do their stuff is rarely ever an effective foundation for what might be done with Supernal magic.<br /> <br /> I'd need to check the wording of the spells again, but I think something as specific and discrete as a name doesn't constitute the surface level stuff or general composition of personality that the Knowing spells get at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T06:48:09-07:00","id":1490785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490735#post1490735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, its important to be careful as how you relinquish. Safe relinquishing costs a Willpower dot, which translates into a XP cost to buy it back.<br /> <br /> Unsafe relinquishing costs a Willpower point, but makes the spell mutate after a while. So you probably want to have someone with skill in dispellation end it before that happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notable DaveB mentioned how unsafely relinquished spells do not invoke the Abyss, they are just reusing (some of) the paradox rules. For example, 5 successes on a unsafely relinquished spell is an exceptional success, and ends the spell cancelling the remaining duration - whereas 5 reach on a paradox anomoly summons a rank 2 abyssal being.<br /> <br /> Changing the subject of the spell, Imposing a condition on the subject, or changing the reach effects, might be annoying. There are two things you can do to mitigate it. 1) reduce the size of the dice pool by avoiding overreaching, and 2) using the fate 2 conditional duration attainment with a specific condition so you can end the spell at your pleasure (or use Runes on the subject and break them to end the spell... Though i do wonder if that still works after the spell has changed subject...)<br /> <br /> Assuming of course you do not have Prime dispellation available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-20-2022, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T07:26:25-07:00","id":1490788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490785#post1490785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Notable DaveB mentioned how unsafely relinquished spells do not invoke the Abyss, they are just reusing (some of) the paradox rules. For example, 5 successes on a unsafely relinquished spell is an exceptional success, and ends the spell cancelling the remaining duration - whereas 5 reach on a paradox anomoly summons a rank 2 abyssal being.<br /> <br /> Changing the subject of the spell, Imposing a condition on the subject, or changing the reach effects, might be annoying. There are two things you can do to mitigate it. 1) reduce the size of the dice pool by avoiding overreaching, and 2) using the fate 2 conditional duration attainment with a specific condition so you can end the spell at your pleasure (or use Runes on the subject and break them to end the spell... Though i do wonder if that still works after the spell has changed subject...)<br /> <br /> Assuming of course you do not have Prime dispellation available.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's not Paradox, the word mutate was deliberately chosen over something like corrupted to reflect that.<br /> <br /> Runes are a decent option if you use UV paint to hide them and a blacklight flashlight to find them. <br /> <br /> Conditional duration is really interesting, depending on what kind of condition you choose. Relinquishing an enhanced gun with the condition of &quot;only I can touch it&quot; for a high duration bonus, which would account for why an Acanthus would be so bothered by lending their lucky gun and why they do all repairs and maintenance themselves. However, that adds a mana cost atop the Willpower one, which can be expensive early on a mage's career. <br /> <br /> Another option is to use <i>One Mind, Two Thoughts</i> to dedicate one thread into a concentration yantra. With enough Potency, the mage can concentrate on multiple spells while being free to do whatever. They all cease if they are hit, but still, it's a fairly easy way to end spells unsafely relinquished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-20-2022, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T08:14:45-07:00","id":1490793,"title":"","content":"Right, checked it, Mental Scan will work if you can lead a person towards thinking their own name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T10:44:03-07:00","id":1490805,"title":"","content":"Can Time Sight detect amortality ? By that I mean when the physical age of someone does not match their chronological age. Vampires are the classic example, being stuck in stasis, looking like whatever age they were Embraced on. But high Primal Urge werewolves and high Wyrd changelings also age slower than most. Certain uses of Life spells could also cause this as a side effect and Time mages that used <i>Veil of Moments</i> would have the differences accumulate as well. All of those would leave a distortion that was caused by supernatural means, would Time Sight register it as something being off about them ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T13:03:41-07:00","id":1490808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490805#post1490805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Time Sight detect amortality ? By that I mean when the physical age of someone does not match their chronological age. Vampires are the classic example, being stuck in stasis, looking like whatever age they were Embraced on. But high Primal Urge werewolves and high Wyrd changelings also age slower than most. Certain uses of Life spells could also cause this as a side effect and Time mages that used <i>Veil of Moments</i> would have the differences accumulate as well. All of those would leave a distortion that was caused by supernatural means, would Time Sight register it as something being off about them ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule that having Life and Tjme Sight up simultaneously would show that kind of information","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T13:25:50-07:00","id":1490809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490808#post1490808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rule that having Life and Tjme Sight up simultaneously would show that kind of information</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I was thinking either Time (altered age), Death (altered reaction to entropy) or Life (altered biological clock) could individually pick up the details as generically weird, with additional spells being necessary to uncover the cause. <br /> <br /> The biggest difference, in my mind, was that the closest Mage Sight would resonate unusually strongly to a matching cause. Like Life sight would pick up more distortions for a werewolf and Death sight for a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T14:06:21-07:00","id":1490812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490809#post1490809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting, I was thinking either Time (altered age), Death (altered reaction to entropy) or Life (altered biological clock) could individually pick up the details as generically weird, with additional spells being necessary to uncover the cause. <br /> <br /> The biggest difference, in my mind, was that the closest Mage Sight would resonate unusually strongly to a matching cause. Like Life sight would pick up more distortions for a werewolf and Death sight for a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life (and Death, for Vampires) would make sense for identifying the biological age of something. Time in its own wouldn't really have a reason to identify entities that are living longer than normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T15:09:15-07:00","id":1490813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490812#post1490812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Life (and Death, for Vampires) would make sense for identifying the biological age of something. Time in its own wouldn't really have a reason to identify entities that are living longer than normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was not just living longer, because Geist technically quality for that (although they continue to age normally from when they died). The idea was that something placed these entities in some kind of temporal stasis, distorting the aging process and that would ping. Aging is within its purview, since spells like Weight of Year harness it, although Death can utilize its entropic side much better.<br /> <br /> Its like one sight determines the body temperature is higher than normal, another that the immune system is in overdrive. Different lens to come to the conclusion that the patient has a fever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T15:42:34-07:00","id":1490815,"title":"","content":"But Time only senses somethings chronological age - it doesn't detect how old something &quot;should&quot; be. A temporal anomaly, like a timetraveler, has a gap in their temporal timeline that the Sight can detect. A Changeling that has high Wyrd is living longer because they're assimilating aspects of their Mein/Arcadia, a Vampire is &quot;living&quot; continuously because their death was denied to them.<br /> <br /> Now, you could use information gleaned from multiple Sights to come to the conclusion that their supernatural templates are what is giving them long life. But that's guesswork and assumption, as opposed to flat-out facts provided by Mage Sight<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, looking at the description of Time Sight in 2e Core, it doesn't even tell you age. So it <i>really</i> has no reason to ping on longevity that derives from aspects that fall under other Arcana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-20-2022, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T16:18:45-07:00","id":1490819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490815#post1490815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Time only senses somethings chronological age - it doesn't detect how old something &amp;quot;should&amp;quot; be. A temporal anomaly, like a timetraveler, has a gap in their temporal timeline that the Sight can detect. A Changeling that has high Wyrd is living longer because they're assimilating aspects of their Mein/Arcadia, a Vampire is &amp;quot;living&amp;quot; continuously because their death was denied to them.<br /> <br /> Now, you could use information gleaned from multiple Sights to come to the conclusion that their supernatural templates are what is giving them long life. But that's guesswork and assumption, as opposed to flat-out facts provided by Mage Sight<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, looking at the description of Time Sight in 2e Core, it doesn't even tell you age. So it <i>really</i> has no reason to ping on longevity that derives from aspects that fall under other Arcana</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, its very niche compared to the other sights. So I was thinking of the other things it could be used for. Since Mage Sight highlights all supernatural phenomena related to an Arcanum, I thought that could have been something a bit more common it could show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T02:59:33-07:00","id":1490860,"title":"","content":"Opinion question - in a speed-based Legacy, is it reasonable to break the &quot;no stacking stats&quot; rule by allowing Attainment-ized Accelerate and Velocity Control to stack? Or is that a bridge too far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T06:35:17-07:00","id":1490876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490860#post1490860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opinion question - in a speed-based Legacy, is it reasonable to break the &amp;quot;no stacking stats&amp;quot; rule by allowing Attainment-ized Accelerate and Velocity Control to stack? Or is that a bridge too far?</div> </div> </div> </div>How fast do you need to go? Temporal pocket type speeds? I think a co-locate type reflexively move in and out of the Temporal pocket (twice per turn) for +2 reach might be more than even a fifth attainment could achieve...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T06:46:18-07:00","id":1490877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490860#post1490860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opinion question - in a speed-based Legacy, is it reasonable to break the &quot;no stacking stats&quot; rule by allowing Attainment-ized Accelerate and Velocity Control to stack? Or is that a bridge too far?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it might be a bridge too far due to how this would interact with the transient stacking rules found on page 199. I think perhaps Teleportation would solve all speed challenges, Temporal Pocket is another (since you can move freely) and I believe clever use of a Patterning or Unmaking of Forces could also allow a mage to reach ludicrous speeds (I am not sure which forces to target though).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T08:15:19-07:00","id":1490884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490860#post1490860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is that a bridge too far?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speed based Legacies are for reaching the bridge regardless of distance. ^^<br /> <br /> I don't have enough experience with the Mage system to weight in on the effects specifically, but since Legacy are very rare, conventional wisdom is they can be the source of a rule exception. So if it is a high level Attainment, it should be fine. You could ask yourself what the primary effect is, and how difficult it would be for money to replicate. If you must go fast, and that is all, then how much to buy a jet-pack? The Attainment should be as roughly as rare. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T08:51:22-07:00","id":1490885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490884#post1490884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have enough experience with the Mage system to weight in on the effects specifically, but since Legacy are very rare, conventional wisdom is they can be the source of a rule exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legacies are incredibly common (most mages develop them, whether personally or through initiation into an established tradition) and their Attainments' explicit capacity for tweaking the rules is specifically advised not to make their abilities significantly more or less powerful than the spells they're built from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T09:59:05-07:00","id":1490890,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that most mages join them, but developing one from scratch is significantly rarer (more details on page 197 of the core book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T13:07:52-07:00","id":1490917,"title":"","content":"My intent was a Legacy that apes The Flash with Time and Forces. Got superheroes on the brain. I'll just figure out a new Adept of Forces optional Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T00:07:48-07:00","id":1490967,"title":"","content":"With ground eater (Space Compelling) add potency to speed, and Acceleration (Time Perfecting) multiply speed by potency. How would the stacking rules apply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T00:11:35-07:00","id":1490968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490967#post1490967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With ground eater (Space Compelling) add potency to speed, and Acceleration (Time Perfecting) multiply speed by potency. How would the stacking rules apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't stack, unfortunately, since they both increase Speed. Specifically, I'd rule that with equal Potency, Acceleration wins out for being the higher practice.<br /> <br /> Edit: unrelated questions <br /> <br /> 1. If you used a wide-Scale Display of Power around casting Mages, then filmed the imagos using Camera Obscura, could you create &quot;Bootleg Grimoires&quot;? That is, photos and video you could use to learn new spells from, not a full grimoire.<br /> <br /> If you <i>can</i>, I like to think it leads to a very high rate of Warped Rotes. Plus a lot of pissed off Order hardliners. Piracy\u2019s a crime kids, and crime doesn't pay.<br /> <br /> 2. Is Energize Object meant to be read as being able to make spell-bullets? 'Cause being able to make a bullet that causes an Earthquake at the point of impact is pretty metal.<br /> <br /> 3. Does Hidden Hoard hide the subject from the caster as well? I assume Incognito Presence and Supernal Veil does, and Invisibility <i>definitely</i> does, so the trend of Veiling would imply so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-22-2022, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T05:36:07-07:00","id":1490990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490968#post1490968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't stack, unfortunately, since they both increase Speed. Specifically, I'd rule that with equal Potency, Acceleration wins out for being the higher practice.<br /> <br /> Edit: unrelated questions <br /> <br /> 1. If you used a wide-Scale Display of Power around casting Mages, then filmed the imagos using Camera Obscura, could you create &quot;Bootleg Grimoires&quot;? That is, photos and video you could use to learn new spells from, not a full grimoire.<br /> <br /> If you <i>can</i>, I like to think it leads to a very high rate of Warped Rotes. Plus a lot of pissed off Order hardliners. Piracy\u2019s a crime kids, and crime doesn't pay.<br /> <br /> 2. Is Energize Object meant to be read as being able to make spell-bullets? 'Cause being able to make a bullet that causes an Earthquake at the point of impact is pretty metal.<br /> <br /> 3. Does Hidden Hoard hide the subject from the caster as well? I assume Incognito Presence and Supernal Veil does, and Invisibility <i>definitely</i> does, so the trend of Veiling would imply so.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- Not exactly, because the mage is casting an improvised spell. If you ask them what they did, they will probably say &quot;I just did the thing by [High Speech mantra description]&quot;. Developing a rote involves researching the Imago and how to encode it into a specific skill, streamlining and optimizing how you do it, which becomes a highly reliable recipe for other mages. A warped rote means either this process was done improperly, some of the execution details were lost, or something similar. Display of Power would give you a place to start, but by default an improvised spell does not encode mudras into its execution, because its just something quickly thrown together. <br /> <br /> 2- I believe so, which puts imbued bullets on the table. They would be a large time investment and require some retrieval method, so I think a combination of Energize Objective and Stored Spell would be quicker to mass produce.<br /> <br /> 3- Yep, but then again, if you have it under your control, you can choose to lose the Clash of Wills for detection or end the spell entirely, so its not the biggest deal breaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T12:02:51-07:00","id":1491017,"title":"","content":"Display of Power refers to a premise of creating images of imagos as visual aids, but the idea of &quot;learning spells&quot; doesn't seem as though it's particularly fraught in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T13:24:10-07:00","id":1491035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491017#post1491017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Display of Power refers to a premise of creating images of imagos as visual aids, but the idea of &amp;quot;learning spells&amp;quot; doesn't seem as though it's particularly fraught in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was probably leaning a bit more on the 1e fluff that the Orders don't share their rotes except under specific circumstances, and brook great umbrage at &quot;theives&quot;. Look at the Awakened Land Pentology's backstory!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490990#post1490990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Not exactly, because the mage is casting an improvised spell. If you ask them what they did, they will probably say &amp;quot;I just did the thing by [High Speech mantra description]&amp;quot;. Developing a rote involves researching the Imago and how to encode it into a specific skill, streamlining and optimizing how you do it, which becomes a highly reliable recipe for other mages. A warped rote means either this process was done improperly, some of the execution details were lost, or something similar. Display of Power would give you a place to start, but by default an improvised spell does not encode mudras into its execution, because its just something quickly thrown together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more thinking about using it when the other mages were using Rotes. The lack of somatic visibility is why i like the idea of it becoming a Warped Rote<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1490990#post1490990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- I believe so, which puts imbued bullets on the table. They would be a large time investment and require some retrieval method, so I think a combination of Energize Objective and Stored Spell would be quicker to mass produce.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could always cast Energize Object with high Scale, then unsafely relinquish it, then store other spells you unsafely relinquish. You'll need to use them up quickly, to avoid the issues of degradation, but you can mass-produce them or spam them on the fly. Especially if you have Mind or Life to recover your Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T14:12:26-07:00","id":1491041,"title":"","content":"Ah, now I see. In that case, perhaps you could if you had an audiovisual recording, but it would still require the mudra and imago to be used so you can evaluate them beyond a standard Imago. Not sure if it would create a Warped Rote or just a place for the research to start. I would be tempted to say yes, because then it could develop into a Legacy with a system similar to Oriana Thomson's Shorthand system from Index.<br /> <br /> What I am certain of is that stealing rotes like that would certainly lead to many Duels Arcane or invocations of the right of Nemesis, unless the mage is well connected enough to offer something in return. Expect the Mysterium to go out of their way to spite them and for it to be popular with Libertines proposing &quot;opensource&quot; magic. If they started stealing Seer rotes, it would be an issue, because you never know if one won't have just the right mudras to &quot;speed up&quot; the process of chosen apprentices having the Iron Door appear in their Oneiros, to gauge their potential. They would probably need a way to detect Befouled ones as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-22-2022, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T14:51:18-07:00","id":1491046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491041#post1491041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be tempted to say yes, because then it could develop into a Legacy</div> </div> </div> </div>Already got a skeleton of a camera crew Legacy based around it, recording Mysteries for posterity. Just having trouble with the Optional Attainments. Surpress Aura would be useful for avoiding contamination, but Spirit has more spells in line with the theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T00:44:39-07:00","id":1491084,"title":"","content":"Is Levitate supposed to be a direct upgrade to Telekinesis's ability to move objects with your mind, or is it just meant to be a way to make people fly? It reads like it can be used both ways, going off the Reach effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T04:30:18-07:00","id":1491085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491084#post1491084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Levitate supposed to be a direct upgrade to Telekinesis's ability to move objects with your mind, or is it just meant to be a way to make people fly? It reads like it can be used both ways, going off the Reach effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moving stuff via Levitation probably looks like trying to fly a balloon or a kite. As opposed to Telekinesis, which allows for fine control. So I wouldn\u2019t say it\u2019s a direct upgrade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T13:36:56-07:00","id":1491119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491035#post1491035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was probably leaning a bit more on the 1e fluff that the Orders don't share their rotes except under specific circumstances, and brook great umbrage at &quot;theives&quot;. Look at the Awakened Land Pentology's backstory!</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition talked up the significance of rotes being proprietary, but the mechanics didn't really bear that out.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, being able to limit access to rotes with their high value Yantras and lots of Reach (in addition to the old benefits of waived mana cost and not having your own nimbus apparent in them, with feel a bit different in the new context) is absolutely worthwhile.<br /> <br /> You can give any Initiate of Time a leg up in learning to divine the future, but there's something a lot more invested and worthwhile in being able to teach them the spell's rote.<br /> <br /> Like, for your newly Awakened person, their rotes are going to be the thing they're most comfortable casting where they get advanced factors without needing to spend several hours on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T20:48:15-07:00","id":1491271,"title":"","content":"Would it be reasonable to apply Web Weaver's Time 2 effect to Create Sympathy?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Add Time \u2022\u2022: The mage can employ Temporal Sympathy (p. 193) to bolster nonexistent connections to anything the subject touched in the target time.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Tangentially related in that it's Time magic, <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m unsure on one of the details of how Shifting Sands works. Could you grab an item and rewind it back a scene with you, thus having the item before you ever actually laid hands on it? It'd provide you a hassel-free exit strategy on smash-and-grabs, if so.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-25-2022, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T11:19:21-07:00","id":1491319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491271#post1491271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be reasonable to apply Web Weaver's Time 2 effect to Create Sympathy?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Add Time \u2022\u2022: The mage can employ Temporal Sympathy (p. 193) to bolster nonexistent connections to anything the subject touched in the target time.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really work because temporal sympathy isn't to separate things, but to points in the subject's history.<br /> <br /> You can use comparable magic to strengthen or weaken such a sympathy sure, and the initial description of it at the start of the Time Arcanum describes some of the consequences. But there's not really a comparable basis for creating a sympathy where there was none without Making magic.<br /> <br /> That being said, it's very unusual for a subject to have non-existent sympathy to some point in its own past without the intervention of magic in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially related in that it's Time magic, <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m unsure on one of the details of how Shifting Sands works. Could you grab an item and rewind it back a scene with you, thus having the item before you ever actually laid hands on it? It'd provide you a hassel-free exit strategy on smash-and-grabs, if so.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so we have to start with a resolution to the question of why a spell such as Shifting Sands works on things like a person's clothes when a spell is cast on them. I'm gonna say that in the symbol logic of the Supernal, things that qualify as one's personal effects all count together as part of the subject's identity. That can even extend as far as things like, say, a holstered gun. I think it does not extend as far as something that one is holding, if it can logically be understood to have a level of separation from them; a clipboard you're holding, for instance.<br /> <br /> So Shifting Sands is a Fraying spell; follow some of the logic of Corridors of Time, and you could see it in terms of functioning by undoing a few turns or scenes of the subject's timeline, in which it gets a bit of a do-over. That, I think entails putting it back in the position it was in its reset time. <br /> <br /> So if you pick a thing up and cast a spell to send both of you back through time, you'll both end up back where you were then.<br /> <br /> I think if you want to use Time magic in that sort of heist, you need to rely on the degree to which the subject retains modifications, and use those to try and set it up so that when it returns to its prior state, you've added something that will aid in its acquisition. <br /> <br /> But for the most part, Shifting Sands is a spell of getting to look at some event that you don't like and saying &quot;that didn't happen&quot;. For the most part; you have to stay stabbed, but you can at least remove the event of your stabbing and any further connotations it might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T11:33:50-07:00","id":1491321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491319#post1491319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But for the most part, Shifting Sands is a spell of getting to look at some event that you don't like and saying &amp;quot;that didn't happen&amp;quot;. For the most part; you have to stay stabbed, but you can at least remove the event of your stabbing and any further connotations it might have.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you can send damage back in time suggests you can use it to get someone bleeding to death, and then send them back to before you attacked them, and deny any involvement in their death (not so useful for a heist, unless you destroy the alarm system/defences, and send them back in time...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:08:29-07:00","id":1491361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491321#post1491321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that you can send damage back in time suggests you can use it to get someone bleeding to death, and then send them back to before you attacked them, and deny any involvement in their death (not so useful for a heist, unless you destroy the alarm system/defences, and send them back in time...)</div> </div> </div> </div>For Sleepers, maybe. It should be kept in mind that mages can perceive the traces of alterations to time. Like, if the Time Arcanum is in somebody's Active Mage Sight, there isn't even any roll needed for that stuff to be perceptible.<br /> <br /> There's also the matter of how changes made with Shifting Sands only become Lasting when it &quot;catches up&quot; to the present, which can provide a window for other magic in the present to counter it. And like... probably that kind of chicanery is something you'll want some distance in. Like, if you shoot somebody in the same room as you in the gut, then rewind time by nine seconds, your proximity is probably going to at least add you to the suspect pool, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T00:29:54-07:00","id":1491399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491361#post1491361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Sleepers, maybe. It should be kept in mind that mages can perceive the traces of alterations to time. Like, if the Time Arcanum is in somebody's Active Mage Sight, there isn't even any roll needed for that stuff to be perceptible.<br /> <br /> There's also the matter of how changes made with Shifting Sands only become Lasting when it &amp;quot;catches up&amp;quot; to the present, which can provide a window for other magic in the present to counter it. And like... probably that kind of chicanery is something you'll want some distance in. Like, if you shoot somebody in the same room as you in the gut, then rewind time by nine seconds, your proximity is probably going to at least add you to the suspect pool, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair.<br /> <br /> I was thinking for a smash and grab/heist, walking into a museum smash the container, then send it back to the start of the scene, and walk into the room the first time to see the specific artifcat you wanted to steal already sitting in a broken container (may be less useful as you a) still have to walk up and steal the item and b) it may set off alarms before you even arrive )<br /> <br /> Doing the same with a person, will they remember what has happened to them? Send them back for long enough to bleed out, right? Then you probably want to inclyyourself in the spell, so you can send them back an hour and not go near them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T01:17:34-07:00","id":1491402,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, if you have enough Mana you could play merry havoc with their security systems by systematically taking apart one section per Rewind. Each run gets progressively easier, and on the final iteration their entire system just collapses without you seeming to have acted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T17:24:08-07:00","id":1491447,"title":"","content":"Can you cast Soul Jar as a Conditional Duration-Hung Spell on someone('s soul) who is soon to die, and circumvent having to use Sever Soul on them?<br /> <br /> I'm asking as an attempt to figure out a somewhat ethical way to aquire souls, since you really shouldn't be making people who are already in their last days miserable. Find some old folks on who're at peace with passing, and offer them one wish within the bounds of your magic in exchange for getting their Soul upon death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-26-2022, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T19:08:24-07:00","id":1491448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491447#post1491447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cast Soul Jar as a Conditional Duration-Hung Spell on someone('s soul) who is soon to die, and circumvent having to use Sever Soul on them?<br /> <br /> I'm asking as an attempt to figure out a somewhat ethical way to aquure souls, since you really shouldn't be making people who are already in their last days miserable. Find some old folks on who're at peace with passing, and offer them one wish within the bounds of your magic in exchange for getting their Soul upon death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m doubtful, since Soul Jar works on \u2018displaced\u2019 ie already removed souls, and AFAIK natural death makes souls just pop out of existence without a middle step. In this case, the dubiously ethical guy would still be casting Sever Soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T22:06:13-07:00","id":1491454,"title":"","content":"Similar question - a human created by Create Life is a Sleeper, right? You can't (barring ST fiat) just magic up new Sleepwalkers whole cloth while circumventing Stealing Fire's downsides? A Prime 5 conjunctive effect would be neat -and need a 3rd degree Master to accomplish- but doesn't really jive with the rest of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T22:44:37-07:00","id":1491455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491454#post1491454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar question - a human created by Create Life is a Sleeper, right? You can't (barring ST fiat) just magic up new Sleepwalkers whole cloth while circumventing Stealing Fire's downsides? A Prime 5 conjunctive effect would be neat -and need a 3rd degree Master to accomplish- but doesn't really jive with the rest of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, being a Sleepwalker isn't consistently a quality that breeds true, the resulting human is still soulless and sustained by your spell control, and Mind 5 lets you create a mind that counts as a Sleepwalker for the purposes of ritual casting (i.e. it can assist you in such a way that it counts as an Environment Yantra).<br /> <br /> Every conceivable mechanical benefit to a created human being a Sleepwalker is balanced out by the fact that it's a the creation of a Master-level spell that requires another Mastery to be more than a meatsuit. Being able to get Sleepwalkers with a Medium connection to you to hold spells is counterbalanced by the fact that they are themselves spells you control that need to agree to hold the spells for you with some degree of informed consent, with all the usual complications doing so entails.<br /> <br /> It's arguably a bigger deal to be able to create Sleepers \u2014 that affects Paradox and Dissonance without involving Abyssal powers like the Nasnas, and your soulless magical creations presumably don't have the Abyssal shard an ordinary person would for the same reason that sticking a Sleeper soul into your Awakened Gnosis doesn't remove your ability to do magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T22:49:08-07:00","id":1491456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491455#post1491455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, being a Sleepwalker isn't consistently a quality that breeds true, the resulting human is still soulless and sustained by your spell control, and Mind 5 lets you create a mind that counts as a Sleepwalker for the purposes of ritual casting (i.e. it can assist you in such a way that it counts as an Environment Yantra).<br /> <br /> Every conceivable mechanical benefit to a created human being a Sleepwalker is balanced out by the fact that it's a the creation of a Master-level spell that requires another Mastery to be more than a meatsuit. Being able to get Sleepwalkers with a Medium connection to you to hold spells is counterbalanced by the fact that they are themselves spells you control that need to agree to hold the spells for you with some degree of informed consent, with all the usual complications doing so entails.<br /> <br /> It's arguably a bigger deal to be able to create Sleepers \u2014 that affects Paradox and Dissonance without involving Abyssal powers like the Nasnas, and your soulless magical creations presumably don't have the Abyssal shard an ordinary person would for the same reason that sticking a Sleeper soul into your Awakened Gnosis doesn't remove your ability to do magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your opinion then is that Create Life's Mind 5 conjunctive effect creates (souless, obviously) Sleepwalkers by default? Seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> Followup questions.<br /> <br /> 1. I assume you could fabricate up memories wholesale for a created human, much like how you're creating a base personality for them, correct? Likewise choose their skills?<br /> <br /> 2. Could you add in a Time conjunctive effect to spawn them with a false timeline? Not one that actually changes history, but one like Shield of Chronos' fabricated timeline Reach effect. If so, what degree of Time is a reasonable requirement? 2, since that's Shield of Chronos' level? 3, because the Fabricated timeline is a Reach effect? 4 or 5, because this is a bit of a hefty ask?<br /> <br /> Yes, there are a slew of ethical problems with this, if used to create a human who doesn't know they're created. Doubly so if they ever find out the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-27-2022, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T06:15:20-07:00","id":1491466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491456#post1491456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I assume you could fabricate up memories wholesale for a created human, much like how you're creating a base personality for them, correct? Likewise choose their skills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Following on from Mind spells to mess with these things, Skills might take additional Reach and interact with Potency, as might getting Social and Mental Attributes higher than 2 or 3, but otherwise, yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Could you add in a Time conjunctive effect to spawn them with a false timeline? Not one that actually changes history, but one like Shield of Chronos' fabricated timeline Reach effect. If so, what degree of Time is a reasonable requirement? 2, since that's Shield of Chronos' level? 3, because the Fabricated timeline is a Reach effect? 4 or 5, because this is a bit of a hefty ask? </div> </div> </div>For just making the person's history read the way you want them to, you could probably manage that with Time 2 and an extra Reach, because that's Shield of Chronos's level and it's a Reach effect that Life doesn't logically make easier (and because it's one more thing Paradox can bug out). More involved stuff will likely require higher Time ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T07:02:09-07:00","id":1491469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491466#post1491466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following on from Mind spells to mess with these things, Skills might take additional Reach and interact with Potency, as might getting Social and Mental Attributes higher than 2 or 3, but otherwise, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>My default assumption was that you either build a Create Life human using the Chronicles of Darkness character creation process as a template, or just grab one of the sample Antagonists out of CoD core. Reach seems like a good fit for adding more dots for them to start with, though I'm not sure how much each one would provide...<br /> <br /> Regardless, thanks for the answers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T00:42:28-07:00","id":1491561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491469#post1491469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My default assumption was that you either build a Create Life human using the Chronicles of Darkness character creation process as a template, or just grab one of the sample Antagonists out of CoD core. Reach seems like a good fit for adding more dots for them to start with, though I'm not sure how much each one would provide...<br /> <br /> Regardless, thanks for the answers</div> </div> </div> </div>You still have a soulless human. What you might be better off with is taking an animal (with a mind already) and weaving it with life+mind to give it human level intelligence, skills and shapeshift (life patterning) to give it a human body.<br /> <br /> Now it isn't a soulless human, it has a animal spirit. You can look at Creative thaumatergy for how to give it supernatural merits (which make it count as a Sleepwalker - but by default animals don't provoke Quiessence or Dissonance). But you have largely avoided requiring mastery, Death to steal any souls, and i dunno about time...<br /> <br /> You can also use +2 reach effect from transform life to pass these traits down to their offspring, spawning a line of creatures...<br /> <br /> There is some question as to whether they can be given Sleepwalker merits, like ritual savvy or Sleepwalker (which has a prerequisite of Integrity, as with no soul why would they have integrity - the measure of the soul's health)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-28-2022, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T00:53:46-07:00","id":1491562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491561#post1491561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You still have a soulless human. What you might be better off with is taking an animal (with a mind already) and weaving it with life+mind to give it human level intelligence, skills and shapeshift (life patterning) to give it a human body.<br /> <br /> Now it isn't a soulless human, it has a animal spirit. You can look at Creative thaumatergy for how to give it supernatural merits to give it supernatural merits (which make it count as a Sleepwalker - but by default animals don't provoke Quiessence or Dissonance). But you have largely avoided requiring mastery, Death to steal any souls, and i dunno about time...<br /> <br /> You can also use +2 reach effect from transform life to pass these traits down to their offspring, spawning a line of creatures...<br /> <br /> There is some question as to whether they can be given Sleepwalker merits, like ritual savvy or Sleepwalker (which has a prerequisite of Integrity, as with no soul why would they have integrity - the measure of the soul's health)...</div> </div> </div> </div>While the animal plan is definately a plausible way to create a minion, it's not THAT hard to get ahold of a soul. With Disciple of Death or two Imbued spells, all you have to do is go to hospice care or an old folks home, find someone who is on the brink of death and at peace with their passing, and offer them one wish in exchange for their soul upon death. You'll probably want to do a deep scan with mind magic and Soul Marks, to check for potential psychological issues, but that's pretty easy for our theoretical 2nd-degree Master. Heck, you aren't forcing them to live Soulless for more than a few minutes, and you paid for it fair and square, so it shouldn't ping too harshly on Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T01:27:18-07:00","id":1491567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491562#post1491562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the animal plan is definately a plausible way to create a minion, it's not THAT hard to get ahold of a soul. With Disciple of Death or two Imbued spells, all you have to do is go to hospice care or an old folks home, find someone who is on the brink of death and at peace with their passing, and offer them one wish in exchange for their soul upon death. You'll probably want to do a deep scan with mind magic and Soul Marks, to check for potential psychological issues, but that's pretty easy for our theoretical 2nd-degree Master. Heck, you aren't forcing them to live Soulless for more than a few minutes, and you paid for it fair and square, so it shouldn't ping too harshly on Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on what your end goal is... A line of human featured animals (only distinguished from human by having animal spirits instead of souls) would be interesting to find...might not be able to breed pure with humans. Werewolves might he confused... <br /> <br /> But yes, you should be able to wait until to moment of death, using a hanging sever soul combined with soul jar. Or just creative thaumatergy a Death spell explicitly designed to prevent to soul from moving on at the moment of death*... <br /> <br /> Might be Space conjunctional... Like Ban or involve Fate to veiling the fact that the soul's time to move on has come - though a ban might trigger a clash of wills with whatever causes souls to move on... Which may be Archmaster level auto-winning the CoW.<br /> <br /> *I am pretty sure there are examples of this kind of spell being discussed in Lichdom for mages casting on themselves. Planning to bind their soul to their ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-28-2022, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T01:38:44-07:00","id":1491568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491567#post1491567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on what your end goal is... A line of human featured animals (only distinguished from human by having animal spirits instead of souls) would be interesting to find...might not be able to breed pure with humans. Werewolves might he confused...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My main line of questioning had mostly to do with ethics. Assuming that most Created Humans are being made for assistants (or concubines, at the skeevy end), the question of awareness comes up. Should they know what they are from the get-go, which in a free-willed entity has the potential for great resentment? Sure, they might be grateful to exist and have a soul, but why should they be beholden to serve you? Should they then have a fake background, and risk it being exposed as false? That could trigger mental breakdowns and existential crisis, if not even greater resentment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491567#post1491567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, you should be able to wait until to moment of death, using a hanging sever soul combined with soul jar. Or just creative thaumatergy a Death spell explicitly designed to prevent to soul from moving on at the moment of death*... <br /> <br /> Might be Space conjunctional... Like Ban or involve Fate to veiling the fact that the soul's time to move on has come - though a ban might trigger a clash of wills with whatever causes souls to move on... Which may be Archmaster level auto-winning the CoW.<br /> <br /> *I am pretty sure there are examples of this kind of spell being discussed in Lichdom for mages casting on themselves. Planning to bind their soul to their ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hung Spell Sever the Soul with a Conditional Duration appropriate to whatever is killing the subject. &quot;Subject goes into cardiac arrest&quot; or &quot;subject enters a coma&quot; would probably be the most common. Shifting the Odds will probably help to find a willing donor anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-28-2022, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T02:45:11-07:00","id":1491571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491568#post1491568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My main line of questioning had mostly to do with ethics. Assuming that most Created Humans are being made for assistants (or concubines, at the skeevy end), the question of awareness comes up. Should they know what they are from the get-go, which in a free-willed entity has the potential for great resentment? Sure, theyre greatful to exist and have a soul, but why should they be beholden to serve you? Should they then have a fake background, and risk it being exposed as false? That could trigger mental breakdowns and existential crisis, if not even greater resentment.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was discussed in 1e core on creating minds (similar less word count used on it in 2e). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1e Psychic Genesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The consciousness dissolves when the spell expires. Unless the creation is specifically designed to accept the inevitability of its own dissolution without emotional trauma, a Wisdom degeneration roll may be required for the creator (unless he has Wisdom 2 or lower).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so it is only worrying about death/end of existence, but i think the principle is the same regardless. 2e is much briefer in its Psychic Genesis example spell.<br /> <br /> And as discussed, doesn't need a soul to act as a Sleepwalker helping with ritual spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hung Spell Sever the Soul with a Conditional Duration appropriate to whatever is killing the subject. &quot;Subject goes into cardiac arrest&quot; or &quot;subject enters a coma&quot; would probably be the most common. Shifting the Odds will probably help to find a willing donor anyway. </div> </div> </div>Still, i don't see the need for a soul, if you are making a Mind, it can be customised however you like, and doesn't need a soul, it is essentially a goetia, and can be given a possession manifestation if it needs a body... (I forget if that requires death/spirit, as goetia don't usually have manifestations). Alternatively you can gives it a body with Matter 4 (Golem), Prime 5 (Eidolon), Death 3(Quicken Corpse) or Life 5 (Create Life) - theoretically also Space 4? (Genius Loci), Fate? (Some kind of sentient destiny?), Time? (Thinking timeline), Spirit 5 already makes sentient spirits... Forces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-28-2022, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T03:04:14-07:00","id":1491573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491571#post1491571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as discussed, doesn't need a soul to act as a Sleepwalker helping with ritual spells.<br /> <br /> Still, i don't see the need for a soul, if you are making a Mind, it can be customised however you like, and doesn't need a soul, it is essentially a goetia, and can be given a possession manifestation if it needs a body... (I forget if that requires death/spirit, as goetia don't usually have manifestations). Alternatively you can gives it a body with Matter 4 (Golem), Prime 5 (Eidolon), Death 3(Quicken Corpse) or Life 5 (Create Life) - theoretically also Space 4? (Genius Loci), Fate? (Some kind of sentient destiny?), Time? (Thinking timeline), Spirit 5 already makes sentient spirits... Forces?</div> </div> </div> </div>So the problem with Golem, Eidolon (sans Forces conjunctive effect), and most Quickened Corpses (sans Corpse Mask) is that they trigger Dissonance. A Create Life body is the only one you can bring around in normal society. Plus, Eidolon would take up a <i>ridiculous </i> amount of Mana to keep fueled, as we've discussed on this thread before. And zombies are <i>not</i> hygienic, and will likely rot before long without ANOTHER spell to preserve them like Veil of Moments.<br /> <br /> Bind Spirit can give Goetia Manifestation Conditions, but that requires Spirit 4 + Mind 4. Goetic Summons with Spirit or Death 2 can allow the summoned Goetia to Materialize for the duration. Depending on the Goetia you might be able to get away with Mortal Mask for having it walk around with you, but it's still more prone to tripping Dissonance than the created Sleepwalker. Which just means wasted effort, and possibly the death of your friend.<br /> <br /> You could also use Astral Grimoire's Lasting Reach effects to create a Dissonance-immune Goetia, although that risks the normal problems of losing a piece of your mind whenever you summon it out. If you scribe it into the Tenemos or Anima Mundi, then you risk those sentient wounds in the Astral whenever you summon it.<br /> <br /> If you allow the hypothetical Goetia to possess the Create Life body, you have several more issues than just creating a straight Sleepwalker. The Sleepwalker only has one spell to maintain/relinquish, which you could also just offload onto them as a banner-bearer. Whereas the Goetia has at least three (Psychic Genesis, Create Life, Bind Spirit, plus probably Bind Familiar), which they can't carry for you. The Goetia's meat-puppet is also a feral wreck when it isn't being Possessed, which means it can't really be left unattended. You could have a rotating roster of Goetia keeping the body docile, but each one is another two to three spells to maintain or relinquish.<br /> <br /> A sentient destiny or thinking timeline just sounds like Ananke, which are firmly in the wheelhouse of Archmages. A neat idea, but just a bit too far off the esoteric side of things for a baseline mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-28-2022, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T04:11:21-07:00","id":1491579,"title":"","content":"One conjunctional spell (create life + mind 5) is good, but requires double mastery (Gnosis 6?).<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting + a ghost who consents and has possession, or is forced into the manifestation condition Revenant, requires Life 4 + Death 4 (a much more reasonable Gnosis 4) - also, don't need a mentor to learn death/life 4 (unless you are an Obrimos).<br /> <br /> Can do it as one combined spell, and hand it off to the ghost, i think. Shouldn't provoke Dissonance, but if it does you end up with a seperated animal and ghost rather than destroying either.<br /> <br /> (I had a question, but have forgotten it...)<br /> <br /> Simpler still, you can use shifting the odds to gain the use of a retainer. &quot;Increasing a Merit is typically a Ruling (\u2022\u2022) spell.&quot; And &quot;Trait dots granted by magic last only as long as the spell\u2019s Duration&quot;<br /> <br /> Much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-28-2022, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T12:58:42-07:00","id":1491638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491579#post1491579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifting + a ghost who consents and has possession, or is forced into the manifestation condition Revenant, requires Life 4 + Death 4 (a much more reasonable Gnosis 4) - also, don't need a mentor to learn death/life 4 (unless you are an Obrimos).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mastigos Pure Sovereign is what I'd normally play, which would be going for Mind 5 / Life 5 anyway. The Gnosis is a factor, sure, but not a huge one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491579#post1491579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can do it as one combined spell, and hand it off to the ghost, i think. Shouldn't provoke Dissonance, but if it does you end up with a seperated animal and ghost rather than destroying either.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm fairly certain Ghosts can't hold spells for you. They aren't Sleepwalkers. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491579#post1491579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simpler still, you can use shifting the odds to gain the use of a retainer. &quot;Increasing a Merit is typically a Ruling (\u2022\u2022) spell.&quot; And &quot;Trait dots granted by magic last only as long as the spell\u2019s Duration&quot;<br /> <br /> Much easier.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, but who knows where they've been? They could be a Lucid, or a Seer pawn. Much safer to just make your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-28-2022, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T04:08:17-07:00","id":1491736,"title":"","content":"What's the differentiating point between a combined spells and conjunctive effects? For example, is there anything stopping you from adding a Prime 2 conjunctive effect to a given spell that obfuscates it \u00e1la Supernal Veil?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T04:21:37-07:00","id":1491741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491638#post1491638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm fairly certain Ghosts can't hold spells for you. They aren't Sleepwalkers. </div> </div> </div> </div>That raises an interesting question. Can you give a ghost the Sleepwalker merit (for the purpose of holding spells/required pre-requisites for other Sleepwalker merits).<br /> <br /> The pre-req for Sleepwalker is Integrity, which ghosts do have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T04:25:37-07:00","id":1491742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491736#post1491736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the differentiating point between a combined spells and conjunctive effects? For example, is there anything stopping you from adding a Prime 2 conjunctive effect to a given spell that obfuscates it \u00e1la Supernal Veil?</div> </div> </div> </div>Conjunctional spells are one effect, combined spells are two effect with one spell control slot.<br /> <br /> So making Life with conjunctional Mind 5 lets you make one thing (which happens to have a mind and a body). Or Word of Command is one effect (activating a magical object) with optional conjunctional Arcana for different types of magical item.<br /> <br /> I think all the conjunctional examples follow this pattern... It is like how the reach effect are still doing the one effect but modified or extended in some way. It is still one spell doing one effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T04:47:48-07:00","id":1491744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491741#post1491741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That raises an interesting question. Can you give a ghost the Sleepwalker merit (for the purpose of holding spells/required pre-requisites for other Sleepwalker merits).<br /> <br /> The pre-req for Sleepwalker is Integrity, which ghosts do have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain you need a soul to shoulder part of the metaphysical burden, even if having a soul isn't a requirement for being a Sleepwalker. But that's just my opinion, nothing I've read supports or detracts from the theory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491742#post1491742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Conjunctional spells are one effect, combined spells are two effect with one spell control slot.<br /> <br /> So making Life with conjunctional Mind 5 lets you make one thing (which happens to have a mind and a body). Or Word of Command is one effect (activating a magical object) with optional conjunctional Arcana for different types of magical item.<br /> <br /> I think all the conjunctional examples follow this pattern... It is like how the reach effect are still doing the one effect but modified or extended in some way. It is still one spell doing one effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, the effect should make sense to be conjunctive. But, for example, using Create Life to create &quot;a normal example of this species&quot; doesn't seem too out of line to attach a veiling effect to. Now it's a normal example of the species, even under all but the most thorough of mage sights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-29-2022, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T06:44:44-07:00","id":1491754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491744#post1491744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fairly certain you need a soul to shoulder part of the metaphysical burden, even if having a soul isn't a requirement for being a Sleepwalker. But that's just my opinion, nothing I've read supports or detracts from the theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting point.<br /> <br /> The requirement could be seen as even more restrictive. Having integrity means you have a soul AND you don't have other supernatural modifiers which change the soul (it is a measure of the health of the soul). So it may be an oddity that ghosts maintain the integrity they had at the point of death...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Agreed, the effect should make sense to be conjunctive. But, for example, using Create Life to create &quot;a normal example of this species&quot; doesn't seem too out of line to attach a veiling effect to. Now it's a normal example of the species, even under all but the most thorough of mage sights. </div> </div> </div>I think that is explicitly a second effect. You are creating a normal example of the species, and creating an effect to disguise the spell. <br /> <br /> Now if you don't use supernal magic then you can create an example of the species without needing a veiling. Which i think it what happens when you get lasting effects by passing down traits to the next generation (with either weaving or making). <br /> <br /> Or you could use a legacy attainment, or other supernatural effect... I was thinking Demon spoofing works to automatically to prevent detection. Or Changeling has some similar effects (turning into hedgebeasts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-29-2022, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T10:27:41-07:00","id":1491781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491741#post1491741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That raises an interesting question. Can you give a ghost the Sleepwalker merit (for the purpose of holding spells/required pre-requisites for other Sleepwalker merits).<br /> <br /> The pre-req for Sleepwalker is Integrity, which ghosts do have.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merit's phrasing of &quot;this is not necessary for a character with another supernatural template&quot; does seem to be predicated on the assumption that such things might experience Dissonance or contribute to Paradox without it, but I think it can be taken as a given that other supernatural beings are not Sleepwalkers by definition. <br /> <br /> I'd also think that some of the metaphysical basis for Sleepwalker shield bearers comes off as emerging from something communal between humans, and while Second Edition games do seem to have largely adopted the stance that ghosts are still possessed of a meaningful personhood, I think they still don't qualify as human like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> But, for example, using Create Life to create &quot;a normal example of this species&quot; doesn't seem too out of line to attach a veiling effect to. Now it's a normal example of the species, even under all but the most thorough of mage sights.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I find a bit of a particular kind of intersection here. On the one hand, I think that any form of Making magic will create the most genuine form of its target that you could imagine, all on its own. Anything you could use to analyse it would conclude that.<br /> <br /> The problem with a mage looking at them with Sight is going to be that they're going to be looking at what in all ways seems to be a genuine animal that is also lit up with a spell. Active Mage Sight of the correct Arcana does not even need to roll to perceive active spells. The spell is the subject of a Prime Veiling, not the substance of what it creates.<br /> <br /> So it's a subject of an entirely separate effect to conceal. Prime is unnecessary to add that depth to its reality, and doing so anyway would not help the fact that it's painted with a visible spell unless explicitly Veiled.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T18:22:29-07:00","id":1491847,"title":"","content":"A mage has a Medium Sympathetic Connection to their spells.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is that <i>all</i> of their spells, or just the ones they've got under their Spell Control?<ul><li>Would the connection to ones that have been relinquished fade out slowly, like a standard connection, or are they immediately cut? It might depend on the relinquishment method, I suppose - <u>Broken Relinquishment</u> or <u>Sacrificial Relinquishment</u> could have a very different effect than cutting of a bleeding chunk of your own selfhood to maintain a spell.</li> </ul></li> <li>Could you use <u>Cut Threads</u> to sever your sympathetic connection to an unrelinquished spell, and if so does it have any impact on the spell's functioning?<ul><li>If you <i>can</i> sever the connection, is the severance temporary? I could see the connection forcably reestablishing itself on a regular basis, such as every ritual interval.</li> </ul></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T18:58:15-07:00","id":1491851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1491847#post1491847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage has a Medium Sympathetic Connection to their spells<br /> Is that <i>all</i> of their spells, or just the ones they've got under their Spell Control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that it's a product of your Gnosis whether you retain control of it or not, I would say it's all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T02:03:28-07:00","id":1491881,"title":"","content":"I would say your connection does get weaker after they are relinquished. But if you cut the threads your control is fine, and it will grow back over time...<br /> <br /> Same with any other connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T18:59:00-07:00","id":1492059,"title":"","content":"Should a Forces master create an environmental effect of radiation and a target be afflicted with Radiation Sickness due to exposure, does the condition end when the spell does ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T23:34:54-07:00","id":1492075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492059#post1492059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a Forces master create an environmental effect of radiation and a target be afflicted with Radiation Sickness due to exposure, does the condition end when the spell does ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T23:07:06-07:00","id":1492136,"title":"","content":"Is there a Goetic equivelant to Magath? Or are they different enough as a &quot;species&quot; that they don't run into the same hazards of diet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T00:15:36-07:00","id":1492138,"title":"","content":"A Goetic Magath would be most unusual. Unlike the Shadow, The Astral is not an ecosystem. Its denizens are built around enacting their roles, rather than eating or being eaten. The closest I could think of to a Magath is a Goetia of an incoherent idea - a mass delusion, maybe muddled thoughts. There's also an option of fusing two Goetia artificially, but Magic can always break the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T00:25:42-07:00","id":1492140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492138#post1492138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Goetic Magath would be most unusual. Unlike the Shadow, The Astral is not an ecosystem. Its denizens are built around enacting their roles, rather than eating or being eaten. The closest I could think of to a Magath is a Goetia of an incoherent idea - a mass delusion, maybe muddled thoughts. There's also an option of fusing two Goetia artificially, but Magic can always break the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but Goetia can be brought into Twilight, or created whole cloth. There's probably a few who were bound as Familiars, but their contractor died, leaving them roaming around too. It would be strange to see them form in the Astral, but being outside the Astral is unusual circumstances already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T01:17:04-07:00","id":1492143,"title":"","content":"Goetia are odd. When people stop believing in a god, the Temenotic representation of that god sticks around, right? It may not get as much essence from folks thinking about it... But when people start believing in a slightly different version of the same god, usually it creates a new goetia or modifies the old one? Mutating the goetia by merging two ideas shouldn't produce a Magath-like entity because those ideas will usually be coherent enough.<br /> <br /> So what teatime said. You could probably try to mundanely create something by influencing a large number of people...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T02:58:30-07:00","id":1492148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492140#post1492140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but Goetia can be brought into Twilight, or created whole cloth. There's probably a few who were bound as Familiars, but their contractor died, leaving them roaming around too. It would be strange to see them form in the Astral, but being outside the Astral is unusual circumstances already.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're in a different frequency of Twilight than spirits, so they're not going to get eaten under most circumstances. Even if Goetia steal Essence from one another, they're not working under the logic of consumption and refinement that spirits are.<br /> <br /> And probably most importantly, you don't get a magath just from a spirit consuming another that is incompatible once, it has to be a frequent enough part of the diet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T23:34:08-07:00","id":1492202,"title":"","content":"Am I right in assuming that Machine Invisibility would make it impossible to use a smartphone? Or, indeed, any form of tech, since the rely on your pressure for input? Or is it just supposed to be recording equipment that is blinded to your existence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T00:47:17-07:00","id":1492203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492202#post1492202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right in assuming that Machine Invisibility would make it impossible to use a smartphone? Or, indeed, any form of tech, since the rely on your pressure for input? Or is it just supposed to be recording equipment that is blinded to your existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the imago. I would assume you could cast a version where you can push buttons and operate switches (like a light switch) but not operate a finger print lock (because it hides anything which would identify you). <br /> <br /> Or you could use a stylish to poke buttons...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T03:46:58-07:00","id":1492209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492202#post1492202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right in assuming that Machine Invisibility would make it impossible to use a smartphone? Or, indeed, any form of tech, since the rely on your pressure for input? Or is it just supposed to be recording equipment that is blinded to your existence?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't phrase it as limited to recording, saying that it functions against all inert matter is pretty broad. I think a touch screen would make sense as working along the same lines of recognition, but something with analogue functions doesn't seem like it would matter","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T02:45:43-07:00","id":1492271,"title":"","content":"Would an animated drawing be a Golem? That is, what Arcana would you use to create a 2D entity that can move similar to a Mage using Shadow Flesh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T02:59:24-07:00","id":1492276,"title":"","content":"Create a golem (Matter 4 Patterning), and transform it into a Shadow (Death 4 Patterning), maybe do it as a combined spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T03:53:21-07:00","id":1492284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492271#post1492271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would an animated drawing be a Golem? That is, what Arcana would you use to create a 2D entity that can move similar to a Mage using Shadow Flesh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter for moving ink/paint. Forces for moving light/colors/pixels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T11:16:53-07:00","id":1492536,"title":"","content":"When a Mage uses scrutiny to reduce the opacity of a Mystery, does that reduce it for all mages or just himself? If it reduces opacity for all mages, why could Mages not just take turns doing a bit at a time(aside from competitiveness of course) so they didn't flood the mystery with their own Nimbus? And if that's the case, why do any Mysteries have difficulty at all to Mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T11:33:56-07:00","id":1492541,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it is personal, but flooding it with mana messed up the Opacity for everyone (like flooding a car engine with petrol... Is that still a thing?). You may understand a mystery, but others will lack the insight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T17:15:57-07:00","id":1492564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris_John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492536#post1492536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Mage uses scrutiny to reduce the opacity of a Mystery, does that reduce it for all mages or just himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly the latter, per the last bullet point in the &quot;Opacity&quot; subheader of &quot;Building a Mystery&quot; on page 93-94 of Mage 2e Core.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T05:00:58-07:00","id":1492587,"title":"","content":"The primary Arcana of a Legacy is straightforward. For the Optional Attainments, is the assumption supposed to be that they come from one Arcana? That is, would it be kosher to have the first two Optional Attainments be Life and the subsequent ones be Space?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T11:56:31-07:00","id":1492616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492587#post1492587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary Arcana of a Legacy is straightforward. For the Optional Attainments, is the assumption supposed to be that they come from one Arcana? That is, would it be kosher to have the first two Optional Attainments be Life and the subsequent ones be Space?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Single optional Arcanum is typical, but there have been occasions where it has varied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T11:57:34-07:00","id":1492617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492587#post1492587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary Arcana of a Legacy is straightforward. For the Optional Attainments, is the assumption supposed to be that they come from one Arcana? That is, would it be kosher to have the first two Optional Attainments be Life and the subsequent ones be Space?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In 1ed there were time where a third Arcanum was needed in some amount to unlock certain extra functionality of the optional Attainment, one or two dots was the most common. But the general rule is that the optional Arcanum is a Ruling one of the parent Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T15:32:21-07:00","id":1492716,"title":"","content":"Purge Illness mentions the severity of illnesses, but I can't spot where in Core or CoD Core severity is actually discussed. The disease section just mentions &quot;This roll is not contested but it is modified by the severity of the disease. Only one success is necessary to avoid damage each time.&quot; <br /> <br /> The Contagion spell mentions Severity as being equal to the Potency of that spell, but that doesn't really help all that much. <br /> <br /> Is there a section I missed somewhere giving a rough approximation for what severity real-world illnesses are, or is it meant to be up to the ST?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T16:06:38-07:00","id":1492719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492716#post1492716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Purge Illness mentions the severity of illnesses, but I can't spot where in Core or CoD Core severity is actually discussed. The disease section just mentions &quot;This roll is not contested but it is modified by the severity of the disease. Only one success is necessary to avoid damage each time.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Contagion spell mentions Severity as being equal to the Potency of that spell, but that doesn't really help all that much.<br /> <br /> Is there a section I missed somewhere giving a rough approximation for what severity real-world illnesses are, or is it meant to be up to the ST?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Overdose section in Mage 2e core has severity samples for diseases <i>and</i> drugs <i>and</i> poisons. Wish they would've used a table instead, like many other sample parameters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T16:45:25-07:00","id":1492723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492719#post1492719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Overdose section in Mage 2e core has severity samples for diseases <i>and</i> drugs <i>and</i> poisons. Wish they would've used a table instead, like many other sample parameters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks! <br /> <br /> I'm amused that there's no disease listed between &quot;common cold&quot; and &quot;cancer &quot;. It's not a problem, but it is funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T23:34:14-07:00","id":1492785,"title":"","content":"If you target multiple subjects with a long-term spell, are those instances dispelled singularly or as a whole?<br /> <br /> For example, say you animated twenty Golems with one spell. Would targeting one of those golems with Dispel Magic shut down that one golem, or would it cancel all twenty? Technically they're being animated by the same imago, but stuff like Withstand is calculated separately in the case of multi-target spells.<br /> <br /> Edit: Alas, my poor Golem army.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-11-2022, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T00:30:48-07:00","id":1492789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492785#post1492785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you target multiple subjects with a long-term spell, are those instances dispelled singularly or as a whole?<br /> <br /> For example, say you animated twenty Golems with one spell. Would targeting one of those golems with Dispel Magic shut down that one golem, or would it cancel all twenty? Technically they're being animated by the same imago, but stuff like Withstand is calculated separately in the case of multi-target spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Add Fate \u2022 option allows for selective targeting, doesn\u2019t it? So, as a whole by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T01:20:14-07:00","id":1492791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492789#post1492789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Add Fate \u2022 option allows for selective targeting, doesn\u2019t it? So, as a whole by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is only one spell to target, not multiple subjects? So yeah, cast the spells multiple times if you want to have multiple spells (at the cost of spell control).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T09:51:12-07:00","id":1492990,"title":"","content":"Should an AoE <i>Temporal Summoning</i> be used to return the area around a house to the state it was that morning, would it also place the area under sunlight (provided it had been a sunny day) ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T10:06:19-07:00","id":1492992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492990#post1492990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should an AoE <i>Temporal Summoning</i> be used to return the area around a house to the state it was that morning, would it also place the area under sunlight (provided it had been a sunny day) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...<br /> <br /> My first impulse was to think that it wouldn't, but I can't really think of a consistent reason as to why, the notion of being that kind of bubble of restored time really seems to lend itself to capturing the full picture, and it probably works out as more interesting if it does.<br /> <br /> If added light levels, or similar environmental features, were undesirable, there's always the option to use Warding Gesture to exclude it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T11:09:02-07:00","id":1493001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492992#post1492992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm...<br /> <br /> My first impulse was to think that it wouldn't, but I can't really think of a consistent reason as to why, the notion of being that kind of bubble of restored time really seems to lend itself to capturing the full picture, and it probably works out as more interesting if it does.<br /> <br /> If added light levels, or similar environmental features, were undesirable, there's always the option to use Warding Gesture to exclude it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thank you. I thought it could make for a terrifying statement to see an Acanthus create a bubble of sunlight around vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T11:48:52-07:00","id":1493012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1492990#post1492990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should an AoE <i>Temporal Summoning</i> be used to return the area around a house to the state it was that morning, would it also place the area under sunlight (provided it had been a sunny day) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no. The Sun is not included in the AoE and light you brought from the past will take mircoseconds to disperse... Symbolically you are bringing things from the past to the present, and in the present there is no sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T12:05:00-07:00","id":1493013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493012#post1493012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say no. The Sun is not included in the AoE and light you brought from the past will take mircoseconds to disperse... Symbolically you are bringing things from the past to the present, and in the present there is no sunlight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that is more of a scientific explanation rather than a symbolic one. There was sunlight in the area, in the same way that the area could have a rock concert stage until that morning. Since you are targeting the area as it existed back then, rather than any individual item, it would summon everything. In the same way that a flame could be summoned if it was within the area, even if the flamethrower that created it was not within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T13:23:08-07:00","id":1493020,"title":"","content":"I'd say there's sunlight... for the few seconds it takes for that light to dissipate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T18:07:35-07:00","id":1493034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493020#post1493020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say there's sunlight... for the few seconds it takes for that light to dissipate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is the spell's duration being applied selectively?<br /> <br /> Like, we're talking about a spell that can convert a derelict building back into its form from years ago. I don't see why it's out of place for it to maintain ambient light levels as they were during that time within its boundaries. <br /> <br /> A 1 dot Forces spell will do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T18:39:17-07:00","id":1493037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493034#post1493034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the spell's duration being applied selectively?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is the spell's <i>effect</i> being applied selectively?<br /> <br /> If you restore a damaged chair to the state it was in before it was broken, that chair does not become indestructible. If you revert the air around you to the state it was in when sunlight was shining through it, you have air that had sunlight shining through it at that point and no source of further sunlight.<br /> <br /> The spell <i>restores targets to the state they were in at the time.</i> It does not create an open portal from the past like a Time version of Co-Location. You can put ancient ruins back in their pre-collapse state, but you can't use Temporal Summoning to locally change the time of day any more than you can use it to resurrect the dead. The thing you pull forward exists in the present under the conditions of the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T20:16:02-07:00","id":1493042,"title":"","content":"Exactly. I was implying that Temporal Summons on an <i>area</i> pulls everything from that point in time with it -although that might get finiky with living creatures and the like- so that summoning would be accompanied by a flash of daylight that rapidly disipates as its nominal source is suddenly an epoch distant. Time is still flowing normaly for the summoned object, it just had a bunch of interveining years cut out.<br /> <br /> Just my personal ruling though - I can completely understand arguments against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T23:06:31-07:00","id":1493045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493037#post1493037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you restore a damaged chair to the state it was in before it was broken, that chair does not become indestructible. If you revert the air around you to the state it was in when sunlight was shining through it, you have air that had sunlight shining through it at that point and no source of further sunlight.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm torn between the idea of the light as a substance within the area, captured in transit and streaming away, or a feature of the area during the moment being reclaimed.<br /> <br /> Spells interacting with something like spectrum radiation seem to differ a bit on whether the target is the source or the substance. If the latter, I'd feel as though the spell compensates for lack of source in terms of fidelity to the period being reclaimed.<br /> <br /> Really, it's like how any area of effect spell is supposed to apply its effect as suitable as things enter the zone, and fall away as they exit it... which I think may be a general point about how those spells work on which you disagree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T05:18:55-07:00","id":1493107,"title":"","content":"Leaving aside <i>why</i> you'd want to make one in the first place, I have a question regarding the theoretical spell &quot;Create Living Daimonomikon/Grimoire&quot;. It would combine Create Life and Living Grimoire, generating a new living entity wholesale that houses spells (or a Legacy). Would it be reasonable to have this entiry circumvent the normal Condition imposed on a Living Grimoire, since they are, by definition, not &quot;born of the Lie&quot;?<br /> <br /> No skin off my nose either way, just an odd thought that came up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T14:14:20-07:00","id":1493132,"title":"","content":"Honestly, doesn't seem like a bad work around, since you are combining a spell, and have to take that into account when forming the Imago. I'd allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 09-15-2022, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T17:31:26-07:00","id":1493136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493107#post1493107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be reasonable to have this entiry circumvent the normal Condition imposed on a Living Grimoire, since they are, by definition, not &quot;born of the Lie&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that I'm reasonably certain that line is just poetic texture on &quot;is a Phenomenal creation and not a perfect Supernal ideal,&quot; I would say no. You could stack on another spell to mitigate the difficulty of whatever spells the creature was laboring under as a consequence, but the drawback is there because living Patterns aren't made to hold Supernal knowledge in that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-15-2022, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T19:05:20-07:00","id":1493140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493136#post1493136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that I'm reasonably certain that line is just poetic texture on &quot;is a Phenomenal creation and not a perfect Supernal ideal,&quot; I would say no. You could stack on another spell to mitigate the difficulty of whatever spells the creature was laboring under as a consequence, but the drawback is there because living Patterns aren't made to hold Supernal knowledge in that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, it's mostly a poetic flourish, but my internal logic was that crafting the creature specifically to contain spells <i>might</i> circumvent it. Makes just as much sense if they're still affected by the condition though, so other workarounds are indeed likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-17-2022, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T12:24:06-07:00","id":1493177,"title":"","content":"Does <i>Velocity Control</i> need to target the source of the collision to reduce it's damage by Potency or does it grant that effect merely by being on a subject that was sped up ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T13:28:32-07:00","id":1493181,"title":"","content":"This is probably is one of those areas that depends on how closely you stick to real world physics. Irl, there really isn\u2019t a \u201csource\u201d of a collision, from both object\u2019s perspective the other is the one moving. Meaning you could cast on either, and enjoy the increased/reduced damage. But Forces doesn\u2019t have to work like that, especially if you are working from the Mage\u2019s perspective as a universal reference frame. In which case, whichever object is moving from the perspective of the mage is the one to target. The wording of the text potentially backs up the second interpretation by saying projectile, which implies motion of one particular object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T18:28:30-07:00","id":1493189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493177#post1493177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does <i>Velocity Control</i> need to target the source of the collision to reduce it's damage by Potency or does it grant that effect merely by being on a subject that was sped up ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Collision damage is based on the Speed or Speeds of the colliding subjects/objects. You reduce the damage <i>by</i> reducing the subject's Speed, which is a separate thing from directly reducing ranged attack damage by Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T19:13:10-07:00","id":1493191,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, I was thinking too much with a physics train of thought rather than symbolic. Do the effects of <i>The Outward &amp; Inward Eye</i> stack with <i>Zoom In</i> ? Since one expands the field of vision and the other the distance you can see, would using both with the mile wide sight effect allow the mage to see everything for miles &quot;on a plane&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T23:31:45-07:00","id":1493201,"title":"","content":"Hello, I'm new to Mage the Awakening and had a small question about experience point costs. <br /> <br /> Do rotes cost 1 exp per dot / level in the rote or 1 exp per rote? <br /> <br /> As an example would it cost a Mage 1 exp or 3 exp to purchase the Fate 3 rote Monkey's Paw?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T23:53:29-07:00","id":1493203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatOneKiasyd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493201#post1493201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I'm new to Mage the Awakening and had a small question about experience point costs. <br /> <br /> Do rotes cost 1 exp per dot / level in the rote or 1 exp per rote? <br /> <br /> As an example would it cost a Mage 1 exp or 3 exp to purchase the Fate 3 rote Monkey's Paw?</div> </div> </div> </div>A flat 1. Cheap. Though she still needs Fate 3 herself, so it\u2019s not too cheap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T22:18:03-07:00","id":1493229,"title":"","content":"Are VASCU agents from Hunter still human enough to Awaken? I assume so, but they're leaning closer to Deviants in their creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Would it be reasonable to tack on a Reach effect to Psychic Projection that makes you visible on the material plane, ala the Illusive Man's hologram avatar? Similarly, a Space Conjunctive effect to manifest the Projection at a target location?<br /> Edit: Forces 2 Conjunctive ala Soul Windows it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-18-2022, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T23:07:43-07:00","id":1493230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493229#post1493229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are VASCU agents from Hunter still human enough to Awaken? I assume so, but they're leaning closer to Deviants in their creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because they have Integrity and are not corrupted by an external force like ghouls or stigmatics. Not everyone who gets supernatural powers from procedures carried out by mortals is a Deviant; having the B-splats of all the other gamelines retroactively be Remade was specifically stated to not be a design goal during Deviant's open development.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it be reasonable to tack on a Reach effect to Psychic Projection that makes you visible on the material plane, ala the Illusive Man's hologram avatar? </div> </div> </div>That would be either a conjunctive effect with another Arcanum or a separate spell, because &quot;making stuff visible outside of an observer's subjective frame of reference&quot; isn't within Mind's purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-18-2022, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T00:13:47-07:00","id":1493232,"title":"","content":"Ah, I didn't mean they <i>were</i> Deviants, just that their creation sounds like the place a Deviant could potentially occur.<br /> <br /> Followup question - does Psychic Projection count as being a scrying window for the purposes of determining Reach? That is, would you need to pay one Reach or two in order to cast spells at the projection's &quot;sensory&quot; range?<br /> <br /> Also, can you enter the higher stories of buildings while in Twilight? RAW in Mage would imply that even building floors are &quot;as solid as fog&quot;, but the fact that you don't drift downward into the core of the earth establishes some common-sense concessions to utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-18-2022, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T02:22:52-07:00","id":1493236,"title":"","content":"&quot;Soul Windows&quot;?<br /> <br /> I think the matter of being alongside buildings might fall under the statement of moving roughly corresponding to the material world despite a lack of gravity. The reference to concrete not being a hindrance puts me in mind of engaging with it as an obstacle rather than a necessity, so if you're engaging with a set of stairs as something to climb you're all right, but if you want to push your way down through them you find no difficulty. Perhaps at times it may be that a naturally material entity could end up sinking through objects they don't mean to if they're not paying attention, and it's a good idea to not lean against anything.<br /> <br /> I've always seen Psychic Projection as meaning the mage is as present as they would be if they were there physically for the purposes of spellcasting, even if current rules mean the inability to naturally touch anything in that state is an added complication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T02:40:32-07:00","id":1493238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493236#post1493236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul Windows?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the Soul Stone spells from page 90 of Signs of Sorcery. Basically, it allows you to see or hear through a soul stone you've created. Reach allows you to see and hear at the same time, and split your perception across multiple soul stones. The Forces conjunctive effect allows you to speak through the stone or even generate a hologram. So you could use it to make a holo-drone like the Illusive Man had on Thessia, but if the intent is to remain sequestered from danger its kinda counter-productive to send in a physical piece of your soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-18-2022, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T03:12:41-07:00","id":1493240,"title":"","content":"I feel as though that getting a Forces conjunctive effect is predicated on it already being a spell about information transmission, whereas I don't find the creation of such an image to be tied so organically to the premise of Psychic Projection. A mage who can Rule Forces can still shape light into an image of themselves while in that intangible state, but I'd think it's an entirely separate spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T03:17:58-07:00","id":1493242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493240#post1493240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though that getting a Forces conjunctive effect is predicated on it already being a spell about information transmission, whereas I don't find the creation of such an image to be tied so organically to the premise of Psychic Projection. A mage who can Rule Forces can still shape light into an image of themselves while in that intangible state, but I'd think it's an entirely separate spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>In your opinion, is there a viable conjunctive for Psychic Projection that would allow for an avatar without physical substance? Spirit maybe, replicating the Image Manifestation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T08:17:04-07:00","id":1493245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493242#post1493242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In your opinion, is there a viable conjunctive for Psychic Projection that would allow for an avatar without physical substance? Spirit maybe, replicating the Image Manifestation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that, by default, it precludes such a thing when it's specified to take a form of lacking an ephemeral body.<br /> <br /> That being said, being an Adept of Mind means you're both able to give people Hallucinations and cast a combined spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T08:28:49-07:00","id":1493246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493232#post1493232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Followup question - does Psychic Projection count as being a scrying window for the purposes of determining Reach? That is, would you need to pay one Reach or two in order to cast spells at the projection's &quot;sensory&quot; range?</div> </div> </div> </div>It counts as you being there, because you're there. You're not occupying your body while you're projected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, can you enter the higher stories of buildings while in Twilight? RAW in Mage would imply that even building floors are &quot;as solid as fog&quot;, but the fact that you don't drift downward into the core of the earth establishes some common-sense concessions to utility. </div> </div> </div>Same page:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The State of Twilight (Mage 2e Core version)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Movement through Twilight roughly corresponds to that of the material world, even though there is no gravity, wind, or pressure. Flight is not possible unless appropriate for the entity\u2019s form; a fiery-winged Goetia might take to the sky, but a clattering, rusting spirit of metal will stick to the material terrain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Equivalent section from the bluebook core:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The State of Twilight (ChroD Core version)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If no ghostly structures get in the way, ephemeral beings in Twilight can move at a walking pace in any direction. Gravity has no sway, though Twilit beings can only truly \u201cfly\u201d if it\u2019s appropriate for their form \u2014 most hug the material terrain. A ghost could walk up the side of a tower block, for example, but couldn\u2019t then float through midair to the next tower.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a matter of imagery. If there's floor or ground to stand on, you can stand on it whether you're material or ephemeral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T05:36:30-07:00","id":1493323,"title":"","content":"Dumb question. Mage uses a Life Ruling spell to give a Sleepwalker the Striking Looks Merit. It doesn't make them unrecognizable, just adjusts the details to make them more attractive / intimidating / pitiable / what have you. Does this trigger Dissonance if a Sleeper who knows the Sleepwalker well sees them during the spell's Duration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T06:29:07-07:00","id":1493325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493323#post1493323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question. Mage uses a Life Ruling spell to give a Sleepwalker the Striking Looks Merit. It doesn't make them unrecognizable, just adjusts the details to make them more attractive / intimidating / pitiable / what have you. Does this trigger Dissonance if a Sleeper who knows the Sleepwalker well sees them during the spell's Duration?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on whether its logically possible. If it is voice related, like having a more energetic, inviting or terrifying tone, then sure, maybe they practiced it. It could manifest as mannerisms complimenting their dress style, making them behave in an elegant manner or walk with a marked amount of confidence, that could have been rehearsed in front of a mirror. But if it is a strong cosmetic difference, then it wouldn't make sense if they didn't have time to recover from plastic surgery, and it would not justify how sometimes they quickly go back to their default look. Maybe they used some movie quality disguises, but that takes time and effort to do, do they seem like someone who would bother ? Paying a professional is expensive, do they have that kind of money, would they invest it in this, do they even know such a person ? If not, then Dissonance hits, the observer suffers the stress of a possible Breaking Point and then Quiescence means those inconsistencies are rationalized away anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-19-2022, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T11:48:13-07:00","id":1493346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493323#post1493323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question. Mage uses a Life Ruling spell to give a Sleepwalker the Striking Looks Merit. It doesn't make them unrecognizable, just adjusts the details to make them more attractive / intimidating / pitiable / what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines, Ruling can increase an existing Merit, but out of all of them I'd feel as though giving a person Striking Looks would be Perfecting (or Fraying) at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this trigger Dissonance if a Sleeper who knows the Sleepwalker well sees them during the spell's Duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Striking Looks could come across as just an alteration in a person's disposition and how they clean up (or not), not dramatic enough a change to trigger Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T19:46:54-07:00","id":1493614,"title":"","content":"Does having a high Resistance stat make self-applied Legacy Attainments like Transform Life useless? Transform Life provides mutations based on Potency, for example, which RAW means that having a high Stamina eats heavily into those bonuses. Last I checked, you can't voluntarily lower your defenses (although I may have missed something).<br /> <br /> Or is that one of the things you can reasonably handwave for a Legacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T20:56:13-07:00","id":1493615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493614#post1493614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does having a high Resistance stat make self-applied Legacy Attainments like Transform Life useless? Transform Life provides mutations based on Potency, for example, which RAW means that having a high Stamina eats heavily into those bonuses. Last I checked, you can't voluntarily lower your defenses (although I may have missed something).<br /> <br /> Or is that one of the things you can reasonably handwave for a Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Mage the Awakening 2ed, page 114</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Before dice are rolled for spellcasting, the caster must consider if her subject can Withstand her magic, as it could affect the dice pool and outcome of the casting. The subject of a spell can always choose not to Withstand a spell, but she must consciously choose to do so as a reflexive action</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, you can choose not to Withstand, but its all or nothing, no partial Withstands. Which means that a Thyrsus can cast Shapechanging on a Sleepwalker and, since its duration primary, they can choose to Withstand the spell until necessary, giving them a wolf or t-rex form with an &quot;on/off switch&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T21:22:01-07:00","id":1493885,"title":"","content":"2 questions<br /> <br /> 1. Why is it that in mage society, the Wise are expected to join legacies? Awakening is a very personal experience, and mages are walking symbols of truth from what I understand, who all seek mysteries of their own and individualistically so (especially in regards to Ascention). And in a culture that encourages individualism, why would they be expected to join a group that explitly involves the process of (voluntarily) reforging their souls and seceding to a theory regarding where Truth can be found? While I can understand why it is not uncommon mages could find cliques they feel resonance with and that they agree with in an academic sense, it does surprise me it would be so common as to be an expectation because of how varied obsessions and the fallen world is<br /> <br /> 2. Is Obsession linked to gnosis, being mystical in of itself? Or is the fact that you gain more Obsessions via higher gnosis simply an abstraction representing how the deeper insight into a mage's path leads them to more easily see the dragons tail and seek it out in multiple things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T22:55:05-07:00","id":1493887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493885#post1493885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 questions<br /> <br /> 1. Why is it that in mage society, the Wise are expected to join legacies? Awakening is a very personal experience, and mages are walking symbols of truth from what I understand, who all seek mysteries of their own and individualistically so (especially in regards to Ascention). And in a culture that encourages individualism, why would they be expected to join a group that explitly involves the process of (voluntarily) reforging their souls and seceding to a theory regarding where Truth can be found? While I can understand why it is not uncommon mages could find cliques they feel resonance with and that they agree with in an academic sense, it does surprise me it would be so common as to be an expectation because of how varied obsessions and the fallen world is<br /> <br /> 2. Is Obsession linked to gnosis, being mystical in of itself? Or is the fact that you gain more Obsessions via higher gnosis simply an abstraction representing how the deeper insight into a mage's path leads them to more easily see the dragons tail and seek it out in multiple things?</div> </div> </div> </div>1.<br /> That\u2019s mostly a matter of perspective; Legacies <i>are</i> a part of actively pursuing said personal paths. You propose yourself to a Legacy you want to pursue. It\u2019s not really something you can force on a mage.<br /> <br /> 2.<br /> I see why it\u2019s not both!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T23:10:43-07:00","id":1493888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493885#post1493885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Why is it that in mage society, the Wise are expected to join legacies? Awakening is a very personal experience, and mages are walking symbols of truth from what I understand, who all seek mysteries of their own and individualistically so (especially in regards to Ascention). And in a culture that encourages individualism, why would they be expected to join a group that explitly involves the process of (voluntarily) reforging their souls and seceding to a theory regarding where Truth can be found? While I can understand why it is not uncommon mages could find cliques they feel resonance with and that they agree with in an academic sense, it does surprise me it would be so common as to be an expectation because of how varied obsessions and the fallen world is</div> </div> </div> </div>Because developing a new Legacy is more difficult than joining an existing one, each dot of Gnosis requires another breakthrough, and there's little point in reinventing the wheel just for the sake of complete personalization of your magical toolbox. Driven seekers after Truth though they are, most mages are not up to inventing a new magical philosophy at the stage in their spiritual development where they are expected to have aligned themselves with such a philosophy.<br /> <br /> Forging a Legacy is a task that requires you to actually undergo the process that forms the basis for initiation \u2014 we're talking about tasks and ordeals not unlike what changelings need to go through to found a Court or attain a kith, or what werewolves need to do to earn a couple dots of Renown. Pinning your Legacy's theory down in practice requires experiential support for its Mysteries, which requires finding Mysteries that mesh with that perspective.<br /> <br /> Also, pretenses of unworldliness notwithstanding, Legacy mentors have an incentive to get other mages to read their books and join their monthly meetings. The Diamond's jackdaw approach to magical praxis does not prevent its mentors from giving its students a nudge toward vaguely-compatible Legacies that have something to offer those mentors for the new recruits. Irreversible though the process typically is, a mage who joins a Legacy and disagrees with the orthodoxy always has the option to develop novel Attainments as they move forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T23:56:00-07:00","id":1493890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493888#post1493888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irreversible though the process typically is, a mage who joins a Legacy and disagrees with the orthodoxy always has the option to develop novel Attainments as they move forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where it says this in 2e but this is exactly how i would run things. You can be initiated into a legacy which works for you, and then develop a personal version of it if you don't like what you find... Alternatively every member of the legacy could have a slightly different capstone attainment, (and there might only be a few members with the 5th attainment) while still considering themselves to be one clique...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T11:01:06-07:00","id":1493912,"title":"","content":"Entirely my own interpretation, not RAW, but\u2026<br /> Based on the supernal being objective Truth, the constraints of the Fallen World being a major theme, and that many of the published legacies (especially 1E) have weird side effects and draw backs [epoch wraiths comes to mind most strongly], my head cannon is that not only is forming a legacy quite difficult, but it also forces the prospect to accept a Truth that can be deeply unsettling, inconvenient, or undermines some of their intentions (but not the entire philosophy). <br /> Supernal truth, like natural law, is not necessarily moral - even without the Exarchs\u2019 corruption - and making a legacy is not only about deciding what magic matters to you and developing a philosophy, but also discovering a primordial truth and become a living anchor for it.<br /> <br /> For example: Tamers of the River are about mastering the nurturing and destructive powers of water - healing, flooding, and rain for crops, especially free from the Lie, are remarkable powers to channel in any agrarian society; anyone might want that. But it\u2019s core Truth is impermanence, and it demands its adherence sacrifice their memories and attachments - which is sure something to balk at. <br /> You can easily imagine the founder of this Legacy seeking out the nourishing powers of water to save their people, and seriously consider giving up when they realize they might have to sacrifice the very relationships they\u2019re trying to protect.<br /> Joining the legacy does not necessarily let you sidestep those drawbacks - but you can learn early on what they are, and they\u2019ve since been fully integrated into the philosophies and trials and recruitment pitch. But the Founder? We can imagine these costs might have undermined their (secondary) goals, and totally blindsided them, after years of obsessive work.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ve strongly emphasized that interpretation of how hard it is to found a legacy in my games - and I include several NPCs who tried to codify their own, but were not willing to accept the Truths they needed, and gave up instead - perhaps leaving notes for someone more willing to walk that path for them.<br /> <br /> For example, my Player wanted to found a Legacy that was all about teaching, networking with other mages, and providing the information they needed to (safely) pursue their obsessions.<br /> The Truth that had to accept was that learning happened when the student was ready; you can\u2019t force enlightenment on another. As a consequence, they can\u2019t just info-dump everything they *think* someone else should hear, or academically bully people into changing opinions. They have to act as an advisor and mentor, providing the information their student is ready and searching for, grimacing at the unasked questions and the \u201cin one ear and out the other\u201d moments when someone doesn\u2019t think a particular fact is important. <br /> It still lets them show up as a SME, provide key information to solve a puzzle, talk people off of a ledge, and have those \u201csweet summer child, you\u2019ve never dealt with werewolves\u201d moments that they were seeking, but curtailed enough to not fundamentally alter the motives (or hubris) of the mages they consulted, or attempt an Awakening gambit.<br /> <br /> As a foil, I have a geomancer NPC that sought out the secrets of Neithian Architecture (Mummy) and Occult Matrixes (Demon) - but would have had to accept a Seer-like attitude of sewing suffering and exploiting Sleepers - so abandoned the nascent Legacy and destroyed its notes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T12:32:47-07:00","id":1493923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493885#post1493885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a culture that encourages individualism</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a simplification that leaves out the entire basis of Orders. The frickin' Free Council promotes the benefits of being part of a system and culture bigger than the individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T19:55:20-07:00","id":1493945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493923#post1493923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a simplification that leaves out the entire basis of Orders. The frickin' Free Council promotes the benefits of being part of a system and culture bigger than the individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Orders find like-minded mages, yes, but other than the seers of the throne, they don't stick mages into tiers of subservience (well, to the extent of the throne) or reforge souls as legacies do. And the free council is a democracy of MANY differing opinions and individuals.<br /> <br /> And also thanks everyone for the myriad of answers! I struggle the most with mage conceptually, so this is a huge help! Again thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T22:24:25-07:00","id":1493949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493945#post1493945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those Orders find like-minded mages, yes, but other than the seers of the throne, they don't stick mages into tiers of subservience (well, to the extent of the throne) or reforge souls as legacies do. And the free council is a democracy of MANY differing opinions and individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally the only form of imposed hierarchy in a Legacy is the need for initiation and the necessary imbalance of knowledge therein, and there is a world of difference between &quot;mages tend to be individualistic and their societal structures are mostly about limiting the collateral damage of powerful people fucking with each other&quot; and &quot;Awakened culture encourages individualism.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are reading more into the process of joining a Legacy than is necessarily implied at base. It's the postgrad specialization to Order training's undergrad education, and as a process that involves dealing with the world (most easily the parts of it that are conversational), you will typically need to navigate long-term human interaction to get that training and the damage substandard training could do to your mentor's reputation means they will usually be somewhat invested in ensuring you are trained properly if they agreed to train you.<br /> <br /> The only subservience involved is that people will typically want compensation for taking that kind of risk, and service and favors tend to be an evergreen currency on that front \u2014 you're forging a sympathetic link as strong as that shared between the average parent and child, and as the one agreeing to the responsibility of imparting secret knowledge the mentor is the party who would be at a disadvantage if this was done for free. &quot;Do as I advise while I'm teaching you so you don't embarrass me or worse&quot; is an ask most mages who are not going full Megalomaniacal can agree to without considering their individuality compromised by the act of deference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T23:21:37-07:00","id":1493956,"title":"","content":"I'd put up with a lot of pedantry to be able to learn the Pure Sovereign Legacy, and I have to imagine most mages take up a similar stance. Just look at the Daoine; prospective apprentices are basically servants until their master deigns to initiate them, but they're free to walk away at any point before the actual initation. And after initiation, they're treated like a junior peer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T15:55:59-07:00","id":1493998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493945#post1493945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they don't stick mages into tiers of subservience [...] as legacies do</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing that on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> or reforge souls as legacies do</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a whole sidebar talking about how, in Second Edition terms, reforging souls is not even what Legacies do anymore.<br /> <br /> To the extent that it matters, the soul is hardly sacrosanct. <br /> <br /> Nevermind that the whole thesis is predicated on an assumption that joining and progressing through Legacies is something coercive. You may as well ask why anybody in real life ever partook in their culture's practice of ritual scarification as an indicator of standing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T01:27:59-07:00","id":1494027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1493998#post1493998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a whole sidebar talking about how, in Second Edition terms, reforging souls is not even what Legacies do anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that the same sidebar which says souls can be stolen and used to learn their owner's legacy? Because sculpting the soul is entirely still one effect of joining a legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T02:02:16-07:00","id":1494028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494027#post1494027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that the same sidebar which says souls can be stolen and used to learn their owner's legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It even goes so far as to explain why that is the case despite the fact that the soul is not altered in and of itself. It's more like it holding an impression of the Gnosis in which it was contained, until such time it is placed into a new vessel.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T05:39:26-07:00","id":1494205,"title":"","content":"Is it true that Prime cannot affect anything material? Would that mean that fraying or unravelling spells like Aetheric Winds or Celestial Fire cannot damage material beings (or affect them with the Heavy Winds tilt, in the case of Aetheric Winds)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T06:36:00-07:00","id":1494207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494205#post1494205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it true that Prime cannot affect anything material? Would that mean that fraying or unravelling spells like Aetheric Winds or Celestial Fire cannot damage material beings (or affect them with the Heavy Winds tilt, in the case of Aetheric Winds)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren\u2019t those two spells the more gross examples of Prime affecting the material? Where did you get that idea from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T07:10:47-07:00","id":1494208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494205#post1494205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it true that Prime cannot affect anything material? Would that mean that fraying or unravelling spells like Aetheric Winds or Celestial Fire cannot damage material beings (or affect them with the Heavy Winds tilt, in the case of Aetheric Winds)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find it a bit of an ambiguously phrased question, but if it's asking if it can only affect spells and mana, the answer is no.<br /> <br /> For a start, you can cast Prime spells on people that expand their sensory range. Prime's purview of Truth is able to engage with physical subjects, in terms of being able to recognise that something is not innately what it appears to be (it can recognise things as mundane as dyed hair). It can affect suitable objects by converting them into grimoires or stores of mana, as well as being able to make them into something like imbued items on a limited basis. It can alter things suitable to function as yantras so spells cast using them get 9- or 8-again. It can render objects capable of interacting with things in Twilight. And yes, its attack spells can strike physical things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T16:01:19-07:00","id":1494269,"title":"","content":"Is gaining a Specialty Perfecting for a Skill you already have, and Patterning for one you don't? I assume it's functioning on the same principle as Gain Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T17:56:25-07:00","id":1494275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494269#post1494269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is gaining a Specialty Perfecting for a Skill you already have, and Patterning for one you don't? I assume it's functioning on the same principle as Gain Skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds correct to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T17:05:36-07:00","id":1494367,"title":"","content":"Alter Integrity has a Withstand of Durability, presumably to avoid the infinite Durability shenanigans that would arrise from spamming the Lasting Reach effect. On the other hand, nothing stops you from spamming the Structure Reach on Lasting. Is that intended, or an oversight? The object won't be any &quot;harder&quot;, but it'll be significantly more dififcult to permenantly destroy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T19:39:06-07:00","id":1494374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494367#post1494367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alter Integrity has a Withstand of Durability, presumably to avoid the infinite Durability shenanigans that would arrise from spamming the Lasting Reach effect. On the other hand, nothing stops you from spamming the Structure Reach on Lasting. Is that intended, or an oversight? The object won't be any &quot;harder&quot;, but it'll be significantly more dififcult to permenantly destroy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you're &quot;spamming&quot; it and you're not an archmaster, you're risking Paradox every time \u2014 those two effects alone add three Reach on a three-dot spell, and the only way you're avoiding that is if you're in a Demesne that semiotically benefits instantaneous addition of Structure to an object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T19:48:55-07:00","id":1494376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494374#post1494374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you're &quot;spamming&quot; it and you're not an archmaster, you're risking Paradox every time \u2014 those two effects alone add three Reach on a three-dot spell, and the only way you're avoiding that is if you're in a Demesne that semiotically benefits instantaneous addition of Structure to an object.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Demense-workshop sounds on-brand for most candidates. There's also dual dedication and/or <i>Time In A Bottle</i> / <i>Everywhere</i>, if you can bear the Mana cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-04-2022, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T20:27:28-07:00","id":1494380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494376#post1494376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Demense-workshop sounds on-brand for most candidates.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Demesne-workshop is going to benefit ritual spells rather than instant spells, as discussed in the section on Demesnes.<br /> <br /> My point is more that sure, if you've Mastered Matter or otherwise focused your magical identity towards this sort of thing, you can make a very chunky object (though my reading of the Reach effect is &quot;one instance of two Structure per casting in addition to a reduced increase in Durability&quot; rather than &quot;replace the entire Durability boost with bonus Structure&quot;), but it's by no means casual.<br /> <br /> Also, the spell is Withstood by Durability because it's a spell that targets an inanimate object and inanimate objects Withstand spells with their Durability. That's it. That's all. It heading off the possibility of making nigh-indestructible objects with the normal Durability-adjustment spell is a useful consequence of that fact.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T20:33:14-07:00","id":1494381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494380#post1494380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it's by no means casual.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... not implying that it is? Just that a sufficiently driven Mage can add a staggering amount of Dissonance-free Structure to an object by RAW. Not that it's game-breaking or particularly useful, just kinda interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494380#post1494380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(though my reading of the Reach effect is &quot;one instance of two Structure per casting in addition to a reduced increase in Durability&quot; rather than &quot;replace the entire Durability boost with bonus Structure&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;+1 Reach: In lieu of increasing Durability, one level of Potency may be \u201cspent\u201d to give the object 2 additional points of Structure.&quot;<br /> Intentionally keep it at an effective Potency 1. As long as you're converting it all to Structure, the Durability is never going up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-04-2022, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T20:58:17-07:00","id":1494384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494381#post1494381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... not implying that it is? Just that a sufficiently driven Mage can add a staggering amount of Dissonance-free Structure to an object by RAW. Not that it's game-breaking or particularly useful, just kinda interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sufficiently driven mage can indefinitely bind a minor Incarna, cure a college campus of cancer, and become a god. &quot;If you don't care that an object is still going to be broken as long as it's not completely destroyed you can extend the functional life of an object a great deal by casting the same spell you would use to make it harder to break&quot; is not terribly interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;+1 Reach: In lieu of increasing Durability, one level of Potency may be \u201cspent\u201d to give the object 2 additional points of Structure.&quot;<br /> Intentionally keep it at an effective Potency 1. As long as you're converting it all to Structure, the Durability is never going up. </div> </div> </div>At which point I think it is plain that you are leaning on this being a quirk of the mechanics rather than something anyone would actually bother to do in-character. It's a weird effect of the spell being written to need Reach to provide Durability that adds to the object's Structure like Zoom In having a Reach effect that references Forces dots. This feels like the kind of thing that led Hone the Perfected Form to not have a Lasting option \u2014 it's mildly entertaining to look at as an accident of the design process and increasingly unfunny to push for as a serious read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T04:59:50-07:00","id":1494404,"title":"","content":"All other considerations aside, a rote would cover the three Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T05:43:08-07:00","id":1494406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494404#post1494404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All other considerations aside, a rote would cover the three Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without other considerations like also being as well-versed in Time as a non-Acanthus can get on their own, a rote providing the Reach of a Master does not do anything to the situation of &quot;even with Mastery of the Arcanum, you cannot instant-cast this effect without overReaching.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T05:49:38-07:00","id":1494407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494406#post1494406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without other considerations like also being as well-versed in Time as a non-Acanthus can get on their own, a rote providing the Reach of a Master does not do anything to the situation of &quot;even with Mastery of the Arcanum, you cannot instant-cast this effect without overReaching.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you're being a bit too pedantic about the use of the word &quot;spam&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T05:57:23-07:00","id":1494408,"title":"","content":"Seconded. Spending a few half-hour stints reinforcing the structural integrity of your Sanctum was more what I was thinking of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T06:13:16-07:00","id":1494411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494407#post1494407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're being a bit too pedantic about the use of the word &quot;spam&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think that in a storytelling game where ritual spellcasting takes at least half the time its Duration chart equates to the length of a scene until the back third of its Supernatural Potency chart it's perfectly reasonable to assume any table with sense is not dedicating multiple scenes of screentime to a player workshopping extra Structure onto equipment with ritual casting. We can disagree on this matter, but deciding whether or not I am being pedantic is not the function of this thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> Given the psychological effects of sympathy, would Create Sympathy be Withstood by an additional Trait for unwilling subjects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T06:25:38-07:00","id":1494412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494411#post1494411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the psychological effects of sympathy, would Create Sympathy be Withstood by an additional Trait for unwilling subjects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gut instinct says \u201cNah\u201d. Though rulings like \u201cuse the higher of Connection strength or Composure\u201d do sound reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T10:07:58-07:00","id":1494424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494411#post1494411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the psychological effects of sympathy, would Create Sympathy be Withstood by an additional Trait for unwilling subjects?</div> </div> </div> </div>My instinct says no.<br /> <br /> I think there are certain things which are sort of surface to a person which don't get withstood, like knowing spells to learn about them...know nature and correspondance... (Know spirit is withstood by the spirits rank, but knowing a mind or someone's sympathic connection are not withstood).<br /> <br /> It is only with the reach that this seems scarey strong. Making a connected sympathy with a reach to make it never fade, is at least withstood by 5 for the strength of the connection...Which seems really easy for a master of space getting all those free steps in potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T19:44:02-07:00","id":1494441,"title":"","content":"Dumb question<br /> <br /> Due to the nature of mages, is a high gnosis and high wisdom (or even high middling) mage even possible? Besides the things one would need to do to achieve high gnosis, would the effects of having it pull too hard on a mage to ever not occasionally use magic in an act of hubris?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T19:52:42-07:00","id":1494442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494441#post1494441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question<br /> <br /> Due to the nature of mages, is a high gnosis and high wisdom (or even high middling) mage even possible? Besides the things one would need to do to achieve high gnosis, would the effects of having it pull too hard on a mage to ever not occasionally use magic in an act of hubris?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the person and how badly they fumble their rolls. I don't think it's impossible, just uncommon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T20:01:21-07:00","id":1494444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494441#post1494441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Due to the nature of mages, is a high gnosis and high wisdom (or even high middling) mage even possible? Besides the things one would need to do to achieve high gnosis, would the effects of having it pull too hard on a mage to ever not occasionally use magic in an act of hubris?</div> </div> </div> </div>High Gnosis tends to incentivize higher Arcana ratings, which in turn tend to increase your safe Reach, which in turn tends to mean the Rampant Condition tends to become harder to resist or to resolve without simply casting in view of Sleepers, which itself risks more Wisdom loss, but multiple Obsession slots and judicious spell inurement mean it's entirely within the realm of possibility.<br /> <br /> There is, admittedly, good reason that the archetype of such characters tends toward sequestered hermitage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T20:20:29-07:00","id":1494445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494444#post1494444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Gnosis tends to incentivize higher Arcana ratings, which in turn tend to increase your safe Reach, which in turn tends to mean the Rampant Condition tends to become harder to resist or to resolve without simply casting in view of Sleepers, which itself risks more Wisdom loss, but multiple Obsession slots and judicious spell inurement mean it's entirely within the realm of possibility.<br /> <br /> There is, admittedly, good reason that the archetype of such characters tends toward sequestered hermitage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose so, and I admit I should've specified that I meant in narrative sense, no rolls. But wouldn't a hermitage not do much, a high gnosis and arcana mage would see so much. Even by herself, there would be tons of Mysteries and therefore Obsessions to look into. That, and you don't need to manipulate humanity for acts of hubris","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T21:13:51-07:00","id":1494446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494445#post1494445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But wouldn't a hermitage not do much, a high gnosis and arcana mage would see so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>And seeing does precious little to hurt your Wisdom in most cases, because the stat is affected by lack of regard for the consequences of your <i>actions</i>. Minimizing the consequences of your studies is most easily managed by isolating your research sites from the wider world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That, and you don't need to manipulate humanity for acts of hubris </div> </div> </div>Sure, but when the vast majority of the example Acts of Hubris are interpersonal it's a lot easier to maintain control of your selfhood by minimizing the time you spend not by yourself. Hard to affect bystanders, force sapient beings to act against their interests, or impulsively murder someone if you avoid contact with people and stick to contemplating mineral Mysteries in the mountains or figuring out Forms on a farm in the forest.<br /> <br /> You need other people or spiritual self-mutilation to mess with your magic's ability to stay put, and being Wise enough to make sure someone comes by to check on them every now and then is part of the reason those hermits are still connected to magical society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T21:29:45-07:00","id":1494447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494446#post1494446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And seeing does precious little to hurt your Wisdom in most cases, because the stat is affected by lack of regard for the consequences of your <i>actions</i>. Minimizing the consequences of your studies is most easily managed by isolating your research sites from the wider world.<br /> <br /> Sure, but when the vast majority of the example Acts of Hubris are interpersonal it's a lot easier to maintain control of your selfhood by minimizing the time you spend not by yourself. Hard to affect bystanders, force sapient beings to act against their interests, or impulsively murder someone if you avoid contact with people and stick to contemplating mineral Mysteries in the mountains or figuring out Forms on a farm in the forest.<br /> <br /> You need other people or spiritual self-mutilation to mess with your magic's ability to stay put, and being Wise enough to make sure someone comes by to check on them every now and then is part of the reason those hermits are still connected to magical society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, seeing doesn't do anything, but mages are obsessive. Its incredibly hard for them to see something and not look into it.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm ignoring the fact that mages are more than their Obsessions. I still struggle to imagine it, but I guess it's not as impossible as I seem to think it is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T01:46:26-07:00","id":1494448,"title":"","content":"When the 2e core says that &quot;Obsessions are just like long-term Aspiration...&quot;, does that mean the rules on swapping out aspirations also covers obsessions?<br /> <br /> (I'm meaning the top two paragraphs on page 83.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T06:26:24-07:00","id":1494453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494448#post1494448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the 2e core says that &quot;Obsessions are just like long-term Aspiration...&quot;, does that mean the rules on swapping out aspirations also covers obsessions?<br /> <br /> (I'm meaning the top two paragraphs on page 83.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. If your character is interested in new Mysteries, already learned all they needed or even focused on a more specific niche, then an update is in order.<br /> <br /> An example is starting with &quot;Code as magic&quot; as an Obsession. Then they see beehives organizing themselves in a system to run algorithms, which takes them to certain sections of a park that naturally created a circuit with ley lines and from there to an obscure part of the Dreaming Earth that is made of biotech (similar to the ones the Dragonians from Chrono Cross used). By now their Obsession might be &quot;Nature's emergent magical code&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-06-2022, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T08:58:17-07:00","id":1494456,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, higher Gnosis coming with several Obsession slots means that you're sacrificing less when you take up an Obsession of improving your Wisdom, and you can spend a while building it up to Enlightened level, at which point you can at least benefit from having 5 dice to roll against losing it. A person's own Oneiros sounds like a good place to go on a sabbatical that is also great for the reflection necessary to pursue that Obsession.<br /> <br /> I'm not really seeing an argument that the sorts of magic available to Masters are totally incompatible with Acts of Hubris against Enlightened Wisdom. Making and Unmaking spells contain quite a few things that there would be no mundane method to replicate, and I think there has to be something there that is not necessarily risky to bystanders. Like, the other side of having lots of Reach is that when you <i>don't</i> have the Rampant Condition, a lot of your magic becomes safer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T14:36:42-07:00","id":1494467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494456#post1494456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really seeing an argument that the sorts of magic available to Masters are totally incompatible with Acts of Hubris against Enlightened Wisdom. Making and Unmaking spells contain quite a few things that there would be no mundane method to replicate, and I think there has to be something there that is not necessarily risky to bystanders. Like, the other side of having lots of Reach is that when you <i>don't</i> have the Rampant Condition, a lot of your magic becomes safer.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is about my initial bit, I was never asserting any incompatibility \u2014 I was saying that the way the Rampant Condition works means being able to do more with magic safely tends to make it harder to shake off the Condition without risking Wisdom by doing inadvisable things to risk Paradox, which, combined with the Willpower surcharge and imposed Obsession, means more powerful mages will find it harder to climb back up the ladder; until Gnosis 6, a Wisdom Condition takes up at least half your available Obsessions and can easily replace itself in the resolution.<br /> <br /> My answer was &quot;It can be difficult, but yes, though there's a reason the archetype associated with that state is the way it is,&quot; not &quot;Masters can't maintain high Wisdom.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-06-2022, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T03:23:29-07:00","id":1494511,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> I was wondering, let's say we have an Obrimos mage (Gnosis 2, Forces 3, Prime 3) on a pretty crowded train. He discovers that a passenger is a small time terrorist, and has set an IED inside a suitcase. Other mages will try to convince this terrorist to surrender, or try and subdue him. Let's say they fail and the IED goes off: what's the best spell our Obrimos can use to contain the blast, and protect himself, his companions and other passengers in that train wagon?<br /> I was thinking about Control Fire, as Environmental Shield doesn't seem the right spell for this (a bomb exploding doesn't seem like an environmental condition. Or is it?). Is there a better spell than that one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26982-avenging-hathor","name":"Avenging Hathor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T03:58:22-07:00","id":1494513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494511#post1494511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone,<br /> I was wondering, let's say we have an Obrimos mage (Gnosis 2, Forces 3, Prime 3) on a pretty crowded train. He discovers that a passenger is a small time terrorist, and has set an IED inside a suitcase. Other mages will try to convince this terrorist to surrender, or try and subdue him. Let's say they fail and the IED goes off: what's the best spell our Obrimos can use to contain the blast, and protect himself, his companions and other passengers in that train wagon?<br /> I was thinking about Control Fire, as Environmental Shield doesn't seem the right spell for this (a bomb exploding doesn't seem like an environmental condition. Or is it?). Is there a better spell than that one?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a similar spell to this in 1e called &quot;Containment&quot;. It was Forces 4, and once activated, the spell protects everything within a small radius around the mage from harm by slowing down fast-moving objects, damping fires and harmlessly grounding dangerous amounts of electricity.<br /> <br /> Environmental Shield could protect against the heat and fire, but might have trouble with shrapnel. Ban would be useful, but you'd need Space and possibly Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-07-2022, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T04:35:17-07:00","id":1494514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494511#post1494511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone,<br /> I was wondering, let's say we have an Obrimos mage (Gnosis 2, Forces 3, Prime 3) on a pretty crowded train. He discovers that a passenger is a small time terrorist, and has set an IED inside a suitcase. Other mages will try to convince this terrorist to surrender, or try and subdue him. Let's say they fail and the IED goes off: what's the best spell our Obrimos can use to contain the blast, and protect himself, his companions and other passengers in that train wagon?<br /> I was thinking about Control Fire, as Environmental Shield doesn't seem the right spell for this (a bomb exploding doesn't seem like an environmental condition. Or is it?). Is there a better spell than that one?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say a Shielding spell would do the trick. Make it Potency 2 to protect from 2 types of hostile forces (kinetic and heat), spend a Willpower for the extra Potency dice, use concentration to avoid detection, mantra if you find a particularly unobserved or loud corner, AoE to protect everyone in the blast area. Shielding is a very good Practice, since it can no sell mundane dangers under its purview.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, just use a Shielding from fire on the IED from sensory range. It becomes kind of useless if a spark does nothing to the chemicals, and it can be dismissed as being badly put together. Less resource intensive and does not risk breaking points for Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-07-2022, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T13:39:16-07:00","id":1494550,"title":"","content":"Is the explosive activated by electricity? Because a Compelling spell can shut down anything electronic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T18:04:50-07:00","id":1494563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494550#post1494550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the explosive activated by electricity? Because a Compelling spell can shut down anything electronic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. Does it make any difference that the mage cannot see the actual device, as it's locked inside the suitcase?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26982-avenging-hathor","name":"Avenging Hathor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T18:52:28-07:00","id":1494564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494563#post1494563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is. Does it make any difference that the mage cannot see the actual device, as it's locked inside the suitcase?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Forces Sight (Active Mage Sight) detects whether a device is powered; I\u2019d rule that this is sufficient sensory input for purposes of forming Imagos for Influence Electricity (the aforementioned Forces 1 spell).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T20:55:18-07:00","id":1494570,"title":"","content":"As I recall, Mage Sight itself explicitly cannot see through objects. However, if a container has seams that are less than perfectly enclosed, I think it would be a simple enough matter for a Ruling of Forces to manipulate light in a manner that lays the contents bare to a chosen observer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T01:37:31-07:00","id":1494581,"title":"","content":"Say you want to pull off an old-school miracle by causing a field to ripen and become an Instant bumper harvest. Ignoring Dissonance for a moment, what would be the optimal Arcana for that?<br /> <br /> Life, so you can use Accelerate Growth? Will produce remain if you cancel the spell after the harvest is complete?<br /> <br /> Time, to replicate a similar effect, likely through Perfecting practices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T02:14:02-07:00","id":1494584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494581#post1494581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say you want to pull off an old-school miracle by causing a field to ripen and become an Instant bumper harvest. Ignoring Dissonance for a moment, what would be the optimal Arcana for that?<br /> <br /> Life, so you can use Accelerate Growth? Will produce remain if you cancel the spell after the harvest is complete?<br /> <br /> Time, to replicate a similar effect, likely through Perfecting practices?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind to make the folks hallucinate they\u2019re reaping a good year\u2019s harvest as they stack handfuls of mud and dust into their sacks. No, I will not divulge my current estimate Wisdom level, nor why the Guardians gave me a warning last month <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Jokes aside, Life really is the safest and most intuitive way I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T02:54:42-07:00","id":1494586,"title":"","content":"If the Guardians aren't keeping an eye on you, you're doing something wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494584#post1494584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jokes aside, Life really is the safest and most intuitive way I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but the most important question remains; does the harvest stick around after you cancel the spell? I'd imagine it doesn't matter once they've become conceptually something else (baked into bread, eaten, ground into dye), but does the raw harvest have enough symbolic independence to exist beyond the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T03:41:03-07:00","id":1494587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494586#post1494586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but does the raw harvest have enough symbolic independence to exist beyond the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't look like it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the spell expires, the subject returns to its actual age. </div> </div> </div>That being said, it seems to me like ending an accelerate growth spell should simply return growth to normal.<br /> <br /> That said, you could also achieve a harvest by messing with ley lines as described on pg. 242 of the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T07:19:27-07:00","id":1494597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494581#post1494581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say you want to pull off an old-school miracle by causing a field to ripen and become an Instant bumper harvest. Ignoring Dissonance for a moment, what would be the optimal Arcana for that?<br /> <br /> Life, so you can use Accelerate Growth? Will produce remain if you cancel the spell after the harvest is complete?<br /> <br /> Time, to replicate a similar effect, likely through Perfecting practices?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably an Unmaking of Time to eliminate the interval between growing and harvesting. Alternatively, use a Weaving of Life or Time to synch the biological clock of the crops to that of a short lived organism, like a mayfly (whose average lifespan is 24 hours). When the organism reaches maturity, so will the plants. Then you collect the crops, end the spell so your field goes back to normal and have a harvest festival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T04:47:34-07:00","id":1494667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494581#post1494581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say you want to pull off an old-school miracle by causing a field to ripen and become an Instant bumper harvest. Ignoring Dissonance for a moment, what would be the optimal Arcana for that?<br /> <br /> Life, so you can use Accelerate Growth? Will produce remain if you cancel the spell after the harvest is complete?<br /> <br /> Time, to replicate a similar effect, likely through Perfecting practices?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Life to make a bumper harvest (growth) will be like healing and have lasting effects, the life spell makes the crops grow and if harvested in time, everything taken will be lasting.<br /> <br /> This is not the same symbolically as accelerate growth aging a baby in 6 months. This is more like controlling when /how fast someone gives birth (and then harvesting... Ok it is supposed to be a horror game).<br /> <br /> Doing it with Time would work, but has the downside of plants can also get sick and die over time, so it is less controlled than Life.<br /> <br /> Death (Unmaking) can undo the negative effects of withered crops and thus restore a crop to perfect health - but (eg deny the reaper) it is much more temporary. <br /> <br /> Forces to get good weather would take longer but like Life have lasting results. Spirit could cultuvate spirits of the plants and healthy harvests, a lot more long term effort, but probably manage larger scale (eventually covering the whole valley) and lasting effects.<br /> <br /> Did someone say prime leylines could help? Definitely lasting, as the growth would be a side effect.<br /> <br /> Matter could fabricated fertiliser and water, slower, but should be lasting once the crops grow .<br /> <br /> Fate, yep.<br /> <br /> In short, the more indirect the magic, the less likely the effect will end when the spell expires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T07:47:50-07:00","id":1494671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494570#post1494570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, Mage Sight itself explicitly cannot see through objects. However, if a container has seams that are less than perfectly enclosed, I think it would be a simple enough matter for a Ruling of Forces to manipulate light in a manner that lays the contents bare to a chosen observer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The container is much like a fiber briefcase, so it's pretty much waterproof, perfectly enclosed.<br /> Maybe this would call for a Shielding practice, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> suggested: by Shielding the whole briefcase from electricity, all of it (contents included) should be protected from sparks and electronic activation devices, right?<br /> <br /> Another question, though: what would happen if for some reason this mage would rather let the IED go off, and use his knowledge of Forces to protect himself and his friends? Kaiser suggested Shielding to give people in the AoE effective immunity from the blast effects, at a low cost of 2 Potency (1 immunity to heat, +1 immunity to kinetic energy). Thus people in the AoE would be immune to all damage, no matter if the bomb has 10 pounds of tnt, 50 pounds or 100 pounds. Should that be so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26982-avenging-hathor","name":"Avenging Hathor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T08:48:51-07:00","id":1494676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avenging Hathor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494671#post1494671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The container is much like a fiber briefcase, so it's pretty much waterproof, perfectly enclosed.<br /> Maybe this would call for a Shielding practice, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> suggested: by Shielding the whole briefcase from electricity, all of it (contents included) should be protected from sparks and electronic activation devices, right?<br /> <br /> Another question, though: what would happen if for some reason this mage would rather let the IED go off, and use his knowledge of Forces to protect himself and his friends? Kaiser suggested Shielding to give people in the AoE effective immunity from the blast effects, at a low cost of 2 Potency (1 immunity to heat, +1 immunity to kinetic energy). Thus people in the AoE would be immune to all damage, no matter if the bomb has 10 pounds of tnt, 50 pounds or 100 pounds. Should that be so?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, I assumed briefcase and bomb are seen as one symbolic whole, like person and clothes, so long as they are not separated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage The Awakening 2ed, page 126</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Protection</span><br /> Most commonly with the Practice of Shielding (\u2022\u2022), a spell may grant protection from forces under the Arcanum\u2019s purview. These spells usually provide blanket immunity to natural or mundane phenomena, while protecting against a number of grant protection from forces under the Arcanum\u2019s purview. These spells usually provide blanket immunity to natural or mundane phenomena, while protecting against supernatural attacks, which must win a Clash of Wills to affect the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah, no matter how much mundane power you throw at it, if its within the purview of what they are Shielded against, they are not affected (with some exceptions, such as <i>Alchemist's Touch</i> and <i>Environmental Shield</i>). The explosion of an IED, a landmine or a nuke will do nothing. The kinetic energy of a bullet, sword, fall at terminal velocity or being rammed by a truck will mean nothing. If the bomb is Shielded from the Fate of being used, then it will slip away if you try to activate it, a dog may steal it, it could be thrown out of the train by a hostage with a sudden surge of bravery and land in a soft area or the police might confiscate it. Mages who have a solid grasp of Shielding should have very few worries about most mundane dangers their Arcana cover. The main limit is how much they care about Paradox, Disbelief and Quiescence. But if an Obrimos is so angry that they stopped caring and they had time to Shield themselves, then neither a shock troop or a tank will be able to stop them.<br /> <br /> Regarding the general possibilities of the Practices, how they affect how the mage perceives themselves (and is perceived), as well as interesting examinations of them, I would recommend <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2019/06/1-mage-awakening-2e-13-practices-of.html\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-09-2022, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T05:55:08-07:00","id":1494725,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit on how many souls can fit in a container for the purposes of Soul Jar? Or is the main limit that the soul needs a &quot;receptacle&quot; to reside in for the purpose of the spell, and the actual container has an unlimited soul-capacity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T13:04:15-07:00","id":1494749,"title":"","content":"If <i>Control Instincts</i> is used to apply an effect similar to morphine, shutting down pain before a medical procedure (but without negative side effects), what condition would be used ? If they use it to create a flood of adrenalin, which one would apply ? In case they were capture and used it to cause the productions of vast quantities of endorphins to resist interrogation, which condition would be adequate ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T16:16:21-07:00","id":1494754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494725#post1494725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a limit on how many souls can fit in a container for the purposes of Soul Jar? Or is the main limit that the soul needs a &quot;receptacle&quot; to reside in for the purpose of the spell, and the actual container has an unlimited soul-capacity?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main limit is that you have to place the soul in the Soul Jar and opening it releases the soul(s) it contains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494749#post1494749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <i>Control Instincts</i> is used to apply an effect similar to morphine, shutting down pain before a medical procedure (but without negative side effects), what condition would be used ? If they use it to create a flood of adrenalin, which one would apply ? In case they were capture and used it to cause the productions of vast quantities of endorphins to resist interrogation, which condition would be adequate ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As described in the spell itself, a custom one using the &quot;Creating Conditions and Tilts&quot; section as a guideline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T18:02:21-07:00","id":1494759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494754#post1494754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main limit is that you have to place the soul in the Soul Jar and opening it releases the soul(s) it contains.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a reasonable facsimile of a soul-stealing weapon would be Imbuing Soul Jar into a weapon with a hollow compartment?<br /> <br /> For example, a dagger (or more dramatically, a sword) whose Siderite handle is hollow and whose pommel is the unscrewable cap. If Imbued with the Lasting version of Soul Jar (And probably Instant Casting), that compartment would be able to hold as many souls as the wielder can accrue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T18:29:20-07:00","id":1494761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494759#post1494759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a reasonable facsimile of a soul-stealing weapon would be Imbuing Soul Jar into a weapon with a hollow compartment?<br /> <br /> For example, a dagger (or more dramatically, a sword) whose Siderite handle is hollow and whose pommel is the unscrewable cap. If Imbued with the Lasting version of Soul Jar (And probably Instant Casting), that compartment would be able to hold as many souls as the wielder can accrue?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how you got to there from &quot;you have to open a thing to put stuff in it, and opening it lets stuff out of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> A reasonable facsimile of a soul-stealing weapon would be attempting to replicate the Tremere's hollowstones/Soul Breath legerdemain. Otherwise it may be necessary to acknowledge that there is a difference between &quot;weapon that removes souls,&quot; &quot;vessel that accumulates loose souls,&quot; and &quot;weapon that has a deleterious effect beyond physical damage on its victims, fluffed as being caused by doing something involving their soul.&quot;<br /> <br /> An Artifact could presumably have a unique effect involving this, but otherwise you manage by putting the released souls back in the thing when you put a new one in \u2014 that's what increased Scale is for and also why you don't hoard the things in a single container without putting them to use \u2014 and maintaining instances of Sever Soul at long Duration so the souls in question don't return to their owners whenever you open the jar.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of Tremere, what's the Hollow rating of a Preta born from falling to Hollow 0 during the <i>koimaomai</i> for the purposes of spending Willpower and deriving sustenance from Preta's Soul Theft?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-10-2022, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T18:59:34-07:00","id":1494765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494754#post1494754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main limit is that you have to place the soul in the Soul Jar and opening it releases the soul(s) it contains.<br /> <br /> As described in the spell itself, a custom one using the &amp;quot;Creating Conditions and Tilts&amp;quot; section as a guideline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I need to clarify my question, the doubt was never on the rules, but on how they were handled at different tables. In other words, which existing conditions have been considered sufficient for those scenarios and which custom ones, if any, have they created otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T20:23:29-07:00","id":1494774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494761#post1494761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how you got to there from &quot;you have to open a thing to put stuff in it, and opening it lets stuff out of it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely a -likely oversimplifed- reading of the spell's description. It specifies that <i>opening</i> the container releases the soul, but not that the container <i>needs to be open</i> for a soul to be bound to it. I can easily see the arguement against allowing that interpretation, but it's the interpretation I prefer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494761#post1494761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A reasonable facsimile of a soul-stealing weapon would be attempting to replicate the Tremere's hollowstones/Soul Breath legerdemain. Otherwise it may be necessary to acknowledge that there is a difference between &quot;weapon that removes souls,&quot; &quot;vessel that accumulates loose souls,&quot; and &quot;weapon that has a deleterious effect beyond physical damage on its victims, fluffed as being caused by doing something involving their soul.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was shooting for &quot;Weapon that traps the souls of those it kills&quot;, ala Frostmourne, Final Blades of Galt, Elder Scrolls weapons with the Soul Trap enchantment, etc. A discussion of which spirals outside &quot;Simple Question&quot;, I think, so I'll leave off there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494761#post1494761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Tremere, what's the Hollow rating of a Preta born from falling to Hollow 0 during the <i>koimaomai</i> for the purposes of spending Willpower and deriving sustenance from Preta's Soul Theft?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pulling off the character sheet on <u>Nameless and Accursed </u>page 135: &quot;Hollow: as the mage\u2019s previous Gnosis/Hollow.&quot;<br /> <br /> So my assumption is that it's the highest Hollow that Preta had achieved before sleeping their way into Preta-hood. Wild guess though, and not one I'd die defending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T20:24:18-07:00","id":1494775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494765#post1494765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe I need to clarify my question, the doubt was never on the rules, but on how they were handled at different tables. In other words, which existing conditions have been considered sufficient for those scenarios and which custom ones, if any, have they created otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a constrained version of the Steadfast Condition, that applies only to relevant failed resist/constest-rolls instead of any failed rolls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T04:31:20-07:00","id":1494781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494774#post1494774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Largely a -likely oversimplifed- reading of the spell's description. It specifies that <i>opening</i> the container releases the soul, but not that the container <i>needs to be open</i> for a soul to be bound to it. I can easily see the arguement against allowing that interpretation, but it's the interpretation I prefer.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was shooting for &quot;Weapon that traps the souls of those it kills&quot;, ala Frostmourne, Final Blades of Galt, Elder Scrolls weapons with the Soul Trap enchantment, etc. A discussion of which spirals outside &quot;Simple Question&quot;, I think, so I'll leave off there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pulling off the character sheet on <u>Nameless and Accursed </u>page 135: &quot;Hollow: as the mage\u2019s previous Gnosis/Hollow.&quot;<br /> <br /> So my assumption is that it's the highest Hollow that Preta had achieved before sleeping their way into Preta-hood. Wild guess though, and not one I'd die defending.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like you want to take the basic functionality of Soul Jar and alter its properties to redefine what counts as release and capture mode. That sounds like the purview of Weaving, which for simplicity's sake could be modeled as a Reach option on the original spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T13:54:00-07:00","id":1494806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494781#post1494781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems like you want to take the basic functionality of Soul Jar and alter its properties to redefine what counts as release and capture mode. That sounds like the purview of Weaving, which for simplicity's sake could be modeled as a Reach option on the original spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. It's a decent solution. <br /> <br /> What kind of service would be an appropriate demand from The Stag, for the Aeon to initiate a Mage into a Life-based Legacy? <br /> <br /> Or any of the Aeons, for that matter? Mordred would probably demand a betrayal, Typhon the destruction of some human construct, but I'm unsure of the rest. Maybe facilitating some precipitous temptation for The Serpent, although I can't quite decide if that's in-line with Spirit or just assigning too much Christian symbolism to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-11-2022, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T14:54:03-07:00","id":1494810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494806#post1494806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly. It's a decent solution. <br /> <br /> What kind of service would be an appropriate demand from The Stag, for the Aeon to initiate a Mage into a Life-based Legacy? <br /> <br /> Or any of the Aeons, for that matter? Mordred would probably demand a betrayal, Typhon the destruction of some human construct, but I'm unsure of the rest. Maybe facilitating some precipitous temptation for The Serpent, although I can't quite decide if that's in-line with Spirit or just assigning too much Christian symbolism to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A neutral task, because the Truth of the Primal Wild is that nature does not take sides. Even humans are part of the cycle of predator and prey, sharp instinct is the key to survival. Its the flight of the eagle, they saw the parent fly and they were taken to see the area, now they need to put it into practice before they meet the ground.<br /> <br /> I would associate him with the horned god. So whatever task he assigns are to make the mage track down the Truths of the Legacy. It will force the candidate to confront a lesson from each of its aspects: the Warrior, the Parent and the Sage. Each successful test leads to the next, an ecstatic hallucination providing clues to the next task or context towards the greater whole. The dreams of Hircine in Bloodmoon are a good point of reference. Its a more intuitive and brutal mentoring style than normal, but effective.<br /> <br /> I see the services of the Primal Wild Aeons reqiring simple and intuitive solutions. But simple does not mean easy, many times simplifying something is a sign of mastery and deep understanding. Similarly, intuitive does not mean lacking challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-11-2022, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T15:08:56-07:00","id":1494813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494806#post1494806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly. It's a decent solution. <br /> <br /> What kind of service would be an appropriate demand from The Stag, for the Aeon to initiate a Mage into a Life-based Legacy? <br /> <br /> Or any of the Aeons, for that matter? Mordred would probably demand a betrayal, Typhon the destruction of some human construct, but I'm unsure of the rest. Maybe facilitating some precipitous temptation for The Serpent, although I can't quite decide if that's in-line with Spirit or just assigning too much Christian symbolism to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Form a harem, Anime/LightNovel style, and prosper enough not to get stabbed in the guts out of a member\u2019s/outsider\u2019s jealousy. Pretty sure there\u2019s a Legacy/Nameless Order out there who encourages that stuff <i>somewhere</i>.<br /> <br /> For the Serpent, the \u2018temptation\u2019 might be just \u2018indulgence\u2019. It\u2019d be the mage\u2019s call to whether she makes it an excuse to descend to decadency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T15:48:31-07:00","id":1494816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494810#post1494810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A neutral task, because the Truth of the Primal Wild is that nature does not take sides. Even humans are part of the cycle of predator and prey, sharp instinct is the key to survival. Its the flight of the eagle, they saw the parent fly and they were taken to see the area, now they need to put it into practice before they meet the ground.<br /> <br /> I would associate him with the horned god. So whatever task he assigns are to make the mage track down the Truths of the Legacy. It will force the candidate to confront a lesson from each of its aspects: the Warrior, the Youth and the Sage. Each successful test leads to the next, an ecstatic hallucination providing clues to the next task or context towards the greater whole. The dreams of Hircine in Bloodmoon are a good point of reference. Its a more intuitive and brutal mentoring style than normal, but effective.<br /> <br /> I see the services of the Primal Wild Aeons reqiring simple and intuitive solutions. But simple does not mean easy, many times simplifying something is a sign of mastery and deep understanding. Similarly, intuitive does not mean lacking challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494813#post1494813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Form a harem, Anime/LightNovel style, and prosper enough not to get stabbed in the guts out of a member\u2019s/outsider\u2019s jealousy. Pretty sure there\u2019s a Legacy/Nameless Order out there who encourages that stuff <i>somewhere</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>M: Your Majesty, I beg you to grant me the boon of the Pure Sovereign Legacy.<br /> <br /> THE STAG: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">A TRUE RULER MUST GIVE EQUAL CARE AND ATTENTION TO ALL THEIR SUBJECTS, UNIFYING THEM INTO AN ORGANIC WHOLE. GATHER UNTO THYSELF A HARMONIOUS HAREM. UNDER THE SIGN OF THE HORNED GOD, GO FORTH AND ORGY.</span><br /> <br /> M: Er, your Majesty... &quot;orgy&quot; isn't a verb. &quot;Conquer&quot; might be a better choice, but the connota-<br /> <br /> THE STAG: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">DID I <i>F#(^ING </i>STUTTER?!</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494813#post1494813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Serpent, the \u2018temptation\u2019 might be just \u2018indulgence\u2019. It\u2019d be the mage\u2019s call to whether she makes it an excuse to descend to decadency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more along the lines of turning the Mage into their catspaw of temptation.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey. Hey you! Yes, you! Wanna read some forbidden tomes?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-11-2022, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T15:53:55-07:00","id":1494817,"title":"","content":"I think it would be interesting for a mage to be assigned a task of restoring some biodiversity, some functional ecology, to an area that has been rendered notably uniform.<br /> <br /> Although on the other hand, Stag is probably attuned to the purview of the Life Arcanum to an extent that it has highly intimate knowledge of already existing ecosystems and might task a petitioner with something that will ultimately result in curating some element that could have long term impacts upon such that are undesirable to the Aeon. A few carefully arranged adjustments in the correct place and a cascade of events will result in the extinction of some as yet undiscovered variety of shrew that Stag perceives to be capable of serving as the vector for some type of plague that would be severely disruptive in a manner Stag dislikes. I'm thinking that could be the kind of task that would serve the suggested role of &quot;Mystery in its own right&quot;.<br /> <br /> In a case such as that, I think one could start with the end result and work it backwards into some starting point that a mage could be made to perform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T16:06:14-07:00","id":1494818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494816#post1494816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M: Your Majesty, I beg you to grant me the boon of the Pure Sovereign Legacy.<br /> <br /> THE STAG: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">A TRUE RULER MUST GIVE EQUAL CARE AND ATTENTION TO ALL THEIR SUBJECTS, UNIFYING THEM INTO AN ORGANIC WHOLE. GATHER UNTO THYSELF A HARMONIOUS HAREM. UNDER THE SIGN OF THE HORNED GOD, GO FORTH AND ORGY.</span><br /> <br /> M: Er, your Majesty... &amp;quot;orgy&amp;quot; isn't a verb. &amp;quot;Conquer&amp;quot; might be a better choice, but the connota-<br /> <br /> THE STAG: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">DID I <i>F#(^ING </i>STUTTER?!</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Truly, the Stag does not stutter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was thinking more along the lines of turning the Mage into their catspaw of temptation.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Hey. Hey you! Yes, you! Wanna read some forbidden tomes?&amp;quot; </div> </div> </div>It sounds nice, but for me it sounds too close to what Dahhak, Aeon of Mind &amp; Space would say. Not that it\u2019s wrong, of course \u2014 I remember the Aeons being described as something along the lines of bickering siblings at one point, trying to one-up each other in purviews, so this could work well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T16:20:19-07:00","id":1494819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494818#post1494818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds nice, but for me it sounds too close to what Dahhak, Aeon of Mind &amp; Space would say. Not that it\u2019s wrong, of course \u2014 I remember the Aeons being described as something along the lines of bickering siblings at one point, trying to one-up each other in purviews, so this could work well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Dahhak would demand the Mage seek out or spread a <i>specific</i> bit of forbidden lore, ideally related to the Legacy. The Serpent would be more about facilitating impulsive behavior, such as giving into the temptation of looking at that one tome your master told you you aren't to read yet. Again, I might be assigning a bit more Serpent of Eden symbology to the Aeon than is appropriate to a shapeshifter, but spirits <i>are</i> basically just raging balls of monomaniacal, impulsive behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T19:29:04-07:00","id":1494830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494806#post1494806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe facilitating some precipitous temptation for The Serpent, although I can't quite decide if that's in-line with Spirit or just assigning too much Christian symbolism to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can solve this conundrum for you: the Aeon's name is Snake.<br /> <br /> The Aeons of the Copse are both described as intertwined ecologies \u2014 spirits being conceptual obsessives doesn't override the Shadow being a bigger picture.<br /> <br /> A thing that warrants remembering about the Aeons is that they're the Fallen World's perspective on What That Arcanum Is \u2014 Medraut is a bastard because he's the Phenomenal expression of Fate as the force that gives that famous quote from &quot;Ozymandias&quot; its punch, Typhon doesn't care about people because the way the world currently works says Death does not care, and so on.<br /> <br /> Snake not being one of the especially strongly-defined Aeons, you have some latitude in this department, but Spirit corresponds to the Path that deals in archetypes and expanded consciousness, the Pillar that corresponds to passions and connection to the wider world, and the dimension ruled by hunger and historical relationships. Prime rules the general phenomenon of &quot;things mean things&quot; that we attach to the Truth underpinning reality, but Spirit commands the Resonance that makes things read as Important. It's where cannibalism imagery lives, it's where the gods of the land emerge from, it's where the consequences of our actions go that the Nemesis blinded humanity to, and it is perennially inclined toward hybridization.<br /> <br /> Think more Ouroboros or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\">Australian Aboriginal</a> than Eden and you may have better luck getting out of the vein of &quot;the Aeon of Spirit is the Biblical Devil.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T19:52:25-07:00","id":1494831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494830#post1494830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can solve this conundrum for you: the Aeon's name is Snake.<br /> <br /> The Aeons of the Copse are both described as intertwined ecologies \u2014 spirits being conceptual obsessives doesn't override the Shadow being a bigger picture.<br /> <br /> A thing that warrants remembering about the Aeons is that they're the Fallen World's perspective on What That Arcanum Is \u2014 Medraut is a bastard because he's the Phenomenal expression of Fate as the force that gives that famous quote from &quot;Ozymandias&quot; its punch, Typhon doesn't care about people because the way the world currently works says Death does not care, and so on.<br /> <br /> Snake not being one of the especially strongly-defined Aeons, you have some latitude in this department, but Spirit corresponds to the Path that deals in archetypes and expanded consciousness, the Pillar that corresponds to passions and connection to the wider world, and the dimension ruled by hunger and historical relationships. Prime rules the general phenomenon of &quot;things mean things&quot; that we attach to the Truth underpinning reality, but Spirit commands the Resonance that makes things read as Important. It's where cannibalism imagery lives, it's where the gods of the land emerge from, it's where the consequences of our actions go that the Nemesis blinded humanity to, and it is perennially inclined toward hybridization.<br /> <br /> Think more Ouroboros or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\">Australian Aboriginal</a> than Eden and you may have better luck getting out of the vein of &quot;the Aeon of Spirit is the Biblical Devil.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you wanna stay within the realm of Judeo-Christian iconography and meaning, snakes are used in a variety of ways within the Torah and the Bible, and both Jewish and Christian temples (often in the Holy of Holies) used intertwining serpent imagery in their connection to rivers, rain, and the Milky Way as denotative of G-d's role as a celestial life giver, and even a pernicious nature ascribed to snakes can apply itself in the same way Aslan centuries later is a not a tame lion and makes no promises to not eat young girls (ie, God is a not a respecter of persons).<br /> <br /> The Edenic Serpent gets the most press because It's Right There At The Beginning, but it's hardly the sum total of thought the Abrahamic Faiths employed on snake as iconographic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-11-2022, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T20:32:03-07:00","id":1494834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494830#post1494830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can solve this conundrum for you: the Aeon's name is Snake.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I appreciate that I made an error in the name, that's a fairly pedantic correction, since it doesn't change the linguistic association. The original word for Eve's tempter is &quot;<i>N\u0101\u1e25\u0101\u0161</i>&quot;, which just means &quot;snake&quot;. Hell, &quot;Snake&quot; is just like &quot;Stag&quot; in that it's a moniker given because that's the most common form for the shapeshifting entity to be seen in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494830#post1494830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Aeons of the Copse are both described as intertwined ecologies \u2014 spirits being conceptual obsessives doesn't override the Shadow being a bigger picture.<br /> <br /> /snip/<br /> <br /> Think more Ouroboros or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\">Australian Aboriginal</a> than Eden and you may have better luck getting out of the vein of 'The Aeon of Spirit is the Biblical Devil'.</div> </div> </div> </div>The snake in the garden isn't the Devil, at least not explicitly so. At best I'd liken it to a shoulder-devil, a parable about how giving into temptation and impulse can have long-term consequences. Granted, I'm an athiest, so I have no horse in that theological race.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Snake is a shapeshifting representation of the sphere of magic that, as you said, governs associative weight and imagery. It doesn't have to be transgressive, but it can <i>absolutely </i>be a trickster-mentor if it so chooses to be at a given moment. Given that the symbolic weight given to snakes in most mythologies is some combination of healing, fertility, chaos, death, and/or rebirth, there's plenty of room for it to behave as any incarnation matches the situation. Atop that, the Shadow as a &quot;big picture&quot; is a weak argument, since that &quot;big picture&quot; is basically just a massive orgy of warring symbolism trying to survive in the most primordial sense. Their obsessions <i>define </i>how that whole realm interacts with iself and the material world, and instigating impulsive behavior is a fairly intergral aspect of life from the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494830#post1494830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing that warrants remembering about the Aeons is that they're the Fallen World's perspective on What That Arcanum Is \u2014 Medraut is a bastard because he's the Phenomenal expression of Fate as the force that gives that famous quote from &quot;Ozymandias&quot; its punch, Typhon doesn't care about people because the way the world currently works says Death does not care, and so on.<br /> <br /> Snake not being one of the especially strongly-defined Aeons, you have some latitude in this department, but Spirit corresponds to the Path that deals in archetypes and expanded consciousness, the Pillar that corresponds to passions and connection to the wider world, and the dimension ruled by hunger and historical relationships. Prime rules the general phenomenon of &quot;things mean things&quot; that we attach to the Truth underpinning reality, but Spirit commands the Resonance that makes things read as Important. It's where cannibalism imagery lives, it's where the gods of the land emerge from, it's where the consequences of our actions go that the Nemesis blinded humanity to, and it is perennially inclined toward hybridization.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are good points, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T22:11:52-07:00","id":1494838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494834#post1494834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I appreciate that I made an error in the name, that's a fairly pedantic correction, since it doesn't change the linguistic association. The original word for Eve's tempter is &quot;<i>N\u0101\u1e25\u0101\u0161</i>&quot;, which just means &quot;snake&quot;. Hell, &quot;Snake&quot; is just like &quot;Stag&quot; in that it's a moniker given because that's the most common form for the shapeshifting entity to be seen in.<br /> <br /> <br /> The snake in the garden isn't the Devil, at least not explicitly so. At best I'd liken it to a shoulder-devil, a parable about how giving into temptation and impulse can have long-term consequences. Granted, I'm an athiest, so I have no horse in that theological race.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Serpent&quot;, however, is a term that has connotations that are distinct from &quot;Snake&quot;, and in particular is used in modern and particularly pop-cultural conceptions of Christianity where in snakes are used in demonic-or-otherwise-evil contexts, and you yourself seemed to be hung up on the Edenic Serpent and it's darker thematics and tropes that you seemed to be having trouble seperating yourself from.<br /> <br /> These things stack on top of each other, and sometimes a shift of words, even if they strictly mean the same thing, can be just the to help a person break out of the rut they were trying to get out of, and firmly establishing what a thing is not alongside what it is can help to fully make the mental divide needed to make progress.<br /> <br /> I realize that it may not have been the sort of help you were looking for in making sense of your concept, but maybe don't bite helping hands regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T23:13:25-07:00","id":1494839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494838#post1494838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Serpent&quot;, however, is a term that has connotations that are distinct from &quot;Snake&quot;, and in particular is used in modern and particularly pop-cultural conceptions of Christianity where in snakes are used in demonic-or-otherwise-evil contexts, and you yourself seemed to be hung up on the Edenic Serpent and it's darker thematics and tropes that you seemed to be having trouble seperating yourself from.<br /> <br /> These things stack on top of each other, and sometimes a shift of words, even if they strictly mean the same thing, can be just the to help a person break out of the rut they were trying to get out of, and firmly establishing what a thing is not alongside what it is can help to fully make the mental divide needed to make progress.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the only time I hear the term &quot;snake&quot; applied in a positive manner is to say something is as fast as one, which is usually followed up with &quot;and twice as ornery&quot;. Every other time tends to be comparisons and allusions that have equal connotation with &quot;serpent&quot;. &quot;Trecherous snake&quot;, snake-in-the-grass&quot;, and &quot;snake-like grace&quot; come to mind.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, I view snakes and trickster-mentors in a fairly positive light, so I didn't intend for my interpretation to come off as dark.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494838#post1494838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize that it may not have been the sort of help you were looking for in making sense of your concept, but maybe don't bite helping hands regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rarely seem to agree with Satchel, and it's started to color how I read their posts as being more hostile than they are. A failing I will have to work on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T23:43:49-07:00","id":1494842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494839#post1494839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rarely seem to agree with Satchel, and it's started to color how I read their posts as being more hostile than they are. A failing I will have to work on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say this as a professional whose main body of work is with Chronicles, Satchel's pretty often right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T00:14:49-07:00","id":1494844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494806#post1494806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mordred would probably demand a betrayal,</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite like the idea of Mordred just giving a mage what they ask without getting anything in return. Make the players think that whatever the outcome, it serves his interests in some manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T17:16:46-07:00","id":1494890,"title":"","content":"Is tome of the watchtower recommended by mage fans, particularly those who focus on being players rather than GMs? All I really know is that the thrysus chapter isn't liked (which sucks since they're my favorite path thematically), but nothing else really. I don't mind if it's only an ok book, as long as it gives me a good understanding of how it feels to awaken to a path and how that form of enlightenment influences and changes a character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T17:19:47-07:00","id":1494891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494890#post1494890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is tome of the watchtower recommended by mage fans, particularly those who focus on being players rather than GMs? All I really know is that the thrysus chapter isn't liked (which sucks since they're my favorite path thematically), but nothing else really. I don't mind if it's only an ok book, as long as it gives me a good understanding of how it feels to awaken to a path and how that form of enlightenment influences and changes a character</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It was the first supplement from 1st Edition if I recall, and it has aged really poorly. Using it these days will actually just confuse the fuck out of players and really draw them from the understanding they need for 2nd Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T18:21:41-07:00","id":1494895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494891#post1494891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. It was the first supplement from 1st Edition if I recall, and it has aged really poorly. Using it these days will actually just confuse the fuck out of players and really draw them from the understanding they need for 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. Thank you for the honest answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T16:51:48-07:00","id":1494994,"title":"","content":"Dissonance erodes spells. How does it affect Imbued Items? Say I have a stone Imbued with a Persistent Levitate. If Dissonance completely erodes the spell, can the item be reactivated, or has the Imbuement been destroyed?<br /> <br /> I've been assuming the actual Imbuement is untouched, but could easily have missed something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-14-2022, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T19:48:10-07:00","id":1495000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1494994#post1494994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dissonance erodes spells. How does it affect Imbued Items? Say I have a stone Imbued with a Persistent Levitate. If Dissonance completely erodes the spell, can the item be reactivated, or has the Imbuement been destroyed?<br /> <br /> I've been assuming the actual Imbuement is untouched, but could easily have missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Imbuement is untouched. Which means that if you are a hunter that is immune to The Curse, these will seem like Lovecraftian items that inflict madness and insanity when seen in action by ordinary folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T21:46:05-07:00","id":1495002,"title":"","content":"I've been told that before that <u>Serendipity</u>'s Reach effects don't require the spell to be ongoing to take effect. That is, if I used <u>Serendipity</u> to figure out how enter a building, I don't need to maintain Advanced Duration to Occult my way in that evening. The <u>Serendipity</u> spell just sets up the dominos to toppel over from the moment it's cast.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, is <u>Reading the Outmost Eddies</u> also a fire-and-forget spell? The twist of fortune will happen once the spell has been cast, regardless of the spell's actual Duration? If so, how does that interact with the &quot;Instant-effect spells repeat their effect every [ritual interval]&quot; rule on page 113? Are you gaining a stacking &quot;charge&quot; of good fortune every [ritual interval], each of which will resolve itself within 24 hours? Because that starts to get silly at high Gnosis. <br /> <br /> Admittedly, the ramifications of a Ta'veren walking around are always fun, and it's on-brand for a Fate Mage.<br /> <br /> <i>EDIT:</i> Ah, completely overlooked Compelling vs Knowing. Makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-16-2022, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T22:47:22-07:00","id":1495004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495002#post1495002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case, is <u>Reading the Outmost Eddies</u> also a fire-and-forget spell? The twist of fortune will happen once the spell has been cast, regardless of the spell's actual Duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell's description explicitly says &quot;As log as the spell remains active,&quot; so strong odds on &quot;No, that's not how it works.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T01:53:31-07:00","id":1495056,"title":"","content":"Serendipity is a knowing spell, so once you know the thing in question the effect is lasting.<br /> <br /> Beyond that point you aren't using magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T10:21:53-07:00","id":1495126,"title":"","content":"Does the existence of a time traveler set off Peripheral Mage Sight (&quot;PMS&quot;)? Or only the act of a spell/effect at the time it sends one back/arrival? I can think of a few scenarios. For these examples Chronos, a Time mage is travelling back in time, and we're wondering if his Cabal mate Quirk is aware. <br /> <br /> a) Chronos shifts back into time one scene with Shifting Sands to a point he was with Quirk. Does Quirk's PMS ping with the arrival of Chronos into the past? <br /> b) Chronos shifts back into time one scene with Shifting Sands to a point he is alone. He then runs into Quirk while still under Shifting Sands, does this ping Quirk's PMS as an active effect?<br /> c) If Scenario B is &quot;No&quot; - Chronos is in the past under Shifting Sands. Quirk is unaware of this, Chronos does something which causes a time dilatation, does this action ping Quirk's PMS as an active effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11410-mclugh","name":"McLugh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T12:33:31-07:00","id":1495132,"title":"","content":"I'd say Peripheral Sight can feel the moment when a time travel takes place, but otherwise does nothing (barring the enhancement through a Merit or spell I recall making it more sensitive). Otherwise it's going to take Active Sight to know something is up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T00:54:37-07:00","id":1495155,"title":"","content":"I think there is a general question over peripheral mage sight. Does it ping constantly while in the presence of an 'active' spell, or just when a spell is cast?<br /> <br /> I like some middle ground, where (say) a shielding spell would trigger pms on casting and each time it shields something (ie has an active magical effect) but then you have to ask things like the above, 'would the time altering effect trigger each time a change is made?' or similarly would co-locate trigger pms each time an object is moved across to another location? (And equivalently would an object entering a portal with co-location or any arbitrary iris trigger pms?)<br /> <br /> Does activating mage armour or spending mana trigger pms? Does activating active mage sight trigger pms? If spending mana trigger pms, does pattern restoration? Or scouring? Or meditating at a Hallow/doing legacy oblations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T05:23:32-07:00","id":1495156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495155#post1495155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a general question over peripheral mage sight. Does it ping constantly while in the presence of an 'active' spell, or just when a spell is cast?<br /> <br /> I like some middle ground, where (say) a shielding spell would trigger pms on casting and each time it shields something (ie has an active magical effect) but then you have to ask things like the above, 'would the time altering effect trigger each time a change is made?' or similarly would co-locate trigger pms each time an object is moved across to another location? (And equivalently would an object entering a portal with co-location or any arbitrary iris trigger pms?)<br /> <br /> Does activating mage armour or spending mana trigger pms? Does activating active mage sight trigger pms? If spending mana trigger pms, does pattern restoration? Or scouring? Or meditating at a Hallow/doing legacy oblations?</div> </div> </div> </div>The peripheral sight triggers when anything supernatural is activated within sensory range. All of those are supernatural effects, so it triggers. The problem then is knowing the details. <br /> <br /> It could be a vampire mesmerizing someone to feed, perhaps its a deliberate move by a Banisher to see who reacts to the bait or a spirit just used an Influence. Who knows, all you know is that something supernatural happened around here (unless its a Veiling effect). Which is really nice because it means mages will pick up on very subtle uses that others will not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T07:13:27-07:00","id":1495161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495156#post1495156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The peripheral sight triggers when anything supernatural is activated within sensory range. All of those are supernatural effects, so it triggers. The problem then is knowing the details.<br /> <br /> It could be a vampire mesmerizing someone to feed, perhaps its a deliberate move by a Banisher to see who reacts to the bait or a spirit just used an Influence. Who knows, all you know is that something supernatural happened around here (unless its a Veiling effect). Which is really nice because it means mages will pick up on very subtle uses that others will not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So would the answers to my scenarios based on the above be a) Yes b) No c) Yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11410-mclugh","name":"McLugh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T10:23:07-07:00","id":1495170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495156#post1495156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The peripheral sight triggers when anything supernatural is activated within sensory range. All of those are supernatural effects, so it triggers. The problem then is knowing the details. <br /> <br /> It could be a vampire mesmerizing someone to feed, perhaps its a deliberate move by a Banisher to see who reacts to the bait or a spirit just used an Influence. Who knows, all you know is that something supernatural happened around here (unless its a Veiling effect). Which is really nice because it means mages will pick up on very subtle uses that others will not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on this, and to repeat my unanswered question, if you are sitting in a bar, a spirit uses mass influence to make everyone act in line with the spirit's influence (i dunno, violent mosh pit, drunken lechery?) As a mage your peripheral mage sight definitely goes off.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you walk into the same bar later and see the extreme behaviour of people still influenced by the spirit or drunken parties, does your peripheral mage sight go off or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T11:41:39-07:00","id":1495173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495156#post1495156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The peripheral sight triggers when anything supernatural is activated within sensory range. All of those are supernatural effects, so it triggers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an issue is a sense of ambiguity about the meaning of a power being &quot;activated&quot;. If a spell or Discipline or whatever is used to bestow a subject with increased strength, does activation mean only when the power was switched on, or does it refer to any time the strength gets used (even though the action itself might not strictly be supernatural or the activation of a power). My feeling is that the language employed tends to favour the interpretation of being reserved for the moment when an effect begins.<br /> <br /> Now that being said, Signs of Sorcery does offer that &quot;events of mystical significance&quot; can trigger Peripheral Sight on everybody within a certain radius of them; things such as a Supernal Being showing up or powerful spirit Manifesting are offered, and later on it's described as the kind of thing that can happen around Awakenings. I wouldn't say every instance of something altering the timeline counts, but at least some of them do.<br /> <br /> Hmm... for dramatic purposes, I'd be inclined to say that the Peripheral Sight of a mage does actually detect when something is making a significant alteration to their own personal timeline.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T18:56:48-07:00","id":1495211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495173#post1495173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think an issue is a sense of ambiguity about the meaning of a power being &amp;quot;activated&amp;quot;. If a spell or Discipline or whatever is used to bestow a subject with increased strength, does activation mean only when the power was switched on, or does it refer to any time the strength gets used (even though the action itself might not strictly be supernatural or the activation of a power). My feeling is that the language employed tends to favour the interpretation of being reserved for the moment when an effect begins.<br /> <br /> Now that being said, Signs of Sorcery does offer that &amp;quot;events of mystical significance&amp;quot; can trigger Peripheral Sight on everybody within a certain radius of them; things such as a Supernal Being showing up or powerful spirit Manifesting are offered, and later on it's described as the kind of thing that can happen around Awakenings. I wouldn't say every instance of something altering the timeline counts, but at least some of them do.<br /> <br /> Hmm... for dramatic purposes, I'd be inclined to say that the Peripheral Sight of a mage does actually detect when something is making a significant alteration to their own personal timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that all items touched by a time traveler become imprinted by their Nimbus. Does that mean every time they do something that diverts an item from its role in the original timeline, it triggers the peripheral sight ? Because if so, just talking to someone with a warning from the future could trigger it, making it remarkably easy to detect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T18:59:48-07:00","id":1495212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495170#post1495170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on this, and to repeat my unanswered question, if you are sitting in a bar, a spirit uses mass influence to make everyone act in line with the spirit's influence (i dunno, violent mosh pit, drunken lechery?) As a mage your peripheral mage sight definitely goes off.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you walk into the same bar later and see the extreme behaviour of people still influenced by the spirit or drunken parties, does your peripheral mage sight go off or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a yes on the first scenario and I think it doesn't trigger on the second. So much so that I remember making a Perfecting of Prime that refines the peripheral sight to trigger on supernatural effects that are passively there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T19:01:18-07:00","id":1495213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495211#post1495211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that all items touched by a time traveler become imprinted by their Nimbus.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nimbus and the marks of temporal distortion are different things, and the latter is both not a spell and specifically visible to Active Time Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T00:47:30-07:00","id":1495225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495173#post1495173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... for dramatic purposes, I'd be inclined to say that the Peripheral Sight of a mage does actually detect when something is making a significant alteration to their own personal timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that gives me an idea. Perhaps there are degrees of mage sight, like with all other senses, and the obviously supernatural things (like a spell going off, or a spirit manifesting) automatically trigger it, but for minor things, like someone with supernatural strength (6 or above) lifting a car, it would require a (wits+composure) roll to notice that something supernatural is going on... Like a twinge of your mage sight, which (because it happens all the time) you typically ignore as background noise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 10-19-2022, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T03:31:18-07:00","id":1495229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495211#post1495211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean every time they do something that diverts an item from its role in the original timeline, it triggers the peripheral sight ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving aside the mistake about Nimbuses, my take on time travel in Mage is that there isn't really a butterfly effect; the present exists in a way that the past does not, and it has a certain rigidity that withstands incidental changes. You can make those changes, but they won't innately have profound ripple effects.<br /> <br /> If you take something that was more significant, like say the gun that a mage was going to use to shoot somebody who was a danger to their agenda, than I think the mage is going to feel something happened. Although I also think timeline ripples are seen more from the present than they are the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T06:56:30-07:00","id":1495240,"title":"","content":"Would a Temporal Sympathy equivalent of Web-Weaver be viable? I like the idea, but there are flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T08:47:48-07:00","id":1495246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495240#post1495240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Temporal Sympathy equivalent of Web-Weaver be viable? I like the idea, but there are flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. Temporal Sympathy levels are given Withstand ratings to be altered, and the idea of strengthening or weakening them is described in their general section.<br /> <br /> The only thing is figuring out if a person having no Temporal Sympthy to something that they otherwise could can even really be a thing, and how it might work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T10:33:51-07:00","id":1495251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495246#post1495246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why not. Temporal Sympathy levels are given Withstand ratings to be altered, and the idea of strengthening or weakening them is described in their general section.<br /> <br /> The only thing is figuring out if a person having no Temporal Sympthy to something that they otherwise could can even really be a thing, and how it might work.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would feeling nostalgia for a thing they never were affect them? And would you be able to create a sympathy for a previous holder of the same shadow name (in a The Dread Pirate Roberts kind of way) toweave a greater narrative?<br /> <br /> Definitely some interesting potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T14:45:14-07:00","id":1495271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495251#post1495251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would feeling nostalgia for a thing they never were affect them? And would you be able to create a sympathy for a previous holder of the same shadow name (in a The Dread Pirate Roberts kind of way) toweave a greater narrative?<br /> <br /> Definitely some interesting potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could make a Sympathetic Connection (though that conflicts a bit with how Shadow Names work...), but a Temporal one seems like it might be a stretch. An interesting one, for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T16:06:09-07:00","id":1495281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495251#post1495251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would feeling nostalgia for a thing they never were affect them? And would you be able to create a sympathy for a previous holder of the same shadow name (in a The Dread Pirate Roberts kind of way) toweave a greater narrative?<br /> <br /> Definitely some interesting potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Not without the intervention of some really weird and powerful magic, or the presence of a noteworthy Mystery. The description of temporal sympathy is fairly clear and consistent about how it is a subject's sense of connection to its own past, its strength a matter of how much it has changed in the intervening time. Look at the description of even weak connections, in comparison to normal sympathy; you can form weak bonds to anything you regularly interact with that means nothing to you, but to have weak temporal sympathy to an event require a profound personal change in the meantime.<br /> <br /> I think it's part of a function of how temporal sympathy applies to a lot less than spatial. Space can be used to make a spell, any spell, affect you from any distance with greater or lesser effect from afar. Temporal sympathy is only about a select number of Time spells that connect to a subject's past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T17:45:25-07:00","id":1495287,"title":"","content":"There's also the question of whether you can make a Temporal Sympathy equivalent to Borrow Threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T17:52:52-07:00","id":1495289,"title":"","content":"Do &quot;Find the Balance&quot; (Matter 2) and Crucible (Matter 3) work on weapons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27121-hyuse","name":"Hyuse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T18:16:57-07:00","id":1495291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495287#post1495287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the question of whether you can make a Temporal Sympathy equivalent to Borrow Threads.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed</b> gives us a partial update of the Stone Scribes Legacy, and their Second Attainment (called \u201cBorrow History\u201d, appropriately enough) does exactly that. (It has a limitation where the Name Taker can\u2019t give his own connections away, but I suspect it\u2019s a Legacy quirk)<br /> <br /> So the question changes: is this Attainment example meant to indicate that Time magic can manipulate temporal sympathetic connections the same way Space does with \u2018normal\u2019 sympathetic connections (despite differences), or does it indicate that it takes a Legacy Attainment\u2019s atypicalness to do so?<br /> Probably a little bit of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T18:19:49-07:00","id":1495292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyuse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495289#post1495289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do &amp;quot;Find the Balance&amp;quot; (Matter 2) and Crucible (Matter 3) work on weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as the former should, but the latter not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T20:03:04-07:00","id":1495298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495292#post1495292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as the former should, but the latter not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I think they both can work, although not stack. A better quality gun is going to jam and deviate less, a better quality sword will hold an edge better, etc.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Stone Scribes, I feel like &quot;kicking ass and taking names&quot; is a joke that Arrow members hear quite often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T20:13:29-07:00","id":1495300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495298#post1495298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I think they both can work, although not stack. A better quality gun is going to jam and deviate less, a better quality sword will hold an edge better, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It specifies \u201cIf its primary purpose is as a tool\u201d and \u201cValuable objects\u201d, which is why I\u2019d rather not make it work on Weapon Modifiers, and thus restrict it to Equipment Bonuses and Availability. <br /> <br /> A Reach option would work, though. Or just a new Matter 3 spell \u2014 Aegis is right there as an example for Armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T20:34:03-07:00","id":1495301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495300#post1495300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It specifies \u201cIf its primary purpose is as a tool\u201d and \u201cValuable objects\u201d, which is why I\u2019d rather not make it work on Weapon Modifiers, and thus restrict it to Equipment Bonuses and Availability.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I may interject, the most common definition of a weapon is a tool used to injure another. I feel like it creates a bit too much complication when one rules a fire axe can only split wood more easily, rather than also splitting people. It\u2019s just a bit much for a generic improvement spell. It\u2019s really not a big deal though, especially when one can make a more specific spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T15:42:48-07:00","id":1495331,"title":"","content":"How does Spell Potion deal with multiple targets?<br /> <br /> EG - I cast Spell Potion with a duration of one week on five bottles of water, then cast Invisibility with a duration of one hour into those 5 bottles. All good so far.<br /> <br /> But Spell Potion says that &quot;the cast spell does not take effect until the item is ingested&quot;. Does this mean that all 5 bottles of water need to be drunk, or just one? They are technically separate targets of the spell.<br /> If it's the case that only one is required to be drunk, what happens to the duration? Since Invisibility is technically one spell with 5 targets, does the spells duration begin for all of the bottles of water once one of them is drunk, or does each of them have it's own separate duration?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-20T16:10:45-07:00","id":1495332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495331#post1495331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Spell Potion deal with multiple targets?<br /> <br /> EG - I cast Spell Potion with a duration of one week on five bottles of water, then cast Invisibility with a duration of one hour into those 5 bottles. All good so far.<br /> <br /> But Spell Potion says that &amp;quot;the cast spell does not take effect until the item is ingested&amp;quot;. Does this mean that all 5 bottles of water need to be drunk, or just one? They are technically separate targets of the spell.<br /> If it's the case that only one is required to be drunk, what happens to the duration? Since Invisibility is technically one spell with 5 targets, does the spells duration begin for all of the bottles of water once one of them is drunk, or does each of them have it's own separate duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Knee-jerk response would be \u201cCount them separately in all cases\u201d, but we\u2019ll have to reread the book for a clearer picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T02:19:39-07:00","id":1495350,"title":"","content":"How feasible is an instant death/euthanasia Death spell short of Making? Something along the lines of a Weaving/Perfecting spell that only works on those suffering from a certain type and/or amount of damage a la Devouring the Slain. Obviously withstood, probably by Stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T03:09:44-07:00","id":1495351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495350#post1495350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How feasible is an instant death/euthanasia Death spell short of Making? Something along the lines of a Weaving/Perfecting spell that only works on those suffering from a certain type and/or amount of damage a la Devouring the Slain. Obviously withstood, probably by Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm thinking of a spell whose base effect is that it accelerates the rate at which lethal damage rolls over into aggravated when somebody is incapacitated, with a Reach effect that allows one to target those who are dying in a more narrative sense to let them slip away immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T16:10:57-07:00","id":1495384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495350#post1495350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How feasible is an instant death/euthanasia Death spell short of Making? Something along the lines of a Weaving/Perfecting spell that only works on those suffering from a certain type and/or amount of damage a la Devouring the Slain. Obviously withstood, probably by Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1495383#post1495383\">this</a> be along the lines of what you are looking for ? Its the closest thing I could think of that mechanically matched the intent, with some additional inspiration from SCP-4999.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-21-2022, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T17:15:00-07:00","id":1495387,"title":"","content":"Pinoccheo question. Say a Mage creates a humanoid Golem, then uses Pattening to transmute it into a flesh-and-blood human. Is the resultant &quot;human&quot; Soulless? I assume yes, but am not sure if it's actually a human or just a biological Golem at that point. Come to think of it, could you use Golem on a corpse, or is that too far outside of Matter's wheelhouse and too far into Death's?<br /> <br /> If it is indeed Soulless, and you attach a soul to the Golem, what happens once the Patterning spell ends? Does the soul behave as if the owner had just died? Or do you now have a Golem with a soul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T17:34:42-07:00","id":1495390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495387#post1495387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pinoccheo question. Say a Mage creates a humanoid Golem, then uses Pattening to transmute it into a flesh-and-blood human. Is the resultant &quot;human&quot; Soulless?<br /> I assume yes, but am not sure if it's actually a human or just a biological Golem at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>My general assumption would be that turning something into a human wholesale with Patterning instead of functionally turning it mostly human in a piecemeal fashion via Weaving effects turns it into a Soulless human, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Come to think of it, could you use Golem on a corpse, or is that too far outside of Matter's wheelhouse and too far into Death's? </div> </div> </div>Golem works on objects. A sufficiently processed corpse might be symbolically distinct from a corpse, but a regular dead body is A Dead Body, not a meat-sculpture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is indeed Soulless, and you attach a soul to the Golem, what happens once the Patterning spell ends? Does the soul behave as if the owner had just died? </div> </div> </div>Same thing that happens if a spell making a subject a valid target for another spell ends: the spell remains, but stops meaningfully doing anything \u2014 Soul Jar is active, but it no longer has a person-body to bind the soul to, so it's no longer able to bind the soul to the body, so the soul is released as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T17:35:51-07:00","id":1495391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495387#post1495387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pinoccheo question. Say a Mage creates a humanoid Golem, then uses Pattening to transmute it into a flesh-and-blood human. Is the resultant &quot;human&quot; Soulless? I assume yes, but am not sure if it's actually a human or just a biological Golem at that point. Come to think of it, could you use Golem on a corpse, or is that too far outside of Matter's wheelhouse and too far into Death's?<br /> <br /> If it is indeed Soulless, and you attach a soul to the Golem, what happens once the Patterning spell ends? Does the soul behave as if the owner had just died? Or do you now have a Golem with a soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>The golem would be soulless.<br /> <br /> I would say you can use Golem on a corpse - death can already do basically the same thing but with Weaving instead of Patterning, there's nothing wrong with Matter being able to do it with slightly more difficulty from a different angle.<br /> <br /> See Satchel's answer. I also don't think you could fit a soul in a mindless golem, even if it had a human body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26659,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","user":"TakWrote","date":". 10-21-2022, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T17:58:43-07:00","id":1495395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495390#post1495390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same thing that happens if a spell making a subject a valid target for another spell ends: the spell remains, but stops meaningfully doing anything \u2014 Soul Jar is active, but it no longer has a person-body to bind the soul to, so it's no longer able to bind the soul to the body, so the soul is released as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more along the lines of Soul Jar's Lasting Reach, in which case the soul is anchored to the body without the spell needing to continue facilitating. But since the transmutation ending effectively &quot;kills&quot; the &quot;human&quot;, I'm assuming you would still rule in favor of the Soul vanishing as per normal &quot;death&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T18:35:24-07:00","id":1495397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495395#post1495395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more along the lines of Soul Jar's Lasting Reach, in which case the soul is anchored to the body without the spell needing to continue facilitating. But since the transmutation ending effectively &quot;kills&quot; the &quot;human&quot;, I'm assuming you would still rule in favor of the Soul vanishing as per normal &quot;death&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the event that the soul has been permanently rendered as belonging to the person that now no longer exists, yes, that would be the way I would run it in the absence of unusual circumstances to further complicate the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T02:45:02-07:00","id":1495409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495384#post1495384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1495383#post1495383\">this</a> be along the lines of what you are looking for ? Its the closest thing I could think of that mechanically matched the intent, with some additional inspiration from SCP-4999.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more like Isator's suggestion than mine, but it's a good idea too. The Palliated Condition is also pretty interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","user":"Obsidian Pharaoh","date":". 10-22-2022, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T21:32:41-07:00","id":1495511,"title":"","content":"In the 1st Edition a Mage could create (Heat, Light, Sound) with 3 dots, and (Electricity, Fire) with 4 dots. Does that still applies to the 2nd Edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","user":"Phillip Morin","date":". 10-24-2022, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","name":"Phillip Morin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T21:44:24-07:00","id":1495512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495511#post1495511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the 1st Edition a Mage could create (Heat, Light, Sound) with 3 dots, and (Electricity, Fire) with 4 dots. Does that still applies to the 2nd Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating anything from nothing is 5-dot now, but manipulating it or controling it is 1-dot and 2-dot respectively. Oversimplification, but at 3 and 4 you can amplify or reduce the phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T23:32:49-07:00","id":1495513,"title":"","content":"Can an Artifact and a Grimoire be made into Dedicated Tools?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","user":"Phillip Morin","date":". 10-24-2022, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","name":"Phillip Morin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T00:23:22-07:00","id":1495514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495513#post1495513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can an Artifact and a Grimoire be made into Dedicated Tools?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as they meet the definition of &quot;Order Tool&quot; or &quot;Path Tool&quot;, I don't see why not. Picking up Broad Dedication might be a good idea tho","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T14:46:06-07:00","id":1495690,"title":"","content":"What are Omphalos Stones and what do they do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","name":"Phillip Morin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-27T16:23:55-07:00","id":1495693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495690#post1495690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Omphalos Stones and what do they do?</div> </div> </div> </div>An omphalos stone is a fragment of the stone heart of a Pangaean, primal divinities from the Border Marches that once bridged the worlds of Flesh and Shadow; they serve as the basis for powerful demesnes, being immune to Dissonance and giving the benefits of a Praxis to spells cast from their Arcanum, being effectively the soul stones of gods. The first of them were given to pre-Sundering Awakened as gifts, though later specimens were taken by force.<br /> <br /> They're a setting element in the chronologically earliest Dark Era in Dark Eras 1, The Sundered World, which concerns itself with the Neolithic Vinca civilization of around 5500-5000 BCE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T10:22:13-07:00","id":1495764,"title":"","content":"I was re-reading Nameless and Accursed, and I have a question concerning Tremere Houses having weaknesses<br /> <br /> What would be the watsonian answer as to why twisting the legacy makes a weakness? This can be open ended and multiple answers, I don't mind. I know it's probably as simple as &quot;twisting the Legacy warps the symbolism provided&quot; but a regular Legacy is the shaping of a soul that yet doesn't cause weakness, only strengths and a likelihood for Obsessions related to the Legacy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T16:04:49-07:00","id":1495790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495764#post1495764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was re-reading Nameless and Accursed, and I have a question concerning Tremere Houses having weaknesses<br /> <br /> What would be the watsonian answer as to why twisting the legacy makes a weakness? This can be open ended and multiple answers, I don't mind. I know it's probably as simple as &quot;twisting the Legacy warps the symbolism provided&quot; but a regular Legacy is the shaping of a soul that yet doesn't cause weakness, only strengths and a likelihood for Obsessions related to the Legacy</div> </div> </div> </div>The Watsonian reason is right there: the Tremere don't have souls, so they have to symbolically reshape their selves in other ways.<br /> <br /> Presumably this is metaphysical neighbors with the reasons why vampires pick up banes from joining bloodlines, werewolves take bans with their membership in packs and lodges, deviants need Scars to develop their Variations, changelings gain new weak points in their Clarity with entitlements, and demons just plain demonstrate their individuality with glitches more readily as their Primum rises; lacking souls of their own, the Tremere presumably don't have a proper Name that their identity derives from, but the described effects of a character's Gnosis on the soul they possess fill a similar role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T20:54:03-07:00","id":1495796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495790#post1495790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Watsonian reason is right there: the Tremere don't have souls, so they have to symbolically reshape their selves in other ways.<br /> <br /> Presumably this is metaphysical neighbors with the reasons why vampires pick up banes from joining bloodlines, werewolves take bans with their membership in packs and lodges, deviants need Scars to develop their Variations, changelings gain new weak points in their Clarity with entitlements, and demons just plain demonstrate their individuality with glitches more readily as their Primum rises; lacking souls of their own, the Tremere presumably don't have a proper Name that their identity derives from, but the described effects of a character's Gnosis on the soul they possess fill a similar role.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, let me put it this way<br /> <br /> As an Order that believes itself superior, how would a tremere made explain the weakness derived from making a legacy into a House?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T22:37:48-07:00","id":1495800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495796#post1495796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true, let me put it this way<br /> <br /> As an Order that believes itself superior, how would a tremere made explain the weakness derived from making a legacy into a House?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The existential tyranny of the Five Dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T05:57:02-07:00","id":1495821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495796#post1495796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, let me put it this way<br /> <br /> As an Order that believes itself superior, how would a tremere made explain the weakness derived from making a legacy into a House?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;To sustain ultimate truth, a Tremere gives up their soul. After that sacrifice, the willworker has the right to any soul they can seize, to study and sacrifice to the great hunger of magic: the entropy that creates beauty.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;As long as a Tremere exists, their sacrifices and insights make them superior to all other Awakened.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Tremere believe they've opened themselves up to an aspect of the world not limited to the safe and the freely available \u2014 the weakness of a House is merely the price of gaining the power of an additional Legacy on a single being's Gnosis-equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T07:20:42-07:00","id":1495827,"title":"","content":"Is there a set appearance for how Prime constructs like Eidolon and Platonic Form manifest? Without the Forces conjunctive effect its &quot;obvious&quot; that the object is magical, but does that mean Halo-esque hard-light constructs? Or does it vary by Mage/Path/Order/Legacy? Acanthus weaving silver spider-silk would be kinda neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T10:35:49-07:00","id":1495837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495827#post1495827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a set appearance for how Prime constructs like Eidolon and Platonic Form manifest? Without the Forces conjunctive effect its &quot;obvious&quot; that the object is magical, but does that mean Halo-esque hard-light constructs? Or does it vary by Mage/Path/Order/Legacy? Acanthus weaving silver spider-silk would be kinda neat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An Obrimos could make one that ripples with visible waves of the music of the spheres, another has a form that seems to be fluidly burning with the fire of truth. One Mastigos makes them looks like a sculpture made of endless bundled chains, another has demonic faces running through its surface. An Acanthus might weave one of silver threads, yet another manifests it as a crystal with a transparent skin covering the clockwork beneath. One mage uses a scrying pool by projecting the image on the water's surface, another makes a drop float and grow into a scrying window, a third has it emit mist and projects the 3D hologram on the water vapor, and another makes it glow and manifest an Iron Man holographic interface screen.<br /> <br /> While the mechanical principals are always the same, the manifestation of Awakened magic depends on the individual, how discrete they are trying to be and how they think about magic in general. So personal flare is very much a thing and is another reason to make mages appear even more diverse and unique to an uninitiated observer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-29-2022, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T14:04:09-07:00","id":1495846,"title":"","content":"I generally just imagine Prime constructs looking like the kind of magic in the Doctor Strange movies. I picture it as a fairly universal thing, because I think that's in keeping with Prime's themes of being something essential and elemental. Like, it's manipulating Mana stripped to the bones, and in that case forming it into something like the framework upon which phenomena sits.<br /> <br /> Kind of make it a more iridescent colour than the orangey-red in the movies, but otherwise no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T15:15:56-07:00","id":1495849,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Imago, and i tend to imagine them being like green lantern powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T17:01:51-07:00","id":1495856,"title":"","content":"What would be necessary to disable the ability to read or understand language, as a guard against forbidden knowledge or mental commands? A Weaving ? Ruling ? Patterning ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T18:30:23-07:00","id":1495857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495856#post1495856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be necessary to disable the ability to read or understand language, as a guard against forbidden knowledge or mental commands? A Weaving ? Ruling ? Patterning ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime Veiling to hide, Fraying to disable. Basically replicates the Bable curse, by hiding the meaning of symbols. Can also be achieved with Mind Veiling and Fraying.<br /> Pretty sure an example rote is on the Creative Thaumaturgy thread somewhere.<br /> Edit: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=941606#post941606\">Here</a> is one example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 10-29-2022, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T18:39:52-07:00","id":1495858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495857#post1495857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime Veiling to hide, Fraying to disable. Basically replicates the Bable curse, by hiding the meaning of symbols. Can also be achieved with Mind Veiling and Fraying.<br /> Pretty sure an example rote is on the Creative Thaumaturgy thread somewhere.<br /> Edit: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=941606#post941606\">Here</a> is one example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perfect, thank you. A very nice way to deal with Lovecraftian secrets, Abyssal memes and other cognitohazards. Excellent gateway spells for Abyssal hunters, Censorea curators and a response, or pathway, to the Logophages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-30-2022, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T18:53:43-07:00","id":1495859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495849#post1495849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the Imago</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the imago can determine what specific thing it is, but there's still a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quiddity\" target=\"_blank\">quiddity</a> to a thing that determines its form when produced by magic. Like, if you transform something into a cat or make one whole cloth, you can determine many of the parameters of its appearance, but it still needs to have features within the range of what a cat is.<br /> <br /> A construct woven of the prima materia might be up to the imagination of the player, but I think that once they decide on what that is it ought to be firmly set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T14:43:56-07:00","id":1495912,"title":"","content":"Does One Mind Two Thoughs give you two ongoing thought-tracks for the Duration, or do you need to reactivate it every time you start a new task? I lean towards ongoing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T15:38:38-07:00","id":1495917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495912#post1495912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does One Mind Two Thoughs give you two ongoing thought-tracks for the Duration, or do you need to reactivate it every time you start a new task? I lean towards ongoing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ongoing, the spell is Compelling the brain's ability to multitask, allowing it to hold multiple threads and making switching between them much easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T01:24:29-07:00","id":1495947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495859#post1495859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the imago can determine what specific thing it is, but there's still a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quiddity\" target=\"_blank\">quiddity</a> to a thing that determines its form when produced by magic. Like, if you transform something into a cat or make one whole cloth, you can determine many of the parameters of its appearance, but it still needs to have features within the range of what a cat is.<br /> <br /> A construct woven of the prima materia might be up to the imagination of the player, but I think that once they decide on what that is it ought to be firmly set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean at one table eidolons look like Dr Strange 'obviously magic', at another the might look like Green Lantern 'obvious magic.<br /> <br /> As opposed to, at my table, describe how your Eidolon looks obviously magical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T01:51:48-07:00","id":1495952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495856#post1495856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be necessary to disable the ability to read or understand language, as a guard against forbidden knowledge or mental commands? A Weaving ? Ruling ? Patterning ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e Mind 4 spell Confuse Language (from Banishers) does just that, depriving the subject of the abstract concept of language: they can't read, write, speak, or understand language, including High Speech. I think porting it over basically as is to 2E works fine. It's an Unraveling spell, though, which is what I believe such a sweeping excision should fall under.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T09:21:22-07:00","id":1495977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495952#post1495952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an Unraveling spell, though, which is what I believe such a sweeping excision should fall under.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure if that is correct. Now I\u2019m not a Neurologist, but language is a taught skill. If not taught early on, language can be a difficult concept to grasp. If one wishes to lower another\u2019s skill at something, it would be to be similar to lowering one\u2019s attributes, since 2e doesn\u2019t differentiate like 1e. Now 2e doesn\u2019t seems to have a example lowering skill spell, but it does have a increase skill spell and a lower attribute spell. Interestingly, both have a minimum of one dot, where Befuddle can not lower from, nor can Enhance Skill increase without a minimum one dot. Which leads me to my question:<br /> <br /> Can a hypothetical Mind Fraying spell reduce skill dots to 0 and inflict the untrained penalty for the duration of the spell?<br /> <br /> If it can, then Fraying should be able to remove a Language without issue. Even if it can\u2019t, Universal Language is weaving. A inverse of that would still strike me as Fraying. <br /> <br /> \u200bAs a side note, if one wanted to inflict a nasty persistent condition based on Aphasia, that absolutely requires Unraveling. But that seems like overkill for protection from dangerous information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T13:46:05-07:00","id":1496006,"title":"","content":"I think spells can lower Skills to zero, although I have a hard time justifying why you can't then lower Attributes to zero. Different symbolism, since dropping to zero is effectively a death-blow, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T14:08:24-07:00","id":1496008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496006#post1496006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think spells can lower Skills to zero, although I have a hard time justifying why you can't then lower Attributes to zero. Different symbolism, since dropping to zero is effectively a death-blow, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since lowering an Attribute to 0 would definitely mess someone up (even if the spell isnt permanent), maybe it would call for a Reach and a Mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T06:19:34-07:00","id":1496034,"title":"","content":"Can multiple ephemeral entities posses the same victim simultaneously?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T07:23:26-07:00","id":1496036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496034#post1496034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can multiple ephemeral entities posses the same victim simultaneously?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean. A single subject can have multiple instances of the Anchor/Resonant Condition, each tagged to multiple entities. Said multiple entities could all use the Fetter Manifestation to give themselves the Fetter Condition and the subject the Urged Condition.<br /> <br /> A victim could then have multiple instances of the Open Condition, but since \u2018natural\u2019 Opens require the subject and the entity to act in concert for some time, this likely does not occur naturally. (But then again, mages.)<br /> <br /> The Possessed Condition, triggered by the Possess Manifestation, is worded such to be likely intended for one entity at a time. Maybe multiple entities could cycle through the poor victim?<br /> <br /> The Controlled Condition is a bridge to the Claimed Condition and pretty much nothing else; same rules as Open should apply. And we know the Hive-Claimed exist for the Claimed Condition, which is an aberration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T09:56:57-07:00","id":1496051,"title":"","content":"Technically yes, because Spiral exists. But since the process to create that Hive-Claimed is being done by a very powerful, highly dedicated Rapt, its probably not something accomplished without dedicated research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T13:36:29-07:00","id":1496061,"title":"","content":"So &quot;no&quot;, for most instances. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> Large Legacies often have their own Tenemos realm. Orders should plausibility have ones. Do Paths? I <i>think</i> they would...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T13:57:07-07:00","id":1496062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496061#post1496061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So &quot;no&quot;, for most instances. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> Large Legacies often have their own Tenemos realm. Orders should plausibility have ones. Do Paths? I <i>think</i> they would...</div> </div> </div> </div>Every idea which at least two humans* have discussed has a (however minor) Temenotic realm, so yes. Paths realms would be fairly big (compared to legacy realms).<br /> <br /> *Including mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 11-01-2022, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T14:26:01-07:00","id":1496065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496034#post1496034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can multiple ephemeral entities posses the same victim simultaneously?</div> </div> </div> </div>Elaborating a little bit, and because some of the exploration is a little buried, it's <i>rare</i>, but it can and does happen. Chris Allen <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1350475-a-present-for-merry-wolfenoot?p=1357051#post1357051\">talks about the case for spirits.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-01T17:07:52-07:00","id":1496074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496061#post1496061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So &quot;no&quot;, for most instances. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> Large Legacies often have their own Tenemos realm. Orders should plausibility have ones. Do Paths? I <i>think</i> they would...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Temenos conceptual realms include every magical tradition ever practiced by more than one person. Various regions belong to <b>Paths,</b> Orders, Legacies, and other cults. The groups so represented take particular interest in these realms, often protecting them with spells and magical guardians.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2e Core, page 248, in the book's section on the Astral discussing the Temenos in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T00:02:50-07:00","id":1496090,"title":"","content":"Are spells casts in Verges not subject to Dissonance? And those cast in a Desmene? Does Paradox stills applies as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","user":"Phillip Morin","date":". 11-02-2022, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","name":"Phillip Morin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T00:32:10-07:00","id":1496091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496090#post1496090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are spells casts in Verges not subject to Dissonance? And those cast in a Desmene? Does Paradox stills applies as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dissonance protection only applies to natural Verges. And the paradox protection only applies if A) the spell doesn't leave the Verge/Demense and B) a sleeper isn't present for the spell's duration*.<br /> <br /> *Some people interpret this differently, as paradox dice roll happens before the spell's duration begins, and so mechanically what happens when a sleeper will appear is not clearly written out. <br /> <br /> One option is to take the spell's casting time, the other is to retroactively apply paradox after the spell is cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T00:47:01-07:00","id":1496093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496091#post1496091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the other is to retroactively apply paradox after the spell is cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you choose to retroactively apply Paradox to a spell somebody cast that didn't Reach at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T02:25:45-07:00","id":1496098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496093#post1496093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you choose to retroactively apply Paradox to a spell somebody cast that didn't Reach at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, i would not retroactively apply paradox at all. But that is just my table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T16:13:36-07:00","id":1496231,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit to the number of familiars you can have? And their Rank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","name":"Phillip Morin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T17:23:52-07:00","id":1496233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496231#post1496231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a limit to the number of familiars you can have? And their Rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>In pages 101 and 183 of the core book, it states that Familiars can be of Rank 2 at most. There is no limit the amount of familiars a mage can have, save for how high the scale of the <i>Familiar</i> spell they can obtain, how many times they purchase the merit or successfully perform the binding ritual (described in <i>Witchfinders</i> and costing a Willpower dot).<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that it is a willing bond and can be terminated at any time. This means there is a shared interest, like mutual protection, a trade of favors for Essence and many more. Moreover, spirits operate with a very different logic than humans, a known familiar can damage the mage's reputation if left to their own devices and they are Connected sympathetic links that a Space practitioner can exploit. Not to mention ex familiars may have privileged information on the mage.<br /> <br /> In summary, managing a large familiar network requires a very diplomatic, careful and and prevident mage. Its certainly doable, its also a path to great versatility and mana reserves, but it requires a whole lot of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T10:14:17-07:00","id":1496258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496233#post1496233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">successfully perform the binding ritual (described in <i>Witchfinders</i> and costing a Willpower dot).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think something in a Hunter: the Vigil supplement is applicable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T16:01:46-07:00","id":1496280,"title":"","content":"What is the difference between MtAw Tremere and VtR Tremere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27614-phillip-morin","name":"Phillip Morin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27614_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T17:14:55-07:00","id":1496281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496280#post1496280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the difference between MtAw Tremere and VtR Tremere?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Tremere in VtR?<br /> <br /> The ones in MtAw are intuitive masters of the soul without one of their own\u2026because they ate theirs. Or maybe sacrificed it to a broken Watchtower. Amounts to the same thing really. They like to chew on or eat more souls for more life, especially those of formerly human supernatural creatures because they are extra tasty, and are much more powerful. <br /> <br /> (If you meant Vampire the Masquerade Tremere, they are a clan of vampires who do blood magic. The difference between them and the ones in Awakening is that the Awakening ones are more powerful and aren\u2019t Vampires. They don\u2019t really have a link each other than draining life force of some kind.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T19:39:42-07:00","id":1496283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496281#post1496281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are Tremere in VtR?<br /> <br /> The ones in MtAw are intuitive masters of the soul without one of their own\u2026because they ate theirs. Or maybe sacrificed it to a broken Watchtower. Amounts to the same thing really. They like to chew on or eat more souls for more life, especially those of formerly human supernatural creatures because they are extra tasty, and are much more powerful. <br /> <br /> (If you meant Vampire the Masquerade Tremere, they are a clan of vampires who do blood magic. The difference between them and the ones in Awakening is that the Awakening ones are more powerful and aren\u2019t Vampires. They don\u2019t really have a link each other than draining life force of some kind.)</div> </div> </div> </div>They do have a link, in the in VtM House Tremere were originally mages who sought immortality. Or were losing their powers as consensual reality changed and so they tried stealing immortality from vampires... Which destroyed the spark of their awakening.<br /> <br /> The MtAw Tremere also start as mages and lose something to gain immortality. Both also have to feed, one on souls the other on blood. I suspect they both have timelines for their creation which line up, but i don't know when either were (Roughly Dark Ages in VtM).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T20:47:47-07:00","id":1496284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phillip Morin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496280#post1496280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the difference between MtAw Tremere and VtR Tremere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clan Tremere are magical vampires. <br /> <br /> Tremere Liches are vampiric mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T13:07:03-08:00","id":1496328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1495387#post1495387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pinoccheo question. Say a Mage creates a humanoid Golem, then uses Pattening to transmute it into a flesh-and-blood human. Is the resultant &quot;human&quot; Soulless? I assume yes, but am not sure if it's actually a human or just a biological Golem at that point. Come to think of it, could you use Golem on a corpse, or is that too far outside of Matter's wheelhouse and too far into Death's?<br /> <br /> If it is indeed Soulless, and you attach a soul to the Golem, what happens once the Patterning spell ends? Does the soul behave as if the owner had just died? Or do you now have a Golem with a soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Inverse of one of my previous questions - say you use Patterning to temporarily transform a person into a Goetia or Spirit, or petrify them into a statue. Is the Soul intergrated into the transformation, or does the victim become Soulless once the transformation ends? Or would it be a factor determined by the caster's Imago?<br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelated - Permenance stipulates that Matter must be the highest Arcana used in the spell for the Utility Attainment to apply. This means that a Matter 5 + Space 5 spell wouldn't be eligible, correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-06-2022, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T17:37:47-08:00","id":1496350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496328#post1496328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Inverse of one of my previous questions - say you use Patterning to temporarily transform a person into a Goetia or Spirit, or petrify them into a statue. Is the Soul intergrated into the transformation, or does the victim become Soulless once the transformation ends? Or would it be a factor determined by the caster's Imago?<br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelated - Permenance stipulates that Matter must be the highest Arcana used in the spell for the Utility Attainment to apply. This means that a Matter 5 + Space 5 spell wouldn't be eligible, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>In reverse order. A matter 5 + space 5 spell has both Matter and Space as the highest arcanum. Not sure how i would apply this to the attainment.<br /> <br /> I think a person turned into a Goetia or Spirit still has a soul, they only lose it if they die, and i think the 'living' part of them is still there (even if you patterned it into Mind/Spirit arcanum). <br /> <br /> Unless you intentionally kill them as part of the process. Like my favourite spell Eidolon (Prime 4/5, Life 4) turn a person into a living mana pattern, does it still have the properties of a living being (needs to sleep and eat - regained willpower from sleeping) or does your imago make all Life functions completely redundant (no need to sleep, no regaining willpower, no need to eat, just gains mana from some oblation to refuel?).<br /> <br /> I think the latter could be seen as being no longer alive, and thus lose their soul (though i would lean towards not taking their soul) while the former still has a lot of Life in their pattern... <br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could try to pattern the soul itself. But that is a whole other fish kettle.<br /> <br /> Alternatively alternatively, you could have the soul R\u00e9altrach itself when they become alive again, because nobody knows what happens to souls, so \u00af\u2060\\\u2060_\u2060(\u2060\u30c4\u2060)\u2060_\u2060/\u2060\u00af","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T19:23:49-08:00","id":1496355,"title":"","content":"Does a Mage's signature Nimbus fade after a week (or more at higher Gnosis) or remain available, via focused mage sight/revelation, as surface information (unless cast as a rote) for as long as the spell is active?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T19:30:07-08:00","id":1496357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496355#post1496355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Mage's signature Nimbus fade after a week (or more at higher Gnosis) or remain available, via focused mage sight/revelation, as surface information (unless cast as a rote) for as long as the spell is active?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an active spell retains the Nimbus. I'm not sure if relinquishing it causes the connection to steadily dim into something resembling a Rote's casting, but an active spell that is still in the Mage's spell control still has a strong connection to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T21:45:32-08:00","id":1496372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496328#post1496328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inverse of one of my previous questions - say you use Patterning to temporarily transform a person into a Goetia or Spirit, or petrify them into a statue. Is the Soul intergrated into the transformation, or does the victim become Soulless once the transformation ends? Or would it be a factor determined by the caster's Imago?</div> </div> </div> </div>In these particular examples, the limits of Patterning come into play \u2014 Morpheans and spirit mages being extraordinary means of evading death are a prime example of how making somebody exist in Mind or Spirit-based Twilight doesn't turn them into an ephemeral being and making an ephemeral being out of designated remnants of oneself is a more lasting process. The subject of the spell is still a human with a non-Lasting spell holding them in an ephemeral state, and the soul can manage to be in a human temporarily occupying a non-human state,<br /> <br /> Same deal with &quot;turning someone into a statue&quot; except easier: they're not a statue, their flesh has been turned to stone and possibly their mind has been shut down. Soul's still in there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unrelated - Permenance stipulates that Matter must be the highest Arcana used in the spell for the Utility Attainment to apply. This means that a Matter 5 + Space 5 spell wouldn't be eligible, correct? </div> </div> </div>The spirit of the language is very much &quot;this is here to let your Matter effects last a long time, not to bootstrap spell effects with no relation to the qualities of matter into safer indefinite Duration by happening to include Matter in them.&quot; Interpret based on what the spell does accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T22:08:24-08:00","id":1496373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496372#post1496372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirit of the language is very much &quot;this is here to let your Matter effects last a long time, not to bootstrap spell effects with no relation to the qualities of matter into safer indefinite Duration by happening to include Matter in them.&quot; Interpret based on what the spell does accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>An extraplanar base was the impetus, so effectively Ex Nihilo contained within Pocket Dimension. Everywhere can manage the Scale either way, and Permenance would free up a further Reach, but it's fairly debatable about whether Matter is prominent enough in that combo to warrant Permenance. <br /> <br /> Ship in furniture, plants, and the like later, but give some substance to the nightmare-void of base Pocket Dimension in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-07-2022, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T03:10:56-08:00","id":1496385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496373#post1496373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An extraplanar base was the impetus, so effectively Ex Nihilo contained within Pocket Dimension. Everywhere can manage the Scale either way, and Permenance would free up a further Reach, but it's fairly debatable about whether Matter is prominent enough in that combo to warrant Permenance. <br /> <br /> Ship in furniture, plants, and the like later, but give some substance to the nightmare-void of base Pocket Dimension in the meantime.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can cast pocket dimension, you can cast from a (temporary) pocket dimension and not worry about reach - though i dislike this, 'spells cast inside a pocket dimension do not incur paradox' is RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T09:19:53-08:00","id":1496398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496373#post1496373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An extraplanar base was the impetus, so effectively Ex Nihilo contained within Pocket Dimension. Everywhere can manage the Scale either way, and Permenance would free up a further Reach, but it's fairly debatable about whether Matter is prominent enough in that combo to warrant Permenance. <br /> <br /> Ship in furniture, plants, and the like later, but give some substance to the nightmare-void of base Pocket Dimension in the meantime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe cast it combined with a Making of Matter that creates [Potency] dots of Safe Place. That way both get the benefits of Durability and your base is well defended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T16:08:16-08:00","id":1496419,"title":"","content":"Can you <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1468420-2e-legacy-optional-attaiments\">refund praxes that are identical to an attainment optional effect</a>?<br /> <br /> You can refund an attainment if you have it as a praxis, but can you <b>also </b>refund the optional effect if you have it as a praxis?<br /> <br /> I have heard &quot;No, because it is a complementary effect of the singular attainment that you buy&quot;, or &quot;Yes, you can refund it as it is a distinct attainment on itself&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-07-2022, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T16:14:18-08:00","id":1496420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496419#post1496419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1468420-2e-legacy-optional-attaiments\">refund praxes that are identical attainments optional effects</a>?<br /> <br /> You can refund an attainment if you have it as a praxis, but can you <b>also </b>refund the optional effect if you have it as a praxis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Regurgitating my opinion from the other thread; If your table rules that you have to buy Optional Attainments separately from the primary Attainments, then yes to a refund. If no, then no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T19:57:36-08:00","id":1496452,"title":"","content":"Silly question, but can Matter Veiling make a object look like a different shape than it really is or larger or smaller?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T20:54:07-08:00","id":1496454,"title":"","content":"<u>Shrink and Grow</u> is Weaving... but that <i>actually</i> changes the size.<br /> <u>Shaping</u> is Ruling... but that legit reshapes the object.<br /> <u>Hidden Hoard</u> is Veiling... but all that does is remove the conceptual tag of &quot;thing&quot; from the target, for the purposes of human perception<br /> <br /> Gaaaah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-08-2022, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T21:00:52-08:00","id":1496455,"title":"","content":"Well, I figure if it\u2019s just a illusion it should be able to mimic the appearance of another spell. I mean it\u2019s really not different from making a illusion of a object that isn\u2019t there. But I don\u2019t know if my logic holds up outside of my head.<br /> <br /> Edit: the example spells I was remembering don\u2019t seem to be a thing. I\u2019m not sure where I got it from then. I thought you could do stuff like make a animal noises with Life, or false spatial distortions with Space. I guess not though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 11-08-2022, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T21:51:09-08:00","id":1496457,"title":"","content":"The only examples of Matter Veiling we have published are <u>Hidden Hoard</u> and <u>Machine Invisibility.</u> Hidden Hoard works by removing the conceptual indexing tag that designates a target as an object. That is, if the Supernal/Astral/Human mind is a search index, Hidden Hoard is deleting the means of referencing that item.<br /> <br /> Maybe a reasonable facsimile would be to use Veiling to change what the tag presents as? Like, designate an apple as an orange, and everyone perceives it as such? I'm pretty sure there was an SCP like that... Anyway, the question then is if that's a Veiling effect, a Weaving effect, or a Patterning effect. Probably also depends on if you're borrowing the tag from an existing example or not...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-08-2022, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T02:53:44-08:00","id":1496474,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's any reason why Veiling of Matter wouldn't be able to make objects seem to be something other than they are. It seems like a basic application of that Practice to that Arcanum, and I don't think it's as if it would alter the parameters of how the object can actually be used. Like how you can make something invisible but it remains tangible; I'm picturing carrying an item through a hole it shouldn't be able to fit in being perceived by a Sleeper, and it conveys the meaning of Dissonance.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking such a spell should have limits on the range of false information it conveys based on Potency, and that the base form should require it looking like a modified version of the same object without Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T18:00:49-08:00","id":1496564,"title":"","content":"<u>One Mind, Two Thoughts</u> allows you to conduct up to two mental actions simultaniously. Is there a reasonable way to increase this number? Add a Reach effect to make it [Potency] actions?<br /> <br /> Not intended as a power-gaming question, I'm just tinkering with the idea of a Legacy that uses Forces-hologram duplicates, which you have to puppet like marionettes. Being able to control one per thought-track seemed like a neat trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T09:36:27-08:00","id":1496604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496564#post1496564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>One Mind, Two Thoughts</u> allows you to conduct up to two mental actions simultaniously. Is there a reasonable way to increase this number? Add a Reach effect to make it [Potency] actions?<br /> <br /> Not intended as a power-gaming question, I'm just tinkering with the idea of a Legacy that uses Forces-hologram duplicates, which you have to puppet like marionettes. Being able to control one per thought-track seemed like a neat trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of two 1e space spells, but looking at them, they basically required mind 1 or 3 for multitasking. Which i think suggests a mind weaving spell, but I'm not sure that is valid in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T13:22:39-08:00","id":1496632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496564#post1496564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>One Mind, Two Thoughts</u> allows you to conduct up to two mental actions simultaniously. Is there a reasonable way to increase this number? Add a Reach effect to make it [Potency] actions?<br /> <br /> Not intended as a power-gaming question, I'm just tinkering with the idea of a Legacy that uses Forces-hologram duplicates, which you have to puppet like marionettes. Being able to control one per thought-track seemed like a neat trick.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since its duration primary, just increasing potency should allow them to further multitask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T01:39:23-08:00","id":1496676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496604#post1496604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of two 1e space spells, but looking at them, they basically required mind 1 or 3 for multitasking. Which i think suggests a mind weaving spell, but I'm not sure that is valid in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to have a look at those, mind sharing their names and/or which books they were in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496632#post1496632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since its duration primary, just increasing potency should allow them to further multitask.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not confident on that, given the spell description specifically says &quot;two&quot;, and doesn't make provisions for increasing that number. On the other hand, Occam's Razor.<br /> <br /> <u>Shadow Crafting</u> can create solid, 3d objects. Is it reasonable to use Matter spells like <u>Golem</u> on those creations? Similarly, would a Death version of <u>Golem</u> be plausible, if cast on a shadow-crafted object?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-10-2022, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T04:00:11-08:00","id":1496682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496676#post1496676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to have a look at those, mind sharing their names and/or which books they were in?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are in the core book, and are called Co-location (Spaces 4) p239 and Manifold Presence (Space 5 + Life 4 or 5 and optional Matter 5 and/or Mind 1 or 3 conjunctional) p242<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <u>Shadow Crafting</u> can create solid, 3d objects. Is it reasonable to use Matter spells like <u>Golem</u> on those creations? Similarly, would a Death version of <u>Golem</u> be plausible, if cast on a shadow-crafted object? </div> </div> </div>I would say that symbolically they are still shadows and thus not in the purview of Matter.<br /> <br /> A Death version of Golem would be reasonable, partly because they is a Death (and Prime) equivalent... Notably, for Prime (pure mana into Tass retainers) it requires Making, Golems are easier with Matter, Death has zombies which are easier again (presumably because they are animated corpses, not animated statues).<br /> <br /> Maybe Shadows are harder to animate than corpses, but are they as hard as Statues or Tass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T04:09:43-08:00","id":1496684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496682#post1496682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are in the core book, and are called Co-location (Spaces 4) p239 and Manifold Presence (Space 5 + Life 4 or 5 and optional Matter 5 and/or Mind 1 or 3 conjunctional) p242</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof, 1e spells are <i>weird</i>. Looks like the Mind optionals are integrating 1e's <u>One Mind Two Thoughts</u> and the direct upgrade <u>Multitasking</u>. 2e has <u>Multitasking</u> already is mostly subsumed into <u>One Mind Two Thoughts</u>, so that's unfortunately not much help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1496682#post1496682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that symbolically they are still shadows and thus not in the purview of Matter.<br /> <br /> A Death version of Golem would be reasonable, partly because they is a Death (and Prime) equivalent... Notably, for Prime (pure mana into Tass retainers) it requires Making, Golems are easier with Matter, Death has zombies which are easier again (presumably because they are animated corpses, not animated statues).<br /> <br /> Maybe Shadows are harder to animate than corpses, but are they as hard as Statues or Tass?</div> </div> </div> </div><u> Quickened Corpses</u> have a direct connection to animate life (that is, they were once in that state), so they just need to be Weaved into an echo of their previous state of being. <br /> <br /> <u>Golems</u> have physical form, but never directly lived as autonomous entities. So they just need to be Patterned into having a facsimile of life. <br /> <br /> <u>Eidolons</u> get forged whole-cloth. Making makes sense.<br /> <br /> Going off those tiers, Shadow-Golem seems like it would work as a Death Adept spell. The animated medium already exists, but never lived.<br /> <br /> My purposes will focus on shadows solidified via <u>Shadow Crafting</u>, but you could probably just Golemize a bog-standard shadow, huh? <u>Shadow Sculpting's</u> Reach effect already sets the precedent for making shadow-puppets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-10-2022, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T14:29:09-08:00","id":1496936,"title":"","content":"If a mage goes invisible and inaudible in combat, do they get to ignore defense if their location is not detected ? Does the same apply for going back into stealth after launching an ambush ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T15:33:12-08:00","id":1496944,"title":"","content":"I would selectively apply the effects of the Blinded and Deafened tilts to combat rolls relating to those specific characters.<br /> <br /> Ie -2 on all dice rolls and -5 on all rolls requiring vision and loses defence against this one attacker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T20:54:58-08:00","id":1496957,"title":"","content":"Matter can refine objects into Perfect versions of their composite materials. Should Perfected amber be treated like Perfected gems? Or maybe Perfected wood? You could almost argue it's the fossilized bones of trees, but that's a real long stretch of logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T21:14:00-08:00","id":1496958,"title":"","content":"It should be treated as a Perfected Gemstone. It\u2019s pretty much just a pretty and interesting stone, despite it\u2019s organic origins. Now I don\u2019t know how Perfected resins since those would be different things, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T22:05:40-08:00","id":1497067,"title":"","content":"While <u>Know Nature</u> is a useful spell, is it useful enough to use as a Legacy Attainment? You'd need to put it in the Disciple slot for any meaningful utility (Cast instantly and at sight range, granting you knowledge of Aspirations and Obsessions), but would it see enough use to justify being at the point in a Legacy where most characters will plateau? It's a good tool for figuring out how to leverage someone around to your side of an argument, but at Mind 3/Gnosis 4-5 you could cast it as a spell just as easily and with little to no consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T02:05:38-08:00","id":1497077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497067#post1497067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While <u>Know Nature</u> is a useful spell, is it useful enough to use as a Legacy Attainment? You'd need to put it in the Disciple slot for any meaningful utility (Cast instantly and at sight range, granting you knowledge of Aspirations and Obsessions), but would it see enough use to justify being at the point in a Legacy where most characters will plateau? It's a good tool for figuring out how to leverage someone around to your side of an argument, but at Mind 3/Gnosis 4-5 you could cast it as a spell just as easily and with little to no consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would dispute that it needs so much reach, think about how certain organisations offer a 'personality test' to get you in the door, that could be ritual casting speed, sensory range. Or i have seen Hakomi Body Psychotherapy, (or just simple massage therapy) which would allow touch range, ritual duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T02:13:46-08:00","id":1497078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497077#post1497077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would dispute that it needs so much reach, think about how certain organisations offer a 'personality test' to get you in the door, that could be ritual casting speed, sensory range. Or i have seen Hakomi Body Psychotherapy, (or just simple massage therapy) which would allow touch range, ritual duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ritual Casting speed for an Attainment is a Scene though, that's not exactly a flexible utility. And I still can't quite decide if it's worth making into an Attainment. The benefits seem... minimal.<br /> <br /> Like, Life's equivalent (<u>Analyze Life</u>) gives you a rundown of physical Tilts, Conditions, illnesses, Attributes, and if the target is a (non-mage) Supernatural. Even if you have to do that at Touch Range or at Ritual Casting, that's pretty useful. You can use it on yourself if nothing else. <u>Know Nature</u> is only useful if used on other people, and while Vitrue and Vice <i>can</i> be useful, there aren't many instances where you could get much use out of it while also conforming to a long Casting time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-14-2022, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T03:39:24-08:00","id":1497083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497078#post1497078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ritual Casting speed for an Attainment is a Scene though, that's not exactly a flexible utility. And I still can't quite decide if it's worth making into an Attainment. The benefits seem... minimal.<br /> <br /> Like, Life's equivalent (<u>Analyze Life</u>) gives you a rundown of physical Tilts, Conditions, illnesses, Attributes, and if the target is a (non-mage) Supernatural. Even if you have to do that at Touch Range or at Ritual Casting, that's pretty useful. You can use it on yourself if nothing else. <u>Know Nature</u> is only useful if used on other people, and while Vitrue and Vice <i>can</i> be useful, there aren't many instances where you could get much use out of it while also conforming to a long Casting time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the utility for an attainment for that would mean it would only be useful for a kind of specialised mystery Cult/legacy where that scene was built into their processes. <br /> <br /> It is not a fleeting thing, i can imagine a seer legacy using it during negotiations to gain the upper hand. Or the Ebon Phoenix legacy using it to help fix people. I don't think it works well as a third level attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T03:51:42-08:00","id":1497084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497067#post1497067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While <u>Know Nature</u> is a useful spell, is it useful enough to use as a Legacy Attainment? You'd need to put it in the Disciple slot for any meaningful utility (Cast instantly and at sight range, granting you knowledge of Aspirations and Obsessions), but would it see enough use to justify being at the point in a Legacy where most characters will plateau? It's a good tool for figuring out how to leverage someone around to your side of an argument, but at Mind 3/Gnosis 4-5 you could cast it as a spell just as easily and with little to no consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Legacy Attainment, we can make the actual effect a bit more \u2018flexible\u2019. Such as\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2022 It can be used in casual conversational distance, without putting Reach to sensory range.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Alternatively to the above, specify it\u2019s an Aimed spell, and let the automatic activation apply to the Aiming roll too.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The +1 option\u2019s effects (read Aspirations/Obsessions) replace the normal effect.<br /> <br /> \u2022 As an ST, rule that NPCs are much more prone to acting according to their Vice or Virtue, whether it\u2019ll grant them Willpower or not, such that the normal effects allows you to predict their future actions and motives with high accuracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-14T04:02:45-08:00","id":1497085,"title":"","content":"Being able to see Aspirations and Obsessions is far more useful, because those are always in flux. But if people know what you are capable of learning, then they will be loath to shake hands. So sensory range would be needed. Since that pushes it to the third Attainment, its just not the best option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T03:01:48-08:00","id":1497167,"title":"","content":"<u>Reaping Relinquishment</u>'s Prime expansion allows you to sacrifice a soulstone, rather than a whole soul. Does that cause the victim to be forever diminished, never able to grow past Gnosis 9?<br /> <br /> EDIT: soulstones are a renewable energy source!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-15-2022, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T03:14:15-08:00","id":1497168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497167#post1497167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Reaping Relinquishment</u>'s Prime expansion allows you to sacrifice a soulstone, rather than a whole soul. Does that cause the victim to be forever diminished, never able to grow past Gnosis 9?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it's not the spell that destroys the soul stone, destroying the soul stone simply follows the rules for how you decide to break it.<br /> I view it a lot like the Sacrament Yantra. The act of breaking something is what powers the spell, not the object itself, thus the remains of the object doesn't lose any spiritual power or meaning. It's just broken in the way that you broke it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T03:03:45-08:00","id":1497519,"title":"","content":"<u>Turn Momentum</u>'s spell description says <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The spell allows the mage to turn a number of moving objects up to Potency. </div> </div> </div>Is that meant to be read as &quot;[Potency] objects per turn&quot;, or &quot;this spell has [Potency] charges, and ends early if they're all used&quot;? I've been assuming the former, but it reads like the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T05:50:14-08:00","id":1497528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497519#post1497519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that meant to be read as &quot;[Potency] objects per turn&quot;, or &quot;this spell has [Potency] charges, and ends early if they're all used&quot;? I've been assuming the former, but it reads like the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The former. It's a Potency-primary spell with a Reach option for reflexive use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T12:53:22-08:00","id":1497556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497528#post1497528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The former. It's a Potency-primary spell with a Reach option for reflexive use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not per turn, per Instant action - which becomes per reflexive action with a reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T13:08:19-08:00","id":1497560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497556#post1497556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not per turn, per Instant action - which becomes per reflexive action with a reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but an instant action consumes your whole turn in combat, which made it a good shorthand to explain my question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T13:35:45-08:00","id":1497563,"title":"","content":"PMS's description says that any effect that conceals an thing doesn't ping PMS. Does this mean a Hidden Hoard concealing poison won't be picked up by PMS?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T13:51:27-08:00","id":1497564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497563#post1497563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PMS's description says that any effect that conceals an thing doesn't ping PMS. Does this mean a Hidden Hoard concealing poison won't be picked up by PMS?</div> </div> </div> </div>Veiling spells that are directly scrutinized trigger a Clash of Wills, but otherwise are below notice. Page 92 has the exact mechanics","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T14:29:35-08:00","id":1497567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497560#post1497560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, but an instant action consumes your whole turn in combat, which made it a good shorthand to explain my question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, it is just that per turn, and duration spell factors, and even scale (for number of subjects affected) all are used in a weird way in this spell. <br /> <br /> The subject seems to be the mage, who gains a once per turn ability, which is [potency] limited. And the subject has this ability every turn for the duration of the spell, but only if they would otherwise be using defence (or dodging for advanced duration??)...ie you can't (for some reason) turn momentum on incoming bullets being fired at somebody else?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the size of the turned objects is also limited by the scale factor... Which is just weird if the turned objects aren't the spell's subject...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T19:07:27-08:00","id":1497601,"title":"","content":"How do artificial spirits/ghost/goetia interact with Dissonance? Obviously if they Manifest without Mortal Mask, they're going to be eroded, but what about using influences and Numina? Is an artifical ghost using the Telekinesis Numen in the presence of a Sleeper being subjected to Dissonance, even if they're otherwise imperceptible to the Sleeper?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T19:21:09-08:00","id":1497602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497601#post1497601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do artificial spirits/ghost/goetia interact with Dissonance? Obviously if they Manifest without Mortal Mask, they're going to be eroded, but what about using influences and Numina? Is an artifical ghost using the Telekinesis Numen in the presence of a Sleeper being subjected to Dissonance, even if they're otherwise imperceptible to the Sleeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dissonance is only for Supernal/Abyssal stuff, iirc.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, misread the question. Still, even a Supernally created ephemeral\u2019s Influences/Numina should be fine I believe. Just as how a Supernally ignited fire\u2019s heat can still kill you, even if the original flame gets Dissonance\u2019d away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-20T13:45:14-08:00","id":1497662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497602#post1497602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dissonance is only for Supernal/Abyssal stuff, iirc.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, misread the question. Still, even a Supernally created ephemeral\u2019s Influences/Numina should be fine I believe. Just as how a Supernally ignited fire\u2019s heat can still kill you, even if the original flame gets Dissonance\u2019d away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat. Dancing Blades are a go then.<br /> <br /> <u>Levitation</u>, especially with the free-flight option, out-and-out replaces your Speed rather than directly enhancing it. Can <u>Ground-Eater</u> supplement that flying speed, or does it count as stat-stacking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-20T18:27:39-08:00","id":1497687,"title":"","content":"What (in game) would mean to have a high (5) Egregore merit, but low (1) Order status in the Mysterium? 1e had the Egregore rating dependent on Order status value, but now those are independent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-20T18:45:23-08:00","id":1497689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497687#post1497687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What (in game) would mean to have a high (5) Egregore merit, but low (1) Order status in the Mysterium? 1e had the Egregore rating dependent on Order status value, but now those are independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You are a clever cookie, apprentice, truely worthy of the deep knowledge we keep. But you lack the administrative skills necessary to run our office on a day to day basis, so sit in the corner until we call you, ok?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-20T18:57:30-08:00","id":1497692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497687#post1497687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What (in game) would mean to have a high (5) Egregore merit, but low (1) Order status in the Mysterium? 1e had the Egregore rating dependent on Order status value, but now those are independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can, for whatever ridiculous reason led to this circumstance, be considered a local bottom-rung member of the Order no matter which Caucus you're in, along with knowing your own Libraries and getting Informed about the local Order membership, being able to get in touch with any Order member you can get a sympathy Yantra for, and being able to benefit better from teamwork casting with other egregori. Possibly you never wanted to stop being an Acquisitor and weren't fussed about getting access to higher-level requisitions.<br /> <br /> Generally, though the fact that the second benefit of Egregore is &quot;your Mysterium Status doesn't degrade in effectiveness with range from your home Caucus&quot; means this should be a non-issue in practice, subject to the same sanity check as &quot;yes, sure, you have the Experience to justify buying Status: United States Senate, but how are you justifying that?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T04:00:23-08:00","id":1497707,"title":"","content":"I would go with it as an idea that the mystagogue in question manages to have an intuitive sense for the full depths of the Order's mysticism that an appropriate mentor decided to nurture, even if they haven't yet gotten the experience or developed the capabilities that allow them to rise from the position of somebody who needs their research assigned and guided by a superior up to the level of being able to conduct independent inquiries and being part of the caucus's decision making body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T08:16:31-08:00","id":1497713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497689#post1497689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You are a clever cookie, apprentice, truely worthy of the deep knowledge we keep. But you lack the administrative skills necessary to run our office on a day to day basis, so sit in the corner until we call you, ok?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. Yeah, I thought about lack of administrative power on the order but in-depth understanding of the ethos.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497707#post1497707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go with it as an idea that the mystagogue in question manages to have an intuitive sense for the full depths of the Order's mysticism that an appropriate mentor decided to nurture, even if they haven't yet gotten the experience or developed the capabilities that allow them to rise from the position of somebody who needs their research assigned and guided by a superior up to the level of being able to conduct independent inquiries and being part of the caucus's decision making body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. It aligns to what Cauthon said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497692#post1497692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can, for whatever ridiculous reason led to this circumstance, be considered a local bottom-rung member of the Order no matter which Caucus you're in, along with knowing your own Libraries and getting Informed about the local Order membership, being able to get in touch with any Order member you can get a sympathy Yantra for, and being able to benefit better from teamwork casting with other egregori. Possibly you never wanted to stop being an Acquisitor and weren't fussed about getting access to higher-level requisitions.<br /> <br /> Generally, though the fact that the second benefit of Egregore is &quot;your Mysterium Status doesn't degrade in effectiveness with range from your home Caucus&quot; means this should be a non-issue in practice, subject to the same sanity check as &quot;yes, sure, you have the Experience to justify buying Status: United States Senate, but how are you justifying that?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. Man, not to sound confrontational, but this is the second or third time you answer a comment of mine so... dismissively. Are there any issues between us that should be addressed?<br /> <br /> I ask in good faith and you are one of the most active people answering, so it grates the frequency that this has been happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-21-2022, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T10:52:52-08:00","id":1497733,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Honestly, I think if Orders have much in the way of administrative work, that's largely done by the Sleepwalkers anyway. The qualifications for being able to run something in a group like the Mysterium aren't in office work, they're in the guidance of new initiates and conferring with fellows to coordinate research and make decisions about affairs related to interaction with other Orders.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497713#post1497713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, not to sound confrontational, but this is the second or third time you answer a comment of mine so... dismissively. Are there any issues between us that should be addressed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's nothing specific to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T13:41:11-08:00","id":1497750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497662#post1497662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neat. Dancing Blades are a go then.<br /> <br /> <u>Levitation</u>, especially with the free-flight option, out-and-out replaces your Speed rather than directly enhancing it. Can <u>Ground-Eater</u> supplement that flying speed, or does it count as stat-stacking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that this should work. Ground-eater is folding Space, so each step covers more ground, Levitation makes you cross space faster. No reason you can cast Ground-eater with a Plane/Car as the subject, so i don't think i would apply the stat stacking rules in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T13:47:38-08:00","id":1497752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497733#post1497733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's nothing specific to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always find it weird how often people seem to read hostility in Satchel's posts way more than he applies it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T13:56:56-08:00","id":1497753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497752#post1497752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always find it weird how often people seem to read hostility in Satchel's posts way more than he applies it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may have to do with;<br /> <br /> A) You know them better than most of us do, since you apparently game together<br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> B) Word choice matters when attempting to convey tone through text, and a lack of positive modifiers stands out just as sharply as purely negative ones. Satchel's posts tend to read as neutral. At best. &quot;You are incorrect. This is my list of why.&quot; Vs &quot;I see where you're coming from, but here's where that doesn't hold up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Satchel isn't in any way obligated to change how they talk, obviously. But it seems like this is a trend more of presentation than interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-21-2022, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T14:51:35-08:00","id":1497755,"title":"","content":"If a Combined Spell is being cast, and the caster spends the Reach to have each spell's Scale separated, how do you calculate the final dice pool for the spell? Do you charge dice for Scale twice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T16:20:39-08:00","id":1497760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497755#post1497755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Combined Spell is being cast, and the caster spends the Reach to have each spell's Scale separated, how do you calculate the final dice pool for the spell? Do you charge dice for Scale twice?</div> </div> </div> </div>No definitive answer, but I suspect so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T03:53:49-08:00","id":1497789,"title":"","content":"How much Sympathy (if any) would a key have for a matching lock? Drafting a keyring that opens portals between doors whose keys are on the ring, but I'm not sure what the Withstand would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T07:23:51-08:00","id":1497797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497789#post1497789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Sympathy (if any) would a key have for a matching lock? Drafting a keyring that opens portals between doors whose keys are on the ring, but I'm not sure what the Withstand would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how they were constructed, I think.<br /> <br /> If there's only one key per lock, each constructed specifically for the other, Strong sympathy.<br /> If there's a master key, or more than one key for the lock, Medium sympathy.<br /> If lock or key are generic, with hundreds or thousands of keys that would open the lock, Weak sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26659,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","user":"TakWrote","date":".  Added weak. 11-22-2022, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T09:30:53-08:00","id":1497805,"title":"","content":"What happens to the original primary spell factor values when switching Primary spell factors?<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting the Odds</b> has primary factor Duration.<br /> <br /> It has an alternative function that you can use no more than Potency times.<br /> <br /> A Gnosis 1, Fate 3 mage casts the spell and uses one reach for Instant Casting and one for Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> As described: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What potency value does the spell have?</li> <li>If <i>instead </i>of Advanced Duration, he reaches to switch primary factor to Potency, what is the duration of the spell?</li> <li>If he uses <i>extra </i>reach to switch primary factor to Potency, what happens to the duration of the spell?</li> <li>How many reach do I need both effects (find specific thing and access to temporary Merits) + instant casting + advanced duration?</li> </ol><br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-22-2022, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T10:20:31-08:00","id":1497810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497805#post1497805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to the original primary spell factor values when switching Primary spell factors?<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting the Odds</b> has primary factor Duration.<br /> <br /> It has an alternative function that you can use no more than Potency times.<br /> <br /> A Gnosis 1, Fate 3 mage casts the spell and uses one reach for Instant Casting and one for Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> As described:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What potency value does the spell have?</li> <li>If <i>instead </i>of Advanced Duration, he reaches to switch primary factor to Potency, what is the duration of the spell?</li> <li>If he uses <i>extra </i>reach to switch primary factor to Potency, what happens to the duration of the spell?</li> <li>How many reach do I need both effects (find specific thing and access to temporary Merits) + instant casting + advanced duration?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm misunderstanding the spell factor system...<br /> <br /> Potency is 1 by default, if no dice are sacrificed to increase it.<br /> <br /> The duration of the spell would be one turn, if no dice are sacrificed to increase it.<br /> <br /> The duration of the spell would be one hour/scene, if no dice are sacrificed to increase it.<br /> <br /> Instant casting is 1, advanced duration is 1, for a total of 2 reach needed. As an ST, I would probably rule that RAW you'd need to combine two castings of the spell because the merit effect is an <i>alternative</i> to finding the specific thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T10:50:50-08:00","id":1497816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497789#post1497789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Sympathy (if any) would a key have for a matching lock? Drafting a keyring that opens portals between doors whose keys are on the ring, but I'm not sure what the Withstand would be.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497797#post1497797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how they were constructed, I think.<br /> <br /> If there's only one key per lock, each constructed specifically for the other, Strong sympathy.<br /> If there's a master key, or more than one key for the lock, Medium sympathy.<br /> If lock or key are generic, with hundreds or thousands of keys that would open the lock, Weak sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathy is described exclusively between two people or between one person and an object. I don't think it's intended that two objects can't have sympathy, but since neither is capable of forming emotional bonds (which is the most common source for sympathetic connections), the strength of the link should naturally be quite limited.<br /> <br /> A lock and a matching key would probably not have a sympathetic connection at all unless they're used together quite often, in which case it should be weak. It's much more likely that whoever holds the key has a connection to both the key and the lock than them having a connection to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T11:11:44-08:00","id":1497817,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Serendipity</b> has primary factor Potence, it has extra reach effects that refer to skill usage. The spell is not lasting, so those effects require recasting (or having active) the spell before using a skill, right?</li> <li>If the primary factor is of a spell is Potence, can you use advanced duration WITHOUT switching the primary factor to Duration? If so, how many reach do you need for it?</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 11-22-2022, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T11:32:01-08:00","id":1497819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497789#post1497789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Sympathy (if any) would a key have for a matching lock? Drafting a keyring that opens portals between doors whose keys are on the ring, but I'm not sure what the Withstand would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>A pair of wedding rings has a Medium connection (Mage the Awakening, p. 173). P. 172 specifies that a strong physical connection can also create sympathy. I would argue that a key and it's lock aren't much different sympathetically than a pair of wedding rings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T12:19:06-08:00","id":1497825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497819#post1497819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A pair of wedding rings has a Medium connection (Mage the Awakening, p. 173). P. 172 specifies that a strong physical connection can also create sympathy. I would argue that a key and it's lock aren't much different sympathetically than a pair of wedding rings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an example of items with strong emotional ties, so a person usually have a medium strength connection to their own wedding ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T12:30:18-08:00","id":1497828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497825#post1497825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an example of items with strong emotional ties, so a person usually have a medium strength connection to their own wedding ring.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I misread the paragraph. Apologies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T13:36:43-08:00","id":1497839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497817#post1497817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Serendipity</b> has primary factor Potence, it has extra reach effects that refer to skill usage. The spell is not lasting, so those effects require recasting (or having active) the spell before using a skill, right?</li> <li>If the primary factor is of a spell is Potence, can you use advanced duration WITHOUT switching the primary factor to Duration? If so, how many reach do you need for it?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Seems so. <br /> <br /> 2. Yup, access to Advanced spell factors have nothing to do with primary spell factors. Just spend 1 Reach. (Though this leaves you at Advanced Duration 1 = 1 scene/hour, so spend some dice to get days, weeks, etc.) (And indefinite Duration requires 1 Reach for accessing Advanced Duration <i>and</i> +1 Reach for a total of 2 Reach <i>and</i> -10 dice <i>and</i> 1 Mana).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T13:46:06-08:00","id":1497842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497839#post1497839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Seems so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm 99% sure that as a Knowing spell, the omens you receive are Lasting knowledge than you can leverage on the one relevant roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T13:51:49-08:00","id":1497843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497842#post1497842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm 99% sure that as a Knowing spell, the omens you receive are Lasting knowledge than you can leverage on the one relevant roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I see it, the knowledge of \u201cI can do This particular thing in That innovative way\u201d is lasting, but ability to answer \u201cCan I do This any other way\u201d is not.<br /> <br /> I.e. only one roll per casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T14:03:47-08:00","id":1497846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497843#post1497843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I see it, the knowledge of \u201cI can do This particular thing in That innovative way\u201d is lasting, but ability to answer \u201cCan I do This any other way\u201d is not.<br /> <br /> I.e. only one roll per casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it as the spell giving the character a brace of symbolism to interpret, which the player gets to define after the fact. That is, if my character wants access to the Blue Sun City Library's restricted section, and I as the player want to substitute, say, Survival, then the omens are something like <br /> <br /> &quot;The knowledge you seek dwells in the house of the azure sun. The gatekeeper can be circumvented through a test of the wilds&quot;. <br /> <br /> It's vague enough to be applied to whatever way you want to interpret the roll (the Librarian you talk to is a doomsday prepper who can be convinced to bend the rules for a &quot;fellow survivalist&quot;, for example), but you still only have that one instance where the knowledge can be reliably applied to a roll. If you botch the roll, you don't get to reuse the substitution and try again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-22-2022, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T14:15:25-08:00","id":1497848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497846#post1497846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read it as the spell giving the character a brace of symbolism to interpret, which the player gets to define after the fact. That is, if my character wants access to the Blue Sun City Library's restricted section, and I as the player want to substitute, say, Survival, then the omens are something like <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The knowledge you seek dwells in the house of the azure sun. The gatekeeper can be circumvented through a test of the wilds&amp;quot;. <br /> <br /> It's vague enough to be applied to whatever way you want to interpret the roll (the Librarian you talk to is a doomsday prepper who can be convinced to bend the rules for a &amp;quot;fellow survivalist&amp;quot;, for example), but you still only have that one instance where the knowledge can be reliably applied to a roll. If you botch the roll, you don't get to reuse the substitution and try again</div> </div> </div> </div>Which\u2026 doesn\u2019t collide with what said, I think?<br /> <br /> No wait, I think I got this \u2014 I say we need to recast the spell because I assume we only ask this question (of whether we need to recast or not) when the Potency \u2018charges\u2019 are all spent. You assume we still have some left. Was this the issue all along?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T14:28:51-08:00","id":1497850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497848#post1497848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which\u2026 doesn\u2019t collide with what said, I think?<br /> <br /> No wait, I think I got this \u2014 I say we need to recast the spell because I assume we only ask this question (of whether we need to recast or not) when the Potency \u2018charges\u2019 are all spent. You assume we still have some left. Was this the issue all along?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yyyyyyes, more or less. The original question was<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Serendipity</b> has primary factor Potence, it has extra reach effects that refer to skill usage. The spell is not lasting, so those effects require recasting (or having active) the spell before using a skill, right?</li> </ol> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Which I read as &quot;the character used <u>Seredipity</u> but didn't make use of the substitution before the spell's Duration elapsed, do they need to recast to keep benefiting?&quot;* To which I say no, since <u>Serendipity</u> is simply producing knowledge you then need to act on to benefit from. <br /> <br /> Your response was &quot;Seems so&quot;, which I interpreted as meaning your stance is needing to have the spell up to use a substitution</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">* <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a>, can you confirm/deny?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T14:50:43-08:00","id":1497851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497850#post1497850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yyyyyyes, more or less. The original question was<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Which I read as &quot;the character used <u>Seredipity</u> but didn't make use of the substitution before the spell's Duration elapsed, do they need to recast to keep benefiting?&quot;* To which I say no, since <u>Serendipity</u> is simply producing knowledge you then need to act on to benefit from.<br /> <br /> Your response was &quot;Seems so&quot;, which I interpreted as meaning your stance is needing to have the spell up to use a substitution</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">* <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a>, can you confirm/deny?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it is weird then since I cast to say use Any skill... Before knowing which skill I will use in that future situation. So, that is why I assumed I got to recast the spell.<br /> <br /> What about a complementary question. If I cast <b>Serendipity </b>WITHOUT using the skill usage capabilities, and after, when the situation arises I want to get the effect of skill substitution, does recasting suffices or I have to make do as it is?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T14:56:00-08:00","id":1497852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497851#post1497851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but it is weird then since I cast to say use Any skill... Before knowing which skill I will use in that future situation. So, that is why I assumed I got to recast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. That's where you have to separate mechanics from character. Your <i>character</i> isn't choosing to use the Survival Skill in my example, they're asking for a method that will play to their strengths. The <i>p</i><i>layer</i> is specifying that it'll be a Survival roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497851#post1497851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a complementary question. If I cast <b>Serendipity </b>WITHOUT using the skill usage capabilities, and after, when the situation arises I want to get the effect of skill substitution, does recasting suffices or I have to make do as it is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would allow recasting with the Reach effect to work. &quot;My first try didn't work. Fate! I call for your aid!&quot; or &quot;I'm not confident I'm charismatic enough for this. Fate! How can I resolve this with my muscles?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T15:50:07-08:00","id":1497859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497755#post1497755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Combined Spell is being cast, and the caster spends the Reach to have each spell's Scale separated, how do you calculate the final dice pool for the spell? Do you charge dice for Scale twice?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that a combined spell is meant to be two effects with the same spell factors so they both have the same scale, potency, duration etc. which allows you calculate the dice pool (-2 dice pool per combined spell).<br /> <br /> But as said elsewhere, the rules are unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T17:54:04-08:00","id":1497872,"title":"","content":"There was a 1e Legacy that involved slowly becoming a spirit. You took a totem and gained influences and I can't seem to find it anywhere anymore, does anyone remember what they were called and/or what sourcebook they were in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T18:35:02-08:00","id":1497875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497872#post1497872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a 1e Legacy that involved slowly becoming a spirit. You took a totem and gained influences and I can't seem to find it anywhere anymore, does anyone remember what they were called and/or what sourcebook they were in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Katsinam Suukya, from Summoners, beginning on page 195.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T22:44:52-08:00","id":1497880,"title":"","content":"This may be a strange question, but are there any rules for how diseases spread in CoD? I want to make a <u>Contagion</u> illness that spreads along Sympathetic Connections, with stronger connections being more virulent vectors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Contagion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;she must target some form of carrier depending on the disease\u2019s transmission methods (water, food, living hosts). It\u2019s contagious as soon as the mage creates it, requiring a reflexive Stamina + Resolve roll, modified by the Severity, to resist contracting it. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>From that I assume any exposure to a given vector causes the same Stamina + Resolve roll, so a Sympathy-based Illness would trigger the roll whenever interacting with and infected Connection. Does that seem accurate?<br /> <br /> <br /> Tangentially related - if you use <u>Borrow Threads</u> (Stealing, not copying) and then use <u>Cut Threads</u> on those stolen connections, are they then severed for the original owner when <u>Borrow Threads</u> ends?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-23-2022, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T23:10:31-08:00","id":1497881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497805#post1497805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to the original primary spell factor values when switching Primary spell factors?<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting the Odds</b> has primary factor Duration.<br /> <br /> It has an alternative function that you can use no more than Potency times.<br /> <br /> A Gnosis 1, Fate 3 mage casts the spell and uses one reach for Instant Casting and one for Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> As described: <br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What potency value does the spell have?</li> <li>If <i>instead </i>of Advanced Duration, he reaches to switch primary factor to Potency, what is the duration of the spell?</li> <li>If he uses <i>extra </i>reach to switch primary factor to Potency, what happens to the duration of the spell?</li> <li>How many reach do I need both effects (find specific thing and access to temporary Merits) + instant casting + advanced duration?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497810#post1497810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I'm misunderstanding the spell factor system...<br /> <br /> Potency is 1 by default, if no dice are sacrificed to increase it.<br /> <br /> The duration of the spell would be one turn, if no dice are sacrificed to increase it.<br /> <br /> The duration of the spell would be one hour/scene, if no dice are sacrificed to increase it.<br /> <br /> Instant casting is 1, advanced duration is 1, for a total of 2 reach needed. As an ST, I would probably rule that RAW you'd need to combine two castings of the spell because the merit effect is an <i>alternative</i> to finding the specific thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i understand it Squeegee is correct except for one important part.<br /> <br /> The caster has Fate 3, so the primary spell factor gets 2 free steps (moving to the third step).<br /> <br /> So you get<br /> 1. The spell has a default potency of 1.<br /> 2. The duration becomes 3 seconds (1 round of combat).<br /> 3. The spell has potency 3 and duration 1 hour/scene.<br /> 4. You can't (with higher Gnosis you could probably do a combined spell, but it looks like the alternative effect is seperate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 11-23-2022, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T23:16:11-08:00","id":1497882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497816#post1497816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Sympathy is described exclusively between two people or between one person and an object. I don't think it's intended that two objects can't have sympathy, but since neither is capable of forming emotional bonds (which is the most common source for sympathetic connections), the strength of the link should naturally be quite limited.<br /> <br /> A lock and a matching key would probably not have a sympathetic connection at all unless they're used together quite often, in which case it should be weak. It's much more likely that whoever holds the key has a connection to both the key and the lock than them having a connection to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sympathy is described as either a physical, emotional or metaphysical connection.<br /> <br /> If you take the last page out of a book, it will have a physical sympathy to that specific book. If you make a soul stone it has a metaphysical connection* to you (as does casting a spell on a subject, or a mage to their spell).<br /> <br /> I think a key could have a physical connection to its lock if they started out as parts of the one item (and aren't modified too much, so maybe they fit together still). But in this case i could also see them having a weak metaphysical connection.<br /> <br /> *There is some question as to how long the metaphysical connection lasts after the thing creating it ends. Eg: if you have a weak connection to the subject of your spell, and the spell ends, does the metaphysical connection end immediately or does it fades slowly (like an emotional connection)? <br /> <br /> I lean towards the former - even if i have run it the other way because i hadn't thought it through. And the book describes all 'types' as connection as being the same (and mostly gives examples of emotional connections fading, i think).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T23:18:41-08:00","id":1497883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497875#post1497875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Katsinam Suukya, from Summoners, beginning on page 195.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Immortals has a mundane ritual for becoming Immortal by transforming into a part spirit entity. Which you could certainly try scrutinizing and learn how to do magically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T00:25:32-08:00","id":1497884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497882#post1497882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a key could have a physical connection to its lock if they started out as parts of the one item (and aren't modified too much, so maybe they fit together still). But in this case i could also see them having a weak metaphysical connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking keys are made from blanks that have never touched the locks during production. Zero physical contact before they're packaged together or used together.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the metaphysical part of sympathy refers to explicitly supernatural connections. A mage and their familiar, spells, spell subjects, and used yantras. These are the examples given that only fit the metaphysical aspect of sympathy.<br /> <br /> If you disagree with my interpretation (which you are free to do; I might be mistaken about that), then it might be worth considering this before deciding when sympathy is applicable and at what strength:<br /> Locks are assembled with pins/disks/etc according to a code, and the key is cut to fit the same code (also known as bitting).<br /> Does a key have sympathy to a lock if it's cut long after the lock is assembled? Does a key cut to a randomly chosen bitting have sympathy to any locks that by coincidence have the same bitting? Does a lock that is reassembled to have a different bitting (even if it's just switching two pins around, meaning you don't actually add or remove any parts) retain or lose sympathy to its keys? If the sympathy is lost, does reassembling it to its previous bitting restore that connection?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T01:32:51-08:00","id":1497886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497884#post1497884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally speaking keys are made from blanks that have never touched the locks during production. Zero physical contact before they're packaged together or used together.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the metaphysical part of sympathy refers to explicitly supernatural connections. A mage and their familiar, spells, spell subjects, and used yantras. These are the examples given that only fit the metaphysical aspect of sympathy.<br /> <br /> If you disagree with my interpretation (which you are free to do; I might be mistaken about that), then it might be worth considering this before deciding when sympathy is applicable and at what strength:<br /> Locks are assembled with pins/disks/etc according to a code, and the key is cut to fit the same code (also known as bitting).<br /> Does a key have sympathy to a lock if it's cut long after the lock is assembled?</div> </div> </div> </div> i would say no.<br /> But i don't understand the point of the line of questioning. I know how physical keys are usually made, i assumed we were talking here about magical keys (discussed in the Space Arcana section), they can be anything, a time of day, a particular song, etc.<br /> <br /> If you wanted a key and lock to have a sympathic connection you could make them from two halves of an amulet (very on brand for mage). Maybe the lock is a particular location, and the key is made from a meteor which landed at that location.<br /> <br /> I think i would agree with you that by default a key and lock don't have a physical connection. Metaphysical however is a seperate question. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does a key cut to a randomly chosen bitting have sympathy to any locks that by coincidence have the same bitting? Does a lock that is reassembled to have a different bitting (even if it's just switching two pins around, meaning you don't actually add or remove any parts) retain or lose sympathy to its keys? If the sympathy is lost, does reassembling it to its previous bitting restore that connection? </div> </div> </div>Those are some good question, i am going to answer two sides. If it has a physical connection (being made from the same meteor, say), then changing it would weaken the connection, i only have Temporal sympathy to go on here, but they do discuss the two as if they are the same thing.<br /> <br /> The given example is a parent and child (which could be misconstrued as an emotional connection) - physically the unborn is a part of the pregnant person's body. So they have a connected sympathy (regardless of any emotional attachment), and it is also made from the sperm of the sperm donor - giving a strong connection - again, i think regardless of any emotional attachment.<br /> <br /> The Connected sympathy to the pregnant person then changes to a Strong sympathy after birth (no longer one and the same body, but still made from the same stuff). There may also be an emotional sympathy... <br /> <br /> But i think the point i am trying to make is by changing the physical relationship between the two things the sympathy changes (similarily to how changing emotional states will change the strength of the sympathic connection). <br /> <br /> It is not stated that using Space magic to alter the strenght of a sympathic connection which is based on physical rather than emotional connectivity will physically alter the object, but i find the idea intriguing.<br /> <br /> The other side is regarding metaphysical relationships, a mage and their familiar, a mage and their spell/the subject of their spell, yantras/dedicated magical tool, and soul stones, are enough examples to infer the existence of a metaphysical relationship between a magical key and the portal that it locks. Even if that is a weak connection. <br /> <br /> I suspect i have digressed far from the point, but also your talk of tumblers and biting suggests we were actually not talking about the same kind of key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 11-23-2022, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T01:39:21-08:00","id":1497887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497886#post1497886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> i would say no.<br /> But i don't understand the point of the line of questioning. I know how physical keys are usually made, i assumed we were talking here about magical keys (discussed in the Space Arcana section), they can be anything, a time of day, a particular song, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question -which started this- was in regard to actual physical keys, since I was working on an Imbued item that relied on them. A pair, the Wayfinder's Keyring and the Perfect Mold.<br /> 1. A keychain that opens portals between doors, as long as you have the key to the opening door and the destination door<br /> 2. A dongle that shapes nearby blank keys or scrap metal into the key of any locks the dongle is pressed against.<br /> <br /> I'm scrapping it; the Arcana requirements for what I was trying to do aren't worth it.<br /> <br /> This may be a strange question, but are there any rules for how diseases spread in CoD? I want to make a <u>Contagion</u> illness that spreads along Sympathetic Connections, with stronger connections being more virulent vectors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Contagion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;she must target some form of carrier depending on the disease\u2019s transmission methods (water, food, living hosts). It\u2019s contagious as soon as the mage creates it, requiring a reflexive Stamina + Resolve roll, modified by the Severity, to resist contracting it. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>From that I assume any exposure to a given vector causes the same Stamina + Resolve roll, so a Sympathy-based Illness would trigger the roll whenever interacting with and infected Connection. Does that seem accurate?<br /> <br /> Tangentially related - if you use <u>Borrow Threads</u> (Stealing, not copying) and then use <u>Cut Threads</u> on those stolen connections, are they then severed for the original owner when <u>Borrow Threads</u> ends?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-23-2022, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T01:41:58-08:00","id":1497888,"title":"","content":"Following on from that, what would you assume happens when a Space mage weakens or strengthened a metaphysical connection? Unmaking the connected sympathy between a mage and their familiar/a mage and their soul stone? Reducing the strength of a Mage's connection to their spell (eg could this forcible relinquish the spell from their spell control?). <br /> <br /> This is probably not a simple question, but i suspect it doesn't need its own thread. Any other good examples? Any reason to strengthen (like maybe making a yantra closer to a dedicated magical tool?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T01:44:11-08:00","id":1497889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497887#post1497887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question -which started this- was in regard to actual physical keys, since I was working on an Imbued item that relied on them. A keychain that opens portals between doors, as long as you have the key to the opening door and the destination door, and a dongle that shapes blank keys or scrap metal into a key of any locks the dongle is pressed against. I'm scrapping it; the Arcana requirements for what I was trying to do aren't worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly that sounds like it is both a physical key and a metaphysical key in the sense i was discussing.<br /> <br /> So no sympathy, based on the physical, and yes based on metaphysical. At least the is my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-24T03:33:47-08:00","id":1497973,"title":"","content":"If you Perfected an object with <u>Hone The Perfected Form</u>, can you then subject it to the more arduous process of manually passing it into ephemera and back dozens of times over, to make the change Lasting? I'm mostly wondering about the more finicky stuff like Perfected Blood, where the manual refining process isn't viable due to time constraints. <br /> <br /> Directly related, can only the seven Metals be refined in the manual method, or could anything -made of a single material, at least- be purified?<br /> <br /> And finally, because Spirit is well outside my wheelhouse, these are the published spells you'd typically use for the manual Perfected refining process, correct?<br /> Death: <u>Create Avernian Gate </u>. <u>Ghost Gate</u> destroys the corporeal form, so it doesn't work.<br /> Spirit: <u>Reaching</u> (With the &quot;Iris&quot; Reach effect), <u>Twilit Body</u>, <u>World Walker</u>, and <u>Spirit Manse</u> (With the &quot;Iris&quot; Reach effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-24-2022, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-25T13:39:30-08:00","id":1498049,"title":"","content":"Is self-cast <u>Dream Reaching</u>'s Reach effect supposed to be read as bypassing the normal requirements to meditate into the Astral? I don't remember anywhere else that talks about meditating in relation to your dreams, and cast on others it seems to deposit you into their Onieros","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-25T14:02:13-08:00","id":1498051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498049#post1498049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is self-cast <u>Dream Reaching</u>'s Reach effect supposed to be read as bypassing the normal requirements to meditate into the Astral? I don't remember anywhere else that talks about meditating in relation to your dreams, and cast on others it seems to deposit you into their Onieros</div> </div> </div> </div>Lucid dreaming is only one componemt, page 247 indicates it allows them to enter their dreams. But page 248 states that creating an Astral Path requires a suitable location. Bypassing it would require either a Making to instany create the gateway or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1317924#post1317924\"> a spell to grant Astral Adept</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-25T15:11:12-08:00","id":1498053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498051#post1498051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lucid dreaming is only one componemt, page 247 indicates it allows them to enter their dreams. But page 248 states that creating an Astral Path requires a suitable location. Bypassing it would require either a Making to instany create the gateway or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1317924#post1317924\"> a spell to grant Astral Adept</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. New questions:<br /> 1. Can <u>Telepathy</u> allow cross-realm communication, such as casting it on your Goetic familiar to talk with it while you're out of the Astral?<br /> <br /> 2. <u>Teleport</u> allows you to access other realms, with the correct Arcana and a Sympathetic Connection. How this affects entities of flesh is debatable (I think that if it works, it would be like using a synesi), but could you use it to teleport a Goetia in Twilight into an Onieros?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-25T15:41:34-08:00","id":1498056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1497888#post1497888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following on from that, what would you assume happens when a Space mage weakens or strengthened a metaphysical connection? Unmaking the connected sympathy between a mage and their familiar/a mage and their soul stone? Reducing the strength of a Mage's connection to their spell (eg could this forcible relinquish the spell from their spell control?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think sympathetic connections emerge from the closeness of relationships rather than being the actual mechanism of them. There's a reciprocal element to an extent, what with the description of cooled or intensified feelings, but I think those should be read in terms of how the actual relationship doesn't inherently change, and can reassert itself to the degree that the connection resumes its natural form.<br /> <br /> In the case of something where the subject is through something outright magical it would be like... the Connected bond is not what makes you able to feel and act through your soul stone, the fact that soul stones work like that is why you have a Connected bond with it. Hence, I don't think changing that connection will mean anything beyond the usual, of affecting how sympathetic magic can be used through it and how you feel towards it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-25T16:50:55-08:00","id":1498059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498056#post1498056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence, I don't think changing that connection will mean anything beyond the usual, of affecting how sympathetic magic can be used through it and how you feel towards it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, i would have assumed that how you feel towards a thing is only affected by emotional sympathic links.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T02:26:39-08:00","id":1498063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498059#post1498059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting, i would have assumed that how you feel towards a thing is only affected by emotional sympathic links.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, if you've been married to a person for twenty years, your feelings about that person are not going to be defined solely by a few days in which the attitude becomes cooled and distant as a consequence of weakened sympathetic link. The other person being there for you when your parents died in that tragic blimp accident is going to count for something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T03:15:09-08:00","id":1498065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498063#post1498063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like, if you've been married to a person for twenty years, your feelings about that person are not going to be defined solely by a few days in which the attitude becomes cooled and distant as a consequence of weakened sympathetic link. The other person being there for you when your parents died in that tragic blimp accident is going to count for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, i see what you read, but it was not what i meant to say. If you have a connected sympathic link to your familiar, or a strong physical connection to your child (regardless of your emotional connection to them - they were made from you) then using magic to change that link would not change how you felt... <br /> <br /> That is a non-emotional sympathic connections - when altered by space magic - would not have an emotional effect. Is what i would have assumed.<br /> <br /> Unmake the connected link between a mage and her soulstone? Or weaken the link between a mage and her spell/subject of her spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 11-26-2022, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T03:57:58-08:00","id":1498067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498065#post1498065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, i see what you read, but it was not what i meant to say. If you have a connected sympathic link to your familiar, or a strong physical connection to your child (regardless of your emotional connection to them - they we're made from you) then using magic to change that link would not change how you felt... <br /> <br /> That is a non-emotional sympathic connections - when altered by space magic - would not have an emotional effect. Is what i would have assumed.<br /> <br /> Unmake the connected link between a mage and her soulstone? Or weaken the link between a mage and her spell/subject of her spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can weaken the link to your soulstone - it's too closely tied to the entirety of &quot;you&quot; as an ephemeral, thaumaturgical, and symbolic entity. <br /> <br /> Likewise, a spell you haven't Relinquished relies on you as a stable conduit to the Supernal. A Relinquishment automates that maintenance by disengaging the symbolic existence of the spell from your own. It goes from being &quot;Cauthon's Spell of Climate Control&quot; to &quot;Independent Spell of the Perfectly-Temprate Livingroom&quot;. The resonance of the Mage's Nimbus will slowly fade, as will the significance of who created the spell (and thus the Sympathetic tie) unless the spell is significant enough to go on being actively considered the Mage's spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T06:01:22-08:00","id":1498069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498067#post1498067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you can weaken the link to your soulstone - it's too closely tied to the entirety of &amp;quot;you&amp;quot; as an ephemeral, thaumaturgical, and symbolic entity. </div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it explicitly calls out requiring Unmaking to destroy a Connected sympathy. My asusmption would be that without the connection it would act like the soulstone of a dead mage, though the alternative is that it could actually break the soulstone's connection to your path... But given how we know soulstones continue to work after the death of their creator, i think the latter is unlikely.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if your control over a spell depends on the sympathic link, then destroying or stealing that link could allow you to force them to (unsafely) relinquish the spell (probably requiring you to spend the willpower cost), or steal spell control... Though transfering spell control usually requires Prime, and the caster to be doing it.<br /> <br /> The point remains, i don't think these kind of sympathic changes should have any emotional effects.<br /> <br /> It is unclear, would changing the strong sympathic connection between parents and child lead to unnoticable genetic changes which makes it look like they are not directly related? For emotional links they naturally vary over time and can organically re-grow, but re-reading the rules it is very explicit that modifying these links should have effects which echo into the Fallen. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of taking an item you have used as a yantra (weak sympathic link) and using space to strengthen the link to the point where is becomes easy to turn into a dedicated magical tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T06:38:29-08:00","id":1498070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498065#post1498065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, i see what you read, but it was not what i meant to say. If you have a connected sympathic link to your familiar, or a strong physical connection to your child (regardless of your emotional connection to them - they were made from you) then using magic to change that link would not change how you felt...</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't change the specific emotional context of your relationship to them, but a sympathetic connection possessed by a feeling being manifests in its emotional relation to the subject of that connection.<br /> <br /> One of the examples of how altering sympathy works literally involves someone being given a bond to a nonliving object, 1e didn't have a description of the emotional effects of sympathetic links and specified that a mage and their familiar could feel each other's emotions, and the Contagion Chronicle's crossover mechanics specifically include &quot;the sympathetic connections a Deviant has for their Touchstones \u2014 the things that ground the Stability of their existence through their obsessive love or hate for them \u2014 are one step stronger than they would normally be.&quot;<br /> <br /> Messing with someone's parental sympathies isn't, by default, going to do anything to their biology \u2014 you're messing with physical/emotional/magical <i>distance</i>, not fidelity. The physical consequences are generally that it's easier or harder to bring the two together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T06:55:02-08:00","id":1498071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498070#post1498070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't change the specific emotional context of your relationship to them, but a sympathetic connection possessed by a feeling being manifests in its emotional relation to the subject of that connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure i understand what you are getting at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Messing with someone's parental sympathies isn't, by default, going to do anything to their biology \u2014 you're messing with physical/emotional/magical <i>distance</i>, not fidelity. The physical consequences are generally that it's easier or harder to bring the two together. </div> </div> </div>I see, i like that... Distance between a parent and their child would be a big deal.<br /> <br /> Applying that same understanding, how does distance added to the metaphysical connection between a mage and their soulstone work? I know this would be Unmaking, so you explicitly make it so the mage and their soulstone are no longer one and the same. <br /> <br /> Probably handy if you have stolen someone's soulstone and don't want them tracking you down... <br /> <br /> And weakening a connection to their spell?<br /> <br /> It feels like strengthening a connection to an item you used as a yantra would make it easier to then dedicate (ie take less time) as you are already closer to that item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T07:01:38-08:00","id":1498072,"title":"","content":"Fuck. I wrote a long post that got ate when I accidentally pressed ctrl+r instead of ctrl+t.<br /> Anyway, my point was that sympathy (regardless of the nature of the bond) is almost exclusively described in emotional terms, and that the Create Sympathy spell explicitly states that creating a sympathetic bond will always affect the subject emotionally.<br /> <br /> So yeah, severing the bond between parent and child will likely make the parent more neglectful and dismissive, and make the child prefer to confide in any other parental figure in their life. It would not change their biology or physical appearance.<br /> A continuous blocking of the connection would make them look less alike, but only because mannerisms wouldn't transfer between them nearly as easily (both because they'd interact less, and because they'd be less receptive during interactions). Mannerisms do incredible things to how people are perceived. Many teens and young adults are said to be similar to a parent by people who don't know it's a step parent or adopted parent.<br /> <br /> Altering mystical sympathetic connections would not change how the magic works unless that magic is specifically and explicitly based on the connection itself.<br /> A soul stone is still made of the same stuff as the mage's soul/gnosis, and would still resonate with them in the way that makes the mage able to use the soul stone as a dedicated tool.<br /> Strengthening the connection to a yantra doesn't change the fact that dedicating a tool is a specific process requiring conscious effort by the mage. Being sympathetically or emotionally closer doesn't mean it resonates with your magical identity any more than usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T07:02:29-08:00","id":1498073,"title":"","content":"Seperate but related question. Changes you make to the strength of a sympathic connection are lasting by default, right? <br /> <br /> I mean for emotional distance, that can change, the examples of a couple going to counselling. <br /> <br /> But for something Mystical or Physical, that distance may be harder to repair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T07:05:25-08:00","id":1498074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498073#post1498073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seperate but related question. Changes you make to the strength of a sympathic connection are lasting by default, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Varies by spell. Web-Weaver isn't lasting. Cut Threads is. Create Sympathy has a Reach option for being lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T07:25:20-08:00","id":1498075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498071#post1498071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure i understand what you are getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing your sympathetic connection to someone won't make you love them or hate them or feel sad about them, but it will affect the degree of emotional investment you're likely to put in the relationship them one way or the other \u2014 drawing once again on the Contagion Chronicle guidelines, having Family Ties to a Beast gives you a Strong sympathetic connection to them and requires that the pair of you become close through significant shared association, the three stages of a vampiric blood bond directly increase the thrall's sympathy to the vampire in question and come with attendant levels of infatuation with them, and Sin-Eaters can indirectly have their Synergy messed with by altering their sympathetic connection to their geist to steer the trends of their behavior (and the only level of Synergy at which the two aren't Connected is the one at which the Sin-Eater has no especial insight into their geist's goals and emotions and vice versa and instead negotiate with each other through favors, threats, and bribes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Applying that same understanding, how does distance added to the metaphysical connection between a mage and their soulstone work? I know this would be Unmaking, so you explicitly make it so the mage and their soulstone are no longer one and the same. </div> </div> </div>Left to their own devices, the mage and their soul stone would be more or less likely to be brought into contact with each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It feels like strengthening a connection to an item you used as a yantra would make it easier to then dedicate (ie take less time) as you are already closer to that item. </div> </div> </div>Nope. In Doylist terms this is a justification for the table to have items recur in the narrative, not a means of accelerating the process of aligning an item with your Nimbus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-26-2022, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T11:59:12-08:00","id":1498148,"title":"","content":"The <u>Wyrdbound Oaths</u> spell allows mages to be part of Wyrd-backed oaths.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oaths allow a free Mantle dot:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Societal oaths</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Societal oaths</b> include oaths sworn when a change-<br /> ling joins a motley, court, or freehold. <b>The changeling<br /> gains the benefits of being part of that group. For a<br /> court, this means the character gains the first dot of the<br /> Mantle Merit (p. 117) without spending Experiences,<br /> and is bound by whatever restrictions that court usually<br /> levies.</b> For a freehold, the changeling becomes a recog-<br /> nized part of the local supernatural landscape; the player<br /> receives a +1 to all rolls to navigate the Hedge wherever<br /> the freehold controls it. <b>For a motley, the changeling en-<br /> ters a pact with his fellows.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The following questions arise: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Assuming that a Court accepts the mage. Does this mean that a mage gains a Mantle rating if allowed? Or does it gain the Allies (Court) / Court Goodwill (Court) instead?</li> <li>Assuming that a Motley accepts the mage. Can they buy Motley merits like Hollow?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T12:53:39-08:00","id":1498156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498148#post1498148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <u>Wyrdbound Oaths</u> spell allows mages to be part of Wyrd-backed oaths.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oaths allow a free Mantle dot:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The following questions arise:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Assuming that a Court accepts the mage. Does this mean that a mage gains a Mantle rating if allowed? Or does it gain the Allies (Court) / Court Goodwill (Court) instead?</li> <li>Assuming that a Motley accepts the mage. Can they buy Motley merits like Hollow?</li> </ol><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) Allies and Court Goodwill, and possibly an adjacent Mystery Cult Initiation, taking cues from the Court of the Leafless Tree and Contagion Player's Guide on the subject. The Supernal can speak words that affect the Mysteries a mage relates to, but in the same way a Mage can't take on Forsaken Gifts or Renown specifically even with an established Spirit-forged link, Mantle requires more of a fairy metaphysical infrastructure than the spell can provide*.<br /> 2) Strictly speaking, the expenditure of EXP for Hollow represents the work put into clearing (or cultivating) and stabilizing a space in the Hedge into a Hollow, and then putting in the work to build a place and stock it up within it. The spell that lets the Mage do their version of Hedgeshaping is the more direct cause of this than strictly Wyrdbound Oaths.<br /> <br /> ....of course, since this is largely a background developed affair, that's all semantics. I suppose the better way to put it is a) Yeah, they can, but also b) They don't strictly need to be in a motley-or-greater fairy organization to get a Hollow.<br /> <br /> *Of course, being the gonzo who still wants to do the Forest of Teeth where in Mantle and Renown are tightly wrapped up in each other, I'm not going to be the one to say that if you wanna interpret it the other way, I'm not going to particularly stop you-just that there's actual precedent and logic in the way I described it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-27T12:54:48-08:00","id":1498157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498148#post1498148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <u>Wyrdbound Oaths</u> spell allows mages to be part of Wyrd-backed oaths.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oaths allow a free Mantle dot:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The following questions arise: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Assuming that a Court accepts the mage. Does this mean that a mage gains a Mantle rating if allowed? Or does it gain the Allies (Court) / Court Goodwill (Court) instead?</li> <li>Assuming that a Motley accepts the mage. Can they buy Motley merits like Hollow?</li> </ol><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1. It's Allies, if I remember right. Mantle is largely irrelevant to a Mage. <br /> <br /> 2. No reason you can't. Unlike, say, Hallow or Mantle, a Hollow has no splat-exclusive primary mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T19:54:58-08:00","id":1498394,"title":"","content":"<u>Create Avernian Gate</u> is a Making spell, since it creates a new Gate wholesale. Would a spell that temporarily turns a Ghost into an Avernian Gate be a reasonable Adept spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T21:19:59-08:00","id":1498396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498394#post1498394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Create Avernian Gate</u> is a Making spell, since it creates a new Gate wholesale. Would a spell that temporarily turns a Ghost into an Avernian Gate be a reasonable Adept spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no, for much the same reason that a spell that temporarily turns a Grimoire into a Hallow would not be reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T23:24:03-08:00","id":1498405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498396#post1498396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say no, for much the same reason that a spell that temporarily turns a Grimoire into a Hallow would not be reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would tend to agree. But that said, most making spells (saying Create Life) can be achieved with Patterning if you start out with something to alter.<br /> <br /> So if you want to make a Dragon from scratch it is Making, but if you want to turn a dragon fly into a Dragon, is it Patterning.<br /> <br /> If you want a connection to the Underworld, you will need to pattern something which is already connected. I think, anything which has drunk from one of the rivers of the Underworld would do... With enough legwork you can create an Avernian gate without magic (if you are willing to kill someone and ritually bury them in a new graveyard - thus mundanely creating a graveyard). Perhaps a blood sacrifice would do it, creating the essence of death by actually killing a living thing as part of your spell.<br /> <br /> It think ST fiat, but normally it is easier to find an existing Avernian gate (at least in the material world). To quote Geist <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Morgues. Graveyards. Crossroads. Battlefields. Once you can see them, Avernian Gates are almost impossible to avoid. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T18:53:57-08:00","id":1498590,"title":"","content":"<u>Ghost Gate</u> is a Duration-primary spell, which represents how long the Iris lasts. Once something passes through the gateway, it stays ephemeral even once the spell ends. If you use the Reach effect, however, the spell instead converts a target directly into ephemera. If using the Reach effect, does that mean the subject stops being ephemeral once the spell ends?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T19:25:11-08:00","id":1498591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498590#post1498590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Ghost Gate</u> is a Duration-primary spell, which represents how long the Iris lasts. Once something passes through the gateway, it stays ephemeral even once the spell ends. If you use the Reach effect, however, the spell instead converts a target directly into ephemera. If using the Reach effect, does that mean the subject stops being ephemeral once the spell ends?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think duration is irrelevant in that case. You just appear in Twilight without losing your items. Without additional magic or knowledge of a way out, you are simply stranded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T21:49:44-08:00","id":1498605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498590#post1498590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Ghost Gate</u> is a Duration-primary spell, which represents how long the Iris lasts. Once something passes through the gateway, it stays ephemeral even once the spell ends. If you use the Reach effect, however, the spell instead converts a target directly into ephemera. If using the Reach effect, does that mean the subject stops being ephemeral once the spell ends?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I run it, buuuut there\u2019s not much ground for me to claim it\u2019s The Right rule.<br /> <br /> Ghost Gate\u2019s normal effect: Duration applies to the gate. The gate poofs away when its Duration expires. Thus, any Twilight-ness caused by passing through the gate is Lasting. Creatures can pass through another gate later to regain material form. Items however have their material form destroyed, becoming ephemeral. <br /> <br /> Ghost Gate\u2019s Reach effect: Duration applies to the Twilight-ness. Anything turned Twilight/ephemeral becomes fully material again once the spell expires. This also means that items don\u2019t have their material form destroyed and turned into ephemera; just remove the spell, and it\u2019s fresh to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T17:49:51-08:00","id":1498713,"title":"","content":"Would Spirit be enough for a mage to animate their reflection or would Forces also be required ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T18:01:36-08:00","id":1498714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498713#post1498713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Spirit be enough for a mage to animate their reflection or would Forces also be required ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d ask the opposite question actually. Forces 4 alone should do it \u00e0 la Matter 4 Golem. Spirit? Hmm\u2026 summon and command a spirit who has a Numen about animating mirror images? Not sure if the Spirit Arcanum alone can do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T18:14:14-08:00","id":1498716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498714#post1498714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019d ask the opposite question actually. Forces 4 alone should do it \u00e0 la Matter 4 Golem. Spirit? Hmm\u2026 summon and command a spirit who has a Numen about animating mirror images? Not sure if the Spirit Arcanum alone can do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe it would be more helpful to state the intent instead. What Arcana combination would be needed to replicate the Hanged Man and Man in the Mirror stands from Jojo ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T18:46:12-08:00","id":1498719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498716#post1498716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it would be more helpful to state the intent instead. What Arcana combination would be needed to replicate the Hanged Man and Man in the Mirror stands from Jojo ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those two Stands are, as more than one person has highlighted by putting dialogue about the former next to demonstrations of the latter, different types of phenomena.<br /> <br /> The Arcana are not generally built to produce weirder phenomena as simple expressions of their lore, and Stands are the kind of weird phenomena that in ChroD would likely have a metaphysical system behind them akin to the Fire, the Wyrd, or the Machine \u2014 you're not going to build in &quot;this thing can access an inverse world through any reflective surface/physically hide in reflections&quot; from first principles without really stretching how spell factors are considered \u2014 but Man in the Mirror's general shtick is Space-related with a side of Fate and Hanged Man likewise accomplishes what it does through Forces with a side of Space.<br /> <br /> The simplest way to accomplish the specific goal of replicating those Stands is, yes, to use Spirit or Death to create an ephemeral being with Numina that do those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T19:06:48-08:00","id":1498722,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t watch JoJo, and I only saw a two minute clip\u2026but isn\u2019t this literally a mirror person or something from mirror space?<br /> <br /> Edit: Yeah, it looks like the character gets dragged into mirror space by Numina or spell.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: the other one is a mirror person and a Fate effect, I think. From a skim it beats up your reflection which is reflected into you, which is definitely Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-03-2022, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T19:40:55-08:00","id":1498724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498722#post1498722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t watch JoJo, and I only saw a two minute clip\u2026but isn\u2019t this literally a mirror person or something from mirror space?<br /> <br /> Edit: Yeah, it looks like the character gets dragged into mirror space by Numina or spell.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: the other one is a mirror person and a Fate effect, I think. From a skim it beats up your reflection which is reflected into you, which is definitely Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, there are mirror being as horrors in the CofD core book and I remember Changeling had a Hall of Mirrors mentioned somewhere. Creating a mirror themed Legacy has been on my mind for a while, but this is the first time the how has become a lot clearer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T19:51:22-08:00","id":1498725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498724#post1498724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, there are mirror being as horrors in the CofD core book and I remember Changeling had a Hall of Mirrors mentioned somewhere. Creating a mirror themed Legacy has been on my mind for a while, but this is the first time the how has become a lot clearer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably going to be very hedge intensive then. Mirror Space is literally a specific section of the Hedge, which tends to collect fetches and spawn mirror people, who were never defined in Changeling 2e as far as I\u2019m aware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-03-2022, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T20:18:13-08:00","id":1498728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498725#post1498725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably going to be very hedge intensive then. Mirror Space is literally a specific section of the Hedge, and which tends to collect fetches and spawn mirror people, who were never defined in Changeling 2e as far as I\u2019m aware.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're created in moments of anguish, doubt, or pain, where you're unable to face your reflection.* Some of them want to experience the sensations of the real world, while others are satisfied with watching, and they don't necessarily wear the face whose rejection created them. Fairest with the Stealing the Solid Reflection Contract can accidentally pull them out when they mess up trying to pull out the reflection of a living being instead of an object.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* It's a very Persona 4 Shadow sort of thing, bringing it back to magical punch-ghosts.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T05:13:46-08:00","id":1498752,"title":"","content":"Is <u>Transmission</u> affecting one transmission per activation, or is it like <u>Tune In</u> in that as long as it's active you can make adjustments to any wave-form you can perceive? I mostly read it as the latter, but the former would be fairly plausible as a narrow reading of RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T05:34:26-08:00","id":1498753,"title":"","content":"My first thought about a mage animating mirror images is making the image inside of the mirror move around in ways that aren't a reflection of what's in front of it, possibly as a way of communicating or freaking people out. I'd actually see such an application as just being a Ruling of Forces (and possibly Matter as an alternative).<br /> <br /> If it's an idea of a reflection stepping out of the mirror and doing stuff... that basically just seems like conjuring up a mobile hologram in a way you choose to be very showy, but the level of Forces you're employing to do so don't really limit you to working with existing reflections, and as Satchel said the Arcana don't really tend to work in terms of being super esoteric such that you could treat a reflection as an entity as a matter of course, or otherwise make drawing it from the mirror more special.<br /> <br /> I do think Forces could construct it as a sort of Star Trek hologram where it has physicality, but again you could do that anywhere. For an Awakened mage, doing it with a mirror seems more like the kind of thing you do circumstantially, if you want to create a scenario where somebody <i>thinks</i> their reflection is popping out to do stuff to them.<br /> <br /> I could see an archmaster using the Practice of Entities to create a reflection entity with fitting powers in a way that involves messing around with mirrors, but that's a whole other thing.<br /> <br /> A mirror-themed Legacy... it depends on what you want to do with it, but I'd say the limited scope of Attainments combined with them not being constrained by Paradox, dispellation, or spell control limit is the kind of thing that lends itself to making them more tied to particular circumstances. It makes a lot more sense to have an Attainment that limits your hard light hologram creation to something that you can draw out of mirrors then it does to make a regular spell like that, especially if it's in service to some message about the value people place in mirrors or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T05:46:40-08:00","id":1498754,"title":"","content":"If we're talking doppelgangers or nemesis, wouldn't Astral Adept and a modified <u>Goetic Summons</u> or <u>Goetic Evocation</u> be easiest? Summon a person's facets out to confront them for the first, and a superficial copy for the second?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T08:42:37-08:00","id":1498765,"title":"","content":"Creating holograms is an interesting idea, and it pairs well with the idea of the Chinese magic mirror and the legend of the mirror people.<br /> <br /> Goetic Invocation also has a lot of potential and allows them to be equipped with the right Numina from the start.<br /> <br /> Another idea I was thinking about was having the mirror person and mage form some variation of the familiar bond, allowing the reflection to tag the mage on existing and work together the rest of the time. But I wasn't sure how to codify it mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T14:35:54-08:00","id":1498992,"title":"","content":"Since food is under the purview of Life, would a Compelling be enough to purify food and drink or would a Ruling be required ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T15:05:21-08:00","id":1498994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1498992#post1498992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since food is under the purview of Life, would a Compelling be enough to purify food and drink or would a Ruling be required ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure food is Matter, primarily, while Life deals with sustenance. At least, that's what I take from Life's Arcana description, and the Ruling Arcana of the Kitchen Alchemists being Matter.<br /> <br /> Compelling could plausibility separate toxins and impurities, although you'd need a way to keep them from being reintroduced. Perfecting would be more easily justified though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-06-2022, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T19:46:05-08:00","id":1499017,"title":"","content":"Where should one place a non standard legacy attainment that allows one to substitute Willpower in the place of Mana? I\u2019m also a bit uncertain of a good ratio, do you think 1:1 good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T19:53:35-08:00","id":1499019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499017#post1499017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where should one place a non standard legacy attainment that allows one to substitute Willpower in the place of Mana? I\u2019m also a bit uncertain of a good ratio, do you think 1:1 good?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Patterning, so at least Fourth for me.<br /> <br /> Dunno about the ratio\u2026 while I\u2019d just give 1:1, I\u2019m also likely to give them all sorts of weird monstrosities that may or may not mangle up their Wp and Mana economies. (Not necessarily as game balance, but because I feel stronger supernatural powers around these blocks should follow Weird Shit and Scary Shit. Also, Hungry Shit.)<br /> <br /> (Speaking of monstrosities, this function does feel more like a Rapt savant ability.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T19:54:00-08:00","id":1499020,"title":"","content":"Essence-to-Mana is a X+1=X conversion rate, so that would probably be a baseline. I'm... leery on WP-to-Mana being kosher, but it would probably be a Patterning effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T20:01:55-08:00","id":1499021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499019#post1499019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like Patterning, so at least Fourth for me.<br /> <br /> Dunno about the ratio\u2026 while I\u2019d just give 1:1, I\u2019m also likely to give them all sorts of weird monstrosities that may or may not mangle up their Wp and Mana economies. (Not necessarily as game balance, but because I feel stronger supernatural powers around these blocks should follow Weird Shit and Scary Shit. Also, Hungry Shit.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499019#post1499019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Speaking of monstrosities, this function does feel more like a Rapt savant ability.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Funny you should say that\u2026the legacy I was considering it for was basically a method to force oneself to either to either ascend or die. Most members either die or go rapt. The only reason it has any members left is that people think that it increases their odds. It\u2019s supposedly a \u201cgift\u201d from Lilith.<br /> <br /> Edit: it\u2019s like throwing oneself in a volcano in the hopes one will eventually become a diamond, and believing one will live through the process. It\u2019s not actually a auto ascend, it just puts the pressure on until something gives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-06-2022, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T20:07:47-08:00","id":1499022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499021#post1499021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny you should say that\u2026the legacy I was considering it for was basically a method to force oneself to either to either ascend or die. Most members either die or go rapt. The only reason it has any members left is that people think that it increases their odds. It\u2019s supposedly a \u201cgift\u201d from Lilith.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Legacies full of Liches and/or Reapers were scary enough, but the prospect of one full of the Rapt was something I missed \u2014 and it\u2019s terrifying.<br /> <br /> Maybe their other Attainments summon lesser/greater Tulpa, then. I mean, <i>someone</i> in-universe must\u2019ve been tinkering with ways to conjure Tulpa without Rapture\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T20:19:19-08:00","id":1499023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499020#post1499020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence-to-Mana is a X+1=X conversion rate, so that would probably be a baseline. I'm... leery on WP-to-Mana being kosher, but it would probably be a Patterning effect.</div> </div> </div> </div> How bad an issue is it? I know willpower is pretty easy to refresh for Mages. Mana kinda is too, to a point. But I guess it\u2019s a extra way to replenish mana effectively. Maybe I shouldn\u2019t allow it to be spent on legacy attainments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T20:25:08-08:00","id":1499024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499023#post1499023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How bad an issue is it? I know willpower is pretty easy to refresh for Mages. Mana kinda is too, to a point. But I guess it\u2019s a extra way to replenish mana effectively. Maybe I shouldn\u2019t allow it to be spent on legacy attainments?</div> </div> </div> </div>My concern would come from how laughably easy it is to refresh Willpower with spells; Mind and Life Disciples can basically spam out <u>Clear Thoughts</u> and <u>Knit/Mend</u> respectively. Mana, at least, is mostly limited to Scouring, Oblations, and Hallows. Maybe have WP-Mana be really unstable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T20:29:53-08:00","id":1499025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499022#post1499022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Legacies full of Liches and/or Reapers were scary enough, but the prospect of one full of the Rapt was something I missed \u2014 and it\u2019s terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it makes it better, I was basing them a bit on the myth of spontaneous human combustion. Ascend or die!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499022#post1499022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe their other Attainments summon lesser/greater Tulpa, then. I mean, <i>someone</i> in-universe must\u2019ve been tinkering with ways to conjure Tulpa without Rapture\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026well I know what I\u2019m doing now. My biggest hurdle right now is I\u2019m having trouble with attainments that are powerful enough to be worth the overlying problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-07-2022, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T20:34:30-08:00","id":1499027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499024#post1499024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My concern would come from how laughably easy it is to refresh Willpower with spells; Mind and Life Disciples can basically spam out <u>Clear Thoughts</u> and <u>Knit/Mend</u> respectively. Mana, at least, is mostly limited to Scouring, Oblations, and Hallows. Maybe have WP-Mana be really unstable?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not sure how I can make it unstable\u2026maybe it lowers the time take before they start catching alight again? Or maybe a breaking point?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T20:35:05-08:00","id":1499029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499025#post1499025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026well I know what I\u2019m doing now. My biggest hurdle right now is I\u2019m having trouble with attainments that are powerful enough to be worth the overlying problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how severe you've made the drawbacks... Walking Demesne, maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499027#post1499027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not sure how I can make it unstable\u2026maybe it lowers the time take before they start catching alight again? Or maybe a breaking point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it becomes Volatile Tass rather than straight Mana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-06-2022, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T20:50:11-08:00","id":1499030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499029#post1499029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on how sever you've made the drawbacks... Walking Demesne, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m starting at extremely painful automatic pattern scouring oneself every day unless one pursues Mystery and Obsession. I\u2019m torn on whether or not to let the Mage keep the mana, or have maybe a reduction. Maybe I could have a more significant drawback? (Or maybe that\u2019s too much, I don\u2019t know)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499029#post1499029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it becomes Volatile Tass rather than straight Mana</div> </div> </div> </div> Manifesting a minor curse on oneself for power? Fits pretty well. I\u2019d have to come up with a sample list of curses, but I\u2019m fine with that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T01:01:36-08:00","id":1499039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499025#post1499025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026well I know what I\u2019m doing now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like you're veering hard away from your ordeals for Ascension concept and into becoming Rapt just for the sake of it.<br /> <br /> I don't really know where 21C Hermit was getting the idea that the Legacy is full of Rapt from a description that its end point has a few who got that as an alternative to dying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Temple Builder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest hurdle right now is I\u2019m having trouble with attainments that are powerful enough to be worth the overlying problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me with a concept like this you work towards something that seems evocative of the concept the characters are driven by rather than taking on risk in exchange for great power.<br /> <br /> It's like the Tremere. Ultimately, they're not much more powerful than other mages, and the need to feed off of souls is a significant imposition. People get involved for somewhere between taking it as an article of faith and being compelled by Obsession that this is the way to understand the deepest mysteries of the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T14:05:55-08:00","id":1499169,"title":"","content":"Do Spirits have Sympathy to the objects they represent, and if so do individual Helions have enough conceptual proximity to have Sympathy to Sol?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T14:54:55-08:00","id":1499171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499169#post1499169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Spirits have Sympathy to the objects they represent, and if so do individual Helions have enough conceptual proximity to have Sympathy to Sol?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m inclined to say No. At least, not any more than what sympathetic connection a wolf has to a deer, or what a deer has to the woods.<br /> <br /> The physical object might serve as a Sympathy Yantra to the spirit (which doesn\u2019t necessarily imply a sympathetic connection), but even this I feel should be reserved for younger spirits that are still too tightly tied to the one physical object from which they sprang out of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T11:52:09-08:00","id":1499232,"title":"","content":"Can you cast Know Spirit and get reliable data from an abyssal creature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T13:55:25-08:00","id":1499242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499232#post1499232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cast Know Spirit and get reliable data from an abyssal creature?</div> </div> </div> </div>1e had a version of Abyssal Mage Sight that required all five Subtle Arcana to use, so that would be my starting point. (Grimoire of Grimoires, for reference)<br /> <br /> In 2e... I'd say an Acamoth should require Mind and maybe Prime rather than Spirit, but the spell would otherwise be identical to <u>Know Spirit</u>. They're primarily past of the Astral, if I'm reading it right.<br /> <br /> Gulmoth are trickier, since they're just as often phenomenal as they are specific entities. Spirit is probably fine, but I'd tack Prime on again.<br /> <br /> Prime is probably a good application in general. Abyssal entites are the opposite of Truth, and Prime is -loosely speaking- raw Truth. Using Prime to figure out what it is based on what it isn't is convoluted but probably accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T01:23:51-08:00","id":1499271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499242#post1499242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1e had a version of Abyssal Mage Sight that required all five Subtle Arcana to use, so that would be my starting point. (Grimoire of Grimoires, for reference)<br /> <br /> In 2e... I'd say an Acamoth should require Mind and maybe Prime rather than Spirit, but the spell would otherwise be identical to <u>Know Spirit</u>. They're primarily past of the Astral, if I'm reading it right.<br /> <br /> Gulmoth are trickier, since they're just as often phenomenal as they are specific entities. Spirit is probably fine, but I'd tack Prime on again.<br /> <br /> Prime is probably a good application in general. Abyssal entites are the opposite of Truth, and Prime is -loosely speaking- raw Truth. Using Prime to figure out what it is based on what it isn't is convoluted but probably accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would tend to avoid being prescriptive. An Abyssal creature of impossible light and reflections might be forces. An Anti-numbers Abyssal might be mind /prime (depending on whether you think Maths is under the purview of Truth or Communication...). And an Abyssal of alternative impossible timelines would be Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T03:43:27-08:00","id":1499274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499271#post1499271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would tend to avoid being prescriptive. An Abyssal creature of impossible light and reflections might be forces. An Anti-numbers Abyssal might be mind /prime (depending on whether you think Maths is under the purview of Truth or Communication...). And an Abyssal of alternative impossible timelines would be Time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, for sure! I'm absolutely not arguing for a be-all end-all Abyss-analysing Arcana. I just favor the idea that you can use Prime to figure out that something <i>is</i> Abyssal, but then have to use your other Arcana to figure out what the details are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T05:57:15-08:00","id":1499275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499274#post1499274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, for sure! I'm absolutely not arguing for a be-all end-all Abyss-analysing Arcana. I just favor the idea that you can use Prime to figure out that something <i>is</i> Abyssal, but then have to use your other Arcana to figure out what the details are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.<br /> <br /> I am now thinking about how you would explore an Abyssal (sentient?) Timeline/splinter. I doubt Prime would be the first arcanum you grabbed to examine it.<br /> <br /> But using Prime to figure out this mystery (or collection of mysteries) is actually Abyssal, would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T15:26:47-08:00","id":1499319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499274#post1499274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, for sure! I'm absolutely not arguing for a be-all end-all Abyss-analysing Arcana. I just favor the idea that you can use Prime to figure out that something <i>is</i> Abyssal, but then have to use your other Arcana to figure out what the details are.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1ed, Spirit was very good at that, so much so that two Legacies with a major focus on the Abyss had it in common: The Secret Order of the Gate and the Gaolers of Ialdabaoth. They probably do it by detecting for Abyssal Resonance.<br /> <br /> I would imagine Prime would also be very good. Prime is how magic knows itself, so its domain of Truth and revelation could expose things that cannot be true. Fate might be able to do it, since anything Abyssal literally cannot be, its purview of probability would probably detect when a thing that has 0% chance of existing is somehow there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T02:26:10-08:00","id":1499354,"title":"","content":"Am I misreading the rules for Imbued Items, or is it <i>easier</i> to cast a more complicated spell from one than a simple spell? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a user triggers the spell, the player rolls to cast it with a dice pool of the spell\u2019s Arcanum rating plus the user\u2019s Gnosis (if Awakened). </div> </div> </div>I'm reading that as you have a fixed Arcana dice pool, plus your Gnosis. That would mean a Gnosis 2 Mage would have a three-die pool to activate a &quot;wand of <u>Analyze Life</u>&quot;, but a six-die pool to activate a &quot;wand of <u>Mending</u>&quot;. Sure, you can use <u>Word of Command</u> to bypass that, but the internal logic of the spell activation difficulty seems... odd.<br /> <br /> Am I misunderstanding?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-11-2022, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T05:25:09-08:00","id":1499362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499354#post1499354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I misreading the rules for Imbued Items, or is it <i>easier</i> to cast a more complicated spell from one than a simple spell?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm reading that as you have a fixed Arcana dice pool, plus your Gnosis. That would mean a Gnosis 2 Mage would have a three-die pool to activate a &quot;wand of <u>Analyze Life</u>&quot;, but a six-die pool to activate a &quot;wand of <u>Manding</u>&quot;. Sure, you can use <u>Word of Command</u> to bypass that, but it seems... odd.<br /> <br /> Am I misunderstanding?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, is it more odd than how that mage would have a dice pool of 3 the first time they become capable of casting the low level spell, and that their dice pool for the advanced one becomes the same as what it is for casting every lower level one?<br /> <br /> I think the dice pools of imbued items need to deal with two queries. The first is &quot;what else are you going to make the casting pool for this thing&quot;, and the second is the matter of whether it should have an extent of flexibility that can properly substitute for being able to cast the spell for oneself.<br /> <br /> Awakened magic is powerful, and the option to get a discrete bit of it that can be carried around and used by somebody who couldn't otherwise cast that spell is strong in itself. There probably ought to be some limit on it, and I'd say that you have limited options for expanding its factors is a fairly straightforward one. The wand of Analyse Life generally needs to be employed with some care and precision.<br /> <br /> I'd say another side of it is that it gives more utility to the Prime spell. Like, in First Edition that was <i>just</i> about activating without needing to fulfil the condition, which... seems pretty circumstantially useful depending on an item that had some very troubling condition or being in a scenario where performing the condition was unfeasible for some reason. I'd say one is getting a bit more out of how the Arcanum can engage with Imbued Items to be able to say that you can increase the factors you use for it and not really be at risk of failing to cast the spell (although an item imbued with a lower level spell will still only be able to push its factors so far).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T13:54:23-08:00","id":1499397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499362#post1499362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, is it more odd than how that mage would have a dice pool of 3 the first time they become capable of casting the low level spell, and that their dice pool for the advanced one becomes the same as what it is for casting every lower level one?<br /> <br /> I think the dice pools of imbued items need to deal with two queries. The first is &amp;quot;what else are you going to make the casting pool for this thing&amp;quot;, and the second is the matter of whether it should have an extent of flexibility that can properly substitute for being able to cast the spell for oneself.<br /> <br /> Awakened magic is powerful, and the option to get a discrete bit of it that can be carried around and used by somebody who couldn't otherwise cast that spell is strong in itself. There probably ought to be some limit on it, and I'd say that you have limited options for expanding its factors is a fairly straightforward one. The wand of Analyse Life generally needs to be employed with some care and precision.<br /> <br /> I'd say another side of it is that it gives more utility to the Prime spell. Like, in First Edition that was <i>just</i> about activating without needing to fulfil the condition, which... seems pretty circumstantially useful depending on an item that had some very troubling condition or being in a scenario where performing the condition was unfeasible for some reason. I'd say one is getting a bit more out of how the Arcanum can engage with Imbued Items to be able to say that you can increase the factors you use for it and not really be at risk of failing to cast the spell (although an item imbued with a lower level spell will still only be able to push its factors so far).</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I could think of for the casting pool would be &quot;original creator's [Arcana] rating&quot;, since the Imbuement is effectively a contained Imago of their understanding of the spell. You're right, there's a level of disassociate you have to do between game mechanics and in-game reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T14:11:50-08:00","id":1499399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499397#post1499397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, there's a level of disassociate you have to do between game mechanics and in-game reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>A possible in-universe explanation of the observarion (which may or may not be \u2018right\u2019): The \u2018heavier\u2019 spells are more driven to Do and Be than the \u2018lighter\u2019 spells. Espoused by the Mysterium, whose motto is \u201cMagic is Alive.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T10:45:41-08:00","id":1499869,"title":"","content":"Would perfected poison have a similar Toxicity to the material it is made from? Or would they have standard toxicity of say, 10?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:04:02-08:00","id":1499882,"title":"","content":"Amplify the toxicity by [Potency], maybe? I'm not sure you can refine poison manually, so I'm assuming the spell is the origin of this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:34:31-08:00","id":1499891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499882#post1499882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amplify the toxicity by [Potency], maybe? I'm not sure you can refine poison manually, so I'm assuming the spell is the origin of this</div> </div> </div> </div>For my purposes, yeah it's from the spell. I'm afraid I'm a bit hesitant since that's somewhat counter to how other perfected materials work. For example, perfected stone has +1 durability, not + Potency durability. I might just go +1 Toxicity with some miscellaneous supernatural traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:37:49-08:00","id":1499893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499869#post1499869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would perfected poison have a similar Toxicity to the material it is made from? Or would they have standard toxicity of say, 10?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d keep Toxicity, and instead state that the toxin\u2019s presence and the damage it inflicts are undetectable until the victim is at death\u2019s door.<br /> <br /> This is me borrowing a common Wuxia trope (well, one common in Korean ones at the least); the \u201cFormless Poison\u201d used by elder masters of the Sichuan Tang clan (the wuxia version, not the real-life people!). It is said to be utterly odorless and tasteless, and thus invisible to all but the most enlightened senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:47:15-08:00","id":1499898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499893#post1499893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019d keep Toxicity, and instead state that the toxin\u2019s presence and the damage it inflicts are undetectable until the victim is at death\u2019s door.<br /> <br /> This is me borrowing a common Wuxia trope (well, one common in Korean ones at the least); the \u201cFormless Poison\u201d used by elder masters of the Sichuan Tang clan (the wuxia version, not the real-life people!). It is said to be utterly odorless and tasteless, and thus invisible to all but the most enlightened senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was already a trope? Awesome. I was already planning on something like that as it\u2019s special property, but I\u2019m glad that not just what I think perfected poison would be like. (A lot of media I\u2019ve seen has poison as bright green or purple for some reason.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:59:15-08:00","id":1499902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499898#post1499898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was already a trope? Awesome. I was already planning on something like that as it\u2019s special property, but I\u2019m glad that not just what I think perfected poison would be like. (A lot of media I\u2019ve seen has poison as bright green or purple for some reason.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Another trope is the \u201cDiscipline-Dispersion Poison\u201d, which prevents the Essence user from spending her motes \u2014 er, I mean, hampers a martial artist rousing his inner Qi to execute all those superhuman moves. Lesser practitioners are practically incapacitated, but ones with greater mastery are less so.<br /> <br /> In CofD, this could be somehow locking Mana and/or other \u2018fuel\u2019 usage (I think Werewolf already had something blocking the victim\u2019s Essence usage?), buuuuut this might be too gimmicky to be a Perfected poison. (Non-metallic Perfected materials seem to go for a more prosaic enhancement.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T14:09:47-08:00","id":1499904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499902#post1499902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another trope is the \u201cDiscipline-Dispersion Poison\u201d, which prevents the Essence user from spending her motes \u2014 er, I mean, hampers a martial artist rousing his inner Qi to execute all those superhuman moves. Lesser practitioners are practically incapacitated, but ones with greater mastery are less so.<br /> <br /> In CofD, this could be somehow locking Mana and/or other \u2018fuel\u2019 usage (I think Werewolf already had something blocking the victim\u2019s Essence usage?), buuuuut this might be too gimmicky to be a Perfected poison. (Non-metallic Perfected materials seem to go for a more prosaic enhancement.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026 So I think it\u2019s pretty clear I\u2019m using this to help my recent legacy. I had the legacy produce Volatile Tass, but this might actually be a better idea. Thank you!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T16:52:12-08:00","id":1499918,"title":"","content":"If an item enchanted with Ephemeral Enchantment is picked up by a twilit ephemeral entity in the view of a sleeper, is the spell subject to Dissonance? Hypothetically, the sleeper would focus on the flying sword, but that is not actually what's magic, which is the fact that it's now tangible to an ephemeral entity in the twilight.<br /> <br /> Edit: phrasing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-16-2022, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T19:18:03-08:00","id":1499924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499918#post1499918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an item enchanted with Ephemeral Enchantment is picked up by a twilit ephemeral entity in the view of a sleeper, is the spell subject to Dissonance? Hypothetically, the sleeper would focus on the flying sword, but that is not actually what's magic, which is the fact that it's now tangible to an ephemeral entity in the twilight.<br /> <br /> Edit: phrasing</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so, since it exposes them to blatant Supernal magic, the Curse activates. A Sleeper can be told about magic, truly believe in it and have seen the fallout of a mage's action. But the second they a Thyrsus become a grizzly bear or similar, the Curse activates all the same, and Dissonance with it. <br /> <br /> Since Dissonance only hits at the end of the scene, it means a mage that is going loud technically has quite a bit of leeway to do damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T19:24:54-08:00","id":1499925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499924#post1499924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think so, since it exposes them to blatant Supernal magic, the Curse activates. A Sleeper can be told about magic, truly believe in it and have seen the fallout of a mage's action. But the second they a Thyrsus become a grizzly bear or similar, the Curse activates all the same, and Dissonance with it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough. I was just wondering if the spell being one step removed from the most like thing to be associated with magic would be enough to protect it. Guess not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499924#post1499924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Dissonance only hits at the end of the scene, it means a mage that is going loud technically has quite a bit of leeway to do damage.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s a fair point, and one I hadn\u2019t considered. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T20:40:49-08:00","id":1499927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499918#post1499918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an item enchanted with Ephemeral Enchantment is picked up by a twilit ephemeral entity in the view of a sleeper, is the spell subject to Dissonance? Hypothetically, the sleeper would focus on the flying sword, but that is not actually what's magic, which is the fact that it's now tangible to an ephemeral entity in the twilight.<br /> <br /> Edit: phrasing</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say no. The magic making the sword solid to the spirit isnt obvious<i> &quot;supernal&quot;</i> magic. (Even casting the spell on the sword in front of sleepers probably wouldnt cause paradox (barring over reaching). A sword floating about is obviously weird but its not floating due to supernal magic. An observer isnt going to think &quot;wow that sword must be enchanted so a spirit can pick it up and make it look like its floating&quot; and then erode the spell making the sword solid to the spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499924#post1499924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think so, since it exposes them to blatant Supernal magic, the Curse activates. A Sleeper can be told about magic, truly believe in it and have seen the fallout of a mage's action. But the second they a Thyrsus become a grizzly bear or similar, the Curse activates all the same, and Dissonance with it.<br /> <br /> Since Dissonance only hits at the end of the scene, it means a mage that is going loud technically has quite a bit of leeway to do damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's blatant about the magic on the sword?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 12-17-2022, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T13:21:47-08:00","id":1499964,"title":"","content":"Would you consider the Cipher Pata from Elden Ring an example of a Eidolon or Platonic Form? Or would that be more like a Artifact? For those that haven\u2019t played, and don\u2019t want to look it up, it\u2019s basically a section of holy script written in light by the closest thing in the setting has to a Angel, which is used as a weapon. You stab people with it like a katar. It has no physical component to it\u2019s damage, instead being pure \u201choly\u201d damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T13:55:16-08:00","id":1499967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1499964#post1499964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you consider the Cipher Pata from Elden Ring an example of a Eidolon or Platonic Form? Or would that be more like a Artifact? For those that haven\u2019t played, and don\u2019t want to look it up, it\u2019s basically a section of holy script written in light by the closest thing in the setting has to a Angel, which is used as a weapon. You stab people with it like a katar. It has no physical component to it\u2019s damage, instead being pure \u201choly\u201d damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That honestly sounds like an Artifact, that's using one of the Subtle Arcana's direct damage spells whenever it's used to &quot;stab&quot; someone. The blade itself sounds like <u>Invisible Runes</u>, anchored to the arm and activating the damage spell as a Contingent effect.<br /> <br /> Tangentially related; can you Imbue a spell into an <u>Invisible Rune</u>? I'm pretty sure you could make a Basilisk out of it, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-17-2022, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T14:45:45-08:00","id":1499971,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a bit weird, but I think you can, with one the spells that alters the imbuement process. I don\u2019t see it as any different than imbuing a living thing, but only using Prime. I\u2019m on the road, though and I don\u2019t have access to the books right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T16:51:33-08:00","id":1499992,"title":"","content":"The Curse isn't triggered by magic that is obviously Supernal, it's triggered by Supernal magic that is obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T11:16:22-08:00","id":1500181,"title":"","content":"What would be some in-game explanations as to why such a high Presence is needed to be Fluent in High Speech?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T11:27:25-08:00","id":1500182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500181#post1500181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be some in-game explanations as to why such a high Presence is needed to be Fluent in High Speech?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that given the general description of High Speech in ways where it seems to not really have much in the way of a vocabulary or grammatical structure that one could become practiced in, the only means by which somebody could become fluent in it (particularly according to the standard of what the book describes fluency as entailing) is if they're well-heeled in and have an intuitive sense for effective communication with other people overall. You're good at projecting yourself, and fluency becomes a case of learning how to make High Speech and its mode of only conveying truth line up with that to be able to speak to people with more depth and nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T14:39:52-08:00","id":1500196,"title":"","content":"Does <u>Display of Power</u> also reveal Attainment use, or are they too far removed from spells? The Dispellation Reach doesn't apply, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T15:16:52-08:00","id":1500204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500196#post1500196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does <u>Display of Power</u> also reveal Attainment use, or are they too far removed from spells? The Dispellation Reach doesn't apply, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>If fae Contracts can be revealed with it (by adding Fate, but still), I don\u2019t see why Attainments wouldn\u2019t be. Especially ones based on spells. <br /> <br /> By the Reach option, I think you mean Counterspell? I feel dispellation spells ought to work on Attainments, and Counterspell not, but this is pure guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T15:30:05-08:00","id":1500206,"title":"","content":"Attainments are not Supernal magic, but they are magic in the sense that the Prime purview would still cover them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T16:25:43-08:00","id":1500222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500204#post1500204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If fae Contracts can be revealed with it (by adding Fate, but still), I don\u2019t see why Attainments wouldn\u2019t be. Especially ones based on spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500204#post1500204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the Reach option, I think you mean Counterspell? I feel dispellation spells ought to work on Attainments, and Counterspell not, but this is pure guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed what I meant - however, by RAW on Page 199, Attainments are immune to countering or dispelling. You can put out the fires caused by a fire-starter Legacy, but you can't directly stop them from igniting flamable objects in the first place. It <i>does</i> say that a Greater Utility Attainment &quot;may offer the ability to counter all supernatural powers of a kind, including the Legacy Attainment&quot;, which I <i>think</i> means a Legacy with <u>Dispel Magic</u> or <u>Supernal Dispellation</u> as their Adept-slot powers can banish Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T17:15:21-08:00","id":1500231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500222#post1500222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> <br /> That is indeed what I meant - however, by RAW on Page 199, Attainments are immune to countering or dispelling. You can put out the fires caused by a fire-starter Legacy, but you can't directly stop them from igniting flamable objects in the first place. It <i>does</i> say that a Greater Utility Attainment &amp;quot;may offer the ability to counter all supernatural powers of a kind, including the Legacy Attainment&amp;quot;, which I <i>think</i> means a Legacy with <u>Dispel Magic</u> or <u>Supernal Dispellation</u> as their Adept-slot powers can banish Attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Missed the page 199 thing. Then RAW is that, simple.<br /> <br /> The part about Greater Utility Attainment likely refers to only Arcanum Attainments, not Legacy Attainments, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T02:56:52-08:00","id":1500278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500222#post1500222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is indeed what I meant - however, by RAW on Page 199, Attainments are immune to countering or dispelling. You can put out the fires caused by a fire-starter Legacy, but you can't directly stop them from igniting flamable objects in the first place. It <i>does</i> say that a Greater Utility Attainment &quot;may offer the ability to counter all supernatural powers of a kind, including the Legacy Attainment&quot;, which I <i>think</i> means a Legacy with <u>Dispel Magic</u> or <u>Supernal Dispellation</u> as their Adept-slot powers can banish Attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>A power that counters a specific effect rather than a type of magic can counter Legacy Attainments. This includes the Greater Utility Attainments (the 4 dot Arcana Attainments). For example, a mage with Death 4+ can use Inviolate Soul to enter a Clash of Wills with a reaper who attempts to steal the mage's soul with a Legacy Attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T10:57:43-08:00","id":1500312,"title":"","content":"So, Prime. Today I\u2019m curious about some of the more out there potential uses of the Arcanum. Mostly, I\u2019m interested whether Prime alone can do something, even if it\u2019s not very well. I\u2019ve asked some of these questions before, but my posts were much messier back then, and I didn\u2019t get a lot of responses. I\u2019m also curious if those responses changed.<br /> <br /> Is it reasonable to say that Prime Veiling can obscure symbolism of, or from a subject? For example, can one hide the symbolism of a stop sign so it appears to be gibberish? Can one extend that spoken language, replicating the Curse of Bable?<br /> <br /> Is it reasonable to use Prime Veiling to hide a subject from just Sleepers, Sleepwalkers, or Mages?<br /> <br /> Is it reasonable to use Prime on someone who has a nimbus tilt already on them to intensify the tilt into a related condition?<br /> <br /> Is it reasonable to use Prime to heal others, through Pattern Restoration? Either by projecting their own Pattern Restoration, or by using another Mage\u2019s Pattern Restoration? (Technically, Prime can give Mage sight to others. Would this be similar?)<br /> <br /> Edit: I had some more right after I walked away. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Is it reasonable to use Prime Ruling to change the Nimbus tilt to whatever?<br /> <br /> Is it reasonable to Prime Compelling to inflict one\u2019s Nimbus tilt as a spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-21-2022, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T19:48:03-08:00","id":1500349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500312#post1500312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Prime. Today I\u2019m curious about some of the more out there potential uses of the Arcanum. Mostly, I\u2019m interested whether Prime alone can do something, even if it\u2019s not very well. I\u2019ve asked some of these questions before, but my posts were much messier back then, and I didn\u2019t get a lot of responses. I\u2019m also curious if those responses changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely off the cuff, with the usual disclaimers that follow from such:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it reasonable to say that Prime Veiling can obscure symbolism of, or from a subject? For example, can one hide the symbolism of a stop sign so it appears to be gibberish? Can one extend that spoken language, replicating the Curse of Bable? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this sounds doable. Conceptual inversions of Prime 2 Invisible Runes and Prime 2 Words of Truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it reasonable to use Prime Veiling to hide a subject from just Sleepers, Sleepwalkers, or Mages? </div> </div> </div>Mmm... Veiling has two uses. One is &quot;hide subject that falls under the Arcanum's purview from general scrutiny.&quot; (Matter 2 Hidden Hoard) With this, Prime could hide something magical from Sleepers, and perhaps Sleepwalkers with a Reach. But Prime couldn't hide something general from general Sleepers/Sleepwalkers with this alone. Well, maybe Yes with enough Reach? Or maybe savants of the Veiling Practice among the Rapt knows something\u2026 (Also, we gotta find some way to balance Dissonance.)<br /> <br /> Veiling's other use is &quot;hide general subject from phenomenon that falls under the Arcanum's purview.&quot; (Matter 2 Machine Invisibility) With this, Prime could hide something general from mages, especially (or only?) their Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it reasonable to use Prime on someone who has a nimbus tilt already on them to intensify the tilt into a related condition? </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Prime Perfecting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it reasonable to use Prime to heal others, through Pattern Restoration? Either by projecting their own Pattern Restoration, or by using another Mage\u2019s Pattern Restoration? (Technically, Prime can give Mage sight to others. Would this be similar?) </div> </div> </div>Nah. Pattern Restoration is largely Life stuff (as Life's utility Attainment suggests). Maybe a Legacy Attainment could allow a mage to use Pattern Restoration at others? (I remember doing something like that in one of my homebrews.) Prime 4 Apocalypse is less about giving Mage Template Features to somebody else, and more about &quot;BEHOLD!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: I had some more right after I walked away. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Is it reasonable to use Prime Ruling to change the Nimbus tilt to whatever?<br /> <br /> Is it reasonable to Prime Compelling to inflict one\u2019s Nimbus tilt as a spell? </div> </div> </div>I'd put &quot;change Nimbus Tilt that's already here&quot; at Weaving.<br /> <br /> Changing what Nimbus Tilt a mage imposes is likely Patterning, given how it's something fundamental enough to require a Gnosis level up.<br /> <br /> Imposing your Nimbus Tilt without flaring your Immediate Nimbus is likely Ruling. Imposing someone else's Nimbus Tilt likely requires Combining this with Prime 2 Nimbus Forgery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Further thoughts 12-21-2022, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T20:54:44-08:00","id":1500352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500349#post1500349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Largely off the cuff, with the usual disclaimers that follow from such:</div> </div> </div> </div> That's fine, I realize I'm asking some out there questions anyways. Thank you for answering.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500349#post1500349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this sounds doable. Conceptual inversions of Prime 2 Invisible Runes and Prime 2 Words of Truth.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500349#post1500349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmm... Veiling has two uses. One is &quot;hide subject that falls under the Arcanum's purview from general scrutiny.&quot; (Matter 2 Hidden Hoard) With this, Prime could hide something magical from Sleepers, and perhaps Sleepwalkers with a Reach. But Prime couldn't hide something general from general Sleepers/Sleepwalkers with this alone. Well, maybe Yes with enough Reach? Or maybe savants of the Veiling Practice among the Rapt knows something\u2026 (Also, we gotta find some way to balance Dissonance.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Would this be enough to hide a Mage from sleepers? Seems like not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500349#post1500349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Veiling's other use is &quot;hide general subject from phenomenon that falls under the Arcanum's purview.&quot; (Matter 2 Machine Invisibility) With this, Prime could hide something general from mages, especially (or only?) their Mage Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. That seems useful. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500349#post1500349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Prime Perfecting.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500349#post1500349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. Pattern Restoration is largely Life stuff (as Life's utility Attainment suggests). Maybe a Legacy Attainment could allow a mage to use Pattern Restoration at others? (I remember doing something like that in one of my homebrews.) Prime 4 Apocalypse is less about giving Mage Template Features to somebody else, and more about &quot;BEHOLD!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. That's disappointing. That seems really weird to me, but it seems consistent with what I've heard before. So, what about triggering it in other Mages, and paying the costs for them? Is that possible in your opinion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500349#post1500349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd put &quot;change Nimbus Tilt that's already here&quot; at Weaving.</div> </div> </div> </div> That seems fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500349#post1500349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing what Nimbus Tilt a mage imposes is likely Patterning, given how it's something fundamental enough to require a Gnosis level up.</div> </div> </div> </div> Really? So you can change your tilt to someone else's with Prime 2, but you have to wait until Prime 4 to change it how you like?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500349#post1500349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imposing your Nimbus Tilt without flaring your Immediate Nimbus is likely Ruling. Imposing someone else's Nimbus Tilt likely requires Combining this with Prime 2 Nimbus Forgery.</div> </div> </div> </div> What if you had the Mage in question present? Could you force their Nimbus tilt on someone else?<br /> <br /> If it wouldn't be too much trouble, could one attach their Nimbus tilt to the comprehension of symbolism, like reading a book, with Prime Weaving?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T06:22:44-08:00","id":1500369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500352#post1500352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. That's disappointing. That seems really weird to me, but it seems consistent with what I've heard before. So, what about triggering it in other Mages, and paying the costs for them? Is that possible in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d like to say No, but we already had spells affecting things like Spell Control (Prime 4 Primal Transfer), so Maybe Yes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Though I said Pattern Restoration is Life, this particular trick may be Prime, in line with Primal Transfer.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really? So you can change your tilt to someone else's with Prime 2, but you have to wait until Prime 4 to change it how you like? </div> </div> </div>Eh, Prime 2 Nimbus Forgery requires you to do a bunch legwork and then restricts you to copying only the one you Scrutinized, while our hypothetical Prime 4 spell would skip all the legwork *and* could get us a never-seen-before Nimbus effect, so it seems fair enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if you had the Mage in question present? Could you force their Nimbus tilt on someone else? </div> </div> </div>It\u2026 sounds doable with some Reach, perhaps? Gonna have to do the actual Creative Thaumaturgy tinkering to work that one out, buuuuut I\u2019m busy right now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it wouldn't be too much trouble, could one attach their Nimbus tilt to the comprehension of symbolism, like reading a book, with Prime Weaving? </div> </div> </div>Not sure what this one means. Something like a basilisk, except you get hammered with a Nimbus Tilt instead of a spell? If so, it sounds like one of the Imbue-variant spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T14:03:18-08:00","id":1500526,"title":"","content":"Several questions about different topics:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>If <u>in-game</u> I create a Perfected Material, do I need to buy the merit with experiences? </b><br /> Example, I am a Moros, I have a small coin made of lead, and I spend the time to make it pass 10 times in and out if Twilight (less than 2 minutes if I make a couple of small portals) making it Perfected Lead, do I need to buy the merit? Do I gain it for &quot;free&quot;?</li> <li><b>How much content (and distribution) does an item need to count as Magical Tool made of a Perfected Material? </b><br /> For example, how much (and where should it go) Perfected silver does the cellphone of my Acanthus Free Councilor need to have to count as being a perfected Magical tool?\u200b</li> <li><b>What is the main Arcana of &quot;Malleable Thorns&quot; (Fate \u2022\u2022 + Mind \u2022\u2022)?</b><br /> By main I ask the one that when growing grants free reach. I assume Fate from the context, but it is not clear.</li> <li><b>&quot;Shifting Sands&quot; do you spend the spell duration in the past and that's it? Or do you time travel and start anew?</b><br /> The spell has Potency primary, if I reach to roll back 1 scene, but do not apply successes to Duration, do I travel 1 scene and then I spend Duration/turns there? Or since this has an effect that can be lasting, Duration is not relevant and I just time traveled one scene to try new things from there?<br /> \u200b</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-17-2023, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T17:15:24-08:00","id":1500542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500526#post1500526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several questions about different topics:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>If <u>in-game</u> I create a Perfected Material, do I need to buy the merit with experiences? </b><br /> Example, I am a Moros, I have a small coin made of lead, and I spend the time to make it pass 10 times in and out if Twilight (less than 2 minutes if I make a couple of small portals) making it Perfected Lead, do I need to buy the merit? Do I gain it for &quot;free&quot;?</li> <li><b>How much content (and distribution) does an item need to count as Magical Tool made of a Perfected Material? </b><br /> For example, how much (and where should it go) Perfected silver does the cellphone of my Acanthus Free Councilor need to have to count as being a perfected Magical tool?\u200b</li> <li><b>What is the main Arcana of &quot;Malleable Thorns&quot; (Fate \u2022\u2022 + Mind \u2022\u2022)?</b><br /> By main I ask the one that when growing grants free reach. I assume Fate from the context, but it is not clear.</li> <li><b>&quot;Shield of Chronos&quot; do you spend the spell duration in the past and that's it? Or do you time travel and start anew?</b><br /> The spell has Potency primary, if I reach to roll back 1 scene, but do not apply successes to Duration, do I travel 1 scene and then I spend Duration/turns there? Or since this has an effect that can be lasting, Duration is not relevant and I just time traveled one scene to try new things from there?<br /> \u200b</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>1. ST's call, but rule of thumb is that no, you don't have to buy Merit dots, but it isn't covered by Sanctity of Merits. So you have the item, but it might get lost, stolen, or destroyed without your approval.<br /> <br /> 2. I'd rule &quot;majority&quot; - so more than half of the structure, or at least a symbolically significant portion. For the cellphone, the casing would be a good portion.<br /> <br /> 3. I... want to say Mind, since the Hedge is largely psychoactive, but the general structure of multi-arcana spells in SoS looks like whichever Arcana is listed first is the &quot;primary&quot; Arcana. On the other hand, it would probably make sense to say that you only get free Reach for the LOWER of the two Arcana, in situations like this.<br /> <br /> 4. ...Do you mean <u>Shifting Sands</u>? <u>Shield of Chronos</u> is a Veiling effect that occludes the subject from temporal scrying - say I cast it on myself for the next hour, anyone trying to use <u>Postcognition</u> on my timeline thereafer would be unable to view that hour, and attepts to foretell me with <u>Divination</u> or <u>Prophecy</u> during that hour would be stymed.<br /> <br /> For <u>Shifting Sands</u>, you start the scene over. Anyone looking at them under Time Mage Sight will see the temporal distortion until you catch up to where you were when you cast the spell, but the effect is otherwise Lasting (I think).<br /> <br /> <br /> Tangentially related question to the Perfected Metals - would it be reasonable to add a Reach effect to <u>Ex Nihilo</u> to create Perfected materials? Say, use it to create a spear made of Siderite, or Dumanium? And if so, how much Reach should it cost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":".  Spelling 01-17-2023, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T17:29:11-08:00","id":1500544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500542#post1500542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. ST's call, but rule of thumb is that no, you don't have to buy Merit dots, but it isn't covered by Sanctity of Merits. So you have the item, but it might get lost, stolen, or destroyed without your approval.<br /> <br /> 2. I'd rule &quot;majority&quot; - so more than half of the structure, or at least a symblically significant portion. For the cellphone, the casing would be a good portion.<br /> <br /> 3. I... want to say Mind, since the Hedge is largely psychoactive, but the general structure of multi-arcana spells in SoS looks like whichever Arcana is listed first is the &quot;primary&quot; Arcana. On the other hand, it would probably make sense to say that you only get free Reach for the LOWER of the two Arcana, in situations like this.<br /> <br /> 4. ...Do you mean <u>Shifting Sands</u>? <u>Shield of Chronos</u> is a Veiling effect that occludes the subject from temporal scrying - say I cast it on myself for the next hour, anyone trying to use <u>Postcognition</u> on my timeline thereafer would be unable to view that hour, and attepts to foretell me with <u>Divination</u> or <u>Prophecy</u> during that hour would be stymed.<br /> <br /> For <u>Shifting Sands</u>, you start the scene over. Anyone looking at them under Time Mage Sight will see the temporal distortion until you catch up to where you were when you cast the spell, but the effect is otherwise Lasting (I think).<br /> <br /> <br /> Tangentially related question to the Perfected Metals - would it be reasonable to add a Reach effect to <u>Ex Nihilo</u> to create Perfected materials? Say, use it to create a spear made of Siderite, or Dumanium? And if so, how much Reach should it cost?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks for all the answers, and yes it was <b>Shifting Sands</b> for question 4. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T17:53:51-08:00","id":1500548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500544#post1500544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for all the answers, and yes it was <b>Shifting Sands</b> for question 4. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>For shifting sands, you'd go back X scenes for the duration of the shifting sands spell (which if it was longer than X scenes would mean you'd catch up to the present.) Any changes become lasting when you return to the present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T21:24:01-08:00","id":1500573,"title":"","content":"Two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Would it be reasonable to add a Reach effect to <u>Ex Nihilo</u> to create Perfected materials? Say, use it to create a spear made of Siderite, or Dumanium? And if so, how much Reach should it cost?<br /> <br /> 2. <u>Transmission</u> is a Duration-primary spell. I assume that, by default, any alterations you make with it are Lasting in that, say, a cloud upload broadcast you altered to say one thing wouldn't revert to the original transmission once the spell ends. Is the spell meant to be adding an inherent ability to the target for the duration, allowing them to alter signals at will? Or do you need to cast the spell every time you make a change, and specificly are targeting the desired signal?<br /> <br /> Or, more simply, does <u>Transmission</u> target the signals, or the editors? \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T22:02:10-08:00","id":1500579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500573#post1500573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Would it be reasonable to add a Reach effect to <u>Ex Nihilo</u> to create Perfected materials? Say, use it to create a spear made of Siderite, or Dumanium? And if so, how much Reach should it cost?</div> </div> </div> </div> For perfected Materials in and of themselves\u2026I wouldn\u2019t say you need a reach. They are natural materials with unusual properties. However, I would assume they require a mana to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500573#post1500573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. <u>Transmission</u> is a Duration-primary spell. I assume that, by default, any alterations you make with it are Lasting in that, say, a cloud upload broadcast you altered to say one thing wouldn't revert to the original transmission once the spell ends. Is the spell meant to be adding an inherent ability to the target for the duration, allowing them to alter signals at will? Or do you need to cast the spell every time you make a change, and specificly are targeting the desired signal?<br /> <br /> Or, more simply, does <u>Transmission</u> target the signals, or the editors? \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div> So the only way I can imagine this working is like a filter placed in the path of a flashlight beam at a particular moment. Let\u2019s say you want to hijack the air waves to give someone a commercial at that moment. You would need to know the direction of the radio tower and place a wall that would filter the light that would reach the device\u2026or you could wrap it around the device and not care about the direction. You could also wrap it around the radio, and accept that everyone is getting a commercial break. If you end the spell too early\u2026everyone goes back to their regularly scheduled programming, and are probably confused. I don\u2019t think you are giving anything an extra property, though I will note that light technically changes as it bends around objects, just like all other types of waves. Perhaps the spell exploits this property to actually change the light.<br /> <br /> Edit: for clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-18-2023, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T22:12:32-08:00","id":1500582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500579#post1500579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the only way I can imagine this working is like a filter placed in the path of a flashlight beam at a particular moment. Let\u2019s say you want to hijack the air waves to give someone a commercial at that moment. You would need to know the direction of the radio tower and place a wall that would filter the light that would reach the device\u2026or you could wrap it around the device and not care about the direction. You could also wrap it around the radio, and accept that everyone is getting a commercial break. If you end the spell too early\u2026everyone goes back to their regularly scheduled programming, and are probably confused. I don\u2019t think you are giving anything an extra property, though I will note that light technically changes as it bends around objects, just like all other types of waves. Perhaps the spell exploits this property to actually change the light.<br /> <br /> Edit: for clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the angle I'm looking at it from is from the perspective of a Mage who already has <u>Tune In</u> cast on themselves. They can perceive data and signals all around them, and <u>Transmission</u> allows you to manipulate those signals. A Matter-Life Mage can give themselves the communicative properties of a cellphone, but I'm a bit confused as to whether a Forces Mage can do something similar without having to constantly spam <u>Transmission</u>. (I'd imagine you could Creative Thaumaturgy-up a Forces spell that allows you to be your own cellphone, I'm mostly trying to work out if you can do it already with published spells.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 01-18-2023, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T22:31:53-08:00","id":1500585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1500582#post1500582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose the angle I'm looking at it from is from the perspective of a Mage who already has <u>Tune In</u> cast on themselves. They can perceive data and signals all around them, and <u>Transmission</u> allows you to manipulate those signals. A Matter-Life Mage can give themselves the communicative properties of a cellphone, but I'm a bit confused as to whether a Forces Mage can do something similar without having to constantly spam <u>Transmission</u>. (I'd imagine you could Creative Thaumaturgy-up a Forces spell that allows you to be your own cellphone, I'm mostly trying to work out if you can do it already with published spells.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I see. I guess it could work like Telekinesis, where it\u2019s not one movement predetermined by the spell, but one where you can change it as you go. I guess that would be like changing the color of the filter on the fly in the metaphor. Basically I would say it requires concentration, and potentially a reach.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}